{"jobs":[{"id":"e8ed59d5-798c-49d3-a6ab-9e628d5dc221","title":"Customer Success Manager, Mid-Market, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Madrid","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-03T12:25:05.315+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e8ed59d5-798c-49d3-a6ab-9e628d5dc221","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e8ed59d5-798c-49d3-a6ab-9e628d5dc221/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid-Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own both value realisation and the commercial renewal for your portfolio of customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You will act as a trusted expert who guides customers through integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals — and, as the owner of your customers' renewals, you will be directly accountable for retaining and growing that relationship. You will deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes, build lasting relationships with users and economic buyers alike, and partner closely with Account Executives to expand Harvey's strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a commercially accountable role: you will carry a retention and net-revenue-retention target and own the renewal motion end to end.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding:</strong> Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, and ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement: </strong>Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships: </strong>Navigate complex organisations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage and maintain relationships with executive and economic buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Renewal Ownership: </strong>Own the full renewal lifecycle for your portfolio — building renewal timelines, forecasting accurately, leading commercial conversations, negotiating terms, and closing renewals on or ahead of schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commercial Accountability:</strong> Carry and deliver against a retention / net-revenue-retention target, manage your book of business as a revenue portfolio, and prioritise accordingly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Risk &amp; Churn Management: </strong>Monitor account health, identify at-risk accounts early, and execute structured mitigation plans to protect renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Value Realisation:</strong> Align with customers on adoption rates and measurable outcomes, and quantify ROI in business terms that support renewal and expansion decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion: </strong>Identify and drive expansion opportunities within your accounts, partnering with Account Executives where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Orchestration: </strong>Coordinate Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Finance to move renewals and expansions to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Mid-Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms, including direct ownership of renewals, retention, or a commercial/account-management target.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning and delivering against a revenue, retention, or net-revenue-retention number.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running the renewal motion end to end — forecasting, building renewal plans, and leading commercial negotiations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commercial and negotiation acumen: comfort discussing pricing, structuring terms, and handling objections through to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Account management and portfolio planning across a book of business, including segmentation and revenue-based prioritization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identifying at-risk accounts and executing churn-mitigation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantifying and communicating ROI and measurable business value to customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders, including economic buyers and executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal/Finance, and Product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid-Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own both value realisation and the commercial renewal for your portfolio of customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You will act as a trusted expert who guides customers through integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals — and, as the owner of your customers' renewals, you will be directly accountable for retaining and growing that relationship. You will deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes, build lasting relationships with users and economic buyers alike, and partner closely with Account Executives to expand Harvey's strategic partnerships.\n\nThis is a commercially accountable role: you will carry a retention and net-revenue-retention target and own the renewal motion end to end.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, and ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organisations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage and maintain relationships with executive and economic buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Renewal Ownership: Own the full renewal lifecycle for your portfolio — building renewal timelines, forecasting accurately, leading commercial conversations, negotiating terms, and closing renewals on or ahead of schedule.\n\n - Commercial Accountability: Carry and deliver against a retention / net-revenue-retention target, manage your book of business as a revenue portfolio, and prioritise accordingly.\n\n - Risk & Churn Management: Monitor account health, identify at-risk accounts early, and execute structured mitigation plans to protect renewals.\n\n - Value Realisation: Align with customers on adoption rates and measurable outcomes, and quantify ROI in business terms that support renewal and expansion decisions.\n\n - Expansion: Identify and drive expansion opportunities within your accounts, partnering with Account Executives where appropriate.\n\n - Cross-Functional Orchestration: Coordinate Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Finance to move renewals and expansions to close.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Mid-Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:\n\n - 3–4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms, including direct ownership of renewals, retention, or a commercial/account-management target.\n\n - A track record of owning and delivering against a revenue, retention, or net-revenue-retention number.\n\n - Experience running the renewal motion end to end — forecasting, building renewal plans, and leading commercial negotiations.\n\n - Commercial and negotiation acumen: comfort discussing pricing, structuring terms, and handling objections through to close.\n\n - Account management and portfolio planning across a book of business, including segmentation and revenue-based prioritization.\n\n - Identifying at-risk accounts and executing churn-mitigation strategies.\n\n - Quantifying and communicating ROI and measurable business value to customers.\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders, including economic buyers and executive sponsors.\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal/Finance, and Product teams.\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth.\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e04146f6-f79a-4023-9523-fe691038b330","title":"Customer Success Manager, Mid Market, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-25T09:45:38.623+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e04146f6-f79a-4023-9523-fe691038b330","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e04146f6-f79a-4023-9523-fe691038b330/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong>: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships</strong>: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics</strong>: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion and Renewal</strong>: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Mid Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing a high volume of customer-facing projects and timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Running in-person meetings w/ executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Driving key customer metrics and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Success Metrics: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.\n\n - Expansion and Renewal: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Mid Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:\n\n - 3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth\n\n - Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization\n\n - Managing a high volume of customer-facing projects and timelines\n\n - Running in-person meetings w/ executives\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders\n\n - Driving key customer metrics and outcomes\n\n - Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0d750bf9-d3f2-4816-9e28-23d12a0ef2e2","title":"Enterprise Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-01T14:18:53.180+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0d750bf9-d3f2-4816-9e28-23d12a0ef2e2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0d750bf9-d3f2-4816-9e28-23d12a0ef2e2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at top enterprises and leading Law Firms. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and serving as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Leverage adoption rates, utilization metrics, and other KPIs to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals with a background in Enterprise SaaS, legal (big law) or top tier management consulting firms and direct experience managing large-scale technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as committed, collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at top enterprises and leading Law Firms. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and serving as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Leverage adoption rates, utilization metrics, and other KPIs to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals with a background in Enterprise SaaS, legal (big law) or top tier management consulting firms and direct experience managing large-scale technology projects.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly\n\n - Team players described as committed, collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Uncapped Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f2f3f6e5-13c3-46a9-be96-b1afb1e82d11","tierSummary":"OTE $160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Uncapped Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":"Offers Uncapped Commission","components":[{"id":"f6e40296-0fb8-4c52-9c07-0cbf2feaa283","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5ff3fa0e-d0ce-4a60-b18a-a9623ccc4eed","summary":"OTE $160K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000}]}},{"id":"748edfbe-f819-47fd-85bb-3c4974f8913f","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Core Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-23T02:02:56.206+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/748edfbe-f819-47fd-85bb-3c4974f8913f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/748edfbe-f819-47fd-85bb-3c4974f8913f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1><strong><br />What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor junior / intern engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Incident.io\">Incident.io</a>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $250,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.\n\nYou'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions\n\n - Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management\n\n - Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues\n\n - Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint\n\n - Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments\n\n - Mentor junior / intern engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration\n\n - Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience\n\n - Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers\n\n - Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking\n\n - Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment\n\n - Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems\n\n - Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)\n\n - Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation\n\n - Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale\n\n - Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, Incident.io http://Incident.io)\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems\n\n - Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements\n\n - Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000 - $250,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dd270602-e349-4581-940e-e36523409361","tierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"67772ff2-c928-4ec0-b6dc-b11b70b6581d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"13856128-1071-4d35-a2c1-e89ce59cda63","summary":"$200K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"6a08b879-47c9-485c-be22-9ca88002afd6","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"04e17f81-d0a7-4f83-8526-ec4c9532ddcc","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2024-03-08T01:46:09.108+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04e17f81-d0a7-4f83-8526-ec4c9532ddcc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04e17f81-d0a7-4f83-8526-ec4c9532ddcc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Software Engineer, Frontend at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of our different products: Assistant, Vault, Workflows, and Harvey in Microsoft Word and Outlook. You will also lead frontend engineering on new products that we are building at Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. If any of this resonates with you, this role might be right for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-to-end UI features for Assistant, Vault, Workflows, our Word/Outlook add-ins, and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize frontend performance at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor peers through thoughtful code reviews and documentation; help refine our frontend standards and developer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use Tailwind CSS)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working at startups and scaleups (anywhere from early-to-late-stage) is a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Senior Software Engineer, Frontend at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of our different products: Assistant, Vault, Workflows, and Harvey in Microsoft Word and Outlook. You will also lead frontend engineering on new products that we are building at Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. If any of this resonates with you, this role might be right for you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI.\n\n - Lead end-to-end UI features for Assistant, Vault, Workflows, our Word/Outlook add-ins, and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration.\n\n - Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling.\n\n - Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system.\n\n - Optimize frontend performance at scale.\n\n - Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.\n\n - Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments.\n\n - Mentor peers through thoughtful code reviews and documentation; help refine our frontend standards and developer experience.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use Tailwind CSS)\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience working at startups and scaleups (anywhere from early-to-late-stage) is a plus\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000 - $260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-TH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"22de4d9f-5f40-44a9-9cde-8ea7f4347dd2","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"adebe729-c2c6-4da7-ad46-da541c2b678d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d79eef25-1386-43ed-b99a-02343b5c6666","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"a35efd1c-e5ad-4556-bfa4-d2e13f8b7f1c","title":"Applied Legal Researcher","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-05T02:45:51.904+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a35efd1c-e5ad-4556-bfa4-d2e13f8b7f1c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a35efd1c-e5ad-4556-bfa4-d2e13f8b7f1c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a legal researcher with a strong understanding of how law firms, financial institutions, large corporations, and other organizations deliver professional services and execute complex legal and knowledge work tasks. We have incredible product-market fit and demand across diverse customer profiles. Executing on this demand requires a strong understanding of our customers' workflows and how those workflows can be accelerated by AI systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To facilitate the development of these systems, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and deliver subject-matter expertise to support AI research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with our engineering, product, and design teams to define and develop AI systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and improve AI systems through prompt engineering, fine tuning, and other techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build proprietary benchmarks and datasets to evaluate models and model systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with clients to understand their workflows, identify pain points, and translate complex business and legal requirements into technical solutions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD from a top US law school or equivalent post-graduate qualification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-7 years of experience at a US law firm, financial institution, or equivalent professional service provider</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For NYC applicants: experience working in-house or at a financial institution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to deliver high quality work product on demanding deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to effectively communicate with a variety internal and external stakeholders and translate complex problems effectively between them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to define positive outcomes in situations with underspecified success criteria</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep intellectual curiosity and eagerness to learn across domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness and desire to do work in the trenches - e.g., grading hundreds of answers, breaking down thousands of documents - getting the models to do junior associate work requires a lot of things that look like junior associate work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 - $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a legal researcher with a strong understanding of how law firms, financial institutions, large corporations, and other organizations deliver professional services and execute complex legal and knowledge work tasks. We have incredible product-market fit and demand across diverse customer profiles. Executing on this demand requires a strong understanding of our customers' workflows and how those workflows can be accelerated by AI systems.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nTo facilitate the development of these systems, you will:\n\n - Develop and deliver subject-matter expertise to support AI research\n\n - Work closely with our engineering, product, and design teams to define and develop AI systems\n\n - Build and improve AI systems through prompt engineering, fine tuning, and other techniques\n\n - Build proprietary benchmarks and datasets to evaluate models and model systems\n\n - Partner directly with clients to understand their workflows, identify pain points, and translate complex business and legal requirements into technical solutions\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD from a top US law school or equivalent post-graduate qualification\n\n - 3-7 years of experience at a US law firm, financial institution, or equivalent professional service provider\n\n - For NYC applicants: experience working in-house or at a financial institution\n\n - Demonstrated ability to deliver high quality work product on demanding deadlines\n\n - Ability to effectively communicate with a variety internal and external stakeholders and translate complex problems effectively between them\n\n - Ability to define positive outcomes in situations with underspecified success criteria\n\n - Deep intellectual curiosity and eagerness to learn across domains\n\n - Willingness and desire to do work in the trenches - e.g., grading hundreds of answers, breaking down thousands of documents - getting the models to do junior associate work requires a lot of things that look like junior associate work\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$180,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"75b87c96-9b40-4557-9ce7-8fe401ff73f8","tierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0ad8f558-5c38-43fc-953a-f05a569f2efe","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8835f8a8-91cb-40d7-989e-27de4e858060","summary":"$180K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"787fe815-2f6d-4a9a-8c1e-6205bd105389","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2024-09-13T15:30:45.898+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/787fe815-2f6d-4a9a-8c1e-6205bd105389","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/787fe815-2f6d-4a9a-8c1e-6205bd105389/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users. \n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. \n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. \n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. \n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"50a8df2a-c50e-4326-ae90-0c9f8ee0cf1d","title":"Senior Product Security Engineer","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:29:29.643+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/50a8df2a-c50e-4326-ae90-0c9f8ee0cf1d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/50a8df2a-c50e-4326-ae90-0c9f8ee0cf1d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Software Engineer on the Product Security team at Harvey, you'll be a key technical contributor shaping how security is built into our AI platform. We store and process our customers’ most sensitive data, and as a result, security is paramount at every stage of our product lifecycle. You'll own the security of critical product areas, conduct deep vulnerability research and code review, and partner closely with engineering teams to raise the security bar in the areas you work in (both for humans and agents). You’ll implement both technical controls and security features within the Harvey platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our security program is driven by our collective offensive security experience: breaking into systems at other companies (in white-hat capacities), responding to real security incidents, and learning from other companies’ data breaches. We regularly conduct penetration tests and red team exercises with external security firms. At the same time, we are all software engineers - contributing code daily and approaching security with an engineering-first mindset.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define and implement security standards across the teams you partner with</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incorporate secure design principles at every stage of development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and review security-critical code across key parts of the product, including authentication and access control</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure-by-default libraries and tooling that make secure path easier for the engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive mitigation during security-related incidents, working cross-functionally as needed with Detection &amp; Response as well as other teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and raise the security bar across teams through code reviews, design reviews, and technical guidance</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in product security, application security, offensive security, and/or security-focused software engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record of identifying and remediating software vulnerabilities, demonstrated through CVEs, bug bounty awards, published research, or prior work experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate on cross-functional security initiatives and influence engineering teams on security best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience educating engineers to improve security practices across a team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills with demonstrated experience writing high-quality, production software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills across technical and non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of executing on complex security projects and delivering measurable security improvements</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building security programs or practices at hyper-growth startups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with cloud environments (Azure, GCP, AWS) and cloud-native security patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML systems and emerging security considerations for LLM-based applications</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation Range</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$188,000-282,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Senior Software Engineer on the Product Security team at Harvey, you'll be a key technical contributor shaping how security is built into our AI platform. We store and process our customers’ most sensitive data, and as a result, security is paramount at every stage of our product lifecycle. You'll own the security of critical product areas, conduct deep vulnerability research and code review, and partner closely with engineering teams to raise the security bar in the areas you work in (both for humans and agents). You’ll implement both technical controls and security features within the Harvey platform.\n\nOur security program is driven by our collective offensive security experience: breaking into systems at other companies (in white-hat capacities), responding to real security incidents, and learning from other companies’ data breaches. We regularly conduct penetration tests and red team exercises with external security firms. At the same time, we are all software engineers - contributing code daily and approaching security with an engineering-first mindset.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Help define and implement security standards across the teams you partner with\n\n - Incorporate secure design principles at every stage of development\n\n - Own and review security-critical code across key parts of the product, including authentication and access control\n\n - Build secure-by-default libraries and tooling that make secure path easier for the engineers\n\n - Drive mitigation during security-related incidents, working cross-functionally as needed with Detection & Response as well as other teams\n\n - Mentor engineers and raise the security bar across teams through code reviews, design reviews, and technical guidance\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - 5+ years of experience in product security, application security, offensive security, and/or security-focused software engineering\n\n - Long track record of identifying and remediating software vulnerabilities, demonstrated through CVEs, bug bounty awards, published research, or prior work experience\n\n - Ability to collaborate on cross-functional security initiatives and influence engineering teams on security best practices\n\n - Experience educating engineers to improve security practices across a team\n\n - Strong programming skills with demonstrated experience writing high-quality, production software\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills across technical and non-technical audiences\n\n - Track record of executing on complex security projects and delivering measurable security improvements\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building security programs or practices at hyper-growth startups\n\n - Background with cloud environments (Azure, GCP, AWS) and cloud-native security patterns\n\n - Experience with AI/ML systems and emerging security considerations for LLM-based applications\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$188,000-282,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$188K – $282K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$188K - $282K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ba378027-a5c2-45a8-b1a7-f32890445765","tierSummary":"$188K – $282K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"08eea7d4-f232-4e69-bb7b-3007cc3e325c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d0338759-bc81-4b76-8e53-28f97386f5b6","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6ae4c67a-309e-477e-86db-9b939e972ddb","summary":"$188K – $282K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":282000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":282000}]}},{"id":"1207bcdf-6186-4f54-ac4d-d0575ed6459a","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T11:07:31.444+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1207bcdf-6186-4f54-ac4d-d0575ed6459a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1207bcdf-6186-4f54-ac4d-d0575ed6459a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role  Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3>#LI-KS1</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE  OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. \n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. \n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n#LI-KS1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"be87aefc-9e03-4294-a86f-a4c5e9fddb44","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-10-09T15:21:36.538+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/be87aefc-9e03-4294-a86f-a4c5e9fddb44","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/be87aefc-9e03-4294-a86f-a4c5e9fddb44/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Product Operations Manager at Harvey, you will be the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams — turning strategy into execution across our entire product lifecycle. You'll build and scale the operating systems that help our product teams make better decisions, ship with confidence, and drive measurable impact for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work as an extension of product leadership, balancing hands-on execution with strategic initiatives. This is a role for someone who builds from 0 to 1, thrives in ambiguity, and creates structure where none exists.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inputs to Product Teams</strong> — Ensuring teams have the information they need to make great decisions</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain Voice of Customer systems that synthesize feedback from law firm partners, in-house clients, CSMs, and sales into actionable product signals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish rigorous mechanisms for measuring product success and user impact, including analytics dashboards, KPIs, and clear hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create high-leverage engagement points with customers and partners throughout the product lifecycle — from alpha through post-GA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Streamline key decision points across teams, reducing friction and improving prioritization quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ops of the Product Org</strong> — Creating the operating systems that enable product teams to thrive</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and improve core product development processes, tooling, and team rituals (planning cycles, monthly reviews, roadmap prioritization, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reliable run-of-business systems that scale as Harvey grows — launch calendars, intake frameworks, RACI structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive cross-functional alignment between Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate roadmap planning by coordinating stakeholder inputs and maintaining transparency across the org</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Outputs from Product Teams</strong> — Amplifying product impact by connecting what we build to those who need it</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run Early Access Programs and alpha testing programs that validate product-market fit and surface refinement signals before broad release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own launch coordination end-to-end — ensuring timely, high-confidence rollouts with clear success metrics and post-launch monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain cross-team roadmap visibility that keeps GTM, Legal, and leadership aligned on what's shipping and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make it clear across Harvey what Product is building, how it's progressing, and what's coming nextd optimize operational workflows to ensure agility and scalability as the company grows.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in Product Operations, Product Management, or a closely related operational role at a high growth tech or SaaS company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've built processes and programs from scratch and scaled them thoughtfully — not just inherited and maintained them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with AI-native products, ideally in a domain where model quality and output reliability are central to the user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to translate complex qualitative and quantitative data — usage metrics, feedback themes, retention signals — into clear recommendations and roadmap inputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive alignment across Product, GTM, and Engineering without direct authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with launch coordination, EAPs, or customer feedback loops in a fast-moving product environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're a natural bridge builder: fluent in strategy, comfortable in the weeds, and skilled at creating clarity where none exists. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down — it's where you do your best work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> $155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Senior Product Operations Manager at Harvey, you will be the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams — turning strategy into execution across our entire product lifecycle. You'll build and scale the operating systems that help our product teams make better decisions, ship with confidence, and drive measurable impact for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.\n\nYou'll work as an extension of product leadership, balancing hands-on execution with strategic initiatives. This is a role for someone who builds from 0 to 1, thrives in ambiguity, and creates structure where none exists.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Inputs to Product Teams — Ensuring teams have the information they need to make great decisions\n   \n   - Build and maintain Voice of Customer systems that synthesize feedback from law firm partners, in-house clients, CSMs, and sales into actionable product signals\n   \n   - Establish rigorous mechanisms for measuring product success and user impact, including analytics dashboards, KPIs, and clear hypotheses\n   \n   - Create high-leverage engagement points with customers and partners throughout the product lifecycle — from alpha through post-GA\n   \n   - Streamline key decision points across teams, reducing friction and improving prioritization quality\n   \n   Ops of the Product Org — Creating the operating systems that enable product teams to thrive\n   \n   - Own and improve core product development processes, tooling, and team rituals (planning cycles, monthly reviews, roadmap prioritization, etc.)\n   \n   - Build reliable run-of-business systems that scale as Harvey grows — launch calendars, intake frameworks, RACI structures\n   \n   - Drive cross-functional alignment between Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success\n   \n   - Facilitate roadmap planning by coordinating stakeholder inputs and maintaining transparency across the org\n   \n   Outputs from Product Teams — Amplifying product impact by connecting what we build to those who need it\n   \n   - Design and run Early Access Programs and alpha testing programs that validate product-market fit and surface refinement signals before broad release\n   \n   - Own launch coordination end-to-end — ensuring timely, high-confidence rollouts with clear success metrics and post-launch monitoring\n   \n   - Maintain cross-team roadmap visibility that keeps GTM, Legal, and leadership aligned on what's shipping and why\n   \n   - Make it clear across Harvey what Product is building, how it's progressing, and what's coming nextd optimize operational workflows to ensure agility and scalability as the company grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in Product Operations, Product Management, or a closely related operational role at a high growth tech or SaaS company\n\n - You've built processes and programs from scratch and scaled them thoughtfully — not just inherited and maintained them\n\n - Experience working with AI-native products, ideally in a domain where model quality and output reliability are central to the user experience\n\n - Strong ability to translate complex qualitative and quantitative data — usage metrics, feedback themes, retention signals — into clear recommendations and roadmap inputs\n\n - Proven ability to drive alignment across Product, GTM, and Engineering without direct authority\n\n - Hands-on experience with launch coordination, EAPs, or customer feedback loops in a fast-moving product environment\n\n - You're a natural bridge builder: fluent in strategy, comfortable in the weeds, and skilled at creating clarity where none exists. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down — it's where you do your best work.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n $155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"49773309-f1f6-452b-b831-d009c1f3c7de","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cdc3e8b1-fb8b-4b72-ad68-edcfbdf144cd","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"19f87824-3d48-4b2a-85af-db78235fd6f9","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cef08195-b122-4419-a6ce-bd5e0a3747da","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}},{"id":"e25c329d-178a-47fa-9278-becd45d9fba3","title":"Account Executive, Mid-Market","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-05-16T17:49:42.550+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e25c329d-178a-47fa-9278-becd45d9fba3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e25c329d-178a-47fa-9278-becd45d9fba3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role  Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$240,000 OTE with a 50/50 split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE  OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. \n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene \n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. \n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION \n\n$240,000 OTE with a 50/50 split \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$240K • OTE with a 50/50 split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$240K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fe5a5e62-cedf-44fa-908b-dc9608838712","tierSummary":"$240K • OTE with a 50/50 split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE with a 50/50 split","components":[{"id":"587261a8-71bf-4f8b-b05a-6ee739d51a10","summary":"$240K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}},{"id":"c9cea360-f0b6-4a93-b7b3-0f0145b02ffe","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-01T23:37:42.468+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c9cea360-f0b6-4a93-b7b3-0f0145b02ffe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c9cea360-f0b6-4a93-b7b3-0f0145b02ffe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Site Reliability team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate across teams to drive reliability, security, and compliance throughout the software lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering or similar roles supporting production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Site Reliability team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you. \n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions\n\n - Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements\n\n - Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention\n\n - Collaborate across teams to drive reliability, security, and compliance throughout the software lifecycle\n\n - Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - 5+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering or similar roles supporting production environments\n\n - Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.).\n\n - Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)\n\n - Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)\n\n - Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)\n\n - Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions\n\n - Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000 - $260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ef2f76f1-b729-462a-8dfa-ca63d6db52ee","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3e41688e-2311-4e68-a5b9-1b1511ec255b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"35bce8cc-b2af-4987-9014-95a0e98cfb84","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"4d661139-19ad-42af-9f6c-a68c71263e14","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-01T23:37:40.482+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4d661139-19ad-42af-9f6c-a68c71263e14","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4d661139-19ad-42af-9f6c-a68c71263e14/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Site Reliability team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish best practices for security, compliance, and reliability and collaborate across teams to drive these principles throughout the software lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical mentorship and leadership, promoting best practices and fostering team growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering or similar roles supporting production environments, with proven ability to mentor and guide technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$238,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Site Reliability team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you. \n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions\n\n - Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements\n\n - Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention\n\n - Establish best practices for security, compliance, and reliability and collaborate across teams to drive these principles throughout the software lifecycle\n\n - Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality\n\n - Provide technical mentorship and leadership, promoting best practices and fostering team growth\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - 10+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering or similar roles supporting production environments, with proven ability to mentor and guide technical teams\n\n - Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.)\n\n - Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)\n\n - Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)\n\n - Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)\n\n - Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions\n\n - Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$238,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$238K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"96288ee5-e766-412a-97c2-7aab9aa38c82","tierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1ee58296-b90d-4aeb-bfd7-4431b76807ae","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2c105b5b-8ecf-462e-94b9-eb0943c22b6e","summary":"$238K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"823658d8-21ae-46e5-ac93-1454e6527c63","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Developer Experience","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-15T23:20:03.662+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/823658d8-21ae-46e5-ac93-1454e6527c63","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/823658d8-21ae-46e5-ac93-1454e6527c63/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$175,000 - $250,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.\n\nIf you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..\n\n - Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.\n\n - Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.\n\n - Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.\n\n - Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.\n\n - Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.\n\n - Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.\n\n - Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).\n\n - A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.\n\n - Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$175,000 - $250,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$175K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$175K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"06790009-5c44-4137-bedc-003afac666b8","tierSummary":"$175K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"30f8588e-9035-433b-a11c-804519f3d704","summary":"$175K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":175000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"8d06075d-5be6-42a9-83ac-206e597ff979","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":175000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6ad3902b-2888-4c02-913d-de942e807133","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-08-07T10:47:38.950+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6ad3902b-2888-4c02-913d-de942e807133","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6ad3902b-2888-4c02-913d-de942e807133/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Backend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build foundational backend infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of distributed systems, REST/gRPC APIs, databases, and scalable service architectures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Additional Information </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Toronto, Ontario (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Canadian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CA $196,800 - CA $270,600</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Backend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration experiences for law firms.\n\nYou will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build foundational backend infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations\n\n - Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams\n\n - Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls\n\n - Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams\n\n - Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact\n\n - Strong knowledge of distributed systems, REST/gRPC APIs, databases, and scalable service architectures\n\n - Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n   \n   \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n\n - Location: Toronto, Ontario (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Canadian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nCA $196,800 - CA $270,600\n\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$196.8K - CA$270.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4433b1c4-cd61-4440-b880-1161429b2272","tierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"00395039-b28e-40e2-aa91-a95c54e89bf4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1f1d3ac0-2fc0-4359-8bf8-98ddf41c3335","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0aa0ca3e-33cf-4bd1-977e-6a5abe2ea2ba","summary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600}]}},{"id":"45a49240-f928-4547-93ec-cd3bf5b0191d","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Developer Experience ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-15T23:20:06.231+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/45a49240-f928-4547-93ec-cd3bf5b0191d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/45a49240-f928-4547-93ec-cd3bf5b0191d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategic direction and roadmap for scaling developer experience as Harvey expands, and contribute strategically to team decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide strong technical leadership and mentorship, upholding a high bar for engineering excellence across the team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven technical leadership throughout the entire project lifecycle, including ideation, design, implementation, and productionization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring engineers, guiding architectural decisions, and shaping culture to foster engineering excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$238,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.\n\nIf you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..\n\n - Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.\n\n - Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.\n\n - Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.\n\n - Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.\n\n - Set the strategic direction and roadmap for scaling developer experience as Harvey expands, and contribute strategically to team decision-making.\n\n - Provide strong technical leadership and mentorship, upholding a high bar for engineering excellence across the team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.\n\n - Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.\n\n - Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.\n\n - Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).\n\n - A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.\n\n - Proven technical leadership throughout the entire project lifecycle, including ideation, design, implementation, and productionization.\n\n - Experience mentoring engineers, guiding architectural decisions, and shaping culture to foster engineering excellence.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.\n\n - Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$238,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$238K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ae582a37-7991-466b-a830-ec64892c4c6c","tierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0ac26073-aa9c-422f-ae05-1bbd715f0773","summary":"$238K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"ee4fd003-c2f0-42e1-a02c-79bbe22b7698","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"28559133-c575-4cda-b9fc-c03141255dfe","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"24616c39-e293-4bcc-a3dd-e6f33a71c8ee","title":"Staff Product Designer","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-09-12T23:39:38.961+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24616c39-e293-4bcc-a3dd-e6f33a71c8ee","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24616c39-e293-4bcc-a3dd-e6f33a71c8ee/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000-$260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.\n\nWe’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.\n\n - Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.\n\n - Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.\n\n - Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.\n\n - Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.\n\n - Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.\n\n - Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.\n\n - Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.\n\n - Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.\n\n - Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.\n\n - Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.\n\n - Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000-$260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"cf6be154-160e-4b6d-b7c3-f186123fcec6","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cb45d24b-2139-45f7-9105-8e03723ef9d7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"69b4a3af-7815-4883-b56f-f1f877e37071","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fd53bbeb-0f90-416b-bb80-f5c9592756dc","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"c34ee114-fd2d-4507-9888-711397e037bd","title":"Strategic Account Executive, DACH","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T14:18:16.299+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c34ee114-fd2d-4507-9888-711397e037bd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c34ee114-fd2d-4507-9888-711397e037bd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an Strategic Account Executive to lead commercial growth across the DACH region. This role is responsible for identifying opportunities, managing complex sales cycles, and building long-term relationships within the legal and professional services sector.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position will play a key role in expanding Harvey’s presence in the DACH region, working cross-functionally to deliver tailored solutions to clients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver against sales targets with a focus on sustainable growth and performance excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and grow a portfolio of named accounts across DACH, driving full-funnel sales activity from prospecting through to commercial negotiation and onboarding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand client pain points, organisational structure, and buying processes; tailor solutions that align with strategic outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead high-impact product demos and client meetings that clearly articulate Harvey’s business value and technical capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, legal, engineering, and GTM to inform roadmap and surface client needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop deep, long-term relationships with legal, innovation, and executive stakeholders across the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document learnings, iterate on messaging, and help build scalable processes to accelerate regional growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, preferably with exposure to AI, legaltech, or vertical software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of success managing complex sales cycles with multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain technical products to non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal industry and a commitment to enhancing knowledge work through technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with enterprise sales practices in the DACH region</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and results-oriented, with a collaborative approach to working cross-functionally</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information for Postings</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Munich</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid German work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our DACH team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are seeking an Strategic Account Executive to lead commercial growth across the DACH region. This role is responsible for identifying opportunities, managing complex sales cycles, and building long-term relationships within the legal and professional services sector.\n\nThis position will play a key role in expanding Harvey’s presence in the DACH region, working cross-functionally to deliver tailored solutions to clients.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Deliver against sales targets with a focus on sustainable growth and performance excellence.\n\n - Own and grow a portfolio of named accounts across DACH, driving full-funnel sales activity from prospecting through to commercial negotiation and onboarding.\n\n - Understand client pain points, organisational structure, and buying processes; tailor solutions that align with strategic outcomes.\n\n - Lead high-impact product demos and client meetings that clearly articulate Harvey’s business value and technical capabilities.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, legal, engineering, and GTM to inform roadmap and surface client needs.\n\n - Develop deep, long-term relationships with legal, innovation, and executive stakeholders across the region.\n\n - Document learnings, iterate on messaging, and help build scalable processes to accelerate regional growth.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, preferably with exposure to AI, legaltech, or vertical software\n\n - Track record of success managing complex sales cycles with multiple stakeholders\n\n - Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain technical products to non-technical audiences\n\n - Interest in the legal industry and a commitment to enhancing knowledge work through technology\n\n - Familiarity with enterprise sales practices in the DACH region\n\n - Self-motivated and results-oriented, with a collaborative approach to working cross-functionally\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION FOR POSTINGS\n\n - Location: Munich\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid German work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our DACH team\n\n - Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth\n   \n   \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"099c04d5-4e8e-4bd2-9e39-2a8c4aaffce0","title":"Legal Engineer (Transactional or In-house)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T11:23:01.248+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/099c04d5-4e8e-4bd2-9e39-2a8c4aaffce0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/099c04d5-4e8e-4bd2-9e39-2a8c4aaffce0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to how Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with English- and German-speaking lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand their workflow challenges, strategic objectives, and broader firm context — then demonstrate how Harvey’s AI solutions can address them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in German and English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent), preferably with a transactional, in-house or transformation experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information for Postings</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Germany</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid German work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Germany team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.\n\nSimilar to how Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Engage with English- and German-speaking lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand their workflow challenges, strategic objectives, and broader firm context — then demonstrate how Harvey’s AI solutions can address them.\n\n - Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types.\n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs.\n\n - Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs.\n\n - Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - Fluent in German and English.\n\n - At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent), preferably with a transactional, in-house or transformation experience.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION FOR POSTINGS\n\n - Location: Germany\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid German work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Germany team\n\n - Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth\n   \n   \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"993e43fa-a9a1-45be-9d74-3a96c7c303ef","title":"Majors Customer Success Manager (Asset Management)","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T01:34:15.896+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/993e43fa-a9a1-45be-9d74-3a96c7c303ef","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/993e43fa-a9a1-45be-9d74-3a96c7c303ef/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 25% of the time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in asset management, banking or financial services or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n - Travel required: Up to 25% of the time\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Background in asset management, banking or financial services or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment\n\n - History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.\n\n - Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.\n\n - Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n - $180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-BS1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $210K • OTE 80/20 Split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b3f8cff0-429f-4806-83e2-de057751663a","tierSummary":"$180K – $210K • OTE 80/20 Split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 80/20 Split","components":[{"id":"8d7e89b6-e022-420b-9552-5d854a2c431f","summary":"$180K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000}]}},{"id":"47d3d763-8c64-4e33-b76e-ca15f584c1fd","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-08-07T10:48:13.507+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/47d3d763-8c64-4e33-b76e-ca15f584c1fd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/47d3d763-8c64-4e33-b76e-ca15f584c1fd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Frontend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build foundational infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years (post-BS/MS) of frontend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of frontend technologies such as React, Typescript, and CSS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$196,800 - $270,600 CAD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Frontend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.\n\nYou will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build foundational infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations\n\n - Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams\n\n - Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls\n\n - Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years (post-BS/MS) of frontend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams\n\n - Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact\n\n - Strong knowledge of frontend technologies such as React, Typescript, and CSS\n\n - Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$196,800 - $270,600 CAD\n\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$196.8K - CA$270.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b82c17cf-791c-42fa-ba42-5449e6752903","tierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0a3ad3a5-b5ce-488c-88e7-27ea7964c2d3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d8bda586-5ebf-44be-991a-7dfa7313c4d4","summary":"CA$196.8K – CA$270.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600},{"id":"42b4ef44-2ff9-4c9a-b91f-224bb598fbb6","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"4154ddf4-99e3-4863-9509-826a6faddeea","title":"Legal Engineer, EMEA (Funds or IP)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:47:00.272+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4154ddf4-99e3-4863-9509-826a6faddeea","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4154ddf4-99e3-4863-9509-826a6faddeea/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges, and then explain and demonstrate the value of Harvey’s AI solutions to address them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must be qualified to practice law in England &amp; Wales, with at least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm in the U.K.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in funds, Intellectual Property or within an in-house team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective. \n\nSimilar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Engage with lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges, and then explain and demonstrate the value of Harvey’s AI solutions to address them.\n\n - Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types. \n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs. \n\n - Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs. \n\n - Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Must be qualified to practice law in England & Wales, with at least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm in the U.K.\n\n - Experience in funds, Intellectual Property or within an in-house team\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7d4d8f8e-8c9b-4105-8136-0dbfe54c3512","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-08-22T14:54:36.004+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7d4d8f8e-8c9b-4105-8136-0dbfe54c3512","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7d4d8f8e-8c9b-4105-8136-0dbfe54c3512/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer, Frontend at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of our different products: Assistant, Vault, Workflows, and Harvey in Microsoft Word and Outlook. You will also lead frontend engineering on new products that we are building at Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. If any of this resonates with you, this role might be right for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-to-end UI features for Assistant, Vault, Workflows, our Word/Outlook add-ins, and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize frontend performance at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor peers through thoughtful code reviews and documentation; help refine our frontend standards and developer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use TailwindCSS)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working at startups and scaleups (anywhere from early-to-late-stage) is a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$238,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer, Frontend at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of our different products: Assistant, Vault, Workflows, and Harvey in Microsoft Word and Outlook. You will also lead frontend engineering on new products that we are building at Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. If any of this resonates with you, this role might be right for you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI.\n\n - Lead end-to-end UI features for Assistant, Vault, Workflows, our Word/Outlook add-ins, and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration.\n\n - Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling.\n\n - Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system.\n\n - Optimize frontend performance at scale.\n\n - Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.\n\n - Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments.\n\n - Mentor peers through thoughtful code reviews and documentation; help refine our frontend standards and developer experience.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use TailwindCSS)\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience working at startups and scaleups (anywhere from early-to-late-stage) is a plus\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$238,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$238K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c8802ce6-16b1-4655-805c-6984623a4adc","tierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3cd685c9-ccbe-4e04-8471-738e1188f9f5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8ef87294-c096-4c76-89e4-fd2a82008b7f","summary":"$238K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"b7398afc-09c5-45c9-bbc1-1d00f722b798","title":"Customer Success Manager, Mid-Market, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Paris","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-03T12:23:22.497+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"France"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b7398afc-09c5-45c9-bbc1-1d00f722b798","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b7398afc-09c5-45c9-bbc1-1d00f722b798/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid-Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own both value realisation and the commercial renewal for your portfolio of customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You will act as a trusted expert who guides customers through integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals — and, as the owner of your customers' renewals, you will be directly accountable for retaining and growing that relationship. You will deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes, build lasting relationships with users and economic buyers alike, and partner closely with Account Executives to expand Harvey's strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a commercially accountable role: you will carry a retention and net-revenue-retention target and own the renewal motion end to end.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding:</strong> Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, and ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement: </strong>Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships: </strong>Navigate complex organisations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage and maintain relationships with executive and economic buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Renewal Ownership: </strong>Own the full renewal lifecycle for your portfolio — building renewal timelines, forecasting accurately, leading commercial conversations, negotiating terms, and closing renewals on or ahead of schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commercial Accountability:</strong> Carry and deliver against a retention / net-revenue-retention target, manage your book of business as a revenue portfolio, and prioritise accordingly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Risk &amp; Churn Management: </strong>Monitor account health, identify at-risk accounts early, and execute structured mitigation plans to protect renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Value Realisation:</strong> Align with customers on adoption rates and measurable outcomes, and quantify ROI in business terms that support renewal and expansion decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion: </strong>Identify and drive expansion opportunities within your accounts, partnering with Account Executives where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Orchestration: </strong>Coordinate Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Finance to move renewals and expansions to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Mid-Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms, including direct ownership of renewals, retention, or a commercial/account-management target.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning and delivering against a revenue, retention, or net-revenue-retention number.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running the renewal motion end to end — forecasting, building renewal plans, and leading commercial negotiations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commercial and negotiation acumen: comfort discussing pricing, structuring terms, and handling objections through to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Account management and portfolio planning across a book of business, including segmentation and revenue-based prioritization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identifying at-risk accounts and executing churn-mitigation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantifying and communicating ROI and measurable business value to customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders, including economic buyers and executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal/Finance, and Product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid-Market Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own both value realisation and the commercial renewal for your portfolio of customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You will act as a trusted expert who guides customers through integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals — and, as the owner of your customers' renewals, you will be directly accountable for retaining and growing that relationship. You will deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes, build lasting relationships with users and economic buyers alike, and partner closely with Account Executives to expand Harvey's strategic partnerships.\n\nThis is a commercially accountable role: you will carry a retention and net-revenue-retention target and own the renewal motion end to end.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, and ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organisations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage and maintain relationships with executive and economic buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Renewal Ownership: Own the full renewal lifecycle for your portfolio — building renewal timelines, forecasting accurately, leading commercial conversations, negotiating terms, and closing renewals on or ahead of schedule.\n\n - Commercial Accountability: Carry and deliver against a retention / net-revenue-retention target, manage your book of business as a revenue portfolio, and prioritise accordingly.\n\n - Risk & Churn Management: Monitor account health, identify at-risk accounts early, and execute structured mitigation plans to protect renewals.\n\n - Value Realisation: Align with customers on adoption rates and measurable outcomes, and quantify ROI in business terms that support renewal and expansion decisions.\n\n - Expansion: Identify and drive expansion opportunities within your accounts, partnering with Account Executives where appropriate.\n\n - Cross-Functional Orchestration: Coordinate Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Finance to move renewals and expansions to close.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Mid-Market CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:\n\n - 3–4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms, including direct ownership of renewals, retention, or a commercial/account-management target.\n\n - A track record of owning and delivering against a revenue, retention, or net-revenue-retention number.\n\n - Experience running the renewal motion end to end — forecasting, building renewal plans, and leading commercial negotiations.\n\n - Commercial and negotiation acumen: comfort discussing pricing, structuring terms, and handling objections through to close.\n\n - Account management and portfolio planning across a book of business, including segmentation and revenue-based prioritization.\n\n - Identifying at-risk accounts and executing churn-mitigation strategies.\n\n - Quantifying and communicating ROI and measurable business value to customers.\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders, including economic buyers and executive sponsors.\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal/Finance, and Product teams.\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth.\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c2e8772a-ca9c-44ee-95fb-bbd64f57e7c4","title":"Mid-Market Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-17T22:45:40.244+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c2e8772a-ca9c-44ee-95fb-bbd64f57e7c4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c2e8772a-ca9c-44ee-95fb-bbd64f57e7c4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$125,000 - $145,000 OTE </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.\n\n - Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.\n\n - Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$125,000 - $145,000 OTE \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $145K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1a821dad-ac8b-49c5-99e0-ea901ac294b1","tierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE","components":[{"id":"77354b93-acfa-4657-b21f-bfc16855b3ea","summary":"$125K – $145K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}},{"id":"2eaf5fe2-a82a-4150-8597-f83a041d7fa2","title":"Senior Accountant","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:28:59.399+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2eaf5fe2-a82a-4150-8597-f83a041d7fa2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2eaf5fe2-a82a-4150-8597-f83a041d7fa2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Accountant joins Harvey's Finance team to support the company's international accounting operations from the Dublin office. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's financial records are accurate, compliant, and scalable as the company expands its global footprint. This role will drive core accounting workflows, month-end close, reconciliations, and statutory financial reporting for Harvey's international entities. The ideal candidate is someone who thrives in a high-growth start-up, is detail-oriented, and has excellent interpersonal and communication skills. This is a compelling opportunity to build foundational international accounting processes at one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the legal technology space</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute the monthly close to tight reporting deadlines under US GAAP for the Harvey AI international entities including journal entry processing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare balance sheet reconciliations across all key international accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare monthly / quarterly entity level flux analysis for the international entities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee local statutory audit and reporting requirements including coordination with external auditors, preparation of bridge files between local and US GAAP financial accounts, audit support and technical documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage third party accounting service providers on daily and month end accounting operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare the monthly funding request for the international subsidiaries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with US Corporate Accounting on accounting and reporting matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the international payroll team on the preparation of payroll journals and reconciliations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the tax team on all international tax filings, payments and initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the company’s global expansion initiatives including new entity set up and operationalization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross functional teams on strategic projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and implement process improvements to strengthen controls and increase efficiency as the international business scales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, recommend, and implement AI solutions to drive measurable process improvements across the team</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified Accountant (ACA, ACCA, CPA, CIMA, or equivalent)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big 4 audit training is preferable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years post qualification experience in high growth multinational environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated technical expertise and practical application of IFRS, FRS102, and US GAAP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with ERP systems (NetSuite or similar cloud-based platforms preferred) as well as Excel/Google Sheets, and close management tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment and is comfortable adapting to changing business requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage competing priorities in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills with a collaborative, team-oriented mindset</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong><br /><br />#LI-JM1</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Accountant joins Harvey's Finance team to support the company's international accounting operations from the Dublin office. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's financial records are accurate, compliant, and scalable as the company expands its global footprint. This role will drive core accounting workflows, month-end close, reconciliations, and statutory financial reporting for Harvey's international entities. The ideal candidate is someone who thrives in a high-growth start-up, is detail-oriented, and has excellent interpersonal and communication skills. This is a compelling opportunity to build foundational international accounting processes at one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the legal technology space\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Execute the monthly close to tight reporting deadlines under US GAAP for the Harvey AI international entities including journal entry processing\n\n - Prepare balance sheet reconciliations across all key international accounts\n\n - Prepare monthly / quarterly entity level flux analysis for the international entities\n\n - Oversee local statutory audit and reporting requirements including coordination with external auditors, preparation of bridge files between local and US GAAP financial accounts, audit support and technical documentation\n\n - Manage third party accounting service providers on daily and month end accounting operations\n\n - Prepare the monthly funding request for the international subsidiaries\n\n - Partner closely with US Corporate Accounting on accounting and reporting matters\n\n - Partner with the international payroll team on the preparation of payroll journals and reconciliations\n\n - Support the tax team on all international tax filings, payments and initiatives\n\n - Support the company’s global expansion initiatives including new entity set up and operationalization\n\n - Partner with cross functional teams on strategic projects\n\n - Identify and implement process improvements to strengthen controls and increase efficiency as the international business scales\n\n - Evaluate, recommend, and implement AI solutions to drive measurable process improvements across the team\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified Accountant (ACA, ACCA, CPA, CIMA, or equivalent)\n\n - Big 4 audit training is preferable\n\n - 5+ years post qualification experience in high growth multinational environment\n\n - Demonstrated technical expertise and practical application of IFRS, FRS102, and US GAAP\n\n - Proficiency with ERP systems (NetSuite or similar cloud-based platforms preferred) as well as Excel/Google Sheets, and close management tools\n\n - A proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment and is comfortable adapting to changing business requirements\n\n - Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage competing priorities in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills with a collaborative, team-oriented mindset\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b774c88e-5d8f-48d3-aed7-948f2e4292b7","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Backend - NYC","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-22T14:28:00.198+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b774c88e-5d8f-48d3-aed7-948f2e4292b7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b774c88e-5d8f-48d3-aed7-948f2e4292b7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in New York City. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\nThis role is based in New York City. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$238K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e56cd6b6-f3af-438d-8dc4-3add10f09f48","tierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"333fb939-7a9e-459c-a69b-a9e43d46d942","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ae396601-d8bd-4565-8979-884275e989f0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c2a8cf82-8643-4c4d-b582-a345b53f0785","summary":"$238K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"fcfdeffe-5890-49b0-a98f-8689a930c151","title":"SMB Account Executive","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T19:43:30.470+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fcfdeffe-5890-49b0-a98f-8689a930c151","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fcfdeffe-5890-49b0-a98f-8689a930c151/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of Harvey’s founding SMB Account Executives, you'll play a pivotal role in driving growth within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing new business relationships with small law firms and in-house legal teams, deeply understanding their challenges, and delivering AI solutions that transform how they work. By combining a high-velocity sales motion with a consultative, solution-driven approach, you’ll set the foundation for how we win in SMB and create long term impact for our clients. We’re looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced, early-stage environments, is energized by building from scratch, and is passionate about bringing Harvey’s mission to life.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by prioritizing warm leads and a named account list to maintain a high velocity sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the new business lifecycle from prospecting to qualifying, validating Harvey’s solution, and contracting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet SMB customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively develop tactics, collateral, and messaging to improve the SMB team’s performance, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology at high velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a multi-threaded sale with executive stakeholders – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 OTE 50/50 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs one of Harvey’s founding SMB Account Executives, you'll play a pivotal role in driving growth within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing new business relationships with small law firms and in-house legal teams, deeply understanding their challenges, and delivering AI solutions that transform how they work. By combining a high-velocity sales motion with a consultative, solution-driven approach, you’ll set the foundation for how we win in SMB and create long term impact for our clients. We’re looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced, early-stage environments, is energized by building from scratch, and is passionate about bringing Harvey’s mission to life.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by prioritizing warm leads and a named account list to maintain a high velocity sales motion.\n\n - Manage the new business lifecycle from prospecting to qualifying, validating Harvey’s solution, and contracting.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet SMB customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Proactively develop tactics, collateral, and messaging to improve the SMB team’s performance, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology at high velocity.\n\n - Capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene\n\n - Ability to lead a multi-threaded sale with executive stakeholders – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000 OTE 50/50 Split \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"aab1d631-6c29-48b6-ae9f-d6f5d14a2b7d","tierSummary":"OTE 50/50 Split $180K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"627b7c9c-d47a-4609-a759-1ab4e3086db6","summary":"OTE 50/50 Split $180K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":180000},{"id":"bf527366-a796-4edd-8d00-b300acca47d1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":180000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8d092528-2554-42e4-a68b-67307b48e6aa","title":"Staff Product Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-10-08T01:47:23.109+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8d092528-2554-42e4-a68b-67307b48e6aa","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8d092528-2554-42e4-a68b-67307b48e6aa/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate – not incrementally, but end-to end. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come. As we scale, our Enterprise Product organization sits at the center of this mission — connecting the systems our customers use, and scaling into new customer segments &amp; verticals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Product Manager with a strong technical foundation and the ability to own and solve complex product and commercial challenges end-to-end. This person will focus on building out integrations with strategic partners and vendors as well as enable search over data source using MCP’s and deep research. You will help architect systems to bring legal context into Harvey and also work with our Partnerships org and internal teams to prioritize which ones to build. This role is equal parts product intuition and technical execution. You’ll be trusted to make fast, high-quality decisions, ship impactful features, work on the cutting edge of applied AI and grow a team that embodies engineering excellence</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We move with urgency, bias toward simplicity, and expect our leaders to be hands-on when needed. If you’re energized by ownership, decisive execution, and solving real user problems, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model (3 days a week) and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the end-to-end product lifecycle, from ideation and strategy to execution and launch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with engineering and partnerships team to identify and execute on high-impact integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with engineers to build, platformize and scale integrations, working cross functionally with adjacent teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expand the breadth and depth of integrations into the Harvey platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Engineering, Applied AI, Research, and Platform teams to deliver high-quality production systems that support reasoning, summarization, and legal research workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building enterprise products in a B2B/commercial environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on Integrations and partnering with cross functional and Partnerships teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to partner with engineers on technical architecture, with enough depth to challenge assumptions, propose solutions, and influence design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to navigate extreme ambiguity to deliver outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A product mindset for balancing user needs, domain complexity, and system constraints to propose high-leverage improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$215,000 - $300,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate – not incrementally, but end-to end. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come. As we scale, our Enterprise Product organization sits at the center of this mission — connecting the systems our customers use, and scaling into new customer segments & verticals.\n\n\n\nWe’re looking for a Product Manager with a strong technical foundation and the ability to own and solve complex product and commercial challenges end-to-end. This person will focus on building out integrations with strategic partners and vendors as well as enable search over data source using MCP’s and deep research. You will help architect systems to bring legal context into Harvey and also work with our Partnerships org and internal teams to prioritize which ones to build. This role is equal parts product intuition and technical execution. You’ll be trusted to make fast, high-quality decisions, ship impactful features, work on the cutting edge of applied AI and grow a team that embodies engineering excellence\n\n\n\nWe move with urgency, bias toward simplicity, and expect our leaders to be hands-on when needed. If you’re energized by ownership, decisive execution, and solving real user problems, we'd love to hear from you.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model (3 days a week) and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead the end-to-end product lifecycle, from ideation and strategy to execution and launch\n\n - Collaborate closely with engineering and partnerships team to identify and execute on high-impact integrations\n\n - Work closely with engineers to build, platformize and scale integrations, working cross functionally with adjacent teams\n\n - Expand the breadth and depth of integrations into the Harvey platform\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Engineering, Applied AI, Research, and Platform teams to deliver high-quality production systems that support reasoning, summarization, and legal research workflows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience building enterprise products in a B2B/commercial environment\n\n - Experience working on Integrations and partnering with cross functional and Partnerships teams\n\n - Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs\n\n - Ability to partner with engineers on technical architecture, with enough depth to challenge assumptions, propose solutions, and influence design.\n\n - Ability to navigate extreme ambiguity to deliver outcomes\n\n - A product mindset for balancing user needs, domain complexity, and system constraints to propose high-leverage improvements.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$215,000 - $300,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$215K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$215K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a2348e83-15b4-4599-acdf-ceaf0d3311ef","tierSummary":"$215K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7b19431b-7072-485b-b59d-918e2171a5a4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f32ddc33-af53-4956-bb77-1bf21536b03a","summary":"$215K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":215000,"maxValue":300000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":215000,"maxValue":300000}]}},{"id":"01da8934-d3e3-4ebb-beb9-681b3c24fb9c","title":"Staff Software Engineer, AI Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-24T21:54:34.510+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/01da8934-d3e3-4ebb-beb9-681b3c24fb9c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/01da8934-d3e3-4ebb-beb9-681b3c24fb9c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Context Engineering &amp; Agent Infrastructure.</strong> Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Model Integration &amp; Routing.</strong> Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluation Infrastructure.</strong> Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Abstractions.</strong> Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering and a track record of technical leadership across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$</strong>231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.\n\nThe AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Context Engineering & Agent Infrastructure. Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.\n\n - Model Integration & Routing. Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.\n\n - Evaluation Infrastructure. Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.\n\n - Shared Abstractions. Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.\n\n - Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.\n\n - Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.\n\n - Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.\n\n - Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering and a track record of technical leadership across teams.\n\n - Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.\n\n - Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.\n\n - A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.\n\n - Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.\n\n - Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.\n\n - A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.\n\n - Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2bf19524-2abe-499e-ab29-e46711198b88","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"02332953-8b36-4e46-89d8-f7c5386526fe","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"5c55dd10-fb5d-4d20-8841-4b1261759dad","title":"SMB Account Executive ","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T18:41:03.303+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5c55dd10-fb5d-4d20-8841-4b1261759dad","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5c55dd10-fb5d-4d20-8841-4b1261759dad/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of Harvey’s founding SMB Account Executives, you'll play a pivotal role in driving growth within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing new business relationships with small law firms and in-house legal teams, deeply understanding their challenges, and delivering AI solutions that transform how they work. By combining a high-velocity sales motion with a consultative, solution-driven approach, you’ll set the foundation for how we win in SMB and create long term impact for our clients. We’re looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced, early-stage environments, is energized by building from scratch, and is passionate about bringing Harvey’s mission to life.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by prioritizing warm leads and a named account list to maintain a high velocity sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the new business lifecycle from prospecting to qualifying, validating Harvey’s solution, and contracting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet SMB customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively develop tactics, collateral, and messaging to improve the SMB team’s performance, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology at high velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a multi-threaded sale with executive stakeholders – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 OTE 50/50 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs one of Harvey’s founding SMB Account Executives, you'll play a pivotal role in driving growth within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing new business relationships with small law firms and in-house legal teams, deeply understanding their challenges, and delivering AI solutions that transform how they work. By combining a high-velocity sales motion with a consultative, solution-driven approach, you’ll set the foundation for how we win in SMB and create long term impact for our clients. We’re looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced, early-stage environments, is energized by building from scratch, and is passionate about bringing Harvey’s mission to life.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by prioritizing warm leads and a named account list to maintain a high velocity sales motion.\n\n - Manage the new business lifecycle from prospecting to qualifying, validating Harvey’s solution, and contracting.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet SMB customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Proactively develop tactics, collateral, and messaging to improve the SMB team’s performance, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology at high velocity.\n\n - Capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene\n\n - Ability to lead a multi-threaded sale with executive stakeholders – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000 OTE 50/50 Split \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 50/50 Split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e667dd26-87c2-4287-85a9-168487b96538","tierSummary":"$180K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 50/50 Split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 50/50 Split","components":[{"id":"8a8d3c92-1ca4-432d-94cb-9440ddbc43b2","summary":"$180K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":180000},{"id":"71a0142d-73b0-4343-a07b-706b65bdcfec","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"02b9de49-ae2a-4203-b1a9-ce878695e832","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":180000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5c30c057-437e-41a7-9b38-bbb6101a3b2b","title":"Legal Engineer, Product Specialist","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T16:09:30.474+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5c30c057-437e-41a7-9b38-bbb6101a3b2b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5c30c057-437e-41a7-9b38-bbb6101a3b2b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Formerly known as Legal Product Specialist</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineer, Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows—driving adoption, increasing utilization, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies—serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineer, Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In our Toronto office, you will be the face of Harvey in Canada—building trust with partners at leading law firms, corporates, and financial institutions across the country; advising them on how Harvey can transform research, drafting, diligence, and compliance; and feeding market insights back to Product and GTM more broadly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey’s AI into their daily practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey’s platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through a lawyer’s lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor usage trends and identify at-risk accounts or untapped opportunities, working cross-functionally to re-engage users and showcase new or underutilized capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to customer-facing content geared toward the Canadian region (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the credibility and brand of Harvey in the Canadian region as the leading AI platform for lawyers by delivering high-quality, domain-specific guidance that meets the expectations of top-tier legal professionals.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in Toronto and eligible to work in Toronto</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Toronto practising certificate (or equivalent common-law qualification) with 3+ years experience as a qualified lawyer practicing in-house, advising a sophisticated corporate legal team and/or at a top-tier firm (e.g., Band 1 Chambers / AFR Top 10).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nFormerly known as Legal Product Specialist\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineer, Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows—driving adoption, increasing utilization, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies—serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.\n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.\n\nIn our Toronto office, you will be the face of Harvey in Canada—building trust with partners at leading law firms, corporates, and financial institutions across the country; advising them on how Harvey can transform research, drafting, diligence, and compliance; and feeding market insights back to Product and GTM more broadly.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey’s AI into their daily practice.\n\n - Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey’s platform.\n\n - Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.\n\n - Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.\n\n - Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through a lawyer’s lens.\n\n - Monitor usage trends and identify at-risk accounts or untapped opportunities, working cross-functionally to re-engage users and showcase new or underutilized capabilities.\n\n - Contribute to customer-facing content geared toward the Canadian region (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.\n\n - Support the credibility and brand of Harvey in the Canadian region as the leading AI platform for lawyers by delivering high-quality, domain-specific guidance that meets the expectations of top-tier legal professionals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Based in Toronto and eligible to work in Toronto\n\n - Toronto practising certificate (or equivalent common-law qualification) with 3+ years experience as a qualified lawyer practicing in-house, advising a sophisticated corporate legal team and/or at a top-tier firm (e.g., Band 1 Chambers / AFR Top 10).\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"10900071-f75f-49da-bff7-7e9db5e9b1f9","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Full Stack - NYC","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-09T21:50:18.541+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/10900071-f75f-49da-bff7-7e9db5e9b1f9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/10900071-f75f-49da-bff7-7e9db5e9b1f9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1000-step planning agents that help take companies public</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products. \n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents\n\n - Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI\n\n - Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions\n\n - 1000-step planning agents that help take companies public\n\n - Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters\n\n - Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks\n\n - Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000 - $260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"482656d7-9fdc-4ec9-8416-3615f75a5a8f","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5219f576-fc1c-4d7b-9126-ba5b3f7019b2","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"94a7b55a-f2df-4151-8886-fdca853b8351","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5c744af2-e496-422f-bbdf-0a97e63ee404","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"0a8ca756-7d41-46cc-8cde-960af47658b2","title":"Associate Commercial Counsel, London","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T09:01:37.566+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0a8ca756-7d41-46cc-8cde-960af47658b2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0a8ca756-7d41-46cc-8cde-960af47658b2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Commercial Counsel to join our legal team. Reporting to the Head of EMEA Legal in London, you will interface with our Go-To-Market team to help ensure the fast and efficient execution of our agreements with customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional service organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More specifically, you will</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate Commercial AI SaaS contracts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Under the leadership of the Head of EMEA Legal, help to continue to establish the legal function in the EMEA, laying down a strong substantive, organizational and relationship foundation for the legal presence in the region</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work on other legal issues as they arise</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">English qualified lawyer with 2+ years post qualification experience, either with the commercial or technology division of a leading private practice law firm and/or in-house with a technology company supporting SaaS or technology Go-To-Market or Business Development teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with technology, and/or IP licensing commercial agreements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI experience welcomed but not required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Commercial Counsel to join our legal team. Reporting to the Head of EMEA Legal in London, you will interface with our Go-To-Market team to help ensure the fast and efficient execution of our agreements with customers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional service organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate Commercial AI SaaS contracts\n\n - Under the leadership of the Head of EMEA Legal, help to continue to establish the legal function in the EMEA, laying down a strong substantive, organizational and relationship foundation for the legal presence in the region\n\n - Work on other legal issues as they arise\n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\nWe use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - English qualified lawyer with 2+ years post qualification experience, either with the commercial or technology division of a leading private practice law firm and/or in-house with a technology company supporting SaaS or technology Go-To-Market or Business Development teams\n\n - Transactional background, including with technology, and/or IP licensing commercial agreements\n\n - AI experience welcomed but not required\n\n -  Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2cbe13b9-a44b-47d3-abb8-45d9a98b05f6","title":"Staff Product Manager, New Verticals","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-27T18:08:05.085+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2cbe13b9-a44b-47d3-abb8-45d9a98b05f6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2cbe13b9-a44b-47d3-abb8-45d9a98b05f6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an Product Manager, New Verticals to define, build, and scale AI agent–powered solutions for Harvey’s most strategic customers – enabling successful deployments and uncovering new solutions to unlock new opportunities for Harvey. This role sits at the intersection of deep customer discovery, sales, complex workflow mapping, AI/LLM capabilities, and hands-on delivery.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with key accounts to understand their highest-value use cases end to end, translate those into agent-powered solutions (out-of-the-box or net-new), and partner with engineering, research, and leadership to bring them to life. You’ll be responsible to drive repeatability—turning bespoke deployments into scalable products, pricing models, and commercial frameworks for entire verticals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner directly with strategic accounts</strong> to uncover high-impact workflows and translate ambiguous requirements into clear, actionable product definitions for agent-powered solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead discovery</strong> for your assigned accounts and verticals, developing a deep understanding of user intentions, data constraints, workflows, and success criteria.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Map workflows to the broader product</strong>, identifying where out-of-the-box agent capabilities fit and where custom development is needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive deployments</strong> end to end—working with forward deployed engineering and customer teams to implement, test, and refine agent solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and track success metrics</strong> for the verticals you support, ensuring solutions deliver measurable productivity and quality outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop account-level and vertical-level roadmaps</strong>, translating customer needs into scalable products or reusable frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate cross-functionally</strong> with founders, executives, engineering, and legal research to align product direction and ensure technical feasibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Influence new commercial models</strong>, including pricing, packaging, and deployment strategies for agent-led solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Champion repeatability</strong>, helping transform one-off solutions into product features, components, or templates that scale across the customer base.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of work experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in <strong>professional services</strong> (legal, consulting, banking, or adjacent fields) with experience operating in complex, high-stakes workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years of product management experience</strong> or closely related roles (e.g., solutions, forward deployed engineering, product consulting).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in <strong>B2B or enterprise environments</strong>, ideally with AI, automation, or workflow tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to ship and iterate on enterprise-grade software or high-complexity solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and a customer obsession mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong strategic thinking paired with detail orientation—able to zoom out to vertical-level needs while handling precise workflow nuances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate both qualitatively and quantitatively; strong command of structuring ambiguous problem spaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort navigating <strong>extreme ambiguity</strong>, defining structure from zero, and driving clarity for cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A <strong>scrappy, ownership mentality</strong>—willing to jump on flights, run QA, troubleshoot with engineering, or support customer teams when needed.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or deploying AI agents, workflow automation tools, or retrieval-augmented systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience as a forward deployed engineer, solutions architect, or consultant with strong product instincts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior role in a hyper-growth startup or high-performing enterprise product org.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$215,000 - $300,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an Product Manager, New Verticals to define, build, and scale AI agent–powered solutions for Harvey’s most strategic customers – enabling successful deployments and uncovering new solutions to unlock new opportunities for Harvey. This role sits at the intersection of deep customer discovery, sales, complex workflow mapping, AI/LLM capabilities, and hands-on delivery.\n\nYou will work closely with key accounts to understand their highest-value use cases end to end, translate those into agent-powered solutions (out-of-the-box or net-new), and partner with engineering, research, and leadership to bring them to life. You’ll be responsible to drive repeatability—turning bespoke deployments into scalable products, pricing models, and commercial frameworks for entire verticals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner directly with strategic accounts to uncover high-impact workflows and translate ambiguous requirements into clear, actionable product definitions for agent-powered solutions.\n\n - Lead discovery for your assigned accounts and verticals, developing a deep understanding of user intentions, data constraints, workflows, and success criteria.\n\n - Map workflows to the broader product, identifying where out-of-the-box agent capabilities fit and where custom development is needed.\n\n - Drive deployments end to end—working with forward deployed engineering and customer teams to implement, test, and refine agent solutions.\n\n - Define and track success metrics for the verticals you support, ensuring solutions deliver measurable productivity and quality outcomes.\n\n - Develop account-level and vertical-level roadmaps, translating customer needs into scalable products or reusable frameworks.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with founders, executives, engineering, and legal research to align product direction and ensure technical feasibility.\n\n - Influence new commercial models, including pricing, packaging, and deployment strategies for agent-led solutions.\n\n - Champion repeatability, helping transform one-off solutions into product features, components, or templates that scale across the customer base.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of work experience\n\n - Background in professional services (legal, consulting, banking, or adjacent fields) with experience operating in complex, high-stakes workflows.\n\n - 3+ years of product management experience or closely related roles (e.g., solutions, forward deployed engineering, product consulting).\n\n - Experience working in B2B or enterprise environments, ideally with AI, automation, or workflow tooling.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to ship and iterate on enterprise-grade software or high-complexity solutions.\n\n - Executive presence and a customer obsession mindset\n\n - Strong strategic thinking paired with detail orientation—able to zoom out to vertical-level needs while handling precise workflow nuances.\n\n - Ability to communicate both qualitatively and quantitatively; strong command of structuring ambiguous problem spaces.\n\n - Comfort navigating extreme ambiguity, defining structure from zero, and driving clarity for cross-functional teams.\n\n - A scrappy, ownership mentality—willing to jump on flights, run QA, troubleshoot with engineering, or support customer teams when needed.\n\n\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience building or deploying AI agents, workflow automation tools, or retrieval-augmented systems.\n\n - Experience as a forward deployed engineer, solutions architect, or consultant with strong product instincts.\n\n - Prior role in a hyper-growth startup or high-performing enterprise product org.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$215,000 - $300,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-CL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$215K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$215K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"97ebdddf-eb0f-46a5-8362-6ed7322bbb0e","tierSummary":"$215K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"37975122-db43-4f9c-952e-c3ea8431a3bd","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e8f3c61c-dd87-4738-8330-9825004ff2bc","summary":"$215K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":215000,"maxValue":300000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":215000,"maxValue":300000}]}},{"id":"463bac67-20c1-49c5-8835-a64ca0e94c73","title":"Legal Innovation Partner","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-23T23:23:39.406+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/463bac67-20c1-49c5-8835-a64ca0e94c73","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/463bac67-20c1-49c5-8835-a64ca0e94c73/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is trusted by the leading law firms and in-house teams to help them harness AI. We work closely with Innovation and Knowledge teams to plan and execute AI transformation efforts.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our Legal Innovation Partners provide strategic counsel to Innovation leaders as they define and execute AI transformation within their organizations. They represent Harvey within this Legal Innovation community and foster the strategic and product insights that help Harvey serve this community better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise innovation and knowledge teams on AI transformation. You’ll leverage your lived experience as an innovation leader to help our customers design and execute their AI strategies, including client AI policies, rollout programs, and measures of success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support innovation leaders in advancing the frontier of firm and client collaboration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to firm efforts to innovate on the business of law.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advance Legal AI thought leadership, including representing the community in industry forums and publishing analyses that advance the frontier of legal innovation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a thriving innovation and knowledge community, including creating opportunities for dialogue and collaboration across law firms, professional organizations, and corporate teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years in a legal innovation role</strong> at a top tier law firm, corporate legal team, or legal tech organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong point of view</strong> on the direction of AI transformation in law firms and a demonstrated interest in steering it for the benefit of lawyers, clients, and firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive presence</strong> with CIOs/CKOs/CISOs and the ability to translate between technical and legal/business audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Track record of shaping product direction</strong> or service design based on deep domain insight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication skills</strong>—written thought pieces, conference speaking, and one-to-one executive advising.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$270,000 - $320,000 USD OTE (70/30 split)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is trusted by the leading law firms and in-house teams to help them harness AI. We work closely with Innovation and Knowledge teams to plan and execute AI transformation efforts.\n\nOur Legal Innovation Partners provide strategic counsel to Innovation leaders as they define and execute AI transformation within their organizations. They represent Harvey within this Legal Innovation community and foster the strategic and product insights that help Harvey serve this community better.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Advise innovation and knowledge teams on AI transformation. You’ll leverage your lived experience as an innovation leader to help our customers design and execute their AI strategies, including client AI policies, rollout programs, and measures of success.\n\n - Support innovation leaders in advancing the frontier of firm and client collaboration.\n\n - Contribute to firm efforts to innovate on the business of law.\n\n - Advance Legal AI thought leadership, including representing the community in industry forums and publishing analyses that advance the frontier of legal innovation.\n\n - Foster a thriving innovation and knowledge community, including creating opportunities for dialogue and collaboration across law firms, professional organizations, and corporate teams.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in a legal innovation role at a top tier law firm, corporate legal team, or legal tech organization.\n\n - Strong point of view on the direction of AI transformation in law firms and a demonstrated interest in steering it for the benefit of lawyers, clients, and firms.\n\n - Executive presence with CIOs/CKOs/CISOs and the ability to translate between technical and legal/business audiences.\n\n - Track record of shaping product direction or service design based on deep domain insight.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills—written thought pieces, conference speaking, and one-to-one executive advising.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$270,000 - $320,000 USD OTE (70/30 split)\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$270K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE (70/30 split)","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$270K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d60337c7-f495-409f-b39d-5069c72d0a2f","tierSummary":"$270K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE (70/30 split)","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE (70/30 split)","components":[{"id":"841e4e6f-99f8-432f-94ef-aa910c47dac4","summary":"$270K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":270000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"d4fe6b7b-ff5a-4092-89f2-53ed8fab2d83","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"46dfd033-65d4-4495-8eb7-8e20016a6af4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":270000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e5272fbe-4431-4841-bf00-b9f59812b82a","title":"Innovation Product Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-11T16:20:46.621+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e5272fbe-4431-4841-bf00-b9f59812b82a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e5272fbe-4431-4841-bf00-b9f59812b82a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role blends elements of product management, innovation strategy, solutions design, and forward-deployed partnership. You’ll work directly with leading law firms and corporate legal teams to translate messy, high-value legal work into AI-powered workflows — and ensure they succeed in production.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We don’t build software <em>for</em> lawyers; we build it <em>with</em> them. Our teams sit shoulder-to-shoulder with partners, associates, innovation groups, and CIOs to understand problems at depth, design first-of-kind workflows, and ship products that reshape how legal work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a thought partner to top global law firms and enterprises — diagnosing pain points, mapping high-value opportunities, and guiding how Harvey integrates into their practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with the go-to-market team to shape pilots and deployments end-to-end: discovery, workflow design, testing, onboarding, iteration, and firm-wide rollout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with innovation leaders, legal operations, and practice groups alongside Customer Success — ensuring the platform becomes embedded in day-to-day legal work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate user insights into product direction to influence roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help clients evaluate the business impact of AI — from improving associate leverage to transforming workflows across practices like M&amp;A, litigation, regulatory, and transactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape how the legal industry adapts to AI. You’ll be in the room where the new operating model of law is being defined.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You come from the legal world, but you’ve always gravitated toward innovation, experimentation, and systems thinking. You’ve seen how complex legal work happens in practice — and you’re excited to redesign it with cutting-edge AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll thrive here if you</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have experience at a top law firm or in-house legal team; innovation, legal ops, or consulting experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the legal tech ecosystem as an employee, founder, or advisor to legal tech startups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are product-savvy and tech-curious. You’re not expected to code, but you can navigate conversations about generative AI, workflow design, privacy, governance, and enterprise rollout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with clarity and confidence across roles — partners, associates, engineers, PMs, CIOs, and legal ops.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Can independently run multiple client engagements in parallel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care deeply about quality and user outcomes while keeping a strong bias for action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are energized by building something new in a domain going through its biggest shift in decades.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$178,500 - $241,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis role blends elements of product management, innovation strategy, solutions design, and forward-deployed partnership. You’ll work directly with leading law firms and corporate legal teams to translate messy, high-value legal work into AI-powered workflows — and ensure they succeed in production.\n\nWe don’t build software for lawyers; we build it with them. Our teams sit shoulder-to-shoulder with partners, associates, innovation groups, and CIOs to understand problems at depth, design first-of-kind workflows, and ship products that reshape how legal work gets done.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Serve as a thought partner to top global law firms and enterprises — diagnosing pain points, mapping high-value opportunities, and guiding how Harvey integrates into their practice.\n\n - Work with the go-to-market team to shape pilots and deployments end-to-end: discovery, workflow design, testing, onboarding, iteration, and firm-wide rollout.\n\n - Work with innovation leaders, legal operations, and practice groups alongside Customer Success — ensuring the platform becomes embedded in day-to-day legal work\n\n - Translate user insights into product direction to influence roadmap\n\n - Help clients evaluate the business impact of AI — from improving associate leverage to transforming workflows across practices like M&A, litigation, regulatory, and transactions.\n\n - Shape how the legal industry adapts to AI. You’ll be in the room where the new operating model of law is being defined.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nYou come from the legal world, but you’ve always gravitated toward innovation, experimentation, and systems thinking. You’ve seen how complex legal work happens in practice — and you’re excited to redesign it with cutting-edge AI.\n\nYou’ll thrive here if you:\n\n - Have experience at a top law firm or in-house legal team; innovation, legal ops, or consulting experience is a plus.\n\n - Familiarity with the legal tech ecosystem as an employee, founder, or advisor to legal tech startups\n\n - Are product-savvy and tech-curious. You’re not expected to code, but you can navigate conversations about generative AI, workflow design, privacy, governance, and enterprise rollout.\n\n - Communicate with clarity and confidence across roles — partners, associates, engineers, PMs, CIOs, and legal ops.\n\n - Can independently run multiple client engagements in parallel.\n\n - Care deeply about quality and user outcomes while keeping a strong bias for action.\n\n - Are energized by building something new in a domain going through its biggest shift in decades.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$178,500 - $241,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-CL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$178.5K – $241.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$178.5K - $241.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"adceaf83-d8cc-46de-84d0-9f5f27a598d0","tierSummary":"$178.5K – $241.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e6e66300-e1e3-468c-bf27-e5f29f5637b1","summary":"$178.5K – $241.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":178500,"maxValue":241500},{"id":"5f3438c7-4dc5-4cbb-bebf-9e4e04d828f4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"bed24263-1f7c-4662-9543-f0ab1ea785b4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":178500,"maxValue":241500},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7c71db12-6edb-441e-b76c-847ef6d00527","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2025-12-18T16:23:51.990+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7c71db12-6edb-441e-b76c-847ef6d00527","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7c71db12-6edb-441e-b76c-847ef6d00527/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Backend Platform Engineer</strong> at Harvey, you will help build and operate the <strong>cohesive backend platform</strong> that all our services run on. In this mid-to-senior level role, you’ll design and implement shared frameworks and libraries that abstract common concerns, improve developer experience, and raise the baseline for reliability and performance across all teams. Your mission aligns with our platform charter: create <em>“a shared foundation that enables product teams to ship reliable, observable, and performant experiences quickly and safely.”</em> By centralizing common work, you’ll let product engineers focus on shipping features rather than re-inventing the wheel. This is a high-impact role where the code you write and the systems you build will <strong>amplify the productivity and quality</strong> of engineering across the entire company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you’re excited about building foundational systems, solving cross-cutting technical challenges, and enabling others to move faster with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain Harvey’s internal backend frameworks and libraries that provide common capabilities (API routing, service lifecycle management, caching and messaging primitives, error handling interfaces, etc.), so product teams don’t have to reinvent them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and improve APIs, service templates, and versioned interfaces that establish consistent patterns for building new services and features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce and champion modern backend architecture patterns like asynchronous I/O (asyncio) and streaming data processing, continually evolving our platform for better performance and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design Harvey-specific abstractions and domain-specific frameworks—covering cross-cutting concerns (e.g., authorization, streaming) and areas like data governance and event processing—to provide product engineers with these capabilities out of the box.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed reliability and observability into the platform by building in tracing, metrics, and automated tests (shift-left), ensuring services built on our foundation are robust and easy to monitor</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Model Infrastructure team to tackle challenges unique to GenAI-native applications — such as supporting high-throughput model inference, managing streaming and long-running API interactions, and designing abstractions for retrieval, context handling, and prompt lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Developer Experience and Infrastructure teams (who own CI/CD pipelines, build tools, and release infrastructure) to integrate our platform components seamlessly into the deployment and monitoring ecosystem</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with product engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” approach a reality — providing strong defaults and clear documentation so teams can move fast with confidence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software engineering experience (post-BS/MS), including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals (APIs, data stores, concurrency, distributed systems)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with web frameworks and service architectures (e.g. Flask/FastAPI, Bounded context services, microservices) and an understanding of designing clean, versioned APIs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with caching, messaging, and database technologies (Redis, Kafka, SQL/NoSQL databases, Vector databases, etc.) and how to use them effectively for high performance and reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of writing high-quality, well-tested code and using tools (unit/integration testing, static typing, CI) to catch issues early and ensure reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to or maintaining internal libraries/frameworks is a plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$238,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Backend Platform Engineer at Harvey, you will help build and operate the cohesive backend platform that all our services run on. In this mid-to-senior level role, you’ll design and implement shared frameworks and libraries that abstract common concerns, improve developer experience, and raise the baseline for reliability and performance across all teams. Your mission aligns with our platform charter: create “a shared foundation that enables product teams to ship reliable, observable, and performant experiences quickly and safely.” By centralizing common work, you’ll let product engineers focus on shipping features rather than re-inventing the wheel. This is a high-impact role where the code you write and the systems you build will amplify the productivity and quality of engineering across the entire company.\n\n\n\nIf you’re excited about building foundational systems, solving cross-cutting technical challenges, and enabling others to move faster with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n - Develop and maintain Harvey’s internal backend frameworks and libraries that provide common capabilities (API routing, service lifecycle management, caching and messaging primitives, error handling interfaces, etc.), so product teams don’t have to reinvent them\n\n - Create and improve APIs, service templates, and versioned interfaces that establish consistent patterns for building new services and features\n\n - Introduce and champion modern backend architecture patterns like asynchronous I/O (asyncio) and streaming data processing, continually evolving our platform for better performance and scalability\n\n - Design Harvey-specific abstractions and domain-specific frameworks—covering cross-cutting concerns (e.g., authorization, streaming) and areas like data governance and event processing—to provide product engineers with these capabilities out of the box.\n\n - Embed reliability and observability into the platform by building in tracing, metrics, and automated tests (shift-left), ensuring services built on our foundation are robust and easy to monitor\n\n - Collaborate with Model Infrastructure team to tackle challenges unique to GenAI-native applications — such as supporting high-throughput model inference, managing streaming and long-running API interactions, and designing abstractions for retrieval, context handling, and prompt lifecycle\n\n - Collaborate with the Developer Experience and Infrastructure teams (who own CI/CD pipelines, build tools, and release infrastructure) to integrate our platform components seamlessly into the deployment and monitoring ecosystem\n\n - Work closely with product engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” approach a reality — providing strong defaults and clear documentation so teams can move fast with confidence\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software engineering experience (post-BS/MS), including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms\n\n - Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals (APIs, data stores, concurrency, distributed systems)\n\n - Hands-on experience with web frameworks and service architectures (e.g. Flask/FastAPI, Bounded context services, microservices) and an understanding of designing clean, versioned APIs\n\n - Familiarity with caching, messaging, and database technologies (Redis, Kafka, SQL/NoSQL databases, Vector databases, etc.) and how to use them effectively for high performance and reliability\n\n - A track record of writing high-quality, well-tested code and using tools (unit/integration testing, static typing, CI) to catch issues early and ensure reliability\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.\n\n - Experience contributing to or maintaining internal libraries/frameworks is a plus.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$238,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$238K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"57f499ba-5455-4a7a-89c7-dfb84947de64","tierSummary":"$238K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"06c19a48-d224-443e-a27e-42d188aa2925","summary":"$238K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"86f0f96c-d04b-4d67-965d-a0523436a278","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"63ccbfb0-87d4-4f7b-9670-427989550004","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":238000,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d527a336-24e3-46ef-8d05-1da557c7bff4","title":"Staff Product Designer","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-22T20:07:43.460+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d527a336-24e3-46ef-8d05-1da557c7bff4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d527a336-24e3-46ef-8d05-1da557c7bff4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000-$260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.\n\nWe’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.\n\n - Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.\n\n - Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.\n\n - Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.\n\n - Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.\n\n - Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.\n\n - Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.\n\n - Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.\n\n - Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.\n\n - Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.\n\n - Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.\n\n - Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$200,000-$260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ff4094b6-5cc7-439c-b0e6-915adb759997","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b58d8180-2234-4d9c-9c93-d92f77b42e7f","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"6c72085d-2dda-4498-b549-deec2becd98a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2af25124-45a4-4c08-a0e8-f156059183e6","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9382f297-c572-4744-a0fd-989861e1bc27","title":"Legal Engineer (Energy or Tax)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Paris","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T14:23:14.377+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"France"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9382f297-c572-4744-a0fd-989861e1bc27","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9382f297-c572-4744-a0fd-989861e1bc27/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to how Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with English- and French-speaking lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand their workflow challenges, strategic objectives, and broader firm context — then demonstrate how Harvey’s AI solutions can address them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in French and English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent), with a corporate, transactional.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Paris</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid French work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our France team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.\n\nSimilar to how Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Engage with English- and French-speaking lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand their workflow challenges, strategic objectives, and broader firm context — then demonstrate how Harvey’s AI solutions can address them.\n\n - Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types.\n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs.\n\n - Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs.\n\n - Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - Fluent in French and English.\n\n - At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent), with a corporate, transactional.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Location: Paris\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid French work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our France team\n\n - Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ec9e2cd5-af31-4f9c-8b12-d2088a83753a","title":"Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (in-house)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T13:19:47.576+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ec9e2cd5-af31-4f9c-8b12-d2088a83753a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ec9e2cd5-af31-4f9c-8b12-d2088a83753a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Formerly known as Legal Product Specialist</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows—driving adoption, increasing utilization, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies—serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineer - Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey’s AI into their daily practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey’s platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through a lawyer’s lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor usage trends and identify at-risk accounts or untapped opportunities, working cross-functionally to re-engage users and showcase new or underutilized capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to customer-facing content (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the credibility and brand of Harvey as the leading AI platform for lawyers by delivering high-quality, domain-specific guidance that meets the expectations of top-tier legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must be qualified in England &amp; Wales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm, preferably with a in-house or transactional focus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nFormerly known as Legal Product Specialist\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows—driving adoption, increasing utilization, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies—serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.\n\nLegal Engineer - Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey’s AI into their daily practice.\n\n - Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey’s platform.\n\n - Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.\n\n - Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.\n\n - Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through a lawyer’s lens.\n\n - Monitor usage trends and identify at-risk accounts or untapped opportunities, working cross-functionally to re-engage users and showcase new or underutilized capabilities.\n\n - Contribute to customer-facing content (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.\n\n - Support the credibility and brand of Harvey as the leading AI platform for lawyers by delivering high-quality, domain-specific guidance that meets the expectations of top-tier legal professionals.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Must be qualified in England & Wales\n\n - At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm, preferably with a in-house or transactional focus.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d911b15e-29e4-453e-b192-4201c7937e1f","title":"Enterprise Customer Success Manager -EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-14T00:27:03.603+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d911b15e-29e4-453e-b192-4201c7937e1f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d911b15e-29e4-453e-b192-4201c7937e1f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong>: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships</strong>: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics</strong>: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion and Renewal</strong>: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing customer-facing projects and timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Running in-person meetings w/ executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Driving key customer metrics and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Success Metrics: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.\n\n - Expansion and Renewal: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:\n\n - 3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth\n\n - Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization\n\n - Managing customer-facing projects and timelines\n\n - Running in-person meetings w/ executives\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders\n\n - Driving key customer metrics and outcomes\n\n - Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d03dcaae-05de-4344-aebc-803993827922","title":"Data Scientist, Marketing","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-16T17:20:33.355+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d03dcaae-05de-4344-aebc-803993827922","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d03dcaae-05de-4344-aebc-803993827922/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring a Marketing Data Scientist to partner closely with Harvey’s Marketing organization and build our marketing data science function from the ground up. In this role, you’ll serve as a trusted analytical partner to Marketing, GTM, and Finance - defining how we measure marketing success, understanding what drives channel and campaign performance, and informing where and how we invest to accelerate growth. As one of the earliest Marketing data science hires, you’ll own the development of core Marketing metrics, scalable dashboards, and analytical frameworks that enable data-driven decision-making across the business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed deeply with the Marketing organization as a trusted partner, identifying opportunities to improve performance and drive growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define, track, and evolve core metrics across marketing and business functions, building scalable dashboards and reporting frameworks that enable data-driven decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and evaluate models (multi-touch attribution, marketing mix modeling, incrementality) for comprehensive Marketing Channel and Campaign performance and contribution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply statistical and machine learning techniques to model user behavior, forecast trends, and identify opportunities for growth and optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate complex analyses into compelling stories, delivering clear recommendations to cross-functional partners and executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Marketing, RevOps and GTM System, to co-develop data infrastructure, ensuring robust pipelines, reliable data sources, and scalable systems that power analytics and modeling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional analytics initiatives that synthesize competitive dynamics, customer feedback, and market trends into actionable opportunities for the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a data-informed culture by establishing best practices, mentoring peers, and shaping the strategic role of data science at Harvey.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in quantitative roles operating in highly ambiguous environments, ideally as an early data scientist or Marketing analyst within a hyper-growth product company or research organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in SQL, with extensive experience extracting large datasets and designing ETL workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise working with Salesforce, Marketo and Ads spent data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with modern data stack, such as DBT, Looker and Omni</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in quantitative programming languages, such as Python and R</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience defining, implementing, and operationalizing Marketing campaign- and channel-level metrics from the ground up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills, with the ability to effectively partner with leaders across Marketing, GTM and Finance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic mindset capable of generating insights that extend beyond traditional statistical significance testing to inform long-term product and business direction</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$170,000 - $260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re hiring a Marketing Data Scientist to partner closely with Harvey’s Marketing organization and build our marketing data science function from the ground up. In this role, you’ll serve as a trusted analytical partner to Marketing, GTM, and Finance - defining how we measure marketing success, understanding what drives channel and campaign performance, and informing where and how we invest to accelerate growth. As one of the earliest Marketing data science hires, you’ll own the development of core Marketing metrics, scalable dashboards, and analytical frameworks that enable data-driven decision-making across the business.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Embed deeply with the Marketing organization as a trusted partner, identifying opportunities to improve performance and drive growth.\n\n - Define, track, and evolve core metrics across marketing and business functions, building scalable dashboards and reporting frameworks that enable data-driven decision-making.\n\n - Design, implement, and evaluate models (multi-touch attribution, marketing mix modeling, incrementality) for comprehensive Marketing Channel and Campaign performance and contribution.\n\n - Apply statistical and machine learning techniques to model user behavior, forecast trends, and identify opportunities for growth and optimization.\n\n - Translate complex analyses into compelling stories, delivering clear recommendations to cross-functional partners and executives.\n\n - Partner with Marketing, RevOps and GTM System, to co-develop data infrastructure, ensuring robust pipelines, reliable data sources, and scalable systems that power analytics and modeling.\n\n - Lead cross-functional analytics initiatives that synthesize competitive dynamics, customer feedback, and market trends into actionable opportunities for the business.\n\n - Champion a data-informed culture by establishing best practices, mentoring peers, and shaping the strategic role of data science at Harvey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in quantitative roles operating in highly ambiguous environments, ideally as an early data scientist or Marketing analyst within a hyper-growth product company or research organization\n\n - Expertise in SQL, with extensive experience extracting large datasets and designing ETL workflows\n\n - Expertise working with Salesforce, Marketo and Ads spent data\n\n - Strong experience with modern data stack, such as DBT, Looker and Omni\n\n - Proficiency in quantitative programming languages, such as Python and R\n\n - Experience defining, implementing, and operationalizing Marketing campaign- and channel-level metrics from the ground up\n\n - Strong communication skills, with the ability to effectively partner with leaders across Marketing, GTM and Finance\n\n - Strategic mindset capable of generating insights that extend beyond traditional statistical significance testing to inform long-term product and business direction\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$170,000 - $260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$170K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$170K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7e661cbb-c0f6-4882-bc27-4a8562f962c2","tierSummary":"$170K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"be4a953a-7917-48cf-a793-c3993df2d613","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6ba1cba4-38cd-4bea-abbd-524e9683d7b1","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9116318f-3418-4f2a-9cd7-9b7984a27128","summary":"$170K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":170000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":170000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"daad560f-c851-4cb9-89ac-efb2186c4031","title":"Staff Software Engineer, OfficeJS","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-25T23:38:45.715+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/daad560f-c851-4cb9-89ac-efb2186c4031","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/daad560f-c851-4cb9-89ac-efb2186c4031/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal professionals spend most of their day in Microsoft Word: drafting, reviewing, and refining complex documents that shape meaningful outcomes. Harvey in Word brings AI-powered capabilities directly into Word, enabling lawyers to draft faster, run playbook reviews, and perform agentic editing, all without leaving their workflow. It's one of our most strategic product lines and a key part of how we meet lawyers where they already work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Embedded Experiences team, you will own and lead the development of Harvey in Word, our Microsoft Office Add-in built on OfficeJS, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations. You'll architect and ship features that integrate seamlessly with Word, handling the unique challenges of building performant, polished experiences within the Office Add-in environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone with deep expertise in OfficeJS and Office Add-in development, ideally from building a similar product at scale. You'll join a team of highly motivated, skilled engineers who hold everything they touch to the highest standards, from architecture to code to user experience. You may also contribute to our Outlook integration and help build the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and lead the technical direction of Harvey in Word, our flagship Office Add-in product, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the AI-native editing experience: agentic document rewrites, real-time redlining, and playbook automation that transforms how lawyers work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build sophisticated integrations with Microsoft Word using the OfficeJS API, including document manipulation, playbook reviews, and AI-assisted drafting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect scalable, maintainable solutions that handle the constraints and quirks of the Office Add-in environment across platforms (Windows, Mac, Web)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build polished, high-performance interfaces with crisp interactions and resilient error handling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product, design, and backend teams to shape APIs and UX for AI-powered features like streaming results and tool-calling workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate Office Add-in requirement sets, versioning, and cross-platform compatibility to ensure broad, reliable support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey in Outlook and shape the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers, drive technical decisions, and raise the bar on quality and developer experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software engineering experience, with significant depth in Office Add-in development using OfficeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping a production Office Add-in product, ideally one used at enterprise scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, and CSS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of Office Add-in architecture, requirement sets, manifest configuration, and cross-platform considerations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React or similar modern frontend frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products with strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Microsoft Office Add-in guidelines and AppSource submission process is a plus</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Outlook Add-ins or other Microsoft 365 integrations (SharePoint, Teams)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in legal tech or enterprise SaaS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products that integrate with AI/LLM capabilities</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PF1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nLegal professionals spend most of their day in Microsoft Word: drafting, reviewing, and refining complex documents that shape meaningful outcomes. Harvey in Word brings AI-powered capabilities directly into Word, enabling lawyers to draft faster, run playbook reviews, and perform agentic editing, all without leaving their workflow. It's one of our most strategic product lines and a key part of how we meet lawyers where they already work.\n\n\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Embedded Experiences team, you will own and lead the development of Harvey in Word, our Microsoft Office Add-in built on OfficeJS, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations. You'll architect and ship features that integrate seamlessly with Word, handling the unique challenges of building performant, polished experiences within the Office Add-in environment.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for someone with deep expertise in OfficeJS and Office Add-in development, ideally from building a similar product at scale. You'll join a team of highly motivated, skilled engineers who hold everything they touch to the highest standards, from architecture to code to user experience. You may also contribute to our Outlook integration and help build the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and lead the technical direction of Harvey in Word, our flagship Office Add-in product, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations.\n\n - Build the AI-native editing experience: agentic document rewrites, real-time redlining, and playbook automation that transforms how lawyers work\n\n - Design and build sophisticated integrations with Microsoft Word using the OfficeJS API, including document manipulation, playbook reviews, and AI-assisted drafting\n\n - Architect scalable, maintainable solutions that handle the constraints and quirks of the Office Add-in environment across platforms (Windows, Mac, Web)\n\n - Build polished, high-performance interfaces with crisp interactions and resilient error handling\n\n - Collaborate with product, design, and backend teams to shape APIs and UX for AI-powered features like streaming results and tool-calling workflows\n\n - Navigate Office Add-in requirement sets, versioning, and cross-platform compatibility to ensure broad, reliable support\n\n - Contribute to Harvey in Outlook and shape the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite\n\n - Mentor engineers, drive technical decisions, and raise the bar on quality and developer experience\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software engineering experience, with significant depth in Office Add-in development using OfficeJS\n\n - Experience building and shipping a production Office Add-in product, ideally one used at enterprise scale\n\n - Strong proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, and CSS\n\n - Deep understanding of Office Add-in architecture, requirement sets, manifest configuration, and cross-platform considerations\n\n - Experience with React or similar modern frontend frameworks\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products with strong attention to detail\n\n - Familiarity with Microsoft Office Add-in guidelines and AppSource submission process is a plus\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Outlook Add-ins or other Microsoft 365 integrations (SharePoint, Teams)\n\n - Background in legal tech or enterprise SaaS\n\n - Experience building products that integrate with AI/LLM capabilities\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-PF1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fefeadf3-0d08-4d3e-aa1e-63fa519143d2","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"857aa134-ee7b-46c9-a54e-42aacc2e5484","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"823a5ac2-b079-4ee8-bd73-c023e8ce1ace","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"24e0805c-3de8-4509-8b9c-054e5abe6280","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"8c07cb74-765a-46ea-a0f1-795f45597d79","title":"Staff Software Engineer, OfficeJS","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-25T23:39:43.797+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8c07cb74-765a-46ea-a0f1-795f45597d79","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8c07cb74-765a-46ea-a0f1-795f45597d79/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal professionals spend most of their day in Microsoft Word: drafting, reviewing, and refining complex documents that shape meaningful outcomes. Harvey in Word brings AI-powered capabilities directly into Word, enabling lawyers to draft faster, run playbook reviews, and perform agentic editing, all without leaving their workflow. It's one of our most strategic product lines and a key part of how we meet lawyers where they already work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Embedded Experiences team, you will own and lead the development of Harvey in Word, our Microsoft Office Add-in built on OfficeJS, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations. You'll architect and ship features that integrate seamlessly with Word, handling the unique challenges of building performant, polished experiences within the Office Add-in environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone with deep expertise in OfficeJS and Office Add-in development, ideally from building a similar product at scale. You'll join a team of highly motivated, skilled engineers who hold everything they touch to the highest standards, from architecture to code to user experience. You may also contribute to our Outlook integration and help build the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in New York, NY. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and lead the technical direction of Harvey in Word, our flagship Office Add-in product, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the AI-native editing experience: agentic document rewrites, real-time redlining, and playbook automation that transforms how lawyers work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build sophisticated integrations with Microsoft Word using the OfficeJS API, including document manipulation, playbook reviews, and AI-assisted drafting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect scalable, maintainable solutions that handle the constraints and quirks of the Office Add-in environment across platforms (Windows, Mac, Web)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build polished, high-performance interfaces with crisp interactions and resilient error handling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product, design, and backend teams to shape APIs and UX for AI-powered features like streaming results and tool-calling workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate Office Add-in requirement sets, versioning, and cross-platform compatibility to ensure broad, reliable support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey in Outlook and shape the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers, drive technical decisions, and raise the bar on quality and developer experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software engineering experience, with significant depth in Office Add-in development using OfficeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping a production Office Add-in product, ideally one used at enterprise scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, and CSS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of Office Add-in architecture, requirement sets, manifest configuration, and cross-platform considerations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React or similar modern frontend frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products with strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Microsoft Office Add-in guidelines and AppSource submission process is a plus</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Outlook Add-ins or other Microsoft 365 integrations (SharePoint, Teams)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in legal tech or enterprise SaaS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products that integrate with AI/LLM capabilities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PF1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nLegal professionals spend most of their day in Microsoft Word: drafting, reviewing, and refining complex documents that shape meaningful outcomes. Harvey in Word brings AI-powered capabilities directly into Word, enabling lawyers to draft faster, run playbook reviews, and perform agentic editing, all without leaving their workflow. It's one of our most strategic product lines and a key part of how we meet lawyers where they already work.\n\n\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Embedded Experiences team, you will own and lead the development of Harvey in Word, our Microsoft Office Add-in built on OfficeJS, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations. You'll architect and ship features that integrate seamlessly with Word, handling the unique challenges of building performant, polished experiences within the Office Add-in environment.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for someone with deep expertise in OfficeJS and Office Add-in development, ideally from building a similar product at scale. You'll join a team of highly motivated, skilled engineers who hold everything they touch to the highest standards, from architecture to code to user experience. You may also contribute to our Outlook integration and help build the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in New York, NY. We use a hybrid in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and lead the technical direction of Harvey in Word, our flagship Office Add-in product, alongside our other Microsoft Office integrations.\n\n - Build the AI-native editing experience: agentic document rewrites, real-time redlining, and playbook automation that transforms how lawyers work\n\n - Design and build sophisticated integrations with Microsoft Word using the OfficeJS API, including document manipulation, playbook reviews, and AI-assisted drafting\n\n - Architect scalable, maintainable solutions that handle the constraints and quirks of the Office Add-in environment across platforms (Windows, Mac, Web)\n\n - Build polished, high-performance interfaces with crisp interactions and resilient error handling\n\n - Collaborate with product, design, and backend teams to shape APIs and UX for AI-powered features like streaming results and tool-calling workflows\n\n - Navigate Office Add-in requirement sets, versioning, and cross-platform compatibility to ensure broad, reliable support\n\n - Contribute to Harvey in Outlook and shape the next generation of agentic AI interfaces across the Microsoft suite\n\n - Mentor engineers, drive technical decisions, and raise the bar on quality and developer experience\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software engineering experience, with significant depth in Office Add-in development using OfficeJS\n\n - Experience building and shipping a production Office Add-in product, ideally one used at enterprise scale\n\n - Strong proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, and CSS\n\n - Deep understanding of Office Add-in architecture, requirement sets, manifest configuration, and cross-platform considerations\n\n - Experience with React or similar modern frontend frameworks\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products with strong attention to detail\n\n - Familiarity with Microsoft Office Add-in guidelines and AppSource submission process is a plus\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Outlook Add-ins or other Microsoft 365 integrations (SharePoint, Teams)\n\n - Background in legal tech or enterprise SaaS\n\n - Experience building products that integrate with AI/LLM capabilities\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-PF1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6813528f-733d-476e-b264-302c8ebc489d","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"acf29f05-0e86-400b-958b-159c275f91c0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a41983a6-08f3-4aad-bcf5-ca30b9404ae3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d2c52ddf-f279-46e5-bec6-bf53bf9395ad","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"7af582ea-39f0-4e4c-ad4d-74f9740686bf","title":"Technical Account Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T17:16:46.977+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7af582ea-39f0-4e4c-ad4d-74f9740686bf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7af582ea-39f0-4e4c-ad4d-74f9740686bf/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its premium customer offerings, we are hiring a <strong>Technical Account Manager </strong>to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent inbound support and escalation resource for Harvey’s largest and most strategic customers in the Majors segment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Premium Support Specialist strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and resolve inbound support tickets from Majors accounts, serving as a primary escalation point for high-severity and technically complex issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">.Familiarity with ticketing queue systems and resolving inbound customer inquiries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to Have</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$119,000 -$161,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its premium customer offerings, we are hiring a Technical Account Manager to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent inbound support and escalation resource for Harvey’s largest and most strategic customers in the Majors segment.\n\nThe Premium Support Specialist strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and resolve inbound support tickets from Majors accounts, serving as a primary escalation point for high-severity and technically complex issues.\n\n - Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.\n\n - Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.\n\n - Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.\n\n - Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.\n\n - Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.\n\n - Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.\n\n - Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.\n\n - Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.\n\n - Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases.\n\n - .Familiarity with ticketing queue systems and resolving inbound customer inquiries\n\n - Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.\n\n - Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers.\n\n - Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.\n\n - Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.\n\n - Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.\n\n - Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n - Nice to Have\n   \n   - Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.\n   \n   - Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.\n   \n   - Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$119,000 -$161,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6fef4451-dbbf-40e7-a41c-5569641bcc16","title":"Director, Government Affairs & Public Policy","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T01:26:10.749+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6fef4451-dbbf-40e7-a41c-5569641bcc16","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6fef4451-dbbf-40e7-a41c-5569641bcc16/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey's founding Director of Government Affairs and Public Policy, you will build the function responsible for how Harvey engages with governments, regulators, judiciaries, and the institutions shaping the future of AI in legal and professional services — in the US and globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a senior leadership role reporting directly to the Chief Strategy Officer. The primary emphasis is on public policy: educating and informing policymakers, building Harvey's credibility as a substantive, trusted voice in consequential conversations about AI governance, the future of the legal profession, and access to justice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The scope spans federal, state, and local bodies in the US, EMEA and APAC — where bar associations, state licensing authorities, and judicial and legislative actions are currently setting the most consequential AI policy. You will own the overall strategy and engagement framework, build the company's presence from a standing start, and hire the regional team beneath you as the function grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role. The playbook doesn't exist yet, and you'll write it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function.</strong> Stand up the strategy, engagement framework, and stakeholder relationships that position Harvey as a trusted, credible voice in the future of AI in legal and professional services. Define what Harvey says — and what it doesn't — on the policy issues that matter most.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the policy relationship landscape.</strong> Build and maintain direct relationships with policymakers, regulators, bar associations, judicial, legislative, and regulatory bodies, and other key institutions across the US and, over time, internationally. You are the person in those meetings, not a coordinator behind them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop Harvey's policy narrative.</strong> Partner with the Chief Strategy Officer, senior legal leadership, and communications to shape Harvey's public positioning on AI governance, the future of the legal profession, responsible technology deployment, and access to justice. Maintain bipartisan and cross-jurisdictional credibility..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Maintain institutional credibility.</strong> You will develop and cultivate collaborative relationships with policy makers around the world, bringing a candid, well-informed perspective on the future of the legal profession and the policy positions best aligned with fostering and supporting a vibrant, resilient legal ecosystem.  You will advocate for positions that enable Harvey’s product strategy will advancing the broader interests of the legal profession, including both in-house lawyers and private practice attorneys.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inform product and market strategy.</strong> Serve as a strategic bridge between the external policy environment and Harvey's product and go-to-market teams — specifically where product decisions carry regulatory triggers or policy implications. Surface emerging compliance requirements, public-sector opportunities, and the kinds of ethically complex questions that arise when AI intersects with sensitive legal and governmental contexts. Help ensure Harvey is well-positioned to serve government legal departments and regulated industries as those markets evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and lead the team.</strong> As the function grows, hire and develop regional government affairs managers across key markets (initially US, with EMEA and APAC to follow). Set up the operational infrastructure — stakeholder tracking, regulatory monitoring, policy calendar management — that keeps Harvey's policy posture sharp, current, and globally coordinated.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A career defined by progressive depth in public policy, government affairs, or regulatory work</strong> — whether in-house at a major technology or professional services company, in senior government or regulatory roles, or in a senior advisory capacity at a leading firm. J.D. strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A policy-first orientation, not a lobbying-first one.</strong> You understand the difference between working the machinery of government and educating policymakers, and you lead with the latter. You build credibility through substance, not access alone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demonstrated ability to build, not just operate.</strong> You have stood up a function, set a strategy, and built relationships from a standing start — or led a significant expansion of scope within a larger organization. You know what it takes to go from zero to credible in a new institutional landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep, trusted relationships with senior government, regulatory, and institutional stakeholders across multiple jurisdictions.</strong> You are known, respected, and sought out for your judgment. Your relationships outlast administrations and election cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Substantive familiarity with the legal industry, the judiciary, or the regulatory environment around legal services and AI.</strong> You understand how bar associations, courts, and government legal departments think, and you can engage credibly at a senior level with people who have spent decades in these institutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bipartisan credibility and intellectual integrity.</strong> You have worked constructively across political environments. You know when to hold a position and when to listen. You can make the case for Harvey's work in rooms where the politics cut differently, without compromising your credibility in either.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Genuine conviction about the role of AI in improving legal services and expanding access to justice.</strong> This is not a defensive compliance role. Harvey's position — that AI can augment professional judgment, reduce barriers to expertise, and strengthen legal institutions — is one worth making, and you'll make it persuasively and responsibly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional written and verbal communication.</strong> You can represent Harvey in high-stakes, high-visibility settings — before bar committees, judicial conferences, congressional staff, and international regulatory bodies — and hold the room.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Principled judgment in complex environments.</strong> You've navigated situations where the right answer wasn't obvious — politically, ethically, or commercially — and made calls you'd stand behind publicly. You can help Harvey develop clear positions on hard questions and represent them credibly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The chance to build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function from scratch, with a genuine mandate from the executive team and direct access to senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A global mandate that grows — starting with the US, with EMEA and APAC to follow — at a company already operating across 60+ countries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A role at the center of one of the most consequential policy conversations happening anywhere in technology: what AI means for the legal profession, the judiciary, and access to justice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A direct line to the CSO and a seat at the table on key strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A clear path to building and leading a growing team as the function scales alongside the company, with this role expected to grow in scope as Harvey matures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A company at a genuine inflection point, with strong product-market fit, rapid growth, and increasing recognition as the defining platform for AI in legal and professional services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$260,000 - $350,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey's founding Director of Government Affairs and Public Policy, you will build the function responsible for how Harvey engages with governments, regulators, judiciaries, and the institutions shaping the future of AI in legal and professional services — in the US and globally.\n\n\n\nThis is a senior leadership role reporting directly to the Chief Strategy Officer. The primary emphasis is on public policy: educating and informing policymakers, building Harvey's credibility as a substantive, trusted voice in consequential conversations about AI governance, the future of the legal profession, and access to justice.\n\n\n\nThe scope spans federal, state, and local bodies in the US, EMEA and APAC — where bar associations, state licensing authorities, and judicial and legislative actions are currently setting the most consequential AI policy. You will own the overall strategy and engagement framework, build the company's presence from a standing start, and hire the regional team beneath you as the function grows.\n\n\n\nThis is a builder's role. The playbook doesn't exist yet, and you'll write it.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function. Stand up the strategy, engagement framework, and stakeholder relationships that position Harvey as a trusted, credible voice in the future of AI in legal and professional services. Define what Harvey says — and what it doesn't — on the policy issues that matter most.\n\n - Own the policy relationship landscape. Build and maintain direct relationships with policymakers, regulators, bar associations, judicial, legislative, and regulatory bodies, and other key institutions across the US and, over time, internationally. You are the person in those meetings, not a coordinator behind them.\n\n - Develop Harvey's policy narrative. Partner with the Chief Strategy Officer, senior legal leadership, and communications to shape Harvey's public positioning on AI governance, the future of the legal profession, responsible technology deployment, and access to justice. Maintain bipartisan and cross-jurisdictional credibility..\n\n - Maintain institutional credibility. You will develop and cultivate collaborative relationships with policy makers around the world, bringing a candid, well-informed perspective on the future of the legal profession and the policy positions best aligned with fostering and supporting a vibrant, resilient legal ecosystem.  You will advocate for positions that enable Harvey’s product strategy will advancing the broader interests of the legal profession, including both in-house lawyers and private practice attorneys.\n\n - Inform product and market strategy. Serve as a strategic bridge between the external policy environment and Harvey's product and go-to-market teams — specifically where product decisions carry regulatory triggers or policy implications. Surface emerging compliance requirements, public-sector opportunities, and the kinds of ethically complex questions that arise when AI intersects with sensitive legal and governmental contexts. Help ensure Harvey is well-positioned to serve government legal departments and regulated industries as those markets evolve.\n\n - Build and lead the team. As the function grows, hire and develop regional government affairs managers across key markets (initially US, with EMEA and APAC to follow). Set up the operational infrastructure — stakeholder tracking, regulatory monitoring, policy calendar management — that keeps Harvey's policy posture sharp, current, and globally coordinated.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A career defined by progressive depth in public policy, government affairs, or regulatory work — whether in-house at a major technology or professional services company, in senior government or regulatory roles, or in a senior advisory capacity at a leading firm. J.D. strongly preferred.\n\n - A policy-first orientation, not a lobbying-first one. You understand the difference between working the machinery of government and educating policymakers, and you lead with the latter. You build credibility through substance, not access alone.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build, not just operate. You have stood up a function, set a strategy, and built relationships from a standing start — or led a significant expansion of scope within a larger organization. You know what it takes to go from zero to credible in a new institutional landscape.\n\n - Deep, trusted relationships with senior government, regulatory, and institutional stakeholders across multiple jurisdictions. You are known, respected, and sought out for your judgment. Your relationships outlast administrations and election cycles.\n\n - Substantive familiarity with the legal industry, the judiciary, or the regulatory environment around legal services and AI. You understand how bar associations, courts, and government legal departments think, and you can engage credibly at a senior level with people who have spent decades in these institutions.\n\n - Bipartisan credibility and intellectual integrity. You have worked constructively across political environments. You know when to hold a position and when to listen. You can make the case for Harvey's work in rooms where the politics cut differently, without compromising your credibility in either.\n\n - Genuine conviction about the role of AI in improving legal services and expanding access to justice. This is not a defensive compliance role. Harvey's position — that AI can augment professional judgment, reduce barriers to expertise, and strengthen legal institutions — is one worth making, and you'll make it persuasively and responsibly.\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication. You can represent Harvey in high-stakes, high-visibility settings — before bar committees, judicial conferences, congressional staff, and international regulatory bodies — and hold the room.\n\n - Principled judgment in complex environments. You've navigated situations where the right answer wasn't obvious — politically, ethically, or commercially — and made calls you'd stand behind publicly. You can help Harvey develop clear positions on hard questions and represent them credibly.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - The chance to build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function from scratch, with a genuine mandate from the executive team and direct access to senior leadership.\n\n - A global mandate that grows — starting with the US, with EMEA and APAC to follow — at a company already operating across 60+ countries.\n\n - A role at the center of one of the most consequential policy conversations happening anywhere in technology: what AI means for the legal profession, the judiciary, and access to justice.\n\n - A direct line to the CSO and a seat at the table on key strategic decisions.\n\n - A clear path to building and leading a growing team as the function scales alongside the company, with this role expected to grow in scope as Harvey matures.\n\n - A company at a genuine inflection point, with strong product-market fit, rapid growth, and increasing recognition as the defining platform for AI in legal and professional services.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$260,000 - $350,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$260K – $350K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$260K - $350K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"aeb95718-58ef-42ed-9a09-6f753733947a","tierSummary":"$260K – $350K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ca50f547-2dbf-404f-b2f6-d4abb833b29f","summary":"$260K – $350K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":350000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":350000}]}},{"id":"3a48daa6-a85f-479f-badd-ca4cf496f72f","title":"Global Senior Accounts Payable Analyst","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:26:28.029+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3a48daa6-a85f-479f-badd-ca4cf496f72f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3a48daa6-a85f-479f-badd-ca4cf496f72f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a new senior individual-contributor role created to help build an accurate, controlled, and increasingly automated global Accounts Payable (AP) operation that can process thousands of invoices per month without requiring linear headcount growth. It sits within Harvey's global AP function and reports directly to the Global Accounts Payable Manager, partnering closely with Procurement, Tax, Treasury, Accounting, IT/Business Systems, and business stakeholders. Harvey is growing quickly across revenue, headcount, and transaction volume, and is putting more systems and structure in place to keep pace, so this role must handle day-to-day AP work while simultaneously improving the systems behind it. The person will initially be hands-on with invoice processing, payments, reconciliations, and exception resolution before helping transform the operation toward a touchless, exception-based model.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own hands-on execution across the global AP process, including invoice processing, multi-entity and multi-currency transactions, VAT/GST handling, and resolution of complex invoice exceptions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support and execute global payment cycles so that payments are accurate, properly approved, secure, and completed on time, and perform and improve AP subledger, payment, and supplier-account reconciliations, investigating and resolving differences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Map Harvey's end-to-end AP and procure-to-pay (P2P) processes, diagnose the root causes of manual work, and redesign workflows for scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own AP requirements, workflow design, and AP-side configuration across Zip, NetSuite, and connected systems, including data quality, testing, and issue resolution, while partnering with IT/Business Systems on integrations and deeper technical changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, test, and implement practical AI and automation opportunities that reduce manual invoice handling while preserving appropriate accounting, tax, and payment controls, moving the operation toward a touchless, exception-based model in which higher-risk or incomplete transactions still receive human review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and monitor meaningful AP performance measures (touchless rate, exception rate, processing time, payment timeliness, reconciliation quality, and manual effort) and create clear process and control documentation that establishes repeatable global standards as Harvey enters new countries.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Substantial hands-on international AP experience, with strong working knowledge of international AP, including VAT/GST, multi-entity and multi-currency AP, global payments, and AP reconciliations; experience with US accounts payable and related requirements is highly beneficial.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A demonstrable track record of improving AP systems and workflows, not merely operating them, with concrete examples of process redesign, automation, or streamlining that you owned end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems fluency and the ability to translate AP requirements into system configurations and improvements, working closely with IT/Business Systems on integrations and more technical changes. Experience with NetSuite, Zip, or comparable ERP and P2P platforms is preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated practical use of AI or automation to improve finance or operational workflows, with clear examples of what you changed or built, the controls applied, and the resulting impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A process-improvement mindset with strong root-cause instincts, the ability to create clarity in ambiguous, fast-scaling environments, and the ownership to fix broken processes without a strict playbook.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, direct communication and cross-functional collaboration skills, including the ability to explain finance issues to non-finance partners and drive alignment across Procurement, Tax, Treasury, IT, and the business.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis is a new senior individual-contributor role created to help build an accurate, controlled, and increasingly automated global Accounts Payable (AP) operation that can process thousands of invoices per month without requiring linear headcount growth. It sits within Harvey's global AP function and reports directly to the Global Accounts Payable Manager, partnering closely with Procurement, Tax, Treasury, Accounting, IT/Business Systems, and business stakeholders. Harvey is growing quickly across revenue, headcount, and transaction volume, and is putting more systems and structure in place to keep pace, so this role must handle day-to-day AP work while simultaneously improving the systems behind it. The person will initially be hands-on with invoice processing, payments, reconciliations, and exception resolution before helping transform the operation toward a touchless, exception-based model.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own hands-on execution across the global AP process, including invoice processing, multi-entity and multi-currency transactions, VAT/GST handling, and resolution of complex invoice exceptions.\n\n - Support and execute global payment cycles so that payments are accurate, properly approved, secure, and completed on time, and perform and improve AP subledger, payment, and supplier-account reconciliations, investigating and resolving differences.\n\n - Map Harvey's end-to-end AP and procure-to-pay (P2P) processes, diagnose the root causes of manual work, and redesign workflows for scale.\n\n - Own AP requirements, workflow design, and AP-side configuration across Zip, NetSuite, and connected systems, including data quality, testing, and issue resolution, while partnering with IT/Business Systems on integrations and deeper technical changes.\n\n - Identify, test, and implement practical AI and automation opportunities that reduce manual invoice handling while preserving appropriate accounting, tax, and payment controls, moving the operation toward a touchless, exception-based model in which higher-risk or incomplete transactions still receive human review.\n\n - Establish and monitor meaningful AP performance measures (touchless rate, exception rate, processing time, payment timeliness, reconciliation quality, and manual effort) and create clear process and control documentation that establishes repeatable global standards as Harvey enters new countries.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Substantial hands-on international AP experience, with strong working knowledge of international AP, including VAT/GST, multi-entity and multi-currency AP, global payments, and AP reconciliations; experience with US accounts payable and related requirements is highly beneficial.\n\n - A demonstrable track record of improving AP systems and workflows, not merely operating them, with concrete examples of process redesign, automation, or streamlining that you owned end-to-end.\n\n - Strong systems fluency and the ability to translate AP requirements into system configurations and improvements, working closely with IT/Business Systems on integrations and more technical changes. Experience with NetSuite, Zip, or comparable ERP and P2P platforms is preferred.\n\n - Demonstrated practical use of AI or automation to improve finance or operational workflows, with clear examples of what you changed or built, the controls applied, and the resulting impact.\n\n - A process-improvement mindset with strong root-cause instincts, the ability to create clarity in ambiguous, fast-scaling environments, and the ownership to fix broken processes without a strict playbook.\n\n - Clear, direct communication and cross-functional collaboration skills, including the ability to explain finance issues to non-finance partners and drive alignment across Procurement, Tax, Treasury, IT, and the business.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c59ad688-0106-4f49-a1d3-94c2ea0f5a48","title":"Director, Government Affairs & Public Policy","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T01:26:36.607+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c59ad688-0106-4f49-a1d3-94c2ea0f5a48","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c59ad688-0106-4f49-a1d3-94c2ea0f5a48/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey's founding Director of Government Affairs and Public Policy, you will build the function responsible for how Harvey engages with governments, regulators, judiciaries, and the institutions shaping the future of AI in legal and professional services — in the US and globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a senior leadership role reporting directly to the Chief Strategy Officer. The primary emphasis is on public policy: educating and informing policymakers, building Harvey's credibility as a substantive, trusted voice in consequential conversations about AI governance, the future of the legal profession, and access to justice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The scope spans federal, state, and local bodies in the US, EMEA and APAC — where bar associations, state licensing authorities, and judicial and legislative actions are currently setting the most consequential AI policy. You will own the overall strategy and engagement framework, build the company's presence from a standing start, and hire the regional team beneath you as the function grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role. The playbook doesn't exist yet, and you'll write it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function.</strong> Stand up the strategy, engagement framework, and stakeholder relationships that position Harvey as a trusted, credible voice in the future of AI in legal and professional services. Define what Harvey says — and what it doesn't — on the policy issues that matter most.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the policy relationship landscape.</strong> Build and maintain direct relationships with policymakers, regulators, bar associations, judicial, legislative, and regulatory bodies, and other key institutions across the US and, over time, internationally. You are the person in those meetings, not a coordinator behind them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop Harvey's policy narrative.</strong> Partner with the Chief Strategy Officer, senior legal leadership, and communications to shape Harvey's public positioning on AI governance, the future of the legal profession, responsible technology deployment, and access to justice. Maintain bipartisan and cross-jurisdictional credibility..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Maintain institutional credibility.</strong> You will develop and cultivate collaborative relationships with policy makers around the world, bringing a candid, well-informed perspective on the future of the legal profession and the policy positions best aligned with fostering and supporting a vibrant, resilient legal ecosystem.  You will advocate for positions that enable Harvey’s product strategy will advancing the broader interests of the legal profession, including both in-house lawyers and private practice attorneys.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inform product and market strategy.</strong> Serve as a strategic bridge between the external policy environment and Harvey's product and go-to-market teams — specifically where product decisions carry regulatory triggers or policy implications. Surface emerging compliance requirements, public-sector opportunities, and the kinds of ethically complex questions that arise when AI intersects with sensitive legal and governmental contexts. Help ensure Harvey is well-positioned to serve government legal departments and regulated industries as those markets evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and lead the team.</strong> As the function grows, hire and develop regional government affairs managers across key markets (initially US, with EMEA and APAC to follow). Set up the operational infrastructure — stakeholder tracking, regulatory monitoring, policy calendar management — that keeps Harvey's policy posture sharp, current, and globally coordinated.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A career defined by progressive depth in public policy, government affairs, or regulatory work</strong> — whether in-house at a major technology or professional services company, in senior government or regulatory roles, or in a senior advisory capacity at a leading firm. J.D. strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A policy-first orientation, not a lobbying-first one.</strong> You understand the difference between working the machinery of government and educating policymakers, and you lead with the latter. You build credibility through substance, not access alone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demonstrated ability to build, not just operate.</strong> You have stood up a function, set a strategy, and built relationships from a standing start — or led a significant expansion of scope within a larger organization. You know what it takes to go from zero to credible in a new institutional landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep, trusted relationships with senior government, regulatory, and institutional stakeholders across multiple jurisdictions.</strong> You are known, respected, and sought out for your judgment. Your relationships outlast administrations and election cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Substantive familiarity with the legal industry, the judiciary, or the regulatory environment around legal services and AI.</strong> You understand how bar associations, courts, and government legal departments think, and you can engage credibly at a senior level with people who have spent decades in these institutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bipartisan credibility and intellectual integrity.</strong> You have worked constructively across political environments. You know when to hold a position and when to listen. You can make the case for Harvey's work in rooms where the politics cut differently, without compromising your credibility in either.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Genuine conviction about the role of AI in improving legal services and expanding access to justice.</strong> This is not a defensive compliance role. Harvey's position — that AI can augment professional judgment, reduce barriers to expertise, and strengthen legal institutions — is one worth making, and you'll make it persuasively and responsibly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional written and verbal communication.</strong> You can represent Harvey in high-stakes, high-visibility settings — before bar committees, judicial conferences, congressional staff, and international regulatory bodies — and hold the room.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Principled judgment in complex environments.</strong> You've navigated situations where the right answer wasn't obvious — politically, ethically, or commercially — and made calls you'd stand behind publicly. You can help Harvey develop clear positions on hard questions and represent them credibly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The chance to build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function from scratch, with a genuine mandate from the executive team and direct access to senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A global mandate that grows — starting with the US, with EMEA and APAC to follow — at a company already operating across 60+ countries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A role at the center of one of the most consequential policy conversations happening anywhere in technology: what AI means for the legal profession, the judiciary, and access to justice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A direct line to the CSO and a seat at the table on key strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A clear path to building and leading a growing team as the function scales alongside the company, with this role expected to grow in scope as Harvey matures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A company at a genuine inflection point, with strong product-market fit, rapid growth, and increasing recognition as the defining platform for AI in legal and professional services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$260,000 - $350,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey's founding Director of Government Affairs and Public Policy, you will build the function responsible for how Harvey engages with governments, regulators, judiciaries, and the institutions shaping the future of AI in legal and professional services — in the US and globally.\n\n\n\nThis is a senior leadership role reporting directly to the Chief Strategy Officer. The primary emphasis is on public policy: educating and informing policymakers, building Harvey's credibility as a substantive, trusted voice in consequential conversations about AI governance, the future of the legal profession, and access to justice.\n\n\n\nThe scope spans federal, state, and local bodies in the US, EMEA and APAC — where bar associations, state licensing authorities, and judicial and legislative actions are currently setting the most consequential AI policy. You will own the overall strategy and engagement framework, build the company's presence from a standing start, and hire the regional team beneath you as the function grows.\n\n\n\nThis is a builder's role. The playbook doesn't exist yet, and you'll write it.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function. Stand up the strategy, engagement framework, and stakeholder relationships that position Harvey as a trusted, credible voice in the future of AI in legal and professional services. Define what Harvey says — and what it doesn't — on the policy issues that matter most.\n\n - Own the policy relationship landscape. Build and maintain direct relationships with policymakers, regulators, bar associations, judicial, legislative, and regulatory bodies, and other key institutions across the US and, over time, internationally. You are the person in those meetings, not a coordinator behind them.\n\n - Develop Harvey's policy narrative. Partner with the Chief Strategy Officer, senior legal leadership, and communications to shape Harvey's public positioning on AI governance, the future of the legal profession, responsible technology deployment, and access to justice. Maintain bipartisan and cross-jurisdictional credibility..\n\n - Maintain institutional credibility. You will develop and cultivate collaborative relationships with policy makers around the world, bringing a candid, well-informed perspective on the future of the legal profession and the policy positions best aligned with fostering and supporting a vibrant, resilient legal ecosystem.  You will advocate for positions that enable Harvey’s product strategy will advancing the broader interests of the legal profession, including both in-house lawyers and private practice attorneys.\n\n - Inform product and market strategy. Serve as a strategic bridge between the external policy environment and Harvey's product and go-to-market teams — specifically where product decisions carry regulatory triggers or policy implications. Surface emerging compliance requirements, public-sector opportunities, and the kinds of ethically complex questions that arise when AI intersects with sensitive legal and governmental contexts. Help ensure Harvey is well-positioned to serve government legal departments and regulated industries as those markets evolve.\n\n - Build and lead the team. As the function grows, hire and develop regional government affairs managers across key markets (initially US, with EMEA and APAC to follow). Set up the operational infrastructure — stakeholder tracking, regulatory monitoring, policy calendar management — that keeps Harvey's policy posture sharp, current, and globally coordinated.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A career defined by progressive depth in public policy, government affairs, or regulatory work — whether in-house at a major technology or professional services company, in senior government or regulatory roles, or in a senior advisory capacity at a leading firm. J.D. strongly preferred.\n\n - A policy-first orientation, not a lobbying-first one. You understand the difference between working the machinery of government and educating policymakers, and you lead with the latter. You build credibility through substance, not access alone.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build, not just operate. You have stood up a function, set a strategy, and built relationships from a standing start — or led a significant expansion of scope within a larger organization. You know what it takes to go from zero to credible in a new institutional landscape.\n\n - Deep, trusted relationships with senior government, regulatory, and institutional stakeholders across multiple jurisdictions. You are known, respected, and sought out for your judgment. Your relationships outlast administrations and election cycles.\n\n - Substantive familiarity with the legal industry, the judiciary, or the regulatory environment around legal services and AI. You understand how bar associations, courts, and government legal departments think, and you can engage credibly at a senior level with people who have spent decades in these institutions.\n\n - Bipartisan credibility and intellectual integrity. You have worked constructively across political environments. You know when to hold a position and when to listen. You can make the case for Harvey's work in rooms where the politics cut differently, without compromising your credibility in either.\n\n - Genuine conviction about the role of AI in improving legal services and expanding access to justice. This is not a defensive compliance role. Harvey's position — that AI can augment professional judgment, reduce barriers to expertise, and strengthen legal institutions — is one worth making, and you'll make it persuasively and responsibly.\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication. You can represent Harvey in high-stakes, high-visibility settings — before bar committees, judicial conferences, congressional staff, and international regulatory bodies — and hold the room.\n\n - Principled judgment in complex environments. You've navigated situations where the right answer wasn't obvious — politically, ethically, or commercially — and made calls you'd stand behind publicly. You can help Harvey develop clear positions on hard questions and represent them credibly.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - The chance to build Harvey's government affairs and public policy function from scratch, with a genuine mandate from the executive team and direct access to senior leadership.\n\n - A global mandate that grows — starting with the US, with EMEA and APAC to follow — at a company already operating across 60+ countries.\n\n - A role at the center of one of the most consequential policy conversations happening anywhere in technology: what AI means for the legal profession, the judiciary, and access to justice.\n\n - A direct line to the CSO and a seat at the table on key strategic decisions.\n\n - A clear path to building and leading a growing team as the function scales alongside the company, with this role expected to grow in scope as Harvey matures.\n\n - A company at a genuine inflection point, with strong product-market fit, rapid growth, and increasing recognition as the defining platform for AI in legal and professional services.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$260,000 - $350,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$260K – $350K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$260K - $350K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b03dc887-31d2-447d-9354-cce1f724ab37","tierSummary":"$260K – $350K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e3b4f333-19c4-487e-b42c-baf35456da1b","summary":"$260K – $350K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":350000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":350000}]}},{"id":"04eb457b-e985-4e3b-9635-0a2b867ada97","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-31T03:39:41.138+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04eb457b-e985-4e3b-9635-0a2b867ada97","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04eb457b-e985-4e3b-9635-0a2b867ada97/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&amp;A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.\n\n - Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.\n\n - Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.\n\n - Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. \n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-BB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"cb3e2141-8e12-45e9-b8fa-0d79696a88cb","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d79be2e7-1d7a-4da7-99c4-48bdfbc4a89c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e044f73e-69fc-414f-9ef8-5bfee255d9e6","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8b047fa4-08e5-4c31-ae9b-f299d2028352","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"ec074cbf-8d48-4661-b26c-1fdfb01df783","title":"Applied Legal Researcher","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-05T02:49:07.110+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ec074cbf-8d48-4661-b26c-1fdfb01df783","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ec074cbf-8d48-4661-b26c-1fdfb01df783/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a legal researcher with a strong understanding of how law firms, financial institutions, large corporations, and other organizations deliver professional services and execute complex legal and knowledge work tasks. We have incredible product-market fit and demand across diverse customer profiles. Executing on this demand requires a strong understanding of our customers' workflows and how those workflows can be accelerated by AI systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To facilitate the development of these systems, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and deliver subject-matter expertise to support AI research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with our engineering, product, and design teams to define and develop AI systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and improve AI systems through prompt engineering, fine tuning, and other techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build proprietary benchmarks and datasets to evaluate models and model systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with clients to understand their workflows, identify pain points, and translate complex business and legal requirements into technical solutions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD from a top US law school or equivalent post-graduate qualification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-7 years of experience at a US law firm, financial institution, or equivalent professional service provider</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For NYC applicants: experience working in-house or at a financial institution </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to deliver high quality work product on demanding deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to effectively communicate with a variety internal and external stakeholders and translate complex problems effectively between them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to define positive outcomes in situations with underspecified success criteria</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep intellectual curiosity and eagerness to learn across domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness and desire to do work in the trenches - e.g., grading hundreds of answers, breaking down thousands of documents - getting the models to do junior associate work requires a lot of things that look like junior associate work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 - $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a legal researcher with a strong understanding of how law firms, financial institutions, large corporations, and other organizations deliver professional services and execute complex legal and knowledge work tasks. We have incredible product-market fit and demand across diverse customer profiles. Executing on this demand requires a strong understanding of our customers' workflows and how those workflows can be accelerated by AI systems.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nTo facilitate the development of these systems, you will:\n\n - Develop and deliver subject-matter expertise to support AI research\n\n - Work closely with our engineering, product, and design teams to define and develop AI systems\n\n - Build and improve AI systems through prompt engineering, fine tuning, and other techniques\n\n - Build proprietary benchmarks and datasets to evaluate models and model systems\n\n - Partner directly with clients to understand their workflows, identify pain points, and translate complex business and legal requirements into technical solutions\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD from a top US law school or equivalent post-graduate qualification\n\n - 3-7 years of experience at a US law firm, financial institution, or equivalent professional service provider\n\n - For NYC applicants: experience working in-house or at a financial institution \n\n - Demonstrated ability to deliver high quality work product on demanding deadlines\n\n - Ability to effectively communicate with a variety internal and external stakeholders and translate complex problems effectively between them\n\n - Ability to define positive outcomes in situations with underspecified success criteria\n\n - Deep intellectual curiosity and eagerness to learn across domains\n\n - Willingness and desire to do work in the trenches - e.g., grading hundreds of answers, breaking down thousands of documents - getting the models to do junior associate work requires a lot of things that look like junior associate work\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$180,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e1231016-c483-4107-95fa-e87569762559","tierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"eae43d4d-50ed-495d-949a-f86fa7ae3e5b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fe595193-4388-4176-b086-43de77ae5683","summary":"$180K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"e2976ecf-f785-4524-8545-bbd519ffdaae","title":"Engineering Manager, Enterprise","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-10T20:47:08.019+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e2976ecf-f785-4524-8545-bbd519ffdaae","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e2976ecf-f785-4524-8545-bbd519ffdaae/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Engineering Manager, Product at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end delivery of core product initiatives, from technical design through execution and iteration, while directly managing a high-performing fullstack engineering team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set technical direction for large-scale, AI-powered systems, including:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retrieval over petabyte-scale document collections.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product interfaces that enable organizations to collaborate with AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long-horizon (1000+ step) planning agents for mission-critical workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Government-grade security for highly sensitive data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluation of LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internet-scale data collection across 50+ jurisdictions.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate product vision into architecture, making pragmatic tradeoffs that balance speed, quality, and long-term scalability in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead hands-on when it matters: contribute to design, code, and architecture reviews, and dive into implementation to unblock the team or tackle the hardest problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and grow your team by hiring exceptional engineers, setting clear technical and behavioral standards, and investing in mentorship and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner deeply with Product, Design, and AI to identify high-leverage opportunities and ship highly intuitive, detail-oriented user experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a strong engineering culture centered on simplicity, ownership, craftsmanship, and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align execution with company goals, ensuring technical investments directly support product strategy and long-term impact.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience as a product-focused fullstack or backend software engineer (post BS/MS), with a history of shipping real products to real users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience leading engineers, with clear ownership over both delivery and team health. Past management experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven ability to design and operate backend platforms that support multiple product lines at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with modern frontend frameworks (e.g. React) or backend systems (e.g. Python, Node, Go).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent technical judgment: you know when to move fast, when to invest, and when to simplify.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong product instinct and attention to detail, with a track record of building intuitive, high-quality user experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building, motivating, and retaining high-performing teams in high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid computer science fundamentals and strong programming skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit and ownership mindset — you’re comfortable operating in ambiguity and taking responsibility for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><u>Bonus: </u></strong>experience with AI-powered applications, large-scale data systems, LLM evaluation, or complex internal platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CA $196,800 - CA $270,600</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Engineering Manager, Product at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.\n\n\n\nYou will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Own end-to-end delivery of core product initiatives, from technical design through execution and iteration, while directly managing a high-performing fullstack engineering team.\n\n - Set technical direction for large-scale, AI-powered systems, including:\n   \n   - Retrieval over petabyte-scale document collections.\n   \n   - Product interfaces that enable organizations to collaborate with AI.\n   \n   - Long-horizon (1000+ step) planning agents for mission-critical workflows.\n   \n   - Government-grade security for highly sensitive data.\n   \n   - Evaluation of LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks.\n   \n   - Internet-scale data collection across 50+ jurisdictions.\n\n - Translate product vision into architecture, making pragmatic tradeoffs that balance speed, quality, and long-term scalability in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Lead hands-on when it matters: contribute to design, code, and architecture reviews, and dive into implementation to unblock the team or tackle the hardest problems.\n\n - Build and grow your team by hiring exceptional engineers, setting clear technical and behavioral standards, and investing in mentorship and career development.\n\n - Partner deeply with Product, Design, and AI to identify high-leverage opportunities and ship highly intuitive, detail-oriented user experiences.\n\n - Establish a strong engineering culture centered on simplicity, ownership, craftsmanship, and continuous improvement.\n\n - Align execution with company goals, ensuring technical investments directly support product strategy and long-term impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of experience as a product-focused fullstack or backend software engineer (post BS/MS), with a history of shipping real products to real users.\n\n - 2+ years of experience leading engineers, with clear ownership over both delivery and team health. Past management experience is a plus.\n\n - A proven ability to design and operate backend platforms that support multiple product lines at scale.\n\n - Strong experience with modern frontend frameworks (e.g. React) or backend systems (e.g. Python, Node, Go).\n\n - Excellent technical judgment: you know when to move fast, when to invest, and when to simplify.\n\n - A strong product instinct and attention to detail, with a track record of building intuitive, high-quality user experiences.\n\n - Demonstrated success building, motivating, and retaining high-performing teams in high-growth environments.\n\n - Solid computer science fundamentals and strong programming skills.\n\n - Grit and ownership mindset — you’re comfortable operating in ambiguity and taking responsibility for outcomes.\n\n - Bonus: experience with AI-powered applications, large-scale data systems, LLM evaluation, or complex internal platforms.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nCA $196,800 - CA $270,600\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$196.8K – $270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$196.8K - $270.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5a41b116-bac7-4b1b-a04b-929b640f2a3b","tierSummary":"$196.8K – $270.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d4f14989-757d-4310-b539-acff1073058b","summary":"$196.8K – $270.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600},{"id":"230809ea-cc4d-4e38-95bc-b5ab92407d96","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"bedb4842-6b4d-41c2-ac5e-d34670a1b8ec","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":270600},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"01f31ece-f3fe-4991-b6fb-b59f21faa8e9","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Full Stack","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-11T01:35:08.668+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/01f31ece-f3fe-4991-b6fb-b59f21faa8e9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/01f31ece-f3fe-4991-b6fb-b59f21faa8e9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Full Stack Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build foundational infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CA $196,800 – CA $295,200</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Full Stack Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.\n\n\n\nYou will design and own systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Design and build foundational infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations\n\n - Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams\n\n - Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls\n\n - Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nCA $196,800 – CA $295,200\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$295.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$196.8K - CA$295.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bcd1b223-5581-4755-b0dc-3d24bee41d05","tierSummary":"CA$196.8K – CA$295.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0b49c367-427c-45b1-81e1-76b8140f79fc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c5f6388d-0a73-4379-a207-98beb56ff93f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a1c92ec7-c6c2-456b-abe6-2aa21d76371e","summary":"CA$196.8K – CA$295.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":295200}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":196800,"maxValue":295200}]}},{"id":"07054b1e-f7ac-4388-8149-2954b30640c7","title":"Strategic Account Executive, Nordics","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Stockholm","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T14:38:36.985+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/07054b1e-f7ac-4388-8149-2954b30640c7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/07054b1e-f7ac-4388-8149-2954b30640c7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategic Account Executive, Nordics at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Strategic Account Executive, Nordics at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"aede4098-91f4-44f5-9d53-27c15cb2bae7","title":"Senior or Staff Design Engineer, Design Systems","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-12T14:51:35.093+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/aede4098-91f4-44f5-9d53-27c15cb2bae7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/aede4098-91f4-44f5-9d53-27c15cb2bae7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey designs and builds for a legal industry being reshaped by AI, moving with the urgency and ambition the moment demands, not just adapting to change but architecting it. As a Design Systems Designer at Harvey, you will define the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a design role with unusual technical depth. You lead with design: craft, systems thinking, and a strong point of view on product experience. But you're equally at home in architecture and implementation. You understand how tokens are structured, how components are composed, and how systems are built to scale, and you use that fluency to push the system forward rather than hand decisions over the wall.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who has lived through the evolution of the discipline, someone who understands not just how modern design systems work, but why they're built the way they are, and where the field is heading, especially as AI-native products reshape what a design system needs to be.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will report to the Design org, and will be based in SF, NYC, or Toronto.</p><h1><strong><br />What you’ll do</strong></h1><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build an AI-native design system that sets the bar for design quality for Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, prototype, and ship production-ready system components in tight collaboration with frontend and platform engineering, with shared ownership of quality, performance, and maintainability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and evolve the core design system foundations (components, patterns, and tokens) that scale across complex, AI-powered experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push both the architecture and the implementation of the system: shape component APIs, token structure, theming, and composition patterns alongside engineering, not downstream of it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for technical approaches with confidence, especially in new or ambiguous territory where established patterns don't yet exist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed accessibility, responsiveness, and performance into the system by default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish clear contribution, governance, and deprecation models that balance velocity with system integrity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar for system quality across the product through design reviews, critique, and hands-on work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build alignment across Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate future product and platform needs, evolving the system proactively as Harvey scales</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own AI design and implementation workflows for the design team, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish in-code prototyping patterns that make it easier to be innovative and consistent as designers increasingly leverage IDEs to experiment and ship.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define AI-assisted design and implementation workflows, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document system usage and best practices in a way that is clear, practical, and trusted by product teams</p></li></ul></li></ol><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What you have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years (Senior) / 8+ years (Staff) of product design experience, with significant ownership of design systems in complex product environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A design portfolio that demonstrates high design craft in system-level thinking, but a strong point of view on quality, and visual cohesion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep design systems expertise, including an understanding of the history and evolution of the discipline. You know why the field moved from style guides to tokens to composable architectures, and you have a point of view on what comes next</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent design engineering communication: you articulate system decisions and tradeoffs fluently to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to clearly articulate system decisions and tradeoffs to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of scalable system architecture and component implementation: component API design, design tokens, theming strategies, and how systems hold up across teams and codebases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design Engineer experience preferred, but not required in an AI-first world where the boundary between design and engineering is shifting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership: you treat the system as a product, not a ticket queue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, loosely held, being comfortable challenging conventions and evolving best practices as the discipline changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguous problem spaces and bringing structure where it doesn't yet exist</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Why design systems matter at Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$205,760 - $315,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey designs and builds for a legal industry being reshaped by AI, moving with the urgency and ambition the moment demands, not just adapting to change but architecting it. As a Design Systems Designer at Harvey, you will define the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.\n\nThis is a design role with unusual technical depth. You lead with design: craft, systems thinking, and a strong point of view on product experience. But you're equally at home in architecture and implementation. You understand how tokens are structured, how components are composed, and how systems are built to scale, and you use that fluency to push the system forward rather than hand decisions over the wall.\n\nWe're looking for someone who has lived through the evolution of the discipline, someone who understands not just how modern design systems work, but why they're built the way they are, and where the field is heading, especially as AI-native products reshape what a design system needs to be.\n\nThis role will report to the Design org, and will be based in SF, NYC, or Toronto.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n 1. Build an AI-native design system that sets the bar for design quality for Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration\n    \n    - Design, prototype, and ship production-ready system components in tight collaboration with frontend and platform engineering, with shared ownership of quality, performance, and maintainability\n    \n    - Define and evolve the core design system foundations (components, patterns, and tokens) that scale across complex, AI-powered experiences\n    \n    - Push both the architecture and the implementation of the system: shape component APIs, token structure, theming, and composition patterns alongside engineering, not downstream of it\n    \n    - Advocate for technical approaches with confidence, especially in new or ambiguous territory where established patterns don't yet exist\n    \n    - Embed accessibility, responsiveness, and performance into the system by default\n    \n    - Establish clear contribution, governance, and deprecation models that balance velocity with system integrity\n    \n    - Raise the bar for system quality across the product through design reviews, critique, and hands-on work\n    \n    - Build alignment across Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration\n    \n    - Anticipate future product and platform needs, evolving the system proactively as Harvey scales\n\n 2. Own AI design and implementation workflows for the design team, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI\n    \n    - Establish in-code prototyping patterns that make it easier to be innovative and consistent as designers increasingly leverage IDEs to experiment and ship.\n    \n    - Define AI-assisted design and implementation workflows, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI\n    \n    - Document system usage and best practices in a way that is clear, practical, and trusted by product teams\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years (Senior) / 8+ years (Staff) of product design experience, with significant ownership of design systems in complex product environments\n\n - A design portfolio that demonstrates high design craft in system-level thinking, but a strong point of view on quality, and visual cohesion\n\n - Deep design systems expertise, including an understanding of the history and evolution of the discipline. You know why the field moved from style guides to tokens to composable architectures, and you have a point of view on what comes next\n\n - Excellent design engineering communication: you articulate system decisions and tradeoffs fluently to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners\n\n - Ability to clearly articulate system decisions and tradeoffs to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners\n\n - Strong knowledge of scalable system architecture and component implementation: component API design, design tokens, theming strategies, and how systems hold up across teams and codebases\n\n - Design Engineer experience preferred, but not required in an AI-first world where the boundary between design and engineering is shifting\n\n - High ownership: you treat the system as a product, not a ticket queue\n\n - Strong opinions, loosely held, being comfortable challenging conventions and evolving best practices as the discipline changes\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguous problem spaces and bringing structure where it doesn't yet exist\n   \n    \n\n\nWHY DESIGN SYSTEMS MATTER AT HARVEY\n\nHarvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$205,760 - $315,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$205,760 – $315,000 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$205,760 - $315,000","compensationTiers":[{"id":"215531e9-7b1f-406e-b969-d1aee321a4e7","tierSummary":"$205,760 – $315,000 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1a1a6dcb-e3d4-459b-a204-51addd770b50","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7d3f7894-6794-4dee-a83a-57c7ff623115","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1b1ea597-f247-4127-a4d5-0e1ee557db1b","summary":"$205,760 – $315,000","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205760,"maxValue":315000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205760,"maxValue":315000}]}},{"id":"9814b9ca-5917-43f8-8f76-6df7aa7e2be3","title":"Senior or Staff Design Engineer, Design Systems","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-12T14:49:37.515+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9814b9ca-5917-43f8-8f76-6df7aa7e2be3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9814b9ca-5917-43f8-8f76-6df7aa7e2be3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey designs and builds for a legal industry being reshaped by AI, moving with the urgency and ambition the moment demands, not just adapting to change but architecting it. As a Design Systems Designer at Harvey, you will define the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a design role with unusual technical depth. You lead with design: craft, systems thinking, and a strong point of view on product experience. But you're equally at home in architecture and implementation. You understand how tokens are structured, how components are composed, and how systems are built to scale, and you use that fluency to push the system forward rather than hand decisions over the wall.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who has lived through the evolution of the discipline, someone who understands not just how modern design systems work, but why they're built the way they are, and where the field is heading, especially as AI-native products reshape what a design system needs to be.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will report to the Design org, and will be based in SF, NYC, or Toronto.</p><h1><strong><br />What you’ll do</strong></h1><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build an AI-native design system that sets the bar for design quality for Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, prototype, and ship production-ready system components in tight collaboration with frontend and platform engineering, with shared ownership of quality, performance, and maintainability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and evolve the core design system foundations (components, patterns, and tokens) that scale across complex, AI-powered experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push both the architecture and the implementation of the system: shape component APIs, token structure, theming, and composition patterns alongside engineering, not downstream of it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for technical approaches with confidence, especially in new or ambiguous territory where established patterns don't yet exist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed accessibility, responsiveness, and performance into the system by default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish clear contribution, governance, and deprecation models that balance velocity with system integrity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar for system quality across the product through design reviews, critique, and hands-on work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build alignment across Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate future product and platform needs, evolving the system proactively as Harvey scales</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own AI design and implementation workflows for the design team, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish in-code prototyping patterns that make it easier to be innovative and consistent as designers increasingly leverage IDEs to experiment and ship.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define AI-assisted design and implementation workflows, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document system usage and best practices in a way that is clear, practical, and trusted by product teams</p></li></ul></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What you have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years (Senior) / 8+ years (Staff) of product design experience, with significant ownership of design systems in complex product environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A design portfolio that demonstrates high design craft in system-level thinking, but a strong point of view on quality, and visual cohesion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep design systems expertise, including an understanding of the history and evolution of the discipline. You know why the field moved from style guides to tokens to composable architectures, and you have a point of view on what comes next</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent design engineering communication: you articulate system decisions and tradeoffs fluently to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to clearly articulate system decisions and tradeoffs to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of scalable system architecture and component implementation: component API design, design tokens, theming strategies, and how systems hold up across teams and codebases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design Engineer experience preferred, but not required in an AI-first world where the boundary between design and engineering is shifting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership: you treat the system as a product, not a ticket queue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, loosely held, being comfortable challenging conventions and evolving best practices as the discipline changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguous problem spaces and bringing structure where it doesn't yet exist</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Why design systems matter at Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$205,760 - $315,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey designs and builds for a legal industry being reshaped by AI, moving with the urgency and ambition the moment demands, not just adapting to change but architecting it. As a Design Systems Designer at Harvey, you will define the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.\n\nThis is a design role with unusual technical depth. You lead with design: craft, systems thinking, and a strong point of view on product experience. But you're equally at home in architecture and implementation. You understand how tokens are structured, how components are composed, and how systems are built to scale, and you use that fluency to push the system forward rather than hand decisions over the wall.\n\nWe're looking for someone who has lived through the evolution of the discipline, someone who understands not just how modern design systems work, but why they're built the way they are, and where the field is heading, especially as AI-native products reshape what a design system needs to be.\n\nThis role will report to the Design org, and will be based in SF, NYC, or Toronto.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n 1. Build an AI-native design system that sets the bar for design quality for Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration\n    \n    - Design, prototype, and ship production-ready system components in tight collaboration with frontend and platform engineering, with shared ownership of quality, performance, and maintainability\n    \n    - Define and evolve the core design system foundations (components, patterns, and tokens) that scale across complex, AI-powered experiences\n    \n    - Push both the architecture and the implementation of the system: shape component APIs, token structure, theming, and composition patterns alongside engineering, not downstream of it\n    \n    - Advocate for technical approaches with confidence, especially in new or ambiguous territory where established patterns don't yet exist\n    \n    - Embed accessibility, responsiveness, and performance into the system by default\n    \n    - Establish clear contribution, governance, and deprecation models that balance velocity with system integrity\n    \n    - Raise the bar for system quality across the product through design reviews, critique, and hands-on work\n    \n    - Build alignment across Design, Engineering, and Product through technical direction and collaboration\n    \n    - Anticipate future product and platform needs, evolving the system proactively as Harvey scales\n\n 2. Own AI design and implementation workflows for the design team, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI\n    \n    - Establish in-code prototyping patterns that make it easier to be innovative and consistent as designers increasingly leverage IDEs to experiment and ship.\n    \n    - Define AI-assisted design and implementation workflows, establishing best practices for prototyping and shipping with AI\n    \n    - Document system usage and best practices in a way that is clear, practical, and trusted by product teams\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years (Senior) / 8+ years (Staff) of product design experience, with significant ownership of design systems in complex product environments\n\n - A design portfolio that demonstrates high design craft in system-level thinking, but a strong point of view on quality, and visual cohesion\n\n - Deep design systems expertise, including an understanding of the history and evolution of the discipline. You know why the field moved from style guides to tokens to composable architectures, and you have a point of view on what comes next\n\n - Excellent design engineering communication: you articulate system decisions and tradeoffs fluently to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners\n\n - Ability to clearly articulate system decisions and tradeoffs to designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners\n\n - Strong knowledge of scalable system architecture and component implementation: component API design, design tokens, theming strategies, and how systems hold up across teams and codebases\n\n - Design Engineer experience preferred, but not required in an AI-first world where the boundary between design and engineering is shifting\n\n - High ownership: you treat the system as a product, not a ticket queue\n\n - Strong opinions, loosely held, being comfortable challenging conventions and evolving best practices as the discipline changes\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguous problem spaces and bringing structure where it doesn't yet exist\n   \n   \n\n\nWHY DESIGN SYSTEMS MATTER AT HARVEY\n\nHarvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$205,760 - $315,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$205,760 – $315,000 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$205,760 - $315,000","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ed72e2dc-de7f-45f3-86ef-541f8db1755b","tierSummary":"$205,760 – $315,000 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7ffc1975-fca6-4902-833e-7ad450b74f67","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"dc8b9c48-d904-4125-a327-4bc9aa8dc9fd","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1e2cf260-ee4d-472b-8541-f03d92dbe7c1","summary":"$205,760 – $315,000","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205760,"maxValue":315000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205760,"maxValue":315000}]}},{"id":"9ea6dcda-7869-4181-b493-2822bbc14097","title":"Technical Program Manager, Developer Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-17T19:34:54.954+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9ea6dcda-7869-4181-b493-2822bbc14097","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9ea6dcda-7869-4181-b493-2822bbc14097/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Technical Program Manager, Quality and Reliability</strong> to champion cross-functional initiatives that enhance the quality, reliability, and operational excellence at Harvey. You will be the ultimate owner of Harvey’s product quality. You will collaborate closely with Engineering, Product, and Operation teams to identify and address critical gaps in test coverage, release safety, incident management, and system observability. You will discover reliability risks and partner with Platform teams to drive broad improvements, focusing on building repeatable, scalable reliability guardrails as Harvey navigates hyper-growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own release management end-to-end, ensuring on-time, high-quality product releases through coordination across all teams in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce and enforce change safety standards, such as risk assessments, rollback procedures, feature flag, and bug bashes to reduce regressions and customer impact.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead horizontal reliability initiatives focused on improving test coverage, observability, and incident response readiness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define, measure, and report on reliability metrics (e.g. change failure rate, MTTR, SLI), and drive accountability for sustained improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify systemic gaps in release processes, testing, monitoring, and incident response; convert findings into structured improvement plans with clear owners and timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive rapid triage and resolution of customer-reported issues in partnership with Product and User Operations, ensuring timely followup and continuous improvements.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and improve the incident management lifecycle: Facilitate rigorous post-incident reviews, ensuring root causes are identified and corrective and preventative actions are tracked to completion..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee vendor reliability and SLA compliance, including performance monitoring, incident escalation, and periodic business reviews.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in technical program management or release management, ideally within SaaS or fast-moving tech companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior Experience working as Software QA or Test Engineer, preferably with SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of engineering workflows, including CI/CD, release cycles, and infrastructure planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with engineering and product leadership to achieve cross-team quality and reliability objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills—you can distill complexity into clarity for both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building systems and processes that scale with growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort in ambiguity and eagerness to build structure where there is none.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with incident management tooling (PagerDuty, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Incident.io\">Incident.io</a>), monitoring stacks (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana), and test automation frameworks (Playwright, Cypress, Selenium)</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,00 - $275,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Technical Program Manager, Quality and Reliability to champion cross-functional initiatives that enhance the quality, reliability, and operational excellence at Harvey. You will be the ultimate owner of Harvey’s product quality. You will collaborate closely with Engineering, Product, and Operation teams to identify and address critical gaps in test coverage, release safety, incident management, and system observability. You will discover reliability risks and partner with Platform teams to drive broad improvements, focusing on building repeatable, scalable reliability guardrails as Harvey navigates hyper-growth.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own release management end-to-end, ensuring on-time, high-quality product releases through coordination across all teams in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Introduce and enforce change safety standards, such as risk assessments, rollback procedures, feature flag, and bug bashes to reduce regressions and customer impact.\n\n - Lead horizontal reliability initiatives focused on improving test coverage, observability, and incident response readiness.\n\n - Define, measure, and report on reliability metrics (e.g. change failure rate, MTTR, SLI), and drive accountability for sustained improvement.\n\n - Identify systemic gaps in release processes, testing, monitoring, and incident response; convert findings into structured improvement plans with clear owners and timelines.\n\n - Drive rapid triage and resolution of customer-reported issues in partnership with Product and User Operations, ensuring timely followup and continuous improvements.\n\n - Own and improve the incident management lifecycle: Facilitate rigorous post-incident reviews, ensuring root causes are identified and corrective and preventative actions are tracked to completion..\n\n - Oversee vendor reliability and SLA compliance, including performance monitoring, incident escalation, and periodic business reviews.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in technical program management or release management, ideally within SaaS or fast-moving tech companies\n\n - Prior Experience working as Software QA or Test Engineer, preferably with SaaS products.\n\n - Strong understanding of engineering workflows, including CI/CD, release cycles, and infrastructure planning.\n\n - Experience partnering with engineering and product leadership to achieve cross-team quality and reliability objectives.\n\n - Excellent communication skills—you can distill complexity into clarity for both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n - A track record of building systems and processes that scale with growth.\n\n - Comfort in ambiguity and eagerness to build structure where there is none.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field.\n\n - Bonus Points\n   \n   - Familiarity with incident management tooling (PagerDuty, Incident.io http://Incident.io), monitoring stacks (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana), and test automation frameworks (Playwright, Cypress, Selenium)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$200,00 - $275,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $275K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $275K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"51b0b7ce-386f-4945-8c4c-0c05a9aa431e","tierSummary":"$200K – $275K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"559afae7-040f-46d3-82a5-098eb8976eef","summary":"$200K – $275K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":275000},{"id":"d40e3967-2671-4f69-9cd4-f5aa4c03a012","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0fdc5e80-8a2a-43d9-bce6-6d14c1781e53","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":275000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c78db388-c1e6-4587-9f6e-17c3921d5564","title":"IT Operations Analyst ","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T16:32:44.115+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c78db388-c1e6-4587-9f6e-17c3921d5564","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c78db388-c1e6-4587-9f6e-17c3921d5564/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We're seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our San Francisco office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />The IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee from new hires to senior leadership has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.<br />You'll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our San Francisco office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and off boarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, employee-first mindset you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.</p></li></ul><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$109,100 - $163,700</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\">here</a>.<br />#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\nWe're seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our San Francisco office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.\n\n\nThe IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee from new hires to senior leadership has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.\nYou'll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our San Francisco office.\n\n - Support onboarding and off boarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.\n\n - Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.\n\n - Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.\n\n - Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.\n\n - Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.\n\n - Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.\n\n - Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.\n\n - Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.\n\n - Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.\n\n - Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.\n\n - A proactive, employee-first mindset you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.\n\n - Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.\n\n - Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$109,100 - $163,700\n\nDepending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices here https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922.\n#LI-DB1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$109.1K – $163.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$109.1K - $163.7K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"20eb3570-78a4-4fdf-a6a8-06192c044ee6","tierSummary":"$109.1K – $163.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"db69dcf8-84e9-4e23-b9aa-fa947f8bde91","summary":"$109.1K – $163.7K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":163700},{"id":"ffe608f6-7378-4107-975d-bb4d81186d53","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d4486ed4-44b0-4a35-bd22-5dab14361aef","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":163700},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"672f45e7-0689-4a6a-92e4-712beaa2eeca","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-08T20:49:22.410+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/672f45e7-0689-4a6a-92e4-712beaa2eeca","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/672f45e7-0689-4a6a-92e4-712beaa2eeca/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&amp;A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.\n\n - Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.\n\n - Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.\n\n - Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. \n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-BB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8314335b-8b91-4cd8-ba6f-60a69b1f2b12","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"70b52fc0-c23d-4f8f-bc87-7d32c4127f23","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"097da54e-7106-4b77-b950-0804b7389678","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"8f413ec4-68cd-45ee-81b0-b72eebbd3ca3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"49d8247b-b604-4105-a3a6-1bb3373763c6","title":"People Business Partner","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-12T21:46:36.520+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/49d8247b-b604-4105-a3a6-1bb3373763c6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/49d8247b-b604-4105-a3a6-1bb3373763c6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how the world’s best legal professionals work. As we continue to scale, we’re looking for a People Business Partner to support our North America Go-To-Market (GTM) teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll partner closely with GTM leaders across sales, customer success, and Legal Engineering to help them build and scale high-performing teams. You’ll work side-by-side with leaders as they navigate growth, develop their organizations, and handle the people challenges that come with a fast-moving environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to the Head of People Business Partners and works closely with leaders across GTM as well as the broader People team. The right person is a thoughtful communicator who builds trust quickly, brings sound judgment to complex situations, and is comfortable operating in an environment where priorities evolve quickly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with GTM leaders.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with GTM leaders as they build and scale their teams - advising on org design, team effectiveness, and performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coach managers and strengthen leadership.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help leaders—from new managers to experienced operators—navigate challenges, develop their teams, and lead with clarity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive performance and accountability.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with managers on performance conversations, feedback, and development planning to ensure teams operate at a high bar.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Navigate complex people matters.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle employee relations situations with care and sound judgment, balancing empathy for individuals with what’s right for the team and the business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stay close to the business.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand what’s happening across the teams you support—surfacing themes, identifying risks early, and helping leaders address issues proactively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help scale our people practices.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Head of PBPs and broader People team to implement and refine programs related to performance, development, and manager effectiveness.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act as a trusted advisor.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide thoughtful guidance to leaders navigating growth, change, and team dynamics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10+ years of experience in a People Business Partner role, ideally supporting GTM teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and the ability to build trust quickly with leaders and employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High emotional intelligence and empathy, especially when navigating sensitive or complex situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment and discretion, particularly when handling employee relations matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coaching and influencing leaders across different levels of an organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in fast-paced, high-growth environments where priorities can evolve quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A thoughtful, pragmatic approach—you bring perspective and ideas but remain adaptable as situations evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work from our New York office at least three days per week.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$170,000 - $230,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how the world’s best legal professionals work. As we continue to scale, we’re looking for a People Business Partner to support our North America Go-To-Market (GTM) teams.\n\nIn this role, you’ll partner closely with GTM leaders across sales, customer success, and Legal Engineering to help them build and scale high-performing teams. You’ll work side-by-side with leaders as they navigate growth, develop their organizations, and handle the people challenges that come with a fast-moving environment.\n\nThis role reports to the Head of People Business Partners and works closely with leaders across GTM as well as the broader People team. The right person is a thoughtful communicator who builds trust quickly, brings sound judgment to complex situations, and is comfortable operating in an environment where priorities evolve quickly.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nPartner with GTM leaders.\n\nWork closely with GTM leaders as they build and scale their teams - advising on org design, team effectiveness, and performance.\n\nCoach managers and strengthen leadership.\n\nHelp leaders—from new managers to experienced operators—navigate challenges, develop their teams, and lead with clarity.\n\nDrive performance and accountability.\n\nPartner with managers on performance conversations, feedback, and development planning to ensure teams operate at a high bar.\n\nNavigate complex people matters.\n\nHandle employee relations situations with care and sound judgment, balancing empathy for individuals with what’s right for the team and the business.\n\nStay close to the business.\n\nUnderstand what’s happening across the teams you support—surfacing themes, identifying risks early, and helping leaders address issues proactively.\n\nHelp scale our people practices.\n\nPartner with the Head of PBPs and broader People team to implement and refine programs related to performance, development, and manager effectiveness.\n\nAct as a trusted advisor.\n\nProvide thoughtful guidance to leaders navigating growth, change, and team dynamics.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or related field.\n\n - 6–10+ years of experience in a People Business Partner role, ideally supporting GTM teams.\n\n - Strong communication skills and the ability to build trust quickly with leaders and employees.\n\n - High emotional intelligence and empathy, especially when navigating sensitive or complex situations.\n\n - Excellent judgment and discretion, particularly when handling employee relations matters.\n\n - Experience coaching and influencing leaders across different levels of an organization.\n\n - Comfort operating in fast-paced, high-growth environments where priorities can evolve quickly.\n\n - A thoughtful, pragmatic approach—you bring perspective and ideas but remain adaptable as situations evolve.\n\n - Ability to work from our New York office at least three days per week.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$170,000 - $230,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$170K – $230K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$170K - $230K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0e4b28a1-353f-4277-a598-67d340700bb5","tierSummary":"$170K – $230K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d98765cd-b93b-41b9-993f-abad2e148b54","summary":"$170K – $230K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":170000,"maxValue":230000},{"id":"26b47e80-011a-4c33-b82c-9cfdbfae4cb3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d505eba2-25be-4e8d-96b3-a2c4827ca85f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":170000,"maxValue":230000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f47e1925-2a89-4264-8a1b-09cd9215f4dd","title":"Senior Software Engineer, AI Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-12T00:24:19.429+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f47e1925-2a89-4264-8a1b-09cd9215f4dd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f47e1925-2a89-4264-8a1b-09cd9215f4dd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Context Engineering &amp; Agent Infrastructure.</strong> Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Model Integration &amp; Routing.</strong> Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluation Infrastructure.</strong> Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Abstractions.</strong> Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering. Staff candidates will typically have 8+ years and a track record of technical leadership across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $300,000</p><h1></h1><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.\n\nThe AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Context Engineering & Agent Infrastructure. Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.\n\n - Model Integration & Routing. Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.\n\n - Evaluation Infrastructure. Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.\n\n - Shared Abstractions. Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.\n\n - Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.\n\n - Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.\n\n - Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.\n\n - Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering. Staff candidates will typically have 8+ years and a track record of technical leadership across teams.\n\n - Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.\n\n - Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.\n\n - A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.\n\n - Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.\n\n - Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.\n\n - A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.\n\n - Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $300,000\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$185K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$185K - $325K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"76e64715-a115-4096-916b-68cf945d34e0","tierSummary":"$185K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8f7068e4-0999-4e96-aa72-90d7aaa814bb","summary":"$185K – $325K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":185000,"maxValue":325000},{"id":"b051f99d-cff3-4cb3-a43b-2da106582656","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"79fc1274-30a2-40fa-a1d8-1c7ecbd18b7e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":185000,"maxValue":325000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"313d5aa8-bfc9-4057-b9a3-b73b4894f6a7","title":"Staff Database Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-20T22:09:46.679+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/313d5aa8-bfc9-4057-b9a3-b73b4894f6a7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/313d5aa8-bfc9-4057-b9a3-b73b4894f6a7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Database Engineer on the Engineering team at Harvey, you will define how our database infrastructure operates and evolves across our legal AI platform. Harvey runs a global fleet of PostgreSQL databases spanning multiple regions and availability zones. You’ll own the technical strategy for this fleet—setting the standards for migration governance, driving architecture decisions for multi-region scaling, and establishing the operational practices that keep our data layer reliable as we grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a leadership role with deep hands-on expectations. You’ll partner directly with Principal and Staff Engineers on infrastructure roadmap decisions while also being the person who can diagnose a replication lag spike at 2am. You’ll build the migration review framework, define the tooling strategy, and raise the bar for how the entire engineering organization thinks about database safety and performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Migration Governance –</strong> Own the migration governance framework end-to-end—design the review workflow, CI gate checks, automated rollback procedures, and fleet-wide deployment sequencing that makes safe migrations the default across the org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architecture &amp; Scaling –</strong> Drive the technical strategy for Harvey’s global database fleet—multi-region replication design, capacity planning, sharding and partitioning approaches, and fleet-wide observability as we scale into new markets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reliability &amp; Performance –</strong> Own database reliability and performance at the fleet level—monitoring replication health, optimizing query performance, tuning vacuum and connection management, and building the alerting that gives us confidence across all production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Platform &amp; Tooling –</strong> Build self-service tooling and developer guardrails—migration dry-runs, schema diff previews, automated health checks, performance regression detection—so engineering teams can move fast without bottlenecking on a single DBA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Incident Leadership –</strong> Lead database incident response and drive systemic improvements—triage production issues, run post-incident reviews, and turn lessons learned into durable process and tooling fixes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Even Better If You Can:</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security &amp; Compliance –</strong> Partner with Security and Compliance to design and enforce data-layer controls for SOC 2, GDPR, and data residency requirements—access controls, audit logging, encryption standards, and data lifecycle policies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Partnership –</strong> Represent database engineering in vendor evaluations, build-vs-buy decisions, and technology strategy discussions with engineering leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Building –</strong> Shape the database engineering function at Harvey—define the operating model, set the hiring bar, mentor engineers on database best practices, and build the culture where teams proactively think about data safety</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of hands-on experience in database administration, database reliability engineering, or infrastructure engineering with PostgreSQL as your primary database, with demonstrated staff-level scope—you’ve set standards across teams, not just operated within one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert-level PostgreSQL knowledge (required)—WAL mechanics, vacuum tuning, logical and physical replication, partitioning strategies, and the ability to debug production issues others can’t. PostgreSQL is our core database and deep fluency is non-negotiable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building migration governance systems—not just reviewing migrations, but designing the frameworks, tooling, and organizational processes that make safe migrations the default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience architecting database infrastructure for multi-region, high-availability environments—replication topologies, failover automation, and data consistency trade-offs at fleet scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep fluency with database observability—you’ve built monitoring strategies using Datadog, pganalyze, or custom instrumentation, and you know which metrics actually predict incidents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading database major version upgrades (e.g., PostgreSQL 14 → 16) or sharding initiatives in production with zero downtime</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to influence technical direction across teams without direct authority—you’ve written RFCs, set standards, and changed how an engineering organization thinks about database operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with cloud database services at scale (Azure Database for PostgreSQL, GCP Cloud SQL, or AWS RDS/Aurora) and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communication across audiences—you can present a database architecture decision to the VP of Engineering and explain a migration risk to a junior developer with equal clarity</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong software engineering skills (Python, Go, or similar)—you build production-grade tooling and automation, not one-off scripts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to vector databases, embedding storage, or adjacent systems (Redis, Elasticsearch, Kafka) relevant to AI/ML workloads in regulated industries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background building or leading a database engineering function from scratch — defining the team charter, hiring, and operating model</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$190,720 - $290,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Database Engineer on the Engineering team at Harvey, you will define how our database infrastructure operates and evolves across our legal AI platform. Harvey runs a global fleet of PostgreSQL databases spanning multiple regions and availability zones. You’ll own the technical strategy for this fleet—setting the standards for migration governance, driving architecture decisions for multi-region scaling, and establishing the operational practices that keep our data layer reliable as we grow.\n\nThis is a leadership role with deep hands-on expectations. You’ll partner directly with Principal and Staff Engineers on infrastructure roadmap decisions while also being the person who can diagnose a replication lag spike at 2am. You’ll build the migration review framework, define the tooling strategy, and raise the bar for how the entire engineering organization thinks about database safety and performance.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Migration Governance – Own the migration governance framework end-to-end—design the review workflow, CI gate checks, automated rollback procedures, and fleet-wide deployment sequencing that makes safe migrations the default across the org\n\n - Architecture & Scaling – Drive the technical strategy for Harvey’s global database fleet—multi-region replication design, capacity planning, sharding and partitioning approaches, and fleet-wide observability as we scale into new markets\n\n - Reliability & Performance – Own database reliability and performance at the fleet level—monitoring replication health, optimizing query performance, tuning vacuum and connection management, and building the alerting that gives us confidence across all production environments\n\n - Platform & Tooling – Build self-service tooling and developer guardrails—migration dry-runs, schema diff previews, automated health checks, performance regression detection—so engineering teams can move fast without bottlenecking on a single DBA\n\n - Incident Leadership – Lead database incident response and drive systemic improvements—triage production issues, run post-incident reviews, and turn lessons learned into durable process and tooling fixes\n\nEven Better If You Can:\n\n - Security & Compliance – Partner with Security and Compliance to design and enforce data-layer controls for SOC 2, GDPR, and data residency requirements—access controls, audit logging, encryption standards, and data lifecycle policies\n\n - Strategic Partnership – Represent database engineering in vendor evaluations, build-vs-buy decisions, and technology strategy discussions with engineering leadership\n\n - Team Building – Shape the database engineering function at Harvey—define the operating model, set the hiring bar, mentor engineers on database best practices, and build the culture where teams proactively think about data safety\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of hands-on experience in database administration, database reliability engineering, or infrastructure engineering with PostgreSQL as your primary database, with demonstrated staff-level scope—you’ve set standards across teams, not just operated within one\n\n - Expert-level PostgreSQL knowledge (required)—WAL mechanics, vacuum tuning, logical and physical replication, partitioning strategies, and the ability to debug production issues others can’t. PostgreSQL is our core database and deep fluency is non-negotiable\n\n - Track record of building migration governance systems—not just reviewing migrations, but designing the frameworks, tooling, and organizational processes that make safe migrations the default\n\n - Experience architecting database infrastructure for multi-region, high-availability environments—replication topologies, failover automation, and data consistency trade-offs at fleet scale\n\n - Deep fluency with database observability—you’ve built monitoring strategies using Datadog, pganalyze, or custom instrumentation, and you know which metrics actually predict incidents\n\n - Experience leading database major version upgrades (e.g., PostgreSQL 14 → 16) or sharding initiatives in production with zero downtime\n\n - Proven ability to influence technical direction across teams without direct authority—you’ve written RFCs, set standards, and changed how an engineering organization thinks about database operations\n\n - Proficiency with cloud database services at scale (Azure Database for PostgreSQL, GCP Cloud SQL, or AWS RDS/Aurora) and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)\n\n - Clear communication across audiences—you can present a database architecture decision to the VP of Engineering and explain a migration risk to a junior developer with equal clarity\n\nBonus\n\n - Strong software engineering skills (Python, Go, or similar)—you build production-grade tooling and automation, not one-off scripts\n\n - Exposure to vector databases, embedding storage, or adjacent systems (Redis, Elasticsearch, Kafka) relevant to AI/ML workloads in regulated industries\n\n - Background building or leading a database engineering function from scratch — defining the team charter, hiring, and operating model\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$190,720 - $290,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$190,720 – $286,080 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$190,720 - $286,080","compensationTiers":[{"id":"623ec02a-d428-4008-900c-dd0b1e8c5628","tierSummary":"$190,720 – $286,080 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ffce07a3-9476-4a05-b947-273dfc388c82","summary":"$190,720 – $286,080","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190720,"maxValue":286080},{"id":"f818b1a5-b216-4b47-83e5-4b56827a5fa5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8d54ef88-9a09-4e4c-9f3f-86585e641bd5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190720,"maxValue":286080},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8ae3a90d-ebf8-4202-96d3-9f74c2737cd7","title":"Head of Customer Success, Enterprise","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-03-20T15:50:05.118+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8ae3a90d-ebf8-4202-96d3-9f74c2737cd7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8ae3a90d-ebf8-4202-96d3-9f74c2737cd7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Head of Customer Success, Enterprise - Americas, you will own the strategy, execution, and outcomes of Harvey's enterprise customer success motion across the United States, Canada, and Latin America. You will lead a team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders, driving value realization for Harvey's largest and most strategic accounts — top law firms and enterprise legal departments — and ensuring they derive maximum, measurable ROI from our AI platform. This is a senior leadership role that reports directly to the VP of Customer Success and requires a builder's mindset: you will define the playbooks, scale the team, and set the standard for what world-class customer success looks like at Harvey across the Americas.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Leadership:</strong> Define and execute the enterprise CS strategy for the Americas, including account segmentation, team structure, success planning, and expansion motions that align to Harvey's revenue and retention goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Building &amp; Development:</strong> Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders. Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, and excellence. Set clear expectations, run effective operating cadences, and manage performance with rigor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Outcomes &amp; Retention:</strong> Own net revenue retention (NRR), adoption, and renewal targets for the Americas enterprise book of business. Partner with Sales leadership to drive expansion and ensure seamless post-sale handoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Build and refine scalable CS processes — onboarding frameworks, QBR cadences, health scoring models, escalation workflows, and renewal playbooks — that enable the team to manage a growing portfolio of enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Partnership:</strong> Serve as the voice of the Americas enterprise customer to Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing. Translate customer feedback into actionable insights that shape the product roadmap and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive Engagement:</strong> Personally engage with C-suite stakeholders at Harvey's most strategic accounts — General Counsels, Chief Knowledge Officers, Managing Partners — to build lasting executive relationships and drive strategic alignment.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in customer success, account management, or strategic consulting, with at least 5 years managing and scaling CS teams in an enterprise SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning and exceeding NRR, adoption, and expansion targets at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and leading teams of 10+ across multiple segments (enterprise, majors) and geographies (US, Canada, LATAM).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and the ability to engage confidently with C-suite legal and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in legal technology, professional services, or selling into law firms and corporate legal departments is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with AI/LLM technology and comfort evangelizing emerging technology to skeptical, risk-averse audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical rigor — you lead with data, build dashboards, and use metrics (adoption rates, health scores, utilization, ARR growth) to drive decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results-driven with the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing demands across a large, complex book of business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder's mentality — you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and are energized by creating structure where none exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how the legal industry operates and evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to shape and scale Harvey's customer success function across an entire region during a period of hyper-growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, high-intensity work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$276,000-$325,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Head of Customer Success, Enterprise - Americas, you will own the strategy, execution, and outcomes of Harvey's enterprise customer success motion across the United States, Canada, and Latin America. You will lead a team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders, driving value realization for Harvey's largest and most strategic accounts — top law firms and enterprise legal departments — and ensuring they derive maximum, measurable ROI from our AI platform. This is a senior leadership role that reports directly to the VP of Customer Success and requires a builder's mindset: you will define the playbooks, scale the team, and set the standard for what world-class customer success looks like at Harvey across the Americas.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Leadership: Define and execute the enterprise CS strategy for the Americas, including account segmentation, team structure, success planning, and expansion motions that align to Harvey's revenue and retention goals.\n\n - Team Building & Development: Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders. Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, and excellence. Set clear expectations, run effective operating cadences, and manage performance with rigor.\n\n - Customer Outcomes & Retention: Own net revenue retention (NRR), adoption, and renewal targets for the Americas enterprise book of business. Partner with Sales leadership to drive expansion and ensure seamless post-sale handoffs.\n\n - Operational Excellence: Build and refine scalable CS processes — onboarding frameworks, QBR cadences, health scoring models, escalation workflows, and renewal playbooks — that enable the team to manage a growing portfolio of enterprise accounts.\n\n - Cross-Functional Partnership: Serve as the voice of the Americas enterprise customer to Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing. Translate customer feedback into actionable insights that shape the product roadmap and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Executive Engagement: Personally engage with C-suite stakeholders at Harvey's most strategic accounts — General Counsels, Chief Knowledge Officers, Managing Partners — to build lasting executive relationships and drive strategic alignment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in customer success, account management, or strategic consulting, with at least 5 years managing and scaling CS teams in an enterprise SaaS environment.\n\n - Proven track record of owning and exceeding NRR, adoption, and expansion targets at scale.\n\n - Deep experience building and leading teams of 10+ across multiple segments (enterprise, majors) and geographies (US, Canada, LATAM).\n\n - Strong executive presence and the ability to engage confidently with C-suite legal and business stakeholders.\n\n - Experience in legal technology, professional services, or selling into law firms and corporate legal departments is strongly preferred.\n\n - Familiarity with AI/LLM technology and comfort evangelizing emerging technology to skeptical, risk-averse audiences.\n\n - Analytical rigor — you lead with data, build dashboards, and use metrics (adoption rates, health scores, utilization, ARR growth) to drive decisions.\n\n - Results-driven with the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing demands across a large, complex book of business.\n\n - A builder's mentality — you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and are energized by creating structure where none exists.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how the legal industry operates and evolves.\n\n - The opportunity to shape and scale Harvey's customer success function across an entire region during a period of hyper-growth.\n\n - A collaborative, high-intensity work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$276,000-$325,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$276K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$276K - $325K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"111c62a8-6b1f-4a63-b950-09d907dcca9d","tierSummary":"$276K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4eaf2cbe-658a-4901-95e9-bdd06d8b5428","summary":"$276K – $325K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":276000,"maxValue":325000},{"id":"e1356f50-1b76-45bc-9346-fde027ed3da7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7002e896-bb94-4898-a3ac-11d5e716c7c7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":276000,"maxValue":325000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"3adf9734-7339-4b21-b361-96288a9a6224","title":"Sales Development Representative (German Speaking)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:41:32.049+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3adf9734-7339-4b21-b361-96288a9a6224","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3adf9734-7339-4b21-b361-96288a9a6224/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h3><strong>Role Overview</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in written and spoken English and German</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.\n\nThis role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.\n\n - Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.\n\n - Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.\n\n - Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.\n\n - Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.\n\n - Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.\n\n - Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.\n\n - Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.\n\n - Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.\n\n\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.\n\n - Fluent in written and spoken English and German\n\n - Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.\n\n - Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.\n\n - Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.\n\n - Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.\n\n - Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KS2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$79.6K – $107.6K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$79.6K - $107.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ec330443-e9ba-4555-8675-dc6fe2259ff0","tierSummary":"$79.6K – $107.6K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d6b568bc-f4f2-42c7-9dd4-4d061448589a","summary":"$79.6K – $107.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":79600,"maxValue":107600}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":79600,"maxValue":107600}]}},{"id":"4a82c276-1113-41f6-baf9-a5be27e5c78f","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Core Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-27T16:49:13.340+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4a82c276-1113-41f6-baf9-a5be27e5c78f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4a82c276-1113-41f6-baf9-a5be27e5c78f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Bengaluru, India.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Representative Projects</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Incident.io\">Incident.io</a>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.\n\nYou'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.\n\nThis role is based in Bengaluru, India.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions\n\n - Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management\n\n - Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues\n\n - Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint\n\n - Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments\n\n - Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership\n\n - Representative Projects\n   \n   - Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration\n   \n   - Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience\n   \n   - Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers\n   \n   - Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking\n   \n   - Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment\n\n - Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems\n\n - Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)\n\n - Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation\n\n - Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale\n\n - Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, Incident.io http://Incident.io)\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence\n   \n   \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems\n\n - Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements\n\n - Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-AS2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2fa7de61-6ca1-4892-822e-bb1d458a7b90","title":"People Business Partner, Product & Design","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-02T20:08:12.118+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2fa7de61-6ca1-4892-822e-bb1d458a7b90","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2fa7de61-6ca1-4892-822e-bb1d458a7b90/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how the world’s best legal professionals work. As we continue to scale, we’re looking for a People Business Partner to support our Product and Design teams, based in San Francisco, with the potential to support additional technical orgs over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll partner closely with Product and Design leaders to help them build and scale high-performing, high-ownership teams. You’ll work side-by-side with leaders as they navigate growth, evolve their org structures, and operate in an environment where priorities shift quickly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to the Head of People Business Partners and works closely with leaders across the technical org as well as the broader People team. The right person brings strong judgment, can quickly build credibility with technical leaders, and is comfortable operating in a fast-moving, often ambiguous environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner deeply with Product and Design leaders</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with leaders as they build and scale their teams, advising on org design, team structure, and how to operate effectively through rapid growth and change.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coach and challenge leaders</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support leaders in navigating complex people and organizational decisions. Provide direct, thoughtful feedback and help raise the bar on leadership across the org.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive performance and accountability</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with managers on performance, feedback, and development, ensuring teams are operating at a high bar and addressing gaps quickly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Navigate complex people situations</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle employee relations matters with sound judgment, balancing empathy for individuals with what’s right for the team and the business.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stay close to the work</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a strong understanding of how Product, Design, and Engineering teams operate, from how decisions are made to where friction exists, and use that context to guide leaders effectively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operate in ambiguity</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help leaders navigate shifting priorities, evolving org structures, and new problem spaces, bringing clarity where things are not yet fully defined.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help scale how we work</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Head of PBPs and broader People team to evolve and implement practices that support high-performing technical teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10+ years of experience in a People Business Partner role, ideally supporting Product, Design, or Engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with technical leaders - you understand how product and engineering organizations operate and can build credibility quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment and the ability to navigate ambiguity -  you’re comfortable operating without perfect information and making decisions in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence and challenge senior leaders in a thoughtful and direct way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting org design, performance management, and team scaling in high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High emotional intelligence and strong communication skills, especially in complex or sensitive situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A pragmatic, no-drama approach - you focus on what works for the business and move things forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work from our San Francisco office at least three days per week.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$165,400 - $248,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how the world’s best legal professionals work. As we continue to scale, we’re looking for a People Business Partner to support our Product and Design teams, based in San Francisco, with the potential to support additional technical orgs over time.\n\nIn this role, you’ll partner closely with Product and Design leaders to help them build and scale high-performing, high-ownership teams. You’ll work side-by-side with leaders as they navigate growth, evolve their org structures, and operate in an environment where priorities shift quickly.\n\nThis role reports to the Head of People Business Partners and works closely with leaders across the technical org as well as the broader People team. The right person brings strong judgment, can quickly build credibility with technical leaders, and is comfortable operating in a fast-moving, often ambiguous environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nPartner deeply with Product and Design leaders\n\n - Work closely with leaders as they build and scale their teams, advising on org design, team structure, and how to operate effectively through rapid growth and change.\n\nCoach and challenge leaders\n\n - Support leaders in navigating complex people and organizational decisions. Provide direct, thoughtful feedback and help raise the bar on leadership across the org.\n\nDrive performance and accountability\n\n - Partner with managers on performance, feedback, and development, ensuring teams are operating at a high bar and addressing gaps quickly.\n\nNavigate complex people situations\n\n - Handle employee relations matters with sound judgment, balancing empathy for individuals with what’s right for the team and the business.\n\nStay close to the work\n\n - Develop a strong understanding of how Product, Design, and Engineering teams operate, from how decisions are made to where friction exists, and use that context to guide leaders effectively.\n\nOperate in ambiguity\n\n - Help leaders navigate shifting priorities, evolving org structures, and new problem spaces, bringing clarity where things are not yet fully defined.\n\nHelp scale how we work\n\n - Partner with the Head of PBPs and broader People team to evolve and implement practices that support high-performing technical teams.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6–10+ years of experience in a People Business Partner role, ideally supporting Product, Design, or Engineering teams.\n\n - Experience working with technical leaders - you understand how product and engineering organizations operate and can build credibility quickly.\n\n - Strong judgment and the ability to navigate ambiguity -  you’re comfortable operating without perfect information and making decisions in real time.\n\n - Ability to influence and challenge senior leaders in a thoughtful and direct way.\n\n - Experience supporting org design, performance management, and team scaling in high-growth environments.\n\n - High emotional intelligence and strong communication skills, especially in complex or sensitive situations.\n\n - A pragmatic, no-drama approach - you focus on what works for the business and move things forward.\n\n - Ability to work from our San Francisco office at least three days per week.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$165,400 - $248,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$165.4K – $248.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$165.4K - $248.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d5d230bc-cf75-4327-a453-9925f6ffc442","tierSummary":"$165.4K – $248.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9691d008-5ada-4996-b3f1-ed38d2b5351d","summary":"$165.4K – $248.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":165400,"maxValue":248200},{"id":"4358542f-f267-4704-aa7c-59b1681c1eb4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"28961f9a-988e-4b26-b496-8d84971d3f17","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":165400,"maxValue":248200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"78c71402-02bf-4533-99c6-10c1bad10b02","title":"Technical Account Manager, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:08:43.478+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/78c71402-02bf-4533-99c6-10c1bad10b02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/78c71402-02bf-4533-99c6-10c1bad10b02/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its customer offerings for strategic customers, we are hiring a Technical Account Manager to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent support resource for Harvey’s most strategic customers, providing rapid, expert handling of complex, time-critical, and sensitive issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technical Account Manager strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a primary escalation point for Enterprise and Majors accounts, owning high-severity and technically complex support cases through resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams. Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its customer offerings for strategic customers, we are hiring a Technical Account Manager to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent support resource for Harvey’s most strategic customers, providing rapid, expert handling of complex, time-critical, and sensitive issues.\n\nThe Technical Account Manager strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as a primary escalation point for Enterprise and Majors accounts, owning high-severity and technically complex support cases through resolution.\n\n - Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.\n\n - Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.\n\n - Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.\n\n - Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.\n\n - Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.\n\n - Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.\n\n - Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.\n\n - Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases\n\n - Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams. Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers\n\n - Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.\n\n - Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.\n\n - Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.\n\n - Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.\n\n - Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.\n\n - Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"22635945-1052-45e7-9b13-f94aabce8e9b","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Full Stack","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T14:53:01.197+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/22635945-1052-45e7-9b13-f94aabce8e9b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/22635945-1052-45e7-9b13-f94aabce8e9b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $314,350 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$231,000 - $314,350 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-NG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231,000 – $314,350 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231,000 - $314,350","compensationTiers":[{"id":"87924692-a6b7-407f-bbf0-b4d5e2f770e5","tierSummary":"$231,000 – $314,350 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"625edfb8-6bc6-4084-b4e6-1539c95ea5eb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d7e4c2eb-a4fa-440b-8042-96de3149ab74","summary":"$231,000 – $314,350","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":314350},{"id":"54d818b2-d7b4-44ab-83f5-241713bd9152","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":314350},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9ab52bf5-0d83-418a-bf03-e7dd75359473","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market - Munich","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T13:49:41.610+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9ab52bf5-0d83-418a-bf03-e7dd75359473","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9ab52bf5-0d83-418a-bf03-e7dd75359473/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. As part of the founding Mid Market team in Munich, you will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients across DACH, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in English and German, both spoken and written</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. As part of the founding Mid Market team in Munich, you will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients across DACH, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Fluency in English and German, both spoken and written\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-KS2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3ea5e27b-0efc-4338-9bf0-292dd49736ab","title":"Manager, Sales Development","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-15T20:45:58.965+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3ea5e27b-0efc-4338-9bf0-292dd49736ab","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3ea5e27b-0efc-4338-9bf0-292dd49736ab/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is looking for a driven, strategic, and entrepreneurial Sales Development Manager to lead and scale a team of SDR team in New York. This person will be responsible for building a high-performing team that generates pipeline across leading law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own hiring, onboarding, coaching, and performance management while partnering closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to build a scalable pipeline generation engine. You'll also help shape Harvey's go-to-market strategy by refining targeting, messaging, and outbound programs that resonate with the North American legal market.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're excited by the idea of building teams, developing talent, and driving impact at a fast-growing AI company transforming legal work, we'd love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own pipeline performance:</strong> Drive the SDR team's contribution to pipeline generation across inbound and outbound channels, ensuring strong alignment with sales targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and scale the team:</strong> Hire, onboard, and develop a high-performing SDR team, helping establish the structure, operating cadence, and performance standards for the New York market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coach and develop SDRs:</strong> Deliver hands-on coaching through regular 1:1s, call reviews, and deal strategy sessions to accelerate rep development and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design onboarding and enablement:</strong> Partner with GTM enablement to create onboarding and ongoing training programs that ramp SDRs quickly and build strong product, industry, and prospecting expertise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally:</strong> Collaborate closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to improve lead routing, campaign effectiveness, and pipeline conversion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Refine targeting and messaging:</strong> Continuously test and improve outbound strategies, messaging, and account targeting based on ICP fit and performance insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leverage data and tools:</strong> Use platforms such as Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong, and ZoomInfo to track team performance and optimize workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build a strong team culture:</strong> Foster a high-performance culture grounded in ownership, learning, and collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in SaaS sales or business development, with at least 1–2 years of direct SDR or BDR leadership experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success in building and managing pipeline-generating teams in a high-growth, outbound-focused environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of modern sales development tools (e.g., Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A data-driven mindset with the ability to analyze team performance, uncover insights, and iterate quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building SDR processes from scratch—comfortable in ambiguity and excited to be the architect of something new.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A coaching-first leadership style: you invest in people, celebrate wins, and hold high standards with care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and executive presence—both internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for AI, innovation, and the transformation of knowledge work—especially in professional services and legal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence tech stack decisions—develop recommendations and drive implementation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal or professional services firms is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$195,400-$260,000 80/20 OTE</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is looking for a driven, strategic, and entrepreneurial Sales Development Manager to lead and scale a team of SDR team in New York. This person will be responsible for building a high-performing team that generates pipeline across leading law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams.\n\nYou will own hiring, onboarding, coaching, and performance management while partnering closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to build a scalable pipeline generation engine. You'll also help shape Harvey's go-to-market strategy by refining targeting, messaging, and outbound programs that resonate with the North American legal market.\n\nIf you're excited by the idea of building teams, developing talent, and driving impact at a fast-growing AI company transforming legal work, we'd love to meet you.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\n - Own pipeline performance: Drive the SDR team's contribution to pipeline generation across inbound and outbound channels, ensuring strong alignment with sales targets.\n\n - Build and scale the team: Hire, onboard, and develop a high-performing SDR team, helping establish the structure, operating cadence, and performance standards for the New York market.\n\n - Coach and develop SDRs: Deliver hands-on coaching through regular 1:1s, call reviews, and deal strategy sessions to accelerate rep development and performance.\n\n - Design onboarding and enablement: Partner with GTM enablement to create onboarding and ongoing training programs that ramp SDRs quickly and build strong product, industry, and prospecting expertise.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally: Collaborate closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to improve lead routing, campaign effectiveness, and pipeline conversion.\n\n - Refine targeting and messaging: Continuously test and improve outbound strategies, messaging, and account targeting based on ICP fit and performance insights.\n\n - Leverage data and tools: Use platforms such as Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong, and ZoomInfo to track team performance and optimize workflows.\n\n - Build a strong team culture: Foster a high-performance culture grounded in ownership, learning, and collaboration.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in SaaS sales or business development, with at least 1–2 years of direct SDR or BDR leadership experience.\n\n - Proven success in building and managing pipeline-generating teams in a high-growth, outbound-focused environment.\n\n - Deep understanding of modern sales development tools (e.g., Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong).\n\n - A data-driven mindset with the ability to analyze team performance, uncover insights, and iterate quickly.\n\n - Experience building SDR processes from scratch—comfortable in ambiguity and excited to be the architect of something new.\n\n - A coaching-first leadership style: you invest in people, celebrate wins, and hold high standards with care.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and executive presence—both internally and externally.\n\n - Passion for AI, innovation, and the transformation of knowledge work—especially in professional services and legal.\n\n - Ability to influence tech stack decisions—develop recommendations and drive implementation.\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal or professional services firms is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$195,400-$260,000 80/20 OTE\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$195.4K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • 80/20 OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$195.4K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ed23e8bf-b5ef-4969-a77a-9ab101146413","tierSummary":"$195.4K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • 80/20 OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"80/20 OTE","components":[{"id":"2583f74b-7893-46fc-a883-538423148528","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7123f74e-7ccb-45c5-8deb-dcaf3603eb51","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f1e0bc8b-73c7-4826-8cda-80c3d6467c9f","summary":"$195.4K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":195400,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":195400,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"302a0914-2763-4e16-b044-b54de4367808","title":"Legal Engineering Manager, APAC","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T08:00:08.418+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/302a0914-2763-4e16-b044-b54de4367808","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/302a0914-2763-4e16-b044-b54de4367808/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey scales its pre-sales function across APAC, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager to lead and grow the team in Singapore. This role exists to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Legal Engineers who sit at the heart of Harvey's commercial motion - bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to law firm and in-house prospects.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms or in-house teams who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and STI companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a team of Legal Engineers, setting clear performance expectations and building a high-trust, high-output team culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the quality and consistency of Harvey's pre-sales legal engineering function, ensuring demos, discovery conversations, and deal support are delivered to the highest standard</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Account Executives and GTM leadership to prioritise, develop deal strategy, and support conversion on complex or strategic opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with lawyers at prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product and Marketing to ensure the team's field insights are feeding into positioning, roadmap, and go-to-market strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h3><strong> Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey scales its pre-sales function across APAC, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager to lead and grow the team in Singapore. This role exists to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Legal Engineers who sit at the heart of Harvey's commercial motion - bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to law firm and in-house prospects.\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms or in-house teams who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and STI companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.\n\nSimilar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a team of Legal Engineers, setting clear performance expectations and building a high-trust, high-output team culture\n\n - Own the quality and consistency of Harvey's pre-sales legal engineering function, ensuring demos, discovery conversations, and deal support are delivered to the highest standard\n\n - Partner closely with Account Executives and GTM leadership to prioritise, develop deal strategy, and support conversion on complex or strategic opportunities\n\n - Engage with lawyers at prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges\n\n - Collaborate with Product and Marketing to ensure the team's field insights are feeding into positioning, roadmap, and go-to-market strategy\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach\n\n\n\n\n\n PLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n \n\n#LI-GE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d78083d9-a203-4ae4-b4b9-454d65df3702","title":"Research Engineer, Post-Training","department":"Engineering","team":"AI Labs","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-26T22:34:50.803+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d78083d9-a203-4ae4-b4b9-454d65df3702","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d78083d9-a203-4ae4-b4b9-454d65df3702/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Post-training is how Harvey turns expert feedback and agent traces into models that are meaningfully better at legal work. We are looking for a research engineer who can help scale that loop: defining and running model training experiments, interpreting results, and working with internal and external research partners to build better data, environments, graders, and training recipes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for someone who can self-manage model training and applied research projects. You will work closely with internal and external research collaborators on post-training efforts that matter to our product roadmap. The ideal candidate has extensive hands-on experience training open weight models, either in a research or production setting, and enough engineering depth to run and debug experiments efficiently.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive post-training experiments, pushing agent performance while navigating the Pareto frontier of cost, latency, security, and governance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent harnesses, including domain-specific skills, tools, subagents, retrieval strategies, and validation loops that improve quality on long-horizon legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and develop grading and reward systems that are reliable enough for evaluation, efficient enough for iteration, and strict enough for high-stakes legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Study agent behavior, identifying patterns that correlate with successful work product, and converting those findings into training data, evals, or harness changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Harvey researchers and external research partners to define experiments, evaluate methodology, review results, and keep projects moving toward concrete model improvements.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with post-training or model-training work, such as SFT, preference optimization, RLHF/RLAIF, reward modeling, distillation, or adapting open-weight models to specialized domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about model behavior: you can read traces, inspect outputs, identify failure modes, and reason about whether a metric is measuring the thing that matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Python and research-engineering ability. You can write clean code, debug experiments, and build the simple but reliable systems needed to make research move faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to self-manage ambiguous applied research projects and communicate clearly with researchers, engineers, product teams, domain experts, and external partners.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building data or evaluation infrastructure for ML workflows, such as dataset curation pipelines, model-output processing, experiment tracking, evaluation dashboards, or regression analysis tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with distributed training, inference systems, GPU workloads, or large-scale ML experimentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research publications, open-source contributions, or shipped industry work in LLMs, agents, evaluation, or ML systems.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nPost-training is how Harvey turns expert feedback and agent traces into models that are meaningfully better at legal work. We are looking for a research engineer who can help scale that loop: defining and running model training experiments, interpreting results, and working with internal and external research partners to build better data, environments, graders, and training recipes.\n\n\n\nThis role is for someone who can self-manage model training and applied research projects. You will work closely with internal and external research collaborators on post-training efforts that matter to our product roadmap. The ideal candidate has extensive hands-on experience training open weight models, either in a research or production setting, and enough engineering depth to run and debug experiments efficiently.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Drive post-training experiments, pushing agent performance while navigating the Pareto frontier of cost, latency, security, and governance.\n\n - Optimize agent harnesses, including domain-specific skills, tools, subagents, retrieval strategies, and validation loops that improve quality on long-horizon legal work.\n\n - Design and develop grading and reward systems that are reliable enough for evaluation, efficient enough for iteration, and strict enough for high-stakes legal work.\n\n - Study agent behavior, identifying patterns that correlate with successful work product, and converting those findings into training data, evals, or harness changes.\n\n - Work with Harvey researchers and external research partners to define experiments, evaluate methodology, review results, and keep projects moving toward concrete model improvements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Hands-on experience with post-training or model-training work, such as SFT, preference optimization, RLHF/RLAIF, reward modeling, distillation, or adapting open-weight models to specialized domains.\n\n - Strong judgment about model behavior: you can read traces, inspect outputs, identify failure modes, and reason about whether a metric is measuring the thing that matters.\n\n - Strong Python and research-engineering ability. You can write clean code, debug experiments, and build the simple but reliable systems needed to make research move faster.\n\n - Ability to self-manage ambiguous applied research projects and communicate clearly with researchers, engineers, product teams, domain experts, and external partners.\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience building data or evaluation infrastructure for ML workflows, such as dataset curation pipelines, model-output processing, experiment tracking, evaluation dashboards, or regression analysis tooling.\n\n - Experience with distributed training, inference systems, GPU workloads, or large-scale ML experimentation.\n\n - Research publications, open-source contributions, or shipped industry work in LLMs, agents, evaluation, or ML systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"157eadc0-b23e-42fc-9745-7680f5678974","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"823c83f4-7b05-4948-b5fc-d360499bf3b8","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4257580e-cb14-46df-ae32-cc47a2b8560b","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"bc0dd4c1-31cf-465d-abeb-8d1d0bb834b3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"992183a0-4526-4ea6-be3d-799a2401da4f","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-21T16:11:11.049+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/992183a0-4526-4ea6-be3d-799a2401da4f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/992183a0-4526-4ea6-be3d-799a2401da4f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.\n\n - Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.\n\n - Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.\n\n - Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.\n\n - Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.\n\n - Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.\n\n - Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.\n\n - Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).\n\n - Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)\n\n - Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.\n\n - Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.\n\n - Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-DM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"49a7d953-df6f-4f03-83b4-49e3b641c5eb","title":"Legal Engineer Manager, Product Specialist, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-08T15:38:25.132+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/49a7d953-df6f-4f03-83b4-49e3b641c5eb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/49a7d953-df6f-4f03-83b4-49e3b641c5eb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey scales its post-sales function across EMEA, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager - Product Specialist to lead and grow the Product Specialist team in London. This role was created to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Product Specialists who support existing customers in maximising their use of the Harvey platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows - driving adoption, increasing utilisation, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel, serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineer - Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a team of Legal Engineers - Product Specialists, providing coaching, performance management, and career development support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the post-implementation customer relationship from a legal engineering perspective, ensuring law firm and in-house clients are effectively onboarded, trained, and supported on an ongoing basis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the senior escalation point for complex or strategic customer engagements, bringing deep product and legal expertise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Account Management and Sales to identify expansion opportunities, support renewals, and contribute to retention strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Product team to surface customer feedback, advocate for platform improvements, and keep the team informed of new features and roadmap developments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and iterate on team processes, playbooks, and frameworks to build a scalable and high-performing function</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience managing or mentoring a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey scales its post-sales function across EMEA, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager - Product Specialist to lead and grow the Product Specialist team in London. This role was created to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Product Specialists who support existing customers in maximising their use of the Harvey platform.\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialists are experienced lawyers from top-tier firms who leverage their legal expertise to help customers seamlessly integrate Harvey into their daily workflows - driving adoption, increasing utilisation, and supporting long-term expansion and renewal. Legal Engineer - Product Specialists collaborate closely with Harvey’s Customer Success Managers to drive all facets of the post-sales strategy. They develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel, serving as trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency.\n\nLegal Engineer - Product Specialists draw on their legal training and practice experience to ask thoughtful questions, uncover adoption barriers, and develop tailored strategies that build credibility with customers. They partner with Customer Success Managers to communicate Harvey’s value through a mix of large group sessions, small workshops, and one-on-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead and develop a team of Legal Engineers - Product Specialists, providing coaching, performance management, and career development support.\n\n - Own the post-implementation customer relationship from a legal engineering perspective, ensuring law firm and in-house clients are effectively onboarded, trained, and supported on an ongoing basis\n\n - Act as the senior escalation point for complex or strategic customer engagements, bringing deep product and legal expertise\n\n - Partner with Account Management and Sales to identify expansion opportunities, support renewals, and contribute to retention strategy\n\n - Collaborate with the Product team to surface customer feedback, advocate for platform improvements, and keep the team informed of new features and roadmap developments\n\n - Define and iterate on team processes, playbooks, and frameworks to build a scalable and high-performing function\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment\n\n - Prior experience managing or mentoring a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2c0285e9-69d6-4cfe-842f-7199bbdfd692","title":"Legal Engineer Manager, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-10T15:29:20.435+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2c0285e9-69d6-4cfe-842f-7199bbdfd692","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2c0285e9-69d6-4cfe-842f-7199bbdfd692/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey scales its pre-sales function across EMEA, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager to lead and grow the team in London. This role exists to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Legal Engineers who sit at the heart of Harvey's commercial motion - bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to law firm and in-house prospects.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a team of Legal Engineers, setting clear performance expectations and building a high-trust, high-output team culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the quality and consistency of Harvey's pre-sales legal engineering function, ensuring demos, discovery conversations, and deal support are delivered to the highest standard</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Account Executives and GTM leadership to prioritise pipeline, develop deal strategy, and support conversion on complex or strategic opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with lawyers at prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product and Marketing to ensure the team's field insights are feeding into positioning, roadmap, and go-to-market strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey scales its pre-sales function across EMEA, we are hiring a Legal Engineer Manager to lead and grow the team in London. This role exists to provide senior leadership and strategic direction to a team of Legal Engineers who sit at the heart of Harvey's commercial motion - bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to law firm and in-house prospects.\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.\n\nSimilar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a team of Legal Engineers, setting clear performance expectations and building a high-trust, high-output team culture\n\n - Own the quality and consistency of Harvey's pre-sales legal engineering function, ensuring demos, discovery conversations, and deal support are delivered to the highest standard\n\n - Partner closely with Account Executives and GTM leadership to prioritise pipeline, develop deal strategy, and support conversion on complex or strategic opportunities\n\n - Engage with lawyers at prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges\n\n - Collaborate with Product and Marketing to ensure the team's field insights are feeding into positioning, roadmap, and go-to-market strategy\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, with experience in a law firm or in-house legal environment\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with an ability to quickly develop and demonstrate platform expertise\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders at law firms and in-house legal teams\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running training, workshops, or client-facing product sessions\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic, solutions-oriented approach\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"45f16834-5b6a-469d-b7ac-94e4e0773e0a","title":"Senior Technical Recruiter, Product & Design","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T20:12:51.652+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/45f16834-5b6a-469d-b7ac-94e4e0773e0a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/45f16834-5b6a-469d-b7ac-94e4e0773e0a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for Senior Technical Recruiter focused on Product &amp; Design. As an early team member, you will work with cross-functional partners to help lay the foundational groundwork for technical hiring in this location. This is a full-cycle recruiting role, where you'll manage the entire recruitment  process; from building pipelines to closing offers.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with technical leadership to deeply understand hiring needs while providing strategic guidance on recruiting best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and nurture a strong pipeline of technical talent to support both current hiring and future growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise hiring managers on market dynamics, compensation insights, and effective talent acquisition strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to streamline recruiting workflows and enhance operational efficiency across the hiring process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure data integrity and accuracy within our Applicant Tracking System (Ashby), maintaining a high standard of system hygiene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and support other team members to elevate overall recruiting performance and execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead strategic sourcing initiatives to engage top-tier, passive candidates across various technical disciplines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally within the company to align recruiting efforts with broader organizational goals</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of full-cycle technical recruiting experience at a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building strong technical teams in a high growth company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Can develop relationships with hiring partners and become a trusted advisor</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knows how to effectively communicate with candidates and be able to efficiently and systematically manage their individual processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You possess low ego and are willing to roll up your sleeves to accomplish our collective goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help mentor other teammates by leading by example and providing guidance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the importance of data and metrics to influence recruiting strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The type of person that keeps up with trends in technology, startups and which companies are the current magnets for top tier talent</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$126,400-$189,600</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for Senior Technical Recruiter focused on Product & Design. As an early team member, you will work with cross-functional partners to help lay the foundational groundwork for technical hiring in this location. This is a full-cycle recruiting role, where you'll manage the entire recruitment  process; from building pipelines to closing offers.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner closely with technical leadership to deeply understand hiring needs while providing strategic guidance on recruiting best practices\n\n - Build and nurture a strong pipeline of technical talent to support both current hiring and future growth\n\n - Advise hiring managers on market dynamics, compensation insights, and effective talent acquisition strategies\n\n - Identify opportunities to streamline recruiting workflows and enhance operational efficiency across the hiring process\n\n - Ensure data integrity and accuracy within our Applicant Tracking System (Ashby), maintaining a high standard of system hygiene\n\n - Mentor and support other team members to elevate overall recruiting performance and execution\n\n - Lead strategic sourcing initiatives to engage top-tier, passive candidates across various technical disciplines\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally within the company to align recruiting efforts with broader organizational goals\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of full-cycle technical recruiting experience at a fast-paced environment\n\n - Proven track record building strong technical teams in a high growth company\n\n - Can develop relationships with hiring partners and become a trusted advisor\n\n - Knows how to effectively communicate with candidates and be able to efficiently and systematically manage their individual processes\n\n - You possess low ego and are willing to roll up your sleeves to accomplish our collective goals\n\n - Help mentor other teammates by leading by example and providing guidance\n\n - Understand the importance of data and metrics to influence recruiting strategies\n\n - The type of person that keeps up with trends in technology, startups and which companies are the current magnets for top tier talent\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$126,400-$189,600\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-ML1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$126.4K – $189.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$126.4K - $189.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2e6e3e6c-da06-4e29-8500-3473b125414e","tierSummary":"$126.4K – $189.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b1958354-ebc5-412e-abcd-fa64ac4da0fe","summary":"$126.4K – $189.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":189600},{"id":"0d0185be-ae23-4fe0-b253-09331994e2d3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1ed18936-8b35-4fc4-838b-27bb43d04553","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":189600},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"af67b63d-b680-4c24-ae6e-3f512cacd98e","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market ","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-30T12:00:32.445+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/af67b63d-b680-4c24-ae6e-3f512cacd98e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/af67b63d-b680-4c24-ae6e-3f512cacd98e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$240,000 OTE 50/50 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts\n\n - Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$240,000 OTE 50/50 Split \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-AB1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$240K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$240K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bef42f9a-8769-4580-bd36-cf7633498cdf","tierSummary":"OTE 50/50 Split $240K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fcac024e-5e54-4934-99ea-2da8f8eccccf","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8fddb798-300a-4137-9caa-c39b865f02d4","summary":"OTE 50/50 Split $240K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}},{"id":"24f9a3fa-476a-490f-87bf-e8cebb7b3928","title":"Frontend Platform Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-28T20:32:43.039+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24f9a3fa-476a-490f-87bf-e8cebb7b3928","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24f9a3fa-476a-490f-87bf-e8cebb7b3928/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for experienced frontend engineers to help build and evolve Harvey’s frontend platform—the systems, tools, and abstractions that enable our engineering team to ship high-quality product experiences quickly and consistently.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This team focuses on developer experience, performance, reliability, and scalability across our frontend stack. Rather than building one-off product features, you’ll create shared foundations that power all of Harvey’s user-facing applications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact role with broad scope across the engineering organization. You’ll work closely with product engineers, design, and infrastructure teams to define and drive the future of frontend development at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve shared frontend infrastructure, including our design system and developer tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to and evolve frontend architecture for scalability and performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve developer experience and engineering velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve application performance and reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product teams to drive adoption of platform systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and reduce friction across the development lifecycle</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience working on large-scale frontend systems or platform-level infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think in systems and abstractions, not just features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of improving developer experience or engineering velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience influencing technical decisions across teams or driving adoption of shared systems</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for experienced frontend engineers to help build and evolve Harvey’s frontend platform—the systems, tools, and abstractions that enable our engineering team to ship high-quality product experiences quickly and consistently.\n\nThis team focuses on developer experience, performance, reliability, and scalability across our frontend stack. Rather than building one-off product features, you’ll create shared foundations that power all of Harvey’s user-facing applications.\n\nThis is a high-impact role with broad scope across the engineering organization. You’ll work closely with product engineers, design, and infrastructure teams to define and drive the future of frontend development at Harvey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and evolve shared frontend infrastructure, including our design system and developer tooling\n\n - Contribute to and evolve frontend architecture for scalability and performance\n\n - Improve developer experience and engineering velocity\n\n - Improve application performance and reliability\n\n - Partner with product teams to drive adoption of platform systems\n\n - Identify and reduce friction across the development lifecycle\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Strong experience working on large-scale frontend systems or platform-level infrastructure\n\n - Ability to think in systems and abstractions, not just features\n\n - A track record of improving developer experience or engineering velocity\n\n - Experience influencing technical decisions across teams or driving adoption of shared systems\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-PM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"44e7e6e3-8cd2-46e9-a432-4f3fb8d5f541","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d7bd081a-5df1-4022-aaa8-40596376d6f9","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"09cf4a1f-98a7-491d-bc95-caeea0ca380e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5f4f5580-ce2d-43a8-b8d9-fdafc4cd23b3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6cb0809d-923f-4119-a0d1-babb0c9289c4","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Core Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-27T20:18:39.094+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6cb0809d-923f-4119-a0d1-babb0c9289c4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6cb0809d-923f-4119-a0d1-babb0c9289c4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in New York City, New York. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1><strong><br />What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Incident.io\">Incident.io</a>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$201,000 - $264,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.\n\nYou'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.\n\nThis role is based in New York City, New York. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions\n\n - Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management\n\n - Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues\n\n - Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint\n\n - Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments\n\n - Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration\n\n - Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience\n\n - Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers\n\n - Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking\n\n - Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment\n\n - Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems\n\n - Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)\n\n - Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation\n\n - Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale\n\n - Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, Incident.io http://Incident.io)\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems\n\n - Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements\n\n - Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$201,000 - $264,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$201K – $264K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$201K - $264K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1423fd85-bb94-460c-b444-0fdf03c4bc6b","tierSummary":"$201K – $264K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3b235ba6-c005-4601-977e-2cf766a6f9d2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7259c99e-2873-4159-b4fc-7cbe86f9b987","summary":"$201K – $264K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201000,"maxValue":264000},{"id":"cb4983ce-9ba8-452c-a1a4-3139728e8d5a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201000,"maxValue":264000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c2d6c21b-1563-4000-a8a3-b751c79535da","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Core Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-27T20:18:36.663+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c2d6c21b-1563-4000-a8a3-b751c79535da","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c2d6c21b-1563-4000-a8a3-b751c79535da/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1><strong><br />What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Incident.io\">Incident.io</a>)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$236,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here.</strong></a></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Core Infrastructure team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in designing and building new infrastructure systems while equally scaling and strengthening our existing infrastructure. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every user interaction with Harvey — processing billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests across our global legal AI platform.\n\nYou'll work in an environment balanced between innovation — building new systems — and operational excellence, ensuring that Harvey remains resilient and efficient as it scales products, regions, customers, and usage. Your contributions will directly impact the reliability, scalability, and security of our platform as we serve the world's leading law firms and professional service providers.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable, fault-tolerant infrastructure systems that power Harvey's AI platform across multiple cloud regions\n\n - Own and evolve our multi-cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP), including Kubernetes orchestration, networking, and container management\n\n - Lead technical initiatives around observability, incident response, and operational excellence — building systems that enable rapid detection and resolution of issues\n\n - Architect and optimize our distributed systems for reliability, including load balancing, quota management, and failover mechanisms\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering and Security teams to ensure our infrastructure is an accelerant, not a constraint\n\n - Drive infrastructure-as-code practices using tools like Terraform and Pulumi to enable reproducible, auditable deployments\n\n - Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar across the organization through code reviews, design reviews, and technical leadership\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Design and implement a next-generation model proxy architecture that routes millions of daily inference requests while maintaining model API compatibility and enabling seamless model integration\n\n - Build distributed rate limiting and quota management systems using Redis-backed algorithms to handle bursty traffic patterns without degrading user experience\n\n - Architect multi-region deployment strategies that meet strict data residency requirements for global enterprise customers\n\n - Develop comprehensive observability infrastructure with granular SLA monitoring, burn rate alerts, and detailed token attribution for cost tracking\n\n - Lead the evolution of our CI/CD pipelines to improve developer velocity while maintaining production stability\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in Infrastructure Engineering or Platform Engineering in a production environment\n\n - Long track record building and scaling complex, large-scale distributed systems\n\n - Deep proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure preferred; GCP or AWS experience transfers well)\n\n - Strong fluency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools — Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation\n\n - Solid understanding of Kubernetes, container orchestration, networking, and cloud security at scale\n\n - Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, Incident.io http://Incident.io)\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, a \"spidey sense\" of where things could go wrong, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building infrastructure for AI/ML workloads or high-throughput inference systems\n\n - Background with distributed rate limiting, load balancing, or quota management systems\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security and compliance requirements\n\n - Track record of leading complex cross-functional projects and delivering measurable impact\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$236,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE. https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$236K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$236K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4bb3e3cd-fa6d-4d33-abf1-f78989e163a1","tierSummary":"$236K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"274523f9-71b8-4c16-af30-bc941faeffd2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f0e02b55-ba84-4a95-8b4a-0ffcf1610bf5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"be0bbc4f-d844-436a-9f2c-ba23ad31edca","summary":"$236K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":236000,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":236000,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"1406ae6f-1dfc-4b5a-985d-cccbffe283e1","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-01T19:19:06.032+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1406ae6f-1dfc-4b5a-985d-cccbffe283e1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1406ae6f-1dfc-4b5a-985d-cccbffe283e1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Backend Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1000-step planning agents that help take companies public</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on product-centric teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Backend Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\nWe use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents\n\n - Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI\n\n - Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions\n\n - 1000-step planning agents that help take companies public\n\n - Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters\n\n - Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks\n\n - Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on product-centric teams\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SA1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6c5cae8e-87eb-43a8-93ad-940a286952d8","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b22421b6-d9eb-4ed8-a291-d140fc8309ec","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"db148cba-f2de-456c-a5eb-6763d93260e7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"97d73f21-16e4-47c6-83af-27645c5b62eb","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9cc08902-8916-47a8-a849-eec2c67ab3bd","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Developer Experience","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-01T23:04:06.576+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9cc08902-8916-47a8-a849-eec2c67ab3bd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9cc08902-8916-47a8-a849-eec2c67ab3bd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategic direction and roadmap for scaling developer experience as Harvey expands, and contribute strategically to team decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide strong technical leadership and mentorship, upholding a high bar for engineering excellence across the team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven technical leadership throughout the entire project lifecycle, including ideation, design, implementation, and productionization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring engineers, guiding architectural decisions, and shaping culture to foster engineering excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Developer Experience team is what keeps Harvey’s fast growth momentum possible — the kind of fast where every week brings new products, new capabilities, and new challenges. We build the CI/CD systems, internal frameworks, and platform-level guardrails that enable all Harvey engineers to ship ambitious AI features rapidly and safely.\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you will be responsible for creating frameworks and systems that maximize the velocity and efficiency of every engineer at Harvey. You’ll work across the entire tech stack and collaborate with every team to instill reliability, automation, and simplicity into our developer workflows. You'll also have a unique opportunity to apply AI directly to the problem of developer productivity, defining the future of software development within an AI-native company.\n\nIf you are passionate about building foundational platforms to enable other engineers to move fast with confidence, we’d love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and scale a world-class developer platform to accelerate Harvey's hyper growth. Boost velocity and stability through robust CI/CD systems, effective test frameworks, and reliable development environments..\n\n - Build load testing and benchmarking infrastructure essential for evaluating and optimizing the performance of AI-native applications.\n\n - Pioneer the future of software development and site reliability engineering by integrating AI agents across the software development, deployment and maintenance lifecycle.\n\n - Collaborate with Backend Platform teams to embed testability, reliability and observability into the platform, ensuring services built on our foundation are robust, easy to test and maintain.\n\n - Work closely with engineering teams to gather feedback, evangelize best practices, and make the “paved road” a reality — empowering every Harvey engineer to move fast with confidence.\n\n - Set the strategic direction and roadmap for scaling developer experience as Harvey expands, and contribute strategically to team decision-making.\n\n - Provide strong technical leadership and mentorship, upholding a high bar for engineering excellence across the team.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of software engineering experience, including building scalable backend systems or internal developer platforms.\n\n - Proficiency in Python (or similar languages) and deep knowledge of backend development fundamentals and distributed systems.\n\n - Hands-on experience with CI/CD systems (Builtekite, Github Actions), test frameworks, or load and performance testing.\n\n - Hands-on experience with container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and infrastructure as code (Pulumi, Terraform).\n\n - A track record of producing high-quality, well-tested code, consistently following software development best practices to ensure quality and reliability.\n\n - Proven technical leadership throughout the entire project lifecycle, including ideation, design, implementation, and productionization.\n\n - Experience mentoring engineers, guiding architectural decisions, and shaping culture to foster engineering excellence.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and a passion for improving developer experience — you enjoy creating tools or frameworks that make other engineers more productive\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work across teams and incorporate feedback.\n\n - Experience integrating AI agents into a developer ecosystem is a strong plus.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"93d6fb00-de1b-43e6-beaa-b7b9086b27b7","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fb358300-fc84-4508-997c-6bb500e8b80e","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"d2aaaa58-eb59-42ba-9a62-ca6ce4cdf206","title":"Staff Product Security Engineer","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:27:31.747+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d2aaaa58-eb59-42ba-9a62-ca6ce4cdf206","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d2aaaa58-eb59-42ba-9a62-ca6ce4cdf206/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Product Security team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in shaping how security is built into our AI platform from the ground up. We store and process our customers’ most sensitive data, and as a result, security is paramount at every stage of our product lifecycle. You'll take ownership of securing critical parts of the product while driving high-leverage security initiatives that raise the bar for the entire engineering org — balancing hands-on technical work with cross-functional leadership and mentorship. This is a rare opportunity to define and build a product security program at a company scaling fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our security program is driven by our collective offensive security experience: breaking into systems at other companies (in white-hat capacities), responding to real security incidents, and learning from other companies’ data breaches. We regularly conduct penetration tests and red team exercises with external security firms. At the same time, we are all software engineers - contributing code daily and approaching security with an engineering-first mindset.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and own the product security roadmap, prioritizing initiatives based on risk, business impact, and engineering org maturity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and evolve security posture across the engineering organization, setting standards that scale with the company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and Platform teams to incorporate secure design principles at every stage of development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and review security-critical code across key parts of the product, including authentication and access control</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect secure-by-default libraries and tools that make the secure path the easiest choice for developers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive mitigation strategies during security-related incident responses, coordinating cross-functional efforts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and raise the security bar across teams through code reviews, design reviews, and technical guidance</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in product security, application security, offensive security, and/or security-focused software engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long track record of identifying and remediating software vulnerabilities, demonstrated through CVEs, bug bounty awards, published research, or prior work experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of leading complex cross-functional security initiatives and delivering measurable improvements, with demonstrated ability to influence engineering teams without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring senior engineers and developing security talent within an engineering organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills with demonstrated experience writing high-quality, production software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and collaboration skills, particularly when translating security risks into business terms for non-security stakeholders</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building security programs or practices at hyper-growth startups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with cloud environments (Azure, GCP, AWS) and cloud-native security patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML systems and emerging security considerations for LLM-based applications</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $330,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Product Security team at Harvey, you'll play a critical role in shaping how security is built into our AI platform from the ground up. We store and process our customers’ most sensitive data, and as a result, security is paramount at every stage of our product lifecycle. You'll take ownership of securing critical parts of the product while driving high-leverage security initiatives that raise the bar for the entire engineering org — balancing hands-on technical work with cross-functional leadership and mentorship. This is a rare opportunity to define and build a product security program at a company scaling fast.\n\nOur security program is driven by our collective offensive security experience: breaking into systems at other companies (in white-hat capacities), responding to real security incidents, and learning from other companies’ data breaches. We regularly conduct penetration tests and red team exercises with external security firms. At the same time, we are all software engineers - contributing code daily and approaching security with an engineering-first mindset.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define and own the product security roadmap, prioritizing initiatives based on risk, business impact, and engineering org maturity.\n\n - Establish and evolve security posture across the engineering organization, setting standards that scale with the company\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and Platform teams to incorporate secure design principles at every stage of development\n\n - Own and review security-critical code across key parts of the product, including authentication and access control\n\n - Architect secure-by-default libraries and tools that make the secure path the easiest choice for developers\n\n - Drive mitigation strategies during security-related incident responses, coordinating cross-functional efforts\n\n - Mentor engineers and raise the security bar across teams through code reviews, design reviews, and technical guidance\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in product security, application security, offensive security, and/or security-focused software engineering\n\n - Long track record of identifying and remediating software vulnerabilities, demonstrated through CVEs, bug bounty awards, published research, or prior work experience\n\n - Track record of leading complex cross-functional security initiatives and delivering measurable improvements, with demonstrated ability to influence engineering teams without direct authority.\n\n - Experience mentoring senior engineers and developing security talent within an engineering organization\n\n - Strong programming skills with demonstrated experience writing high-quality, production software\n\n - Excellent communication and collaboration skills, particularly when translating security risks into business terms for non-security stakeholders\n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   Nice to Have\n   \n   - Experience building security programs or practices at hyper-growth startups\n   \n   - Background with cloud environments (Azure, GCP, AWS) and cloud-native security patterns\n   \n   - Experience with AI/ML systems and emerging security considerations for LLM-based applications\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $330,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $330K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"975b7e78-aacb-4ce2-a3b5-e8b846fad15d","tierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c5ec3f07-c3e8-4a3d-8bd9-24e6f9e5e76a","summary":"$220K – $330K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"id":"c8f8b1e9-de69-4411-89a1-9ccd730db8a4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"39c48019-d1f5-426c-aae0-0098654daf51","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"fc038666-be6f-4365-be8d-fb46e520473d","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-01T18:53:51.015+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fc038666-be6f-4365-be8d-fb46e520473d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fc038666-be6f-4365-be8d-fb46e520473d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&amp;A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.\n\n - Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.\n\n - Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.\n\n - Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 8+ years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. \n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-BB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"566d25e6-e6c6-49e2-b13e-e0e792ca7c9c","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f2db9b52-3a5e-4fde-ae0e-92e3449009ca","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b1f64f1e-de3e-4d85-bf04-3013a4e425af","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"59c3741e-89aa-47d9-ac6d-3f4b0fa4ae44","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"24a1df80-c1b7-4e16-b938-1cb3b129463d","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-01T18:53:54.354+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24a1df80-c1b7-4e16-b938-1cb3b129463d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24a1df80-c1b7-4e16-b938-1cb3b129463d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&amp;A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Save weeks of effort on high pressure M&A deals by automating information requests and diligence checks across hundreds of thousands of files with retrieval and file editing agents.\n\n - Dramatically speed up deal turnaround speed by improving the latency and quality of agents on applying a standard legal \"playbook\" to contracts.\n\n - Ensure that our clients win their complex, data-hungry litigation cases by optimizing our multi-source retrieval agents.\n\n - Enable board-ready PowerPoint generation by tuning the harness and libraries for coding agents.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 8+ years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience. \n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-BB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8d711487-3569-4bb7-a19d-47fba4b538f7","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"54e45aa7-d4c8-4550-a81f-4d445f53699b","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"d56c186a-8410-4d0d-bf5a-d8876c769f44","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"60f27d58-91fa-4c03-b342-6b04f0ba38c0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8da5efb4-4659-4ff7-aca9-b9a88c040ba3","title":"Mid-Market Customer Success Manager (Chicago)","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-15T22:09:03.348+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8da5efb4-4659-4ff7-aca9-b9a88c040ba3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8da5efb4-4659-4ff7-aca9-b9a88c040ba3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$125,000 - $145,000 OTE </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.\n\n - Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.\n\n - Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$125,000 - $145,000 OTE \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $145K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"23cb0f78-46fd-4173-b1e1-6ef11235d837","tierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE","components":[{"id":"882a92b0-c0c5-4ce3-9e5f-51f72362d6df","summary":"$125K – $145K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}},{"id":"9b7ae8f4-773e-4f83-83fa-096d157ae00d","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-05T16:43:54.462+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9b7ae8f4-773e-4f83-83fa-096d157ae00d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9b7ae8f4-773e-4f83-83fa-096d157ae00d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Backend Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1000-step planning agents that help take companies public</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on product-centric teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Backend Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\nWe use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents\n\n - Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI\n\n - Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions\n\n - 1000-step planning agents that help take companies public\n\n - Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters\n\n - Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks\n\n - Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on product-centric teams\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SA1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"132862e8-2b8f-4615-92b0-1d3feb28027d","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"087b36d8-60c4-45bd-b996-0769a715b809","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"91d52679-6df7-4f68-8747-aca66ed3df14","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0bcdff81-2b00-4037-b3ae-583a3764371a","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"83a438ac-a6f8-4388-983a-ec95155a2604","title":"Mid Market Sales Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-05T16:59:10.781+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/83a438ac-a6f8-4388-983a-ec95155a2604","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/83a438ac-a6f8-4388-983a-ec95155a2604/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>As a Mid Market Sales Manager at Harvey, </em>you will lead and coach high-performing Account Executives in driving the growth and success of our AI solutions within mid sized and boutique law firms and in house legal teams. You’ll be responsible for the team’s delivery on ambitious sales targets and rolling up your sleeves to work directly with prospective Harvey customers. You’ll help refine the operational foundations of our rapidly growing Mid Market organization by developing playbooks, best practices, and a best-in-class sales toolkit. We are looking for a self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and solve complex problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have superb core sales skills, experience scaling high-velocity teams and mentoring colleagues, outstanding communication skills, and an affinity for understanding customer needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a team of consultative, solution-based, Mid Market software sales professionals to achieve ARR targets through both net new logo and expansion deals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own managing and reporting on your book of business, including accurate revenue forecasting and pipeline maintenance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively assist with recruiting and hiring new team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach and develop Mid Market account executives to promote career growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Refine our sales playbook to enable all sellers to better deliver consultative sales engagements at high velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally across the organization to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey’s clients.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of tech sales experience 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performance sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$320,000 - $340,000 OTE (50/50 split)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Sales Manager at Harvey, you will lead and coach high-performing Account Executives in driving the growth and success of our AI solutions within mid sized and boutique law firms and in house legal teams. You’ll be responsible for the team’s delivery on ambitious sales targets and rolling up your sleeves to work directly with prospective Harvey customers. You’ll help refine the operational foundations of our rapidly growing Mid Market organization by developing playbooks, best practices, and a best-in-class sales toolkit. We are looking for a self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and solve complex problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have superb core sales skills, experience scaling high-velocity teams and mentoring colleagues, outstanding communication skills, and an affinity for understanding customer needs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead a team of consultative, solution-based, Mid Market software sales professionals to achieve ARR targets through both net new logo and expansion deals.\n\n - Own managing and reporting on your book of business, including accurate revenue forecasting and pipeline maintenance.\n\n - Proactively assist with recruiting and hiring new team members.\n\n - Coach and develop Mid Market account executives to promote career growth\n\n - Refine our sales playbook to enable all sellers to better deliver consultative sales engagements at high velocity\n\n - Work cross-functionally across the organization to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey’s clients.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of tech sales experience 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performance sales team.\n\n - Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment.\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$320,000 - $340,000 OTE (50/50 split)\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AB1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$320K – $340K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$320K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5717792d-25b0-46f7-9c83-4876b36b61de","tierSummary":"OTE 50/50 Split $320K – $340K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"404dc506-f625-4c29-9ce9-c8eb52adf666","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a29b9a1e-e79b-49b7-8900-26de4fb48064","summary":"OTE 50/50 Split $320K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":320000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":320000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"dcacb8c5-d91b-4f8f-a444-d8c86cb606c9","title":"Mid-Market Customer Success Manager (San Francisco)","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-15T22:10:56.225+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dcacb8c5-d91b-4f8f-a444-d8c86cb606c9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dcacb8c5-d91b-4f8f-a444-d8c86cb606c9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$125,000 - $145,000 OTE </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.\n\n - Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.\n\n - Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$125,000 - $145,000 OTE \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $145K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e3136f87-7f61-4053-9f70-4b0204372069","tierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE","components":[{"id":"e4ee2f3a-c1e6-45e0-b285-033f3994feef","summary":"$125K – $145K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}},{"id":"8b16bcf7-9255-4859-8416-a7ff921032e6","title":"Senior Staff Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-28T17:20:27.142+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8b16bcf7-9255-4859-8416-a7ff921032e6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8b16bcf7-9255-4859-8416-a7ff921032e6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.\n\n - Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.\n\n - Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.\n\n - Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.\n\n - Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.\n\n - Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.\n\n - Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.\n\n - Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 15+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).\n\n - Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)\n\n - Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.\n\n - Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.\n\n - Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-DM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fd3eee99-2c94-4127-8b82-3582a79cd418","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:36:48.460+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fd3eee99-2c94-4127-8b82-3582a79cd418","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fd3eee99-2c94-4127-8b82-3582a79cd418/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f6aea569-729e-46ae-b4a5-556d34027bad","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"77455095-55a2-40af-8782-4e1a813ecfa2","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"f4d70ed0-010e-40f5-b194-2813e55f6e0c","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:36:40.375+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4d70ed0-010e-40f5-b194-2813e55f6e0c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4d70ed0-010e-40f5-b194-2813e55f6e0c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0a253bb8-ef30-485d-b922-0b0e8f4f338f","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"933dca2c-7c12-4869-a84f-1ee59897585b","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"49d4e629-518e-4f64-9dd8-293f844d3171","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6f74cc2a-bf7b-4dcb-b07b-8641b783939f","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"8684a735-fbef-422f-8fec-5ee08e264e1d","title":"Staff Motion Designer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-01T21:54:28.217+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8684a735-fbef-422f-8fec-5ee08e264e1d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8684a735-fbef-422f-8fec-5ee08e264e1d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is hiring a Staff Motion Designer in San Francisco to define how motion shows up across Harvey’s brand, product storytelling, launch moments, web experiences, customer education, and executive-facing creative work. The role should sit within Brand and Design, reporting into Shawn Farsai, whose current scope includes Brand Marketing and Creative leadership in San Francisco. This is a new senior IC role intended to raise the motion craft bar while still operating with the low-ego, hands-on generalist posture expected of Harvey’s senior brand hires. The role should build on existing motion and brand hiring standards, including deep portfolio review, visible process, cross-functional collaboration with PMM and Marketing, and practical assessment of prioritization under ambiguity. The person in this role will help Harvey turn complex AI product ideas into clear, memorable, and reusable motion systems that can scale across product launches, web surfaces, campaign assets, Academy or education assets, events, and internal/external storytelling.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the motion design language for Harvey’s brand across launch videos, product explainers, web and campaign moments, event assets, social cuts, sales enablement, and other high-leverage creative surfaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create motion concepts, storyboards, styleframes, animatics, and final motion assets that make complex AI workflows feel clear, premium, and unmistakably Harvey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Brand, Product Marketing, Product Design, Creative Operations, and other GTM stakeholders to translate positioning, product context, and user needs into motion narratives that can ship quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop reusable motion systems, templates, animation principles, and production workflows so Harvey can scale motion output without reinventing the wheel on every request.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use judgment to scope work appropriately across polished hero moments, scrappy launch needs, quick-turnaround edits, and longer-term brand-system investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the craft bar for motion while remaining willing to do the unglamorous but important production work required in a fast-moving creative team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong portfolio of motion work that demonstrates storytelling, art direction, animation craft, visual systems thinking, and the ability to explain the process behind finished work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep fluency in motion design tools and workflows such as After Effects, Figma, Cinema 4D, Lottie, Rive, code-adjacent motion, or comparable production tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building motion for brand, product, marketing, launch, or education contexts, ideally in a product-led technology company or high-growth SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A demonstrated ability to simplify complex concepts visually without overloading the viewer, including strong instincts for pacing, sequencing, hierarchy, narration, and accessibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional communication skills, including the ability to clarify a brief, align with PMM or Marketing goals, handle competing feedback, and prioritize multiple stakeholder requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A staff-level ownership mindset: able to bring ideas, shape systems, operate through ambiguity, give and receive feedback well, and still roll up sleeves when the team needs execution support.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$157,000-$235,600</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is hiring a Staff Motion Designer in San Francisco to define how motion shows up across Harvey’s brand, product storytelling, launch moments, web experiences, customer education, and executive-facing creative work. The role should sit within Brand and Design, reporting into Shawn Farsai, whose current scope includes Brand Marketing and Creative leadership in San Francisco. This is a new senior IC role intended to raise the motion craft bar while still operating with the low-ego, hands-on generalist posture expected of Harvey’s senior brand hires. The role should build on existing motion and brand hiring standards, including deep portfolio review, visible process, cross-functional collaboration with PMM and Marketing, and practical assessment of prioritization under ambiguity. The person in this role will help Harvey turn complex AI product ideas into clear, memorable, and reusable motion systems that can scale across product launches, web surfaces, campaign assets, Academy or education assets, events, and internal/external storytelling.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the motion design language for Harvey’s brand across launch videos, product explainers, web and campaign moments, event assets, social cuts, sales enablement, and other high-leverage creative surfaces.\n\n - Create motion concepts, storyboards, styleframes, animatics, and final motion assets that make complex AI workflows feel clear, premium, and unmistakably Harvey.\n\n - Partner closely with Brand, Product Marketing, Product Design, Creative Operations, and other GTM stakeholders to translate positioning, product context, and user needs into motion narratives that can ship quickly.\n\n - Develop reusable motion systems, templates, animation principles, and production workflows so Harvey can scale motion output without reinventing the wheel on every request.\n\n - Use judgment to scope work appropriately across polished hero moments, scrappy launch needs, quick-turnaround edits, and longer-term brand-system investments.\n\n - Raise the craft bar for motion while remaining willing to do the unglamorous but important production work required in a fast-moving creative team.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A strong portfolio of motion work that demonstrates storytelling, art direction, animation craft, visual systems thinking, and the ability to explain the process behind finished work.\n\n - Deep fluency in motion design tools and workflows such as After Effects, Figma, Cinema 4D, Lottie, Rive, code-adjacent motion, or comparable production tools.\n\n - Experience building motion for brand, product, marketing, launch, or education contexts, ideally in a product-led technology company or high-growth SaaS environment.\n\n - A demonstrated ability to simplify complex concepts visually without overloading the viewer, including strong instincts for pacing, sequencing, hierarchy, narration, and accessibility.\n\n - Strong cross-functional communication skills, including the ability to clarify a brief, align with PMM or Marketing goals, handle competing feedback, and prioritize multiple stakeholder requests.\n\n - A staff-level ownership mindset: able to bring ideas, shape systems, operate through ambiguity, give and receive feedback well, and still roll up sleeves when the team needs execution support.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$157,000-$235,600\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-AM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$157K – $235.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$157K - $235.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"95508099-7c52-4135-adae-d4a190b936ad","tierSummary":"$157K – $235.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"49327ce9-fe94-4778-80a1-d4431ad031c5","summary":"$157K – $235.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":157000,"maxValue":235600},{"id":"f66eb014-3655-4c0b-ab3f-627208637e07","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d2bfc27c-9c54-42f9-b15b-cb44f57e3498","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":157000,"maxValue":235600},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"b4f45d7f-6a88-40d5-83a6-e4db27f3e402","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Full Stack","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-13T23:34:40.007+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b4f45d7f-6a88-40d5-83a6-e4db27f3e402","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b4f45d7f-6a88-40d5-83a6-e4db27f3e402/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-NG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"88cebe0d-32bf-43b5-8f65-3537a63dec1a","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"80c34e5f-8d01-4aa5-a260-ee788308d7c2","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"bc5fd79a-c5aa-4501-b573-563b69f472b0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e58570e1-b7ac-41b7-97f0-6d0e86d28238","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c3b9e500-dc27-4afe-9b8a-31223c6b18fe","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:36:44.704+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c3b9e500-dc27-4afe-9b8a-31223c6b18fe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c3b9e500-dc27-4afe-9b8a-31223c6b18fe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b4e4456a-9700-4e9f-895b-c42e4f657c4e","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0f1554de-800d-4733-9792-5404e5e8d706","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cdab73dc-a079-4f16-bcf1-341e20cc6d1d","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"c05f4bfc-fb4e-48b1-8d70-c8c34a60f4ec","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7325a214-908d-48a4-bbc2-f5c3a6c9ed00","title":"Staff Product Designer","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-12T18:15:49.040+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7325a214-908d-48a4-bbc2-f5c3a6c9ed00","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7325a214-908d-48a4-bbc2-f5c3a6c9ed00/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Product Designer at Harvey, you’ll manage multiple projects from ideation to launch. You’ll create high-quality designs, interactions, and prototypes that transform complex problems into intuitive solutions. Working closely with engineers, AI researchers, product managers, and lawyers, you’ll incorporate AI in meaningful ways—crafting interfaces that help users understand, trust, and effectively guide AI outputs.\n\nWe’re looking for someone with strong interaction design instincts, visual design sensibility, and collaboration—someone who sweats the details, welcomes feedback, and elevates ideas through tight cross-functional teamwork.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Lead the design of end-to-end product experiences, from initial concept through polished execution.\n\n - Collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and AI researchers to translate business objectives into user-centered designs.\n\n - Shape and refine our design system to ensure a cohesive and scalable visual language across the product.\n\n - Conduct user research to uncover pain points and opportunities, leveraging insights to inform design decisions.\n\n - Develop prototypes to explore and validate new features, workflows, and interactions.\n\n - Champion a high design bar, helping the team make thoughtful, intentional decisions at every step.\n\n - Promote and develop best practices in designing with AI.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience designing products in a fast-paced environment, with a portfolio that demonstrates your best work.\n\n - Ability to tackle complex challenges and transform them into simple, intuitive experiences.\n\n - Ability to change altitude from design details to big picture thinking, while maintaining a high pace of execution and quality bar.\n\n - Deep understanding of design systems and a strong sense of visual and interaction design craft.\n\n - Experience conducting user research and applying insights to design decisions.\n\n - Excellent communication and storytelling skills to articulate design concepts and rationale.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c6e602c1-57d7-4af7-9b98-e52b5b4ff76a","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:36:36.114+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c6e602c1-57d7-4af7-9b98-e52b5b4ff76a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c6e602c1-57d7-4af7-9b98-e52b5b4ff76a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e8dbf438-3086-42af-810e-4f4459cf7400","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Litigation/Regulatory)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:36.444+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e8dbf438-3086-42af-810e-4f4459cf7400","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e8dbf438-3086-42af-810e-4f4459cf7400/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"81d74de2-8749-46cc-bffe-be597d1a4aab","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e2373fbe-c293-4b14-bc3c-5f70676050a1","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"be03da93-23ce-4ab9-8d4b-8976acb3747f","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d9f3d648-2c62-496d-9d84-b15ef86a3eb0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7e7261f2-307d-43ff-a339-cbd2e26d70cd","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Litigation/Regulatory)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:43.022+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7e7261f2-307d-43ff-a339-cbd2e26d70cd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7e7261f2-307d-43ff-a339-cbd2e26d70cd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"66ff848f-6df2-4870-9a58-24586a265aba","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2ef75f16-2052-4301-82c6-a90cbdaaf4e6","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"46d2d7e6-9f7e-4890-ac51-a7072aefed43","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a78e20a4-c7a1-46e5-8395-5fbbba7b023b","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"b8348643-507b-4793-8e8c-62ffa6a0c254","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Litigation/Regulatory)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:46.331+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b8348643-507b-4793-8e8c-62ffa6a0c254","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b8348643-507b-4793-8e8c-62ffa6a0c254/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"41add6a2-b0b1-4129-a18c-1972f3f0ecb6","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f4191eb2-82f3-483a-bd32-edc0fd8b09b4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"164dd392-47a2-41ce-af10-9a1d7ffb1df4","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9b1b17fa-c60c-4893-a72d-ed1dbe7115a0","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"7103fd26-a5c9-4619-9ecf-e1fca89c0d6b","title":"Legal Engineer (Law Firm, Litigation/Regulatory)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:39.498+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7103fd26-a5c9-4619-9ecf-e1fca89c0d6b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7103fd26-a5c9-4619-9ecf-e1fca89c0d6b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of law firms, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"149546d1-8c28-4512-b1af-0bc84b86e584","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2a9a4184-aad6-46d6-ad9f-682140af7cb8","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9d8db9a6-49fd-461f-bab2-67e28b6d3bc9","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a7abdedb-9295-4911-a736-ec394afb228d","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"963db922-ea97-47f1-9731-ed0ec1dc026a","title":"Legal Engineer (In-House)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:00.695+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/963db922-ea97-47f1-9731-ed0ec1dc026a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/963db922-ea97-47f1-9731-ed0ec1dc026a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n\n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n\n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n\n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n\n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n\n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2d6258a6-c3f1-4f46-b219-e4d3bc7143d7","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"26c1089d-6804-475d-b78d-fef4cbbf667f","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ad753735-5621-4f62-a7a9-d5358d3f986e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"08133a44-9f35-4f3b-ae2c-eb4c1a6aec00","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"4de85e3d-1810-4d93-b821-fcc442302e4f","title":"Legal Engineer (In-House)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:03.905+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4de85e3d-1810-4d93-b821-fcc442302e4f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4de85e3d-1810-4d93-b821-fcc442302e4f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fd7ee36f-c68b-4a0d-8765-78d58fdfa64c","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"41c9f2eb-1d99-43ca-952e-756056ec77df","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"bda4e160-4108-46ea-8273-bb4c10f244bf","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b0e57276-bcec-487b-98aa-31f6828601e1","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"f4e343c0-a7c9-491b-b330-3ca74fc75351","title":"Legal Engineer (In-House)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:12.910+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4e343c0-a7c9-491b-b330-3ca74fc75351","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4e343c0-a7c9-491b-b330-3ca74fc75351/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5ad23c1a-4d74-4f76-860e-45849b12d0c4","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fd2d79db-bee7-425e-84c3-7d7681f78b08","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"193a5bd7-3964-4582-8c0e-aee321491e7a","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e22f6305-1aca-4042-8887-ae644dfbc41b","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000}]}},{"id":"aa2ee4f0-e9d9-4773-ac70-820aabb1a95a","title":"Legal Engineer (In-House)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T14:37:08.396+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/aa2ee4f0-e9d9-4773-ac70-820aabb1a95a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/aa2ee4f0-e9d9-4773-ac70-820aabb1a95a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Function Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales).</strong> Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.</p><h1></h1><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer (Pre-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">LECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nFUNCTION OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineering team is composed of former practicing attorneys who work to bring value to Harvey's prospects and customers. Legal Engineers lead discovery, demos, trainings, and onboarding alongside our AEs and CSMs. They translate real legal work into Harvey solutions, serving as the trust layer across the entire customer lifecycle, from the first pilot to the most complex, custom-built workflow.\n\n \n\nAt Harvey, we segment the Legal Engineering function into three teams: Legal Engineers (Pre-Sales), Legal Engineers, Product Specialists (Post-Sales), and Legal Engineers, Custom Solutions (Pre- and Post-Sales). Legal Engineers across all three subgroups understand how lawyers think and work, and use that expertise to design, build, and refine solutions that hold up under live in-practice pressure. In doing so, they don't just drive adoption; they shape Harvey's product roadmap, ensuring every release is grounded in what the legal profession needs. It's a team built to power Harvey as the platform lawyers can trust with their most important work.\n\n \n\nYou may be asked to travel around 2-3+ times per month. Travel is always for a significant business need and typically is for 1-3 days at a time.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLegal Engineer (Pre-Sales)\n\nLegal Engineers are lawyers who left practice to help build the future of legal work. Working closely with Account Executives, they engage with many of the world’s leading law firms and legal teams throughout the pre-sales process. They lead collaborative pilot programs, guide prospects through what’s possible with AI, and work alongside lawyers to understand their workflows, build tailored solutions, and demonstrate meaningful value in real legal use cases. Along the way, they bring prospect feedback back into the product, helping shape the future of Harvey.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Product Specialist (Post-Sales)\n\nLEPS take over once a prospect becomes a customer. LEPS build trusted relationships with many of the world's leading legal teams by learning their workflows and showing them how to weave Harvey into daily practice.  The LEPS role spans the entire customer journey, from leading onboarding and enablement, to sitting down with a full practice group to build agents on real matters. Along the way, the LEPS translates legal practice needs into actionable feedback for product and engineering, contributes to customer-facing content across practice areas, and upholds Harvey's credibility as the leading AI platform for lawyers.\n\n \n\nLegal Engineer, Custom Solutions (Pre-Sale and Post-Sale)\n\nLECS are a specialist group that work on complex no-code custom Harvey in-app solutions. LECS meet with group heads, general counsel, and other senior stakeholders to learn how key processes run today. Drawing on their legal expertise, they use natural language prompting to design bespoke resources, including agents, playbooks, and other tools, that improve the quality, speed, and experience of that process. The build is collaborative. The LECS scope it with the customer, prototype against sample documents, and refine it alongside their team. Most LECS work happens post-sale, but the team also supports strategic accounts pre-sale on an advisory basis. LECS concentrates narrowly on designing tools that automate a specific process, and on building relationships with the senior leaders who own it.\n\n \n\n*In your initial interview with our recruiting team, you'll learn more about all three roles, and we'll identify which may be the best fit based on your background and our current hiring needs.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 3 + years of practicing law in-house, at a top-tier law firm, or advising a sophisticated corporate legal team.\n\n - Strong understanding of the workflows, challenges, and demands of in-house legal teams, including balancing legal risk with business priorities.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish credibility with legal and business stakeholders at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding communication and presentation skills — comfortable leading a live demo, facilitating a workshop, or engaging in strategic customer conversations.\n\n - Deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, paired with a practical, solutions-oriented mindset and bias toward action.\n\n - Track record partnering with senior stakeholders to drive results, with curiosity for testing approaches and optimizing for customer outcomes.\n\n - Cross-functional experience (business, ops, compliance, product), sales/customer-facing experience (law firm BD, secondment), and/or hands-on experience using AI tools in legal practice are all pluses.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $320,000 USD OTE 75/25 split\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LS1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dc8d1644-1588-4c6f-88ab-df8d130d4eaa","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"efde6ede-1085-4d92-a3f2-473e5f86bf5c","summary":"OTE 75/25 Split $220K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"1d0727bb-c793-4ed1-ade3-8901aa038b4c","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"528f4b17-162a-4933-a037-b76eeec01387","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8e513820-55f8-4cbd-8bdd-28a67992469c","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Full Stack - NYC","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-15T03:43:31.768+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8e513820-55f8-4cbd-8bdd-28a67992469c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8e513820-55f8-4cbd-8bdd-28a67992469c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1000-step planning agents that help take companies public</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$238,000 -$290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Retrieval over peta-byte scale documents\n\n - Organizational-level interfaces to collaborate with AI\n\n - Managing dedicated GPU capacity across 5+ regions\n\n - 1000-step planning agents that help take companies public\n\n - Government-level security for the world's most sensitive matters\n\n - Evaluating LLMs across a 10k+ leaf taxonomy of tasks\n\n - Internet-scale data collection from over 50+ jurisdictions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ YoE (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$238,000 -$290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n\n#LI-SB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$260K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$260K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e9ad68b0-0162-4723-b97a-8d92659aa274","tierSummary":"$260K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"933767ee-8cb7-4ad9-9a0c-ad4be902326f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7d56e090-fa74-409c-b64d-23ee169091de","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4a293124-d473-44cf-99a7-ce3d5f7dd5a4","summary":"$260K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"5a22d5da-6be0-4f97-87d2-bb6a52aba554","title":"Majors Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T22:46:35.734+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5a22d5da-6be0-4f97-87d2-bb6a52aba554","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5a22d5da-6be0-4f97-87d2-bb6a52aba554/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 25% of the time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in management consulting or technology advisory at a top tier management consulting firm, or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n - Travel required: Up to 25% of the time\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Background in management consulting or technology advisory at a top tier management consulting firm, or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment\n\n - History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.\n\n - Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.\n\n - Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n - $180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-GK1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $210K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"762d4dde-2686-461c-a2ea-1fcabbc14da5","tierSummary":"OTE 80/20 Split $180K – $210K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b5ad6cfc-6814-4235-ad1f-5335f43c11c4","summary":"OTE 80/20 Split $180K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"id":"3b9bc08a-9240-4bf1-9a3c-2c130f68aa79","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2a2e3951-d685-405d-9138-40409aee0f73","title":"Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T18:22:59.241+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2a2e3951-d685-405d-9138-40409aee0f73","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2a2e3951-d685-405d-9138-40409aee0f73/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager is a strategic operator who partners closely with Harvey's Enterprise sales organization to accelerate rep effectiveness and drive revenue outcomes. Sitting within the GTM Enablement team, this person designs and scales the programs that prepare Enterprise Account Executives to sell AI solutions to the world's largest law firms and corporate legal departments. The role owns the end-to-end enablement strategy for the Enterprise segment—from skills development and methodology reinforcement to change management and launch readiness—operating as a trusted partner to Enterprise Sales leadership, Product Marketing, and cross-functional GTM teams. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company equips its highest-performing sellers to win in a rapidly evolving market.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and deliver Enterprise-specific enablement programs spanning onboarding, product launches, methodology rollouts, and competitive positioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with the executive leaders and frontline managers to identify skill gaps, define competency standards, and build tailored coaching frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage enablement content, playbooks, and resources aligned to the Enterprise buyer journey and MEDDPICC sales methodology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own program measurement and reporting, tracking leading and lagging indicators of Enablement programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Legal Engineering to translate product and market updates into field-ready assets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive change management for new tools, processes, and go-to-market motions across the Enterprise segment</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–6 years of experience in sales enablement, revenue enablement, or GTM program management, with demonstrated ownership of programs supporting Enterprise or complex sales motions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams, prioritize ruthlessly, and deliver against tight timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication, facilitation, and executive presence; comfortable presenting to and influencing senior sales leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with enterprise sales methodologies (e.g., MEDDPICC, Challenger, Force Management) and experience embedding them into enablement programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in B2B SaaS, legal tech, or AI preferred; strong intellectual curiosity about the legal industry and emerging technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias for action, comfort with ambiguity, and a track record of driving impact in high-growth environments</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000-204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager is a strategic operator who partners closely with Harvey's Enterprise sales organization to accelerate rep effectiveness and drive revenue outcomes. Sitting within the GTM Enablement team, this person designs and scales the programs that prepare Enterprise Account Executives to sell AI solutions to the world's largest law firms and corporate legal departments. The role owns the end-to-end enablement strategy for the Enterprise segment—from skills development and methodology reinforcement to change management and launch readiness—operating as a trusted partner to Enterprise Sales leadership, Product Marketing, and cross-functional GTM teams. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company equips its highest-performing sellers to win in a rapidly evolving market.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and deliver Enterprise-specific enablement programs spanning onboarding, product launches, methodology rollouts, and competitive positioning\n\n - Partner directly with the executive leaders and frontline managers to identify skill gaps, define competency standards, and build tailored coaching frameworks\n\n - Develop and manage enablement content, playbooks, and resources aligned to the Enterprise buyer journey and MEDDPICC sales methodology\n\n - Own program measurement and reporting, tracking leading and lagging indicators of Enablement programs\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Legal Engineering to translate product and market updates into field-ready assets\n\n - Drive change management for new tools, processes, and go-to-market motions across the Enterprise segment\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4–6 years of experience in sales enablement, revenue enablement, or GTM program management, with demonstrated ownership of programs supporting Enterprise or complex sales motions\n\n - Strong program management skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams, prioritize ruthlessly, and deliver against tight timelines\n\n - Excellent communication, facilitation, and executive presence; comfortable presenting to and influencing senior sales leadership\n\n - Familiarity with enterprise sales methodologies (e.g., MEDDPICC, Challenger, Force Management) and experience embedding them into enablement programs\n\n - Experience in B2B SaaS, legal tech, or AI preferred; strong intellectual curiosity about the legal industry and emerging technology\n\n - A bias for action, comfort with ambiguity, and a track record of driving impact in high-growth environments\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000-204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TM1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3c670200-8455-48ab-8b7b-e13546d3a3c0","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c461eddb-5899-4f4f-b6e8-49180487c9e2","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"6e7db125-55c0-41e8-b191-a973adeff5ba","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"bd54cfd8-933d-46a8-9796-e249b82cef7f","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-25T16:55:41.391+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bd54cfd8-933d-46a8-9796-e249b82cef7f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bd54cfd8-933d-46a8-9796-e249b82cef7f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>..</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Backend Engineer on Harvey’s product engineering team, you will design and operate the backend systems that turn cutting-edge AI capabilities into seamless, dependable product experiences. You’ll build secure, multi-tenant services, orchestrate interactions with LLMs and agentic tools, and help define the backend architecture that powers Harvey’s rapidly expanding product surface. Your work will have immediate business and customer impact as you ship the foundational systems behind our next generation of AI products.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Collaborate closely with Product to prioritize customer-focused work and deliver reliable features quickly in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Design and own backend services and APIs that power Harvey’s web applications, workflows, and integrations.\n\n - Model and manage data in Postgres and related data stores to support low-latency, reliable user experiences.\n\n - Build secure, multi-tenant, permissions-aware systems with appropriate auditing for enterprise and government customers.\n\n - Implement backend features and workflows that use LLMs and agentic tools, orchestrating calls to our AI systems from robust, well-structured services.\n\n - Collaborate with frontend, product, and design partners to shape solutions, define clear API contracts, and ship features end-to-end.\n\n - Add meaningful logging, metrics, and tracing so services are observable, debuggable, and ready for on-call ownership.\n\n - Improve performance and scalability by profiling bottlenecks, tuning queries, and refining service boundaries as usage grows.\n\n - Participate in code reviews, technical design discussions, and an on-call rotation for the services you own.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 12+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production web applications or SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products by leveraging PWA technologies\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and experience with a modern web framework (e.g., FastAPI or Flask).\n\n - Hands-on experience with relational databases (e.g., Postgres)\n\n - Solid understanding of API design, authentication/authorization, background job patterns, and robust error handling.\n\n - Experience building for Cloud Infrastructure such as Azure, AWS, or GCP.\n\n - Comfort operating services in production using logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts, including participation in an on-call rotation.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice..\n\n\n\n#LI-DM1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a150789e-6b01-4780-9325-7ec968252ddc","title":"CX Operations Engineer","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-22T16:43:45.923+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a150789e-6b01-4780-9325-7ec968252ddc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a150789e-6b01-4780-9325-7ec968252ddc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$124,000 - $185,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.\n\nReporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.\n\nThis role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features\n\n - Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers\n\n - Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends\n\n - Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality\n\n - Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need\n\n - Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack\n\n - Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it\n\n - Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data\n\n - Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment\n\n - Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments\n\n - Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale\n\n - Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration\n\n - Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end\n\n - Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like\n\n - Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$124,000 - $185,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n \n\n#LI-AD1\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$124K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"cdaab4f2-664c-4686-99c2-a7410cc052de","tierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"87a42a2e-d2e5-4ee9-8c63-82dd5a64b1b6","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e2898019-e8e7-4331-ad33-e379008ba367","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"263e853d-f9d2-40a0-be8c-c64db0d76fdf","summary":"$124K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000}]}},{"id":"4727eb5e-0ff2-4866-bba2-91bb43796d12","title":"CX Operations Engineer","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-22T16:42:56.140+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4727eb5e-0ff2-4866-bba2-91bb43796d12","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4727eb5e-0ff2-4866-bba2-91bb43796d12/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$124,000 - $185,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.\n\nReporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.\n\nThis role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features\n\n - Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers\n\n - Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends\n\n - Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality\n\n - Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need\n\n - Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack\n\n - Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it\n\n - Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data\n\n - Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment\n\n - Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments\n\n - Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale\n\n - Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration\n\n - Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end\n\n - Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like\n\n - Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$124,000 - $185,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AD1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$124K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1b305592-01bc-409c-affc-2ae757cc6b60","tierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"56963c42-5518-4a50-8e28-afa200d763c0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"be82ca2b-4f03-4d56-b8b6-a5272892fd66","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"89efc076-2bd2-4601-a5ee-4ba49b4c1654","summary":"$124K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000}]}},{"id":"649c64f3-a67f-4029-a8ab-b2cc07fc0ddc","title":"CX Operations Engineer","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-22T16:43:24.730+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/649c64f3-a67f-4029-a8ab-b2cc07fc0ddc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/649c64f3-a67f-4029-a8ab-b2cc07fc0ddc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$124,000 - $185,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's support org is growing fast, and keeping our specialists equipped to handle an increasingly complex product requires more than good processes, it requires smart tooling. We're looking for a CX Operations Engineer who has built this before and can hit the ground running.\n\nReporting to the CX Operations Manager, you'll own the automation infrastructure, AI-assisted workflows, and reporting systems that make our specialists faster and more effective. Working alongside the Support Systems Administrator (platform infrastructure and config) and the CX Operations Lead (Zendesk-native features including Copilot and Chatbot), your lane is everything built on top of or extending beyond that foundation, custom integrations, cross-stack automation, and the technical layer that connects it all.\n\nThis role is for someone who deeply understands CX operations, has a track record of building AI and automation tooling in production environments, and is energized by making support and human agents better.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and maintain AI-assisted tools that improve how support specialists triage, research, and resolve tickets; including agent-facing copilots, knowledge surfacing tools, and response assist features\n\n - Own the automation layer across the support stack, building custom integrations, cross-tool workflows, and solutions that extend beyond what Zendesk natively offers\n\n - Partner with Data team to build and maintain reporting infrastructure that gives the support org real-time and historical visibility into volume, quality, efficiency, and trends\n\n - Identify manual or repetitive agent workflows and architect automated or AI-assisted alternatives that reduce friction without sacrificing quality\n\n - Partner with the Support Enablement Lead to integrate tooling improvements into how agents are trained and how knowledge is surfaced in the moment of need\n\n - Collaborate with the Support Systems Administrator to ensure automation and AI initiatives are implemented and maintained cleanly within the core support stack\n\n - Partner closely with the Support Systems Administrator and CX Operations Lead — they own the Zendesk platform and its native features; you own what's built beyond it\n\n - Evaluate new tools, run structured pilots, and bring recommendations to leadership with clear rationale and data\n\n - Document systems, integration logic, and automation workflows to ensure maintainability as the org scales\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5-7+ years of experience in CX operations or CX tooling in an AI-forward environment\n\n - Demonstrated track record of shipping AI-assisted workflows and automation in live support environments\n\n - Deep hands-on experience with AI tooling in the support/CX space: LLM-powered copilots, RAG systems, agent assist platforms, and how to deploy them responsibly at scale\n\n - Expert-level familiarity with support platforms (Zendesk strongly preferred), including working with APIs and integration layers beyond out-of-the-box configuration\n\n - Built and owned reporting systems end-to-end\n\n - Strong operational intuition: you've worked in or alongside support teams and understand what agent friction actually looks like\n\n - Clear communicator who can translate technical decisions for non-technical stakeholders and leadership\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$124,000 - $185,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n \n\n#LI-AD1\n\n \n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$124K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c18765b5-3e20-442a-ac83-d72650a8aee3","tierSummary":"$124K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5e6bc2af-2451-4ad1-bd7d-1bf1b4751659","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ae98a1e1-7e68-4239-9435-c99ecf11c77e","summary":"$124K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000},{"id":"c3fce85f-0096-4cc2-9674-4427bac77be2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":185000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"754bb046-a622-40dd-8416-0af87f1f0301","title":"Senior Analytics Engineer, Product","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-04T00:14:59.530+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/754bb046-a622-40dd-8416-0af87f1f0301","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/754bb046-a622-40dd-8416-0af87f1f0301/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a versatile Senior Analytics Engineer focusing on Product to architect event data models that power decision-making at Harvey. With product-market fit already proven and demand surging across diverse customer segments, you’ll design clean, reliable pipelines and semantic data models that turn raw events into usable insights. As an Analytics Engineer on our team, you’ll help evolve our data stack, champion best practices in testing and documentation, and collaborate closely with product, GTM, and leadership to ensure every team can answer its own questions with confidence. If you combine engineering rigor with a love of storytelling through data we’d love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable data models and pipelines using dbt to transform raw data into clean, reliable assets that power company-wide analytics and decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and implement a robust semantic layer (e.g. LookML/Omni/Other) that standardizes key business metrics, dimensions, and data products, ensuring self-serve capabilities for stakeholders across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with Product, GTM, Finance, and the Exec Team to deliver intuitive, consistent dashboards and analytical tools that surface business health metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and champion data modeling standards and best practices, guiding the organization in how to model data for accuracy, performance, usability, and long-term maintainability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Managers, Engineers, and Data teams to design tracking plans for new product surfaces, ensuring events are implemented accurately, consistently, and with downstream analytics use cases in mind.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the product event tracking strategy, including event naming conventions, property schemas, identity resolution, sessionization, versioning, deprecation, and documentation standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empower stakeholders with data by making analytical assets easily discoverable, reliable, and well-documented – turning complex datasets into actionable insights for the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll define the structure, taxonomy, governance, and modeling patterns for product event data, ensuring that user behavior, product usage, and customer journeys are captured consistently from instrumentation through analytics-ready models.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Science, or similar field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in SQL, dbt, Python, Snowflake.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with modern BI tools like (Looker/Omni, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at defining core business and product metrics, uncovering insights, and resolving data inconsistencies across complex systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong familiarity with version control (GitHub), CI/CD, and modern development workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias for action – you prefer launching usable, iterative data models that deliver immediate value over waiting for perfect solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can build trusted partnerships across Product, GTM, Finance, and Exec stakeholders.<br />Comfortable working through ambiguity in fast-moving, cross-functional environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balances big-picture thinking with precision in execution – knowing when to sweat the details and when to move quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience modeling high-volume, semi-structured product event data, including JSON payloads, nested properties, user/account identifiers, sessions, funnels, cohorts, and behavioral metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with product analytics tools (Mixpanel, Segment, Amplitude)</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bonus</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Early employee at a hyper-growth startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data Engineering Experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing data warehouse (preferably Snowflake)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at world-class enterprise orgs (ex: Brex, Ramp, Stripe, Palantir)</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,800 - $233,600 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for a versatile Senior Analytics Engineer focusing on Product to architect event data models that power decision-making at Harvey. With product-market fit already proven and demand surging across diverse customer segments, you’ll design clean, reliable pipelines and semantic data models that turn raw events into usable insights. As an Analytics Engineer on our team, you’ll help evolve our data stack, champion best practices in testing and documentation, and collaborate closely with product, GTM, and leadership to ensure every team can answer its own questions with confidence. If you combine engineering rigor with a love of storytelling through data we’d love to meet you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable data models and pipelines using dbt to transform raw data into clean, reliable assets that power company-wide analytics and decision-making.\n\n - Define and implement a robust semantic layer (e.g. LookML/Omni/Other) that standardizes key business metrics, dimensions, and data products, ensuring self-serve capabilities for stakeholders across teams.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with Product, GTM, Finance, and the Exec Team to deliver intuitive, consistent dashboards and analytical tools that surface business health metrics.\n\n - Establish and champion data modeling standards and best practices, guiding the organization in how to model data for accuracy, performance, usability, and long-term maintainability.\n\n - Partner with Product Managers, Engineers, and Data teams to design tracking plans for new product surfaces, ensuring events are implemented accurately, consistently, and with downstream analytics use cases in mind.\n\n - Own the product event tracking strategy, including event naming conventions, property schemas, identity resolution, sessionization, versioning, deprecation, and documentation standards.\n\n - Empower stakeholders with data by making analytical assets easily discoverable, reliable, and well-documented – turning complex datasets into actionable insights for the business.\n\n - You’ll define the structure, taxonomy, governance, and modeling patterns for product event data, ensuring that user behavior, product usage, and customer journeys are captured consistently from instrumentation through analytics-ready models.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Science, or similar field.\n\n - Deep expertise in SQL, dbt, Python, Snowflake.\n\n - Experience with modern BI tools like (Looker/Omni, or similar).\n\n - Skilled at defining core business and product metrics, uncovering insights, and resolving data inconsistencies across complex systems.\n\n - Strong familiarity with version control (GitHub), CI/CD, and modern development workflows.\n\n - Bias for action – you prefer launching usable, iterative data models that deliver immediate value over waiting for perfect solutions.\n\n - Strong communicator who can build trusted partnerships across Product, GTM, Finance, and Exec stakeholders.\n   Comfortable working through ambiguity in fast-moving, cross-functional environments.\n\n - Balances big-picture thinking with precision in execution – knowing when to sweat the details and when to move quickly.\n\n - Experience modeling high-volume, semi-structured product event data, including JSON payloads, nested properties, user/account identifiers, sessions, funnels, cohorts, and behavioral metrics.\n\n - Experience with product analytics tools (Mixpanel, Segment, Amplitude)\n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Early employee at a hyper-growth startup\n\n - Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs\n\n - Data Engineering Experience\n\n - Experience managing data warehouse (preferably Snowflake)\n\n - Experience at world-class enterprise orgs (ex: Brex, Ramp, Stripe, Palantir)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,800 - $233,600 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.8K – $233.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.8K - $233.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6b99abfd-17b8-4461-a920-8fe5c1db77ca","tierSummary":"$155.8K – $233.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"43f2f85b-2212-4a18-922b-a2226f07f010","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fbf368fd-9e7f-424e-965b-77d37d29a4e3","summary":"$155.8K – $233.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155800,"maxValue":233600},{"id":"18ca6781-b5df-4b60-9c59-910f1492dce1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155800,"maxValue":233600},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"cf7b6b62-44c6-40ae-ac94-7f903370dcd5","title":"Senior Analytics Engineer, Finance","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-05-25T17:14:25.241+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cf7b6b62-44c6-40ae-ac94-7f903370dcd5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cf7b6b62-44c6-40ae-ac94-7f903370dcd5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a versatile Senior Analytics Engineer to partner closely with our Finance team in building the financial data foundation that drives decision-making at Harvey. With product-market fit already proven and demand surging across diverse customer segments, you’ll design clean, reliable pipelines and semantic data models that turn source data into usable insights. As an Analytics Engineer on our team, you’ll help evolve our data stack, champion best practices in testing and documentation, and collaborate closely with product, finance, and leadership to ensure every team can answer its own questions with confidence. If you combine engineering rigor with a love of storytelling through data we’d love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build scalable data models and pipelines using dbt to transform raw data into clean, reliable assets that power company-wide financial analytics and decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and implement a robust semantic layer (e.g. LookML/Omni/Other) that standardizes financial and operating metrics, including revenue, retention, customer growth, usage, margin, and forecast inputs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with Product, Finance, and the Exec Team to deliver intuitive, consistent dashboards and analytical tools that surface business health metrics (ARR, NRR).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and champion data modeling standards and best practices, guiding the organization in how to model data for accuracy, performance, usability, and long-term maintainability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead data governance initiatives, ensuring high standards of data quality, consistency, documentation, and access control across the analytics ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structure financial metric definitions, business logic, and accounting context in ways that can support AI-assisted reporting, natural language analytics, and automated anomaly detection.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Science, or similar field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in SQL, dbt, Python, Snowflake.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with modern BI tools like (Looker/Omni, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at defining core financial and operating metrics, uncovering insights, and resolving data inconsistencies across complex systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong familiarity with version control (GitHub), CI/CD, and modern development workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias for action – you prefer launching usable, iterative data models that deliver immediate value over waiting for perfect solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can build trusted partnerships across Finance, GTM, Product, and Exec stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working through ambiguity in fast-moving, cross-functional environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balances big-picture thinking with precision in execution — knowing when to sweat the details and when to move quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience modeling financial, billing, subscription, CRM, or usage-based revenue data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of business metrics such as ARR, MRR, churn, retention, expansion, bookings, billings, and revenue recognition.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Early employee at a hyper-growth startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data Engineering Experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing data warehouse (preferably Snowflake)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at world-class enterprise orgs (ex: Brex, Ramp, Stripe, Palantir)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,000 - $235,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for a versatile Senior Analytics Engineer to partner closely with our Finance team in building the financial data foundation that drives decision-making at Harvey. With product-market fit already proven and demand surging across diverse customer segments, you’ll design clean, reliable pipelines and semantic data models that turn source data into usable insights. As an Analytics Engineer on our team, you’ll help evolve our data stack, champion best practices in testing and documentation, and collaborate closely with product, finance, and leadership to ensure every team can answer its own questions with confidence. If you combine engineering rigor with a love of storytelling through data we’d love to meet you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and build scalable data models and pipelines using dbt to transform raw data into clean, reliable assets that power company-wide financial analytics and decision-making.\n\n - Define and implement a robust semantic layer (e.g. LookML/Omni/Other) that standardizes financial and operating metrics, including revenue, retention, customer growth, usage, margin, and forecast inputs.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with Product, Finance, and the Exec Team to deliver intuitive, consistent dashboards and analytical tools that surface business health metrics (ARR, NRR).\n\n - Establish and champion data modeling standards and best practices, guiding the organization in how to model data for accuracy, performance, usability, and long-term maintainability.\n\n - Lead data governance initiatives, ensuring high standards of data quality, consistency, documentation, and access control across the analytics ecosystem.\n\n - Structure financial metric definitions, business logic, and accounting context in ways that can support AI-assisted reporting, natural language analytics, and automated anomaly detection.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Science, or similar field.\n\n - Deep expertise in SQL, dbt, Python, Snowflake.\n\n - Experience with modern BI tools like (Looker/Omni, or similar).\n\n - Skilled at defining core financial and operating metrics, uncovering insights, and resolving data inconsistencies across complex systems.\n\n - Strong familiarity with version control (GitHub), CI/CD, and modern development workflows.\n\n - Bias for action – you prefer launching usable, iterative data models that deliver immediate value over waiting for perfect solutions.\n\n - Strong communicator who can build trusted partnerships across Finance, GTM, Product, and Exec stakeholders.\n\n - Comfortable working through ambiguity in fast-moving, cross-functional environments.\n\n - Balances big-picture thinking with precision in execution — knowing when to sweat the details and when to move quickly.\n\n - Experience modeling financial, billing, subscription, CRM, or usage-based revenue data.\n\n - Strong understanding of business metrics such as ARR, MRR, churn, retention, expansion, bookings, billings, and revenue recognition.\n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Early employee at a hyper-growth startup\n\n - Experience with or knowledge of AI and LLMs\n\n - Data Engineering Experience\n\n - Experience managing data warehouse (preferably Snowflake)\n\n - Experience at world-class enterprise orgs (ex: Brex, Ramp, Stripe, Palantir)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,000 - $235,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155K – $235K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155K - $235K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"68a22b0e-2bd2-42c0-9cf2-5ef4aad6bb3e","tierSummary":"$155K – $235K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"83188ca1-c2b4-4760-954f-d06ff63260bf","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5b82c97c-fb6e-4471-944c-4b1966de585f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4972c5cd-5670-4312-9b09-43d37f8ad5a8","summary":"$155K – $235K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":235000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":235000}]}},{"id":"d05dd346-a604-4299-b770-bb1210f7436b","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Milan","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-11T04:30:47.194+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d05dd346-a604-4299-b770-bb1210f7436b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d05dd346-a604-4299-b770-bb1210f7436b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1>Role Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an Enterprise Account Executive to lead commercial growth across Italy. This role is responsible for identifying opportunities, managing complex sales cycles, and building long-term relationships within the legal and professional services sector.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position will play a key role in expanding Harvey’s presence in the Italian region, working cross-functionally to deliver tailored solutions to clients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You’ll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver against sales targets with a focus on sustainable growth and performance excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and grow a portfolio of named enterprise accounts across Italy, driving full-funnel sales activity from prospecting through to commercial negotiation and onboarding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand client pain points, organisational structure, and buying processes; tailor solutions that align with strategic outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead high-impact product demos and client meetings that clearly articulate Harvey’s business value and technical capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, legal, engineering, and GTM to inform roadmap and surface client needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop deep, long-term relationships with legal, innovation, and executive stakeholders across the region.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You Have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, preferably with exposure to AI, legaltech, or vertical software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of success managing complex sales cycles with multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain technical products to non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal industry and a commitment to enhancing knowledge work through technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with enterprise sales practices in Italy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and results-oriented, with a collaborative approach to working cross-functionally</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Additional Information for Postings</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Italy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Italian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Italy team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><u>here</u></a>].</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are seeking an Enterprise Account Executive to lead commercial growth across Italy. This role is responsible for identifying opportunities, managing complex sales cycles, and building long-term relationships within the legal and professional services sector.\n\nThis position will play a key role in expanding Harvey’s presence in the Italian region, working cross-functionally to deliver tailored solutions to clients.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Deliver against sales targets with a focus on sustainable growth and performance excellence.\n\n - Own and grow a portfolio of named enterprise accounts across Italy, driving full-funnel sales activity from prospecting through to commercial negotiation and onboarding.\n\n - Understand client pain points, organisational structure, and buying processes; tailor solutions that align with strategic outcomes.\n\n - Lead high-impact product demos and client meetings that clearly articulate Harvey’s business value and technical capabilities.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, legal, engineering, and GTM to inform roadmap and surface client needs.\n\n - Develop deep, long-term relationships with legal, innovation, and executive stakeholders across the region.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, preferably with exposure to AI, legaltech, or vertical software\n\n - Track record of success managing complex sales cycles with multiple stakeholders\n\n - Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain technical products to non-technical audiences\n\n - Interest in the legal industry and a commitment to enhancing knowledge work through technology\n\n - Familiarity with enterprise sales practices in Italy\n\n - Self-motivated and results-oriented, with a collaborative approach to working cross-functionally\n\n\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION FOR POSTINGS\n\n - Location: Italy\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Italian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Italy team\n\n - Opportunities to work on cross-functional go-to-market initiatives, with a focus on scaling sales strategy and driving revenue growth\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"88fea7f9-b477-49ee-b1bf-5ad98a8e68e6","title":"Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T18:23:08.670+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88fea7f9-b477-49ee-b1bf-5ad98a8e68e6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88fea7f9-b477-49ee-b1bf-5ad98a8e68e6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager is a strategic operator who partners closely with Harvey's Enterprise sales organization to accelerate rep effectiveness and drive revenue outcomes. Sitting within the GTM Enablement team, this person designs and scales the programs that prepare Enterprise Account Executives to sell AI solutions to the world's largest law firms and corporate legal departments. The role owns the end-to-end enablement strategy for the Enterprise segment—from skills development and methodology reinforcement to change management and launch readiness—operating as a trusted partner to Enterprise Sales leadership, Product Marketing, and cross-functional GTM teams. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company equips its highest-performing sellers to win in a rapidly evolving market.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and deliver Enterprise-specific enablement programs spanning onboarding, product launches, methodology rollouts, and competitive positioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with the executive leaders and frontline managers to identify skill gaps, define competency standards, and build tailored coaching frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage enablement content, playbooks, and resources aligned to the Enterprise buyer journey and MEDDPICC sales methodology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own program measurement and reporting, tracking leading and lagging indicators of Enablement programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Legal Engineering to translate product and market updates into field-ready assets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive change management for new tools, processes, and go-to-market motions across the Enterprise segment</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–6 years of experience in sales enablement, revenue enablement, or GTM program management, with demonstrated ownership of programs supporting Enterprise or complex sales motions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams, prioritize ruthlessly, and deliver against tight timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication, facilitation, and executive presence; comfortable presenting to and influencing senior sales leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with enterprise sales methodologies (e.g., MEDDPICC, Challenger, Force Management) and experience embedding them into enablement programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in B2B SaaS, legal tech, or AI preferred; strong intellectual curiosity about the legal industry and emerging technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias for action, comfort with ambiguity, and a track record of driving impact in high-growth environments</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000-204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Enterprise Sales Enablement Manager is a strategic operator who partners closely with Harvey's Enterprise sales organization to accelerate rep effectiveness and drive revenue outcomes. Sitting within the GTM Enablement team, this person designs and scales the programs that prepare Enterprise Account Executives to sell AI solutions to the world's largest law firms and corporate legal departments. The role owns the end-to-end enablement strategy for the Enterprise segment—from skills development and methodology reinforcement to change management and launch readiness—operating as a trusted partner to Enterprise Sales leadership, Product Marketing, and cross-functional GTM teams. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company equips its highest-performing sellers to win in a rapidly evolving market.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and deliver Enterprise-specific enablement programs spanning onboarding, product launches, methodology rollouts, and competitive positioning\n\n - Partner directly with the executive leaders and frontline managers to identify skill gaps, define competency standards, and build tailored coaching frameworks\n\n - Develop and manage enablement content, playbooks, and resources aligned to the Enterprise buyer journey and MEDDPICC sales methodology\n\n - Own program measurement and reporting, tracking leading and lagging indicators of Enablement programs\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Legal Engineering to translate product and market updates into field-ready assets\n\n - Drive change management for new tools, processes, and go-to-market motions across the Enterprise segment\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4–6 years of experience in sales enablement, revenue enablement, or GTM program management, with demonstrated ownership of programs supporting Enterprise or complex sales motions\n\n - Strong program management skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams, prioritize ruthlessly, and deliver against tight timelines\n\n - Excellent communication, facilitation, and executive presence; comfortable presenting to and influencing senior sales leadership\n\n - Familiarity with enterprise sales methodologies (e.g., MEDDPICC, Challenger, Force Management) and experience embedding them into enablement programs\n\n - Experience in B2B SaaS, legal tech, or AI preferred; strong intellectual curiosity about the legal industry and emerging technology\n\n - A bias for action, comfort with ambiguity, and a track record of driving impact in high-growth environments\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000-204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TM1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bdc3763b-4562-4952-a13c-7786186b2567","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ed6a87d5-7fad-48a3-ab0e-edfc46ac204d","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"7080de8f-2f9d-4f64-abd3-609f293154cb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2afeecc1-d272-4562-a8df-50f720f5991d","title":"Trust Engineer","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-02T15:29:07.708+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2afeecc1-d272-4562-a8df-50f720f5991d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2afeecc1-d272-4562-a8df-50f720f5991d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform and earning that trust is a business enabler we value above all else. In this role, you'll report to the Head of Trust and serve as the engineering backbone of Harvey's compliance and assurance programs. You'll build and own the data infrastructure, automation tooling, and AI-powered workflows that allow our Trust team to scale audit readiness, continuous monitoring, and risk reporting without scaling headcount. This means selecting best-in-class compliance automation platforms, building our own compliance data layer, and developing AI-powered workflows to automate evidence collection, control testing, and assurance reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the implementation and optimization of Harvey's compliance automation tooling to automate workflows across compliance programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build a compliance data layer in Snowflake — ingesting signals from infrastructure, security tools, and SaaS platforms to create a real-time view of control health and audit readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop AI agents and automated pipelines for evidence collection, control testing, and continuous monitoring at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering and Security to map technical implementations to compliance controls and maintain a living, accurate control inventory</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reporting layers that translate compliance signals into clear narratives on risk posture and certification status for executive and cross-functional audiences</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years in software, data, or security engineering with exposure to compliance automation or trust and assurance programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building data pipelines on Snowflake, BigQuery, or comparable platforms; strong SQL and Python</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing or administering compliance automation platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of at least one compliance framework — enough to understand control requirements and map them to technical implementations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building AI-powered workflows or agents using LLMs</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a high-growth SaaS company building or scaling a Trust or compliance engineering function from the ground up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure) and how infrastructure-as-code tools connect to compliance evidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior involvement in government compliance programs</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $330,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform and earning that trust is a business enabler we value above all else. In this role, you'll report to the Head of Trust and serve as the engineering backbone of Harvey's compliance and assurance programs. You'll build and own the data infrastructure, automation tooling, and AI-powered workflows that allow our Trust team to scale audit readiness, continuous monitoring, and risk reporting without scaling headcount. This means selecting best-in-class compliance automation platforms, building our own compliance data layer, and developing AI-powered workflows to automate evidence collection, control testing, and assurance reporting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the implementation and optimization of Harvey's compliance automation tooling to automate workflows across compliance programs\n\n - Design and build a compliance data layer in Snowflake — ingesting signals from infrastructure, security tools, and SaaS platforms to create a real-time view of control health and audit readiness\n\n - Develop AI agents and automated pipelines for evidence collection, control testing, and continuous monitoring at scale\n\n - Partner with Engineering and Security to map technical implementations to compliance controls and maintain a living, accurate control inventory\n\n - Build reporting layers that translate compliance signals into clear narratives on risk posture and certification status for executive and cross-functional audiences\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years in software, data, or security engineering with exposure to compliance automation or trust and assurance programs\n\n - Hands-on experience building data pipelines on Snowflake, BigQuery, or comparable platforms; strong SQL and Python\n\n - Experience implementing or administering compliance automation platforms\n\n - Working knowledge of at least one compliance framework — enough to understand control requirements and map them to technical implementations\n\n - Experience building AI-powered workflows or agents using LLMs\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience at a high-growth SaaS company building or scaling a Trust or compliance engineering function from the ground up\n\n - Familiarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure) and how infrastructure-as-code tools connect to compliance evidence\n\n - Prior involvement in government compliance programs\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$220,000 - $330,000 USD\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $330K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e4cb48a5-0e3f-4998-8000-dd5152b9d011","tierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"acd00913-e8d9-46e8-878f-21e73ea453fd","summary":"$220K – $330K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"id":"975f0d22-16a9-4fcf-b1fd-720d400ebe38","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ff9af90d-f6ee-4f44-b646-744dbd722f2c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"467049ce-b5ea-4063-95aa-71c9742768d5","title":"Technical Program Manager, Platform & Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-02T15:09:12.400+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/467049ce-b5ea-4063-95aa-71c9742768d5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/467049ce-b5ea-4063-95aa-71c9742768d5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Staff Technical Program Manager, Platform &amp; Infrastructure</strong> to drive Harvey's most critical platform and infrastructure programs as the business scales. You will be the connective tissue across Core Infrastructure, Backend Platform, and product engineering teams, and cross-functional teams such as Security and Finance, owning the multi-quarter horizontal initiatives that define how Harvey scales: cloud migrations, cost optimization, capacity and performance planning, BYOC, and the buildout of Harvey's internal platform foundations. You will be going deep technically with senior platform and infrastructure engineers, aligning EMs and execs around durable plans, and driving programs from ambiguous mandate through measurable delivery.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end execution of Harvey's most strategic platform &amp; infrastructure programs, including cloud migrations, infrastructure cost optimization, capacity planning, BYOC, and the buildout of the new Backend Platform team's foundations, partnering deeply with Infra and Platform leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Harvey's infrastructure cost program: establish ownership, accountability, and reporting mechanisms across engineering teams; partner with Finance on forecasting and unit economics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive horizontal platform &amp; infrastructure initiatives end-to-end, coordinating across engineering, security, and GTM teams as needed to unblock execution and align stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own structured engagement with strategic external vendors (AWS, Azure, OpenAI, Anthropic), including capacity commitments, contract optimization, escalation paths, and joint planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define, measure, and report on platform &amp; infrastructure health metrics (cost, capacity headroom, migration progress, platform adoption, reliability SLOs), and hold the org accountable for sustained improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify systemic gaps in platform maturity, infrastructure planning, capacity, and observability; convert findings into structured multi-quarter roadmaps with clear owners, milestones, and risk surfacing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run the operating cadence for platform &amp; infrastructure programs: working groups, steering reviews, exec readouts, and risk reviews. Make program status legible to leadership without creating overhead for engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with senior ICs and EMs to evaluate architectural tradeoffs, sequence dependencies across teams, and unblock execution when programs hit friction.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in technical program management, with a track record of driving large, ambiguous, multi-quarter platform or infrastructure programs to completion at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep technical fluency in core platform and infrastructure domains: cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP), Kubernetes, databases, networking, observability, CI/CD, and platform/service frameworks. You don't need to write production code, but you read system designs critically and push back substantively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience driving at least one of: a cloud migration at scale, a major infrastructure cost program with measurable financial impact, an internal platform buildout, or a comparably large horizontal platform/infrastructure initiative.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead and influence senior engineering stakeholders, including Staff+ ICs, engineering managers, and executive sponsors, without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication, with a particular ability to distill complex technical tradeoffs into crisp narratives for exec audiences and across functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building durable mechanisms (review forums, metrics, operating cadences) that outlive any individual program and scale with the org.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity. You're energized by problems that aren't yet well-defined and where the first step is to scope the problem itself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience driving infrastructure cost programs in a high-growth environment (target metrics like cost per tenant, infrastructure as % of revenue).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading a cloud migration, BYOC rollout, or major platform consolidation end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience standing up or scaling an internal platform / developer experience function from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing strategic vendor relationships with hyperscalers (AWS, Azure, GCP) or foundation model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the modern infra stack at scale: Terraform, Kubernetes, service meshes, data platforms, and observability tools (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as an engineering manager, platform/infrastructure engineer, or SRE before moving into program management.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$188,000 - $278,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Staff Technical Program Manager, Platform & Infrastructure to drive Harvey's most critical platform and infrastructure programs as the business scales. You will be the connective tissue across Core Infrastructure, Backend Platform, and product engineering teams, and cross-functional teams such as Security and Finance, owning the multi-quarter horizontal initiatives that define how Harvey scales: cloud migrations, cost optimization, capacity and performance planning, BYOC, and the buildout of Harvey's internal platform foundations. You will be going deep technically with senior platform and infrastructure engineers, aligning EMs and execs around durable plans, and driving programs from ambiguous mandate through measurable delivery.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end execution of Harvey's most strategic platform & infrastructure programs, including cloud migrations, infrastructure cost optimization, capacity planning, BYOC, and the buildout of the new Backend Platform team's foundations, partnering deeply with Infra and Platform leadership.\n\n - Lead Harvey's infrastructure cost program: establish ownership, accountability, and reporting mechanisms across engineering teams; partner with Finance on forecasting and unit economics.\n\n - Drive horizontal platform & infrastructure initiatives end-to-end, coordinating across engineering, security, and GTM teams as needed to unblock execution and align stakeholders.\n\n - Own structured engagement with strategic external vendors (AWS, Azure, OpenAI, Anthropic), including capacity commitments, contract optimization, escalation paths, and joint planning.\n\n - Define, measure, and report on platform & infrastructure health metrics (cost, capacity headroom, migration progress, platform adoption, reliability SLOs), and hold the org accountable for sustained improvement.\n\n - Identify systemic gaps in platform maturity, infrastructure planning, capacity, and observability; convert findings into structured multi-quarter roadmaps with clear owners, milestones, and risk surfacing.\n\n - Run the operating cadence for platform & infrastructure programs: working groups, steering reviews, exec readouts, and risk reviews. Make program status legible to leadership without creating overhead for engineering teams.\n\n - Partner with senior ICs and EMs to evaluate architectural tradeoffs, sequence dependencies across teams, and unblock execution when programs hit friction.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in technical program management, with a track record of driving large, ambiguous, multi-quarter platform or infrastructure programs to completion at scale.\n\n - Deep technical fluency in core platform and infrastructure domains: cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP), Kubernetes, databases, networking, observability, CI/CD, and platform/service frameworks. You don't need to write production code, but you read system designs critically and push back substantively.\n\n - Experience driving at least one of: a cloud migration at scale, a major infrastructure cost program with measurable financial impact, an internal platform buildout, or a comparably large horizontal platform/infrastructure initiative.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead and influence senior engineering stakeholders, including Staff+ ICs, engineering managers, and executive sponsors, without direct authority.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication, with a particular ability to distill complex technical tradeoffs into crisp narratives for exec audiences and across functions.\n\n - A track record of building durable mechanisms (review forums, metrics, operating cadences) that outlive any individual program and scale with the org.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity. You're energized by problems that aren't yet well-defined and where the first step is to scope the problem itself.\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field.\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience driving infrastructure cost programs in a high-growth environment (target metrics like cost per tenant, infrastructure as % of revenue).\n\n - Experience leading a cloud migration, BYOC rollout, or major platform consolidation end-to-end.\n\n - Experience standing up or scaling an internal platform / developer experience function from the ground up.\n\n - Experience managing strategic vendor relationships with hyperscalers (AWS, Azure, GCP) or foundation model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic).\n\n - Familiarity with the modern infra stack at scale: Terraform, Kubernetes, service meshes, data platforms, and observability tools (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana).\n\n - Prior experience as an engineering manager, platform/infrastructure engineer, or SRE before moving into program management.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$188,000 - $278,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$188K – $278K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$188K - $278K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ca8be7f3-839b-44e3-814d-cc77f36b4222","tierSummary":"$188K – $278K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"08f3dcfe-fde8-42de-869d-5f41988a23da","summary":"$188K – $278K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":278000},{"id":"946a7105-3ff6-412f-be78-1aa6e1f2dc9d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e8407a6d-4611-4cdd-8b77-7290203e3ced","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":278000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e89103ca-765f-42f1-882a-80364f3c2321","title":"Staff Product Manager, New Products","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-02T19:57:06.721+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e89103ca-765f-42f1-882a-80364f3c2321","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e89103ca-765f-42f1-882a-80364f3c2321/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the platform that defines how legal and professional services teams work with AI. As our product matures and adoption scales, our ecosystem — integrations, APIs, data partnerships, and third-party extensibility — is becoming a core growth lever and strategic differentiator.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Staff Product Manager to lead 0→1 product development on one of Harvey's strategic bets. In this role, you'll own the vision, roadmap, and execution for a new product at the intersection of AI, legal data, and how legal work gets done. You'll work across product pillars to define what we build and partner closely with engineering, product, and design to bring it to life. The right person has strong instincts for enterprise workflows, thrives with ambiguity, and can translate buyer and user needs into decisions that create durable value.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a highly strategic role at the intersection of platform, product, and partnerships. You'll work closely with engineering, design, partnerships, and GTM teams to build integrations that are not just functional, but transformative—making Harvey the system of intelligence for professional work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the Product Vision:</strong> Define and execute the product strategy for Harvey's new product across the Harvey application, Word Add-In, Outlook plugin, and beyond</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Integration Prioritization:</strong> Work closely with the Integrations engineering pod and Partnerships team to prioritize, scope, and ship integrations that drive customer value and competitive differentiation. Translate partner and customer demand signals into a coherent product roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Leadership:</strong> Collaborate closely with Engineering, GTM, Customer Success, and PMM to ensure investments are aligned with commercial strategy and customer needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commercial Sense:</strong> Partner with GTM and Partnerships to translate new capabilities into sales enablement, positioning, and customer-facing narratives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Measurement &amp; Iteration:</strong> Define success metrics for health and iterate based on data.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$213,600 - $300,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the platform that defines how legal and professional services teams work with AI. As our product matures and adoption scales, our ecosystem — integrations, APIs, data partnerships, and third-party extensibility — is becoming a core growth lever and strategic differentiator.\n\nWe're looking for a Staff Product Manager to lead 0→1 product development on one of Harvey's strategic bets. In this role, you'll own the vision, roadmap, and execution for a new product at the intersection of AI, legal data, and how legal work gets done. You'll work across product pillars to define what we build and partner closely with engineering, product, and design to bring it to life. The right person has strong instincts for enterprise workflows, thrives with ambiguity, and can translate buyer and user needs into decisions that create durable value.\n\nThis is a highly strategic role at the intersection of platform, product, and partnerships. You'll work closely with engineering, design, partnerships, and GTM teams to build integrations that are not just functional, but transformative—making Harvey the system of intelligence for professional work.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the Product Vision: Define and execute the product strategy for Harvey's new product across the Harvey application, Word Add-In, Outlook plugin, and beyond\n\n - Integration Prioritization: Work closely with the Integrations engineering pod and Partnerships team to prioritize, scope, and ship integrations that drive customer value and competitive differentiation. Translate partner and customer demand signals into a coherent product roadmap.\n\n - Cross-Functional Leadership: Collaborate closely with Engineering, GTM, Customer Success, and PMM to ensure investments are aligned with commercial strategy and customer needs.\n\n - Commercial Sense: Partner with GTM and Partnerships to translate new capabilities into sales enablement, positioning, and customer-facing narratives.\n\n - Measurement & Iteration: Define success metrics for health and iterate based on data.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.\n\n - Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.\n\n - Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.\n\n - Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$213,600 - $300,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$213.6K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$213.6K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"194363c8-6931-4743-90a2-e658a59a7d01","tierSummary":"$213.6K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9003272e-bd48-4e67-a8ca-837e5c9e56a3","summary":"$213.6K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":213600,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"b53ae6a0-135a-4145-bd02-3a91df038d70","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4c7c22ea-37a3-4e6a-b933-54031e3f6dca","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":213600,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2f35e50f-2978-44c3-a495-7cbfc1f512d4","title":"Compliance Analyst","department":"Security","team":"Trust","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T22:05:25.977+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2f35e50f-2978-44c3-a495-7cbfc1f512d4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2f35e50f-2978-44c3-a495-7cbfc1f512d4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you'll report to the Senior Compliance Manager and serve as a core executor on Harvey's certification and audit portfolio. You will be responsible for the hands-on compliance work that keeps our compliance programs healthy, maintaining control documentation, coordinating evidence collection, supporting third-party assessments, and working closely with Engineering and Security teams to ensure controls are implemented, tested, and continuously monitored. This is a role for a detail-oriented practitioner who takes pride in getting the compliance fundamentals exactly right.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and maintain core compliance documentation — including compliance packages and security assessment reports — keeping them accurate and audit-ready</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate evidence collection across Engineering, Infrastructure, and Security for regulated assessments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support third-party assessor engagements end-to-end: scheduling, preparing teams, triaging findings, and drafting responses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct gap analyses against applicable frameworks and produce remediation tracking artifacts teams can act on directly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage continuous monitoring activities including control reviews, change notifications, and incident documentation to maintain compliance status</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering and Security to validate control implementations and translate regulatory language into testable technical configurations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5+ years in information security compliance with hands-on exposure to government and industry frameworks in a SaaS or cloud environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid working knowledge of applicable government compliance frameworks; ability to map controls to technical implementations and evaluate evidence quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience maintaining compliance documentation and tracking remediation activities; familiarity with compliance automation tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams and keep documentation aligned with a dynamic cloud environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator: able to write crisp control implementation statements and explain compliance requirements to engineering audiences</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $181,300</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.\n\n\n\nOur customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.\n\n\n\nIn this role, you'll report to the Senior Compliance Manager and serve as a core executor on Harvey's certification and audit portfolio. You will be responsible for the hands-on compliance work that keeps our compliance programs healthy, maintaining control documentation, coordinating evidence collection, supporting third-party assessments, and working closely with Engineering and Security teams to ensure controls are implemented, tested, and continuously monitored. This is a role for a detail-oriented practitioner who takes pride in getting the compliance fundamentals exactly right.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and maintain core compliance documentation — including compliance packages and security assessment reports — keeping them accurate and audit-ready\n\n - Coordinate evidence collection across Engineering, Infrastructure, and Security for regulated assessments\n\n - Support third-party assessor engagements end-to-end: scheduling, preparing teams, triaging findings, and drafting responses\n\n - Conduct gap analyses against applicable frameworks and produce remediation tracking artifacts teams can act on directly\n\n - Manage continuous monitoring activities including control reviews, change notifications, and incident documentation to maintain compliance status\n\n - Partner with Engineering and Security to validate control implementations and translate regulatory language into testable technical configurations\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3–5+ years in information security compliance with hands-on exposure to government and industry frameworks in a SaaS or cloud environment\n\n - Solid working knowledge of applicable government compliance frameworks; ability to map controls to technical implementations and evaluate evidence quality\n\n - Experience maintaining compliance documentation and tracking remediation activities; familiarity with compliance automation tooling\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams and keep documentation aligned with a dynamic cloud environment\n\n - Clear communicator: able to write crisp control implementation statements and explain compliance requirements to engineering audiences\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $181,300\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $181.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"71f3cca8-72b9-4bf1-bf22-69b9fecfdc4f","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f38e78ed-9ea4-48dd-8b2b-2f294ec3980b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6eb0f034-c701-48e5-af34-490b22fdef01","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8e59edcb-cf2c-4f42-a192-cbdf21364329","summary":"$99.2K – $181.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":181300}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":181300}]}},{"id":"637d5f7d-759d-40f3-868d-f3a45d37ff10","title":"Sales Manager, Enterprise","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T04:24:50.051+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/637d5f7d-759d-40f3-868d-f3a45d37ff10","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/637d5f7d-759d-40f3-868d-f3a45d37ff10/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Enterprise Sales Manager, Singapore will be the founding sales leader in the market, responsible for establishing and scaling Harvey's enterprise go-to-market motion across Southeast Asia. This role will build and coach a team of high-performing Account Executives driving the growth of Harvey's AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets in the region. As the first sales manager on the ground in Singapore, this person will define the local playbook, develop regional client relationships, and serve as a key member of Harvey's APAC founding team. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and build from scratch with limited oversight — combining the mindset of a player-coach with the strategic vision to scale. This is a rare opportunity to shape Harvey's presence in one of the world's most dynamic legal markets from the ground up.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish Harvey's enterprise sales presence in Singapore, building the foundation for a high-performing regional team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recruit, mentor, and lead a team of consultative, solution-based Enterprise sales professionals as the market grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own long-term strategy and day-to-day operations of the Singapore sales team, including pipeline development, forecasting, and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and adapt Harvey's sales playbook for the Southeast Asian market, documenting learnings that can be applied regionally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Legal Engineering, and Customer Success to build effective processes and solutions for regional clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cultivate relationships with law firms, in-house legal teams, and professional services organizations across the region.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of tech sales experience and 5+ years of people management experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or scaling Enterprise sales teams in APAC or emerging markets, ideally within SaaS or legal technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients using a consultative, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences, including senior legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for AI and its potential applications in knowledge work, with interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers work more effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by ambiguity, early-stage environments, and building foundational processes from the ground up.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong> Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Enterprise Sales Manager, Singapore will be the founding sales leader in the market, responsible for establishing and scaling Harvey's enterprise go-to-market motion across Southeast Asia. This role will build and coach a team of high-performing Account Executives driving the growth of Harvey's AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets in the region. As the first sales manager on the ground in Singapore, this person will define the local playbook, develop regional client relationships, and serve as a key member of Harvey's APAC founding team. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and build from scratch with limited oversight — combining the mindset of a player-coach with the strategic vision to scale. This is a rare opportunity to shape Harvey's presence in one of the world's most dynamic legal markets from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Establish Harvey's enterprise sales presence in Singapore, building the foundation for a high-performing regional team.\n\n - Recruit, mentor, and lead a team of consultative, solution-based Enterprise sales professionals as the market grows.\n\n - Own long-term strategy and day-to-day operations of the Singapore sales team, including pipeline development, forecasting, and revenue targets.\n\n - Develop and adapt Harvey's sales playbook for the Southeast Asian market, documenting learnings that can be applied regionally.\n\n - Work cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Legal Engineering, and Customer Success to build effective processes and solutions for regional clients.\n\n - Cultivate relationships with law firms, in-house legal teams, and professional services organizations across the region.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of tech sales experience and 5+ years of people management experience.\n\n - Experience building or scaling Enterprise sales teams in APAC or emerging markets, ideally within SaaS or legal technology.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients using a consultative, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences, including senior legal professionals.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for AI and its potential applications in knowledge work, with interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers work more effectively.\n\n - Energized by ambiguity, early-stage environments, and building foundational processes from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\n PLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-GE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"99aceabe-916e-4491-97e9-42f2471bf087","title":"Account Executive, Mid-Market","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T17:49:23.691+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/99aceabe-916e-4491-97e9-42f2471bf087","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/99aceabe-916e-4491-97e9-42f2471bf087/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$240,000 OTE with a 50/50 split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. \n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene \n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. \n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION \n\n$240,000 OTE with a 50/50 split \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LH1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$240K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$240K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5a2ec7f3-5484-485f-a18d-b621f1117179","tierSummary":"OTE 50/50 Split $240K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fec32f24-69bb-47fc-b76c-c1ce28ecec46","summary":"OTE 50/50 Split $240K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":240000,"maxValue":240000}]}},{"id":"3e12bb8e-1647-40b4-9447-2dea4a5b3e25","title":"Legal Engineering Manager (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T20:21:03.939+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3e12bb8e-1647-40b4-9447-2dea4a5b3e25","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3e12bb8e-1647-40b4-9447-2dea4a5b3e25/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&amp;A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.\n\nLegal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.\n\nThis role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.\n\n - Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.\n\n - Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.\n\n - Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.\n\n - Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.\n\n - Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.\n\n - Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3b99f4c3-2209-4cad-bf77-71d9790bc7c7","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4b39d4f9-945e-4a0d-9ce3-9532f270bd49","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"59cea626-1f26-4f9f-b40b-e804c44fa5c6","summary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}},{"id":"18454695-e72d-40a5-a6c1-99677ef516ad","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-11T13:39:11.480+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/18454695-e72d-40a5-a6c1-99677ef516ad","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/18454695-e72d-40a5-a6c1-99677ef516ad/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Backend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in constructing the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build foundational backend infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of distributed systems, REST/gRPC APIs, databases, and scalable service architectures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Additional Information </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Toronto, Ontario (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Canadian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CA $164,000 - CA $225,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Backend Software Engineer at Harvey, you’ll play a pivotal role in constructing the foundation of our product platform while directly building user-facing features for some of the world’s leading law firms and enterprise customers. This team owns and operates the platform layer that enables secure, reliable, and flexible experiences for our customers including notifications, permissions and feature flag infrastructure. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration experiences for law firms.\n\n\n\nYou will design systems that not only serve as critical infrastructure for the rest of the company, but also directly impact how our users engage with Harvey’s AI-powered legal tools. This role is ideal for engineers who are excited by the opportunity to move between deep platform thinking and hands-on product iteration.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build foundational backend infrastructure including authentication, permissions, feature flagging, notifications, and document management integrations\n\n - Build and evolve Harvey’s internal product platform, accelerating development across multiple product lines and engineering teams\n\n - Lead development of enterprise-facing features, such as secure multi-party collaboration, cross-organization workflows, and robust admin controls\n\n - Maintain high standards for security, privacy, and system reliability, particularly in handling sensitive legal data\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, AI, design, and GTM teams to deliver delightful, enterprise-ready experiences\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years (post-BS/MS) of backend-focused software engineering experience on platform and/or product-oriented teams\n\n - Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact\n\n - Strong knowledge of distributed systems, REST/gRPC APIs, databases, and scalable service architectures\n\n - Familiarity with or interest in enterprise SaaS patterns, such as role-based access control (RBAC), feature flag systems, and third-party integrations is a plus\n\n - Strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience building backend platforms that can support multiple product lines\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n   \n   \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n\n - Location: Toronto, Ontario (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Canadian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nCA $164,000 - CA $225,000\n\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$164K – CA$225K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$164K - CA$225K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1d6ceafd-bb6a-4f75-8b26-004ee7c52847","tierSummary":"CA$164K – CA$225K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a8f0a236-1a8b-462f-a1c4-cf13abd114bb","summary":"CA$164K – CA$225K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":225000},{"id":"9ad5edc0-7ceb-4d9a-816f-862de8840228","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4a4913f9-a110-4047-8619-3d47a2cc40e9","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":225000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"b26ccc21-fb10-4428-90be-a7af2076ff77","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-10T17:25:45.409+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b26ccc21-fb10-4428-90be-a7af2076ff77","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b26ccc21-fb10-4428-90be-a7af2076ff77/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Social Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Social Growth\n\n - Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.\n\n - Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.\n\n - Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.\n\n - Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.\n\n - Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.\n\n - Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n - Bachelor's Degree\n\n - 5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.\n\n - Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.\n\n - Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.\n\n - Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.\n\n - Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1feb7049-e13f-42bc-9d74-25d390d250b6","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"88c73d88-79f7-49f3-a103-df464c12a8d7","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"79ed8dcb-77e5-4695-bd51-a6dcd2530adf","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6f349bf3-da75-4243-bd18-e2255ad4b43d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c6e7267c-877e-479c-8dc6-f34ffbbb44dd","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-10T17:25:48.986+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c6e7267c-877e-479c-8dc6-f34ffbbb44dd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c6e7267c-877e-479c-8dc6-f34ffbbb44dd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Social Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Social Growth\n\n - Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.\n\n - Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.\n\n - Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.\n\n - Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.\n\n - Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.\n\n - Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n - Bachelor's degree\n\n - 5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.\n\n - Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.\n\n - Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.\n\n - Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.\n\n - Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fa725276-f30a-46a1-8184-0e36ebcbc8bc","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1af94d06-77dc-4b7d-b553-8b7b379c59aa","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"50fa96a9-7f7e-43d3-b54b-f4b71041a615","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d4a9cf16-b024-4ba7-b9f5-60c0b26dddfa","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"377fcb88-cbf6-493f-8440-92708f4c9931","title":"Legal Engineer, Product Specialist Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T18:03:07.032+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/377fcb88-cbf6-493f-8440-92708f4c9931","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/377fcb88-cbf6-493f-8440-92708f4c9931/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialist Managers lead and scale a high-performing team of Legal Engineer - Product Specialists responsible for driving customer adoption, expansion, renewal and long-term success across Harvey’s global customer base. This role sits at the center of Harvey’s post-sales motion, ensuring that customers realize meaningful value from Harvey’s platform and expand their usage over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will oversee a team of former practicing lawyers who serve as trusted advisors to customers, guiding them in integrating Harvey into their workflows. As a manager, you will be responsible for elevating team performance, shaping customer engagement strategy, and partnering cross-functionally with Customer Success, Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive retention, expansion, and product evolution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is both a strategic and hands-on leadership role. You will directly engage with Harvey’s most important customers, coach your team through complex engagements, and build the systems, playbooks, and infrastructure needed to scale a world-class post-sales function.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop a high-performing team: </strong>Recruit, mentor, and manage a team of Legal Engineer – Product Specialists, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and product expertise. Coach team members through complex customer situations, provide actionable feedback, and create clear paths for growth and performance excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive customer adoption, retention, and expansion: </strong>Own the team’s impact on customer outcomes, including adoption, utilization, renewals, and expansion. Partner closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to ensure coordinated account strategies that deepen engagement and demonstrate measurable value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Oversee customer engagement strategy: </strong>Guide how the team engages with customers across implementation, onboarding and ongoing enablement. Ensure consistent, high-quality delivery of workshops, trainings, and hands-on agent building sessions that help legal professionals integrate Harvey deeply into their workflows across practice areas and geographies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act as a senior escalation point for key accounts: </strong>Directly engage with Harvey’s most strategic and complex customers, building relationships with partners, general counsel, and other senior legal stakeholders. Step into critical moments to unblock adoption challenges and reinforce Harvey’s value proposition.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own team operations and performance management: </strong>Manage team capacity, account allocation, and coverage to ensure efficient support across the customer base. Establish clear performance metrics tied to adoption, engagement, and customer health. Drive accountability through data-informed decision making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build scalable processes and enablement: </strong>Design and refine playbooks, onboarding frameworks, training programs, and best practices that enable the team to operate consistently and effectively at scale. Partner with Legal Enablement and Product to continuously improve materials and approaches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally to improve customer outcomes: </strong>Collaborate closely with Customer Success, Sales, Product, Engineering, and Applied Legal Research to align on customer needs and deliver cohesive solutions. Ensure insights from customer engagements are translated into actionable improvements across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Influence product strategy and roadmap: </strong>Aggregate and synthesize feedback from your team and customers to inform product development. Advocate for features and workflows that address real-world legal use cases and improve usability, adoption, and impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape Harvey’s customer-facing narrative: </strong>Partner with Marketing and Enablement to develop high-quality content, use case materials, and thought leadership that reflect deep legal expertise and resonate with customers. Help define how Harvey communicates value in a post-sales context.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent) and/or in-house at a F500 or leading tech company, with significant client-facing experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of direct people-management experience, with a demonstrated track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams - including hiring, performance management, and career development of direct reports. Experience managing legal professionals is preferred, but candidates with strong management track records leading non-legal teams will also be considered, provided they bring the legal background described above.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence, with experience building relationships with senior stakeholders such as law firm partners, general counsel, c-suite/senior innovation team members and legal operations leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of legal workflows and the challenges faced by modern legal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success in customer-facing roles (e.g., client advisory, customer success, legal tech, or innovation teams).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment and drive both strategic initiatives and day-to-day execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interest in AI and its potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working cross-functionally with Product and Engineering teams is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialist Managers lead and scale a high-performing team of Legal Engineer - Product Specialists responsible for driving customer adoption, expansion, renewal and long-term success across Harvey’s global customer base. This role sits at the center of Harvey’s post-sales motion, ensuring that customers realize meaningful value from Harvey’s platform and expand their usage over time.\n\nYou will oversee a team of former practicing lawyers who serve as trusted advisors to customers, guiding them in integrating Harvey into their workflows. As a manager, you will be responsible for elevating team performance, shaping customer engagement strategy, and partnering cross-functionally with Customer Success, Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive retention, expansion, and product evolution.\n\nThis is both a strategic and hands-on leadership role. You will directly engage with Harvey’s most important customers, coach your team through complex engagements, and build the systems, playbooks, and infrastructure needed to scale a world-class post-sales function.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead and develop a high-performing team: Recruit, mentor, and manage a team of Legal Engineer – Product Specialists, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and product expertise. Coach team members through complex customer situations, provide actionable feedback, and create clear paths for growth and performance excellence.\n\n - Drive customer adoption, retention, and expansion: Own the team’s impact on customer outcomes, including adoption, utilization, renewals, and expansion. Partner closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to ensure coordinated account strategies that deepen engagement and demonstrate measurable value.\n\n - Oversee customer engagement strategy: Guide how the team engages with customers across implementation, onboarding and ongoing enablement. Ensure consistent, high-quality delivery of workshops, trainings, and hands-on agent building sessions that help legal professionals integrate Harvey deeply into their workflows across practice areas and geographies.\n\n - Act as a senior escalation point for key accounts: Directly engage with Harvey’s most strategic and complex customers, building relationships with partners, general counsel, and other senior legal stakeholders. Step into critical moments to unblock adoption challenges and reinforce Harvey’s value proposition.\n\n - Own team operations and performance management: Manage team capacity, account allocation, and coverage to ensure efficient support across the customer base. Establish clear performance metrics tied to adoption, engagement, and customer health. Drive accountability through data-informed decision making.\n\n - Build scalable processes and enablement: Design and refine playbooks, onboarding frameworks, training programs, and best practices that enable the team to operate consistently and effectively at scale. Partner with Legal Enablement and Product to continuously improve materials and approaches.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally to improve customer outcomes: Collaborate closely with Customer Success, Sales, Product, Engineering, and Applied Legal Research to align on customer needs and deliver cohesive solutions. Ensure insights from customer engagements are translated into actionable improvements across teams.\n\n - Influence product strategy and roadmap: Aggregate and synthesize feedback from your team and customers to inform product development. Advocate for features and workflows that address real-world legal use cases and improve usability, adoption, and impact.\n\n - Shape Harvey’s customer-facing narrative: Partner with Marketing and Enablement to develop high-quality content, use case materials, and thought leadership that reflect deep legal expertise and resonate with customers. Help define how Harvey communicates value in a post-sales context.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 5+ years practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent) and/or in-house at a F500 or leading tech company, with significant client-facing experience.\n\n - 4+ years of direct people-management experience, with a demonstrated track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams - including hiring, performance management, and career development of direct reports. Experience managing legal professionals is preferred, but candidates with strong management track records leading non-legal teams will also be considered, provided they bring the legal background described above.\n\n - Strong executive presence, with experience building relationships with senior stakeholders such as law firm partners, general counsel, c-suite/senior innovation team members and legal operations leaders.\n\n - Deep understanding of legal workflows and the challenges faced by modern legal teams.\n\n - Demonstrated success in customer-facing roles (e.g., client advisory, customer success, legal tech, or innovation teams).\n\n - Ability to operate in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment and drive both strategic initiatives and day-to-day execution.\n\n - Strong interest in AI and its potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Experience working cross-functionally with Product and Engineering teams is a plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 75/25 Split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"681afa7f-291d-4fb0-94e4-4ec8376d8289","tierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 75/25 Split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 75/25 Split","components":[{"id":"d9194431-938c-4e7b-8538-b92fc7ed9dcc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"3efe1fb1-ed3f-41dc-8f22-af52a927d74b","summary":"$315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000},{"id":"b88c2cf1-9d66-4108-a515-1946ca4e96d2","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"07d354ff-5d99-4432-bbad-68818ee2b25e","title":"Legal Engineer, Product Specialist Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T18:03:08.310+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/07d354ff-5d99-4432-bbad-68818ee2b25e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/07d354ff-5d99-4432-bbad-68818ee2b25e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialist Managers lead and scale a high-performing team of Legal Engineer - Product Specialists responsible for driving customer adoption, expansion, renewal and long-term success across Harvey’s global customer base. This role sits at the center of Harvey’s post-sales motion, ensuring that customers realize meaningful value from Harvey’s platform and expand their usage over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will oversee a team of former practicing lawyers who serve as trusted advisors to customers, guiding them in integrating Harvey into their workflows. As a manager, you will be responsible for elevating team performance, shaping customer engagement strategy, and partnering cross-functionally with Customer Success, Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive retention, expansion, and product evolution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is both a strategic and hands-on leadership role. You will directly engage with Harvey’s most important customers, coach your team through complex engagements, and build the systems, playbooks, and infrastructure needed to scale a world-class post-sales function.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop a high-performing team: </strong>Recruit, mentor, and manage a team of Legal Engineer – Product Specialists, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and product expertise. Coach team members through complex customer situations, provide actionable feedback, and create clear paths for growth and performance excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive customer adoption, retention, and expansion: </strong>Own the team’s impact on customer outcomes, including adoption, utilization, renewals, and expansion. Partner closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to ensure coordinated account strategies that deepen engagement and demonstrate measurable value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Oversee customer engagement strategy: </strong>Guide how the team engages with customers across implementation, onboarding and ongoing enablement. Ensure consistent, high-quality delivery of workshops, trainings, and hands-on agent building sessions that help legal professionals integrate Harvey deeply into their workflows across practice areas and geographies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act as a senior escalation point for key accounts: </strong>Directly engage with Harvey’s most strategic and complex customers, building relationships with partners, general counsel, and other senior legal stakeholders. Step into critical moments to unblock adoption challenges and reinforce Harvey’s value proposition.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own team operations and performance management: </strong>Manage team capacity, account allocation, and coverage to ensure efficient support across the customer base. Establish clear performance metrics tied to adoption, engagement, and customer health. Drive accountability through data-informed decision making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build scalable processes and enablement: </strong>Design and refine playbooks, onboarding frameworks, training programs, and best practices that enable the team to operate consistently and effectively at scale. Partner with Legal Enablement and Product to continuously improve materials and approaches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally to improve customer outcomes: </strong>Collaborate closely with Customer Success, Sales, Product, Engineering, and Applied Legal Research to align on customer needs and deliver cohesive solutions. Ensure insights from customer engagements are translated into actionable improvements across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Influence product strategy and roadmap: </strong>Aggregate and synthesize feedback from your team and customers to inform product development. Advocate for features and workflows that address real-world legal use cases and improve usability, adoption, and impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape Harvey’s customer-facing narrative: </strong>Partner with Marketing and Enablement to develop high-quality content, use case materials, and thought leadership that reflect deep legal expertise and resonate with customers. Help define how Harvey communicates value in a post-sales context.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD or equivalent legal qualification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent) and/or in-house at a F500 or leading tech company, with significant client-facing experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of direct people-management experience, with a demonstrated track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams - including hiring, performance management, and career development of direct reports. Experience managing legal professionals is preferred, but candidates with strong management track records leading non-legal teams will also be considered, provided they bring the legal background described above.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence, with experience building relationships with senior stakeholders such as law firm partners, general counsel, c-suite/senior innovation team members and legal operations leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of legal workflows and the challenges faced by modern legal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success in customer-facing roles (e.g., client advisory, customer success, legal tech, or innovation teams).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment and drive both strategic initiatives and day-to-day execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interest in AI and its potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working cross-functionally with Product and Engineering teams is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineer - Product Specialist Managers lead and scale a high-performing team of Legal Engineer - Product Specialists responsible for driving customer adoption, expansion, renewal and long-term success across Harvey’s global customer base. This role sits at the center of Harvey’s post-sales motion, ensuring that customers realize meaningful value from Harvey’s platform and expand their usage over time.\n\nYou will oversee a team of former practicing lawyers who serve as trusted advisors to customers, guiding them in integrating Harvey into their workflows. As a manager, you will be responsible for elevating team performance, shaping customer engagement strategy, and partnering cross-functionally with Customer Success, Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive retention, expansion, and product evolution.\n\nThis is both a strategic and hands-on leadership role. You will directly engage with Harvey’s most important customers, coach your team through complex engagements, and build the systems, playbooks, and infrastructure needed to scale a world-class post-sales function.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead and develop a high-performing team: Recruit, mentor, and manage a team of Legal Engineer – Product Specialists, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and product expertise. Coach team members through complex customer situations, provide actionable feedback, and create clear paths for growth and performance excellence.\n\n - Drive customer adoption, retention, and expansion: Own the team’s impact on customer outcomes, including adoption, utilization, renewals, and expansion. Partner closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to ensure coordinated account strategies that deepen engagement and demonstrate measurable value.\n\n - Oversee customer engagement strategy: Guide how the team engages with customers across implementation, onboarding and ongoing enablement. Ensure consistent, high-quality delivery of workshops, trainings, and hands-on agent building sessions that help legal professionals integrate Harvey deeply into their workflows across practice areas and geographies.\n\n - Act as a senior escalation point for key accounts: Directly engage with Harvey’s most strategic and complex customers, building relationships with partners, general counsel, and other senior legal stakeholders. Step into critical moments to unblock adoption challenges and reinforce Harvey’s value proposition.\n\n - Own team operations and performance management: Manage team capacity, account allocation, and coverage to ensure efficient support across the customer base. Establish clear performance metrics tied to adoption, engagement, and customer health. Drive accountability through data-informed decision making.\n\n - Build scalable processes and enablement: Design and refine playbooks, onboarding frameworks, training programs, and best practices that enable the team to operate consistently and effectively at scale. Partner with Legal Enablement and Product to continuously improve materials and approaches.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally to improve customer outcomes: Collaborate closely with Customer Success, Sales, Product, Engineering, and Applied Legal Research to align on customer needs and deliver cohesive solutions. Ensure insights from customer engagements are translated into actionable improvements across teams.\n\n - Influence product strategy and roadmap: Aggregate and synthesize feedback from your team and customers to inform product development. Advocate for features and workflows that address real-world legal use cases and improve usability, adoption, and impact.\n\n - Shape Harvey’s customer-facing narrative: Partner with Marketing and Enablement to develop high-quality content, use case materials, and thought leadership that reflect deep legal expertise and resonate with customers. Help define how Harvey communicates value in a post-sales context.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD or equivalent legal qualification.\n\n - 5+ years practicing law at a top-tier law firm (Vault 50 or equivalent) and/or in-house at a F500 or leading tech company, with significant client-facing experience.\n\n - 4+ years of direct people-management experience, with a demonstrated track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams - including hiring, performance management, and career development of direct reports. Experience managing legal professionals is preferred, but candidates with strong management track records leading non-legal teams will also be considered, provided they bring the legal background described above.\n\n - Strong executive presence, with experience building relationships with senior stakeholders such as law firm partners, general counsel, c-suite/senior innovation team members and legal operations leaders.\n\n - Deep understanding of legal workflows and the challenges faced by modern legal teams.\n\n - Demonstrated success in customer-facing roles (e.g., client advisory, customer success, legal tech, or innovation teams).\n\n - Ability to operate in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment and drive both strategic initiatives and day-to-day execution.\n\n - Strong interest in AI and its potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Experience working cross-functionally with Product and Engineering teams is a plus.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 75/25 split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"03fcb1d4-76fd-49e6-873e-bcfb7146b406","tierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 75/25 split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 75/25 split","components":[{"id":"08969706-24b5-429c-affa-4efaeb9977cc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"319b137e-d166-47b9-b6e7-34b959568dc0","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e748ebf9-2a9e-4209-9911-be416fd55954","summary":"$315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}},{"id":"04ee546e-7432-4154-abf2-cb3b2d7abf7a","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-11T22:14:57.748+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04ee546e-7432-4154-abf2-cb3b2d7abf7a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04ee546e-7432-4154-abf2-cb3b2d7abf7a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Frontend Software Engineer at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of users of Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-to-end UI features for Shared Spaces and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize frontend performance at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years (post-BS/MS) of frontend-focused software engineering experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use Tailwind CSS)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CA $164,000 - CA $225,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Frontend Software Engineer at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects that define the user experience of users of Harvey. The team is composed of highly motivated, skilled, and considerate engineers. Everything we touch is polished to high standards extending to all aspects of our work –  from design to architecture to code to slack communication. We also build enterprise-grade collaboration product experiences for law firms.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in Toronto, Canada. We use a hybrid, 3+ days-per week in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build new interfaces for lawyers and organizations to collaborate with AI\n\n - Lead end-to-end UI features for Shared Spaces and future Harvey products — from scoping and design reviews to implementation, launch, and iteration\n\n - Build polished, high-performance React + TypeScript interfaces using TailwindCSS, with crisp interactions, resilient state management, and strong error handling\n\n - Architect reusable components and patterns and evolve our internal design system\n\n - Optimize frontend performance at scale\n\n - Collaborate tightly with design and backend/infrastructure to shape APIs and UX for long-running jobs, streaming results, and tool-calling workflows.\n\n - Raise the bar on frontend reliability and security UX for enterprise and regulated environments\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years (post-BS/MS) of frontend-focused software engineering experience\n\n - Experience working across the stack to ship user-facing features with measurable impact\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, and CSS (we use Tailwind CSS)\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nCA $164,000 - CA $225,000\n\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KT1\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$164K – CA$225K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$164K - CA$225K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e16068b1-e95a-4674-87ad-f51e1831e5af","tierSummary":"CA$164K – CA$225K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f3bf60f0-9edc-4ba6-8544-f2ce52b066dc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"330d6d6c-a600-4c9e-8e37-f3966d3deef9","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f90a521d-7e02-4fa4-83ad-71ce154b6db4","summary":"CA$164K – CA$225K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":225000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":225000}]}},{"id":"66c88eaf-37a7-499b-aa0b-db94933d1700","title":"Business Recruiter","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T21:47:50.943+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/66c88eaf-37a7-499b-aa0b-db94933d1700","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/66c88eaf-37a7-499b-aa0b-db94933d1700/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a key member of our growing talent team, you’ll work closely with hiring managers to find and attract top talent while helping refine and scale our recruiting operations during a period of rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with hiring managers to understand hiring needs and support effective, efficient recruiting strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source and screen candidates through various channels including job boards, social platforms, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide timely updates and feedback to hiring teams, ensuring alignment and strong communication throughout the process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver a thoughtful and engaging candidate experience from outreach to offer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Carry a full slate of 8–10 requisitions at a time, managing competing priorities with strong organization and follow-through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to improving recruiting workflows and documentation across business functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with coordinators and other recruiters to ensure a smooth and streamlined process.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on G&amp;A or GTM roles (Sales, Customer Success, Finance, IT, HR, Marketing).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with candidates and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to prioritize across multiple open roles and tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with recruiting metrics, and a willingness to learn and apply data to improve outcomes.<br />Adaptable and proactive, with a collaborative approach to problem-solving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools like Ashby, Gem, Notion, Slack, and Google Workspace for recruiting workflows and pipeline management.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $160,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a key member of our growing talent team, you’ll work closely with hiring managers to find and attract top talent while helping refine and scale our recruiting operations during a period of rapid growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with hiring managers to understand hiring needs and support effective, efficient recruiting strategies.\n\n - Source and screen candidates through various channels including job boards, social platforms, and referrals.\n\n - Provide timely updates and feedback to hiring teams, ensuring alignment and strong communication throughout the process.\n\n - Deliver a thoughtful and engaging candidate experience from outreach to offer.\n\n - Carry a full slate of 8–10 requisitions at a time, managing competing priorities with strong organization and follow-through.\n\n - Contribute to improving recruiting workflows and documentation across business functions.\n\n - Collaborate with coordinators and other recruiters to ensure a smooth and streamlined process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth environment.\n\n - Experience working on G&A or GTM roles (Sales, Customer Success, Finance, IT, HR, Marketing).\n\n - Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with candidates and internal stakeholders.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to prioritize across multiple open roles and tasks.\n\n - Familiarity with recruiting metrics, and a willingness to learn and apply data to improve outcomes.\n   Adaptable and proactive, with a collaborative approach to problem-solving.\n\nNice to Have:\n\n - Experience with tools like Ashby, Gem, Notion, Slack, and Google Workspace for recruiting workflows and pipeline management.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,000 - $160,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $160K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"203d44dc-7353-438b-9164-77364f26e34b","tierSummary":"$120K – $160K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"57716eca-a9ab-42ef-85a2-5580174e7bc1","summary":"$120K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000},{"id":"a1a31fa0-ac92-4a6b-b7cf-99df71f4fa09","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"00511e29-715a-458e-b2a6-265b478cfb6a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c685bc9e-d7c8-4443-ba0f-b19690ba033b","title":"Business Recruiter","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T21:48:07.304+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c685bc9e-d7c8-4443-ba0f-b19690ba033b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c685bc9e-d7c8-4443-ba0f-b19690ba033b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a key member of our growing talent team, you’ll work closely with hiring managers to find and attract top talent while helping refine and scale our recruiting operations during a period of rapid growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with hiring managers to understand hiring needs and support effective, efficient recruiting strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source and screen candidates through various channels including job boards, social platforms, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide timely updates and feedback to hiring teams, ensuring alignment and strong communication throughout the process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver a thoughtful and engaging candidate experience from outreach to offer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Carry a full slate of 8–10 requisitions at a time, managing competing priorities with strong organization and follow-through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to improving recruiting workflows and documentation across business functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with coordinators and other recruiters to ensure a smooth and streamlined process.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on G&amp;A or GTM roles (Sales, Customer Success, Finance, IT, HR, Marketing).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with candidates and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to prioritize across multiple open roles and tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with recruiting metrics, and a willingness to learn and apply data to improve outcomes.<br />Adaptable and proactive, with a collaborative approach to problem-solving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools like Ashby, Gem, Notion, Slack, and Google Workspace for recruiting workflows and pipeline management.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $160,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a key member of our growing talent team, you’ll work closely with hiring managers to find and attract top talent while helping refine and scale our recruiting operations during a period of rapid growth.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with hiring managers to understand hiring needs and support effective, efficient recruiting strategies.\n\n - Source and screen candidates through various channels including job boards, social platforms, and referrals.\n\n - Provide timely updates and feedback to hiring teams, ensuring alignment and strong communication throughout the process.\n\n - Deliver a thoughtful and engaging candidate experience from outreach to offer.\n\n - Carry a full slate of 8–10 requisitions at a time, managing competing priorities with strong organization and follow-through.\n\n - Contribute to improving recruiting workflows and documentation across business functions.\n\n - Collaborate with coordinators and other recruiters to ensure a smooth and streamlined process.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth environment.\n\n - Experience working on G&A or GTM roles (Sales, Customer Success, Finance, IT, HR, Marketing).\n\n - Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with candidates and internal stakeholders.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to prioritize across multiple open roles and tasks.\n\n - Familiarity with recruiting metrics, and a willingness to learn and apply data to improve outcomes.\n   Adaptable and proactive, with a collaborative approach to problem-solving.\n\nNice to Have:\n\n - Experience with tools like Ashby, Gem, Notion, Slack, and Google Workspace for recruiting workflows and pipeline management.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,000 - $160,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $160K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fc762a1e-5739-4da0-a976-b6ec2fff3377","tierSummary":"$120K – $160K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3a240e60-722b-4ede-bb64-0655ed3ec3be","summary":"$120K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000},{"id":"482ca834-09c9-495d-9266-dc734bf649b2","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9d89c650-1799-4848-8e7d-76a1eaed1790","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2faddc24-1463-4878-9b43-ec8090a39c88","title":"Engagement Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-23T21:14:42.995+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2faddc24-1463-4878-9b43-ec8090a39c88","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2faddc24-1463-4878-9b43-ec8090a39c88/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.</p><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own transformation engagements end to end.</strong> Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Map workflows and target the highest-value opportunities.</strong> Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value.</strong> Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive relationships and advise on the operating model</strong>. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hand off with rigor.</strong> Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute learnings to build and improve playbooks.</strong> Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 50% of the time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$159,200 - $238,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW \n\nAs an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.\n\nThis is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\nOwn transformation engagements end to end. Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.\n\n\n\nMap workflows and target the highest-value opportunities. Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.\n\n\n\nCoordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value. Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.\n\n\n\nBuild executive relationships and advise on the operating model. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.\n\n\n\nHand off with rigor. Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.\n\n\n\nContribute learnings to build and improve playbooks. Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.\n\n\n\nTravel required: Up to 50% of the time.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.\n\n - Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.\n\n - Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$159,200 - $238,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$159.2K – $238.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$159.2K - $238.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d8603c1d-59f2-46aa-a4fd-3419890131a5","tierSummary":"$159.2K – $238.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ecd8d559-4696-47e3-b986-474148b22428","summary":"$159.2K – $238.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":159200,"maxValue":238800},{"id":"c9d5acf8-f8ea-410d-81f0-ee0126e38560","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"56ebd967-c8ad-4d13-b5dd-73902e64aae2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":159200,"maxValue":238800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f1679188-b64e-435c-b0c6-bbcf552bed38","title":"Engagement Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-25T16:59:53.460+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f1679188-b64e-435c-b0c6-bbcf552bed38","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f1679188-b64e-435c-b0c6-bbcf552bed38/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.</p><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own transformation engagements end to end.</strong> Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Map workflows and target the highest-value opportunities.</strong> Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value.</strong> Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive relationships and advise on the operating model</strong>. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hand off with rigor.</strong> Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute learnings to build and improve playbooks.</strong> Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 50% of the time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$159,200 - $238,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW \n\nAs an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.\n\nThis is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\nOwn transformation engagements end to end. Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.\n\n\n\nMap workflows and target the highest-value opportunities. Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.\n\n\n\nCoordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value. Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.\n\n\n\nBuild executive relationships and advise on the operating model. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.\n\n\n\nHand off with rigor. Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.\n\n\n\nContribute learnings to build and improve playbooks. Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.\n\n\n\nTravel required: Up to 50% of the time.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.\n\n - Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.\n\n - Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$159,200 - $238,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$159.2K – $238.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$159.2K - $238.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"28646958-6637-42b0-8366-d8c99303840c","tierSummary":"$159.2K – $238.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"750408fd-df9d-4a6f-81ce-e342fc6962b0","summary":"$159.2K – $238.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":159200,"maxValue":238800},{"id":"cfbb8b94-fb09-4c77-a720-67918d805fdd","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"dfe6a3cd-71a7-41ab-92a2-df3027c7c9b8","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":159200,"maxValue":238800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"70ac0c85-e987-4657-aae4-95337e344d4e","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager, Evaluation","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-12T23:45:17.865+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/70ac0c85-e987-4657-aae4-95337e344d4e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/70ac0c85-e987-4657-aae4-95337e344d4e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a technical, systems-minded operator to build and scale the evaluation engine behind Harvey’s platform. As we expand globally, ensuring our models behave reliably, accurately, and jurisdictionally correctly is mission-critical—and evaluation complexity is increasing 10x.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a member of our Product Operations team, you’ll work closely with Applied Legal Researchers, Product, Engineering, AI Research, and human data providers to operationalize evaluation methodologies and embed them into our product development lifecycle. You’ll create the workflows, systems, and tooling that make evaluation a first-class product capability at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership role for someone who thrives in ambiguity, loves building structure, and wants to help scale the evaluation infrastructure of a global AI company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and scale the systems that power model and product evaluations across Harvey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run intake, triage, and prioritization for the evaluation request queue, routing capacity to the highest-value coverage gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed evaluation workflows and readiness checkpoints into the product development lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create the single source of truth for evaluation status, results, history, and launch readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn Expert-designed evaluation methodologies into scalable, repeatable operational processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage human data providers and stand up our internal contract-attorney pipeline, ensuring evaluation quality meets legal standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Engineering and Research to improve evaluation tooling, automation, and dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive evaluation readiness for major product and model launches across geographies and jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document and operationalize evaluation governance as complexity increases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define how Harvey ensures model accuracy, reliability, and trust at global scale</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–7+ years in technical program management, product operations, research operations, or evaluation/benchmarking roles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with ML/AI evaluations, benchmarking frameworks, or scientific workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with statistical methodologies and SQL or Python, or similar tools to interpret evaluation data (either natively or with AI tool support)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business acumen with an ability to apply an ROI-focused mindset to scaling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work deeply with legal experts and operationalize complex evaluation methodologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional coordination skills across Product, Engineering, Research, and data providers/vendors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and a bias toward clarity, rigor, and reproducibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to navigate an evolving landscape and bring order to complex systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and comfort translating technical nuance for diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Desire to do whatever it takes to make evaluation systems successful—from writing documentation to diagnosing pipeline issues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for a technical, systems-minded operator to build and scale the evaluation engine behind Harvey’s platform. As we expand globally, ensuring our models behave reliably, accurately, and jurisdictionally correctly is mission-critical—and evaluation complexity is increasing 10x.\n\nAs a member of our Product Operations team, you’ll work closely with Applied Legal Researchers, Product, Engineering, AI Research, and human data providers to operationalize evaluation methodologies and embed them into our product development lifecycle. You’ll create the workflows, systems, and tooling that make evaluation a first-class product capability at Harvey.\n\nThis is a high-ownership role for someone who thrives in ambiguity, loves building structure, and wants to help scale the evaluation infrastructure of a global AI company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and scale the systems that power model and product evaluations across Harvey\n\n - Run intake, triage, and prioritization for the evaluation request queue, routing capacity to the highest-value coverage gaps\n\n - Embed evaluation workflows and readiness checkpoints into the product development lifecycle\n\n - Create the single source of truth for evaluation status, results, history, and launch readiness\n\n - Turn Expert-designed evaluation methodologies into scalable, repeatable operational processes\n\n - Manage human data providers and stand up our internal contract-attorney pipeline, ensuring evaluation quality meets legal standards\n\n - Work with Engineering and Research to improve evaluation tooling, automation, and dashboards\n\n - Drive evaluation readiness for major product and model launches across geographies and jurisdictions\n\n - Document and operationalize evaluation governance as complexity increases\n\n - Help define how Harvey ensures model accuracy, reliability, and trust at global scale\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4–7+ years in technical program management, product operations, research operations, or evaluation/benchmarking roles\n\n - Experience working with ML/AI evaluations, benchmarking frameworks, or scientific workflows\n\n - Comfort with statistical methodologies and SQL or Python, or similar tools to interpret evaluation data (either natively or with AI tool support)\n\n - Strong business acumen with an ability to apply an ROI-focused mindset to scaling\n\n - Ability to work deeply with legal experts and operationalize complex evaluation methodologies\n\n - Strong cross-functional coordination skills across Product, Engineering, Research, and data providers/vendors\n\n - High attention to detail and a bias toward clarity, rigor, and reproducibility\n\n - Ability to navigate an evolving landscape and bring order to complex systems\n\n - Strong communication skills and comfort translating technical nuance for diverse stakeholders\n\n - Desire to do whatever it takes to make evaluation systems successful—from writing documentation to diagnosing pipeline issues\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $210K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c6f6c076-d13e-4e3e-ab8c-2af3b550a044","tierSummary":"$150K – $210K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f8230286-ad19-43c5-aa8a-bc130e89344a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e171b84b-5e3d-409d-86cc-de71d4cfb504","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"3c2699df-c5cf-42ec-ab34-05e3eba670ea","summary":"$150K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":210000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":210000}]}},{"id":"ecfc45be-fc15-4c16-a419-509c998b6c80","title":"CX Data Analyst","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-15T20:19:24.236+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ecfc45be-fc15-4c16-a419-509c998b6c80","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ecfc45be-fc15-4c16-a419-509c998b6c80/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Plus</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Attributes</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$112,000 - $168,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nCustomer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.\n\nAs Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.\n\nThis is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences\n\n - Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it\n\n - Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time\n\n - Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance\n\n - Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need\n\n - Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources\n\n - Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should\n\n - Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success\n\n - Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures\n\n - Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures\n\n - Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness\n\n - Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools\n\n - Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nRequired\n\n - 3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function\n\n - Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't\n\n - SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)\n\n - Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent\n\n - Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly\n\n - Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative\n\n - Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at\n\nStrong Plus\n\n - Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation\n\n - Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling\n\n - Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs\n\n - Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products\n\n - Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting\n\nKey Attributes\n\n - AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier\n\n - Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask\n\n - Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong\n\n - Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself\n\n - Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$112,000 - $168,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$112K - $168K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f72faa5b-f203-41b5-92f7-f8326c791c7f","tierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"bcf235e3-0ef8-4e08-b0ea-616bfdb7de83","summary":"$112K – $168K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"id":"21df193f-ea36-4142-95a4-6ad359399962","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"86a14f89-ba35-41d6-8705-7024462d352d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e69f2050-b4c0-4fbb-9852-2c60d2adbb45","title":"CX Data Analyst","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-15T20:19:41.684+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e69f2050-b4c0-4fbb-9852-2c60d2adbb45","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e69f2050-b4c0-4fbb-9852-2c60d2adbb45/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Plus</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Attributes</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$112,000 - $168,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nCustomer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.\n\nAs Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.\n\nThis is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences\n\n - Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it\n\n - Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time\n\n - Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance\n\n - Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need\n\n - Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources\n\n - Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should\n\n - Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success\n\n - Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures\n\n - Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures\n\n - Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness\n\n - Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools\n\n - Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nRequired\n\n - 3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function\n\n - Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't\n\n - SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)\n\n - Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent\n\n - Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly\n\n - Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative\n\n - Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at\n\nStrong Plus\n\n - Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation\n\n - Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling\n\n - Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs\n\n - Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products\n\n - Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting\n\nKey Attributes\n\n - AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier\n\n - Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask\n\n - Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong\n\n - Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself\n\n - Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$112,000 - $168,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-ML1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$112K - $168K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"78514cda-441a-42be-bf88-ed3cee8556b4","tierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"dae36ee7-df02-4436-9662-5d46efd388cc","summary":"$112K – $168K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"id":"51e65b13-8832-42be-bc63-4e488bb3a9e8","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ed0790af-e552-465a-9522-b9bdb6aba64e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f8857e81-4062-4669-a7e3-7b73b114979b","title":"CX Data Analyst","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-15T20:19:44.526+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f8857e81-4062-4669-a7e3-7b73b114979b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f8857e81-4062-4669-a7e3-7b73b114979b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Plus</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Attributes</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$112,000 - $168,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nCustomer Experience runs on data — but right now, that data lives in too many places, speaks too many languages, and reaches the wrong people too late. This role exists to fix that.\n\nAs Harvey's first Support Operations Data Analyst, you'll own the analytics function for the Customer Experience org. You'll build and maintain the dashboards, reports, and feedback loops that tell us whether we're hitting our north stars — cSAT, TTR, QA scores, escalation rates — and surface the signal underneath the numbers so we can act on it. You'll sit within the Support Operations team, reporting to the Support Operations Manager, and work closely with Customer Experience leadership and Harvey's central data team to ensure the org is equipped with the right instrumentation as we scale.\n\nThis is a solo role. You won't have a team beneath you. You will need to be fluent enough in support analytics to hold the function independently, confident enough to push back on how metrics are framed, and fast enough to operate at Harvey's pace.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own recurring reporting for Customer Experience — weekly, monthly, and QBR-ready — tailored to ops, leadership, and cross-functional audiences\n\n - Translate support data into clear narratives: what's happening, why, and what to do about it\n\n - Track and maintain north star metrics: cSAT, TTR by tier, QA scores, bug escalation rate to EPD, and First Response Time\n\n - Build and maintain self-serve dashboards that give the ops team and leadership real-time visibility into support performance\n\n - Partner with Support Systems to ensure Zendesk is instrumented to capture the data we need\n\n - Work with Harvey's central data team to connect support data to broader product and customer data sources\n\n - Identify and close data collection gaps — if we can't measure it, help define how we should\n\n - Design feedback loops that connect support signals to Product, Engineering, and Customer Success\n\n - Quantify the operational cost of product bugs, feature gaps, and onboarding failures\n\n - Contribute to QA analytics as the QA program matures\n\n - Track ticket deflection, AI/chatbot performance, and self-service effectiveness\n\n - Measure the impact of AI-driven support — containment rate, escalation rate from AI interactions, resolution quality — and surface findings that drive how we tune and invest in those tools\n\n - Support ad hoc analytical requests from the Support Operations Manager, Customer Experience leadership, and senior stakeholders\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nRequired\n\n - 3–5 years of experience in analytics, with at least 2 years directly in support operations, customer success operations, or a closely adjacent function\n\n - Fluency in support platform data — you know how Zendesk (or equivalent) is structured, what data it produces, and what it doesn't\n\n - SQL proficiency — you can write complex queries against large datasets without hand-holding (CTEs, window functions, joins across schemas)\n\n - Dashboard experience — you've built and maintained operational dashboards in Looker, Tableau, Sigma, Omni, or equivalent\n\n - Reporting for multiple audiences — you know the difference between what a frontline manager needs and what a CFO needs, and you build accordingly\n\n - Strong data storytelling — you don't just present numbers, you write the narrative\n\n - Comfort operating solo — you don't need a team around you to deliver, and you don't need a ticket to tell you what to look at\n\nStrong Plus\n\n - Experience with Python for data manipulation or automation\n\n - Familiarity with dbt or similar data transformation tooling\n\n - Experience building or contributing to QA analytics programs\n\n - Background supporting enterprise SaaS or AI-native products\n\n - Experience working with Zendesk APIs or extracting data beyond standard reporting\n\nKey Attributes\n\n - AI-native: you use AI tooling actively in your analytical workflows — not as a novelty, but as a force multiplier\n\n - Pace: you move in hours and days, not weeks. You surface findings before anyone has to ask\n\n - Judgment: you know which metrics matter and which are vanity. You push back when framing is wrong\n\n - Clarity: your outputs are direct, jargon-free, and actionable. You write for the reader, not yourself\n\n - Ownership: you treat Customer Experience analytics as your problem to solve, not a ticket queue to process\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$112,000 - $168,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$112K - $168K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a8b9aa39-f998-4404-92dd-69884059a9c3","tierSummary":"$112K – $168K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3600d4d7-b1c8-45d0-af6a-b6439501e4ce","summary":"$112K – $168K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"id":"3f2d5f4b-b035-4cbd-a032-7eca8cc05afc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"dcca6d19-18ee-47fa-9365-d92bcd570bbf","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":112000,"maxValue":168000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"eea0f275-cf5b-409b-9898-bbc386d47652","title":"Corporate Business Development Manager, Ecosystems","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T17:57:32.986+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/eea0f275-cf5b-409b-9898-bbc386d47652","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/eea0f275-cf5b-409b-9898-bbc386d47652/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h2><strong>Role Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Partnerships team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns Harvey’s product partner ecosystem, driving the end-to-end partner lifecycle—sourcing, negotiating, and operationalizing ecosystem relationships—while designing repeatable processes that allow the program to scale globally.  They partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal, and GTM teams to ensure every integration delivers measurable customer and revenue impact.  It is a rare opportunity to shape the connective tissue of a category-defining legal AI platform at a moment when the ecosystem is still being built from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />• Identify, evaluate, and scale ecosystem partnerships that expand Harvey's product capabilities and competitive moat.<br />• Build and own the operational processes, playbooks, and tooling that move partnerships from pipeline through execution to live deployment at scale.<br />• Manage active partner relationships globally, ensuring integrations remain healthy, adoption grows, and new opportunities surface from existing partnerships.<br />• Serve as a visible face of Harvey’s ecosystem, building trusted relationships and representing Harvey in the broader startup community.<br />• Systematically identify and prioritize high-potential startups and emerging companies that are well-positioned to build with Harvey, using structured theses, ecosystem mapping, and data-driven signals.<br />• Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing to translate partner requirements into integration specifications, influence roadmap prioritization, incorporate ecosystem partnerships into go-to-market motions, and drive technical delivery and customer value creation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong><br />• 5+ years of experience in business development, product management, business operations and strategy, or a related field.<br />• Proven track record of engaging with external partners or customers to build, launch, and scale programs or integrations, ideally in SaaS, AI, or adjacent B2B technology markets.<br />• Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Sales, and/or Operations teams to design and execute multi-stakeholder initiatives.<br />• Strong analytical skills and comfort using both qualitative and quantitative inputs to develop theses, prioritize opportunities, and measure impact. <br />• Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to context-switch between executive, operator, and technical audiences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $260,000 USD OTE 70/30</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Partnerships team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.\n\nThis role owns Harvey’s product partner ecosystem, driving the end-to-end partner lifecycle—sourcing, negotiating, and operationalizing ecosystem relationships—while designing repeatable processes that allow the program to scale globally.  They partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal, and GTM teams to ensure every integration delivers measurable customer and revenue impact.  It is a rare opportunity to shape the connective tissue of a category-defining legal AI platform at a moment when the ecosystem is still being built from the ground up.\n\nWhat You’ll Do \n\n\n• Identify, evaluate, and scale ecosystem partnerships that expand Harvey's product capabilities and competitive moat.\n• Build and own the operational processes, playbooks, and tooling that move partnerships from pipeline through execution to live deployment at scale.\n• Manage active partner relationships globally, ensuring integrations remain healthy, adoption grows, and new opportunities surface from existing partnerships.\n• Serve as a visible face of Harvey’s ecosystem, building trusted relationships and representing Harvey in the broader startup community.\n• Systematically identify and prioritize high-potential startups and emerging companies that are well-positioned to build with Harvey, using structured theses, ecosystem mapping, and data-driven signals.\n• Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing to translate partner requirements into integration specifications, influence roadmap prioritization, incorporate ecosystem partnerships into go-to-market motions, and drive technical delivery and customer value creation.\n\nWhat You Have\n• 5+ years of experience in business development, product management, business operations and strategy, or a related field.\n• Proven track record of engaging with external partners or customers to build, launch, and scale programs or integrations, ideally in SaaS, AI, or adjacent B2B technology markets.\n• Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Sales, and/or Operations teams to design and execute multi-stakeholder initiatives.\n• Strong analytical skills and comfort using both qualitative and quantitative inputs to develop theses, prioritize opportunities, and measure impact. \n• Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to context-switch between executive, operator, and technical audiences.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$200,000 - $260,000 USD OTE 70/30\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 70/30","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7215eca5-327c-4dc0-9e6a-09d423cd6d9b","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 70/30","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 70/30","components":[{"id":"be223aa7-ffe6-4d93-9e80-6e1ce0f8d2cb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d1dbf52b-ef57-4fde-bfc9-bd593ba68ae8","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"aeec52a4-0b2d-4214-bfb0-c3936db00a42","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"9e017dc5-fb22-4d09-be8c-d7cb3442a739","title":"Corporate Business Development Manager, Ecosystems","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T17:57:14.861+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9e017dc5-fb22-4d09-be8c-d7cb3442a739","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9e017dc5-fb22-4d09-be8c-d7cb3442a739/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h2><strong>Role Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Partnerships team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns Harvey’s product partner ecosystem, driving the end-to-end partner lifecycle—sourcing, negotiating, and operationalizing ecosystem relationships—while designing repeatable processes that allow the program to scale globally.  They partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal, and GTM teams to ensure every integration delivers measurable customer and revenue impact.  It is a rare opportunity to shape the connective tissue of a category-defining legal AI platform at a moment when the ecosystem is still being built from the ground up.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do </strong><br />• Identify, evaluate, and scale ecosystem partnerships that expand Harvey's product capabilities and competitive moat.<br />• Build and own the operational processes, playbooks, and tooling that move partnerships from pipeline through execution to live deployment at scale.<br />• Manage active partner relationships globally, ensuring integrations remain healthy, adoption grows, and new opportunities surface from existing partnerships.<br />• Serve as a visible face of Harvey’s ecosystem, building trusted relationships and representing Harvey in the broader startup community.<br />• Systematically identify and prioritize high-potential startups and emerging companies that are well-positioned to build with Harvey, using structured theses, ecosystem mapping, and data-driven signals.<br />• Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing to translate partner requirements into integration specifications, influence roadmap prioritization, incorporate ecosystem partnerships into go-to-market motions, and drive technical delivery and customer value creation.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong><br />• 5+ years of experience in business development, product management, business operations and strategy, or a related field.<br />• Proven track record of engaging with external partners or customers to build, launch, and scale programs or integrations, ideally in SaaS, AI, or adjacent B2B technology markets.<br />• Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Sales, and/or Operations teams to design and execute multi-stakeholder initiatives.<br />• Strong analytical skills and comfort using both qualitative and quantitative inputs to develop theses, prioritize opportunities, and measure impact. <br />• Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to context-switch between executive, operator, and technical audiences.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $260,000 USD OTE 70/30</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Partnerships team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.\n\nThis role owns Harvey’s product partner ecosystem, driving the end-to-end partner lifecycle—sourcing, negotiating, and operationalizing ecosystem relationships—while designing repeatable processes that allow the program to scale globally.  They partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal, and GTM teams to ensure every integration delivers measurable customer and revenue impact.  It is a rare opportunity to shape the connective tissue of a category-defining legal AI platform at a moment when the ecosystem is still being built from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do \n• Identify, evaluate, and scale ecosystem partnerships that expand Harvey's product capabilities and competitive moat.\n• Build and own the operational processes, playbooks, and tooling that move partnerships from pipeline through execution to live deployment at scale.\n• Manage active partner relationships globally, ensuring integrations remain healthy, adoption grows, and new opportunities surface from existing partnerships.\n• Serve as a visible face of Harvey’s ecosystem, building trusted relationships and representing Harvey in the broader startup community.\n• Systematically identify and prioritize high-potential startups and emerging companies that are well-positioned to build with Harvey, using structured theses, ecosystem mapping, and data-driven signals.\n• Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing to translate partner requirements into integration specifications, influence roadmap prioritization, incorporate ecosystem partnerships into go-to-market motions, and drive technical delivery and customer value creation.\n\n\n\n\nWhat You Have\n• 5+ years of experience in business development, product management, business operations and strategy, or a related field.\n• Proven track record of engaging with external partners or customers to build, launch, and scale programs or integrations, ideally in SaaS, AI, or adjacent B2B technology markets.\n• Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Sales, and/or Operations teams to design and execute multi-stakeholder initiatives.\n• Strong analytical skills and comfort using both qualitative and quantitative inputs to develop theses, prioritize opportunities, and measure impact. \n• Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to context-switch between executive, operator, and technical audiences.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$200,000 - $260,000 USD OTE 70/30\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-EP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 70/30","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3d464815-59fb-41e3-b39e-b0651a73cd4e","tierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 70/30","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 70/30","components":[{"id":"d220a96e-fd51-40d8-bfe2-4655f4b02480","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b26ed28d-1596-4a0f-9a42-81190b415bef","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ac5a83b8-095d-4721-af4c-cbc2372e9d93","summary":"$200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"f336367a-fa7c-4515-88ce-6a1f5353c3b5","title":"Manager, Sales Development","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T14:36:21.438+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f336367a-fa7c-4515-88ce-6a1f5353c3b5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f336367a-fa7c-4515-88ce-6a1f5353c3b5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is looking for a driven, strategic, and entrepreneurial Sales Development Manager to lead and scale a team of SDRs in San Francisco and New York. This person will be responsible for building a high-performing team that generates pipeline across leading law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own hiring, onboarding, coaching, and performance management while partnering closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to build a scalable pipeline generation engine. You'll also help shape Harvey's go-to-market strategy by refining targeting, messaging, and outbound programs that resonate with the North American legal market.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're excited by the idea of building teams, developing talent, and driving impact at a fast-growing AI company transforming legal work, we'd love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own pipeline performance:</strong> Drive the SDR team's contribution to pipeline generation across inbound and outbound channels, ensuring strong alignment with sales targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and scale the team:</strong> Hire, onboard, and develop a high-performing SDR team, helping establish the structure, operating cadence, and performance standards for the New York market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coach and develop SDRs:</strong> Deliver hands-on coaching through regular 1:1s, call reviews, and deal strategy sessions to accelerate rep development and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design onboarding and enablement:</strong> Partner with GTM enablement to create onboarding and ongoing training programs that ramp SDRs quickly and build strong product, industry, and prospecting expertise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally:</strong> Collaborate closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to improve lead routing, campaign effectiveness, and pipeline conversion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Refine targeting and messaging:</strong> Continuously test and improve outbound strategies, messaging, and account targeting based on ICP fit and performance insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leverage data and tools:</strong> Use platforms such as Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong, and ZoomInfo to track team performance and optimize workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build a strong team culture:</strong> Foster a high-performance culture grounded in ownership, learning, and collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in SaaS sales or business development, with at least 1–2 years of direct SDR or BDR leadership experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success in building and managing pipeline-generating teams in a high-growth, outbound-focused environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of modern sales development tools (e.g., Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A data-driven mindset with the ability to analyze team performance, uncover insights, and iterate quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building SDR processes from scratch—comfortable in ambiguity and excited to be the architect of something new.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A coaching-first leadership style: you invest in people, celebrate wins, and hold high standards with care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and executive presence—both internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for AI, innovation, and the transformation of knowledge work—especially in professional services and legal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence tech stack decisions—develop recommendations and drive implementation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal or professional services firms is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$195,400 - $260,000 USD OTE 80/20</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is looking for a driven, strategic, and entrepreneurial Sales Development Manager to lead and scale a team of SDRs in San Francisco and New York. This person will be responsible for building a high-performing team that generates pipeline across leading law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams.\n\nYou will own hiring, onboarding, coaching, and performance management while partnering closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to build a scalable pipeline generation engine. You'll also help shape Harvey's go-to-market strategy by refining targeting, messaging, and outbound programs that resonate with the North American legal market.\n\nIf you're excited by the idea of building teams, developing talent, and driving impact at a fast-growing AI company transforming legal work, we'd love to meet you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\n - Own pipeline performance: Drive the SDR team's contribution to pipeline generation across inbound and outbound channels, ensuring strong alignment with sales targets.\n\n - Build and scale the team: Hire, onboard, and develop a high-performing SDR team, helping establish the structure, operating cadence, and performance standards for the New York market.\n\n - Coach and develop SDRs: Deliver hands-on coaching through regular 1:1s, call reviews, and deal strategy sessions to accelerate rep development and performance.\n\n - Design onboarding and enablement: Partner with GTM enablement to create onboarding and ongoing training programs that ramp SDRs quickly and build strong product, industry, and prospecting expertise.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally: Collaborate closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to improve lead routing, campaign effectiveness, and pipeline conversion.\n\n - Refine targeting and messaging: Continuously test and improve outbound strategies, messaging, and account targeting based on ICP fit and performance insights.\n\n - Leverage data and tools: Use platforms such as Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong, and ZoomInfo to track team performance and optimize workflows.\n\n - Build a strong team culture: Foster a high-performance culture grounded in ownership, learning, and collaboration.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n - 4+ years of experience in SaaS sales or business development, with at least 1–2 years of direct SDR or BDR leadership experience.\n\n - Proven success in building and managing pipeline-generating teams in a high-growth, outbound-focused environment.\n\n - Deep understanding of modern sales development tools (e.g., Salesforce, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong).\n\n - A data-driven mindset with the ability to analyze team performance, uncover insights, and iterate quickly.\n\n - Experience building SDR processes from scratch—comfortable in ambiguity and excited to be the architect of something new.\n\n - A coaching-first leadership style: you invest in people, celebrate wins, and hold high standards with care.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and executive presence—both internally and externally.\n\n - Passion for AI, innovation, and the transformation of knowledge work—especially in professional services and legal.\n\n - Ability to influence tech stack decisions—develop recommendations and drive implementation.\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal or professional services firms is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$195,400 - $260,000 USD OTE 80/20\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$195.4K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 80/20","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$195.4K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2941598b-3881-4d63-8550-7789a510e668","tierSummary":"$195.4K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 80/20","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 80/20","components":[{"id":"624fe5eb-77a1-41c4-8966-ac461b295b36","summary":"$195.4K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":195400,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"8ec5a609-b966-4dd8-b24a-15c02af2b848","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4d2a63a8-3b1f-41c8-b60a-daaf98b11ecf","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":195400,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c43ab149-aa8c-4a6a-a97a-a21ad26ae4c5","title":"Legal Engineering Manager (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T20:21:17.280+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c43ab149-aa8c-4a6a-a97a-a21ad26ae4c5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c43ab149-aa8c-4a6a-a97a-a21ad26ae4c5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&amp;A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.\n\nLegal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.\n\nThis role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.\n\n - Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.\n\n - Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.\n\n - Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.\n\n - Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.\n\n - Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.\n\n - Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ee8cf556-549a-40c5-895d-ad43ed0faaf6","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9ac88c84-ede1-448b-9361-43dd8534cedb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"63a87653-14d5-4c42-b463-37b74b6fd46e","summary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}},{"id":"b0be6c25-8b6c-4b5c-92a9-c58b50e68fa3","title":"Legal Engineering Manager (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T20:21:07.191+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b0be6c25-8b6c-4b5c-92a9-c58b50e68fa3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b0be6c25-8b6c-4b5c-92a9-c58b50e68fa3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&amp;A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.\n\nLegal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.\n\nThis role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.\n\n - Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.\n\n - Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.\n\n - Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.\n\n - Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.\n\n - Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.\n\n - Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b605fce0-93eb-416a-9d2c-d71c03ee7b35","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a0b0e74f-53bb-4e8b-ae84-14fbc1538c50","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"3409bd2e-08a8-429b-9248-5a2b482f6428","summary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000}]}},{"id":"5f5715a1-7fc1-4604-8baa-98381ed0a4b8","title":"Legal Engineering Manager (Law Firm, Corporate)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T20:21:10.126+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5f5715a1-7fc1-4604-8baa-98381ed0a4b8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5f5715a1-7fc1-4604-8baa-98381ed0a4b8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&amp;A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its Legal Engineering function, we are hiring Legal Engineering Managers to lead and grow high-performing teams supporting our go-to-market efforts. This role sits at the intersection of legal expertise, customer engagement, and commercial strategy — helping prospective and existing customers understand how Harvey can transform the way legal work gets done.\n\nLegal Engineering Managers lead teams of Legal Engineers who partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales process, bringing legal credibility, product expertise, and consultative support to customer engagements. In addition to managing and developing the team, you will work directly with strategic customers, help shape Harvey’s go-to-market approach, and partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Enablement, and Engineering to improve how Harvey serves the legal industry.\n\nThis role is both strategic and hands-on. We are looking for experienced legal professionals with a corporate law background who are comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, navigating ambiguity, and solving complex problems with a high degree of ownership.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Legal Engineers, setting a high bar for customer engagement, legal credibility, and commercial impact.\n\n - Partner closely with Sales leadership and Account Executives to support strategic accounts, develop deal strategy, and drive successful customer outcomes.\n\n - Oversee and support your team, as they engage in complex customer engagements by conducting discovery, leading product demonstrations, and advising customers on how Harvey can improve corporate, transactional, and commercial legal workflows.\n\n - Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, including corporate partners, transactional attorneys, General Counsel, and other legal and business leaders.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Applied Legal Research, Marketing, and Enablement to improve positioning, workflows, customer solutions, and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Act as the voice of the customer by synthesizing frontline feedback and helping inform product roadmap decisions, feature development, and new use cases.\n\n - Help build and scale the Legal Engineering organization by improving processes, enablement materials, demo strategies, and team best practices.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey’s presence in the market through customer workshops, thought leadership, speaking engagements, and industry events.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 7+ PQE, including significant experience practicing corporate law, commercial contracting, mergers and acquisitions, private equity, emerging companies and venture capital, capital markets, or other corporate transactional work, or advising on corporate governance at a leading law firm.\n\n - Must have prior experience managing a team, with a track record of developing talent and driving performance.\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, with the ability to quickly develop expertise in Harvey’s platform and workflows.\n\n - Strong understanding of corporate and transactional legal workflows, including M&A, commercial contracting, corporate governance, financing transactions, and due diligence.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and the ability to engage credibly with senior stakeholders across law firms, legal departments, and business organizations.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, including experience leading trainings, workshops, demos, or customer-facing sessions.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.\n\n - Strong point of view on the future of the legal industry and the impact of AI on legal services.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$315,000 - $385,000 USD OTE 75/25 Split \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$315K – $385K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$315K - $385K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5f4b64f4-7f6c-447c-8ff1-3375612eb396","tierSummary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"92768311-1489-45a7-bce2-15ee354d4324","summary":"OTE 75/25 $315K – $385K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000},{"id":"f15883f9-65d2-4f6a-b9ae-002337c0abc6","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":315000,"maxValue":385000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"caafbe5d-bd29-4d23-b3c2-e1cdb64c387e","title":"Technology Enablement Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T22:02:19.289+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/caafbe5d-bd29-4d23-b3c2-e1cdb64c387e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/caafbe5d-bd29-4d23-b3c2-e1cdb64c387e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows\n\n - Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content\n\n - Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI\n\n - Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts\n\n - Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management\n\n - Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)\n\n - Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences\n\n - Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders\n\n - Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bc87af4d-9638-4592-a3db-648f90f36f6c","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"73b89a9b-0348-4cd5-9493-872317e10670","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"id":"5890f8ab-db79-46cb-984b-8090ff679dd5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f1d918c4-d5cd-461b-bc6c-bae461995366","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2ab9606f-4d25-4aef-b62f-43103de1d5a4","title":"Senior Systems Analyst, Recruiting Operations","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T00:42:37.218+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2ab9606f-4d25-4aef-b62f-43103de1d5a4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2ab9606f-4d25-4aef-b62f-43103de1d5a4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1>Role Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Recruiting Operations Manager joins Harvey's Talent team to drive the systems infrastructure, process design, and AI-enabled automation that power a world-class recruiting function. The team's mission is to ensure every recruiter, hiring manager, and candidate experiences a seamless, data-informed hiring process from requisition open through Day 1. This role owns the end-to-end health of Harvey's recruiting technology stack—including Ashby architecture, integrations, and emerging AI tooling—and turns operational insights into scalable process improvements. Partnering closely with the Analytics team, they help define reporting requirements and interpret insights rather than building dashboards directly, ensuring data is translated into clear decisions for the talent organization. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape recruiting infrastructure at one of the fastest-growing AI companies during a period of rapid global expansion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own administration, configuration, and optimization of the recruiting tech stack (Ashby, integrations, downstream systems), ensuring data integrity and seamless workflows across global teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement process improvements that reduce recruiter friction, improve hiring velocity, and scale with organizational growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Analytics team to define reporting requirements, interpret recruiting data, and translate insights into actionable recommendations on pipeline health, funnel conversion, and capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage core recruiting operations workflows, including PID and requisition management, responding to recruiter and hiring manager tickets, and troubleshooting issues with offers and candidate communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and deploy AI-powered solutions across recruiting workflows—automating repetitive tasks, enhancing candidate experience, and enabling data-driven decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Finance on headcount planning, People Operations on onboarding handoffs, and IT on system integrations to ensure cross-functional alignment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You Have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations, HR technology, or business systems administration, with progressive ownership of a recruiting tech stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on expertise with modern ATS platforms (Ashby strongly preferred) including configuration, workflow design, and reporting configuration/usage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of implementing process improvements and automation—including AI/ML tooling—that measurably improved operational outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical mindset with the ability to partner with Analytics on dashboards and reporting, interpret data, and translate findings into strategic recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Systems thinking orientation—ability to map dependencies across tools, teams, and processes, and anticipate downstream effects of changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills and comfort partnering with Finance, Engineering, People, and IT stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$131,300 - $196,900 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Recruiting Operations Manager joins Harvey's Talent team to drive the systems infrastructure, process design, and AI-enabled automation that power a world-class recruiting function. The team's mission is to ensure every recruiter, hiring manager, and candidate experiences a seamless, data-informed hiring process from requisition open through Day 1. This role owns the end-to-end health of Harvey's recruiting technology stack—including Ashby architecture, integrations, and emerging AI tooling—and turns operational insights into scalable process improvements. Partnering closely with the Analytics team, they help define reporting requirements and interpret insights rather than building dashboards directly, ensuring data is translated into clear decisions for the talent organization. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape recruiting infrastructure at one of the fastest-growing AI companies during a period of rapid global expansion.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own administration, configuration, and optimization of the recruiting tech stack (Ashby, integrations, downstream systems), ensuring data integrity and seamless workflows across global teams.\n\n - Design and implement process improvements that reduce recruiter friction, improve hiring velocity, and scale with organizational growth.\n\n - Partner with the Analytics team to define reporting requirements, interpret recruiting data, and translate insights into actionable recommendations on pipeline health, funnel conversion, and capacity planning.\n\n - Manage core recruiting operations workflows, including PID and requisition management, responding to recruiter and hiring manager tickets, and troubleshooting issues with offers and candidate communications.\n\n - Identify and deploy AI-powered solutions across recruiting workflows—automating repetitive tasks, enhancing candidate experience, and enabling data-driven decision-making.\n\n - Partner with Finance on headcount planning, People Operations on onboarding handoffs, and IT on system integrations to ensure cross-functional alignment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations, HR technology, or business systems administration, with progressive ownership of a recruiting tech stack.\n\n - Deep hands-on expertise with modern ATS platforms (Ashby strongly preferred) including configuration, workflow design, and reporting configuration/usage.\n\n - Demonstrated track record of implementing process improvements and automation—including AI/ML tooling—that measurably improved operational outcomes.\n\n - Strong analytical mindset with the ability to partner with Analytics on dashboards and reporting, interpret data, and translate findings into strategic recommendations.\n\n - Systems thinking orientation—ability to map dependencies across tools, teams, and processes, and anticipate downstream effects of changes.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills and comfort partnering with Finance, Engineering, People, and IT stakeholders.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$131,300 - $196,900 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$131.3K – $196.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$131.3K - $196.9K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"36f97bfe-a3d4-4266-91fa-53f15b24af9a","tierSummary":"$131.3K – $196.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ebd982fd-020b-4f1c-b990-1ecf2563ea6b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c8f3323a-6eda-439a-afe1-e0149d6a9dbd","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"66b56285-0bc3-44d8-bea6-2a5063e1d321","summary":"$131.3K – $196.9K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":131300,"maxValue":196900}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":131300,"maxValue":196900}]}},{"id":"203e2d3b-6aeb-4d13-8e2f-62f7526658df","title":"IT Operations Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-23T16:17:46.945+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/203e2d3b-6aeb-4d13-8e2f-62f7526658df","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/203e2d3b-6aeb-4d13-8e2f-62f7526658df/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$109,100 - $163,700</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.\n\nThe IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.\n\nYou’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.\n\n - Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.\n\n - Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.\n\n - Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.\n\n - Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.\n\n - Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.\n\n - Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.\n\n - Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.\n\n - Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.\n\n - Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.\n\n - A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.\n\n - Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.\n\n - Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$109,100 - $163,700\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$109.1K – $163.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$109.1K - $163.7K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"85a1019d-7310-4d47-b4c7-dd69ff800842","tierSummary":"$109.1K – $163.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"514b1df9-3431-42b8-87c3-c19081e83b3d","summary":"$109.1K – $163.7K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":163700},{"id":"8161d0da-717e-48ba-9e68-2f48d0518a69","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"585e23dd-7865-4e2f-9075-6c8f9a838e08","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":163700},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8b3d2aef-b604-4c24-9c09-823a3cad984e","title":"Partner Program Lead","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T18:17:36.782+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8b3d2aef-b604-4c24-9c09-823a3cad984e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8b3d2aef-b604-4c24-9c09-823a3cad984e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Partner Programs Lead builds and scales the infrastructure that powers Harvey's partner ecosystem across technology, consulting, and channel relationships. They sit on the Partnerships Business Development team, translating Harvey's go-to-market priorities into clear, structured programs that partners can execute against. This role ensures Harvey's partner motion is repeatable, measurable, and tightly aligned with customer outcomes as the ecosystem grows. They act as the connective tissue between Partnerships, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to keep partners enabled and accountable. It is an opportunity to define the systems, programs, and incentives underpinning a category-defining AI partner ecosystem from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, launch, and continually refine Harvey's global partner program structure (tiers, benefits, requirements, and incentives) to drive ecosystem health and revenue impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the partner portal and core partner systems experience, ensuring that content, tools, and workflows make it easy for partners to onboard, get enabled, and co-sell with Harvey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run partner enablement and certification programs, including curricula, certification paths, and evaluation mechanisms that align to product updates and GTM priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and maintain the core partner KPI framework (e.g., sourced/influenced pipeline, activation, certification, NPS), and use data to recommend and drive program changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the operational and escalation point for partner issues — coordinating with Sales, CS, Support, Product, and Legal to resolve problems quickly while protecting Harvey's brand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Marketing, Sales, and Business Development to design and execute scalable motions (launch plays, campaigns, co-marketing) that increase partner productivity and satisfaction.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in partner programs, ecosystem operations, or channel programs within high-growth SaaS, AI, ML, or platform businesses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record designing and operating global partner or channel programs, including program structure, benefits/requirements, and partner lifecycle management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management and organizational skills — able to translate strategy into clear roadmaps, timelines, and cross-functional execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical strength with experience defining, instrumenting, and acting on partner metrics; comfortable making decisions with imperfect data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior partner leadership and internal executives in written, verbal, and presentation formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Calm, customer- and partner-obsessed mindset; able to navigate escalations and ambiguity while maintaining strong relationships and a focus on outcomes.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 - $270,000 OTE </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\nThe Partner Programs Lead builds and scales the infrastructure that powers Harvey's partner ecosystem across technology, consulting, and channel relationships. They sit on the Partnerships Business Development team, translating Harvey's go-to-market priorities into clear, structured programs that partners can execute against. This role ensures Harvey's partner motion is repeatable, measurable, and tightly aligned with customer outcomes as the ecosystem grows. They act as the connective tissue between Partnerships, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to keep partners enabled and accountable. It is an opportunity to define the systems, programs, and incentives underpinning a category-defining AI partner ecosystem from the ground up.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n - Design, launch, and continually refine Harvey's global partner program structure (tiers, benefits, requirements, and incentives) to drive ecosystem health and revenue impact.\n\n - Own the partner portal and core partner systems experience, ensuring that content, tools, and workflows make it easy for partners to onboard, get enabled, and co-sell with Harvey.\n\n - Build and run partner enablement and certification programs, including curricula, certification paths, and evaluation mechanisms that align to product updates and GTM priorities.\n\n - Define and maintain the core partner KPI framework (e.g., sourced/influenced pipeline, activation, certification, NPS), and use data to recommend and drive program changes.\n\n - Serve as the operational and escalation point for partner issues — coordinating with Sales, CS, Support, Product, and Legal to resolve problems quickly while protecting Harvey's brand.\n\n - Partner with Marketing, Sales, and Business Development to design and execute scalable motions (launch plays, campaigns, co-marketing) that increase partner productivity and satisfaction.\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 7+ years of experience in partner programs, ecosystem operations, or channel programs within high-growth SaaS, AI, ML, or platform businesses.\n\n - Proven track record designing and operating global partner or channel programs, including program structure, benefits/requirements, and partner lifecycle management.\n\n - Strong program management and organizational skills — able to translate strategy into clear roadmaps, timelines, and cross-functional execution.\n\n - Analytical strength with experience defining, instrumenting, and acting on partner metrics; comfortable making decisions with imperfect data.\n\n - Executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior partner leadership and internal executives in written, verbal, and presentation formats.\n\n - Calm, customer- and partner-obsessed mindset; able to navigate escalations and ambiguity while maintaining strong relationships and a focus on outcomes.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000 - $270,000 OTE \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-TA1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $270K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"414421e7-b726-4882-9085-e10ac09c075d","tierSummary":"$180K – $270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1de21679-f893-4ea6-b227-0741c8cdaf57","summary":"$180K – $270K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":270000},{"id":"c4756f69-809c-44e5-9bc2-16fe0bfa1ecc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e9864979-950d-403f-a65e-5377b83a07fa","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":270000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"51f9f397-c7ca-4b4f-a8f1-f5ff17076503","title":"Partner Program Lead","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T18:17:59.738+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/51f9f397-c7ca-4b4f-a8f1-f5ff17076503","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/51f9f397-c7ca-4b4f-a8f1-f5ff17076503/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Partner Programs Lead builds and scales the infrastructure that powers Harvey's partner ecosystem across technology, consulting, and channel relationships. They sit on the Partnerships Business Development team, translating Harvey's go-to-market priorities into clear, structured programs that partners can execute against. This role ensures Harvey's partner motion is repeatable, measurable, and tightly aligned with customer outcomes as the ecosystem grows. They act as the connective tissue between Partnerships, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to keep partners enabled and accountable. It is an opportunity to define the systems, programs, and incentives underpinning a category-defining AI partner ecosystem from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, launch, and continually refine Harvey's global partner program structure (tiers, benefits, requirements, and incentives) to drive ecosystem health and revenue impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the partner portal and core partner systems experience, ensuring that content, tools, and workflows make it easy for partners to onboard, get enabled, and co-sell with Harvey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run partner enablement and certification programs, including curricula, certification paths, and evaluation mechanisms that align to product updates and GTM priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and maintain the core partner KPI framework (e.g., sourced/influenced pipeline, activation, certification, NPS), and use data to recommend and drive program changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the operational and escalation point for partner issues — coordinating with Sales, CS, Support, Product, and Legal to resolve problems quickly while protecting Harvey's brand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Marketing, Sales, and Business Development to design and execute scalable motions (launch plays, campaigns, co-marketing) that increase partner productivity and satisfaction.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in partner programs, ecosystem operations, or channel programs within high-growth SaaS, AI, ML, or platform businesses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record designing and operating global partner or channel programs, including program structure, benefits/requirements, and partner lifecycle management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management and organizational skills — able to translate strategy into clear roadmaps, timelines, and cross-functional execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical strength with experience defining, instrumenting, and acting on partner metrics; comfortable making decisions with imperfect data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior partner leadership and internal executives in written, verbal, and presentation formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Calm, customer- and partner-obsessed mindset; able to navigate escalations and ambiguity while maintaining strong relationships and a focus on outcomes.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 - $270,000 OTE</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\nThe Partner Programs Lead builds and scales the infrastructure that powers Harvey's partner ecosystem across technology, consulting, and channel relationships. They sit on the Partnerships Business Development team, translating Harvey's go-to-market priorities into clear, structured programs that partners can execute against. This role ensures Harvey's partner motion is repeatable, measurable, and tightly aligned with customer outcomes as the ecosystem grows. They act as the connective tissue between Partnerships, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to keep partners enabled and accountable. It is an opportunity to define the systems, programs, and incentives underpinning a category-defining AI partner ecosystem from the ground up.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n - Design, launch, and continually refine Harvey's global partner program structure (tiers, benefits, requirements, and incentives) to drive ecosystem health and revenue impact.\n\n - Own the partner portal and core partner systems experience, ensuring that content, tools, and workflows make it easy for partners to onboard, get enabled, and co-sell with Harvey.\n\n - Build and run partner enablement and certification programs, including curricula, certification paths, and evaluation mechanisms that align to product updates and GTM priorities.\n\n - Define and maintain the core partner KPI framework (e.g., sourced/influenced pipeline, activation, certification, NPS), and use data to recommend and drive program changes.\n\n - Serve as the operational and escalation point for partner issues — coordinating with Sales, CS, Support, Product, and Legal to resolve problems quickly while protecting Harvey's brand.\n\n - Partner with Marketing, Sales, and Business Development to design and execute scalable motions (launch plays, campaigns, co-marketing) that increase partner productivity and satisfaction.\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 7+ years of experience in partner programs, ecosystem operations, or channel programs within high-growth SaaS, AI, ML, or platform businesses.\n\n - Proven track record designing and operating global partner or channel programs, including program structure, benefits/requirements, and partner lifecycle management.\n\n - Strong program management and organizational skills — able to translate strategy into clear roadmaps, timelines, and cross-functional execution.\n\n - Analytical strength with experience defining, instrumenting, and acting on partner metrics; comfortable making decisions with imperfect data.\n\n - Executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior partner leadership and internal executives in written, verbal, and presentation formats.\n\n - Calm, customer- and partner-obsessed mindset; able to navigate escalations and ambiguity while maintaining strong relationships and a focus on outcomes.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000 - $270,000 OTE\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-TA1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $270K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e734404f-e504-4389-8bb9-4b1ee8f35996","tierSummary":"$180K – $270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8bb9b05d-621c-45e5-9af7-335e18909aa2","summary":"$180K – $270K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":270000},{"id":"a68add8c-f7ac-4461-a45b-455d0feffd16","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4046db85-8303-44ea-97d3-c1ebc3e12362","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":270000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1321b20d-d6f8-4bdb-b2de-ec33c0948b53","title":"Data Scientist, Product","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T23:21:52.287+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1321b20d-d6f8-4bdb-b2de-ec33c0948b53","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1321b20d-d6f8-4bdb-b2de-ec33c0948b53/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Data Scientist, you will be a core member of Harvey's product development organization and one of the foundational members of the Data Science function. You will partner with Product, Engineering, Design, Go-to-Market, and company leadership to define how we measure product success, understand user behavior, and make high-quality decisions in a fast-moving environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both strategic and hands-on. You will define north-star and product-level metrics, design experiments and causal analyses, build source-of-truth reporting, and turn ambiguous product questions into clear recommendations. You should be comfortable operating where the data is imperfect, the product is evolving quickly, and the right answer requires both analytical rigor and strong product judgment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed with Product and Engineering teams as a trusted analytical partner, identifying opportunities to improve user experience, adoption, retention, and business impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and maintain core metrics that create a shared understanding of product performance and customer value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and evaluate experiments, including A/B tests and causal inference methods, to measure the impact of product, model, and workflow changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze product usage, customer segments, and go-to-market signals to surface insights, size opportunities, and inform roadmap decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build dashboards, reports, and self-serve tools that help teams answer product questions with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop models, forecasts, and analytical frameworks to explain user behavior, detect anomalies, and guide prioritization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate complex analyses into clear recommendations for technical, business, and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering and Data teams to improve the infrastructure that powers analytics, experimentation, and decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish the standards, practices, and culture for Product Data Science at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in data science, product analytics, economics, statistics, or another quantitative field, ideally in a high-growth product company, AI company, research organization, or similarly ambiguous environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong track record of using SQL, Python, and statistical methods to answer product questions and turn analysis into product or business impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience defining new metrics and measurement frameworks from scratch, especially for products where usage patterns, customer value, or success criteria are still being discovered.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep fluency in experimentation, causal inference, A/B testing, and statistical modeling, with good judgment about when precision matters and when directional clarity is enough.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product instincts and curiosity about how users adopt, evaluate, and expand their use of AI-enabled workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to influence Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, and executive stakeholders through clear reasoning and compelling data stories.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort creating structure in fast-moving, ambiguous environments and raising the quality of decision-making for the teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML products, large language models, developer tools, enterprise software, or products used in complex professional workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience as an early data science or analytics hire at a hyper-growth startup, including helping define team norms, tooling, and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting enterprise or B2B products, including analysis of adoption, engagement, retention, expansion, or go-to-market motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with modern data infrastructure and the practical tradeoffs involved in building reliable analytics in a rapidly evolving product environment.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,000 - $260,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Data Scientist, you will be a core member of Harvey's product development organization and one of the foundational members of the Data Science function. You will partner with Product, Engineering, Design, Go-to-Market, and company leadership to define how we measure product success, understand user behavior, and make high-quality decisions in a fast-moving environment.\n\nThis role is both strategic and hands-on. You will define north-star and product-level metrics, design experiments and causal analyses, build source-of-truth reporting, and turn ambiguous product questions into clear recommendations. You should be comfortable operating where the data is imperfect, the product is evolving quickly, and the right answer requires both analytical rigor and strong product judgment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Embed with Product and Engineering teams as a trusted analytical partner, identifying opportunities to improve user experience, adoption, retention, and business impact.\n\n - Define and maintain core metrics that create a shared understanding of product performance and customer value.\n\n - Design and evaluate experiments, including A/B tests and causal inference methods, to measure the impact of product, model, and workflow changes.\n\n - Analyze product usage, customer segments, and go-to-market signals to surface insights, size opportunities, and inform roadmap decisions.\n\n - Build dashboards, reports, and self-serve tools that help teams answer product questions with confidence.\n\n - Develop models, forecasts, and analytical frameworks to explain user behavior, detect anomalies, and guide prioritization.\n\n - Translate complex analyses into clear recommendations for technical, business, and executive audiences.\n\n - Partner with Engineering and Data teams to improve the infrastructure that powers analytics, experimentation, and decision-making.\n\n - Establish the standards, practices, and culture for Product Data Science at Harvey.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in data science, product analytics, economics, statistics, or another quantitative field, ideally in a high-growth product company, AI company, research organization, or similarly ambiguous environment.\n\n - A strong track record of using SQL, Python, and statistical methods to answer product questions and turn analysis into product or business impact.\n\n - Experience defining new metrics and measurement frameworks from scratch, especially for products where usage patterns, customer value, or success criteria are still being discovered.\n\n - Deep fluency in experimentation, causal inference, A/B testing, and statistical modeling, with good judgment about when precision matters and when directional clarity is enough.\n\n - Strong product instincts and curiosity about how users adopt, evaluate, and expand their use of AI-enabled workflows.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to influence Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, and executive stakeholders through clear reasoning and compelling data stories.\n\n - Comfort creating structure in fast-moving, ambiguous environments and raising the quality of decision-making for the teams.\n\nBonus\n\n - Experience with AI/ML products, large language models, developer tools, enterprise software, or products used in complex professional workflows.\n\n - Experience as an early data science or analytics hire at a hyper-growth startup, including helping define team norms, tooling, and best practices.\n\n - Experience supporting enterprise or B2B products, including analysis of adoption, engagement, retention, expansion, or go-to-market motion.\n\n - Familiarity with modern data infrastructure and the practical tradeoffs involved in building reliable analytics in a rapidly evolving product environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,000 - $260,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-SB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"377b8b66-cd15-48bf-b2c0-39fdf4fedad7","tierSummary":"$155K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b035955a-c158-4df9-9833-31e4d640bdf5","summary":"$155K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"3fc43eec-bb17-4a81-b6d5-ef8f4c2146bf","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f5d7114c-e80d-4182-93ea-a0a4cc61e6f1","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"667ee044-f6ae-4714-8339-ff949f8faef1","title":"Customer Success Manager, Enterprise, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T12:28:56.086+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/667ee044-f6ae-4714-8339-ff949f8faef1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/667ee044-f6ae-4714-8339-ff949f8faef1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong>: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships</strong>: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics</strong>: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion and Renewal</strong>: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing customer-facing projects and timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Running in-person meetings w/ executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Driving key customer metrics and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Success Metrics: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.\n\n - Expansion and Renewal: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:\n\n - 3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth\n\n - Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization\n\n - Managing customer-facing projects and timelines\n\n - Running in-person meetings w/ executives\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders\n\n - Driving key customer metrics and outcomes\n\n - Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0fd353e8-616d-44f4-b93a-bed92f15b043","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend - NYC","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-22T21:39:12.740+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0fd353e8-616d-44f4-b93a-bed92f15b043","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0fd353e8-616d-44f4-b93a-bed92f15b043/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$</strong>193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-PM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5cf35ec2-4ce2-483f-8949-d43e35b24034","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2c6b3b81-06cf-4dde-82e9-01eabb50e29a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"eefa4af6-323b-4659-bde8-ab291ecc983b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f276cf14-e67b-454c-bf75-e7b41e496ea9","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"76d7a078-01c9-48d1-8481-3bfb728b657e","title":"Technical Program Manager, Incident Response","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-23T15:39:58.810+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/76d7a078-01c9-48d1-8481-3bfb728b657e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/76d7a078-01c9-48d1-8481-3bfb728b657e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Incident Response Technical Program Manager is a senior cross-functional operator who will lead Harvey's response to security and reliability incidents, coordinating across engineering, security, and business teams under pressure. You will join the Detection &amp; Response function within Harvey's Information Security organization, whose mission is to detect, contain, and remediate threats to the platform that serves the world's leading law firms and enterprises. This role defines the standard for how Harvey runs and learns from incidents — building the coordination playbooks, communication protocols, and post-incident remediation programs that close structural gaps. As the first dedicated incident response program hire, you will partner directly with security engineering, product, and executive leadership to shape a function from the ground up. This is a rare opportunity to build the incident management discipline at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with meaningful influence over how a high-trust platform protects its most sensitive customer data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end coordination of security and reliability incidents — from initial triage through resolution — ensuring clear roles, rapid decision-making, and structured communication across engineering, security, legal, and customer-facing teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement incident management processes, runbooks, and escalation frameworks that scale with Harvey's growth and reflect the realities of operating AI-native SaaS infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead post-incident reviews and drive remediation programs to completion, tracking follow-up items across teams and holding stakeholders accountable to timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain incident readiness — including tabletop exercises, on-call coordination improvements, and tooling for real-time situational awareness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the communication hub during active incidents, translating technical status into clear updates for executives, legal, and customer success without losing fidelity.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in incident management, technical program management, or a related coordination-heavy role within a software or security organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams through high-pressure situations with composure, clarity, and strong interpersonal judgment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sufficient technical depth to understand distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, and security concepts at a level that enables effective triage and stakeholder translation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams, track dependencies, and drive accountability without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building incident response or operational programs from scratch, including defining processes, documentation, and success metrics in ambiguous environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High emotional intelligence and the communication skills to operate credibly with engineers, executives, legal counsel, and external stakeholders alike.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$150,900 - $226,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Incident Response Technical Program Manager is a senior cross-functional operator who will lead Harvey's response to security and reliability incidents, coordinating across engineering, security, and business teams under pressure. You will join the Detection & Response function within Harvey's Information Security organization, whose mission is to detect, contain, and remediate threats to the platform that serves the world's leading law firms and enterprises. This role defines the standard for how Harvey runs and learns from incidents — building the coordination playbooks, communication protocols, and post-incident remediation programs that close structural gaps. As the first dedicated incident response program hire, you will partner directly with security engineering, product, and executive leadership to shape a function from the ground up. This is a rare opportunity to build the incident management discipline at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with meaningful influence over how a high-trust platform protects its most sensitive customer data.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end coordination of security and reliability incidents — from initial triage through resolution — ensuring clear roles, rapid decision-making, and structured communication across engineering, security, legal, and customer-facing teams.\n\n - Design and implement incident management processes, runbooks, and escalation frameworks that scale with Harvey's growth and reflect the realities of operating AI-native SaaS infrastructure.\n\n - Lead post-incident reviews and drive remediation programs to completion, tracking follow-up items across teams and holding stakeholders accountable to timelines.\n\n - Build and maintain incident readiness — including tabletop exercises, on-call coordination improvements, and tooling for real-time situational awareness.\n\n - Serve as the communication hub during active incidents, translating technical status into clear updates for executives, legal, and customer success without losing fidelity.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in incident management, technical program management, or a related coordination-heavy role within a software or security organization.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams through high-pressure situations with composure, clarity, and strong interpersonal judgment.\n\n - Sufficient technical depth to understand distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, and security concepts at a level that enables effective triage and stakeholder translation.\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams, track dependencies, and drive accountability without direct authority.\n\n - Experience building incident response or operational programs from scratch, including defining processes, documentation, and success metrics in ambiguous environments.\n\n - High emotional intelligence and the communication skills to operate credibly with engineers, executives, legal counsel, and external stakeholders alike.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$150,900 - $226,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150.9K – $226.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150.9K - $226.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"92314dd2-3ba0-43a2-97d0-1bbf010bf867","tierSummary":"$150.9K – $226.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e09ab862-caba-4938-9e6d-e7cb69f8a3cf","summary":"$150.9K – $226.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150900,"maxValue":226300},{"id":"bb346e01-e184-4ddb-8404-04dfd5712fa9","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"3b25e1a4-7b4a-4f84-a001-09b833c7913b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150900,"maxValue":226300},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"36bce60d-eedc-4347-af80-9321aaa88b48","title":"Technical Program Manager, Incident Response","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-23T15:40:02.601+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/36bce60d-eedc-4347-af80-9321aaa88b48","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/36bce60d-eedc-4347-af80-9321aaa88b48/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Incident Response Technical Program Manager is a senior cross-functional operator who will lead Harvey's response to security and reliability incidents, coordinating across engineering, security, and business teams under pressure. You will join the Detection &amp; Response function within Harvey's Information Security organization, whose mission is to detect, contain, and remediate threats to the platform that serves the world's leading law firms and enterprises. This role defines the standard for how Harvey runs and learns from incidents — building the coordination playbooks, communication protocols, and post-incident remediation programs that close structural gaps. As the first dedicated incident response program hire, you will partner directly with security engineering, product, and executive leadership to shape a function from the ground up. This is a rare opportunity to build the incident management discipline at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with meaningful influence over how a high-trust platform protects its most sensitive customer data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end coordination of security and reliability incidents — from initial triage through resolution — ensuring clear roles, rapid decision-making, and structured communication across engineering, security, legal, and customer-facing teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement incident management processes, runbooks, and escalation frameworks that scale with Harvey's growth and reflect the realities of operating AI-native SaaS infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead post-incident reviews and drive remediation programs to completion, tracking follow-up items across teams and holding stakeholders accountable to timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain incident readiness — including tabletop exercises, on-call coordination improvements, and tooling for real-time situational awareness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the communication hub during active incidents, translating technical status into clear updates for executives, legal, and customer success without losing fidelity.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in incident management, technical program management, or a related coordination-heavy role within a software or security organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams through high-pressure situations with composure, clarity, and strong interpersonal judgment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sufficient technical depth to understand distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, and security concepts at a level that enables effective triage and stakeholder translation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams, track dependencies, and drive accountability without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building incident response or operational programs from scratch, including defining processes, documentation, and success metrics in ambiguous environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High emotional intelligence and the communication skills to operate credibly with engineers, executives, legal counsel, and external stakeholders alike.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$150,900 - $226,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Incident Response Technical Program Manager is a senior cross-functional operator who will lead Harvey's response to security and reliability incidents, coordinating across engineering, security, and business teams under pressure. You will join the Detection & Response function within Harvey's Information Security organization, whose mission is to detect, contain, and remediate threats to the platform that serves the world's leading law firms and enterprises. This role defines the standard for how Harvey runs and learns from incidents — building the coordination playbooks, communication protocols, and post-incident remediation programs that close structural gaps. As the first dedicated incident response program hire, you will partner directly with security engineering, product, and executive leadership to shape a function from the ground up. This is a rare opportunity to build the incident management discipline at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with meaningful influence over how a high-trust platform protects its most sensitive customer data.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end coordination of security and reliability incidents — from initial triage through resolution — ensuring clear roles, rapid decision-making, and structured communication across engineering, security, legal, and customer-facing teams.\n\n - Design and implement incident management processes, runbooks, and escalation frameworks that scale with Harvey's growth and reflect the realities of operating AI-native SaaS infrastructure.\n\n - Lead post-incident reviews and drive remediation programs to completion, tracking follow-up items across teams and holding stakeholders accountable to timelines.\n\n - Build and maintain incident readiness — including tabletop exercises, on-call coordination improvements, and tooling for real-time situational awareness.\n\n - Serve as the communication hub during active incidents, translating technical status into clear updates for executives, legal, and customer success without losing fidelity.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in incident management, technical program management, or a related coordination-heavy role within a software or security organization.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams through high-pressure situations with composure, clarity, and strong interpersonal judgment.\n\n - Sufficient technical depth to understand distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, and security concepts at a level that enables effective triage and stakeholder translation.\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills — able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams, track dependencies, and drive accountability without direct authority.\n\n - Experience building incident response or operational programs from scratch, including defining processes, documentation, and success metrics in ambiguous environments.\n\n - High emotional intelligence and the communication skills to operate credibly with engineers, executives, legal counsel, and external stakeholders alike.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\n$150,900 - $226,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150.9K – $226.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150.9K - $226.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3d5cff5a-3b5e-4411-99eb-9f828a2f6ef4","tierSummary":"$150.9K – $226.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"52e620ca-6bc2-43b7-8044-14ab0a4991f5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a22c6e96-40eb-4de8-adae-68881ee0a39c","summary":"$150.9K – $226.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150900,"maxValue":226300},{"id":"fa8f783a-d414-4914-9d6c-873498cf8a8b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150900,"maxValue":226300},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a194c24f-38ee-4c7e-908b-060a16dfaa9d","title":"Law School Student Ambassador","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-25T16:59:33.472+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a194c24f-38ee-4c7e-908b-060a16dfaa9d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a194c24f-38ee-4c7e-908b-060a16dfaa9d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Law School Student Ambassador is a current JD candidate who serves as Harvey's on-campus champion, connecting the product with the student community at their law school. This role sits within the Law School Partnerships team, whose mission is to make Harvey an indispensable part of legal education by embedding the platform into how students learn and work. By building peer-to-peer awareness and hosting hands-on programming, the Ambassador accelerates student adoption and generates insights that shape Harvey's academic go-to-market strategy. They partner with faculty, student organizations, and Harvey's internal partnerships and marketing teams to tailor campus engagement to their school's unique culture. It is a rare opportunity for a law student to gain frontline experience at one of the fastest-growing AI companies while developing skills in community building, product evangelism, and cross-functional collaboration.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as Harvey's on-campus representative, hosting workshops, demos, and informational sessions that drive awareness and active usage across your law school community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain relationships with law school faculty, librarians, student organizations, and career services to integrate Harvey into academic programming.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute a campus engagement plan each semester, tailored to your school's community, events calendar, and student needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect and relay student feedback—including feature requests, adoption barriers, and use-case insights—to the Partnerships team to inform product and program strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and report on engagement metrics such as sign-ups, active users, and event attendance to measure program impact at your school.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently enrolled in a JD program at an accredited law school (1L, 2L, or 3L) that is part of Harvey’s Law School Program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated leadership in student organizations, journals, moot court, or campus initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage peers, faculty, and administrators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine enthusiasm for AI and its potential to transform the practice of law.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and able to execute independently in a remote, distributed environment with minimal day-to-day oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with technology and willingness to develop deep product knowledge of Harvey's platform.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LW1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Law School Student Ambassador is a current JD candidate who serves as Harvey's on-campus champion, connecting the product with the student community at their law school. This role sits within the Law School Partnerships team, whose mission is to make Harvey an indispensable part of legal education by embedding the platform into how students learn and work. By building peer-to-peer awareness and hosting hands-on programming, the Ambassador accelerates student adoption and generates insights that shape Harvey's academic go-to-market strategy. They partner with faculty, student organizations, and Harvey's internal partnerships and marketing teams to tailor campus engagement to their school's unique culture. It is a rare opportunity for a law student to gain frontline experience at one of the fastest-growing AI companies while developing skills in community building, product evangelism, and cross-functional collaboration.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as Harvey's on-campus representative, hosting workshops, demos, and informational sessions that drive awareness and active usage across your law school community.\n\n - Build and maintain relationships with law school faculty, librarians, student organizations, and career services to integrate Harvey into academic programming.\n\n - Develop and execute a campus engagement plan each semester, tailored to your school's community, events calendar, and student needs.\n\n - Collect and relay student feedback—including feature requests, adoption barriers, and use-case insights—to the Partnerships team to inform product and program strategy.\n\n - Track and report on engagement metrics such as sign-ups, active users, and event attendance to measure program impact at your school.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Currently enrolled in a JD program at an accredited law school (1L, 2L, or 3L) that is part of Harvey’s Law School Program.\n\n - Demonstrated leadership in student organizations, journals, moot court, or campus initiatives.\n\n - Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage peers, faculty, and administrators.\n\n - Genuine enthusiasm for AI and its potential to transform the practice of law.\n\n - Self-motivated and able to execute independently in a remote, distributed environment with minimal day-to-day oversight.\n\n - Comfort with technology and willingness to develop deep product knowledge of Harvey's platform.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-LW1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3931a1b7-573d-4bd8-8fed-3fa8132c3201","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T23:33:01.903+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3931a1b7-573d-4bd8-8fed-3fa8132c3201","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3931a1b7-573d-4bd8-8fed-3fa8132c3201/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend—to architect intuitive UX and robust APIs for streaming results, long-running processes, and complex tool-calling workflows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-PM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4c0991bb-37fe-4aca-bf1e-6e027ca46e2d","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a8a41dd3-5abe-49fa-85ca-03d0d048d823","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"8448e215-292d-4941-a5fe-6294036d0c51","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"480e3c0e-a96b-4a8e-87a7-974fabac0c4f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8afd7e79-96be-413f-a8a8-391e7d2113e6","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Frontend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T22:58:43.094+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8afd7e79-96be-413f-a8a8-391e7d2113e6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8afd7e79-96be-413f-a8a8-391e7d2113e6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York City. We follow an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build government-level security for top governments and firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-PM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Product Engineering team at Harvey, you will own and lead engineering projects across our various product lines. You will work closely with our AI, Legal, and GTM teams to build secure systems that deliver value to our customers. We are looking for individuals who have worked across the stack on incredible products across consumer, enterprise, and various industries and who are excited about building the future of application layer and genAI products.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York City. We follow an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Scale document ingestion and processing that is growing at 10x every 6 months\n\n - Design massive data collection from over 50+ legal jurisdictions\n\n - Build government-level security for top governments and firms\n\n - Lead projects that delight customers in bringing AI to web, desktop, mobile, Google Docs, MS Word, and API experiences.\n\n - Build AI-platform and AI-native features like agentic orchestration layers, tool calls, and retrieval systems.\n\n - Ship across the full stack—leveraging React and TypeScript on the frontend alongside Python and Postgres on the backend.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ Years of experience (post-BS/MS) in a product focused full-stack software engineering role.\n\n - Experience with React, Typescript, CSS (we use TailwindCSS), Python, or related.\n\n - Track record of building fast-growing SaaS products.\n\n - Track record of shipping highly intuitive products, strong attention to detail.\n\n - Experience building scalable and extensible solutions across the stack that can support multiple product lines.\n\n - Strong programming skills and general Computer Science knowledge.\n\n - Grit - experience working at early-stage startups is a plus.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-PM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f0f0cc9a-ce19-4b6d-9c97-a24c70e98398","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"81f11239-dfef-4eb0-ade9-8f9c175d6a86","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"017242ed-af59-4090-a2cd-51d838a62eb2","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5a76fdd1-cc98-453d-af7a-0b586a4f09d4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"99c7e2f7-9fe9-4373-9bf3-5470044bcd77","title":"Head of GTM Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T18:32:56.815+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/99c7e2f7-9fe9-4373-9bf3-5470044bcd77","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/99c7e2f7-9fe9-4373-9bf3-5470044bcd77/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Head of GTM Finance at Harvey, you will serve as the financial partner to our GTM organization, providing the analytical rigor and strategic insight that drives revenue growth and commercial decision-making. Reporting to the VP of Strategic Finance and working closely with the CBO and GTM leadership, you will own the financial model for Harvey's revenue engine — from bookings and pipeline to sales productivity and customer economics. The ideal candidate combines deep SaaS finance expertise with a builder's mindset and a strong bias toward actionable insight.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the unit economics. </strong>CAC, payback, magic number, net revenue retention, contribution margin by segment and motion. Know what makes money and what doesn't.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Plan sales capacity. </strong> Partner with the GTM team to determine how many reps, where, ramped how fast, carrying what quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the GTM financial model,</strong> including bookings, ARR, sales capacity planning, and quota design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead the GTM planning</strong> <strong>and budgeting</strong> processes, ensuring we are investing appropriately  across Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships to support our top-line targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Serve as the financial lead for deal structuring and pricing decisions,</strong> including non-standard commercial terms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify trends, risks, and opportunities</strong> across the revenue funnel; translate data into clear recommendations for GTM leadership and the executive team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Establish and maintain a monthly/quarterly GTM reporting package</strong> for the executive team and Board, including pipeline, bookings, and retention metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive ongoing improvement of GTM financial processes and tooling,</strong> with a focus on CRM integrity, forecasting accuracy, and automation.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years experience, including 3+ years Sales Finance experience at a high-growth and scaled enterprise software company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A first-principles thinker. You build from a blank page and question every input.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You partner with senior GTM leaders; have exceptional cross-functional communication skills and are able to influence and operate effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You move fast and own outcomes, not tasks.  You turn analysis into decisions and explain them in plain language.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of SaaS and usage-based business models, including ARR, NRR, CAC, LTV, and sales productivity metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional analytical skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder mindset.  Process and systems- oriented.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable in SQL or BI tools — you can pull your own data.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in a quantitative field preferred.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$201,200-284,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Head of GTM Finance at Harvey, you will serve as the financial partner to our GTM organization, providing the analytical rigor and strategic insight that drives revenue growth and commercial decision-making. Reporting to the VP of Strategic Finance and working closely with the CBO and GTM leadership, you will own the financial model for Harvey's revenue engine — from bookings and pipeline to sales productivity and customer economics. The ideal candidate combines deep SaaS finance expertise with a builder's mindset and a strong bias toward actionable insight.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the unit economics. CAC, payback, magic number, net revenue retention, contribution margin by segment and motion. Know what makes money and what doesn't.\n\n - Plan sales capacity.  Partner with the GTM team to determine how many reps, where, ramped how fast, carrying what quota\n\n - Own the GTM financial model, including bookings, ARR, sales capacity planning, and quota design.\n\n - Lead the GTM planning and budgeting processes, ensuring we are investing appropriately  across Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships to support our top-line targets.\n\n - Serve as the financial lead for deal structuring and pricing decisions, including non-standard commercial terms.\n\n - Identify trends, risks, and opportunities across the revenue funnel; translate data into clear recommendations for GTM leadership and the executive team.\n\n - Establish and maintain a monthly/quarterly GTM reporting package for the executive team and Board, including pipeline, bookings, and retention metrics.\n\n - Drive ongoing improvement of GTM financial processes and tooling, with a focus on CRM integrity, forecasting accuracy, and automation.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years experience, including 3+ years Sales Finance experience at a high-growth and scaled enterprise software company.\n\n - A first-principles thinker. You build from a blank page and question every input.\n\n - You partner with senior GTM leaders; have exceptional cross-functional communication skills and are able to influence and operate effectively.\n\n - You move fast and own outcomes, not tasks.  You turn analysis into decisions and explain them in plain language.\n\n - Deep understanding of SaaS and usage-based business models, including ARR, NRR, CAC, LTV, and sales productivity metrics.\n\n - Exceptional analytical skills.\n\n - Builder mindset.  Process and systems- oriented.\n\n - Comfortable in SQL or BI tools — you can pull your own data.\n\n - Bachelor's degree in a quantitative field preferred.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$201,200-284,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TA1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$201.2K – $284.3K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$201.2K - $284.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8644cb67-6ccb-4bd0-aa85-9363937f28f4","tierSummary":"$201.2K – $284.3K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"963c4216-b8d5-4763-8a68-4906910d73f8","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"30842055-0c1d-4262-ad19-55e2a6c34957","summary":"$201.2K – $284.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201200,"maxValue":284300}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201200,"maxValue":284300}]}},{"id":"d5d27b01-b6d7-4e34-976d-9d04b334afdc","title":"Head of GTM Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T18:32:50.223+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d5d27b01-b6d7-4e34-976d-9d04b334afdc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d5d27b01-b6d7-4e34-976d-9d04b334afdc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Head of GTM Finance at Harvey, you will serve as the financial partner to our GTM organization, providing the analytical rigor and strategic insight that drives revenue growth and commercial decision-making. Reporting to the VP of Strategic Finance and working closely with the CBO and GTM leadership, you will own the financial model for Harvey's revenue engine — from bookings and pipeline to sales productivity and customer economics. The ideal candidate combines deep SaaS finance expertise with a builder's mindset and a strong bias toward actionable insight.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the unit economics. </strong>CAC, payback, magic number, net revenue retention, contribution margin by segment and motion. Know what makes money and what doesn't.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Plan sales capacity. </strong> Partner with the GTM team to determine how many reps, where, ramped how fast, carrying what quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the GTM financial model,</strong> including bookings, ARR, sales capacity planning, and quota design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead the GTM planning</strong> <strong>and budgeting</strong> processes, ensuring we are investing appropriately  across Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships to support our top-line targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Serve as the financial lead for deal structuring and pricing decisions,</strong> including non-standard commercial terms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify trends, risks, and opportunities</strong> across the revenue funnel; translate data into clear recommendations for GTM leadership and the executive team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Establish and maintain a monthly/quarterly GTM reporting package</strong> for the executive team and Board, including pipeline, bookings, and retention metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive ongoing improvement of GTM financial processes and tooling,</strong> with a focus on CRM integrity, forecasting accuracy, and automation.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years experience, including 3+ years Sales Finance experience at a high-growth and scaled enterprise software company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A first-principles thinker. You build from a blank page and question every input.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You partner with senior GTM leaders; have exceptional cross-functional communication skills and are able to influence and operate effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You move fast and own outcomes, not tasks.  You turn analysis into decisions and explain them in plain language.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of SaaS and usage-based business models, including ARR, NRR, CAC, LTV, and sales productivity metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional analytical skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder mindset.  Process and systems- oriented.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable in SQL or BI tools — you can pull your own data.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in a quantitative field preferred.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$201,200-284,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Head of GTM Finance at Harvey, you will serve as the financial partner to our GTM organization, providing the analytical rigor and strategic insight that drives revenue growth and commercial decision-making. Reporting to the VP of Strategic Finance and working closely with the CBO and GTM leadership, you will own the financial model for Harvey's revenue engine — from bookings and pipeline to sales productivity and customer economics. The ideal candidate combines deep SaaS finance expertise with a builder's mindset and a strong bias toward actionable insight.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the unit economics. CAC, payback, magic number, net revenue retention, contribution margin by segment and motion. Know what makes money and what doesn't.\n\n - Plan sales capacity.  Partner with the GTM team to determine how many reps, where, ramped how fast, carrying what quota\n\n - Own the GTM financial model, including bookings, ARR, sales capacity planning, and quota design.\n\n - Lead the GTM planning and budgeting processes, ensuring we are investing appropriately  across Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships to support our top-line targets.\n\n - Serve as the financial lead for deal structuring and pricing decisions, including non-standard commercial terms.\n\n - Identify trends, risks, and opportunities across the revenue funnel; translate data into clear recommendations for GTM leadership and the executive team.\n\n - Establish and maintain a monthly/quarterly GTM reporting package for the executive team and Board, including pipeline, bookings, and retention metrics.\n\n - Drive ongoing improvement of GTM financial processes and tooling, with a focus on CRM integrity, forecasting accuracy, and automation.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years experience, including 3+ years Sales Finance experience at a high-growth and scaled enterprise software company.\n\n - A first-principles thinker. You build from a blank page and question every input.\n\n - You partner with senior GTM leaders; have exceptional cross-functional communication skills and are able to influence and operate effectively.\n\n - You move fast and own outcomes, not tasks.  You turn analysis into decisions and explain them in plain language.\n\n - Deep understanding of SaaS and usage-based business models, including ARR, NRR, CAC, LTV, and sales productivity metrics.\n\n - Exceptional analytical skills.\n\n - Builder mindset.  Process and systems- oriented.\n\n - Comfortable in SQL or BI tools — you can pull your own data.\n\n - Bachelor's degree in a quantitative field preferred.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$201,200-284,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TA1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$201.2K – $284.3K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$201.2K - $284.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f9bbcb15-0cb0-4b1e-9b98-fdd760a993cb","tierSummary":"$201.2K – $284.3K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"10936d53-8f88-4a92-a896-8e2f13554836","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f1027f24-c535-4b8a-a226-cfe7bbd769fa","summary":"$201.2K – $284.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201200,"maxValue":284300}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":201200,"maxValue":284300}]}},{"id":"fa1b9be4-3270-45fd-9226-223b71616db9","title":"Law Schools Founding CSM","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-14T15:04:56.442+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fa1b9be4-3270-45fd-9226-223b71616db9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fa1b9be4-3270-45fd-9226-223b71616db9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Law School Founding CSM is the global CS and activation function for the law school program. You serve all geo managers — US East, US West, and International — as the operational backbone for product training, onboarding, account health, and activation across every school in the portfolio. This is not a US role that also covers international; it is a global IC role that all geo managers draw on.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think of it as a tag-team model: geo managers own the school relationships and program strategy; you own the deeper product delivery and account management. This is the first dedicated CS hire for law schools. You will build the playbook as you go. Reports to the Head of Legal Partnerships, Law Schools.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run the scaled post-sign partnership model for long tail school partners across all geographies — playbooks, templated cadences, training materials, and activation milestones</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Legal Engineers and Law School Managers to translate school feedback into program improvements and deeper embeds on key campuses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own portfolio-wide reporting: track usage trends, activation status, and account health globally; surface risks and opportunities to all geo managers and to Grace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own product training and demo delivery across the full law school portfolio — onboarding sessions, faculty demos, librarian trainings, classroom embeds, and workspace setup.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the law school CRM across all geographies — account notes, POC data, meeting logs, and opportunity tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-of-term recap cycles, capturing Y1 learnings and aligning on Y2 activation goals with key internal stakeholders and Law School champions.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in customer success, account or program management, or client services — preferably in a high-growth SaaS, legal tech, or professional services environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the machine mindset: you build systems, write playbooks, and hold yourself to metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Player-coach approach: You are a founding CSM for this team and will have a strong part in growing it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong trainer and presenter — you can run a room of law professors or a 1:1 demo with a student org leader and make both count</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal background or strong legal context is a plus, not a requirement — comfort explaining legal AI tools to a sophisticated legal audience matters more than a JD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building scaled or tech-touch CS programs for large, distributed account portfolios</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, direct communicator who doesn't let follow-ups fall through the cracks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working across time zones and geographies in close coordination with a distributed team</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000-185,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Law School Founding CSM is the global CS and activation function for the law school program. You serve all geo managers — US East, US West, and International — as the operational backbone for product training, onboarding, account health, and activation across every school in the portfolio. This is not a US role that also covers international; it is a global IC role that all geo managers draw on.\n\nThink of it as a tag-team model: geo managers own the school relationships and program strategy; you own the deeper product delivery and account management. This is the first dedicated CS hire for law schools. You will build the playbook as you go. Reports to the Head of Legal Partnerships, Law Schools.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and run the scaled post-sign partnership model for long tail school partners across all geographies — playbooks, templated cadences, training materials, and activation milestones\n\n - Partner with Legal Engineers and Law School Managers to translate school feedback into program improvements and deeper embeds on key campuses.\n\n - Own portfolio-wide reporting: track usage trends, activation status, and account health globally; surface risks and opportunities to all geo managers and to Grace\n\n - Own product training and demo delivery across the full law school portfolio — onboarding sessions, faculty demos, librarian trainings, classroom embeds, and workspace setup.\n\n - Maintain the law school CRM across all geographies — account notes, POC data, meeting logs, and opportunity tracking\n\n - Lead end-of-term recap cycles, capturing Y1 learnings and aligning on Y2 activation goals with key internal stakeholders and Law School champions.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in customer success, account or program management, or client services — preferably in a high-growth SaaS, legal tech, or professional services environment\n\n - Build the machine mindset: you build systems, write playbooks, and hold yourself to metrics\n\n - Player-coach approach: You are a founding CSM for this team and will have a strong part in growing it.\n\n - Strong trainer and presenter — you can run a room of law professors or a 1:1 demo with a student org leader and make both count\n\n - Legal background or strong legal context is a plus, not a requirement — comfort explaining legal AI tools to a sophisticated legal audience matters more than a JD\n\n - Experience building scaled or tech-touch CS programs for large, distributed account portfolios\n\n - Clear, direct communicator who doesn't let follow-ups fall through the cracks\n\n - Comfortable working across time zones and geographies in close coordination with a distributed team\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$160,000-185,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-TM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 80/20 Split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b3002508-b647-4689-93b0-c3ec268b2b71","tierSummary":"$160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • OTE 80/20 Split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 80/20 Split","components":[{"id":"5cff6f11-c8f9-4341-9a2a-3093a5c7a21e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"371da031-906a-4582-adac-d72a37f5f525","summary":"$160K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000},{"id":"c4fd19e7-0c17-4540-921e-28a8030a8e7a","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"fe28fb9b-c7bf-42ec-8fca-ac775ee3a1c3","title":"Technical Account Manager, APAC","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sydney","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-29T22:18:38.307+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Australia","addressLocality":"Sydney"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fe28fb9b-c7bf-42ec-8fca-ac775ee3a1c3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fe28fb9b-c7bf-42ec-8fca-ac775ee3a1c3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technical Account Manager joins Harvey's Premium Technical Support team to serve as a dedicated, technically expert partner for Harvey's most strategic customers across the APAC region. Sitting within the broader post-sales organization, the team's mission is to deliver rapid, high-fidelity technical support that strengthens customer trust and accelerates product adoption in one of Harvey's fastest-growing markets. This role drives end-to-end resolution of complex, time-critical issues for enterprise clients — including law firms and in-house legal teams — while partnering closely with Customer Success, Engineering, and Product to surface insights that improve the platform. It is a rare opportunity to shape the Premium Support function in APAC from the ground up, combining deep technical problem-solving with relationship-driven customer engagement at a category-defining legal AI company.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a primary escalation point for Majors accounts across APAC, owning high-severity and technically complex support cases through resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain deep account context — including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities — and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead clear, proactive incident communications for APAC customers, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity across the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling tailored to APAC customer needs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family &amp; Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement &amp; Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wellness &amp; Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GW1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Technical Account Manager joins Harvey's Premium Technical Support team to serve as a dedicated, technically expert partner for Harvey's most strategic customers across the APAC region. Sitting within the broader post-sales organization, the team's mission is to deliver rapid, high-fidelity technical support that strengthens customer trust and accelerates product adoption in one of Harvey's fastest-growing markets. This role drives end-to-end resolution of complex, time-critical issues for enterprise clients — including law firms and in-house legal teams — while partnering closely with Customer Success, Engineering, and Product to surface insights that improve the platform. It is a rare opportunity to shape the Premium Support function in APAC from the ground up, combining deep technical problem-solving with relationship-driven customer engagement at a category-defining legal AI company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as a primary escalation point for Majors accounts across APAC, owning high-severity and technically complex support cases through resolution.\n\n - Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.\n\n - Maintain deep account context — including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities — and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.\n\n - Lead clear, proactive incident communications for APAC customers, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.\n\n - Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity across the region.\n\n - Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling tailored to APAC customer needs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.\n\n - Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.\n\n - Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.\n\n - Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home\n\n - Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.\n\n - Family & Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.\n\n - Retirement & Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.\n\n - Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.\n\n - Wellness & Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.\n\n - Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.\n\n - Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.\n\n - Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-GW1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"88095128-3c1c-48c1-b37b-68e1349d9834","title":"Head of Customer Success, Enterprise","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-29T18:17:15.147+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88095128-3c1c-48c1-b37b-68e1349d9834","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88095128-3c1c-48c1-b37b-68e1349d9834/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Head of Customer Success, Enterprise - Americas, you will own the strategy, execution, and outcomes of Harvey's enterprise customer success motion across the United States, Canada, and Latin America. You will lead a team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders, driving value realization for Harvey's largest and most strategic accounts — top law firms and enterprise legal departments — and ensuring they derive maximum, measurable ROI from our AI platform. This is a senior leadership role that reports directly to the VP of Customer Success and requires a builder's mindset: you will define the playbooks, scale the team, and set the standard for what world-class customer success looks like at Harvey across the Americas.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Leadership:</strong> Define and execute the enterprise CS strategy for the Americas, including account segmentation, team structure, success planning, and expansion motions that align to Harvey's revenue and retention goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Building &amp; Development:</strong> Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders. Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, and excellence. Set clear expectations, run effective operating cadences, and manage performance with rigor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Outcomes &amp; Retention:</strong> Own net revenue retention (NRR), adoption, and renewal targets for the Americas enterprise book of business. Partner with Sales leadership to drive expansion and ensure seamless post-sale handoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Build and refine scalable CS processes — onboarding frameworks, QBR cadences, health scoring models, escalation workflows, and renewal playbooks — that enable the team to manage a growing portfolio of enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Partnership:</strong> Serve as the voice of the Americas enterprise customer to Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing. Translate customer feedback into actionable insights that shape the product roadmap and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive Engagement:</strong> Personally engage with C-suite stakeholders at Harvey's most strategic accounts — General Counsels, Chief Knowledge Officers, Managing Partners — to build lasting executive relationships and drive strategic alignment.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in customer success, account management, or strategic consulting, with at least 5 years managing and scaling CS teams in an enterprise SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning and exceeding NRR, adoption, and expansion targets at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and leading teams of 10+ across multiple segments (enterprise, majors) and geographies (US, Canada, LATAM).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and the ability to engage confidently with C-suite legal and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in legal technology, professional services, or selling into law firms and corporate legal departments is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with AI/LLM technology and comfort evangelizing emerging technology to skeptical, risk-averse audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical rigor — you lead with data, build dashboards, and use metrics (adoption rates, health scores, utilization, ARR growth) to drive decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results-driven with the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing demands across a large, complex book of business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder's mentality — you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and are energized by creating structure where none exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how the legal industry operates and evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to shape and scale Harvey's customer success function across an entire region during a period of hyper-growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, high-intensity work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$276,000-$325,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Head of Customer Success, Enterprise - Americas, you will own the strategy, execution, and outcomes of Harvey's enterprise customer success motion across the United States, Canada, and Latin America. You will lead a team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders, driving value realization for Harvey's largest and most strategic accounts — top law firms and enterprise legal departments — and ensuring they derive maximum, measurable ROI from our AI platform. This is a senior leadership role that reports directly to the VP of Customer Success and requires a builder's mindset: you will define the playbooks, scale the team, and set the standard for what world-class customer success looks like at Harvey across the Americas.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Leadership: Define and execute the enterprise CS strategy for the Americas, including account segmentation, team structure, success planning, and expansion motions that align to Harvey's revenue and retention goals.\n\n - Team Building & Development: Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Enterprise CSMs and CS Leaders. Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, and excellence. Set clear expectations, run effective operating cadences, and manage performance with rigor.\n\n - Customer Outcomes & Retention: Own net revenue retention (NRR), adoption, and renewal targets for the Americas enterprise book of business. Partner with Sales leadership to drive expansion and ensure seamless post-sale handoffs.\n\n - Operational Excellence: Build and refine scalable CS processes — onboarding frameworks, QBR cadences, health scoring models, escalation workflows, and renewal playbooks — that enable the team to manage a growing portfolio of enterprise accounts.\n\n - Cross-Functional Partnership: Serve as the voice of the Americas enterprise customer to Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing. Translate customer feedback into actionable insights that shape the product roadmap and go-to-market strategy.\n\n - Executive Engagement: Personally engage with C-suite stakeholders at Harvey's most strategic accounts — General Counsels, Chief Knowledge Officers, Managing Partners — to build lasting executive relationships and drive strategic alignment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in customer success, account management, or strategic consulting, with at least 5 years managing and scaling CS teams in an enterprise SaaS environment.\n\n - Proven track record of owning and exceeding NRR, adoption, and expansion targets at scale.\n\n - Deep experience building and leading teams of 10+ across multiple segments (enterprise, majors) and geographies (US, Canada, LATAM).\n\n - Strong executive presence and the ability to engage confidently with C-suite legal and business stakeholders.\n\n - Experience in legal technology, professional services, or selling into law firms and corporate legal departments is strongly preferred.\n\n - Familiarity with AI/LLM technology and comfort evangelizing emerging technology to skeptical, risk-averse audiences.\n\n - Analytical rigor — you lead with data, build dashboards, and use metrics (adoption rates, health scores, utilization, ARR growth) to drive decisions.\n\n - Results-driven with the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing demands across a large, complex book of business.\n\n - A builder's mentality — you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and are energized by creating structure where none exists.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how the legal industry operates and evolves.\n\n - The opportunity to shape and scale Harvey's customer success function across an entire region during a period of hyper-growth.\n\n - A collaborative, high-intensity work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$276,000-$325,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$276K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$276K - $325K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0b4fbc01-5d03-4b11-8d1f-2e130cba321c","tierSummary":"$276K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7dc828a5-bd9d-4b48-899b-4d3e41f34716","summary":"$276K – $325K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":276000,"maxValue":325000},{"id":"9633b430-c227-466e-a682-2589e1380c9e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0f115041-6043-49c1-ab48-de30a8f709c8","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":276000,"maxValue":325000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"62570156-bb6a-42b5-aae4-ea544d9f1beb","title":"Sales Development Representative  (German Speaking)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:41:41.333+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/62570156-bb6a-42b5-aae4-ea544d9f1beb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/62570156-bb6a-42b5-aae4-ea544d9f1beb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h3>Please note that this role requires relocation to Dublin, Ireland.</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Role Overview</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in written and spoken English and German</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nPLEASE NOTE THAT THIS ROLE REQUIRES RELOCATION TO DUBLIN, IRELAND.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.\n\nThis role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.\n\n - Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.\n\n - Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.\n\n - Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.\n\n - Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.\n\n - Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.\n\n - Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.\n\n - Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.\n\n - Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.\n\n\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.\n\n - Fluent in written and spoken English and German\n\n - Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.\n\n - Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.\n\n - Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.\n\n - Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.\n\n - Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KS2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cd652dbd-9f67-4e1e-a64e-e524415ec38f","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Search","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-30T20:31:56.680+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cd652dbd-9f67-4e1e-a64e-e524415ec38f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cd652dbd-9f67-4e1e-a64e-e524415ec38f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Search Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Search Growth\n\n - Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.\n\n - Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.\n\n - Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.\n\n - Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.\n\n - Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.\n\n - Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.\n\n - Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.\n\n - Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.\n\n - Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.\n\n - Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.\n\n - Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.\n\n - Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.\n\n - Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LT1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"100bed60-7cea-47ff-909f-335318b87440","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3334504e-836c-4dfe-aee0-b86dc0db1e72","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"666d40b5-1d4f-4188-90bb-ba3dc648433c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fb9442c3-dd6c-49be-b05d-33c96635e400","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"39688e87-ddf1-42bf-ad98-d968faf360a1","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Search","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-30T20:31:59.932+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/39688e87-ddf1-42bf-ad98-d968faf360a1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/39688e87-ddf1-42bf-ad98-d968faf360a1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Search Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Search Growth\n\n - Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.\n\n - Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.\n\n - Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.\n\n - Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.\n\n - Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.\n\n - Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.\n\n - Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.\n\n - Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.\n\n - Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.\n\n - Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.\n\n - Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.\n\n - Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.\n\n - Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LT1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"83ee46d8-ca34-4547-94da-da44fc19b302","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b5008916-6dc7-494c-ac22-67a35c315367","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"42a0cac3-eb11-491b-b181-c010d65d35ad","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1d7bfd4c-cf1a-4358-8a60-c9e1a1c0ef83","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ba51dd1e-8b7f-4e14-8696-5b4d4f77dd19","title":"Technology Enablement Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T22:02:12.224+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ba51dd1e-8b7f-4e14-8696-5b4d4f77dd19","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ba51dd1e-8b7f-4e14-8696-5b4d4f77dd19/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows\n\n - Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content\n\n - Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI\n\n - Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts\n\n - Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management\n\n - Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)\n\n - Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences\n\n - Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders\n\n - Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c892d02a-ca32-4523-bde0-26ed02b67952","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c2ef886a-be63-436f-bf94-55102a041531","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800}]}},{"id":"d267352c-b865-42b9-af28-422f3f2eec8b","title":"Technical Account Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-01T14:27:06.813+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d267352c-b865-42b9-af28-422f3f2eec8b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d267352c-b865-42b9-af28-422f3f2eec8b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Harvey continues to scale its premium customer offerings, we are hiring a <strong>Technical Account Manager</strong> to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent inbound support and escalation resource for Harvey’s largest and most strategic customers in the Majors segment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Premium Support Specialist strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and resolve inbound support tickets from Majors accounts, serving as a primary escalation point for high-severity and technically complex issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">.Familiarity with ticketing queue systems and resolving inbound customer inquiries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to Have</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$119,000 -$161,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs Harvey continues to scale its premium customer offerings, we are hiring a Technical Account Manager to join our Customer Success organization. This role serves as a high-touch, technically fluent inbound support and escalation resource for Harvey’s largest and most strategic customers in the Majors segment.\n\nThe Premium Support Specialist strengthens Harvey’s post-sale presence by partnering closely with Customer Success Managers and internal teams to deliver exceptional technical support, proactive incident management, and clear, credible customer communications. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in high-stakes environments, enjoys deep problem-solving, and takes pride in delivering a world-class customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and resolve inbound support tickets from Majors accounts, serving as a primary escalation point for high-severity and technically complex issues.\n\n - Triage, investigate, and resolve urgent customer issues with speed and sound judgment, coordinating across Support, Customer Success, Engineering, Product, and Security teams.\n\n - Maintain deep account context, including customer workflows, configurations, integrations, and sensitivities, and apply that context to troubleshooting and communications.\n\n - Provide real-time, hands-on technical support for senior customer stakeholders, including Knowledge Management, Innovation, and IT leaders.\n\n - Lead clear and proactive incident communications, translating technical updates into customer-specific impact, expectations, and next steps.\n\n - Participate in incident response workflows, including severity classification, escalation handling, and post-incident retrospectives.\n\n - Document root causes, resolutions, and preventative actions to improve product reliability, internal knowledge coverage, and operational maturity.\n\n - Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of escalation playbooks, runbooks, and support tooling.\n\n - Partner closely with Customer Success Managers to enhance Harvey’s post-sale technical engagement and overall customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting enterprise or highly regulated software products in technical support, escalation management, or technical account-facing roles.\n\n - Proven experience engaging and managing high-level stakeholders both internally and externally.\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to manage and resolve complex, multi-layered support cases.\n\n - .Familiarity with ticketing queue systems and resolving inbound customer inquiries\n\n - Strong technical foundation, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively with Engineering and Product teams.\n\n - Ability to bridge technical and non-technical communication by translating complex back-end and front-end concepts into clear, accessible language for customers.\n\n - Deep customer obsession and ownership mindset - end-to-end accountability for customer outcomes and going beyond issue resolution to actively champion the customer's long-term success with the product.\n\n - Exceptional judgment under pressure, with comfort operating in high-severity, time-sensitive, and confidential situations.\n\n - Clear, polished written and verbal communication skills, with experience engaging senior customer stakeholders.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to manage multiple urgent issues simultaneously while maintaining accuracy, composure, and customer trust.\n\n - Highly collaborative mindset and strong partnership orientation with Customer Success and cross-functional teams.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and contributing to process-building in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n - Nice to Have\n   \n   - Experience supporting AI-powered, data-intensive, or security- and compliance-sensitive products.\n   \n   - Familiarity with incident management frameworks, on-call models, or escalation playbooks.\n   \n   - Prior experience working with law firms or professional services organizations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$119,000 -$161,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2c1be26f-51d4-4688-8671-f6c2f2a53751","title":"Customer Success Leader, Enterprise","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T20:35:17.169+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2c1be26f-51d4-4688-8671-f6c2f2a53751","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2c1be26f-51d4-4688-8671-f6c2f2a53751/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is hiring an Enterprise Customer Success Leader to build, lead, and scale a high-performing team of Customer Success Managers focused on our enterprise clients. This role will drive customer adoption, satisfaction, and long-term partnership with some of the world’s most sophisticated law firms and fortune 100 companies. You will be responsible for developing strategic customer success initiatives, implementing scalable processes, and ensuring our enterprise clients achieve measurable value with Harvey. The team is growing rapidly, and this leader will play a critical role in shaping our enterprise success strategy and culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and develop a team of Enterprise Customer Success Managers to deliver exceptional client outcomes and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive customer adoption, engagement, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute scalable success strategies, processes, and metrics tailored to the enterprise segment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as an executive sponsor for key enterprise accounts, providing strategic guidance and building trusted relationships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify risks and opportunities across the customer base to drive proactive engagement and ensure customer satisfaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent the voice of the customer internally, influencing product roadmaps and operational improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or related client-facing roles, with at least 3+ years leading enterprise CS teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience working with complex, global enterprise clients in the AI, SaaS, legal, or technology sector.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong strategic thinking and operational execution skills with an ability to build frameworks and scale programs from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication and executive presence, with the ability to build trusted relationships at the C-suite level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A coaching mindset and passion for developing high-performing teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in law or experience in the legal technology sector</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in consulting or professional services firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with or supporting large financial institutions or asset managers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$191,800 - $250,000 USD OTE 80/20</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is hiring an Enterprise Customer Success Leader to build, lead, and scale a high-performing team of Customer Success Managers focused on our enterprise clients. This role will drive customer adoption, satisfaction, and long-term partnership with some of the world’s most sophisticated law firms and fortune 100 companies. You will be responsible for developing strategic customer success initiatives, implementing scalable processes, and ensuring our enterprise clients achieve measurable value with Harvey. The team is growing rapidly, and this leader will play a critical role in shaping our enterprise success strategy and culture.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead, mentor, and develop a team of Enterprise Customer Success Managers to deliver exceptional client outcomes and retention.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive customer adoption, engagement, and expansion.\n\n - Develop and execute scalable success strategies, processes, and metrics tailored to the enterprise segment.\n\n - Serve as an executive sponsor for key enterprise accounts, providing strategic guidance and building trusted relationships.\n\n - Identify risks and opportunities across the customer base to drive proactive engagement and ensure customer satisfaction.\n\n - Represent the voice of the customer internally, influencing product roadmaps and operational improvements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or related client-facing roles, with at least 3+ years leading enterprise CS teams.\n\n - Proven experience working with complex, global enterprise clients in the AI, SaaS, legal, or technology sector.\n\n - Strong strategic thinking and operational execution skills with an ability to build frameworks and scale programs from the ground up.\n\n - Exceptional communication and executive presence, with the ability to build trusted relationships at the C-suite level.\n\n - A coaching mindset and passion for developing high-performing teams.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Background in law or experience in the legal technology sector\n\n - Previous experience in consulting or professional services firms\n\n - Experience working with or supporting large financial institutions or asset managers\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$191,800 - $250,000 USD OTE 80/20\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-GK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$191.8K – $250K • Offers Equity • OTE 80/20","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$191.8K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"04fcb463-efcd-46b3-8636-ac248e0f04d1","tierSummary":"$191.8K – $250K • Offers Equity • OTE 80/20","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 80/20","components":[{"id":"0a061c30-727e-4345-a323-70fee959d508","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a0a5c1c1-1dd3-4931-953f-1ae858a112ca","summary":"$191.8K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":191800,"maxValue":250000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":191800,"maxValue":250000}]}},{"id":"6d2063e8-8152-41f4-90a7-72b864afc52d","title":"Law School Manager, International","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T10:48:59.339+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6d2063e8-8152-41f4-90a7-72b864afc52d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6d2063e8-8152-41f4-90a7-72b864afc52d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's law school program has reached 50+ US schools in year one. Now we are taking it global, and we need the right person to lead that charge expanding in the UK, EMEA, and APAC markets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Law School Manager, UK &amp; International, you will own the full lifecycle of Harvey's academic partnerships across your markets — signing new schools, building faculty and dean relationships, running trainings, launching ambassador programs, and driving the curriculum and on-campus embeds that make Harvey helpful to each institution with whom we work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will start with deep UK penetration and expand into France, Germany, Singapore, and the Nordics by September 2026. London-based time zone allows meaningful flex coverage for Australian partner schools. You report directly to the Head of Legal Partnerships, Law Schools (New York).</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>School Partnerships: </strong>Lead outreach, relationship development, and onboarding for UK and EMEA law schools — from flagship institutions to smaller schools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Account Management: </strong>Serve as the primary point of contact for every school in your portfolio — owning relationships with faculty, library staff, student organizations, and administrators across each partner institution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement: </strong>Run all product training, demos, workspace setup, and activation events for your portfolio — including semester-start all-hands pushes, large-group faculty workshops, and 1:1 curriculum advisory sessions. Draw on the global Content Specialist and CS Lead for materials and operational support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ambassador Programs: </strong>Launch and own the UK/EMEA student ambassador and faculty champion networks, adapting the US model for UK and European legal education norms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Curriculum Advisory: </strong>Advise faculty and curriculum committees on how to integrate Harvey into courses, clinics, and legal writing programs — doing the hands-on work that makes academic embeds real.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Market Expansion: </strong>Build the playbook for each new market; execute the September 2026 international launch across Paris, Berlin, Singapore, and the Nordics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-functional: </strong>Partner with Harvey's UK commercial team, legal engineering, and marketing on in-market events, firm-to-school pipeline, and co-activation opportunities.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Law School Manager, UK &amp; International role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">UK law degree preferred (LLB, LPC, or equivalent) — deep understanding of how UK law schools are structured and how faculty, students, and administrators operate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience in legal practice, legal tech, legal innovation, or academic programs — experience in a client-facing or externally-facing role is a strong differentiator</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage a portfolio of relationships in a high-growth or startup environment — you keep up with a high volume without losing account depth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable running product trainings and demos for audiences ranging from first-year students to senior faculty and deans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entrepreneurial and self-directed — you build from scratch, operate without a playbook, and hold yourself accountable across multiple markets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational instincts — you can manage many schools across multiple countries and time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in London; willing and able to travel across the UK, Europe, and APAC</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's law school program has reached 50+ US schools in year one. Now we are taking it global, and we need the right person to lead that charge expanding in the UK, EMEA, and APAC markets.\n\nAs Law School Manager, UK & International, you will own the full lifecycle of Harvey's academic partnerships across your markets — signing new schools, building faculty and dean relationships, running trainings, launching ambassador programs, and driving the curriculum and on-campus embeds that make Harvey helpful to each institution with whom we work.\n\nYou will start with deep UK penetration and expand into France, Germany, Singapore, and the Nordics by September 2026. London-based time zone allows meaningful flex coverage for Australian partner schools. You report directly to the Head of Legal Partnerships, Law Schools (New York).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - School Partnerships: Lead outreach, relationship development, and onboarding for UK and EMEA law schools — from flagship institutions to smaller schools.\n\n - Account Management: Serve as the primary point of contact for every school in your portfolio — owning relationships with faculty, library staff, student organizations, and administrators across each partner institution.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Run all product training, demos, workspace setup, and activation events for your portfolio — including semester-start all-hands pushes, large-group faculty workshops, and 1:1 curriculum advisory sessions. Draw on the global Content Specialist and CS Lead for materials and operational support.\n\n - Ambassador Programs: Launch and own the UK/EMEA student ambassador and faculty champion networks, adapting the US model for UK and European legal education norms.\n\n - Curriculum Advisory: Advise faculty and curriculum committees on how to integrate Harvey into courses, clinics, and legal writing programs — doing the hands-on work that makes academic embeds real.\n\n - Market Expansion: Build the playbook for each new market; execute the September 2026 international launch across Paris, Berlin, Singapore, and the Nordics.\n\n - Cross-functional: Partner with Harvey's UK commercial team, legal engineering, and marketing on in-market events, firm-to-school pipeline, and co-activation opportunities.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Law School Manager, UK & International role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following:\n\n - UK law degree preferred (LLB, LPC, or equivalent) — deep understanding of how UK law schools are structured and how faculty, students, and administrators operate\n\n - Strong experience in legal practice, legal tech, legal innovation, or academic programs — experience in a client-facing or externally-facing role is a strong differentiator\n\n - Proven ability to manage a portfolio of relationships in a high-growth or startup environment — you keep up with a high volume without losing account depth\n\n - Comfortable running product trainings and demos for audiences ranging from first-year students to senior faculty and deans\n\n - Entrepreneurial and self-directed — you build from scratch, operate without a playbook, and hold yourself accountable across multiple markets\n\n - Strong organizational instincts — you can manage many schools across multiple countries and time zones.\n\n - Based in London; willing and able to travel across the UK, Europe, and APAC\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"15d5cba6-1979-414a-9a6e-bc8a852f3d79","title":"Sales Manager - SMB","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T13:47:32.663+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/15d5cba6-1979-414a-9a6e-bc8a852f3d79","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/15d5cba6-1979-414a-9a6e-bc8a852f3d79/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The SMB Sales Manager joins Harvey's Commercial Sales organization to lead a team of Account Executives selling Harvey's AI platform to small and mid-sized law firms and legal teams out of the San Francisco office. Reporting to the Vice President of Commercial Sales, this role owns territory planning, pipeline development, and revenue execution across the region. The manager drives a disciplined sales process while coaching AEs through the full cycle — from discovery and qualification through close — and holds the team accountable to rigorous forecasting and performance standards. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape the sales culture and operating rhythm for a fast-growing segment at one of the most innovative companies in legal technology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, coach, and performance-manage a team of SMB Account Executives focused on selling Harvey's platform to law firms and corporate legal departments in the San Francisco region</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own territory planning, pipeline development, and accurate forecasting to deliver against quarterly and annual revenue targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive a disciplined sales process using MEDDPIC or similar methodology, ensuring AEs execute high-quality discovery, qualification, objection handling, and close motions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a local operating cadence — team standups, deal reviews, pipeline hygiene — that mirrors Harvey's high-performance sales culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a player-coach by actively engaging in strategic deals and modeling best practices in discovery, demo, and negotiation</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of tech sales experience — ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performing sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to sophisticated buyers, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of coaching AEs through complex sales cycles, including deal strategy, objection handling, and negotiation, with a growth-oriented and coachable mindset</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OTE 50/50 Split $280,000 - $320,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe SMB Sales Manager joins Harvey's Commercial Sales organization to lead a team of Account Executives selling Harvey's AI platform to small and mid-sized law firms and legal teams out of the San Francisco office. Reporting to the Vice President of Commercial Sales, this role owns territory planning, pipeline development, and revenue execution across the region. The manager drives a disciplined sales process while coaching AEs through the full cycle — from discovery and qualification through close — and holds the team accountable to rigorous forecasting and performance standards. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape the sales culture and operating rhythm for a fast-growing segment at one of the most innovative companies in legal technology.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, coach, and performance-manage a team of SMB Account Executives focused on selling Harvey's platform to law firms and corporate legal departments in the San Francisco region\n\n - Own territory planning, pipeline development, and accurate forecasting to deliver against quarterly and annual revenue targets\n\n - Drive a disciplined sales process using MEDDPIC or similar methodology, ensuring AEs execute high-quality discovery, qualification, objection handling, and close motions\n\n - Establish a local operating cadence — team standups, deal reviews, pipeline hygiene — that mirrors Harvey's high-performance sales culture\n\n - Serve as a player-coach by actively engaging in strategic deals and modeling best practices in discovery, demo, and negotiation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of tech sales experience — ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performing sales team.\n\n - Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to sophisticated buyers, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Track record of coaching AEs through complex sales cycles, including deal strategy, objection handling, and negotiation, with a growth-oriented and coachable mindset\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n\n\nOTE 50/50 Split $280,000 - $320,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$280K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$280K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bbb5cdde-b3fb-4f51-9eb5-ce940e3eebff","tierSummary":"OTE 50/50 Split $280K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1a5feca5-6983-4417-b89d-808c8aec3a7f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"31c5bb32-c02a-4325-bdc6-59d6faf9aec1","summary":"OTE 50/50 Split $280K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":280000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"d30ef73b-8a4a-4b88-9134-815f1458f324","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":280000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a4668463-24f1-4b58-85d0-ac6e9637ae97","title":"Legal Engineer, Madrid","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Madrid","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T14:21:03.151+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a4668463-24f1-4b58-85d0-ac6e9637ae97","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a4668463-24f1-4b58-85d0-ac6e9637ae97/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Similar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges, and then explain and demonstrate the value of Harvey’s AI solutions to address them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidate will be qualified to practice law in Spain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm in Spain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are skilled lawyers from top-tier law firms who apply their legal experience to ensure that current and prospective customers understand how Harvey’s solutions enhance specific day-to-day workflows, working alongside Harvey’s Account Executives to support all aspects of our sales strategy. Legal Engineers build consultative relationships with law firm partners and associates and in-house attorneys at private equity firms and Fortune 500 companies, becoming trusted advisors on how Harvey’s AI solutions can make them more effective.\n\nSimilar to the way Solutions Architects secure the “technical win” in the sales process, Legal Engineers secure the “legal win” by performing in-depth customer discovery and education on Harvey’s solutions through targeted meetings and demos that resonate with the customer’s day-to-day workflows specific to their legal practice area.\n\nLegal Engineers utilize their experience practicing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Engage with lawyers at existing and prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges, and then explain and demonstrate the value of Harvey’s AI solutions to address them.\n\n - Establish yourself as a credible expert in solving customers’ specific legal problems (e.g. researching public and private databases for certain types of information, drafting and analyzing contractual provisions and whole documents, analyzing briefs and filings, corporate governance, conducting due diligence).\n\n - Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.\n\n - Partner with the marketing team to develop content that will resonate with lawyers, tailored to the unique needs of their practice areas and client types. \n\n - Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.\n\n - Tailor the introduction of new solutions to specific customer needs. \n\n - Further the market perception of Harvey as uniquely credible, substantive, and helpful in applying its AI solutions to make lawyers better at their jobs. \n\n - Conduct research and analysis on customers and competitors.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Ideal candidate will be qualified to practice law in Spain.\n\n - At least 3 years of experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm in Spain.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals.\n\n - Curiosity about AI’s potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-RC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"85de4e2f-9ece-40a6-bea4-3ee94bba6c97","title":"Senior/Staff Product Manager, Vault","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T23:22:41.021+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/85de4e2f-9ece-40a6-bea4-3ee94bba6c97","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/85de4e2f-9ece-40a6-bea4-3ee94bba6c97/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Product Manager for Vault at Harvey, you will own and drive the product vision, strategy, and execution for our document and knowledge management platform-a critical foundation that powers how legal professionals interact with Harvey's AI capabilities. Vault enables law firms and enterprise clients to securely store, organize, search, and leverage their documents and institutional knowledge within Harvey's AI-powered ecosystem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will lead cross-functional teams to build and scale Vault's capabilities, including file management, AI-enabled search and Q&amp;A, document extraction, secure sharing across workspaces, and seamless integrations with enterprise document management systems like iManage, SharePoint, and Dropbox. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role where you'll directly shape how the world's leading law firms and enterprises organize and unlock value from their most sensitive documents.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and own the Vault product vision and roadmap:</strong> Develop a compelling product strategy that aligns with Harvey's mission to transform legal and professional services through AI, balancing near-term customer needs with long-term platform investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive end-to-end product development:</strong> Lead cross-functional teams including engineering, design, AI/ML, and go-to-market to ship high-quality features from ideation through launch and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner deeply with engineering:</strong> Work closely with engineering leadership to make technical and architectural decisions, dive deep into complex problems, and ensure we're building scalable, secure, and performant systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Understand and champion customer needs:</strong> Collaborate with Customer Success, Sales, and Legal Product Specialists to deeply understand how law firms and enterprise clients use Vault, identify adoption barriers, and translate insights into product improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own enterprise integrations strategy:</strong> Drive the vision for how Vault integrates with document management systems (iManage, SharePoint, Dropbox, Box) and other enterprise tools, ensuring seamless workflows for customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and track success metrics:</strong> Establish KPIs for Vault adoption, engagement, and value realization; use data to inform product decisions and demonstrate customer impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate cross-functionally:</strong> Partner with Product Marketing, Partnerships, and Admin/Governance teams to ensure successful product launches, effective positioning, and alignment with broader platform capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute to Harvey's product culture:</strong> Mentor other product managers, share learnings, and help establish best practices as the product organization scales.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Must-Have Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML-powered products, semantic search, retrieval systems, or document processing pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in legal technology, professional services, or deep understanding of law firm workflows and enterprise legal operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with enterprise integrations (APIs, authentication frameworks like SSO/SCIM/OAuth, third-party DMS platforms).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience at a company during a high-growth stage (Series B through IPO).</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$177,700 - $266,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Product Manager for Vault at Harvey, you will own and drive the product vision, strategy, and execution for our document and knowledge management platform-a critical foundation that powers how legal professionals interact with Harvey's AI capabilities. Vault enables law firms and enterprise clients to securely store, organize, search, and leverage their documents and institutional knowledge within Harvey's AI-powered ecosystem.\n\nYou will lead cross-functional teams to build and scale Vault's capabilities, including file management, AI-enabled search and Q&A, document extraction, secure sharing across workspaces, and seamless integrations with enterprise document management systems like iManage, SharePoint, and Dropbox. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role where you'll directly shape how the world's leading law firms and enterprises organize and unlock value from their most sensitive documents.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define and own the Vault product vision and roadmap: Develop a compelling product strategy that aligns with Harvey's mission to transform legal and professional services through AI, balancing near-term customer needs with long-term platform investments.\n\n - Drive end-to-end product development: Lead cross-functional teams including engineering, design, AI/ML, and go-to-market to ship high-quality features from ideation through launch and iteration.\n\n - Partner deeply with engineering: Work closely with engineering leadership to make technical and architectural decisions, dive deep into complex problems, and ensure we're building scalable, secure, and performant systems.\n\n - Understand and champion customer needs: Collaborate with Customer Success, Sales, and Legal Product Specialists to deeply understand how law firms and enterprise clients use Vault, identify adoption barriers, and translate insights into product improvements.\n\n - Own enterprise integrations strategy: Drive the vision for how Vault integrates with document management systems (iManage, SharePoint, Dropbox, Box) and other enterprise tools, ensuring seamless workflows for customers.\n\n - Define and track success metrics: Establish KPIs for Vault adoption, engagement, and value realization; use data to inform product decisions and demonstrate customer impact.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally: Partner with Product Marketing, Partnerships, and Admin/Governance teams to ensure successful product launches, effective positioning, and alignment with broader platform capabilities.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey's product culture: Mentor other product managers, share learnings, and help establish best practices as the product organization scales.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nMust-Have Qualifications:\n\n - 8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.\n\n - Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.\n\n - Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.\n\n - Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n - Experience with AI/ML-powered products, semantic search, retrieval systems, or document processing pipelines.\n\n - Background in legal technology, professional services, or deep understanding of law firm workflows and enterprise legal operations.\n\n - Experience with enterprise integrations (APIs, authentication frameworks like SSO/SCIM/OAuth, third-party DMS platforms).\n\n - Prior experience at a company during a high-growth stage (Series B through IPO).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$177,700 - $266,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$177.7K - $266.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4c4840fd-3605-4ff3-ab8c-a854164c8d93","tierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f10e2950-2962-43dd-bebd-4977b9a85d46","summary":"$177.7K – $266.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"id":"b0ea092c-d4db-4499-bee2-8caac20b6f3b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b265686d-847a-40e6-8710-f85cca431268","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"08bf31a9-9e6d-4fa0-b552-a55e68915a71","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager, Core","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T14:11:59.501+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08bf31a9-9e6d-4fa0-b552-a55e68915a71","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08bf31a9-9e6d-4fa0-b552-a55e68915a71/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a <strong>Senior Product Marketing Manager</strong> to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$137,600-206,400 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Senior Product Marketing Manager to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.\n\n - Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.\n\n - Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.\n\n - Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.\n\n - Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.\n\n - Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.\n\n - Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.\n\n - Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.\n\n - Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$137,600-206,400 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$137.6K - $206.4K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2498fc39-1ac6-408d-a0d6-0c4e8576faf1","tierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"20a831ea-5592-4abd-8e33-49dedbb01706","summary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400},{"id":"31739a90-ba8c-4043-8b57-17d52e73a418","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"48513477-81ca-40c5-b099-0f587fd4e7fc","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager, Core","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T14:11:57.211+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/48513477-81ca-40c5-b099-0f587fd4e7fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/48513477-81ca-40c5-b099-0f587fd4e7fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a <strong>Senior Product Marketing Manager</strong> to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$137,600-206,400 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Senior Product Marketing Manager to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.\n\n - Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.\n\n - Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.\n\n - Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.\n\n - Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.\n\n - Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.\n\n - Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.\n\n - Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.\n\n - Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$137,600-206,400 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$137.6K - $206.4K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1d539e39-a5c3-4480-b52f-7dbc54974f6f","tierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4176013e-459c-44d4-ae9b-0e89c89598b9","summary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}},{"id":"0c5c9a62-3872-4dd2-9dc6-091259fab9b0","title":"Director, IT","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T19:16:22.717+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0c5c9a62-3872-4dd2-9dc6-091259fab9b0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/0c5c9a62-3872-4dd2-9dc6-091259fab9b0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast and our internal technology backbone has to scale with it. We're hiring a Director of IT to own IT Operations and Systems &amp; Network Engineering end to end, including the help desk and endpoint experience every employee depends on, the identity and collaboration stack that keeps us secure, the network and infrastructure that powers our offices worldwide, and the A/V, live production, and event technology that powers Harvey's all-hands and internal broadcasts. You'll lead a team of managers and senior engineers, set the technical and operational strategy, and partner closely with Security, Engineering, People Ops, and Workplace to keep Harvey running as we grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a hands-on technical leader who has scaled IT operations and infrastructure inside a high-growth company, builds and develops strong engineering teams, and operates with a security-first mindset in an enterprise-grade environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the strategy and day-to-day execution for IT Operations and Systems &amp; Network Engineering, including end-user support, endpoint management, identity, collaboration, and network infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's A/V, conference room, and live production technology, leading the Manager, Media Productions and partnering with Comms and Workplace on all-hands, executive broadcasts, and live events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and grow a team of managers and senior engineers, and stand up new IT infrastructure engineering roles as the function scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold service-level standards for global IT - response times, uptime, and a high-quality employee experience across every office and region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the technical roadmap for systems and network architecture: identity lifecycle, SCIM/SAML/SSO, zero-trust network design, and high-availability infrastructure across new and existing offices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security to ensure every system and process meets Harvey's bar - SOC 2, encryption at rest and in transit, and SSO/SCIM for anything touching employee data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own IT infrastructure delivery for office buildouts and global expansion, working with Workplace and vendors from design through go-live.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the IT operations and infrastructure budget, vendor relationships, and procurement in partnership with Finance and Procurement, leveraging Harvey's scale in negotiations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish the operational rigor the function needs to scale — change control, incident and root-cause processes, asset management, and an ITSM practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a roadmap and reporting cadence that gives leadership clear visibility into IT health, risk, and investment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 10 years of experience in IT operations and/or systems and network engineering, with at least 4 years leading teams (including managing managers or senior ICs).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on grounding in modern IT infrastructure: identity and access management (Okta or equivalent), endpoint management (JAMF/MDM), cloud collaboration (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365), and enterprise networking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of scaling IT operations and infrastructure in a high-growth company, including multi-office or global environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated security-first judgment — you've partnered with Security/Compliance teams and understand SOC 2, SSO/SCIM, and data protection requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning budgets, vendor relationships, and procurement decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience overseeing A/V, conference room, or live event production technology, or managing a media/production function.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting a security-conscious or regulated environment (legal, fintech, healthcare, or similar).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$224,000 - $336,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast and our internal technology backbone has to scale with it. We're hiring a Director of IT to own IT Operations and Systems & Network Engineering end to end, including the help desk and endpoint experience every employee depends on, the identity and collaboration stack that keeps us secure, the network and infrastructure that powers our offices worldwide, and the A/V, live production, and event technology that powers Harvey's all-hands and internal broadcasts. You'll lead a team of managers and senior engineers, set the technical and operational strategy, and partner closely with Security, Engineering, People Ops, and Workplace to keep Harvey running as we grow.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a hands-on technical leader who has scaled IT operations and infrastructure inside a high-growth company, builds and develops strong engineering teams, and operates with a security-first mindset in an enterprise-grade environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the strategy and day-to-day execution for IT Operations and Systems & Network Engineering, including end-user support, endpoint management, identity, collaboration, and network infrastructure.\n\n - Own Harvey's A/V, conference room, and live production technology, leading the Manager, Media Productions and partnering with Comms and Workplace on all-hands, executive broadcasts, and live events.\n\n - Lead, coach, and grow a team of managers and senior engineers, and stand up new IT infrastructure engineering roles as the function scales.\n\n - Set and hold service-level standards for global IT - response times, uptime, and a high-quality employee experience across every office and region.\n\n - Drive the technical roadmap for systems and network architecture: identity lifecycle, SCIM/SAML/SSO, zero-trust network design, and high-availability infrastructure across new and existing offices.\n\n - Partner with Security to ensure every system and process meets Harvey's bar - SOC 2, encryption at rest and in transit, and SSO/SCIM for anything touching employee data.\n\n - Own IT infrastructure delivery for office buildouts and global expansion, working with Workplace and vendors from design through go-live.\n\n - Manage the IT operations and infrastructure budget, vendor relationships, and procurement in partnership with Finance and Procurement, leveraging Harvey's scale in negotiations.\n\n - Establish the operational rigor the function needs to scale — change control, incident and root-cause processes, asset management, and an ITSM practice.\n\n - Build a roadmap and reporting cadence that gives leadership clear visibility into IT health, risk, and investment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 10 years of experience in IT operations and/or systems and network engineering, with at least 4 years leading teams (including managing managers or senior ICs).\n\n - Deep hands-on grounding in modern IT infrastructure: identity and access management (Okta or equivalent), endpoint management (JAMF/MDM), cloud collaboration (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365), and enterprise networking.\n\n - A track record of scaling IT operations and infrastructure in a high-growth company, including multi-office or global environments.\n\n - Demonstrated security-first judgment — you've partnered with Security/Compliance teams and understand SOC 2, SSO/SCIM, and data protection requirements.\n\n - Experience owning budgets, vendor relationships, and procurement decisions.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\nBonus Points:\n\n - Experience overseeing A/V, conference room, or live event production technology, or managing a media/production function.\n\n - Background supporting a security-conscious or regulated environment (legal, fintech, healthcare, or similar).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$224,000 - $336,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$224K - $336K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"487fd4e3-a7e3-4403-9b1e-c30920aac3fe","tierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fba66115-2f76-4352-80d6-93851d689b6b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1cb36485-01a2-4a76-8c2c-475aaced2eb8","summary":"$224K – $336K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"id":"fafd458a-bbfe-4835-895c-a86f23f4bd5c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f4c3eb88-0ab4-495e-b506-be615a269283","title":"Director, IT","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T19:16:18.286+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4c3eb88-0ab4-495e-b506-be615a269283","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4c3eb88-0ab4-495e-b506-be615a269283/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast and our internal technology backbone has to scale with it. We're hiring a Director of IT to own IT Operations and Systems &amp; Network Engineering end to end, including the help desk and endpoint experience every employee depends on, the identity and collaboration stack that keeps us secure, the network and infrastructure that powers our offices worldwide, and the A/V, live production, and event technology that powers Harvey's all-hands and internal broadcasts. You'll lead a team of managers and senior engineers, set the technical and operational strategy, and partner closely with Security, Engineering, People Ops, and Workplace to keep Harvey running as we grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a hands-on technical leader who has scaled IT operations and infrastructure inside a high-growth company, builds and develops strong engineering teams, and operates with a security-first mindset in an enterprise-grade environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the strategy and day-to-day execution for IT Operations and Systems &amp; Network Engineering, including end-user support, endpoint management, identity, collaboration, and network infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's A/V, conference room, and live production technology, leading the Manager, Media Productions and partnering with Comms and Workplace on all-hands, executive broadcasts, and live events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and grow a team of managers and senior engineers, and stand up new IT infrastructure engineering roles as the function scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold service-level standards for global IT - response times, uptime, and a high-quality employee experience across every office and region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the technical roadmap for systems and network architecture: identity lifecycle, SCIM/SAML/SSO, zero-trust network design, and high-availability infrastructure across new and existing offices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security to ensure every system and process meets Harvey's bar - SOC 2, encryption at rest and in transit, and SSO/SCIM for anything touching employee data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own IT infrastructure delivery for office buildouts and global expansion, working with Workplace and vendors from design through go-live.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the IT operations and infrastructure budget, vendor relationships, and procurement in partnership with Finance and Procurement, leveraging Harvey's scale in negotiations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish the operational rigor the function needs to scale — change control, incident and root-cause processes, asset management, and an ITSM practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a roadmap and reporting cadence that gives leadership clear visibility into IT health, risk, and investment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 10 years of experience in IT operations and/or systems and network engineering, with at least 4 years leading teams (including managing managers or senior ICs).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on grounding in modern IT infrastructure: identity and access management (Okta or equivalent), endpoint management (JAMF/MDM), cloud collaboration (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365), and enterprise networking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of scaling IT operations and infrastructure in a high-growth company, including multi-office or global environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated security-first judgment — you've partnered with Security/Compliance teams and understand SOC 2, SSO/SCIM, and data protection requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning budgets, vendor relationships, and procurement decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience overseeing A/V, conference room, or live event production technology, or managing a media/production function.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting a security-conscious or regulated environment (legal, fintech, healthcare, or similar).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$224,000 - $336,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast and our internal technology backbone has to scale with it. We're hiring a Director of IT to own IT Operations and Systems & Network Engineering end to end, including the help desk and endpoint experience every employee depends on, the identity and collaboration stack that keeps us secure, the network and infrastructure that powers our offices worldwide, and the A/V, live production, and event technology that powers Harvey's all-hands and internal broadcasts. You'll lead a team of managers and senior engineers, set the technical and operational strategy, and partner closely with Security, Engineering, People Ops, and Workplace to keep Harvey running as we grow.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a hands-on technical leader who has scaled IT operations and infrastructure inside a high-growth company, builds and develops strong engineering teams, and operates with a security-first mindset in an enterprise-grade environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the strategy and day-to-day execution for IT Operations and Systems & Network Engineering, including end-user support, endpoint management, identity, collaboration, and network infrastructure.\n\n - Own Harvey's A/V, conference room, and live production technology, leading the Manager, Media Productions and partnering with Comms and Workplace on all-hands, executive broadcasts, and live events.\n\n - Lead, coach, and grow a team of managers and senior engineers, and stand up new IT infrastructure engineering roles as the function scales.\n\n - Set and hold service-level standards for global IT - response times, uptime, and a high-quality employee experience across every office and region.\n\n - Drive the technical roadmap for systems and network architecture: identity lifecycle, SCIM/SAML/SSO, zero-trust network design, and high-availability infrastructure across new and existing offices.\n\n - Partner with Security to ensure every system and process meets Harvey's bar - SOC 2, encryption at rest and in transit, and SSO/SCIM for anything touching employee data.\n\n - Own IT infrastructure delivery for office buildouts and global expansion, working with Workplace and vendors from design through go-live.\n\n - Manage the IT operations and infrastructure budget, vendor relationships, and procurement in partnership with Finance and Procurement, leveraging Harvey's scale in negotiations.\n\n - Establish the operational rigor the function needs to scale — change control, incident and root-cause processes, asset management, and an ITSM practice.\n\n - Build a roadmap and reporting cadence that gives leadership clear visibility into IT health, risk, and investment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 10 years of experience in IT operations and/or systems and network engineering, with at least 4 years leading teams (including managing managers or senior ICs).\n\n - Deep hands-on grounding in modern IT infrastructure: identity and access management (Okta or equivalent), endpoint management (JAMF/MDM), cloud collaboration (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365), and enterprise networking.\n\n - A track record of scaling IT operations and infrastructure in a high-growth company, including multi-office or global environments.\n\n - Demonstrated security-first judgment — you've partnered with Security/Compliance teams and understand SOC 2, SSO/SCIM, and data protection requirements.\n\n - Experience owning budgets, vendor relationships, and procurement decisions.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\nBonus Points:\n\n - Experience overseeing A/V, conference room, or live event production technology, or managing a media/production function.\n\n - Background supporting a security-conscious or regulated environment (legal, fintech, healthcare, or similar).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$224,000 - $336,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$224K - $336K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9f692620-9884-436b-9ab5-41f12c658249","tierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4a234323-037a-419b-96c7-583acb43ad00","summary":"$224K – $336K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"id":"0b601efc-dd70-4ee3-afdd-118ef5be8e66","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cef266d1-8a5f-45ad-b33e-72e17f0abb3f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d1669780-6956-4e5b-bc84-590267c565ea","title":"Senior/Staff Product Manager, Vault","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-07T23:22:44.243+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d1669780-6956-4e5b-bc84-590267c565ea","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d1669780-6956-4e5b-bc84-590267c565ea/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Product Manager for Vault at Harvey, you will own and drive the product vision, strategy, and execution for our document and knowledge management platform-a critical foundation that powers how legal professionals interact with Harvey's AI capabilities. Vault enables law firms and enterprise clients to securely store, organize, search, and leverage their documents and institutional knowledge within Harvey's AI-powered ecosystem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will lead cross-functional teams to build and scale Vault's capabilities, including file management, AI-enabled search and Q&amp;A, document extraction, secure sharing across workspaces, and seamless integrations with enterprise document management systems like iManage, SharePoint, and Dropbox. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role where you'll directly shape how the world's leading law firms and enterprises organize and unlock value from their most sensitive documents.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and own the Vault product vision and roadmap:</strong> Develop a compelling product strategy that aligns with Harvey's mission to transform legal and professional services through AI, balancing near-term customer needs with long-term platform investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive end-to-end product development:</strong> Lead cross-functional teams including engineering, design, AI/ML, and go-to-market to ship high-quality features from ideation through launch and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner deeply with engineering:</strong> Work closely with engineering leadership to make technical and architectural decisions, dive deep into complex problems, and ensure we're building scalable, secure, and performant systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Understand and champion customer needs:</strong> Collaborate with Customer Success, Sales, and Legal Product Specialists to deeply understand how law firms and enterprise clients use Vault, identify adoption barriers, and translate insights into product improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own enterprise integrations strategy:</strong> Drive the vision for how Vault integrates with document management systems (iManage, SharePoint, Dropbox, Box) and other enterprise tools, ensuring seamless workflows for customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Define and track success metrics:</strong> Establish KPIs for Vault adoption, engagement, and value realization; use data to inform product decisions and demonstrate customer impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate cross-functionally:</strong> Partner with Product Marketing, Partnerships, and Admin/Governance teams to ensure successful product launches, effective positioning, and alignment with broader platform capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute to Harvey's product culture:</strong> Mentor other product managers, share learnings, and help establish best practices as the product organization scales.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Must-Have Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML-powered products, semantic search, retrieval systems, or document processing pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in legal technology, professional services, or deep understanding of law firm workflows and enterprise legal operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with enterprise integrations (APIs, authentication frameworks like SSO/SCIM/OAuth, third-party DMS platforms).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience at a company during a high-growth stage (Series B through IPO).</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$177,700 - $266,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Product Manager for Vault at Harvey, you will own and drive the product vision, strategy, and execution for our document and knowledge management platform-a critical foundation that powers how legal professionals interact with Harvey's AI capabilities. Vault enables law firms and enterprise clients to securely store, organize, search, and leverage their documents and institutional knowledge within Harvey's AI-powered ecosystem.\n\nYou will lead cross-functional teams to build and scale Vault's capabilities, including file management, AI-enabled search and Q&A, document extraction, secure sharing across workspaces, and seamless integrations with enterprise document management systems like iManage, SharePoint, and Dropbox. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role where you'll directly shape how the world's leading law firms and enterprises organize and unlock value from their most sensitive documents.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define and own the Vault product vision and roadmap: Develop a compelling product strategy that aligns with Harvey's mission to transform legal and professional services through AI, balancing near-term customer needs with long-term platform investments.\n\n - Drive end-to-end product development: Lead cross-functional teams including engineering, design, AI/ML, and go-to-market to ship high-quality features from ideation through launch and iteration.\n\n - Partner deeply with engineering: Work closely with engineering leadership to make technical and architectural decisions, dive deep into complex problems, and ensure we're building scalable, secure, and performant systems.\n\n - Understand and champion customer needs: Collaborate with Customer Success, Sales, and Legal Product Specialists to deeply understand how law firms and enterprise clients use Vault, identify adoption barriers, and translate insights into product improvements.\n\n - Own enterprise integrations strategy: Drive the vision for how Vault integrates with document management systems (iManage, SharePoint, Dropbox, Box) and other enterprise tools, ensuring seamless workflows for customers.\n\n - Define and track success metrics: Establish KPIs for Vault adoption, engagement, and value realization; use data to inform product decisions and demonstrate customer impact.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally: Partner with Product Marketing, Partnerships, and Admin/Governance teams to ensure successful product launches, effective positioning, and alignment with broader platform capabilities.\n\n - Contribute to Harvey's product culture: Mentor other product managers, share learnings, and help establish best practices as the product organization scales.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nMust-Have Qualifications:\n\n - 8+ years of product management experience, with at least 3 years at a Staff or Senior PM level at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Proven track record of owning and scaling complex platform or infrastructure products, ideally in enterprise SaaS, document management, knowledge management, or data-intensive domains.\n\n - Strong technical acumen with the ability to engage deeply with engineering on system design, distributed systems, data pipelines, and retrieval architectures.\n\n - Experience building products that handle sensitive data with robust security, compliance, and access control requirements.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders at various levels, from engineers to executives.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and drive clarity through complexity.\n\n - Strong product sense and attention to detail-ability to think through both high-level strategy and nitty-gritty implementation details.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n - Experience with AI/ML-powered products, semantic search, retrieval systems, or document processing pipelines.\n\n - Background in legal technology, professional services, or deep understanding of law firm workflows and enterprise legal operations.\n\n - Experience with enterprise integrations (APIs, authentication frameworks like SSO/SCIM/OAuth, third-party DMS platforms).\n\n - Prior experience at a company during a high-growth stage (Series B through IPO).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$177,700 - $266,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$177.7K - $266.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"33e55326-d7fe-4fab-9dea-4bb741e54cc5","tierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"18c5ac56-da24-4342-864a-54f91a6e3d91","summary":"$177.7K – $266.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"id":"5bdc21a5-2c93-4114-9db5-33fc7bb5fb85","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fe65a421-3992-442d-8362-e361a37e6c57","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6be9a875-eb12-4d02-939d-1221f01a711f","title":"Sales Manager - SMB","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T13:47:40.292+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6be9a875-eb12-4d02-939d-1221f01a711f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6be9a875-eb12-4d02-939d-1221f01a711f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The SMB Sales Manager joins Harvey's Commercial Sales organization to lead a team of Account Executives selling Harvey's AI platform to small and mid-sized law firms and legal teams out of the New York City office. Reporting to the Vice President of Commercial Sales, this role owns territory planning, pipeline development, and revenue execution across the region. The manager drives a disciplined sales process while coaching AEs through the full cycle — from discovery and qualification through close — and holds the team accountable to rigorous forecasting and performance standards. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape the sales culture and operating rhythm for a fast-growing segment at one of the most innovative companies in legal technology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, coach, and performance-manage a team of SMB Account Executives focused on selling Harvey's platform to law firms and corporate legal departments in the New York City region</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own territory planning, pipeline development, and accurate forecasting to deliver against quarterly and annual revenue targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive a disciplined sales process using MEDDPIC or similar methodology, ensuring AEs execute high-quality discovery, qualification, objection handling, and close motions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a local operating cadence — team standups, deal reviews, pipeline hygiene — that mirrors Harvey's high-performance sales culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a player-coach by actively engaging in strategic deals and modeling best practices in discovery, demo, and negotiation</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of tech sales experience — ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performing sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to sophisticated buyers, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of coaching AEs through complex sales cycles, including deal strategy, objection handling, and negotiation, with a growth-oriented and coachable mindset</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$280,000 - $320,000 USD with 50/50 OTE split</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe SMB Sales Manager joins Harvey's Commercial Sales organization to lead a team of Account Executives selling Harvey's AI platform to small and mid-sized law firms and legal teams out of the New York City office. Reporting to the Vice President of Commercial Sales, this role owns territory planning, pipeline development, and revenue execution across the region. The manager drives a disciplined sales process while coaching AEs through the full cycle — from discovery and qualification through close — and holds the team accountable to rigorous forecasting and performance standards. It is a high-impact opportunity to shape the sales culture and operating rhythm for a fast-growing segment at one of the most innovative companies in legal technology.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, coach, and performance-manage a team of SMB Account Executives focused on selling Harvey's platform to law firms and corporate legal departments in the New York City region\n\n - Own territory planning, pipeline development, and accurate forecasting to deliver against quarterly and annual revenue targets\n\n - Drive a disciplined sales process using MEDDPIC or similar methodology, ensuring AEs execute high-quality discovery, qualification, objection handling, and close motions\n\n - Establish a local operating cadence — team standups, deal reviews, pipeline hygiene — that mirrors Harvey's high-performance sales culture\n\n - Serve as a player-coach by actively engaging in strategic deals and modeling best practices in discovery, demo, and negotiation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of tech sales experience — ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; 2+ years of people management experience training and coaching a high-performing sales team.\n\n - Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to sophisticated buyers, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Energized by mentoring account executives, contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Track record of coaching AEs through complex sales cycles, including deal strategy, objection handling, and negotiation, with a growth-oriented and coachable mindset\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$280,000 - $320,000 USD with 50/50 OTE split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$280K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • 50/50 OTE Split","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$280K - $320K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"74284598-5ef1-4c66-9ca8-59c50f19b61f","tierSummary":"$280K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • 50/50 OTE Split","title":null,"additionalInformation":"50/50 OTE Split","components":[{"id":"9c623f45-6293-467b-8fea-039d758aa161","summary":"$280K – $320K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":280000,"maxValue":320000},{"id":"829a93b4-2767-4886-bf65-a9c6262e8072","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d93f1a80-1b90-48a1-900d-7913d80d2930","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":280000,"maxValue":320000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"18f569eb-49e9-4766-bb4b-49c2b3243f41","title":"Staff Site Reliability Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-31T03:16:28.180+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/18f569eb-49e9-4766-bb4b-49c2b3243f41","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/18f569eb-49e9-4766-bb4b-49c2b3243f41/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Site Reliability (SRE) team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish best practices for security, compliance, and reliability and collaborate across teams to drive these principles throughout the software lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical mentorship and leadership, promoting best practices and fostering team growth</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) or similar roles supporting production environments, with proven ability to mentor and guide technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Site Reliability (SRE) team at Harvey, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our legal AI platform. You’ll join a high-leverage team that sits at the intersection of infrastructure and product, owning the systems that keep our platform fast, secure, and always on. From scaling across 50+ regions to automating mission-critical operations, your work will ensure that Harvey remains resilient as we grow. If you’re passionate about building robust systems and reducing complexity through automation, we’d love to work with you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use an in-person work model and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, implement, and manage monitoring, alerting, and infrastructure resources (compute, storage, networking) across 50+ global regions\n\n - Lead incident management processes, including postmortems, root cause analyses, and driving actionable improvements\n\n - Automate operational tasks and workflows, building tools and processes for capacity planning, graceful rollouts, and safe data access to maintain high reliability and reduce manual intervention\n\n - Establish best practices for security, compliance, and reliability and collaborate across teams to drive these principles throughout the software lifecycle\n\n - Optimize infrastructure costs through strategic capacity planning and build-versus-buy decisions while maintaining system performance, reliability, and functionality\n\n - Provide technical mentorship and leadership, promoting best practices and fostering team growth\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 12+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) or similar roles supporting production environments, with proven ability to mentor and guide technical teams\n\n - Expertise in infrastructure as code(IaC) tools (Pulumi, Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.)\n\n - Deep familiarity with observability tools (Datadog, Sentry, etc.) and incident response practices (PagerDuty, IncidentIO, etc.)\n\n - Proficiency with cloud infrastructure platforms (Azure, GCP, AWS, etc.)\n\n - Strong programming skills (Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages)\n\n - Proven track record of diagnosing complex system problems and implementing durable solutions\n\n - Solid understanding of CI/CD, Kubernetes, containerization, networking, databases, and cloud security principles\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to operational excellence\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-AS2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"dabda43b-ab7a-45b3-9fcf-2b6b70bb26c7","title":"Sales Manager, Enterprise","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Mexico","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T22:52:31.324+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Mexico"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dabda43b-ab7a-45b3-9fcf-2b6b70bb26c7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dabda43b-ab7a-45b3-9fcf-2b6b70bb26c7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Enterprise Sales Manager, Mexico City joins the Enterprise Sales organization to lead and scale the company's presence across Latin American legal and professional services markets. The team's mission is to drive adoption of Harvey's AI solutions among the region's leading law firms and in-house legal departments, establishing Mexico City as a key hub for LATAM growth. This role shapes the go-to-market strategy for the region, building and coaching a high-performing team of Account Executives while directly engaging with prospective customers. Working in close partnership with Legal Engineering, Solutions Architecture, and Customer Success, the Enterprise Sales Manager influences how Harvey lands and expands in one of its fastest-growing international markets. It is an opportunity to define the playbook for a new geography at a category-defining AI company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recruit, mentor and lead a team of consultative, solution-based, Enterprise sales professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the LATAM in-house team from the ground up, including sourcing and closing early hires where Harvey has no limited local sales presence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own long-term strategy and day-to-day operations of the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be accountable for delivering on revenue targets, forecasting accurately, and scaling the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally across the organization to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey's clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as Harvey's ambassador across LATAM's in-house legal community — building visibility through speaking opportunities, GC and legal-ops networks, and relationships that establish Harvey as a category leader region-wide.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate the distinct business and regulatory nuances of each LATAM market you operate in (e.g. Mexico vs. Brazil), adapting Harvey's positioning and go-to-market approach accordingly rather than treating LATAM as one homogeneous market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cultivate a culture of development to promote career growth of direct reports.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of tech sales experience and 5+ years of people management experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience training and coaching a high-performance enterprise sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment — ideally including standing up a new team, region, or territory from scratch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships within the LATAM in-house legal / legal ops community (GCs, Heads of Legal, regional legal innovation circles) — someone who is already a known and respected name in-market, not starting from zero.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish required; Portuguese is a strong plus given Brazil's importance to the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal departments is a strong bonus, though not required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work — genuinely energized by the idea of transforming an industry with technology, and comfortable being seen as a public advocate for that change, and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with frequent in-market travel across multiple LATAM countries (30%+).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to haves:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal departments is a strong bonus, though not required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships within the LATAM in-house legal / legal ops community (GCs, Heads of Legal, regional legal innovation circles) — someone who is already a known and respected name in-market, not starting from zero.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Portuguese is a strong plus given Brazil's importance to the region.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br /></strong>Location</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mexico City (CDMX), with regular travel across LATAM (Brazil in particular).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Enterprise Sales Manager, Mexico City joins the Enterprise Sales organization to lead and scale the company's presence across Latin American legal and professional services markets. The team's mission is to drive adoption of Harvey's AI solutions among the region's leading law firms and in-house legal departments, establishing Mexico City as a key hub for LATAM growth. This role shapes the go-to-market strategy for the region, building and coaching a high-performing team of Account Executives while directly engaging with prospective customers. Working in close partnership with Legal Engineering, Solutions Architecture, and Customer Success, the Enterprise Sales Manager influences how Harvey lands and expands in one of its fastest-growing international markets. It is an opportunity to define the playbook for a new geography at a category-defining AI company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Recruit, mentor and lead a team of consultative, solution-based, Enterprise sales professionals.\n\n - Build the LATAM in-house team from the ground up, including sourcing and closing early hires where Harvey has no limited local sales presence.\n\n - Own long-term strategy and day-to-day operations of the team.\n\n - Be accountable for delivering on revenue targets, forecasting accurately, and scaling the team.\n\n - Work cross-functionally across the organization to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey's clients.\n\n - Act as Harvey's ambassador across LATAM's in-house legal community — building visibility through speaking opportunities, GC and legal-ops networks, and relationships that establish Harvey as a category leader region-wide.\n\n - Navigate the distinct business and regulatory nuances of each LATAM market you operate in (e.g. Mexico vs. Brazil), adapting Harvey's positioning and go-to-market approach accordingly rather than treating LATAM as one homogeneous market.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Cultivate a culture of development to promote career growth of direct reports.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of tech sales experience and 5+ years of people management experience.\n\n - Experience training and coaching a high-performance enterprise sales team.\n\n - Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment — ideally including standing up a new team, region, or territory from scratch.\n\n - Existing relationships within the LATAM in-house legal / legal ops community (GCs, Heads of Legal, regional legal innovation circles) — someone who is already a known and respected name in-market, not starting from zero.\n\n - Fluency in Spanish required; Portuguese is a strong plus given Brazil's importance to the region.\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal departments is a strong bonus, though not required.\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work — genuinely energized by the idea of transforming an industry with technology, and comfortable being seen as a public advocate for that change, and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Comfortable with frequent in-market travel across multiple LATAM countries (30%+).\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\nNice to haves:\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal departments is a strong bonus, though not required.\n\n - Existing relationships within the LATAM in-house legal / legal ops community (GCs, Heads of Legal, regional legal innovation circles) — someone who is already a known and respected name in-market, not starting from zero.\n\n - Portuguese is a strong plus given Brazil's importance to the region.\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\n - Mexico City (CDMX), with regular travel across LATAM (Brazil in particular).\n   \n   \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c4b8bccd-019d-4e20-8fe6-d4bc492dcce7","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T23:36:55.271+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c4b8bccd-019d-4e20-8fe6-d4bc492dcce7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c4b8bccd-019d-4e20-8fe6-d4bc492dcce7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, with a proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients and the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 5 years of experience in enterprise B2B SaaS sales, with a proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients and the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JB1\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n\n\nThe annualized base salary ranges for the role are listed below. Harvey pay ranges vary based on work location. As a part of the total compensation package, this role may be eligible for the Harvey Bonus Plan or a role-specific commission/bonus, as well as annual refresh equity grants. Recruiters can share more detail during the hiring process. Each candidate’s compensation offer will be based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, geography, experience, skills, job duties, and business need, among other things.\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"594f114f-8389-4412-a2ae-d78b16abfa12","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Mexico","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T23:46:16.052+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Mexico"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/594f114f-8389-4412-a2ae-d78b16abfa12","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/594f114f-8389-4412-a2ae-d78b16abfa12/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mexico City</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with law firms and other large enterprise clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and manage a named account list and be responsible for the full sales cycle from prospecting to contracting to onboarding, launching, and growing new users.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions to enterprise clients, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work and interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our sales processes and team-driven sales culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nMexico City\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"86e909de-f2fb-4c3d-99bc-e0352cbf03b8","title":"Executive Assistant","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:39:39.938+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/86e909de-f2fb-4c3d-99bc-e0352cbf03b8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/86e909de-f2fb-4c3d-99bc-e0352cbf03b8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is seeking highly strategic, proactive, and polished Executive Assistants to support senior leaders across the organization. This role goes beyond traditional administrative support. It requires a partner who can help maximize executive leverage, operate as a force multiplier, and bring structure to a fast-moving, high-stakes environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate has experience supporting senior, externally-facing executives and is comfortable navigating complex stakeholder landscapes across internal teams, customers, and partners. This person exercises strong judgment, is highly discerning about priorities, and plays an active role in ensuring the executive’s time is deployed against the highest-impact opportunities. They bring a track record of owning executive time, acting as an opinionated partner, and helping drive meaningful business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive executive leverage by owning and optimizing complex calendars, ensuring time is allocated to the highest-priority internal and external engagements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic gatekeeper for the executive’s time, triaging inbound requests, prioritizing effectively, and making clear, confident recommendations on where attention is needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and scale the executive request flow, bringing structure and clarity across a wide set of stakeholders and ensuring efficient intake, prioritization, and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a central point of coordination across internal teams and external stakeholders, ensuring communication is seamless, proactive, and high quality while maintaining strong relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own meeting preparation end to end, including agenda setting, materials development, and driving follow-ups to ensure strong execution and momentum</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage complex inboxes and communications, helping synthesize information, draft responses, and ensure the executive is consistently well-prepared and ahead by surfacing key decisions and recommending actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute high-impact travel and logistics with a focus on efficiency, foresight, and minimizing friction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support strategic projects and initiatives, bringing organization, follow-through, and a bias for action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to presentations and materials, ensuring executive communications are clear, polished, and aligned to priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a steady, calm, and positive presence across a broad set of relationships, helping maintain alignment and trust</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle highly sensitive and confidential information with discretion and sound judgment</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience supporting senior executives, ideally in a high-growth, externally-facing environment, with a strong preference for experience supporting C-level or equivalent leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage complex stakeholder ecosystems, including senior external partners and cross-functional internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment and prioritization skills, with the ability to triage competing demands and make clear, confident decisions on behalf of the executive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing high-volume, complex inboxes and communications, with a focus on creating leverage and clarity while proactively driving decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building and operating scalable systems for managing requests, workflows, and executive engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to draft executive-level messaging and engage credibly with senior stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High degree of professionalism and executive presence, with the ability to influence and build trust across all levels of an organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Calm, steady, and solutions-oriented under pressure, with the ability to bring structure to ambiguous situations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly proactive and resourceful, with a strong ownership mindset and bias for action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discreet and trustworthy when handling sensitive information</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$119,000 - $140,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is seeking highly strategic, proactive, and polished Executive Assistants to support senior leaders across the organization. This role goes beyond traditional administrative support. It requires a partner who can help maximize executive leverage, operate as a force multiplier, and bring structure to a fast-moving, high-stakes environment.\n\nThe ideal candidate has experience supporting senior, externally-facing executives and is comfortable navigating complex stakeholder landscapes across internal teams, customers, and partners. This person exercises strong judgment, is highly discerning about priorities, and plays an active role in ensuring the executive’s time is deployed against the highest-impact opportunities. They bring a track record of owning executive time, acting as an opinionated partner, and helping drive meaningful business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Drive executive leverage by owning and optimizing complex calendars, ensuring time is allocated to the highest-priority internal and external engagements\n\n - Act as a strategic gatekeeper for the executive’s time, triaging inbound requests, prioritizing effectively, and making clear, confident recommendations on where attention is needed\n\n - Operate and scale the executive request flow, bringing structure and clarity across a wide set of stakeholders and ensuring efficient intake, prioritization, and follow-through\n\n - Serve as a central point of coordination across internal teams and external stakeholders, ensuring communication is seamless, proactive, and high quality while maintaining strong relationships\n\n - Own meeting preparation end to end, including agenda setting, materials development, and driving follow-ups to ensure strong execution and momentum\n\n - Manage complex inboxes and communications, helping synthesize information, draft responses, and ensure the executive is consistently well-prepared and ahead by surfacing key decisions and recommending actions\n\n - Plan and execute high-impact travel and logistics with a focus on efficiency, foresight, and minimizing friction\n\n - Support strategic projects and initiatives, bringing organization, follow-through, and a bias for action\n\n - Contribute to presentations and materials, ensuring executive communications are clear, polished, and aligned to priorities\n\n - Act as a steady, calm, and positive presence across a broad set of relationships, helping maintain alignment and trust\n\n - Handle highly sensitive and confidential information with discretion and sound judgment\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience supporting senior executives, ideally in a high-growth, externally-facing environment, with a strong preference for experience supporting C-level or equivalent leaders\n\n - Proven ability to manage complex stakeholder ecosystems, including senior external partners and cross-functional internal teams\n\n - Strong judgment and prioritization skills, with the ability to triage competing demands and make clear, confident decisions on behalf of the executive\n\n - Experience managing high-volume, complex inboxes and communications, with a focus on creating leverage and clarity while proactively driving decision-making\n\n - Track record of building and operating scalable systems for managing requests, workflows, and executive engagement\n\n - Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to draft executive-level messaging and engage credibly with senior stakeholders\n\n - High degree of professionalism and executive presence, with the ability to influence and build trust across all levels of an organization\n\n - Calm, steady, and solutions-oriented under pressure, with the ability to bring structure to ambiguous situations\n\n - Highly proactive and resourceful, with a strong ownership mindset and bias for action\n\n - Discreet and trustworthy when handling sensitive information\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$119,000 - $140,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-CA1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$119K – $140K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$119K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"728718d3-11d3-442c-8875-402a40cf0c0d","tierSummary":"$119K – $140K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"47860a47-cb19-4ad6-bf58-7b3d790eb6dd","summary":"$119K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":119000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"1f41aad0-887c-4ecc-9aec-08aaaeecbeda","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"20e6cb2f-52b3-4605-92df-92ced0b0eab2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":119000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"824ef487-4f82-4ff1-a0b3-34d50d906100","title":"Lead Copywriter","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T20:48:04.528+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/824ef487-4f82-4ff1-a0b3-34d50d906100","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/824ef487-4f82-4ff1-a0b3-34d50d906100/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services. As our product changes the way legal work gets done, the way we communicate it matters just as much. We're looking for our first <strong>Lead Copywriter</strong> to help define how Harvey sounds, establish the standards for our voice, and shape the ideas behind everything we put into the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is more than a writing role. It's a creative leadership role. You'll partner with designers, product marketers, motion designers, and leadership from the earliest stages of a project to turn business objectives into ideas people remember. Great writing starts with great thinking, and you'll help ensure Harvey is known not just for what we build, but for how we communicate it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be a hands-on creative, owning some of the company's highest-impact work while establishing the principles and standards that define Harvey's voice. As the company grows, you'll have the opportunity to help shape and scale our copywriting practice, mentoring future writers and influencing how the function evolves.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within Harvey's Brand &amp; Creative team. It's a rare opportunity to help define the voice of one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's voice, tone, and editorial standards across every customer and employee touchpoint.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The creative thinking behind campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives, helping shape ideas before a single word is written.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Copy across the marketing site, campaigns, product launches, social, executive communications, sales enablement, and other strategic brand moments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistency across an expanding network of marketers, product teams, agencies, and contributors, ensuring Harvey always sounds like one company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The continued evolution of Harvey's writing practice as the company scales.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's voice from first principles and create practical guidelines the entire company can use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Design, Motion, Web, Product Marketing, and company leadership to develop concepts and narratives from the earliest stages of a project.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and edit across a broad range of work, from campaign concepts and product launches to website copy, executive storytelling, sales materials, and social content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push beyond the brief to uncover the idea that makes the work memorable, not simply the message that needs to be communicated.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review, edit, and elevate copy from teammates, agencies, and cross-functional partners to maintain a consistently high creative standard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as Harvey's internal authority on language, helping teams communicate with greater clarity, confidence, and originality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish the foundations of Harvey's copywriting practice and mentor future writers as the team grows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in copywriting, brand storytelling, or creative leadership, ideally across agency, in-house, or high-growth technology environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio demonstrating exceptional conceptual thinking alongside world-class execution across campaigns, brand, web, product, and launch work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong point of view on language, voice, and storytelling, with the judgment to know when consistency matters and when the rules should be broken.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing creative concepts, not simply executing copy against an existing brief.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional editing instincts and the ability to elevate the writing of others through thoughtful, direct feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring or guiding other writers, even if not through formal people management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to navigate ambiguity, influence senior stakeholders, and move comfortably between strategic thinking and hands-on execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Bonus</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or redefining a brand voice from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring writers or helping establish editorial standards and creative processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Why This Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every iconic company is remembered not only for what it built, but for how it spoke.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey has the opportunity to become one of those companies.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our first <strong>Lead Copywriter</strong>, you'll help define the language behind one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world, influencing everything from product launches and campaigns to executive storytelling and the customer experience itself. You'll have the opportunity to shape Harvey's voice from the ground up while partnering with a creative team that believes exceptional writing is one of the greatest competitive advantages a brand can have.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$164,000 - $246,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services. As our product changes the way legal work gets done, the way we communicate it matters just as much. We're looking for our first Lead Copywriter to help define how Harvey sounds, establish the standards for our voice, and shape the ideas behind everything we put into the world.\n\nThis is more than a writing role. It's a creative leadership role. You'll partner with designers, product marketers, motion designers, and leadership from the earliest stages of a project to turn business objectives into ideas people remember. Great writing starts with great thinking, and you'll help ensure Harvey is known not just for what we build, but for how we communicate it.\n\nYou'll be a hands-on creative, owning some of the company's highest-impact work while establishing the principles and standards that define Harvey's voice. As the company grows, you'll have the opportunity to help shape and scale our copywriting practice, mentoring future writers and influencing how the function evolves.\n\nThis role reports to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within Harvey's Brand & Creative team. It's a rare opportunity to help define the voice of one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL OWN\n\n - Harvey's voice, tone, and editorial standards across every customer and employee touchpoint.\n\n - The creative thinking behind campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives, helping shape ideas before a single word is written.\n\n - Copy across the marketing site, campaigns, product launches, social, executive communications, sales enablement, and other strategic brand moments.\n\n - Consistency across an expanding network of marketers, product teams, agencies, and contributors, ensuring Harvey always sounds like one company.\n\n - The continued evolution of Harvey's writing practice as the company scales.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define Harvey's voice from first principles and create practical guidelines the entire company can use.\n\n - Partner closely with Design, Motion, Web, Product Marketing, and company leadership to develop concepts and narratives from the earliest stages of a project.\n\n - Write and edit across a broad range of work, from campaign concepts and product launches to website copy, executive storytelling, sales materials, and social content.\n\n - Push beyond the brief to uncover the idea that makes the work memorable, not simply the message that needs to be communicated.\n\n - Review, edit, and elevate copy from teammates, agencies, and cross-functional partners to maintain a consistently high creative standard.\n\n - Serve as Harvey's internal authority on language, helping teams communicate with greater clarity, confidence, and originality.\n\n - Help establish the foundations of Harvey's copywriting practice and mentor future writers as the team grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in copywriting, brand storytelling, or creative leadership, ideally across agency, in-house, or high-growth technology environments.\n\n - A portfolio demonstrating exceptional conceptual thinking alongside world-class execution across campaigns, brand, web, product, and launch work.\n\n - A strong point of view on language, voice, and storytelling, with the judgment to know when consistency matters and when the rules should be broken.\n\n - Experience developing creative concepts, not simply executing copy against an existing brief.\n\n - Exceptional editing instincts and the ability to elevate the writing of others through thoughtful, direct feedback.\n\n - Experience mentoring or guiding other writers, even if not through formal people management.\n\n - The ability to navigate ambiguity, influence senior stakeholders, and move comfortably between strategic thinking and hands-on execution.\n   \n   \n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.\n\n - Experience building or redefining a brand voice from the ground up.\n\n - Experience mentoring writers or helping establish editorial standards and creative processes.\n\n - Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE\n\nEvery iconic company is remembered not only for what it built, but for how it spoke.\n\nHarvey has the opportunity to become one of those companies.\n\nAs our first Lead Copywriter, you'll help define the language behind one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world, influencing everything from product launches and campaigns to executive storytelling and the customer experience itself. You'll have the opportunity to shape Harvey's voice from the ground up while partnering with a creative team that believes exceptional writing is one of the greatest competitive advantages a brand can have.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$164,000 - $246,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$164K – $246K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$164K - $246K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"67f02dd7-91c3-4386-8bc6-a7b58438fd96","tierSummary":"$164K – $246K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"bac3055d-3965-4475-9129-2b07167451d2","summary":"$164K – $246K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":246000},{"id":"59f901f1-5638-4d84-a1a7-a59c39840356","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e4f4b6c4-2f77-47f6-ba68-d545176e9b4e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":246000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"79b98a8b-14cc-4cec-83ff-32969cc0cbfe","title":"Mid Market Sales Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Mexico","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-14T21:19:17.141+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Mexico"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/79b98a8b-14cc-4cec-83ff-32969cc0cbfe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/79b98a8b-14cc-4cec-83ff-32969cc0cbfe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Mid Market Sales Manager</strong> at Harvey, you will build and lead our <strong>founding Mid Market sales pod in Mexico City</strong>, helping establish Harvey's presence across Mexico. You'll lead and coach high-performing Account Executives in driving the growth and adoption of our AI platform within midsized and boutique law firms, as well as in-house legal teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of our earliest sales leaders in the region, you'll play a critical role in building the team, shaping our culture, and defining how Harvey scales in Mexico. You'll be responsible for delivering ambitious sales targets while remaining hands-on with customers, coaching your team through complex deals, and helping establish the playbooks, operating rhythms, and best practices that will serve as the foundation for future growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in this role requires someone who can move seamlessly between local and global teams, building strong relationships with customers and cross-functional partners across both Mexico and the United States. We're looking for a builder who thrives in ambiguity, enjoys creating structure from scratch, and is excited by the opportunity to launch and scale a new market.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, lead, and develop Harvey's founding Mid Market sales pod in Mexico City, creating a high-performing, collaborative team culture from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a team of consultative, solution-based Mid Market Account Executives to achieve ARR targets through both net new logo acquisition and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own forecasting, pipeline management, and overall business performance for your region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Recruiting to hire and onboard exceptional talent as the Mexico team continues to grow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach and develop Mid Market Account Executives through every stage of the sales cycle, helping them grow their careers while consistently raising the performance bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish and refine Harvey's Mid Market sales playbook, adapting global best practices to the needs of the Mexico market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with Marketing, Customer Success, Legal Engineers, Product, and Sales Leadership to build scalable sales processes and deliver an exceptional customer experience.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of technology sales experience, including 2+ years of people management experience leading and coaching high-performing sales teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional fluency in both <strong>Spanish and English</strong>, with the ability to coach teams and build executive relationships in both languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early-stage or high-growth environment where you've helped build teams, processes, or new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the Mexican business landscape and experience selling into or leading teams serving customers across Mexico.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions using a consultative, value-based sales methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong forecasting, operational rigor, and pipeline management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for mentoring Account Executives, refining sales processes, and building a high-performing, collaborative sales culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and excitement about helping establish our long-term presence in Mexico.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Sales Manager at Harvey, you will build and lead our founding Mid Market sales pod in Mexico City, helping establish Harvey's presence across Mexico. You'll lead and coach high-performing Account Executives in driving the growth and adoption of our AI platform within midsized and boutique law firms, as well as in-house legal teams.\n\nAs one of our earliest sales leaders in the region, you'll play a critical role in building the team, shaping our culture, and defining how Harvey scales in Mexico. You'll be responsible for delivering ambitious sales targets while remaining hands-on with customers, coaching your team through complex deals, and helping establish the playbooks, operating rhythms, and best practices that will serve as the foundation for future growth.\n\nSuccess in this role requires someone who can move seamlessly between local and global teams, building strong relationships with customers and cross-functional partners across both Mexico and the United States. We're looking for a builder who thrives in ambiguity, enjoys creating structure from scratch, and is excited by the opportunity to launch and scale a new market.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, lead, and develop Harvey's founding Mid Market sales pod in Mexico City, creating a high-performing, collaborative team culture from the ground up.\n\n - Lead a team of consultative, solution-based Mid Market Account Executives to achieve ARR targets through both net new logo acquisition and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Own forecasting, pipeline management, and overall business performance for your region.\n\n - Partner closely with Recruiting to hire and onboard exceptional talent as the Mexico team continues to grow.\n\n - Coach and develop Mid Market Account Executives through every stage of the sales cycle, helping them grow their careers while consistently raising the performance bar.\n\n - Help establish and refine Harvey's Mid Market sales playbook, adapting global best practices to the needs of the Mexico market.\n\n - Work cross-functionally with Marketing, Customer Success, Legal Engineers, Product, and Sales Leadership to build scalable sales processes and deliver an exceptional customer experience.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of technology sales experience, including 2+ years of people management experience leading and coaching high-performing sales teams.\n\n - Professional fluency in both Spanish and English, with the ability to coach teams and build executive relationships in both languages.\n\n - Experience operating in an early-stage or high-growth environment where you've helped build teams, processes, or new markets.\n\n - Strong understanding of the Mexican business landscape and experience selling into or leading teams serving customers across Mexico.\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions using a consultative, value-based sales methodology.\n\n - Strong forecasting, operational rigor, and pipeline management skills.\n\n - Outstanding communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n - Passion for mentoring Account Executives, refining sales processes, and building a high-performing, collaborative sales culture.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and excitement about helping establish our long-term presence in Mexico.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"63439ab1-eceb-40fc-9326-476335db26fb","title":"Lead Copywriter","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T20:47:41.865+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/63439ab1-eceb-40fc-9326-476335db26fb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/63439ab1-eceb-40fc-9326-476335db26fb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services. As our product changes the way legal work gets done, the way we communicate it matters just as much. We're looking for our first <strong>Lead Copywriter</strong> to help define how Harvey sounds, establish the standards for our voice, and shape the ideas behind everything we put into the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is more than a writing role. It's a creative leadership role. You'll partner with designers, product marketers, motion designers, and leadership from the earliest stages of a project to turn business objectives into ideas people remember. Great writing starts with great thinking, and you'll help ensure Harvey is known not just for what we build, but for how we communicate it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be a hands-on creative, owning some of the company's highest-impact work while establishing the principles and standards that define Harvey's voice. As the company grows, you'll have the opportunity to help shape and scale our copywriting practice, mentoring future writers and influencing how the function evolves.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within Harvey's Brand &amp; Creative team. It's a rare opportunity to help define the voice of one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's voice, tone, and editorial standards across every customer and employee touchpoint.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The creative thinking behind campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives, helping shape ideas before a single word is written.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Copy across the marketing site, campaigns, product launches, social, executive communications, sales enablement, and other strategic brand moments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistency across an expanding network of marketers, product teams, agencies, and contributors, ensuring Harvey always sounds like one company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The continued evolution of Harvey's writing practice as the company scales.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's voice from first principles and create practical guidelines the entire company can use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Design, Motion, Web, Product Marketing, and company leadership to develop concepts and narratives from the earliest stages of a project.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and edit across a broad range of work, from campaign concepts and product launches to website copy, executive storytelling, sales materials, and social content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push beyond the brief to uncover the idea that makes the work memorable, not simply the message that needs to be communicated.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review, edit, and elevate copy from teammates, agencies, and cross-functional partners to maintain a consistently high creative standard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as Harvey's internal authority on language, helping teams communicate with greater clarity, confidence, and originality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish the foundations of Harvey's copywriting practice and mentor future writers as the team grows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in copywriting, brand storytelling, or creative leadership, ideally across agency, in-house, or high-growth technology environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio demonstrating exceptional conceptual thinking alongside world-class execution across campaigns, brand, web, product, and launch work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong point of view on language, voice, and storytelling, with the judgment to know when consistency matters and when the rules should be broken.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing creative concepts, not simply executing copy against an existing brief.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional editing instincts and the ability to elevate the writing of others through thoughtful, direct feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring or guiding other writers, even if not through formal people management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to navigate ambiguity, influence senior stakeholders, and move comfortably between strategic thinking and hands-on execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Bonus</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or redefining a brand voice from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring writers or helping establish editorial standards and creative processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Why This Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every iconic company is remembered not only for what it built, but for how it spoke.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey has the opportunity to become one of those companies.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our first <strong>Lead Copywriter</strong>, you'll help define the language behind one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world, influencing everything from product launches and campaigns to executive storytelling and the customer experience itself. You'll have the opportunity to shape Harvey's voice from the ground up while partnering with a creative team that believes exceptional writing is one of the greatest competitive advantages a brand can have.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$164,000 - $246,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services. As our product changes the way legal work gets done, the way we communicate it matters just as much. We're looking for our first Lead Copywriter to help define how Harvey sounds, establish the standards for our voice, and shape the ideas behind everything we put into the world.\n\nThis is more than a writing role. It's a creative leadership role. You'll partner with designers, product marketers, motion designers, and leadership from the earliest stages of a project to turn business objectives into ideas people remember. Great writing starts with great thinking, and you'll help ensure Harvey is known not just for what we build, but for how we communicate it.\n\nYou'll be a hands-on creative, owning some of the company's highest-impact work while establishing the principles and standards that define Harvey's voice. As the company grows, you'll have the opportunity to help shape and scale our copywriting practice, mentoring future writers and influencing how the function evolves.\n\nThis role reports to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within Harvey's Brand & Creative team. It's a rare opportunity to help define the voice of one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL OWN\n\n - Harvey's voice, tone, and editorial standards across every customer and employee touchpoint.\n\n - The creative thinking behind campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives, helping shape ideas before a single word is written.\n\n - Copy across the marketing site, campaigns, product launches, social, executive communications, sales enablement, and other strategic brand moments.\n\n - Consistency across an expanding network of marketers, product teams, agencies, and contributors, ensuring Harvey always sounds like one company.\n\n - The continued evolution of Harvey's writing practice as the company scales.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define Harvey's voice from first principles and create practical guidelines the entire company can use.\n\n - Partner closely with Design, Motion, Web, Product Marketing, and company leadership to develop concepts and narratives from the earliest stages of a project.\n\n - Write and edit across a broad range of work, from campaign concepts and product launches to website copy, executive storytelling, sales materials, and social content.\n\n - Push beyond the brief to uncover the idea that makes the work memorable, not simply the message that needs to be communicated.\n\n - Review, edit, and elevate copy from teammates, agencies, and cross-functional partners to maintain a consistently high creative standard.\n\n - Serve as Harvey's internal authority on language, helping teams communicate with greater clarity, confidence, and originality.\n\n - Help establish the foundations of Harvey's copywriting practice and mentor future writers as the team grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in copywriting, brand storytelling, or creative leadership, ideally across agency, in-house, or high-growth technology environments.\n\n - A portfolio demonstrating exceptional conceptual thinking alongside world-class execution across campaigns, brand, web, product, and launch work.\n\n - A strong point of view on language, voice, and storytelling, with the judgment to know when consistency matters and when the rules should be broken.\n\n - Experience developing creative concepts, not simply executing copy against an existing brief.\n\n - Exceptional editing instincts and the ability to elevate the writing of others through thoughtful, direct feedback.\n\n - Experience mentoring or guiding other writers, even if not through formal people management.\n\n - The ability to navigate ambiguity, influence senior stakeholders, and move comfortably between strategic thinking and hands-on execution.\n   \n   \n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.\n\n - Experience building or redefining a brand voice from the ground up.\n\n - Experience mentoring writers or helping establish editorial standards and creative processes.\n\n - Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE\n\nEvery iconic company is remembered not only for what it built, but for how it spoke.\n\nHarvey has the opportunity to become one of those companies.\n\nAs our first Lead Copywriter, you'll help define the language behind one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world, influencing everything from product launches and campaigns to executive storytelling and the customer experience itself. You'll have the opportunity to shape Harvey's voice from the ground up while partnering with a creative team that believes exceptional writing is one of the greatest competitive advantages a brand can have.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$164,000 - $246,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$164K – $246K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$164K - $246K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1d1bd0f1-025f-4de3-8827-151d0bb2fffd","tierSummary":"$164K – $246K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e15bd807-ef8f-41ad-9552-86b5a0bdf9c0","summary":"$164K – $246K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":246000},{"id":"6df850cc-5d56-45ee-b4a0-bbbf126cac52","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"25e8fb1b-b4b6-4870-8b6d-957f89fd2e97","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":164000,"maxValue":246000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e59924d6-248a-4385-bc78-371cfdf6b783","title":"IT Operations Analyst, Bengaluru","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-19T17:41:15.301+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e59924d6-248a-4385-bc78-371cfdf6b783","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e59924d6-248a-4385-bc78-371cfdf6b783/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our Bengaluru office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our Bengaluru office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding, including provisioning/deprovisioning accounts and setting up new hire equipment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage user accounts, access, and security settings across Okta, Google Workspace, Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with basic security best practices and help enforce IT policies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and track recurring problems and their root causes, working with system owners to solve them permanently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 2+ years of IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting skills with macOS, Windows, and mobile devices (iOS/Android).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong customer service mindset—friendly, patient, and proactive—with a relentless focus on quality of experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with basic networking concepts (Wi-Fi, VPNs, firewalls, IP troubleshooting).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GW1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our Bengaluru office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.\n\nYou’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our Bengaluru office.\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding, including provisioning/deprovisioning accounts and setting up new hire equipment.\n\n - Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.\n\n - Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.\n\n - Manage user accounts, access, and security settings across Okta, Google Workspace, Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.\n\n - Assist with basic security best practices and help enforce IT policies.\n\n - Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.\n\n - Identify and track recurring problems and their root causes, working with system owners to solve them permanently.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 2+ years of IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.\n\n - Strong troubleshooting skills with macOS, Windows, and mobile devices (iOS/Android).\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - A strong customer service mindset—friendly, patient, and proactive—with a relentless focus on quality of experience.\n\n - Familiarity with basic networking concepts (Wi-Fi, VPNs, firewalls, IP troubleshooting).\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-GW1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d629fa64-599d-435c-b4ef-a925299ddac8","title":"Staff Product Manager, Infrastructure","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-14T00:04:08.326+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d629fa64-599d-435c-b4ef-a925299ddac8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d629fa64-599d-435c-b4ef-a925299ddac8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Manager on the Core Platform team at Harvey, you'll own the strategy, roadmap, and execution for the infrastructure that powers every user interaction with our global legal AI platform. Harvey serves the world's leading legal teams, processing trillions of tokens and millions of daily requests, and your work will shape how that capability reaches our users.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll operate at the intersection of deep customer need and hard technical constraints, translating the workflows of lawyers and other professionals into product requirements that engineering can build against. You'll balance ambitious, zero-to-one product bets with the operational discipline required to keep a mission-critical platform reliable, scalable, and secure as we expand across products, regions, and customers. Your decisions will directly influence adoption, retention, and the trust that our enterprise customers place in Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll partner directly with our Head of Infrastructure to  define and drive the product vision and roadmap for a core area of the Harvey platform, aligning it with company strategy and grounding it in evidence from customers (external and internal), data, and the market. You'll work closely with engineering, product, and go-to-market teams to ship high-quality products on a predictable cadence, and you'll own the outcomes those products produce.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Day to day, you will own the entire infrastructure planning, prioritization, and roadmapping. You’ll make and communicate crisp prioritization decisions, balancing new capabilities against reliability, performance, and security. You'll define the metrics that matter for your area — adoption, engagement, quality, and business impact — and hold the team accountable to them. You'll also serve as the connective tissue across functions, ensuring that customer feedback, competitive dynamics, and technical realities all inform the product direction, and you'll raise the product bar across the organization through rigorous specs, reviews, and decision-making. Some projects include architecting multi-region deployment strategies, developing comprehensive observability infrastructure, and more.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of product management experience shipping and scaling software platforms in a production environment, with a track record of measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning complex, technical products end to end, including  platform, infrastructure, or AI/ML capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to translate ambiguous problems and deep customer needs into clear strategy, crisp requirements, and prioritized roadmaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency working with engineering and design teams on technical trade-offs, and comfort engaging with concepts like distributed systems, APIs, and cloud infrastructure at a level sufficient to make informed decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical skills, with the ability to define metrics and use data to guide decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication, and a demonstrated ability to influence and align stakeholders across functions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A high bar for quality, strong product judgment, and a \"spidey sense\" for where a product experience could break down</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products for legal, professional-services, or other expert users with demanding accuracy and trust requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background with AI/ML products, LLM-powered applications, or high-throughput inference systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-tenant, enterprise platforms subject to strict security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience partnering closely with infrastructure or platform engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A prior career in law or another professional-services field, or experience building tools for those users</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$213,600 - $300,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Manager on the Core Platform team at Harvey, you'll own the strategy, roadmap, and execution for the infrastructure that powers every user interaction with our global legal AI platform. Harvey serves the world's leading legal teams, processing trillions of tokens and millions of daily requests, and your work will shape how that capability reaches our users.\n\nYou'll operate at the intersection of deep customer need and hard technical constraints, translating the workflows of lawyers and other professionals into product requirements that engineering can build against. You'll balance ambitious, zero-to-one product bets with the operational discipline required to keep a mission-critical platform reliable, scalable, and secure as we expand across products, regions, and customers. Your decisions will directly influence adoption, retention, and the trust that our enterprise customers place in Harvey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nYou'll partner directly with our Head of Infrastructure to  define and drive the product vision and roadmap for a core area of the Harvey platform, aligning it with company strategy and grounding it in evidence from customers (external and internal), data, and the market. You'll work closely with engineering, product, and go-to-market teams to ship high-quality products on a predictable cadence, and you'll own the outcomes those products produce.\n\nDay to day, you will own the entire infrastructure planning, prioritization, and roadmapping. You’ll make and communicate crisp prioritization decisions, balancing new capabilities against reliability, performance, and security. You'll define the metrics that matter for your area — adoption, engagement, quality, and business impact — and hold the team accountable to them. You'll also serve as the connective tissue across functions, ensuring that customer feedback, competitive dynamics, and technical realities all inform the product direction, and you'll raise the product bar across the organization through rigorous specs, reviews, and decision-making. Some projects include architecting multi-region deployment strategies, developing comprehensive observability infrastructure, and more.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of product management experience shipping and scaling software platforms in a production environment, with a track record of measurable impact\n\n - Experience owning complex, technical products end to end, including  platform, infrastructure, or AI/ML capabilities\n\n - Strong ability to translate ambiguous problems and deep customer needs into clear strategy, crisp requirements, and prioritized roadmaps\n\n - Fluency working with engineering and design teams on technical trade-offs, and comfort engaging with concepts like distributed systems, APIs, and cloud infrastructure at a level sufficient to make informed decisions\n\n - Excellent analytical skills, with the ability to define metrics and use data to guide decisions\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication, and a demonstrated ability to influence and align stakeholders across functions\n\n - A high bar for quality, strong product judgment, and a \"spidey sense\" for where a product experience could break down\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience building products for legal, professional-services, or other expert users with demanding accuracy and trust requirements\n\n - Background with AI/ML products, LLM-powered applications, or high-throughput inference systems\n\n - Experience with multi-tenant, enterprise platforms subject to strict security and compliance requirements\n\n - Prior experience partnering closely with infrastructure or platform engineering teams\n\n - A prior career in law or another professional-services field, or experience building tools for those users\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$213,600 - $300,000\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$213.6K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$213.6K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c2254dae-be06-40d0-a2d2-0cdd4a984058","tierSummary":"$213.6K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4c5cfab9-006d-4340-9d8f-9496599dc45e","summary":"$213.6K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":213600,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"6e5d1c04-9837-4821-b435-33dd77495c7f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0f1c25c2-265b-47d3-a7b2-a972dd6f3353","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":213600,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8e420b36-6711-49dd-8a64-f246270af7d3","title":"Engineering Manager, Production Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-13T23:51:16.213+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8e420b36-6711-49dd-8a64-f246270af7d3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8e420b36-6711-49dd-8a64-f246270af7d3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world's leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Engineering Manager to lead our Infrastructure Production Engineering organization. This team is responsible for building and operating Harvey's core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations that enable engineering teams to move quickly with confidence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you'll own the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey's infrastructure platform. You'll lead a team of high-performing engineers responsible for compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You'll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey's rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to the Head of Infrastructure and play a key leadership role in shaping the future of Harvey's infrastructure platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value <strong>Decisiveness</strong>, <strong>Simplicity</strong>, and the belief that <strong>Job's Not Finished</strong>. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h3><strong>Leadership &amp; Strategy</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and grow a team of high-performing infrastructure engineers responsible for Harvey's production infrastructure foundation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of operational excellence, engineering quality, customer ownership, and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering, Security, Product, and AI Infrastructure leaders to define long-term infrastructure strategy and execution priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive technical direction for compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional initiatives to improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost optimization.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Infrastructure Foundation &amp; Production Operations</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and operate Harvey's global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage compute resources to maximize utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead capacity planning, demand forecasting, and fleet lifecycle management to ensure infrastructure scales efficiently with business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and continuously improve Harvey's Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's Temporal-based workflow orchestration platform, ensuring reliable, scalable, and observable execution of distributed application workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure cost optimization through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload efficiency improvements, and utilization monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish comprehensive observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness practices across the infrastructure platform.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software or infrastructure engineering experience, including 5+ years leading engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating large-scale distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating observability platforms, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success leading complex cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering strategy across organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to both engineering and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems-thinking mindset and passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating workflow orchestration platforms such as Temporal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$260,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world's leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.\n\nWe're looking for a Engineering Manager to lead our Infrastructure Production Engineering organization. This team is responsible for building and operating Harvey's core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations that enable engineering teams to move quickly with confidence.\n\nIn this role, you'll own the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey's infrastructure platform. You'll lead a team of high-performing engineers responsible for compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You'll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey's rapid growth.\n\nYou'll report to the Head of Infrastructure and play a key leadership role in shaping the future of Harvey's infrastructure platform.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job's Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nLEADERSHIP & STRATEGY\n\n - Lead, mentor, and grow a team of high-performing infrastructure engineers responsible for Harvey's production infrastructure foundation.\n\n - Foster a culture of operational excellence, engineering quality, customer ownership, and continuous improvement.\n\n - Partner with Engineering, Security, Product, and AI Infrastructure leaders to define long-term infrastructure strategy and execution priorities.\n\n - Drive technical direction for compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.\n\n - Lead cross-functional initiatives to improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost optimization.\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDATION & PRODUCTION OPERATIONS\n\n - Own and operate Harvey's global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.\n\n - Manage compute resources to maximize utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.\n\n - Lead capacity planning, demand forecasting, and fleet lifecycle management to ensure infrastructure scales efficiently with business growth.\n\n - Operate and continuously improve Harvey's Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.\n\n - Own Harvey's Temporal-based workflow orchestration platform, ensuring reliable, scalable, and observable execution of distributed application workflows.\n\n - Drive infrastructure cost optimization through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload efficiency improvements, and utilization monitoring.\n\n - Build and maintain secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.\n\n - Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.\n\n - Establish comprehensive observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness practices across the infrastructure platform.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of software or infrastructure engineering experience, including 5+ years leading engineering teams.\n\n - Deep expertise operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.\n\n - Experience building and operating large-scale distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.\n\n - Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.\n\n - Experience designing and operating observability platforms, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response processes.\n\n - Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.\n\n - Demonstrated success leading complex cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering strategy across organizations.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to both engineering and executive audiences.\n\n - A systems-thinking mindset and passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience operating workflow orchestration platforms such as Temporal.\n\n - Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.\n\n - Experience managing GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.\n\n - Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$260,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$260K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$260K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0546a9bb-1d73-4c24-85b1-98f264a63305","tierSummary":"$260K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"457901ce-053f-4403-a426-3b98b6a63aeb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"be9778ba-b45c-49f2-84d4-5d97fad6f6f3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"48cb13f8-8d37-4408-9009-86a8e3f5c511","summary":"$260K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"2b35e24d-72bc-4588-b823-50e514c3d430","title":"Head of Creative Design","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T19:18:27.820+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2b35e24d-72bc-4588-b823-50e514c3d430","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2b35e24d-72bc-4588-b823-50e514c3d430/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services, and the caliber of our design has to match the ambition of the product. We're looking for a <strong>Head of Creative Design</strong> to lead a team of designers and help elevate the quality, consistency, and execution of Harvey's creative work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player-coach role. You'll partner closely with Harvey's Creative Director to bring creative concepts to life, translating creative direction into exceptional design across Harvey's highest-impact work. You'll manage and mentor designers, provide thoughtful creative feedback, and remain hands-on with key projects when needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll help drive design across Harvey's creative activations—including events, brand campaigns, partnerships, and product launches—ensuring every touchpoint reflects a high standard of craft while helping the team grow and scale alongside the business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports directly to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within the Harvey Brand &amp; Creative team. It's an opportunity to help shape one of the fastest-growing AI brands in the world while building and leading a high-performing design team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design execution across Harvey's activations vertical, including events, brand campaigns, partnerships, product launches, and other strategic brand initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translating creative direction into compelling visual work across multiple projects simultaneously.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative feedback and design quality across the team, helping raise the standard of work through thoughtful reviews and mentorship.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Management, coaching, and development of Harvey's design team, including workload planning, career growth, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design consistency and operational excellence across a growing volume of high-impact creative work.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Harvey's VP of Creative and peer Creative Director to bring creative concepts to life through exceptional design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the visual direction for projects from early concepts through final execution, ensuring work meets a high standard of craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a team of designers through regular feedback, coaching, and creative direction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay hands-on with design work when appropriate, balancing management responsibilities with individual contribution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Creative Operations, Copy, Motion, and Marketing to deliver cohesive, high-quality creative work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive design across Harvey's flagship events, campaigns, partnership launches, product launches, and other high-visibility initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push work beyond the brief, helping uncover creative ideas that make campaigns memorable rather than simply well executed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish effective design workflows and review processes that help the team move quickly without sacrificing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of craft, collaboration, and continuous improvement across the design team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in brand or creative design, with largest experience managing or mentoring designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio demonstrating exceptional visual craft and strong conceptual thinking across campaigns, brand work, events, or product marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading design for high-visibility initiatives, including launches, activations, or integrated campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong creative judgment and the ability to provide clear, actionable feedback that improves both the work and the people creating it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience balancing multiple complex projects while maintaining a consistently high bar for quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort moving between leadership, creative direction, and hands-on execution depending on the needs of the project.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Bonus</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing for large-scale events or brand activations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience helping build or scale a growing creative organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why This Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The work Harvey's Brand &amp; Creative team produces reaches many of the world's leading law firms, corporations, and professional services organizations. The campaigns, launches, and experiences we create are some of the most visible expressions of our brand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Head of Creative Design, you'll play a critical role in shaping how that work comes to life—leading talented designers, raising the quality of every deliverable, and helping build a creative organization capable of supporting one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$233,000-295,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the defining AI platform for professional services, and the caliber of our design has to match the ambition of the product. We're looking for a Head of Creative Design to lead a team of designers and help elevate the quality, consistency, and execution of Harvey's creative work.\n\nThis is a player-coach role. You'll partner closely with Harvey's Creative Director to bring creative concepts to life, translating creative direction into exceptional design across Harvey's highest-impact work. You'll manage and mentor designers, provide thoughtful creative feedback, and remain hands-on with key projects when needed.\n\nYou'll help drive design across Harvey's creative activations—including events, brand campaigns, partnerships, and product launches—ensuring every touchpoint reflects a high standard of craft while helping the team grow and scale alongside the business.\n\nThis role reports directly to Scott Smith, VP of Creative, and sits within the Harvey Brand & Creative team. It's an opportunity to help shape one of the fastest-growing AI brands in the world while building and leading a high-performing design team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL OWN\n\n - Design execution across Harvey's activations vertical, including events, brand campaigns, partnerships, product launches, and other strategic brand initiatives.\n\n - Translating creative direction into compelling visual work across multiple projects simultaneously.\n\n - Creative feedback and design quality across the team, helping raise the standard of work through thoughtful reviews and mentorship.\n\n - Management, coaching, and development of Harvey's design team, including workload planning, career growth, and performance.\n\n - Design consistency and operational excellence across a growing volume of high-impact creative work.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner closely with Harvey's VP of Creative and peer Creative Director to bring creative concepts to life through exceptional design.\n\n - Set the visual direction for projects from early concepts through final execution, ensuring work meets a high standard of craft.\n\n - Lead and develop a team of designers through regular feedback, coaching, and creative direction.\n\n - Stay hands-on with design work when appropriate, balancing management responsibilities with individual contribution.\n\n - Partner closely with Creative Operations, Copy, Motion, and Marketing to deliver cohesive, high-quality creative work.\n\n - Drive design across Harvey's flagship events, campaigns, partnership launches, product launches, and other high-visibility initiatives.\n\n - Push work beyond the brief, helping uncover creative ideas that make campaigns memorable rather than simply well executed.\n\n - Establish effective design workflows and review processes that help the team move quickly without sacrificing quality.\n\n - Foster a culture of craft, collaboration, and continuous improvement across the design team.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in brand or creative design, with largest experience managing or mentoring designers.\n\n - A portfolio demonstrating exceptional visual craft and strong conceptual thinking across campaigns, brand work, events, or product marketing.\n\n - Experience leading design for high-visibility initiatives, including launches, activations, or integrated campaigns.\n\n - Strong creative judgment and the ability to provide clear, actionable feedback that improves both the work and the people creating it.\n\n - Experience balancing multiple complex projects while maintaining a consistently high bar for quality.\n\n - Comfort moving between leadership, creative direction, and hands-on execution depending on the needs of the project.\n   \n   \n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Experience at a high-growth B2B SaaS, AI, or enterprise technology company.\n\n - Experience designing for large-scale events or brand activations.\n\n - Experience helping build or scale a growing creative organization.\n\n - Familiarity with legal, professional services, or other complex enterprise industries.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE\n\nThe work Harvey's Brand & Creative team produces reaches many of the world's leading law firms, corporations, and professional services organizations. The campaigns, launches, and experiences we create are some of the most visible expressions of our brand.\n\nAs Head of Creative Design, you'll play a critical role in shaping how that work comes to life—leading talented designers, raising the quality of every deliverable, and helping build a creative organization capable of supporting one of the fastest-growing AI companies in the world.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$233,000-295,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LH1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$233K – $295K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$233K - $295K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"95b4d711-15b6-462d-8422-802fc91e8038","tierSummary":"$233K – $295K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"97c252fb-dbf7-4643-8500-ea7f3825b91f","summary":"$233K – $295K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":233000,"maxValue":295000},{"id":"3e53f320-7c29-458d-be7d-ad0f148df5a4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5095d504-1f57-4740-a2b1-2c8c62d6b90c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":233000,"maxValue":295000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e736b822-3d24-4c72-bf70-b8f5b2c7fad8","title":"Marketing Engineer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T18:57:24.287+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e736b822-3d24-4c72-bf70-b8f5b2c7fad8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e736b822-3d24-4c72-bf70-b8f5b2c7fad8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is the first role of its kind at Harvey — and one of the highest-leverage seats in the company. The Marketing Engineer sits at the exact point where growth strategy meets world-class AI execution: you'll take the ideas marketing bets on and turn them into shipped, compounding systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll partner directly with marketing leadership, demand gen, digital marketing, brand, product marketing, and marketing operations to spot the highest-leverage AI opportunities and ship them. Owning everything from the automation running behind the scenes to the experiments running live on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a>. It's a rare opportunity to sit at the intersection of engineering and marketing at a category-defining legal AI company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h3></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the identification, scoping, and implementation of AI and automation use cases that improve demand generation velocity, campaign operations, pipeline conversion and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain AI workflows from automated content creation to intelligent audience targeting and personalization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and deploy automation workflows (e.g., Claude, Clay, n8n, or equivalent) that eliminate manual work across the demand gen stack, integrating with Marketo, Salesforce, web CMS, and digital platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run experimentation infrastructure: A/B tests, landing pages, and conversion-flow changes, directly on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and campaign surfaces, not just backend automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the cost and efficiency of automated workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations, Content, and Performance Marketing to translate strategic marketing needs into technical solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging AI capabilities, including new models, agent frameworks, and MCP integrations, and prototype applications that give Harvey's marketing team a competitive edge.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in growth engineering, marketing engineering, GTM engineering, or a technical role within a marketing/growth function at a B2B SaaS company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building <em>with</em> AI — you use tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or equivalent as part of your daily workflow, not just as something you build on top of.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with LLM APIs or AI-powered tools to generate content, automate workflows, or optimize marketing performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with marketing automation platforms (e.g., Marketo, HubSpot), CRMs (e.g., Salesforce), workflow/automation tools (e.g., Clay, n8n, Zapier, Make), and analytics/experimentation tooling (e.g., Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, PostHog, GA4).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder mentality, comfortable operating in ambiguity, shipping iteratively, and taking ownership of 0→1 projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with the ability to design experiments, own attribution, and translate data into decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional collaboration: work closely with internal teams across data science, marketing operations, performance marketing, product marketing, and sales to ensure campaign success. Drive alignment on priorities and share insights to refine strategies.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data warehouses/BI tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building on a marketing site or product surface (landing pages, onboarding, referral or lifecycle systems).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS or AI-native company.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000-204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis is the first role of its kind at Harvey — and one of the highest-leverage seats in the company. The Marketing Engineer sits at the exact point where growth strategy meets world-class AI execution: you'll take the ideas marketing bets on and turn them into shipped, compounding systems.\n\nYou'll partner directly with marketing leadership, demand gen, digital marketing, brand, product marketing, and marketing operations to spot the highest-leverage AI opportunities and ship them. Owning everything from the automation running behind the scenes to the experiments running live on harvey.ai http://harvey.ai. It's a rare opportunity to sit at the intersection of engineering and marketing at a category-defining legal AI company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\n - Own the identification, scoping, and implementation of AI and automation use cases that improve demand generation velocity, campaign operations, pipeline conversion and more.\n\n - Build and maintain AI workflows from automated content creation to intelligent audience targeting and personalization at scale.\n\n - Design and deploy automation workflows (e.g., Claude, Clay, n8n, or equivalent) that eliminate manual work across the demand gen stack, integrating with Marketo, Salesforce, web CMS, and digital platforms.\n\n - Build and run experimentation infrastructure: A/B tests, landing pages, and conversion-flow changes, directly on harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and campaign surfaces, not just backend automation.\n\n - Manage the cost and efficiency of automated workflows.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations, Content, and Performance Marketing to translate strategic marketing needs into technical solutions.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging AI capabilities, including new models, agent frameworks, and MCP integrations, and prototype applications that give Harvey's marketing team a competitive edge.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in growth engineering, marketing engineering, GTM engineering, or a technical role within a marketing/growth function at a B2B SaaS company.\n\n - Hands-on experience building with AI — you use tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or equivalent as part of your daily workflow, not just as something you build on top of.\n\n - Experience working with LLM APIs or AI-powered tools to generate content, automate workflows, or optimize marketing performance.\n\n - Familiarity with marketing automation platforms (e.g., Marketo, HubSpot), CRMs (e.g., Salesforce), workflow/automation tools (e.g., Clay, n8n, Zapier, Make), and analytics/experimentation tooling (e.g., Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, PostHog, GA4).\n\n - A builder mentality, comfortable operating in ambiguity, shipping iteratively, and taking ownership of 0→1 projects.\n\n - Strong analytical skills with the ability to design experiments, own attribution, and translate data into decisions.\n\n - Cross-functional collaboration: work closely with internal teams across data science, marketing operations, performance marketing, product marketing, and sales to ensure campaign success. Drive alignment on priorities and share insights to refine strategies.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE \n\n - Experience with data warehouses/BI tools\n\n - Strong programming skills\n\n - Experience building on a marketing site or product surface (landing pages, onboarding, referral or lifecycle systems).\n\n - Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS or AI-native company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000-204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"04b520fb-dc85-40f4-90b8-f71c70a66e86","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"11267767-4372-4561-87f3-b77abbac5022","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"eee5ca2a-f418-47e6-a52b-5baeb09f8213","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"edbe9b1b-1adf-4819-8bd2-8e8ec88537ef","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8d42b0eb-db37-4a67-a0b2-caf2e08b91a0","title":"Marketing Engineer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T18:57:00.410+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8d42b0eb-db37-4a67-a0b2-caf2e08b91a0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8d42b0eb-db37-4a67-a0b2-caf2e08b91a0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is the first role of its kind at Harvey — and one of the highest-leverage seats in the company. The Marketing Engineer sits at the exact point where growth strategy meets world-class AI execution: you'll take the ideas marketing bets on and turn them into shipped, compounding systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll partner directly with marketing leadership, demand gen, digital marketing, brand, product marketing, and marketing operations to spot the highest-leverage AI opportunities and ship them. Owning everything from the automation running behind the scenes to the experiments running live on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a>. It's a rare opportunity to sit at the intersection of engineering and marketing at a category-defining legal AI company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h3></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the identification, scoping, and implementation of AI and automation use cases that improve demand generation velocity, campaign operations, pipeline conversion and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain AI workflows from automated content creation to intelligent audience targeting and personalization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and deploy automation workflows (e.g., Claude, Clay, n8n, or equivalent) that eliminate manual work across the demand gen stack, integrating with Marketo, Salesforce, web CMS, and digital platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run experimentation infrastructure: A/B tests, landing pages, and conversion-flow changes, directly on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and campaign surfaces, not just backend automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the cost and efficiency of automated workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations, Content, and Performance Marketing to translate strategic marketing needs into technical solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging AI capabilities, including new models, agent frameworks, and MCP integrations, and prototype applications that give Harvey's marketing team a competitive edge.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in growth engineering, marketing engineering, GTM engineering, or a technical role within a marketing/growth function at a B2B SaaS company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building <em>with</em> AI — you use tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or equivalent as part of your daily workflow, not just as something you build on top of.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with LLM APIs or AI-powered tools to generate content, automate workflows, or optimize marketing performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with marketing automation platforms (e.g., Marketo, HubSpot), CRMs (e.g., Salesforce), workflow/automation tools (e.g., Clay, n8n, Zapier, Make), and analytics/experimentation tooling (e.g., Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, PostHog, GA4).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder mentality, comfortable operating in ambiguity, shipping iteratively, and taking ownership of 0→1 projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with the ability to design experiments, own attribution, and translate data into decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional collaboration: work closely with internal teams across data science, marketing operations, performance marketing, product marketing, and sales to ensure campaign success. Drive alignment on priorities and share insights to refine strategies.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data warehouses/BI tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building on a marketing site or product surface (landing pages, onboarding, referral or lifecycle systems).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS or AI-native company.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000-204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis is the first role of its kind at Harvey — and one of the highest-leverage seats in the company. The Marketing Engineer sits at the exact point where growth strategy meets world-class AI execution: you'll take the ideas marketing bets on and turn them into shipped, compounding systems.\n\nYou'll partner directly with marketing leadership, demand gen, digital marketing, brand, product marketing, and marketing operations to spot the highest-leverage AI opportunities and ship them. Owning everything from the automation running behind the scenes to the experiments running live on harvey.ai http://harvey.ai. It's a rare opportunity to sit at the intersection of engineering and marketing at a category-defining legal AI company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\n - Own the identification, scoping, and implementation of AI and automation use cases that improve demand generation velocity, campaign operations, pipeline conversion and more.\n\n - Build and maintain AI workflows from automated content creation to intelligent audience targeting and personalization at scale.\n\n - Design and deploy automation workflows (e.g., Claude, Clay, n8n, or equivalent) that eliminate manual work across the demand gen stack, integrating with Marketo, Salesforce, web CMS, and digital platforms.\n\n - Build and run experimentation infrastructure: A/B tests, landing pages, and conversion-flow changes, directly on harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and campaign surfaces, not just backend automation.\n\n - Manage the cost and efficiency of automated workflows.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations, Content, and Performance Marketing to translate strategic marketing needs into technical solutions.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging AI capabilities, including new models, agent frameworks, and MCP integrations, and prototype applications that give Harvey's marketing team a competitive edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in growth engineering, marketing engineering, GTM engineering, or a technical role within a marketing/growth function at a B2B SaaS company.\n\n - Hands-on experience building with AI — you use tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or equivalent as part of your daily workflow, not just as something you build on top of.\n\n - Experience working with LLM APIs or AI-powered tools to generate content, automate workflows, or optimize marketing performance.\n\n - Familiarity with marketing automation platforms (e.g., Marketo, HubSpot), CRMs (e.g., Salesforce), workflow/automation tools (e.g., Clay, n8n, Zapier, Make), and analytics/experimentation tooling (e.g., Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, PostHog, GA4).\n\n - A builder mentality, comfortable operating in ambiguity, shipping iteratively, and taking ownership of 0→1 projects.\n\n - Strong analytical skills with the ability to design experiments, own attribution, and translate data into decisions.\n\n - Cross-functional collaboration: work closely with internal teams across data science, marketing operations, performance marketing, product marketing, and sales to ensure campaign success. Drive alignment on priorities and share insights to refine strategies.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE \n\n - Experience with data warehouses/BI tools\n\n - Strong programming skills\n\n - Experience building on a marketing site or product surface (landing pages, onboarding, referral or lifecycle systems).\n\n - Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS or AI-native company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000-204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"04b520fb-dc85-40f4-90b8-f71c70a66e86","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"11267767-4372-4561-87f3-b77abbac5022","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"eee5ca2a-f418-47e6-a52b-5baeb09f8213","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"edbe9b1b-1adf-4819-8bd2-8e8ec88537ef","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9fe1324c-8eeb-4138-ab85-f4d75968e48a","title":"Corporate Business Development Manager, Product","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T20:34:10.992+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9fe1324c-8eeb-4138-ab85-f4d75968e48a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9fe1324c-8eeb-4138-ab85-f4d75968e48a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Business Development team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role involves quarterbacking high-visibility, cross-functional initiatives from idea through execution. You will communicate proactively to meet the needs of our internal and external stakeholders, evaluating potential partnerships, negotiating agreements, and overseeing the integration of partner capabilities into Harvey’s offerings. You will work closely with senior stakeholders across product, finance, legal, and go-to-market functions to drive strategic initiatives and ensure successful partnership outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's product and sales strategy, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop and execute a strategic plan</strong> for partner pursuits, aligned with Harvey’s overall product and GTM strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Independently identify, evaluate, and establish a range of partnerships</strong> to enhance product functionality and GTM motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Negotiate complex partnership agreements</strong>, ensuring mutually beneficial terms and alignment with company goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Conduct quantitative analysis</strong>, create business cases, and present them to executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate closely with product, finance, legal and GTM teams</strong> to oversee the successful integration of new partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and nurture strong long-term relationships</strong> with key partners, ensuring mutual success and achievement of partnership goals and business objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operate autonomously</strong>, being both a proactive executor and strategic thinker.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years of experience</strong> in business development, product, or corporate development. Experience working at the early stage at a high-growth company, where programs are in their infancy and the partner motion is building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Proven ability to develop executive relationships</strong>, negotiate complex contracts, and problem-solve with external partners to drive distribution in new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience collaborating with product teams</strong> to develop and distribute new technology solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team player</strong> who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (Product, Legal, GTM, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission</strong> and a strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity</strong> and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Excellent communication and interpersonal skills</strong>—can influence without authority and drive urgency with empathy.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OTE 70/30 Split $200,000-260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Business Development team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.\n\nThis role involves quarterbacking high-visibility, cross-functional initiatives from idea through execution. You will communicate proactively to meet the needs of our internal and external stakeholders, evaluating potential partnerships, negotiating agreements, and overseeing the integration of partner capabilities into Harvey’s offerings. You will work closely with senior stakeholders across product, finance, legal, and go-to-market functions to drive strategic initiatives and ensure successful partnership outcomes.\n\nYour ability to articulate the value of Harvey's product and sales strategy, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and execute a strategic plan for partner pursuits, aligned with Harvey’s overall product and GTM strategy.\n\n - Independently identify, evaluate, and establish a range of partnerships to enhance product functionality and GTM motions.\n\n - Negotiate complex partnership agreements, ensuring mutually beneficial terms and alignment with company goals.\n\n - Conduct quantitative analysis, create business cases, and present them to executives.\n\n - Collaborate closely with product, finance, legal and GTM teams to oversee the successful integration of new partners.\n\n - Build and nurture strong long-term relationships with key partners, ensuring mutual success and achievement of partnership goals and business objectives.\n\n - Operate autonomously, being both a proactive executor and strategic thinker.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in business development, product, or corporate development. Experience working at the early stage at a high-growth company, where programs are in their infancy and the partner motion is building.\n\n - Proven ability to develop executive relationships, negotiate complex contracts, and problem-solve with external partners to drive distribution in new markets.\n\n - Experience collaborating with product teams to develop and distribute new technology solutions.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (Product, Legal, GTM, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and a strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment.\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills—can influence without authority and drive urgency with empathy.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nOTE 70/30 Split $200,000-260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TA1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fa2393c5-12e8-4aa6-a90c-b51f1f45cd54","tierSummary":"OTE 70/30 Split $200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fbdfb34b-b7d6-4154-9452-5a8e92b64561","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"08686265-ce55-46a5-a336-1f65991cc8ae","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d561bd1e-085a-41b0-8c13-3e99f9cd0bf7","summary":"OTE 70/30 Split $200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"a3e67f81-3c8a-443d-80d0-9f405cd5a456","title":"Corporate Business Development Manager, Product","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T20:34:14.807+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a3e67f81-3c8a-443d-80d0-9f405cd5a456","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a3e67f81-3c8a-443d-80d0-9f405cd5a456/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Business Development team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role involves quarterbacking high-visibility, cross-functional initiatives from idea through execution. You will communicate proactively to meet the needs of our internal and external stakeholders, evaluating potential partnerships, negotiating agreements, and overseeing the integration of partner capabilities into Harvey’s offerings. You will work closely with senior stakeholders across product, finance, legal, and go-to-market functions to drive strategic initiatives and ensure successful partnership outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's product and sales strategy, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop and execute a strategic plan</strong> for partner pursuits, aligned with Harvey’s overall product and GTM strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Independently identify, evaluate, and establish a range of partnerships</strong> to enhance product functionality and GTM motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Negotiate complex partnership agreements</strong>, ensuring mutually beneficial terms and alignment with company goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Conduct quantitative analysis</strong>, create business cases, and present them to executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate closely with product, finance, legal and GTM teams</strong> to oversee the successful integration of new partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and nurture strong long-term relationships</strong> with key partners, ensuring mutual success and achievement of partnership goals and business objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operate autonomously</strong>, being both a proactive executor and strategic thinker.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years of experience</strong> in business development, product, or corporate development. Experience working at the early stage at a high-growth company, where programs are in their infancy and the partner motion is building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Proven ability to develop executive relationships</strong>, negotiate complex contracts, and problem-solve with external partners to drive distribution in new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience collaborating with product teams</strong> to develop and distribute new technology solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team player</strong> who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (Product, Legal, GTM, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission</strong> and a strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity</strong> and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Excellent communication and interpersonal skills</strong>—can influence without authority and drive urgency with empathy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OTE 70/30 Split $200,000-260,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Business Development team at Harvey is responsible for enabling step-change outcomes, working in lock-step with sales and product leadership. We rapidly adapt to the changing market environment, unlock new product experiences, and deliver new business. As a member of this team, you will help us build differentiated product offerings and scalable go-to-market motions.\n\nThis role involves quarterbacking high-visibility, cross-functional initiatives from idea through execution. You will communicate proactively to meet the needs of our internal and external stakeholders, evaluating potential partnerships, negotiating agreements, and overseeing the integration of partner capabilities into Harvey’s offerings. You will work closely with senior stakeholders across product, finance, legal, and go-to-market functions to drive strategic initiatives and ensure successful partnership outcomes.\n\nYour ability to articulate the value of Harvey's product and sales strategy, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Develop and execute a strategic plan for partner pursuits, aligned with Harvey’s overall product and GTM strategy.\n\n - Independently identify, evaluate, and establish a range of partnerships to enhance product functionality and GTM motions.\n\n - Negotiate complex partnership agreements, ensuring mutually beneficial terms and alignment with company goals.\n\n - Conduct quantitative analysis, create business cases, and present them to executives.\n\n - Collaborate closely with product, finance, legal and GTM teams to oversee the successful integration of new partners.\n\n - Build and nurture strong long-term relationships with key partners, ensuring mutual success and achievement of partnership goals and business objectives.\n\n - Operate autonomously, being both a proactive executor and strategic thinker.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in business development, product, or corporate development. Experience working at the early stage at a high-growth company, where programs are in their infancy and the partner motion is building.\n\n - Proven ability to develop executive relationships, negotiate complex contracts, and problem-solve with external partners to drive distribution in new markets.\n\n - Experience collaborating with product teams to develop and distribute new technology solutions.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (Product, Legal, GTM, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and a strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment.\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills—can influence without authority and drive urgency with empathy.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nOTE 70/30 Split $200,000-260,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-TA1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fa2393c5-12e8-4aa6-a90c-b51f1f45cd54","tierSummary":"OTE 70/30 Split $200K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fbdfb34b-b7d6-4154-9452-5a8e92b64561","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"08686265-ce55-46a5-a336-1f65991cc8ae","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d561bd1e-085a-41b0-8c13-3e99f9cd0bf7","summary":"OTE 70/30 Split $200K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":260000}]}},{"id":"139f48db-e090-4716-9939-c48e5a04eaa2","title":"Head of Marketing Operations & Analytics","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T16:52:51.833+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/139f48db-e090-4716-9939-c48e5a04eaa2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/139f48db-e090-4716-9939-c48e5a04eaa2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is redefining what an AI-native marketing organization looks like, and this role designs the operating system behind it. The Head of Marketing Operations and Analytics owns the platforms, data, and automation that power Harvey's marketing engine. It's a rare shot at architecting a category-defining function with a brilliant team, an AI-native mandate, and full latitude to build it right for the long term.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build the measurement frameworks, technology stack, and reporting systems that connect every marketing dollar to pipeline and revenue, partnering closely with revenue operations, GTM systems, product marketing, and sales leadership to make Harvey's systems and operations data-driven, compliant, and efficient.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role will report directly to our Head of Demand Generation, working closely across our entire marketing team.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the marketing technology stack —</strong> evaluate, implement, and optimize tools across marketing automation, CRM, ad platforms, attribution, lead routing and enrichment, and data visualization to support a modern, AI-first operating model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead AI and automation adoption —</strong> identify and ship agentic workflows and automation that remove manual work across the funnel; go beyond piloting tools to running them in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build unified marketing analytics and reporting —</strong> attribution models, pipeline dashboards, and campaign ROI measurement that serve as a single source of truth for marketing, finance, and sales leadership, and translate into clear, actionable insight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architect lead lifecycle infrastructure —</strong> define funnel stages, scoring models, routing logic, and handoff criteria in partnership with revenue operations and sales development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own marketing data governance and compliance —</strong> ensure data quality, consent management, and privacy frameworks are built into every system and workflow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive operational excellence —</strong> build scalable workflows, automations, experimentation and optimization practices (e.g., A/B testing), and QA processes that ensure data integrity and let the team move fast without sacrificing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own budget and vendor management —</strong> manage the marketing operations budget and technology renewals, and evaluate/negotiate vendor contracts in partnership with finance and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop the team —</strong> lead and develop a high-performing global organization as Harvey scales its marketing investment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally —</strong> work with GTM systems, product marketing, customer engagement, sales leadership, and finance to align on targets, surface insights, inform investment decisions, and lead change management across a fast-moving organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing analytics, or growth operations, including 5+ years managing and developing teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, hands-on expertise in the modern B2B marketing technology stack across marketing automation, CRM, attribution tools, lead routing/enrichment, automation/orchestration platforms and data visualization tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working fluency in SQL and marketing data pipelines, with the ability to query, QA, and troubleshoot data directly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience applying AI, automation, and agentic workflows to marketing operations. You've shipped production systems, not just piloted tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building marketing analytics and attribution frameworks that connect marketing activity to pipeline and revenue in a sales-led SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning data governance, privacy, and consent frameworks for a marketing organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing marketing technology budgets and negotiating vendor contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing and developing teams in high-growth environments, ideally at fast-growing, AI-native companies familiar with modern technology stacks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional partnership and change-management skills, with demonstrated ability to align marketing, sales, finance, and systems teams around shared goals and data, and to translate complex data into clear insight for executive decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder's mindset - you have taken marketing operations infrastructure from early-stage to scaled, and you thrive in environments where you can design systems rather than inherit them.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$206,800 - $310,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is redefining what an AI-native marketing organization looks like, and this role designs the operating system behind it. The Head of Marketing Operations and Analytics owns the platforms, data, and automation that power Harvey's marketing engine. It's a rare shot at architecting a category-defining function with a brilliant team, an AI-native mandate, and full latitude to build it right for the long term.\n\nYou'll build the measurement frameworks, technology stack, and reporting systems that connect every marketing dollar to pipeline and revenue, partnering closely with revenue operations, GTM systems, product marketing, and sales leadership to make Harvey's systems and operations data-driven, compliant, and efficient.\n\nThis role will report directly to our Head of Demand Generation, working closely across our entire marketing team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the marketing technology stack — evaluate, implement, and optimize tools across marketing automation, CRM, ad platforms, attribution, lead routing and enrichment, and data visualization to support a modern, AI-first operating model.\n\n - Lead AI and automation adoption — identify and ship agentic workflows and automation that remove manual work across the funnel; go beyond piloting tools to running them in production.\n\n - Build unified marketing analytics and reporting — attribution models, pipeline dashboards, and campaign ROI measurement that serve as a single source of truth for marketing, finance, and sales leadership, and translate into clear, actionable insight.\n\n - Architect lead lifecycle infrastructure — define funnel stages, scoring models, routing logic, and handoff criteria in partnership with revenue operations and sales development.\n\n - Own marketing data governance and compliance — ensure data quality, consent management, and privacy frameworks are built into every system and workflow.\n\n - Drive operational excellence — build scalable workflows, automations, experimentation and optimization practices (e.g., A/B testing), and QA processes that ensure data integrity and let the team move fast without sacrificing quality.\n\n - Own budget and vendor management — manage the marketing operations budget and technology renewals, and evaluate/negotiate vendor contracts in partnership with finance and procurement.\n\n - Lead and develop the team — lead and develop a high-performing global organization as Harvey scales its marketing investment.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally — work with GTM systems, product marketing, customer engagement, sales leadership, and finance to align on targets, surface insights, inform investment decisions, and lead change management across a fast-moving organization.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing analytics, or growth operations, including 5+ years managing and developing teams\n\n - Deep, hands-on expertise in the modern B2B marketing technology stack across marketing automation, CRM, attribution tools, lead routing/enrichment, automation/orchestration platforms and data visualization tools\n\n - Working fluency in SQL and marketing data pipelines, with the ability to query, QA, and troubleshoot data directly.\n\n - Demonstrated experience applying AI, automation, and agentic workflows to marketing operations. You've shipped production systems, not just piloted tools.\n\n - Proven track record building marketing analytics and attribution frameworks that connect marketing activity to pipeline and revenue in a sales-led SaaS environment.\n\n - Experience owning data governance, privacy, and consent frameworks for a marketing organization.\n\n - Experience managing marketing technology budgets and negotiating vendor contracts.\n\n - Experience managing and developing teams in high-growth environments, ideally at fast-growing, AI-native companies familiar with modern technology stacks.\n\n - Strong cross-functional partnership and change-management skills, with demonstrated ability to align marketing, sales, finance, and systems teams around shared goals and data, and to translate complex data into clear insight for executive decision-making.\n\n - A builder's mindset - you have taken marketing operations infrastructure from early-stage to scaled, and you thrive in environments where you can design systems rather than inherit them.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$206,800 - $310,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$206.8K – $310.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$206.8K - $310.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"be713401-72bf-42d2-b070-b4359e79b653","tierSummary":"$206.8K – $310.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d8154e68-ee22-4980-b1f4-4bd7a6f67535","summary":"$206.8K – $310.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":206800,"maxValue":310200},{"id":"9c98ce5e-2bf0-470b-91a9-a12cd8a1bba0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c6316b9a-3c60-4189-a1c5-1882d20d8c37","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":206800,"maxValue":310200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d3020d23-b162-4552-98b5-4d9b06332ffd","title":"Head of Marketing Operations & Analytics","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T16:53:34.330+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d3020d23-b162-4552-98b5-4d9b06332ffd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d3020d23-b162-4552-98b5-4d9b06332ffd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is redefining what an AI-native marketing organization looks like, and this role designs the operating system behind it. The Head of Marketing Operations and Analytics owns the platforms, data, and automation that power Harvey's marketing engine. It's a rare shot at architecting a category-defining function with a brilliant team, an AI-native mandate, and full latitude to build it right for the long term.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build the measurement frameworks, technology stack, and reporting systems that connect every marketing dollar to pipeline and revenue, partnering closely with revenue operations, GTM systems, product marketing, and sales leadership to make Harvey's systems and operations data-driven, compliant, and efficient.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role will report directly to our Head of Demand Generation, working closely across our entire marketing team.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the marketing technology stack —</strong> evaluate, implement, and optimize tools across marketing automation, CRM, ad platforms, attribution, lead routing and enrichment, and data visualization to support a modern, AI-first operating model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead AI and automation adoption —</strong> identify and ship agentic workflows and automation that remove manual work across the funnel; go beyond piloting tools to running them in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build unified marketing analytics and reporting —</strong> attribution models, pipeline dashboards, and campaign ROI measurement that serve as a single source of truth for marketing, finance, and sales leadership, and translate into clear, actionable insight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architect lead lifecycle infrastructure —</strong> define funnel stages, scoring models, routing logic, and handoff criteria in partnership with revenue operations and sales development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own marketing data governance and compliance —</strong> ensure data quality, consent management, and privacy frameworks are built into every system and workflow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive operational excellence —</strong> build scalable workflows, automations, experimentation and optimization practices (e.g., A/B testing), and QA processes that ensure data integrity and let the team move fast without sacrificing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own budget and vendor management —</strong> manage the marketing operations budget and technology renewals, and evaluate/negotiate vendor contracts in partnership with finance and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop the team —</strong> lead and develop a high-performing global organization as Harvey scales its marketing investment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally —</strong> work with GTM systems, product marketing, customer engagement, sales leadership, and finance to align on targets, surface insights, inform investment decisions, and lead change management across a fast-moving organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing analytics, or growth operations, including 5+ years managing and developing teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, hands-on expertise in the modern B2B marketing technology stack across marketing automation, CRM, attribution tools, lead routing/enrichment, automation/orchestration platforms and data visualization tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working fluency in SQL and marketing data pipelines, with the ability to query, QA, and troubleshoot data directly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience applying AI, automation, and agentic workflows to marketing operations. You've shipped production systems, not just piloted tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building marketing analytics and attribution frameworks that connect marketing activity to pipeline and revenue in a sales-led SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning data governance, privacy, and consent frameworks for a marketing organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing marketing technology budgets and negotiating vendor contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing and developing teams in high-growth environments, ideally at fast-growing, AI-native companies familiar with modern technology stacks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional partnership and change-management skills, with demonstrated ability to align marketing, sales, finance, and systems teams around shared goals and data, and to translate complex data into clear insight for executive decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder's mindset - you have taken marketing operations infrastructure from early-stage to scaled, and you thrive in environments where you can design systems rather than inherit them.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$206,800 - $310,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is redefining what an AI-native marketing organization looks like, and this role designs the operating system behind it. The Head of Marketing Operations and Analytics owns the platforms, data, and automation that power Harvey's marketing engine. It's a rare shot at architecting a category-defining function with a brilliant team, an AI-native mandate, and full latitude to build it right for the long term.\n\nYou'll build the measurement frameworks, technology stack, and reporting systems that connect every marketing dollar to pipeline and revenue, partnering closely with revenue operations, GTM systems, product marketing, and sales leadership to make Harvey's systems and operations data-driven, compliant, and efficient.\n\nThis role will report directly to our Head of Demand Generation, working closely across our entire marketing team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the marketing technology stack — evaluate, implement, and optimize tools across marketing automation, CRM, ad platforms, attribution, lead routing and enrichment, and data visualization to support a modern, AI-first operating model.\n\n - Lead AI and automation adoption — identify and ship agentic workflows and automation that remove manual work across the funnel; go beyond piloting tools to running them in production.\n\n - Build unified marketing analytics and reporting — attribution models, pipeline dashboards, and campaign ROI measurement that serve as a single source of truth for marketing, finance, and sales leadership, and translate into clear, actionable insight.\n\n - Architect lead lifecycle infrastructure — define funnel stages, scoring models, routing logic, and handoff criteria in partnership with revenue operations and sales development.\n\n - Own marketing data governance and compliance — ensure data quality, consent management, and privacy frameworks are built into every system and workflow.\n\n - Drive operational excellence — build scalable workflows, automations, experimentation and optimization practices (e.g., A/B testing), and QA processes that ensure data integrity and let the team move fast without sacrificing quality.\n\n - Own budget and vendor management — manage the marketing operations budget and technology renewals, and evaluate/negotiate vendor contracts in partnership with finance and procurement.\n\n - Lead and develop the team — lead and develop a high-performing global organization as Harvey scales its marketing investment.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally — work with GTM systems, product marketing, customer engagement, sales leadership, and finance to align on targets, surface insights, inform investment decisions, and lead change management across a fast-moving organization.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing analytics, or growth operations, including 5+ years managing and developing teams\n\n - Deep, hands-on expertise in the modern B2B marketing technology stack across marketing automation, CRM, attribution tools, lead routing/enrichment, automation/orchestration platforms and data visualization tools\n\n - Working fluency in SQL and marketing data pipelines, with the ability to query, QA, and troubleshoot data directly.\n\n - Demonstrated experience applying AI, automation, and agentic workflows to marketing operations. You've shipped production systems, not just piloted tools.\n\n - Proven track record building marketing analytics and attribution frameworks that connect marketing activity to pipeline and revenue in a sales-led SaaS environment.\n\n - Experience owning data governance, privacy, and consent frameworks for a marketing organization.\n\n - Experience managing marketing technology budgets and negotiating vendor contracts.\n\n - Experience managing and developing teams in high-growth environments, ideally at fast-growing, AI-native companies familiar with modern technology stacks.\n\n - Strong cross-functional partnership and change-management skills, with demonstrated ability to align marketing, sales, finance, and systems teams around shared goals and data, and to translate complex data into clear insight for executive decision-making.\n\n - A builder's mindset - you have taken marketing operations infrastructure from early-stage to scaled, and you thrive in environments where you can design systems rather than inherit them.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$206,800 - $310,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$206.8K – $310.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$206.8K - $310.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b2749f55-4e6e-43a8-af68-d95554d96a92","tierSummary":"$206.8K – $310.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d8ce41f5-4093-49ba-befe-c2030f696415","summary":"$206.8K – $310.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":206800,"maxValue":310200},{"id":"85825f40-fe9e-479b-980e-c6baa002d7a5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c1f8ca81-6bf4-424e-8859-ea17b6961ff5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":206800,"maxValue":310200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d00dc18e-862b-4391-a3f1-5cd49c07f8e7","title":"Senior Software Engineer, AI Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T20:45:05.711+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d00dc18e-862b-4391-a3f1-5cd49c07f8e7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d00dc18e-862b-4391-a3f1-5cd49c07f8e7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Representative Projects</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Context Engineering &amp; Agent Infrastructure.</strong> Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Model Integration &amp; Routing.</strong> Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluation Infrastructure.</strong> Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Abstractions.</strong> Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You Have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering. Staff candidates will typically have 8+ years and a track record of technical leadership across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.\n\nThe AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Context Engineering & Agent Infrastructure. Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.\n\n - Model Integration & Routing. Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.\n\n - Evaluation Infrastructure. Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.\n\n - Shared Abstractions. Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.\n\n - Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.\n\n - Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.\n\n - Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.\n\n - Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering. Staff candidates will typically have 8+ years and a track record of technical leadership across teams.\n\n - Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.\n\n - Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.\n\n - A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.\n\n - Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.\n\n - Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.\n\n - A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.\n\n - Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"32744f3d-c4d9-4a8c-9155-abe5a2c250c7","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9465637d-fbd7-4e7e-8025-0002a486e0ba","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"90e7d6c3-ab66-4ff7-80e2-bbbd88d661aa","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"dcde0fc1-7b25-4f95-ac4c-297b351e66ca","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ebf00b72-4693-4894-b540-5f82a60fdbdc","title":"Staff Software Engineer, AI Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T20:44:57.493+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ebf00b72-4693-4894-b540-5f82a60fdbdc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ebf00b72-4693-4894-b540-5f82a60fdbdc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Projects</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Context Engineering &amp; Agent Infrastructure.</strong> Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Model Integration &amp; Routing.</strong> Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluation Infrastructure.</strong> Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Abstractions.</strong> Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering and a track record of technical leadership across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$</strong>231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s products all depend on a shared AI foundation: the model layer and agent infrastructure that determine the quality of work our agents deliver. Legal is one of the hardest domains for AI: documents run to hundreds of pages, matters can span millions of files, and there is zero margin for error on accuracy.\n\nThe AI Platform team builds the foundation that every product and agent team at Harvey builds upon. This team is early and there’s a lot to build: model routing, agent architecture, context management, evals. Your work here sets the ceiling for what Harvey’s AI can do.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROJECTS\n\n - Context Engineering & Agent Infrastructure. Build the platform-level systems for context management, session state, and memory that all of Harvey’s agents and products rely on.\n\n - Model Integration & Routing. Own the infrastructure that lets Harvey onboard new foundation models fast and route to the right one for every task - a capability every product team depends on.\n\n - Evaluation Infrastructure. Build the shared eval tooling and frameworks that let every team across Harvey measure and improve AI quality systematically.\n\n - Shared Abstractions. Create the SDKs, platform primitives, and developer tooling that make it dramatically easier for product teams to ship AI-powered features.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design and build abstractions and platform-level systems that improve all of Harvey’s agentic products.\n\n - Own infrastructure for model integration, routing, and evaluation that helps Harvey choose and deploy the right foundation model for any given context.\n\n - Build evaluation frameworks and tooling that let every team across Harvey iterate on AI quality effectively.\n\n - Partner closely with product engineering teams, PMs, and design to launch cutting-edge AI products.\n\n - Evaluate, prototype, and integrate the latest advancements in AI and agentic systems as they emerge.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of experience building backend systems, with at least 1+ year focused on AI/ML engineering and a track record of technical leadership across teams.\n\n - Experience building and shipping multi-model or multi-provider AI systems in production.\n\n - Familiarity with context management, session state, or memory systems in AI or distributed systems. You’ve thought about what the model sees and why it matters.\n\n - A track record of building internal platforms, SDKs, or shared infrastructure that other engineering teams actually adopted - and an understanding of why developer experience matters as much as raw capability.\n\n - Strong judgment about abstractions. Opinionated about good design but pragmatic about shipping incrementally.\n\n - Excitement about agentic AI and the infrastructure challenges of making autonomous systems reliable when the stakes are real.\n\n - A bias toward full ownership: you navigate ambiguity well and don’t wait for a roadmap to start solving problems.\n\n - Bonus: experience building evaluation frameworks, working with agent/function-calling architectures, familiarity with legal or other high-stakes professional services domains, or time at early-stage or hyper-growth startups where the underlying technology changes regularly.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dec73561-14a5-448b-8510-6cc97aa97812","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"68770499-1d90-489a-bb6c-096fffbed7f4","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"3e274395-e714-46d4-8ab3-95a7c8f4190c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f95dea18-478b-4057-912d-81b37994b37c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"4d5cd9d0-1ae7-49b5-b681-b2f95fb1eec0","title":"Sales Manager, Mid-Market - APAC","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T00:32:47.812+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4d5cd9d0-1ae7-49b5-b681-b2f95fb1eec0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4d5cd9d0-1ae7-49b5-b681-b2f95fb1eec0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Mid Market Sales Manager is the founding leader of Harvey's Mid-Market sales team in Singapore, responsible for building and scaling the region's commercial sales presence from the ground up. This person joins the Commercial Sales organization under Harvey's global mid-market leadership and will own the full cycle of hiring, enabling, and managing a team of Account Executives focused on mid-market law firms and corporate legal departments across the APAC region. The role drives Harvey's geographic expansion strategy by establishing a repeatable sales motion, building pipeline, and closing deals in a high-growth market. They will partner cross-functionally with Customer Success, Legal Engineering, and Solutions Architecture to deliver a world-class buyer experience in a new region. This is a rare opportunity to shape an entirely new market for one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with direct executive visibility and significant autonomy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build Harvey's Mid-Market sales team in Singapore from zero — recruit, hire, onboard, and develop a team of high-performing Account Executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and iterate on a regional sales motion and playbook tailored to APAC mid-market buyers, including territory planning, pipeline generation strategy, and deal execution frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Directly manage and coach AEs on deal strategy, qualification, negotiation, and close — operating as a player-coach in early stages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own forecasting, pipeline management, and quarterly planning for the APAC Mid-Market segment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams — Customer Success, Legal Engineering, Solutions Architecture, and Marketing — to establish Harvey's go-to-market foundation in the region</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent the voice of the APAC mid-market customer internally, informing product roadmap and regional strategy</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of B2B SaaS sales experience with at least 2 years in a front-line sales management role, ideally within legal technology, enterprise software, or a high-growth startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of building or significantly scaling a sales team in a new market or segment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to operate in ambiguous, fast-moving environments — comfortable making decisions with incomplete information and iterating rapidly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven coaching and performance management skills, with the ability to develop individual contributors and hold them accountable to high standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with the APAC legal or professional services market, including buyer personas, procurement dynamics, and regional nuances</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical mindset with strong business sense — able to think strategically about territory design, segmentation, and go-to-market priorities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Mid Market Sales Manager is the founding leader of Harvey's Mid-Market sales team in Singapore, responsible for building and scaling the region's commercial sales presence from the ground up. This person joins the Commercial Sales organization under Harvey's global mid-market leadership and will own the full cycle of hiring, enabling, and managing a team of Account Executives focused on mid-market law firms and corporate legal departments across the APAC region. The role drives Harvey's geographic expansion strategy by establishing a repeatable sales motion, building pipeline, and closing deals in a high-growth market. They will partner cross-functionally with Customer Success, Legal Engineering, and Solutions Architecture to deliver a world-class buyer experience in a new region. This is a rare opportunity to shape an entirely new market for one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with direct executive visibility and significant autonomy.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build Harvey's Mid-Market sales team in Singapore from zero — recruit, hire, onboard, and develop a team of high-performing Account Executives\n\n - Develop and iterate on a regional sales motion and playbook tailored to APAC mid-market buyers, including territory planning, pipeline generation strategy, and deal execution frameworks\n\n - Directly manage and coach AEs on deal strategy, qualification, negotiation, and close — operating as a player-coach in early stages\n\n - Own forecasting, pipeline management, and quarterly planning for the APAC Mid-Market segment\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams — Customer Success, Legal Engineering, Solutions Architecture, and Marketing — to establish Harvey's go-to-market foundation in the region\n\n - Represent the voice of the APAC mid-market customer internally, informing product roadmap and regional strategy\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of B2B SaaS sales experience with at least 2 years in a front-line sales management role, ideally within legal technology, enterprise software, or a high-growth startup\n\n - Demonstrated track record of building or significantly scaling a sales team in a new market or segment\n\n - Strong ability to operate in ambiguous, fast-moving environments — comfortable making decisions with incomplete information and iterating rapidly\n\n - Proven coaching and performance management skills, with the ability to develop individual contributors and hold them accountable to high standards\n\n - Deep familiarity with the APAC legal or professional services market, including buyer personas, procurement dynamics, and regional nuances\n\n - Analytical mindset with strong business sense — able to think strategically about territory design, segmentation, and go-to-market priorities\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-GE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"879d9051-0f20-4fcf-8e73-7293044dd7a2","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T16:44:11.173+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/879d9051-0f20-4fcf-8e73-7293044dd7a2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/879d9051-0f20-4fcf-8e73-7293044dd7a2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience.\n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AP1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4fd22d94-ebda-4f26-91b8-5331923d80dd","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0832cba2-658a-4770-8b74-3cbe68116ac9","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4deddb00-bffd-4577-afec-e628a01dc29a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"45a49603-46f3-4b27-91b9-3e664122cee0","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"af2f6c0b-f470-4f79-b2d7-3004a3dce472","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Agents","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T16:44:01.701+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/af2f6c0b-f470-4f79-b2d7-3004a3dce472","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/af2f6c0b-f470-4f79-b2d7-3004a3dce472/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Agents, you'll build the systems that make our AI agents indispensable to legal professionals.\n\nYou will design environments and actions for agentic professional work, make model selection decisions, manage context windows, create optimal tools, and develop evals that enable faster iteration loops to unlock new capabilities.\n\nWe're looking for engineers and researchers who are immersed in the space, driven to ship impactful products, and are experienced in using practical evaluations to drive task completion quality and customer delight.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with customers and PMs to understand legal workflows, design practical evaluations that capture what “excellent” means, and ship agents that get the job done.\n\n - Optimize agent performance through prompt engineering, model selection, tool design, skill writing, context window management, and eval harness development.\n\n - Work with our model infra team to design and implement infrastructure for low-latency agent execution, including caching strategies, parallel tool calls, or subagent patterns.\n\n - Improve our observability and instrumentation to profile agent behavior, identify bottlenecks, and drive optimization decisions.\n\n - Stay current on new developments in agentic systems and bring those learnings back to the products we build.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Passion for building effective domain-specific agents.\n\n - Iterative mindset: you develop proof of concepts, make decisions quickly, and ship v0s.\n\n - Comfortable with when and how to use evaluations to drive quality.\n\n - Humble and adaptable about code and frameworks. We expect you to drive adoption of new best practices as they develop.\n\n - 5-8 years (post-BS/MS) of software engineering experience.\n\n - We are hiring for this role across Mid, Senior, and Staff levels.\n\n - Proficiency in Python and experience working with LLM APIs and agent frameworks.\n\n - Experience with shipping user-facing products, either on the backend or full-stack.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AP1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"489e4048-aac4-42b0-8f7a-55178dbd0df9","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"be0e195f-a37d-4e7f-ab1d-b0ffcccd5bc4","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"f4212737-dbd3-4a3d-96f8-75699703c10d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a9bb1c17-fea5-42d7-a970-247c3adc567b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"fae2f3df-b785-4aaa-b11d-2bc328a47a48","title":"Engineering Manager, Model Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T00:08:59.705+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fae2f3df-b785-4aaa-b11d-2bc328a47a48","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fae2f3df-b785-4aaa-b11d-2bc328a47a48/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Engineering Manager for Model Infrastructure, you'll lead the team responsible for the platform powering every model request across Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external AI providers to ensure our platform remains reliable, scalable, and cost-efficient as our business grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model Infrastructure is one of Harvey's most strategic engineering organizations. Every product capability—from chat experiences and agents to document workflows and future reasoning systems—depends on this platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over the next several years, the team will evolve beyond operating third-party models to building the infrastructure that enables Harvey to train, evaluate, deploy, and operate our own frontier AI models. This role offers the opportunity to shape the technical foundation of Harvey's AI platform and build an organization that will power the company's next phase of growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and grow a high-performing team of software engineers responsible for Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the technical roadmap for model reliability, scalability, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build highly reliable systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and incident response across multiple AI providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's multi-provider model platform, including provider integrations, SDK upgrades, API migrations, and onboarding new model providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the evolution of our Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect degraded models and intelligently route traffic based on health, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end model telemetry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering to support new model launches, capacity planning, experimentation, and proactive production monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead initiatives to improve inference efficiency, reduce infrastructure costs, and increase model utilization across providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the infrastructure foundation for Harvey's future model training efforts, including data pipelines, model operations, training environments, and AI platform capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with executive leadership on long-term AI infrastructure strategy and vendor relationships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recruit, mentor, and develop exceptional engineering talent while fostering a culture of technical excellence and operational ownership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of software engineering experience, including multiple years managing high-performing engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading teams responsible for large-scale distributed systems or cloud infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical background that enables you to guide architectural decisions and mentor senior engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating highly available production services with strong reliability and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building platforms that require scalability, observability, automation, and cost optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional leadership skills with the ability to partner effectively across Engineering, Research, Product, and external vendors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to influence technical strategy across organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A passion for building teams and developing engineering talent.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple model providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source model ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building inference platforms, model gateways, traffic routing systems, or policy-based serving infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, distributed systems, and large-scale observability platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting GPU infrastructure, model training platforms, or ML infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data platforms and technologies such as Spark, Kafka, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading organizations through periods of rapid growth and technical transformation.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$260,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Engineering Manager for Model Infrastructure, you'll lead the team responsible for the platform powering every model request across Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external AI providers to ensure our platform remains reliable, scalable, and cost-efficient as our business grows.\n\nModel Infrastructure is one of Harvey's most strategic engineering organizations. Every product capability—from chat experiences and agents to document workflows and future reasoning systems—depends on this platform.\n\nOver the next several years, the team will evolve beyond operating third-party models to building the infrastructure that enables Harvey to train, evaluate, deploy, and operate our own frontier AI models. This role offers the opportunity to shape the technical foundation of Harvey's AI platform and build an organization that will power the company's next phase of growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead and grow a high-performing team of software engineers responsible for Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.\n\n - Define the technical roadmap for model reliability, scalability, and operational excellence.\n\n - Build highly reliable systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and incident response across multiple AI providers.\n\n - Own Harvey's multi-provider model platform, including provider integrations, SDK upgrades, API migrations, and onboarding new model providers.\n\n - Drive the evolution of our Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect degraded models and intelligently route traffic based on health, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.\n\n - Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end model telemetry.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering to support new model launches, capacity planning, experimentation, and proactive production monitoring.\n\n - Lead initiatives to improve inference efficiency, reduce infrastructure costs, and increase model utilization across providers.\n\n - Build the infrastructure foundation for Harvey's future model training efforts, including data pipelines, model operations, training environments, and AI platform capabilities.\n\n - Partner with executive leadership on long-term AI infrastructure strategy and vendor relationships.\n\n - Recruit, mentor, and develop exceptional engineering talent while fostering a culture of technical excellence and operational ownership.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of software engineering experience, including multiple years managing high-performing engineering teams.\n\n - Experience leading teams responsible for large-scale distributed systems or cloud infrastructure.\n\n - Strong technical background that enables you to guide architectural decisions and mentor senior engineers.\n\n - Experience operating highly available production services with strong reliability and operational excellence.\n\n - Experience building platforms that require scalability, observability, automation, and cost optimization.\n\n - Strong cross-functional leadership skills with the ability to partner effectively across Engineering, Research, Product, and external vendors.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to influence technical strategy across organizations.\n\n - A passion for building teams and developing engineering talent.\n   \n   \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.\n\n - Experience working with multiple model providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source model ecosystems.\n\n - Experience building inference platforms, model gateways, traffic routing systems, or policy-based serving infrastructure.\n\n - Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, distributed systems, and large-scale observability platforms.\n\n - Experience supporting GPU infrastructure, model training platforms, or ML infrastructure.\n\n - Familiarity with data platforms and technologies such as Spark, Kafka, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.\n\n - Experience leading organizations through periods of rapid growth and technical transformation.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$260,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$260K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$260K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"165f5486-9d60-4cdb-b347-1216ad210d12","tierSummary":"$260K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"890a67e6-d10b-4559-9075-66ea1023a784","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8326f324-9120-4131-a6aa-c63d9b0510f0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"55e1d838-4686-41c1-9606-2213bee4b300","summary":"$260K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":260000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"ef7616f0-dbf6-456b-8167-a85f1ef9b0e3","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Model Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T19:13:22.829+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ef7616f0-dbf6-456b-8167-a85f1ef9b0e3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ef7616f0-dbf6-456b-8167-a85f1ef9b0e3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.</p><h1><strong><br />What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Build </strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll help build the core platform behind Harvey's AI capabilities, including:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Model Reliability &amp; Operations</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated failover and recovery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity provisioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational tooling and incident automation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Unified Model Controller (UMC)</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Policy-based model routing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intelligent Model Selector</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Traffic management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliability and latency optimization</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Provider Platform</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multi-provider architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">API and SDK integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rapid adoption of new frontier models</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Observability &amp; Cost Platform</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Token usage analytics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cost attribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Latency and reliability dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilization optimization</p></li></ul><h3><strong>AI Platform Foundation</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Infrastructure supporting model evaluation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model deployment and operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Future model training platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agent infrastructure and CcaaS</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating highly available production services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$236,000 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.\n\n - Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.\n\n - Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.\n\n - Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.\n\n - Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.\n\n - Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.\n\n - Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.\n\n - Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.\n\n - Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BUILD \n\nYou'll help build the core platform behind Harvey's AI capabilities, including:\n\n\n\n\nMODEL RELIABILITY & OPERATIONS\n\n - Model health monitoring\n\n - Automated failover and recovery\n\n - Capacity provisioning\n\n - Operational tooling and incident automation\n\n\nUNIFIED MODEL CONTROLLER (UMC)\n\n - Policy-based model routing\n\n - Intelligent Model Selector\n\n - Model health monitoring\n\n - Traffic management\n\n - Reliability and latency optimization\n\n\nPROVIDER PLATFORM\n\n - Multi-provider architecture\n\n - API and SDK integrations\n\n - OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers\n\n - Rapid adoption of new frontier models\n\n\nOBSERVABILITY & COST PLATFORM\n\n - Token usage analytics\n\n - Cost attribution\n\n - Latency and reliability dashboards\n\n - Capacity forecasting\n\n - Utilization optimization\n\n\nAI PLATFORM FOUNDATION\n\n - Infrastructure supporting model evaluation\n\n - Model deployment and operations\n\n - Future model training platform\n\n - Agent infrastructure and CcaaS\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.\n\n - Experience designing and operating highly available production services.\n\n - Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.\n\n - Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.\n\n - Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.\n\n - Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\n - Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.\n\n - Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.\n\n - Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.\n\n - Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.\n\n - Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.\n\n - Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.\n\n - Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$236,000 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$236K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$236K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e97b4d29-98e6-472f-a2f0-a26f2c29f440","tierSummary":"$236K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"bf750449-33ed-442d-b7a6-2d56e87fad06","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1b37a361-3edb-425d-858b-cac6ea1c3313","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d1676ed4-a661-42e0-b84c-1c74ff3d4f84","summary":"$236K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":236000,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":236000,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"7aecc883-f979-43fa-afbb-65def674f556","title":"Senior or Staff User Researcher","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-21T00:30:12.266+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7aecc883-f979-43fa-afbb-65def674f556","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7aecc883-f979-43fa-afbb-65def674f556/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the future of AI for legal professionals, and understanding our users is core to how we do that. We are looking for a seasoned strategic <strong>User Researcher</strong> to to join our research function. You are a senior individual contributor who drives high-impact research across multiple teams or a major product area. You move beyond single studies to shape problem definition, influence roadmaps, and elevate research quality through strong craft and partnership. You are comfortable with AI technologies and excited to build research and insight tooling to accelerate our workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success looks like teams meaningfully change direction based on your insights and influencing roadmap, research quality improves in the teams you support, and you are trusted as a strategic partner and moves at speed, where Harvey builds shared conviction around user truths.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role directly reports to the Head of User Research and focuses on accelerating the quality and speed at which Harvey ships user-centered AI products. You have the opportunity to co-create tooling or identify the right capabilities to strengthen our research practice. You'll partner closely with research and design leadership, cross-functional stakeholders that keep research and insights running at peak efficiency.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company shapes its products from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Complex Research Programs</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own research strategy for a product area or cross-team initiative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute end-to-end qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify patterns across studies and connect insights to product decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research how legal professionals work with Harvey and outside of the platform. Translate that into product and design recommendations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape Product Thinking</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product Managers and Designers to frame the right problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence roadmaps by surfacing unmet user needs, risks, and opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push teams beyond validation toward deeper discovery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop strong legal domain expertise and excited to become an expert in both the Harvey product and the legal industry</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the Bar on Craft</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Produce clear, compelling synthesis and storytelling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify where AI reduces friction in research process and comfortable building custom scripts, integrations, or AI agents where off-the-shelf tools fall short</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model strong research rigor, ethics, and judgment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to prototype and ship research insight tooling improvements yourself before pulling in Eng support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate as a Trusted Partner</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring rigor to ambiguous, fast-moving problem spaces where the underlying technology (and user expectations of it) shift quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence without authority across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help partners develop stronger research instincts</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of user research experience of digital products in fast-paced, high-growth or technically complex environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Psychology, Human-Computer Interaction, Human Factors, Cognitive Science, or a related field required. Advanced degree preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record or portfolio of portfolio-level impact. Experience conducting and defining user research methodologies, integrating qualitative and quantitative insights into design and product strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to navigate and simplify multifaceted, ambiguous problem spaces while maintaining a high bar for execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional storytelling and communication skills—capable of influencing cross-functional partners and aligning diverse perspectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or customizing internal tooling (Zapier workflows, Claude skills, Notion workflows, and custom GPTs or research agents) to support insight acceleration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong design and product judgment and business acumen. Ability to engage deeply in design critiques and dedicated product area roadmap reviews to contribute insights into planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, low-ego approach that helps teams move quickly, thoughtfully, and inclusively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience researching AI-powered technology products, and understand how to assess experiences and quality of conversational products.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$158,500 - $264,500</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-MV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the future of AI for legal professionals, and understanding our users is core to how we do that. We are looking for a seasoned strategic User Researcher to to join our research function. You are a senior individual contributor who drives high-impact research across multiple teams or a major product area. You move beyond single studies to shape problem definition, influence roadmaps, and elevate research quality through strong craft and partnership. You are comfortable with AI technologies and excited to build research and insight tooling to accelerate our workflows.\n\nSuccess looks like teams meaningfully change direction based on your insights and influencing roadmap, research quality improves in the teams you support, and you are trusted as a strategic partner and moves at speed, where Harvey builds shared conviction around user truths.\n\nThis role directly reports to the Head of User Research and focuses on accelerating the quality and speed at which Harvey ships user-centered AI products. You have the opportunity to co-create tooling or identify the right capabilities to strengthen our research practice. You'll partner closely with research and design leadership, cross-functional stakeholders that keep research and insights running at peak efficiency.\n\nIt's a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company shapes its products from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nLead Complex Research Programs\n\n - Own research strategy for a product area or cross-team initiative\n\n - Design and execute end-to-end qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research\n\n - Identify patterns across studies and connect insights to product decisions\n\n - Research how legal professionals work with Harvey and outside of the platform. Translate that into product and design recommendations.\n\nShape Product Thinking\n\n - Partner closely with Product Managers and Designers to frame the right problems\n\n - Influence roadmaps by surfacing unmet user needs, risks, and opportunities\n\n - Push teams beyond validation toward deeper discovery\n\n - Develop strong legal domain expertise and excited to become an expert in both the Harvey product and the legal industry\n\nRaise the Bar on Craft\n\n - Produce clear, compelling synthesis and storytelling\n\n - Identify where AI reduces friction in research process and comfortable building custom scripts, integrations, or AI agents where off-the-shelf tools fall short\n\n - Model strong research rigor, ethics, and judgment\n\n - Ability to prototype and ship research insight tooling improvements yourself before pulling in Eng support\n\nOperate as a Trusted Partner\n\n - Bring rigor to ambiguous, fast-moving problem spaces where the underlying technology (and user expectations of it) shift quickly\n\n - Influence without authority across teams\n\n - Help partners develop stronger research instincts\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of user research experience of digital products in fast-paced, high-growth or technically complex environments\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Psychology, Human-Computer Interaction, Human Factors, Cognitive Science, or a related field required. Advanced degree preferred\n\n - Track record or portfolio of portfolio-level impact. Experience conducting and defining user research methodologies, integrating qualitative and quantitative insights into design and product strategy.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to navigate and simplify multifaceted, ambiguous problem spaces while maintaining a high bar for execution.\n\n - Exceptional storytelling and communication skills—capable of influencing cross-functional partners and aligning diverse perspectives.\n\n - Experience building or customizing internal tooling (Zapier workflows, Claude skills, Notion workflows, and custom GPTs or research agents) to support insight acceleration.\n\n - Strong design and product judgment and business acumen. Ability to engage deeply in design critiques and dedicated product area roadmap reviews to contribute insights into planning.\n\n - A collaborative, low-ego approach that helps teams move quickly, thoughtfully, and inclusively\n\n - Experience researching AI-powered technology products, and understand how to assess experiences and quality of conversational products.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$158,500 - $264,500\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-MV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$158.5K – $264.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$158.5K - $264.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"015b9531-9e2f-4660-bac6-30912ceeee3f","tierSummary":"$158.5K – $264.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"bcba3f0c-4313-41fd-96a8-2c896aa3d6a9","summary":"$158.5K – $264.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":158500,"maxValue":264500},{"id":"3555aa69-cdc1-40a8-9944-7c561616b7e1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2a07e7fc-b7d8-4295-843c-1f949c97b582","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":158500,"maxValue":264500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"08d3d70d-80a6-429d-8a27-d5efd41372f5","title":"Sales Development Representative","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T18:14:37.845+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08d3d70d-80a6-429d-8a27-d5efd41372f5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08d3d70d-80a6-429d-8a27-d5efd41372f5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving growth and success of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for supporting the Sales team in driving pipeline, qualifying and establishing relationships with inbound outreach from law and other professional services firms, as well as in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost work product quality. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies and rigorous work ethic will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and channels and a highly personalized approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source new sales opportunities through inbound and outbound outreach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and distribute inbound leads, ensuring prompt follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualify leads through tailored evaluations, including product demonstrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Account Executives with administrative tasks to ensure smooth sales procedures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to developing our sales playbook and document learnings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed qualified lead targets and key sales metrics.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$110,000 OTE, 80/20 split</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving growth and success of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for supporting the Sales team in driving pipeline, qualifying and establishing relationships with inbound outreach from law and other professional services firms, as well as in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost work product quality. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies and rigorous work ethic will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and channels and a highly personalized approach\n\n - Source new sales opportunities through inbound and outbound outreach.\n\n - Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies.\n\n - Manage and distribute inbound leads, ensuring prompt follow-up.\n\n - Qualify leads through tailored evaluations, including product demonstrations.\n\n - Support Account Executives with administrative tasks to ensure smooth sales procedures.\n\n - Contribute to developing our sales playbook and document learnings.\n\n - Achieve and exceed qualified lead targets and key sales metrics.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 1-2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.\n\n - Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.\n\n - Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.\n\n - Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.\n\n - Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.\n\n - Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$110,000 OTE, 80/20 split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$110K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$110K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"110c56bb-c57b-480c-816f-d84114c9d27d","tierSummary":"80/20 Split OTE $110K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"542cc36c-5fd8-4fad-8569-47d8bbee4f3e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1328aa3b-b685-4a54-9cc2-32461b8c580b","summary":"80/20 Split OTE $110K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":110000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":110000}]}},{"id":"284a0861-026b-45ff-a4ad-c2d187d7184d","title":"Analyst, Customer Trust","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T21:36:49.353+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/284a0861-026b-45ff-a4ad-c2d187d7184d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/284a0861-026b-45ff-a4ad-c2d187d7184d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer &amp; AE Partnership:</strong> Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-Powered Automation:</strong> Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metrics &amp; Reporting:</strong> Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sales Enablement &amp; Thought Leadership:</strong> Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$94,500 - $141,700 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.\n\nOur customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.\n\nIn this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Customer & AE Partnership: Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.\n\n - AI-Powered Automation: Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.\n\n - Metrics & Reporting: Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.\n\n - Sales Enablement & Thought Leadership: Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.\n\n - Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.\n\n - Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.\n\n - Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - 1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).\n\n - Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$94,500 - $141,700 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$94.5K – $141.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$94.5K - $141.7K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"72ce2d78-6ee9-4eb2-ae66-d6ee1aa97102","tierSummary":"$94.5K – $141.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d9d821c2-ce1a-4d12-b82c-ec622b6787fc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fafffe15-608b-493b-ae54-45d1bfb8e285","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"733ff963-188f-4ea8-aca0-aaa982799964","summary":"$94.5K – $141.7K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":94500,"maxValue":141700}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":94500,"maxValue":141700}]}},{"id":"1cf585c3-27e2-4813-ade9-dc8c53c2d5b0","title":"Analyst, Customer Trust","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T21:38:26.550+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1cf585c3-27e2-4813-ade9-dc8c53c2d5b0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1cf585c3-27e2-4813-ade9-dc8c53c2d5b0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer &amp; AE Partnership:</strong> Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-Powered Automation:</strong> Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metrics &amp; Reporting:</strong> Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sales Enablement &amp; Thought Leadership:</strong> Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$94,500 - $141,700 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.\n\nOur customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.\n\nIn this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Customer & AE Partnership: Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.\n\n - AI-Powered Automation: Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.\n\n - Metrics & Reporting: Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.\n\n - Sales Enablement & Thought Leadership: Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.\n\n - Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.\n\n - Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.\n\n - Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - 1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).\n\n - Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$94,500 - $141,700 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$94.5K – $141.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$94.5K - $141.7K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f120f0a6-8d31-4a65-ac7a-9218c85a4a66","tierSummary":"$94.5K – $141.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7afac4cd-b709-4bdd-b48c-a6204e30e918","summary":"$94.5K – $141.7K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":94500,"maxValue":141700},{"id":"79e6eade-3063-4a18-b0f5-51832e1243cd","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a6911688-955f-49bd-8ad1-b1a685faecbc","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":94500,"maxValue":141700},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8caa7beb-d41c-4802-a23d-4e72b6838f13","title":"Analyst, Customer Trust","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T21:31:40.181+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8caa7beb-d41c-4802-a23d-4e72b6838f13","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8caa7beb-d41c-4802-a23d-4e72b6838f13/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer &amp; AE Partnership:</strong> Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-Powered Automation:</strong> Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metrics &amp; Reporting:</strong> Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sales Enablement &amp; Thought Leadership:</strong> Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KV1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey’s AI capabilities to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale and efficiency. Harvey allows high-performing professionals to gain deep domain knowledge faster, understand the big picture, and tackle more complex challenges in less time.\n\nOur customers depend on us to deliver a secure, trustworthy, and compliant platform. Earning the trust of our customers is a business enabler and we value it more than anything else.\n\nIn this role, you will report to the Customer Trust lead. You will drive company growth by addressing customer security inquiries, supporting our Go-To-Market (GTM) team with accurate and timely responses, and elevating our overall security posture. You will operate at the intersection of technical security, customer success, audit, and AI innovation, leveraging Harvey’s own tools to improve the speed, automation, and accuracy of our responses. This is a unique opportunity to shape the customer trust narrative, manage our Trust Center, and empower Harvey to win complex deals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Customer & AE Partnership: Act as a technical point of contact for our Go-To-Market (GTM) team and customers regarding security questions. Provide timely, accurate, and empathetic responses to questionnaires and concerns, ensuring we answer customer questions and unblock deals while maintaining high security standards.\n\n - AI-Powered Automation: Leverage AI and Harvey’s internal tools to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of our response process. Build scalable workflows to reduce manual overhead and improve response times while optimizing quality.\n\n - Metrics & Reporting: Establish and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for the Customer Trust function. Use data to track team impact, response velocity, quality of answers, and the influence of trust on sales outcomes.\n\n - Sales Enablement & Thought Leadership: Manage our Trust Center, create and maintain a high-quality security and regulatory knowledge base, and help develop thought leadership supporting our GTM teams to handle complex security discussions.\n\n - Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner closely with Product Security, Legal, and GTM/Sales to align on security positioning, product roadmaps, and evolving customer requirements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Information Security, Customer Trust, Technical Program Management, or Security Consulting, with a proven track record of supporting and improving compliance programs.\n\n - Audit Experience: You are comfortable navigating complex compliance frameworks and communicating those controls and capabilities to customers as needed.\n\n - Exceptional customer/client service skills. You are adept at understanding the \"why\" behind customer concerns and can communicate complex technical and regulatory topics to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - 1-2+ years of experience leveraging AI models or automation to drive program efficiencies (e.g., automating knowledge base management or response drafting).\n\n - Strong analytical skills with a focus on metrics. You are comfortable creating dashboards and reporting on functional performance to leadership.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a high level of patience and the ability to remain calm and decisive under pressure.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-KV1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d406ece5-f7c9-471c-89f0-9482ba703095","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market (Italian Speaker)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-21T13:03:25.811+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d406ece5-f7c9-471c-89f0-9482ba703095","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d406ece5-f7c9-471c-89f0-9482ba703095/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role  Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3>#LI-KS1</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE  OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology. \n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently. \n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n\n#LI-KS1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1ef68ef0-a2e6-4214-93a1-cabab1c85b86","title":" Majors Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-21T15:10:43.081+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1ef68ef0-a2e6-4214-93a1-cabab1c85b86","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1ef68ef0-a2e6-4214-93a1-cabab1c85b86/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 25% of the time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in management consulting or technology advisory at a top tier management consulting firm, or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Majors Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our largest customers through their journey with Harvey and defining the future of work at elite law firms, Fortune 500 companies and premier asset managers. This position is pivotal in ensuring our customers not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes, providing expert industry advice and shaping Harvey’s product roadmap.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for customers with a prescriptive and consultative approach and as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into daily workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Proactively and strategically manage overall account health by monitoring key indicators, addressing risks early and driving initiatives that support long-term customer success and retention.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and collaborate with Legal Product Specialists to enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Direct stakeholder engagement and facilitate executive engagement, transforming customers into Harvey champions within their organizations.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay customer insights to our internal teams and collaborate with Product to aid in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n - Travel required: Up to 25% of the time\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Background in management consulting or technology advisory at a top tier management consulting firm, or strategic customer success/account management experience in an Enterprise SaaS or legal (big law or in-house or in-house) environment\n\n - History and comfort conducting change management and wide-scale adoption for large technology projects.\n\n - Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, and a capability of influencing stakeholders at every level, including at the executive level.\n\n - Results driven mindset and the ability to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - A strong commitment to be collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our customers' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n - $180,000-$210,000 OTE with an 80/20 split\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-GK1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $210K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ea869777-667a-4b2e-9922-bdd116a86c42","tierSummary":"OTE 80/20 Split $180K – $210K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3f6e120a-3700-4abc-8f69-1e1510a68615","summary":"OTE 80/20 Split $180K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"id":"7ae18169-905c-402f-bcdd-48a49a625775","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"42e57a87-9dcb-4858-b840-ed607003d8fc","title":"Legal Engineer, Sydney","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sydney","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.476+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Australia","addressLocality":"Sydney"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/42e57a87-9dcb-4858-b840-ed607003d8fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/42e57a87-9dcb-4858-b840-ed607003d8fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Role Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey’s Legal Engineers are former practising lawyers who bridge customers, sales, and product to support all aspects of our sales strategy and product development. As trusted advisors to the lawyers they work with, they lead sharp discovery and tailored product demonstrations, translating real legal work into Harvey solutions that provide clear value for lawyers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As strategic partners to law firms and in-house teams, Legal Engineers thrive in ambiguity and help lawyers do higher-quality work faster and with more confidence using Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You’ll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with lawyers at current and prospective customers to uncover workflow pain points, recommend solutions, and show how Harvey fits into real legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the voice of the customer, translating feedback and legal workflow insights into concrete, lawyer-ready product direction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product, engineering, sales, and marketing to shape Harvey’s roadmap and ensure the product evolves in ways lawyers trust and adopt.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine product demonstrations, workflows, and use cases that reflect how legal teams actually work, including how AI is changing that work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce new capabilities in a way that’s tailored, credible, and compelling for each customer, continuously raising the bar for how Harvey is deployed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide competitive and market intelligence specific to the APAC legal tech landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Further strengthen Harvey’s reputation in the APAC region as a credible, substantive, and forward-looking AI partner to the legal industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>What You Have</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You move confidently through uncertainty, you operate at speed, and ship solutions that work—iterating quickly with lawyers, sales teams, and product partners to help Harvey and its customers win. You bring deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, a bias towards action, and the creativity to solve problems nobody's cracked yet.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in Sydney and eligible to work in Australia.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Australian practising certificate (or equivalent common-law qualification).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience as a qualified lawyer at a top-tier law firm (e.g., Band 1 Chambers / AFR Top 10) and/or/in-house with strong exposure to complex legal workflows and client expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and make confident, well-reasoned recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate seamlessly across legal, product, and sales contexts—translating between stakeholders with clarity and precision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with comfort engaging partners, senior associates, in-house counsel, and legal leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales, customer-facing, or law firm business development experience is a plus, particularly where you’ve helped shape solutions rather than just present them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>Additional Information</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work eligibility:</strong> Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Structured hybrid working arrangement:</strong> 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Coverage:</strong> Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family &amp; Fertility Support:</strong> Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Retirement &amp; Security:</strong> Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Paid Leave:</strong> Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Perks:</strong> Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Development:</strong> Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote Work Allowance:</strong> Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Harvey Holiday:</strong> After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GW1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey’s Legal Engineers are former practising lawyers who bridge customers, sales, and product to support all aspects of our sales strategy and product development. As trusted advisors to the lawyers they work with, they lead sharp discovery and tailored product demonstrations, translating real legal work into Harvey solutions that provide clear value for lawyers.\n\nAs strategic partners to law firms and in-house teams, Legal Engineers thrive in ambiguity and help lawyers do higher-quality work faster and with more confidence using Harvey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Work directly with lawyers at current and prospective customers to uncover workflow pain points, recommend solutions, and show how Harvey fits into real legal work.\n\n - Serve as the voice of the customer, translating feedback and legal workflow insights into concrete, lawyer-ready product direction.\n\n - Partner closely with product, engineering, sales, and marketing to shape Harvey’s roadmap and ensure the product evolves in ways lawyers trust and adopt.\n\n - Build and refine product demonstrations, workflows, and use cases that reflect how legal teams actually work, including how AI is changing that work.\n\n - Introduce new capabilities in a way that’s tailored, credible, and compelling for each customer, continuously raising the bar for how Harvey is deployed.\n\n - Provide competitive and market intelligence specific to the APAC legal tech landscape.\n\n - Further strengthen Harvey’s reputation in the APAC region as a credible, substantive, and forward-looking AI partner to the legal industry.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nYou move confidently through uncertainty, you operate at speed, and ship solutions that work—iterating quickly with lawyers, sales teams, and product partners to help Harvey and its customers win. You bring deep curiosity about AI's potential to transform legal work, a bias towards action, and the creativity to solve problems nobody's cracked yet.\n\n - Based in Sydney and eligible to work in Australia.\n\n - Australian practising certificate (or equivalent common-law qualification).\n\n - At least 3 years of experience as a qualified lawyer at a top-tier law firm (e.g., Band 1 Chambers / AFR Top 10) and/or/in-house with strong exposure to complex legal workflows and client expectations.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and make confident, well-reasoned recommendations.\n\n - Ability to operate seamlessly across legal, product, and sales contexts—translating between stakeholders with clarity and precision.\n\n - Executive presence and relationship-building skills, with comfort engaging partners, senior associates, in-house counsel, and legal leadership.\n\n - Sales, customer-facing, or law firm business development experience is a plus, particularly where you’ve helped shape solutions rather than just present them.\n   \n   \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home.\n\n - Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.\n\n - Family & Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.\n\n - Retirement & Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.\n\n - Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.\n\n - Wellness & Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.\n\n - Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.\n\n - Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.\n\n - Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-GW1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fb8e9cea-b698-4261-9ffd-5ce7a39d4a85","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Milan","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T07:18:06.775+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fb8e9cea-b698-4261-9ffd-5ce7a39d4a85","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fb8e9cea-b698-4261-9ffd-5ce7a39d4a85/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients across Italy, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in English and Italian, both spoken and written</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients across Italy, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Fluency in English and Italian, both spoken and written\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-SH1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b288350c-f942-4b1f-b5b2-be36a70ac683","title":"Technology Enablement Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T22:02:06.521+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b288350c-f942-4b1f-b5b2-be36a70ac683","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b288350c-f942-4b1f-b5b2-be36a70ac683/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows\n\n - Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content\n\n - Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI\n\n - Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts\n\n - Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management\n\n - Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)\n\n - Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences\n\n - Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders\n\n - Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"58ba06e8-82ae-4075-a584-db2f67676e99","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d8a84f2a-7a52-4f6c-a091-82d22503c280","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"id":"1a571f3e-5b8c-43fe-abb7-37b087bd752f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8f2d11c2-343c-4559-8ef1-174e55368575","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"dca79fa6-502e-4ded-96b9-a39fd1707e03","title":"Technology Enablement Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T22:01:58.585+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dca79fa6-502e-4ded-96b9-a39fd1707e03","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dca79fa6-502e-4ded-96b9-a39fd1707e03/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Technology Enablement Analyst joins Harvey's Technical Program Management team to drive how internal teams adopt, integrate, and realize value from enterprise technology platforms. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's rapidly scaling workforce has frictionless access to the tools and systems that power their work, bridging the gap between BizTech and organizational productivity. This role is accountable for turning complex technical programs into clear, actionable enablement plans that different teams can execute against. They will own stakeholder alignment, rollout strategy, and ongoing iteration based on feedback and metrics. They will partner closely with product, engineering, customer success, and go-to-market teams to ensure that documentation, training, and communications effectively support behavior change at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end enablement strategy for major internal technology initiatives, with an emphasis on internal AI tooling and related workflows\n\n - Monitor adoption, usage, and feedback, and use those insights to iterate on enablement plans, documentation, and training content\n\n - Plan and execute change management activities (e.g., communications, training, office hours) that drive adoption and sustained usage of new tools and processes\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and reports that provide leadership with visibility into technology health, utilization, and ROI\n\n - Partner with all BizTech teams to evaluate new tools, drive integrations, and ensure smooth rollouts\n\n - Develop process documentation, runbooks, and training materials to support technology onboarding and change management\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - At least 5 years of experience in technology‑enabled program delivery, technical training, or organization change management\n\n - Demonstrated track record leading change across multiple teams or functions (e.g., rolling out new tools, workflows, or processes)\n\n - Background in technology enablement, organization change management, or as a technical trainer, with comfort translating complex concepts for non‑technical audiences\n\n - Experience designing and maintaining program documentation or enablement materials as a single source of truth for diverse stakeholders\n\n - Strong stakeholder management skills, including partnering with product, engineering, operations, and go‑to‑market teams to drive measurable outcomes (e.g., higher adoption of internal AI tooling and new workflows, reduced support tickets, improved time‑to‑proficiency for end users)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4e815912-3bb9-47d9-863c-346d0dbbdbdf","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fd913fb7-442c-4478-8bc0-20fdfcff7e2c","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"id":"f65768e1-8440-423a-9b9d-9511709dc851","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"047635ca-aa24-4a9d-9f4a-68afaf5a8484","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"808dd9dc-8c79-4435-9e07-badc3f8c0d01","title":"Head of Technical Accounting and Reporting","department":"Finance","team":"Accounting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-04T22:01:35.641+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/808dd9dc-8c79-4435-9e07-badc3f8c0d01","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/808dd9dc-8c79-4435-9e07-badc3f8c0d01/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Head of Technical Accounting and Reporting will own technical accounting, financial reporting, and internal controls in a dynamic, multi-product SaaS environment. This role is highly cross-functional, partnering closely with the Product, Sales, Legal, Partnerships, Revenue Accounting, Corporate Accounting and StratFin teams to ensure that new products, pricing structures, and commercial arrangements are accounted for accurately and in accordance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS. This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who thrives in a fast-paced, evolving business, can bring structure and scalability to accounting operations, and can help lay the groundwork for future public-company readiness.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h3><strong>Technical Accounting</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the company's subject matter expert on complex accounting matters, researching and documenting positions in accordance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare clear, well-reasoned technical accounting memos on significant and non-routine transactions, including business combinations, equity and stock-based compensation, leases, and revenue arrangements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams, including Product, Sales, Legal, and Partnerships, to assess the accounting implications of new partnerships, products, pricing structures, and other arrangements, and work with the Corporate and Revenue accounting teams to operationalize the accounting, and systematization of the accounting, for new agreements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor, assess, and implement new accounting standards and pronouncements, communicating the impact to senior management and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with external auditors and external technical accounting consultants to support the timely resolution of technical accounting questions and audit inquiries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the accounting impact of differences between U.S. GAAP and IFRS relevant to the company’s operations, including any dual-reporting, statutory, or foreign-subsidiary reporting requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the company’s accounting policies and design and implementation of related controls including leases, stock-based compensation, business combinations, and revenue recognition (standalone selling price methodology, allocation of transaction price across performance obligations, and the timing and pattern of revenue recognition).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assess material complex and non-standard contracts, including custom terms, usage-based pricing, and partner/reseller arrangements, and partner with the Revenue Accounting team to operationalize technical conclusions.<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Financial Reporting and Controls</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the preparation and review of internal and external financial statements, including footnote disclosures, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and compliance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and maintain a scalable internal control environment, including documentation of key processes and controls, in preparation for future public-company readiness and SOX compliance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical accounting and reporting workstreams in support of IPO readiness, including preparation of registration statement disclosures, coordination with underwriters and auditors, and remediation of legacy accounting positions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close processes, driving improvements in accuracy, efficiency, and timeliness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain accounting policies and procedures, ensuring consistent application across the organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare reporting and analysis for senior leadership, the board, investors, and lenders as needed.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15+ years of progressive accounting experience, including a combination of public accounting (Big 4 preferred) and industry experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, current expertise in U.S. GAAP (including ASC 606 revenue recognition), with working knowledge of IFRS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a SaaS, technology, or other high-growth environment strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with technical accounting research and the preparation of technical memos on complex, non-routine transactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of internal controls and SOX, with experience supporting IPO readiness or public-company reporting a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of technical accounting across areas such as business combinations, equity and stock-based compensation, leases, and revenue recognition.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Key Competencies</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex technical matters into clear, actionable guidance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, comfortable partnering with both finance and non-finance stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A hands-on, roll-up-your-sleeves mindset, with the ability to balance technical rigor against the practical needs of a fast-moving business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build scalable processes and controls in an evolving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High degree of ownership, integrity, and attention to detail.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$224,000 - $336,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Head of Technical Accounting and Reporting will own technical accounting, financial reporting, and internal controls in a dynamic, multi-product SaaS environment. This role is highly cross-functional, partnering closely with the Product, Sales, Legal, Partnerships, Revenue Accounting, Corporate Accounting and StratFin teams to ensure that new products, pricing structures, and commercial arrangements are accounted for accurately and in accordance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS. This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who thrives in a fast-paced, evolving business, can bring structure and scalability to accounting operations, and can help lay the groundwork for future public-company readiness.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nTECHNICAL ACCOUNTING\n\n - Serve as the company's subject matter expert on complex accounting matters, researching and documenting positions in accordance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS.\n\n - Prepare clear, well-reasoned technical accounting memos on significant and non-routine transactions, including business combinations, equity and stock-based compensation, leases, and revenue arrangements.\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams, including Product, Sales, Legal, and Partnerships, to assess the accounting implications of new partnerships, products, pricing structures, and other arrangements, and work with the Corporate and Revenue accounting teams to operationalize the accounting, and systematization of the accounting, for new agreements.\n\n - Monitor, assess, and implement new accounting standards and pronouncements, communicating the impact to senior management and other stakeholders.\n\n - Partner with external auditors and external technical accounting consultants to support the timely resolution of technical accounting questions and audit inquiries.\n\n - Evaluate the accounting impact of differences between U.S. GAAP and IFRS relevant to the company’s operations, including any dual-reporting, statutory, or foreign-subsidiary reporting requirements.\n\n - Own the company’s accounting policies and design and implementation of related controls including leases, stock-based compensation, business combinations, and revenue recognition (standalone selling price methodology, allocation of transaction price across performance obligations, and the timing and pattern of revenue recognition).\n\n - Assess material complex and non-standard contracts, including custom terms, usage-based pricing, and partner/reseller arrangements, and partner with the Revenue Accounting team to operationalize technical conclusions.\n   \n\n\nFINANCIAL REPORTING AND CONTROLS\n\n - Own the preparation and review of internal and external financial statements, including footnote disclosures, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and compliance with U.S. GAAP and, where applicable, IFRS.\n\n - Design, implement, and maintain a scalable internal control environment, including documentation of key processes and controls, in preparation for future public-company readiness and SOX compliance.\n\n - Lead technical accounting and reporting workstreams in support of IPO readiness, including preparation of registration statement disclosures, coordination with underwriters and auditors, and remediation of legacy accounting positions.\n\n - Support the month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close processes, driving improvements in accuracy, efficiency, and timeliness.\n\n - Develop and maintain accounting policies and procedures, ensuring consistent application across the organization.\n\n - Prepare reporting and analysis for senior leadership, the board, investors, and lenders as needed.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA required.\n\n - 15+ years of progressive accounting experience, including a combination of public accounting (Big 4 preferred) and industry experience.\n\n - Deep, current expertise in U.S. GAAP (including ASC 606 revenue recognition), with working knowledge of IFRS.\n\n - Prior experience in a SaaS, technology, or other high-growth environment strongly preferred.\n\n - Experience with technical accounting research and the preparation of technical memos on complex, non-routine transactions.\n\n - Working knowledge of internal controls and SOX, with experience supporting IPO readiness or public-company reporting a strong plus.\n\n - Strong understanding of technical accounting across areas such as business combinations, equity and stock-based compensation, leases, and revenue recognition.\n\n\nKEY COMPETENCIES\n\n - Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex technical matters into clear, actionable guidance.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, comfortable partnering with both finance and non-finance stakeholders.\n\n - A hands-on, roll-up-your-sleeves mindset, with the ability to balance technical rigor against the practical needs of a fast-moving business.\n\n - Proven ability to build scalable processes and controls in an evolving environment.\n\n - High degree of ownership, integrity, and attention to detail.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$224,000 - $336,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$224K - $336K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4131cb53-d0a9-441c-bcbf-69256ddacc54","tierSummary":"$224K – $336K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ab5e174c-b944-42a4-9271-c11f0d7ad45d","summary":"$224K – $336K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"id":"86daf356-14d8-4d4b-9ea5-20ba19138f1d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"194f99dc-5b17-41a4-8e77-114f1de0945f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":224000,"maxValue":336000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c011f3f0-205e-4e65-8ae1-c01ac885e25f","title":"Enterprise Customer Success Manager (Asset Management)","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T16:31:59.879+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c011f3f0-205e-4e65-8ae1-c01ac885e25f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c011f3f0-205e-4e65-8ae1-c01ac885e25f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at top enterprises and leading Law Firms. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and serving as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Leverage adoption rates, utilization metrics, and other KPIs to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced background in asset management, banking or financial services or strategic customer success/account management experience, legal (big law) or top tier management consulting firms and direct experience managing large-scale technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as committed, collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at top enterprises and leading Law Firms. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and serving as a thought partner to deliver a superior customer experience.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Leverage adoption rates, utilization metrics, and other KPIs to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n - Travel may be required from time to time, including visits to customer office locations and company offices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced background in asset management, banking or financial services or strategic customer success/account management experience, legal (big law) or top tier management consulting firms and direct experience managing large-scale technology projects.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly\n\n - Team players described as committed, collaborative and proactive with a team-first mentality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our rapidly-evolving Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Uncapped Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1f131296-7c15-4aa4-85fa-ca904e06edc5","tierSummary":"OTE $160K – $185K • Offers Equity • Offers Uncapped Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":"Offers Uncapped Commission","components":[{"id":"f9a9778c-caa5-4224-bf59-115d5f2d1f0a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8b3d6b1d-9205-4f9c-9216-00a2c0c23e3e","summary":"OTE $160K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":185000}]}},{"id":"9318ba76-60df-4b39-b036-95f488a46c7c","title":"Engagement Manager, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T17:32:46.256+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9318ba76-60df-4b39-b036-95f488a46c7c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9318ba76-60df-4b39-b036-95f488a46c7c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own transformation engagements end to end.</strong> Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Map workflows and target the highest-value opportunities.</strong> Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value.</strong> Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive relationships and advise on the operating model</strong>. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hand off with rigor.</strong> Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute learnings to build and improve playbooks.</strong> Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: Up to 50% of the time.</p><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Engagement Manager at Harvey, you will lead AI transformation engagements at our most strategic accounts: elite law firms, Fortune 500 legal departments, and premier financial institutions. You are the person our largest customers trust to turn ambitious transformation goals into embedded, measurable change.\n\nThis is a deployment-focused role. You will own the full arc of each strategic transformation engagement, from aligning executive sponsors and mapping how the firm works today to pinpoint the highest-value workflows for Harvey, to coordinating across teams like Legal Engineering to reimagine those workflows and capture measurable impact. When an engagement reaches sustainable adoption, you hand off to the account's Customer Success Manager and move to the next challenge.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn transformation engagements end to end. Lead strategic transformation engagements at Harvey's largest accounts. Set the plan, align stakeholders across the firm, drive execution, and hold everyone, including the customer, accountable to outcomes. You are the person making sure things actually happen.\n\nMap workflows and target the highest-value opportunities. Work alongside customers to map how legal and professional services work is done today, identify where Harvey can have the highest impact, and build a concrete roadmap for reimagining those workflows in partnership with Legal Engineering and Legal Innovation. This isn't theoretical; you're designing real workflows that real attorneys will use.\n\nCoordinate cross-functional delivery and capture value. Reinforce adoption through structured change management: equipping change champions, running enablement sessions, monitoring usage, and resolving blockers before they become problems.\n\nBuild executive relationships and advise on the operating model. Engage directly with senior partners, General Counsel, and legal leadership on the strategic and organizational shifts that AI-native ways of working require, including governance, talent, process, and KPIs. You are a credible advisor, not a project coordinator.\n\nHand off with rigor. Deliver a clear, documented account transition to the Customer Success Manager: adoption summary, open risks, recommended next steps. The handoff sets the Customer Success team up to sustain and build on what you started.\n\nContribute learnings to build and improve playbooks. Document what works. Contribute to Harvey's transformation methodology, templates, and frameworks so every engagement gets faster and more repeatable.\n\nTravel required: Up to 50% of the time.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in management consulting or senior client advisory, including time at the Engagement Manager or Project Leader level (or equivalent) where you owned a complex transformation program end to end: scoping, stakeholder alignment, delivery, and measurable outcomes. We are looking for people who have run the engagement, not only staffed it.\n\n - Experience managing large-scale technology deployments or change management programs at enterprise organizations, ideally in legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Exceptional executive presence; you are comfortable leading conversations with senior partners and C-suite leaders and can build credibility quickly in demanding environments.\n\n - Strong program management instincts: you own the plan, surface risk early, and drive to outcomes rather than just managing process.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of legal work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and building in environments where the playbook is still being written.\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"42ac77ed-3fd5-40da-a379-113fdb563f02","title":"Technical Revenue Accounting Lead","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T18:09:17.104+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/42ac77ed-3fd5-40da-a379-113fdb563f02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/42ac77ed-3fd5-40da-a379-113fdb563f02/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is looking for a Technical Revenue Accounting Lead to help us scale revenue recognition across a rapidly expanding portfolio of customer and partnership arrangements. Reporting to the Revenue Accounting Manager, this role will partner closely with Finance, Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Product and serve as the company’s subject-matter expert on ASC 606 and technical revenue accounting. In this highly collaborative, hands-on role, you'll review and help structure complex commercial contracts, author defensible accounting positions, and build the scalable processes, systems, and controls that will support Harvey through its next phases of growth. This is a high-impact opportunity for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and is excited to help shape a best-in-class revenue accounting function.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical accounting guidance on non-standard revenue transactions, including partnership agreements and complex subscription and usage-based deal structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the revenue accounting implications of new products, pricing models, and go-to-market motions, and advise cross-functional teams accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, document, and maintain revenue recognition policies, position papers, and accounting playbooks that scale with the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support month-end close processes and coordinate with external auditors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help implement and optimize revenue systems and automation to improve accuracy, efficiency, and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and maintain internal controls over revenue in support of audit and future SOX readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with ad hoc financial reporting requests</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of experience in revenue accounting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPA preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in public accounting and at a high-growth technology company, with an emphasis in technical accounting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep knowledge of ASC 606 and demonstrated experience applying guidance to non-standard contracts, including ASC 340-40 (costs to obtain a contract)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to write clear technical accounting memos. Can research guidance, state a position, and defend the conclusion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to partner cross-functionally with Sales, Legal, Deal Desk, and Product in a fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized and detail-oriented, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills and comfort operating amid ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Netsuite and Netsuite ARM (or similar)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$117,400 - $176,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is looking for a Technical Revenue Accounting Lead to help us scale revenue recognition across a rapidly expanding portfolio of customer and partnership arrangements. Reporting to the Revenue Accounting Manager, this role will partner closely with Finance, Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Product and serve as the company’s subject-matter expert on ASC 606 and technical revenue accounting. In this highly collaborative, hands-on role, you'll review and help structure complex commercial contracts, author defensible accounting positions, and build the scalable processes, systems, and controls that will support Harvey through its next phases of growth. This is a high-impact opportunity for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and is excited to help shape a best-in-class revenue accounting function.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Provide technical accounting guidance on non-standard revenue transactions, including partnership agreements and complex subscription and usage-based deal structures\n\n - Evaluate the revenue accounting implications of new products, pricing models, and go-to-market motions, and advise cross-functional teams accordingly\n\n - Develop, document, and maintain revenue recognition policies, position papers, and accounting playbooks that scale with the business\n\n - Support month-end close processes and coordinate with external auditors\n\n - Help implement and optimize revenue systems and automation to improve accuracy, efficiency, and scalability\n\n - Design and maintain internal controls over revenue in support of audit and future SOX readiness\n\n - Assist with ad hoc financial reporting requests\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3-5 years of experience in revenue accounting\n\n - CPA preferred\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field\n\n - Experience in public accounting and at a high-growth technology company, with an emphasis in technical accounting.\n\n - Deep knowledge of ASC 606 and demonstrated experience applying guidance to non-standard contracts, including ASC 340-40 (costs to obtain a contract)\n\n - Demonstrated ability to write clear technical accounting memos. Can research guidance, state a position, and defend the conclusion\n\n - Proven ability to partner cross-functionally with Sales, Legal, Deal Desk, and Product in a fast-moving environment\n\n - Highly organized and detail-oriented, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills and comfort operating amid ambiguity\n\n - Experience with Netsuite and Netsuite ARM (or similar)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$117,400 - $176,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$117.4K – $176K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$117.4K - $176K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2b72c273-04ed-4fad-a22a-76be7501fbf6","tierSummary":"$117.4K – $176K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"85415cdb-b9f9-4cba-8d04-f150379ad2df","summary":"$117.4K – $176K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":117400,"maxValue":176000},{"id":"2937d627-cf03-466b-94c8-6776b568d3c1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1eb5039a-2dbd-4814-bfaa-55ef48f3fcf4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":117400,"maxValue":176000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"46d3d283-1271-41d9-9cff-2839cb00432b","title":"Technical Revenue Accounting Lead","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T17:04:17.603+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/46d3d283-1271-41d9-9cff-2839cb00432b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/46d3d283-1271-41d9-9cff-2839cb00432b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is looking for a Technical Revenue Accounting Lead to help us scale revenue recognition across a rapidly expanding portfolio of customer and partnership arrangements. Reporting to the Revenue Accounting Manager, this role will partner closely with Finance, Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Product and serve as the company’s subject-matter expert on ASC 606 and technical revenue accounting. In this highly collaborative, hands-on role, you'll review and help structure complex commercial contracts, author defensible accounting positions, and build the scalable processes, systems, and controls that will support Harvey through its next phases of growth. This is a high-impact opportunity for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and is excited to help shape a best-in-class revenue accounting function.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical accounting guidance on non-standard revenue transactions, including partnership agreements and complex subscription and usage-based deal structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the revenue accounting implications of new products, pricing models, and go-to-market motions, and advise cross-functional teams accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, document, and maintain revenue recognition policies, position papers, and accounting playbooks that scale with the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support month-end close processes and coordinate with external auditors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help implement and optimize revenue systems and automation to improve accuracy, efficiency, and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and maintain internal controls over revenue in support of audit and future SOX readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with ad hoc financial reporting requests</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in revenue accounting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPA preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in public accounting and at a high-growth technology company, with an emphasis in technical accounting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep knowledge of ASC 606 and demonstrated experience applying guidance to non-standard contracts, including ASC 340-40 (costs to obtain a contract)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to write clear technical accounting memos. Can research guidance, state a position, and defend the conclusion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to partner cross-functionally with Sales, Legal, Deal Desk, and Product in a fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized and detail-oriented, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills and comfort operating amid ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Netsuite and Netsuite ARM (or similar)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$117,400 - $176,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is looking for a Technical Revenue Accounting Lead to help us scale revenue recognition across a rapidly expanding portfolio of customer and partnership arrangements. Reporting to the Revenue Accounting Manager, this role will partner closely with Finance, Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, and Product and serve as the company’s subject-matter expert on ASC 606 and technical revenue accounting. In this highly collaborative, hands-on role, you'll review and help structure complex commercial contracts, author defensible accounting positions, and build the scalable processes, systems, and controls that will support Harvey through its next phases of growth. This is a high-impact opportunity for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and is excited to help shape a best-in-class revenue accounting function.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Provide technical accounting guidance on non-standard revenue transactions, including partnership agreements and complex subscription and usage-based deal structures\n\n - Evaluate the revenue accounting implications of new products, pricing models, and go-to-market motions, and advise cross-functional teams accordingly\n\n - Develop, document, and maintain revenue recognition policies, position papers, and accounting playbooks that scale with the business\n\n - Support month-end close processes and coordinate with external auditors\n\n - Help implement and optimize revenue systems and automation to improve accuracy, efficiency, and scalability\n\n - Design and maintain internal controls over revenue in support of audit and future SOX readiness\n\n - Assist with ad hoc financial reporting requests\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in revenue accounting\n\n - CPA preferred.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field\n\n - Experience in public accounting and at a high-growth technology company, with an emphasis in technical accounting.\n\n - Deep knowledge of ASC 606 and demonstrated experience applying guidance to non-standard contracts, including ASC 340-40 (costs to obtain a contract)\n\n - Demonstrated ability to write clear technical accounting memos. Can research guidance, state a position, and defend the conclusion\n\n - Proven ability to partner cross-functionally with Sales, Legal, Deal Desk, and Product in a fast-moving environment\n\n - Highly organized and detail-oriented, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills and comfort operating amid ambiguity\n\n - Experience with Netsuite and Netsuite ARM (or similar)\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$117,400 - $176,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$117.4K – $176K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$117.4K - $176K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"997a1ed5-d917-41da-bb1e-693443e8fc40","tierSummary":"$117.4K – $176K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"71d8514a-ee25-491c-a07c-eda49863e809","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"998c7539-cd65-4984-97e4-3825e7661bca","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f0506561-7987-4e4d-aaf1-970685682a2b","summary":"$117.4K – $176K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":117400,"maxValue":176000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":117400,"maxValue":176000}]}},{"id":"eb11a622-d435-4c24-946f-c3fdb6fcbbdf","title":"Workplace Project Manager","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T15:37:25.896+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/eb11a622-d435-4c24-946f-c3fdb6fcbbdf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/eb11a622-d435-4c24-946f-c3fdb6fcbbdf/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Workplace Project Manager, you'll take our workplace playbooks and standards and turn them into delivered projects and programs on the ground - office moves and openings, and global special projects like health &amp; safety programming, design standards, emergency response planning, WVPPs, sustainability, and new tooling rollouts. This is a hands-on delivery role: you own scope, schedule, and budget for each project or program and drive it from kickoff to close.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Where the program sets the standard, your projects and programs bring it to life - on time, on budget, and to spec.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Global Special Projects</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project manage Workplace's global special projects: health &amp; safety (H&amp;S) programming, global design standards, global emergency response programming, Workplace Violence Prevention Plans (WVPPs), and sustainability programming across Harvey's office portfolio.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security, HR, Legal, and regional Workplace leads to build and roll out emergency response plans and WVPPs that meet local regulatory requirements while staying consistent with Harvey's global standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and evolve global design standards (furniture, finishes, signage) so offices feel consistently \"Harvey\" as we scale into new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive sustainability initiatives across offices - vendor and materials selection, energy and waste programs - and track progress against goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the global rollout of Workplace tooling and software - evaluating, piloting, and implementing platforms like desk booking, occupancy, and ticketing, and driving stakeholder training and adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own global and national vendor contracts (F&amp;B, janitorial, plants, and similar categories) - procurement, negotiation, and the master vendor relationship - while regional workplace managers own the day-to-day relationship, performance, and feedback in their offices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Global Playbook &amp; Portfolio Management (Moves &amp; Openings)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain the FDOB checklist and playbook that regional workplace leads execute against for satellite moves, expansions, and new-office openings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the portfolio-level calendar tracking when and where expansions and new offices are happening across the org, so Workplace can sequence and resource projects appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Step in to lead a move, opening, or buildout directly where a region doesn't yet have an established workplace manager, or where the existing regional team doesn't have the bandwidth - expect this to be a shrinking share of the role over time as regional coverage matures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with IT, Security, and AV to keep day-one readiness standards current in the playbook, so regional teams can deliver consistently without you running each project personally.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Program Management</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain project plans, schedules, and budgets across global programs and the FDOB playbook; track milestones, dependencies, and risks, and communicate status clearly to stakeholders and leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the portfolio-level view across all in-flight and planned moves, openings, and buildouts, flagging sequencing and resourcing risks to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage vendor relationships tied to your global contracts and programs, holding them accountable to schedule and quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Report to the Global Workplace Operations Manager to ensure every program and playbook meets Harvey's workplace standards and sets regional teams up for smooth steady-state operations.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in workplace operations, program management, or project management, with experience leading cross-functional programs such as health &amp; safety, emergency preparedness, sustainability, or systems/tooling rollouts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program design and playbook-building instincts - you'd rather build a system and standard that others execute against well than run every project yourself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing vendor and procurement relationships at a national or global scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of project management fundamentals - scope, schedule, budget, risk, and stakeholder communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with (not necessarily owning) construction, real estate, or facilities teams on office moves or buildouts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organizational and communication skills; you keep complex, fast-moving programs on track and everyone informed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a hands-on, get-it-done approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in New York and able to work on-site at our NYC office, with willingness to travel to other sites as projects require.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Nice to Have </h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or administering H&amp;S programs, emergency response plans, or WVPPs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with sustainability program design or reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with project / workplace tools - e.g., Asana, Smartsheet, Envoy, OfficeSpace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building playbooks or programs that scale across a distributed, multi-region team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,900 - $181,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Workplace Project Manager, you'll take our workplace playbooks and standards and turn them into delivered projects and programs on the ground - office moves and openings, and global special projects like health & safety programming, design standards, emergency response planning, WVPPs, sustainability, and new tooling rollouts. This is a hands-on delivery role: you own scope, schedule, and budget for each project or program and drive it from kickoff to close.\n\n\n\nWhere the program sets the standard, your projects and programs bring it to life - on time, on budget, and to spec.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\nGlobal Special Projects\n\n\n\n - Project manage Workplace's global special projects: health & safety (H&S) programming, global design standards, global emergency response programming, Workplace Violence Prevention Plans (WVPPs), and sustainability programming across Harvey's office portfolio.\n\n - Partner with Security, HR, Legal, and regional Workplace leads to build and roll out emergency response plans and WVPPs that meet local regulatory requirements while staying consistent with Harvey's global standards.\n\n - Maintain and evolve global design standards (furniture, finishes, signage) so offices feel consistently \"Harvey\" as we scale into new markets.\n\n - Drive sustainability initiatives across offices - vendor and materials selection, energy and waste programs - and track progress against goals.\n\n - Own the global rollout of Workplace tooling and software - evaluating, piloting, and implementing platforms like desk booking, occupancy, and ticketing, and driving stakeholder training and adoption.\n\n - Own global and national vendor contracts (F&B, janitorial, plants, and similar categories) - procurement, negotiation, and the master vendor relationship - while regional workplace managers own the day-to-day relationship, performance, and feedback in their offices.\n\n\n\n\nGlobal Playbook & Portfolio Management (Moves & Openings)\n\n - Build and maintain the FDOB checklist and playbook that regional workplace leads execute against for satellite moves, expansions, and new-office openings.\n\n - Own the portfolio-level calendar tracking when and where expansions and new offices are happening across the org, so Workplace can sequence and resource projects appropriately.\n\n - Step in to lead a move, opening, or buildout directly where a region doesn't yet have an established workplace manager, or where the existing regional team doesn't have the bandwidth - expect this to be a shrinking share of the role over time as regional coverage matures.\n\n - Coordinate with IT, Security, and AV to keep day-one readiness standards current in the playbook, so regional teams can deliver consistently without you running each project personally.\n\n\n\nProgram Management\n\n\n\n - Build and maintain project plans, schedules, and budgets across global programs and the FDOB playbook; track milestones, dependencies, and risks, and communicate status clearly to stakeholders and leadership.\n\n - Maintain the portfolio-level view across all in-flight and planned moves, openings, and buildouts, flagging sequencing and resourcing risks to leadership.\n\n - Manage vendor relationships tied to your global contracts and programs, holding them accountable to schedule and quality.\n\n - Report to the Global Workplace Operations Manager to ensure every program and playbook meets Harvey's workplace standards and sets regional teams up for smooth steady-state operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in workplace operations, program management, or project management, with experience leading cross-functional programs such as health & safety, emergency preparedness, sustainability, or systems/tooling rollouts.\n\n - Strong program design and playbook-building instincts - you'd rather build a system and standard that others execute against well than run every project yourself.\n\n - Experience managing vendor and procurement relationships at a national or global scale.\n\n - Strong command of project management fundamentals - scope, schedule, budget, risk, and stakeholder communication.\n\n - Experience partnering with (not necessarily owning) construction, real estate, or facilities teams on office moves or buildouts.\n\n - Excellent organizational and communication skills; you keep complex, fast-moving programs on track and everyone informed.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a hands-on, get-it-done approach.\n\n - Based in New York and able to work on-site at our NYC office, with willingness to travel to other sites as projects require.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE \n\n - Experience building or administering H&S programs, emergency response plans, or WVPPs.\n\n - Experience with sustainability program design or reporting.\n\n - Familiarity with project / workplace tools - e.g., Asana, Smartsheet, Envoy, OfficeSpace.\n\n - Experience building playbooks or programs that scale across a distributed, multi-region team.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,900 - $181,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120.9K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120.9K - $181.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"805577ab-f65b-4f88-9327-bf0ea5e9f146","tierSummary":"$120.9K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"03a6c702-4939-4173-be70-4a89a48c0704","summary":"$120.9K – $181.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120900,"maxValue":181300},{"id":"79dd8e5c-93e8-4643-88ac-1377d4b6acdc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"37eae927-2db4-4eab-9ebd-364931c091d1","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120900,"maxValue":181300},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"19db4c0a-8883-43c3-b667-60463098feb2","title":"Frontend Platform Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-31T16:29:30.149+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/19db4c0a-8883-43c3-b667-60463098feb2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/19db4c0a-8883-43c3-b667-60463098feb2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for experienced frontend engineers to help build and evolve Harvey’s frontend platform—the systems, tools, and abstractions that enable our engineering team to ship high-quality product experiences quickly and consistently.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This team focuses on developer experience, performance, reliability, and scalability across our frontend stack. Rather than building one-off product features, you’ll create shared foundations that power all of Harvey’s user-facing applications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact role with broad scope across the engineering organization. You’ll work closely with product engineers, design, and infrastructure teams to define and drive the future of frontend development at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve shared frontend infrastructure, including our design system and developer tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to and evolve frontend architecture for scalability and performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve developer experience and engineering velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve application performance and reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product teams to drive adoption of platform systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and reduce friction across the development lifecycle</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience working on large-scale frontend systems or platform-level infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think in systems and abstractions, not just features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of improving developer experience or engineering velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience influencing technical decisions across teams or driving adoption of shared systems</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JJ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for experienced frontend engineers to help build and evolve Harvey’s frontend platform—the systems, tools, and abstractions that enable our engineering team to ship high-quality product experiences quickly and consistently.\n\nThis team focuses on developer experience, performance, reliability, and scalability across our frontend stack. Rather than building one-off product features, you’ll create shared foundations that power all of Harvey’s user-facing applications.\n\nThis is a high-impact role with broad scope across the engineering organization. You’ll work closely with product engineers, design, and infrastructure teams to define and drive the future of frontend development at Harvey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and evolve shared frontend infrastructure, including our design system and developer tooling\n\n - Contribute to and evolve frontend architecture for scalability and performance\n\n - Improve developer experience and engineering velocity\n\n - Improve application performance and reliability\n\n - Partner with product teams to drive adoption of platform systems\n\n - Identify and reduce friction across the development lifecycle\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Strong experience working on large-scale frontend systems or platform-level infrastructure\n\n - Ability to think in systems and abstractions, not just features\n\n - A track record of improving developer experience or engineering velocity\n\n - Experience influencing technical decisions across teams or driving adoption of shared systems\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-JJ1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1bb50777-5b4a-4fc2-893e-69a235ae743c","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"606fcf8a-3ac5-4bc8-bbdd-613de11bee2e","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"7235777c-7eea-4445-8efe-212c5dae5ae1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"81fb83c5-f8bc-4fb0-b2ae-aa5df8781334","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"53ce64ab-8628-4832-b30e-dc17df696b15","title":"Global Manager, Recruiting Operations and Coordination","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T00:02:24.884+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/53ce64ab-8628-4832-b30e-dc17df696b15","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/53ce64ab-8628-4832-b30e-dc17df696b15/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Head of Recruiting Coordination joins Harvey's Talent team to lead and scale the recruiting coordination function across the company's global offices. The team's mission is to deliver an exceptional candidate experience while driving operational efficiency throughout the interview lifecycle. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns the strategy and execution for recruiting coordination programs, automation initiatives, and process improvement that enable Harvey to hire world-class talent at the pace a hypergrowth AI company demands. They partner directly with recruiting leadership, People Operations, and systems teams to architect scalable workflows that maintain a high-quality bar as the organization grows. It is a rare opportunity to build and lead a coordination function at a company redefining an industry through AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and manage a team of recruiting coordinators across multiple offices, setting standards for candidate experience, interview logistics, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own internal recruiting programs including interviewer enablement, onboarding for new interviewers, and coordination training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Tier 1 operational backlog, including things like creating and closing job requisitions, ATS data upkeep, interview plan maintenance, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement process improvements within tier one operations that reduce friction for recruiters, hiring managers, and candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Recruiting Operations on ATS architecture, workflow optimization, and data integrity to support hiring at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain metrics and dashboards that track coordination team performance, candidate experience, and process efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as an escalation point for scheduling and coordination issues, ensuring a consistently high-quality candidate and interviewer experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations or coordination, with progressive team management responsibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building and managing a coordination team in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in ATS platforms (e.g., Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever) and workflow automation tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use data to drive process improvements and inform stakeholder decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills and the ability to influence without authority across recruiting, People Operations, and hiring manager stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000- $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Head of Recruiting Coordination joins Harvey's Talent team to lead and scale the recruiting coordination function across the company's global offices. The team's mission is to deliver an exceptional candidate experience while driving operational efficiency throughout the interview lifecycle. \n\n\n\nThis role owns the strategy and execution for recruiting coordination programs, automation initiatives, and process improvement that enable Harvey to hire world-class talent at the pace a hypergrowth AI company demands. They partner directly with recruiting leadership, People Operations, and systems teams to architect scalable workflows that maintain a high-quality bar as the organization grows. It is a rare opportunity to build and lead a coordination function at a company redefining an industry through AI.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, mentor, and manage a team of recruiting coordinators across multiple offices, setting standards for candidate experience, interview logistics, and operational excellence.\n\n - Own internal recruiting programs including interviewer enablement, onboarding for new interviewers, and coordination training.\n\n - Own Tier 1 operational backlog, including things like creating and closing job requisitions, ATS data upkeep, interview plan maintenance, etc.\n\n - Design and implement process improvements within tier one operations that reduce friction for recruiters, hiring managers, and candidates\n\n - Partner with Recruiting Operations on ATS architecture, workflow optimization, and data integrity to support hiring at scale.\n\n - Develop and maintain metrics and dashboards that track coordination team performance, candidate experience, and process efficiency.\n\n - Serve as an escalation point for scheduling and coordination issues, ensuring a consistently high-quality candidate and interviewer experience\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations or coordination, with progressive team management responsibility.\n\n - Demonstrated success building and managing a coordination team in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.\n\n - Deep expertise in ATS platforms (e.g., Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever) and workflow automation tools.\n\n - Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use data to drive process improvements and inform stakeholder decisions.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills and the ability to influence without authority across recruiting, People Operations, and hiring manager stakeholders.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000- $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"be0dafcd-31ff-4984-8270-64571e0864b4","tierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0e558a07-695c-4063-b94d-0b499166444c","summary":"$180K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000},{"id":"4d5b3ace-3222-474e-b773-10a3325e3b5d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fa2a9aa6-5d7a-4a93-a7a6-8a7ead3bf370","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5cb453a8-664e-48a6-98b4-a44ee12bf59f","title":"Technical User Operations Specialist – EMEA (Wed–Sun)","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T14:30:51.773+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5cb453a8-664e-48a6-98b4-a44ee12bf59f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5cb453a8-664e-48a6-98b4-a44ee12bf59f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a User Operations Specialist, you will be the frontline support within the User Operations team, reporting to the User Operations Manager. Your role is crucial in providing empathetic and efficient support to our customers. We are seeking someone who loves problem-solving, is adept at handling multiple priorities, and is passionate about working with enterprise customers to ensure a seamless support experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role follows a fixed Wednesday-Sunday schedule, with weekend coverage included as part of the standard five-day workweek.</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the first point of contact for customer support inquiries, delivering empathetic, accurate, and timely resolutions across a range of technical and product-related issues (including AI output quality, app access, APIs, authentication, and error logs).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple competing priorities while maintaining a high level of responsiveness, reliability, and accountability during assigned support shifts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate effectively with teammates and cross-functional partners to troubleshoot complex issues, escalate when appropriate, and contribute to a strong overall customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain deep, up-to-date knowledge of products, features, and services to provide informed, current support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document customer interactions, issues, and feedback to support continuous improvement of products, processes, and support materials (e.g., FAQs and knowledge base articles).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own tasks independently while contributing thoughtfully to team workflows and the ongoing refinement of support processes.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in office, 2 days working from home</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A comprehensive 4-week onboarding and training program designed to set you up for success from day one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development stipend to support your continued learning and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to work on cross-functional projects and initiatives that impact user operations company-wide</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as we continue to build support operations at Harvey</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What You Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of proven experience in a fast-paced technical support role, delivering white-glove or premium support to large enterprise customers for AI-driven products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional empathy and communication skills (written and verbal), with the ability to build trust, connect with customers, and clearly explain complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving and critical-thinking abilities, with a creative approach to diagnosing and resolving complex issues.<br />Highly organised and adaptable, able to manage multiple tasks and competing priorities effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of APIs, with the ability to troubleshoot and articulate API-related concepts clearly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with customer support tools and CRM systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team player who builds positive cross-functional relationships while contributing effectively in a shared environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for learning and continuous improvement, with a commitment to staying current on industry trends and best practices.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a User Operations Specialist, you will be the frontline support within the User Operations team, reporting to the User Operations Manager. Your role is crucial in providing empathetic and efficient support to our customers. We are seeking someone who loves problem-solving, is adept at handling multiple priorities, and is passionate about working with enterprise customers to ensure a seamless support experience.\n\nThis role follows a fixed Wednesday-Sunday schedule, with weekend coverage included as part of the standard five-day workweek.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Serve as the first point of contact for customer support inquiries, delivering empathetic, accurate, and timely resolutions across a range of technical and product-related issues (including AI output quality, app access, APIs, authentication, and error logs).\n\n - Manage multiple competing priorities while maintaining a high level of responsiveness, reliability, and accountability during assigned support shifts.\n\n - Collaborate effectively with teammates and cross-functional partners to troubleshoot complex issues, escalate when appropriate, and contribute to a strong overall customer experience.\n\n - Maintain deep, up-to-date knowledge of products, features, and services to provide informed, current support.\n\n - Document customer interactions, issues, and feedback to support continuous improvement of products, processes, and support materials (e.g., FAQs and knowledge base articles).\n\n - Own tasks independently while contributing thoughtfully to team workflows and the ongoing refinement of support processes.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in office, 2 days working from home\n\n - A comprehensive 4-week onboarding and training program designed to set you up for success from day one\n\n - Professional development stipend to support your continued learning and growth\n\n - Opportunities to work on cross-functional projects and initiatives that impact user operations company-wide\n\n - Be part of building something special as we continue to build support operations at Harvey\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of proven experience in a fast-paced technical support role, delivering white-glove or premium support to large enterprise customers for AI-driven products.\n\n - Exceptional empathy and communication skills (written and verbal), with the ability to build trust, connect with customers, and clearly explain complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n - Strong problem-solving and critical-thinking abilities, with a creative approach to diagnosing and resolving complex issues.\n   Highly organised and adaptable, able to manage multiple tasks and competing priorities effectively.\n\n - Solid understanding of APIs, with the ability to troubleshoot and articulate API-related concepts clearly.\n\n - Proficiency with customer support tools and CRM systems.\n\n - Collaborative team player who builds positive cross-functional relationships while contributing effectively in a shared environment.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for learning and continuous improvement, with a commitment to staying current on industry trends and best practices.\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n \n\n#LI-LM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f996dd71-e08c-487d-abe1-9900c8d29331","title":"Account Executive, Mid Market","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-31T22:45:18.835+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f996dd71-e08c-487d-abe1-9900c8d29331","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f996dd71-e08c-487d-abe1-9900c8d29331/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Mid Market Account Executive at Harvey, you will drive the growth and success of our AI solutions within the legal and professional services markets. You will be responsible for establishing and growing relationships with mid-sized law firms and corporate and financial services clients, understanding their unique challenges, and presenting AI solutions that streamline their processes and boost productivity. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, coupled with your passion for groundbreaking AI technologies, will help us shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Own your book of business by managing a named account list, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads, and outbounding directly to high-potential prospects.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, growing, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI systems to prospects and clients.\n\n - Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Harvey’s solutions to meet customer needs. Collaborate closely with the engineering and product teams to stay updated on the latest AI advancements and tailor solutions to meet client goals.\n\n - Develop our sales playbook to enable scaling, documenting learnings that can be applied across accounts.\n\n - Travel is occasionally required to meet with customers, approximately 1–3 times per quarter.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from executives across various functions to day-to-day product users – especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey’s mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in knowledge work. Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently.\n\n - Team player who can collaborate effectively across internal functions (product, legal, etc.) to achieve common goals.\n\n - Energized by contributing to the development of our team, sales processes, and culture, refining the value proposition of our solutions and creating sales resources to drive our success.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the Legal industry a plus but not required\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Be part of building something special as a founding member of our Toronto team\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Toronto office, 2 days working from home\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\nWe are an AI company and we use AI to improve all of our processes, including in the recruitment process. Whilst we do use AI to help improve efficiency in our recruitment process, we do not rely on AI to make any automated decisions and ensure that a human reviews AI output.\n\n#LI-AD2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b0570329-6c45-4446-9314-146c9dead90b","title":"Director, Legal Engineering, EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T12:19:32.286+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b0570329-6c45-4446-9314-146c9dead90b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b0570329-6c45-4446-9314-146c9dead90b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the VP, Legal Engineering &amp; Regulatory Investigations, you will lead Harvey's Legal Engineering teams across EMEA.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will directly manage Legal Engineering Managers and oversee the teams focused on supporting Harvey's pre-sales customer engagements. This is a second-line leadership role focused on organizational leadership, operational excellence, and cross-functional execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in this role requires exceptional people leadership, strong business judgment, and the ability to build systems and processes that enable teams to operate effectively at scale. You will partner closely with leaders across Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to deliver exceptional outcomes for customers while helping shape the future of Legal Engineering at Harvey.</p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, develop, and scale a team of Legal Engineering Managers and their organizations serving Harvey's in-house customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the systems, processes, and operating mechanisms that enable Legal Engineering to deliver exceptional customer outcomes at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to align priorities and drive execution across the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a trusted advisor to law firm and legal department leaders and an influential partner to senior stakeholders across Harvey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive organizational performance through effective planning, resource management, talent development, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define the future of Legal Engineering.</p></li></ul><h1>What You Have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 12+ years of post-qualification experience (PQE).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm and/or in-house at a leading company, with significant client-facing experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading managers and manager-led organizations, not solely individual contributors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building and scaling high-performing teams in complex, fast-paced environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning organizational systems, processes, and operating models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build strong cross-functional partnerships and drive results across multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record of managing upward and influencing senior leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience representing an organization externally and building trusted relationships with executive-level stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of law firms and enterprise legal teams, including corporate, litigation, investigations, regulatory, compliance, and legal operations functions, as well as the evolving legal technology landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, leadership, and organizational skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Preferred Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading teams outside of a traditional law firm hierarchy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in legal technology, professional services, consulting, legal innovation, legal operations, or other customer-facing organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading globally distributed teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to create structure and drive execution in rapidly evolving environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across multiple legal practice areas, including corporate, litigation, investigations, regulatory, compliance, and legal operations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nReporting to the VP, Legal Engineering & Regulatory Investigations, you will lead Harvey's Legal Engineering teams across EMEA.\n\nYou will directly manage Legal Engineering Managers and oversee the teams focused on supporting Harvey's pre-sales customer engagements. This is a second-line leadership role focused on organizational leadership, operational excellence, and cross-functional execution.\n\nSuccess in this role requires exceptional people leadership, strong business judgment, and the ability to build systems and processes that enable teams to operate effectively at scale. You will partner closely with leaders across Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to deliver exceptional outcomes for customers while helping shape the future of Legal Engineering at Harvey.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, develop, and scale a team of Legal Engineering Managers and their organizations serving Harvey's in-house customers.\n\n - Build the systems, processes, and operating mechanisms that enable Legal Engineering to deliver exceptional customer outcomes at scale.\n\n - Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to align priorities and drive execution across the business.\n\n - Act as a trusted advisor to law firm and legal department leaders and an influential partner to senior stakeholders across Harvey.\n\n - Drive organizational performance through effective planning, resource management, talent development, and operational excellence.\n\n - Help define the future of Legal Engineering.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 12+ years of post-qualification experience (PQE).\n\n - Experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm and/or in-house at a leading company, with significant client-facing experience.\n\n - Experience leading managers and manager-led organizations, not solely individual contributors.\n\n - Demonstrated success building and scaling high-performing teams in complex, fast-paced environments.\n\n - Experience owning organizational systems, processes, and operating models.\n\n - Proven ability to build strong cross-functional partnerships and drive results across multiple stakeholders.\n\n - Strong track record of managing upward and influencing senior leaders.\n\n - Experience representing an organization externally and building trusted relationships with executive-level stakeholders.\n\n - Deep understanding of law firms and enterprise legal teams, including corporate, litigation, investigations, regulatory, compliance, and legal operations functions, as well as the evolving legal technology landscape.\n\n - Exceptional communication, leadership, and organizational skills.\n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience leading teams outside of a traditional law firm hierarchy.\n\n - Experience in legal technology, professional services, consulting, legal innovation, legal operations, or other customer-facing organizations.\n\n - Experience operating in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Experience leading globally distributed teams.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to create structure and drive execution in rapidly evolving environments.\n\n - Experience working across multiple legal practice areas, including corporate, litigation, investigations, regulatory, compliance, and legal operations.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fdca1f67-ebd8-4f95-98af-eeab21f083e0","title":"Mid-Market Customer Success Manager (Toronto)","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T15:15:16.393+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fdca1f67-ebd8-4f95-98af-eeab21f083e0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fdca1f67-ebd8-4f95-98af-eeab21f083e0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$125,000 - $145,000 OTE </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.\n\n - Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.\n\n - Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A chance to be at the forefront of AI technology and innovation, directly impacting how our clients' businesses operate and thrive.\n\n - An opportunity to contribute to the growth and direction of our Customer Success program, building out best-in-class playbooks and processes.\n\n - A collaborative work environment that promotes growth, learning, and development.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$125,000 - $145,000 OTE \n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-JL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $145K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6d5e406d-8cfa-46fd-86d5-6837b72939f5","tierSummary":"$125K – $145K • OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE","components":[{"id":"19ea7160-5e0f-4f5e-be3b-e7d2fefb010c","summary":"$125K – $145K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":145000}]}},{"id":"e63ca043-4d5b-4c46-93be-beb2b300d34e","title":"Strategic Finance Business Partner - Corporate Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T19:41:07.040+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e63ca043-4d5b-4c46-93be-beb2b300d34e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e63ca043-4d5b-4c46-93be-beb2b300d34e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategic Finance Partner at Harvey, you will play a crucial role in guiding the financial strategy and planning for the company to support both rapid growth and our long-term financial profile. You will be responsible for providing key insights and financial frameworks that underpin the company's most consequential decisions and help shape the company’s biggest investments. This is a cross-functional and strategic role that will partner with executives and teams across the entire company.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build &amp; own core operating models to help identify key business drivers and maintain a dynamic forecast in a fast changing environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and deliver clear, concise, and insightful financial analyses to support strategic decision-making by executives and cross-functional partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Uplevel our financial infrastructure and reporting - build scalable processes, dashboards, and systems that grow with the company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide thoughtful recommendations on financial strategies, investments, and resource allocation decisions, grounded in an in-depth understanding of the company's financial objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive annual and long-range planning cycles, including target-setting, budgeting, benchmarking, and scenario analysis across the corporate cost base.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience, including strategic finance roles at high-growth technology companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Low-ego high-drive work style, with a focus on detail and high personal bar for quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong financial modeling skills and the ability to build complex operating models from scratch, including experience with unit economics and cost structure analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills - the ability to distill complex financial concepts into clear, actionable insights for executive and cross-functional audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward ownership - a track record of thriving in fast-moving, unstructured environments and driving stakeholders toward decisions.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000 - $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Strategic Finance Partner at Harvey, you will play a crucial role in guiding the financial strategy and planning for the company to support both rapid growth and our long-term financial profile. You will be responsible for providing key insights and financial frameworks that underpin the company's most consequential decisions and help shape the company’s biggest investments. This is a cross-functional and strategic role that will partner with executives and teams across the entire company.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build & own core operating models to help identify key business drivers and maintain a dynamic forecast in a fast changing environment.\n\n - Prepare and deliver clear, concise, and insightful financial analyses to support strategic decision-making by executives and cross-functional partners.\n\n - Uplevel our financial infrastructure and reporting - build scalable processes, dashboards, and systems that grow with the company.\n\n - Provide thoughtful recommendations on financial strategies, investments, and resource allocation decisions, grounded in an in-depth understanding of the company's financial objectives.\n\n - Drive annual and long-range planning cycles, including target-setting, budgeting, benchmarking, and scenario analysis across the corporate cost base.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of experience, including strategic finance roles at high-growth technology companies.\n\n - Low-ego high-drive work style, with a focus on detail and high personal bar for quality\n\n - Strong financial modeling skills and the ability to build complex operating models from scratch, including experience with unit economics and cost structure analysis.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills - the ability to distill complex financial concepts into clear, actionable insights for executive and cross-functional audiences.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward ownership - a track record of thriving in fast-moving, unstructured environments and driving stakeholders toward decisions.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$160,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-BG1 \n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a38885de-1013-430d-bf5d-aee31fb7d054","tierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"960365ca-c3bc-47f0-beea-fdceec60323a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"33ea9b68-3fa2-4ed5-9d36-1155b15a90e3","summary":"$160K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000},{"id":"c4599fc6-8994-48ae-8d25-25483a56033b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c096de74-6c8f-4f55-a39b-eff469ec2654","title":"Strategic Finance Business Partner - Corporate Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T19:41:12.845+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c096de74-6c8f-4f55-a39b-eff469ec2654","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c096de74-6c8f-4f55-a39b-eff469ec2654/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategic Finance Partner at Harvey, you will play a crucial role in guiding the financial strategy and planning for the company to support both rapid growth and our long-term financial profile. You will be responsible for providing key insights and financial frameworks that underpin the company's most consequential decisions and help shape the company’s biggest investments. This is a cross-functional and strategic role that will partner with executives and teams across the entire company.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build &amp; own core operating models to help identify key business drivers and maintain a dynamic forecast in a fast changing environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and deliver clear, concise, and insightful financial analyses to support strategic decision-making by executives and cross-functional partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Uplevel our financial infrastructure and reporting - build scalable processes, dashboards, and systems that grow with the company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide thoughtful recommendations on financial strategies, investments, and resource allocation decisions, grounded in an in-depth understanding of the company's financial objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive annual and long-range planning cycles, including target-setting, budgeting, benchmarking, and scenario analysis across the corporate cost base.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience, including strategic finance roles at high-growth technology companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Low-ego high-drive work style, with a focus on detail and high personal bar for quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong financial modeling skills and the ability to build complex operating models from scratch, including experience with unit economics and cost structure analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills - the ability to distill complex financial concepts into clear, actionable insights for executive and cross-functional audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward ownership - a track record of thriving in fast-moving, unstructured environments and driving stakeholders toward decisions.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000 - $220,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Strategic Finance Partner at Harvey, you will play a crucial role in guiding the financial strategy and planning for the company to support both rapid growth and our long-term financial profile. You will be responsible for providing key insights and financial frameworks that underpin the company's most consequential decisions and help shape the company’s biggest investments. This is a cross-functional and strategic role that will partner with executives and teams across the entire company.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build & own core operating models to help identify key business drivers and maintain a dynamic forecast in a fast changing environment.\n\n - Prepare and deliver clear, concise, and insightful financial analyses to support strategic decision-making by executives and cross-functional partners.\n\n - Uplevel our financial infrastructure and reporting - build scalable processes, dashboards, and systems that grow with the company.\n\n - Provide thoughtful recommendations on financial strategies, investments, and resource allocation decisions, grounded in an in-depth understanding of the company's financial objectives.\n\n - Drive annual and long-range planning cycles, including target-setting, budgeting, benchmarking, and scenario analysis across the corporate cost base.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of experience, including strategic finance roles at high-growth technology companies.\n\n - Low-ego high-drive work style, with a focus on detail and high personal bar for quality\n\n - Strong financial modeling skills and the ability to build complex operating models from scratch, including experience with unit economics and cost structure analysis.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills - the ability to distill complex financial concepts into clear, actionable insights for executive and cross-functional audiences.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward ownership - a track record of thriving in fast-moving, unstructured environments and driving stakeholders toward decisions.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$160,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n \n\n#LI-BG1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"08521e0c-0e03-4b99-8658-33b98c6a6828","tierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e9c438c1-f3ed-4af8-8fb4-1534bb22544e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a3f9e709-6e34-47e2-905e-039da04be960","summary":"$160K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000},{"id":"8c297f50-f03e-45fa-ae54-ea4b9efc4e1f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a3981433-9f7c-46f7-8245-7b1013a0f9f0","title":"Legal Engineering Program Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-04T15:45:16.601+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a3981433-9f7c-46f7-8245-7b1013a0f9f0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a3981433-9f7c-46f7-8245-7b1013a0f9f0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Program Manager for the Legal Engineering organization, you will be joining Harvey's Legal Engineering organization to drive the operational infrastructure that enables one of the company's fastest-growing GTM functions to scale effectively. The Legal Engineering team partners directly with the world's leading law firms and professional services providers to deploy AI-powered solutions, and this role ensures that the programs, processes, and systems underpinning the team operate with rigor and consistency. You will partner with Legal Engineering managers, Sales Operations, Product, and leadership to translate strategic priorities into executable programs that drive measurable outcomes. It is a rare opportunity to build program management from the ground up within a high-growth function at the intersection of AI and legal services.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute end-to-end programs that support the Legal Engineering team's operational rhythm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain the processes, tooling, and documentation that enable Legal Engineering managers to operate consistently across regions (US, EMEA, APAC).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive change management initiatives as the Legal Engineering organization scales, ensuring smooth adoption of new processes and tools.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–7 years of experience in program management, operations, or enablement within a high-growth technology or professional services environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to design and deliver cross-functional programs from concept through execution, managing multiple stakeholders and competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and facilitation skills with the ability to influence without authority across a distributed organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with change management, process design, and operational scaling in fast-paced environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward action—able to build structure where none exists and iterate quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with GTM functions, legal technology, or AI products is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,100-$232,700 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LS1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Program Manager for the Legal Engineering organization, you will be joining Harvey's Legal Engineering organization to drive the operational infrastructure that enables one of the company's fastest-growing GTM functions to scale effectively. The Legal Engineering team partners directly with the world's leading law firms and professional services providers to deploy AI-powered solutions, and this role ensures that the programs, processes, and systems underpinning the team operate with rigor and consistency. You will partner with Legal Engineering managers, Sales Operations, Product, and leadership to translate strategic priorities into executable programs that drive measurable outcomes. It is a rare opportunity to build program management from the ground up within a high-growth function at the intersection of AI and legal services.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and execute end-to-end programs that support the Legal Engineering team's operational rhythm.\n\n - Build and maintain the processes, tooling, and documentation that enable Legal Engineering managers to operate consistently across regions (US, EMEA, APAC).\n\n - Drive change management initiatives as the Legal Engineering organization scales, ensuring smooth adoption of new processes and tools.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4–7 years of experience in program management, operations, or enablement within a high-growth technology or professional services environment.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to design and deliver cross-functional programs from concept through execution, managing multiple stakeholders and competing priorities.\n\n - Strong communication and facilitation skills with the ability to influence without authority across a distributed organization.\n\n - Experience with change management, process design, and operational scaling in fast-paced environments.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and a bias toward action—able to build structure where none exists and iterate quickly.\n\n - Familiarity with GTM functions, legal technology, or AI products is a strong plus.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,100-$232,700 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LS1 \n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.1K – $232.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.1K - $232.7K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b3e2f085-b142-4030-9da0-61242314cf88","tierSummary":"$155.1K – $232.7K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3bdea19d-b021-4a90-8a93-b595ba1fbc9f","summary":"$155.1K – $232.7K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155100,"maxValue":232700},{"id":"00f17a2f-976e-44fb-9999-625bba780529","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a54a403a-864b-4df8-932e-8bcab65f7a4b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155100,"maxValue":232700},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6a840e0d-6af8-4ad6-a182-7534ce64e7e2","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Production Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T23:36:32.930+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6a840e0d-6af8-4ad6-a182-7534ce64e7e2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6a840e0d-6af8-4ad6-a182-7534ce64e7e2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h2>Infrastructure Engineering &amp; Technical Leadership</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.</p></li></ul><h2>Infrastructure Foundation &amp; Production Operations</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$161,300 - $241,900 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.\n\nWe’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.\n\nIn this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE ENGINEERING & TECHNICAL LEADERSHIP\n\n - Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.\n\n - Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.\n\n - Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.\n\n - Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.\n\n - Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDATION & PRODUCTION OPERATIONS\n\n - Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.\n\n - Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.\n\n - Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.\n\n - Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.\n\n - Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.\n\n - Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.\n\n - Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.\n\n - Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.\n\n - Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.\n\n - Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.\n\n - Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.\n\n - Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.\n\n - Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.\n\n - Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.\n\n - A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.\n\n - A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.\n\n - Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.\n\n - Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.\n\n - Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$161,300 - $241,900 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$161.3K – $241.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$161.3K - $241.9K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c7a6c8ec-6ae6-4eeb-ac6f-0c13d6968450","tierSummary":"$161.3K – $241.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ead1b09a-b631-4cb0-89d3-34cdcb031090","summary":"$161.3K – $241.9K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161300,"maxValue":241900},{"id":"a8e069ca-0ad6-4dc9-bb4c-9d5072ab362a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"03879e95-9bd2-4541-9c24-042d79419b3a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161300,"maxValue":241900},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"11571c63-2fc5-41ce-b855-c949ead5efca","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Production Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T23:37:06.693+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/11571c63-2fc5-41ce-b855-c949ead5efca","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/11571c63-2fc5-41ce-b855-c949ead5efca/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h2>Infrastructure Engineering &amp; Technical Leadership</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.</p></li></ul><h2>Infrastructure Foundation &amp; Production Operations</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.\n\nWe’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.\n\nIn this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE ENGINEERING & TECHNICAL LEADERSHIP\n\n - Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.\n\n - Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.\n\n - Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.\n\n - Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.\n\n - Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDATION & PRODUCTION OPERATIONS\n\n - Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.\n\n - Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.\n\n - Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.\n\n - Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.\n\n - Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.\n\n - Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.\n\n - Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.\n\n - Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.\n\n - Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.\n\n - Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.\n\n - Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.\n\n - Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.\n\n - Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.\n\n - Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.\n\n - A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.\n\n - A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.\n\n - Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.\n\n - Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.\n\n - Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"83d91328-fdd0-44f0-a883-f674426bdd1f","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e2df0c40-621e-49f3-8ae8-472341613a9a","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"bd051feb-fc58-4465-a8a1-c8ce95dd659f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ce7aae73-0eb2-4e11-9e82-0af6e413395b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"dbd9a156-a841-42a0-a3e5-beed8de60a7c","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Production Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T23:37:30.751+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dbd9a156-a841-42a0-a3e5-beed8de60a7c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dbd9a156-a841-42a0-a3e5-beed8de60a7c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h2>Infrastructure Engineering &amp; Technical Leadership</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.</p></li></ul><h2>Infrastructure Foundation &amp; Production Operations</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$161,300 - $241,900 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.\n\nWe’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.\n\nIn this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE ENGINEERING & TECHNICAL LEADERSHIP\n\n - Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.\n\n - Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.\n\n - Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.\n\n - Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.\n\n - Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDATION & PRODUCTION OPERATIONS\n\n - Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.\n\n - Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.\n\n - Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.\n\n - Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.\n\n - Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.\n\n - Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.\n\n - Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.\n\n - Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.\n\n - Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.\n\n - Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.\n\n - Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.\n\n - Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.\n\n - Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.\n\n - Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.\n\n - A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.\n\n - A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.\n\n - Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.\n\n - Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.\n\n - Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$161,300 - $241,900 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$161.3K – $241.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$161.3K - $241.9K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6428914b-af7f-491c-9709-e22f8bc40106","tierSummary":"$161.3K – $241.9K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7ebb46cf-8999-4b69-8e85-dbe4aa5788b4","summary":"$161.3K – $241.9K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161300,"maxValue":241900},{"id":"78299120-b7d9-40e8-bb34-b75b9d74495b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b7337697-fc08-4445-ad10-d839fa419c45","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161300,"maxValue":241900},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"dad3437f-9f4c-444a-bf4a-ae2a9a1047c2","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Production Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T23:36:49.147+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dad3437f-9f4c-444a-bf4a-ae2a9a1047c2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dad3437f-9f4c-444a-bf4a-ae2a9a1047c2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h2>Infrastructure Engineering &amp; Technical Leadership</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.</p></li></ul><h2>Infrastructure Foundation &amp; Production Operations</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the AI platform trusted by the world’s leading law firms and enterprises. Our infrastructure is the foundation that powers every customer interaction, every model inference, and every production workload.\n\nWe’re looking for a Production Engineer to help build and operate Harvey’s core compute and networking infrastructure, Kubernetes platform, workflow orchestration platform, and production infrastructure foundations. You’ll work on the systems that enable engineering teams to move quickly and operate reliable services at scale.\n\nIn this role, you’ll improve the reliability, scalability, security, and efficiency of Harvey’s infrastructure platform. You’ll solve complex production challenges across compute fleet management, capacity planning, infrastructure automation, and production operations. You’ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to ensure our infrastructure scales with Harvey’s rapid growth.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the belief that Job’s Not Finished. We move quickly, prioritize clarity, and continuously raise the bar for engineering excellence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE ENGINEERING & TECHNICAL LEADERSHIP\n\n - Design, build, and operate the production infrastructure that powers Harvey’s products and AI workloads.\n\n - Drive technical direction across compute infrastructure, networking, Kubernetes, workflow orchestration, and production operations.\n\n - Lead complex, cross-functional technical initiatives that improve reliability, scalability, security, operational efficiency, and infrastructure cost.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering, Security, AI Infrastructure, and Platform teams to translate product and business requirements into resilient infrastructure solutions.\n\n - Establish reusable patterns, tooling, and paved paths that help engineering teams ship and operate production services safely.\n\n - Raise the engineering bar through thoughtful design reviews, clear technical documentation, operational rigor, and mentorship.\n\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDATION & PRODUCTION OPERATIONS\n\n - Build and operate Harvey’s global compute and network infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance.\n\n - Improve compute utilization, performance, and service availability while supporting rapidly growing AI workloads.\n\n - Develop capacity models, demand forecasts, and fleet lifecycle automation to help infrastructure scale efficiently with business growth.\n\n - Operate and continuously improve Harvey’s Kubernetes platform, including cluster provisioning, upgrades, networking, monitoring, reliability, performance, and operational automation.\n\n - Drive infrastructure cost efficiency through capacity management, resource rightsizing, workload optimization, and utilization monitoring.\n\n - Build secure infrastructure foundations, including identity and access management, network isolation, secrets management, auditing, and compliance controls.\n\n - Develop scalable Infrastructure-as-Code and automation frameworks using technologies such as Terraform and Pulumi.\n\n - Improve observability, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and operational readiness across the infrastructure platform.\n\n - Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response when needed, and turn production learnings into durable engineering improvements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of software, infrastructure, site reliability, or production engineering experience.\n\n - Deep experience building and operating large-scale cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience operating Kubernetes in production, including cluster lifecycle management, networking, and reliability.\n\n - Experience building and operating distributed systems with strong reliability, scalability, and performance characteristics.\n\n - Experience with infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code using tools such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - Strong understanding of compute infrastructure, networking, capacity planning, fleet management, and production operations.\n\n - Experience designing and operating observability systems, including monitoring, logging, alerting, and incident response.\n\n - Strong understanding of infrastructure security, including IAM, network security, secrets management, and compliance best practices.\n\n - A track record of driving complex, cross-functional technical initiatives and influencing engineering decisions without relying on formal authority.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to engineering partners and other stakeholders.\n\n - A systems-thinking mindset and a passion for building simple, reliable, and scalable infrastructure platforms.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting AI/ML or LLM infrastructure at scale.\n\n - Experience operating GPU fleets, high-performance compute infrastructure, or large-scale capacity planning.\n\n - Experience with multi-cloud infrastructure or hybrid cloud environments.\n\n - Experience building internal platforms or developer tooling that improves engineering velocity and production safety.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fb097d35-c87c-44be-ac40-790c2a273bf2","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"124bfd0c-9419-464d-851d-4ecab29cd2f4","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"4e8a7e24-ea53-4255-acae-56040a60c1c7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b9c74e0e-4e6c-4b67-be94-e993588323a7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a7773695-38c2-41e2-bdfc-179693711556","title":"Head of Legal Engineering, Product Specialists - EMEA","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T20:51:17.383+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a7773695-38c2-41e2-bdfc-179693711556","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a7773695-38c2-41e2-bdfc-179693711556/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the VP, Legal Engineering, you will lead Harvey's Legal Engineering (Product Specialist) teams across EMEA.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will directly manage Legal Engineer Managers - Product Specialists and oversee the teams focused on supporting Harvey's post-sales customer engagements across law firms and in-house legal departments. This is a second-line leadership role focused on organisational leadership, operational excellence, and cross-functional execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in this role requires exceptional people leadership, strong business judgment, and the ability to build systems and processes that enable teams to operate effectively at scale. You will partner closely with leaders across Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to deliver exceptional outcomes for customers while helping shape the future of Legal Engineering at Harvey.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, develop, and scale a team of Legal Engineer Managers - Product Specialists and their organisations serving Harvey's law firm and in-house customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the systems, processes, and operating mechanisms that enable Legal Engineering to deliver exceptional customer outcomes at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to align priorities and drive execution across the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a trusted advisor to law firm and in-house legal leaders and an influential partner to senior stakeholders across Harvey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive organisational performance through effective planning, resource management, talent development, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define the future of Legal Engineering and how Harvey partners with the world's leading law firms and corporate legal departments.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified lawyer with 9+ years of post-qualification experience (PQE).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm and/or in-house at a leading company, with significant client-facing experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading managers and manager-led organisations, not solely individual contributors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building and scaling high-performing teams in complex, fast-paced environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning organisational systems, processes, and operating models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build strong cross-functional partnerships and drive results across multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record of managing upward and influencing senior leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience representing an organisation externally and building trusted relationships with executive-level stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, and a strong understanding of how law firms and in-house legal teams operate day to day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, leadership, and organisational skills.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading teams outside of a traditional law firm or in-house hierarchy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in legal technology, professional services, consulting, legal innovation, legal operations, or other customer-facing organisations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading globally distributed or pan-EMEA teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to create structure and drive execution in rapidly evolving environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across multiple legal practice areas or with a broad range of law firm and in-house stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nReporting to the VP, Legal Engineering, you will lead Harvey's Legal Engineering (Product Specialist) teams across EMEA.\n\nYou will directly manage Legal Engineer Managers - Product Specialists and oversee the teams focused on supporting Harvey's post-sales customer engagements across law firms and in-house legal departments. This is a second-line leadership role focused on organisational leadership, operational excellence, and cross-functional execution.\n\nSuccess in this role requires exceptional people leadership, strong business judgment, and the ability to build systems and processes that enable teams to operate effectively at scale. You will partner closely with leaders across Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to deliver exceptional outcomes for customers while helping shape the future of Legal Engineering at Harvey.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, develop, and scale a team of Legal Engineer Managers - Product Specialists and their organisations serving Harvey's law firm and in-house customers.\n\n - Build the systems, processes, and operating mechanisms that enable Legal Engineering to deliver exceptional customer outcomes at scale.\n\n - Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, Customer Success, and Operations to align priorities and drive execution across the business.\n\n - Act as a trusted advisor to law firm and in-house legal leaders and an influential partner to senior stakeholders across Harvey.\n\n - Drive organisational performance through effective planning, resource management, talent development, and operational excellence.\n\n - Help define the future of Legal Engineering and how Harvey partners with the world's leading law firms and corporate legal departments.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified lawyer with 9+ years of post-qualification experience (PQE).\n\n - Experience practicing law at a top-tier law firm and/or in-house at a leading company, with significant client-facing experience.\n\n - Experience leading managers and manager-led organisations, not solely individual contributors.\n\n - Demonstrated success building and scaling high-performing teams in complex, fast-paced environments.\n\n - Experience owning organisational systems, processes, and operating models.\n\n - Proven ability to build strong cross-functional partnerships and drive results across multiple stakeholders.\n\n - Strong track record of managing upward and influencing senior leaders.\n\n - Experience representing an organisation externally and building trusted relationships with executive-level stakeholders.\n\n - Deep familiarity with legal technology and AI tools, and a strong understanding of how law firms and in-house legal teams operate day to day.\n\n - Exceptional communication, leadership, and organisational skills.\n   \n   \n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience leading teams outside of a traditional law firm or in-house hierarchy.\n\n - Experience in legal technology, professional services, consulting, legal innovation, legal operations, or other customer-facing organisations.\n\n - Experience operating in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Experience leading globally distributed or pan-EMEA teams.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to create structure and drive execution in rapidly evolving environments.\n\n - Experience working across multiple legal practice areas or with a broad range of law firm and in-house stakeholders.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f30a1b59-279c-43cb-bf56-1745a84dfd82","title":"Staff Corporate Security Engineer","department":"Security","team":"CorpSec","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-01T00:44:39.928+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f30a1b59-279c-43cb-bf56-1745a84dfd82","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f30a1b59-279c-43cb-bf56-1745a84dfd82/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale, entrusting Harvey with their most sensitive documents in the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role joins Harvey's corporate security function, which secures the company's IT and business systems as Harvey grows rapidly, balancing risk with user experience while validating every assumption through threat modeling and real-world testing rather than relying on best practice alone.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It is a strong fit for someone at the intersection of security engineering and enterprise systems- someone who understands how data flows between SaaS applications, can pinpoint where security breaks down in complex integrations, and knows how to build controls that scale. Experience with eDiscovery workflows and legal holds is a meaningful differentiator given the nature of Harvey's customer base.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enterprise Integrations &amp; SaaS Security:</strong> Design, implement, and govern security controls for cross-application data flows, API integrations, OAuth connections, and third-party SaaS platforms. Own the security review lifecycle for new integrations and automate posture monitoring to catch drift early.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>eDiscovery &amp; Legal Hold Program:</strong> Continue to build and operate Harvey's legal hold infrastructure, including data preservation, collection workflows, and custodian management. Partner with Legal and Compliance to meet litigation readiness requirements across our collaboration and productivity stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>IT &amp; Business Systems Partnership:</strong> Provide security oversight across the SaaS application lifecycle — vendor onboarding assessments, ongoing configuration review, and decommissioning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Endpoint Security:</strong> Support endpoint security policies and vulnerability management, ensuring endpoint telemetry feeds into detection and response workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security Detection &amp; Response:</strong> Develop scripts and integrations that extend visibility across corporate systems, partnering with the Detection &amp; Response team to surface signals from SaaS and business applications.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience securing enterprise SaaS environments, including integration security, API token management, OAuth governance, and cross-application data flow risk — with working knowledge of authentication/authorization standards (SAML, OIDC, SCIM, X.509) and the ability to debug real-world integration failures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or managing eDiscovery and legal hold programs, including data preservation workflows, custodian management, and coordination with Legal and outside counsel. Familiarity with tools such as Purview, Vault, Relativity, Everlaw, or similar platforms is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong software engineering fundamentals with proficiency in Python and/or Go, including building integrations against SaaS APIs (not just configuring through consoles), and experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform and/or Pulumi for managing security configurations in a repeatable, auditable way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify risks and vulnerabilities in IT and business systems and communicate that risk clearly to stakeholders across engineering, legal, and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with endpoint security for macOS and Windows environments, and experience with tools such as Okta, Google Workspace, Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Microsoft Entra/Azure/Intune, JAMF, Tines, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in security engineering, corporate engineering, IT, or a related program management function with a security focus. Experience with generative AI or the legal industry is not required — but genuine curiosity about both will serve you well here.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $330,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale, entrusting Harvey with their most sensitive documents in the process.\n\nThis role joins Harvey's corporate security function, which secures the company's IT and business systems as Harvey grows rapidly, balancing risk with user experience while validating every assumption through threat modeling and real-world testing rather than relying on best practice alone.\n\nIt is a strong fit for someone at the intersection of security engineering and enterprise systems- someone who understands how data flows between SaaS applications, can pinpoint where security breaks down in complex integrations, and knows how to build controls that scale. Experience with eDiscovery workflows and legal holds is a meaningful differentiator given the nature of Harvey's customer base.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Enterprise Integrations & SaaS Security: Design, implement, and govern security controls for cross-application data flows, API integrations, OAuth connections, and third-party SaaS platforms. Own the security review lifecycle for new integrations and automate posture monitoring to catch drift early.\n\n - eDiscovery & Legal Hold Program: Continue to build and operate Harvey's legal hold infrastructure, including data preservation, collection workflows, and custodian management. Partner with Legal and Compliance to meet litigation readiness requirements across our collaboration and productivity stack.\n\n - IT & Business Systems Partnership: Provide security oversight across the SaaS application lifecycle — vendor onboarding assessments, ongoing configuration review, and decommissioning.\n\n - Endpoint Security: Support endpoint security policies and vulnerability management, ensuring endpoint telemetry feeds into detection and response workflows.\n\n - Security Detection & Response: Develop scripts and integrations that extend visibility across corporate systems, partnering with the Detection & Response team to surface signals from SaaS and business applications.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Demonstrated experience securing enterprise SaaS environments, including integration security, API token management, OAuth governance, and cross-application data flow risk — with working knowledge of authentication/authorization standards (SAML, OIDC, SCIM, X.509) and the ability to debug real-world integration failures.\n\n - Experience building or managing eDiscovery and legal hold programs, including data preservation workflows, custodian management, and coordination with Legal and outside counsel. Familiarity with tools such as Purview, Vault, Relativity, Everlaw, or similar platforms is a plus.\n\n - Strong software engineering fundamentals with proficiency in Python and/or Go, including building integrations against SaaS APIs (not just configuring through consoles), and experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform and/or Pulumi for managing security configurations in a repeatable, auditable way.\n\n - Ability to identify risks and vulnerabilities in IT and business systems and communicate that risk clearly to stakeholders across engineering, legal, and executive audiences.\n\n - Familiarity with endpoint security for macOS and Windows environments, and experience with tools such as Okta, Google Workspace, Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Microsoft Entra/Azure/Intune, JAMF, Tines, or similar platforms.\n\n - 4+ years of experience in security engineering, corporate engineering, IT, or a related program management function with a security focus. Experience with generative AI or the legal industry is not required — but genuine curiosity about both will serve you well here.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $330,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AH1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $330K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f63030e8-ab75-4b7b-9f77-0bed0bb8da60","tierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"430a3943-d4b4-4010-b7b0-a12311e25b94","summary":"$220K – $330K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"id":"5bff8975-d5b7-49b5-8f1d-48d38bc64c0c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2cdc875a-44cb-4d70-a184-e9579f561d6c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"fa02d0c2-4a44-4deb-a409-6a3b3bd05e9c","title":"Staff Corporate Security Engineer","department":"Security","team":"CorpSec","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-01T00:44:42.658+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fa02d0c2-4a44-4deb-a409-6a3b3bd05e9c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fa02d0c2-4a44-4deb-a409-6a3b3bd05e9c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale, entrusting Harvey with their most sensitive documents in the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role joins Harvey's corporate security function, which secures the company's IT and business systems as Harvey grows rapidly, balancing risk with user experience while validating every assumption through threat modeling and real-world testing rather than relying on best practice alone.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It is a strong fit for someone at the intersection of security engineering and enterprise systems- someone who understands how data flows between SaaS applications, can pinpoint where security breaks down in complex integrations, and knows how to build controls that scale. Experience with eDiscovery workflows and legal holds is a meaningful differentiator given the nature of Harvey's customer base.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enterprise Integrations &amp; SaaS Security:</strong> Design, implement, and govern security controls for cross-application data flows, API integrations, OAuth connections, and third-party SaaS platforms. Own the security review lifecycle for new integrations and automate posture monitoring to catch drift early.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>eDiscovery &amp; Legal Hold Program:</strong> Continue to build and operate Harvey's legal hold infrastructure, including data preservation, collection workflows, and custodian management. Partner with Legal and Compliance to meet litigation readiness requirements across our collaboration and productivity stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>IT &amp; Business Systems Partnership:</strong> Provide security oversight across the SaaS application lifecycle — vendor onboarding assessments, ongoing configuration review, and decommissioning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Endpoint Security:</strong> Support endpoint security policies and vulnerability management, ensuring endpoint telemetry feeds into detection and response workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security Detection &amp; Response:</strong> Develop scripts and integrations that extend visibility across corporate systems, partnering with the Detection &amp; Response team to surface signals from SaaS and business applications.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience securing enterprise SaaS environments, including integration security, API token management, OAuth governance, and cross-application data flow risk — with working knowledge of authentication/authorization standards (SAML, OIDC, SCIM, X.509) and the ability to debug real-world integration failures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or managing eDiscovery and legal hold programs, including data preservation workflows, custodian management, and coordination with Legal and outside counsel. Familiarity with tools such as Purview, Vault, Relativity, Everlaw, or similar platforms is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong software engineering fundamentals with proficiency in Python and/or Go, including building integrations against SaaS APIs (not just configuring through consoles), and experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform and/or Pulumi for managing security configurations in a repeatable, auditable way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify risks and vulnerabilities in IT and business systems and communicate that risk clearly to stakeholders across engineering, legal, and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with endpoint security for macOS and Windows environments, and experience with tools such as Okta, Google Workspace, Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Microsoft Entra/Azure/Intune, JAMF, Tines, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in security engineering, corporate engineering, IT, or a related program management function with a security focus. Experience with generative AI or the legal industry is not required — but genuine curiosity about both will serve you well here.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$220,000 - $330,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nSome of the world's largest companies and their law firms use Harvey's AI to deliver world-class client services at unprecedented scale, entrusting Harvey with their most sensitive documents in the process.\n\nThis role joins Harvey's corporate security function, which secures the company's IT and business systems as Harvey grows rapidly, balancing risk with user experience while validating every assumption through threat modeling and real-world testing rather than relying on best practice alone.\n\nIt is a strong fit for someone at the intersection of security engineering and enterprise systems- someone who understands how data flows between SaaS applications, can pinpoint where security breaks down in complex integrations, and knows how to build controls that scale. Experience with eDiscovery workflows and legal holds is a meaningful differentiator given the nature of Harvey's customer base.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Enterprise Integrations & SaaS Security: Design, implement, and govern security controls for cross-application data flows, API integrations, OAuth connections, and third-party SaaS platforms. Own the security review lifecycle for new integrations and automate posture monitoring to catch drift early.\n\n - eDiscovery & Legal Hold Program: Continue to build and operate Harvey's legal hold infrastructure, including data preservation, collection workflows, and custodian management. Partner with Legal and Compliance to meet litigation readiness requirements across our collaboration and productivity stack.\n\n - IT & Business Systems Partnership: Provide security oversight across the SaaS application lifecycle — vendor onboarding assessments, ongoing configuration review, and decommissioning.\n\n - Endpoint Security: Support endpoint security policies and vulnerability management, ensuring endpoint telemetry feeds into detection and response workflows.\n\n - Security Detection & Response: Develop scripts and integrations that extend visibility across corporate systems, partnering with the Detection & Response team to surface signals from SaaS and business applications.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Demonstrated experience securing enterprise SaaS environments, including integration security, API token management, OAuth governance, and cross-application data flow risk — with working knowledge of authentication/authorization standards (SAML, OIDC, SCIM, X.509) and the ability to debug real-world integration failures.\n\n - Experience building or managing eDiscovery and legal hold programs, including data preservation workflows, custodian management, and coordination with Legal and outside counsel. Familiarity with tools such as Purview, Vault, Relativity, Everlaw, or similar platforms is a plus.\n\n - Strong software engineering fundamentals with proficiency in Python and/or Go, including building integrations against SaaS APIs (not just configuring through consoles), and experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform and/or Pulumi for managing security configurations in a repeatable, auditable way.\n\n - Ability to identify risks and vulnerabilities in IT and business systems and communicate that risk clearly to stakeholders across engineering, legal, and executive audiences.\n\n - Familiarity with endpoint security for macOS and Windows environments, and experience with tools such as Okta, Google Workspace, Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Microsoft Entra/Azure/Intune, JAMF, Tines, or similar platforms.\n\n - 4+ years of experience in security engineering, corporate engineering, IT, or a related program management function with a security focus. Experience with generative AI or the legal industry is not required — but genuine curiosity about both will serve you well here.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$220,000 - $330,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AH1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $330K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5286d5cf-e6a4-4274-adde-836cab7f3bda","tierSummary":"$220K – $330K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ad2284de-6427-4767-9321-83ec933bdbfc","summary":"$220K – $330K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"id":"f3717fdf-7013-47e0-a892-802569cabe2d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"48af9a8c-9343-48e0-89d8-40c0c994adc5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":330000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ef285771-5770-42b9-8edd-542447793924","title":"Staff Web Engineer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T23:02:12.595+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ef285771-5770-42b9-8edd-542447793924","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ef285771-5770-42b9-8edd-542447793924/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Web Engineer joins Harvey's Web team as the senior technical leader for the architecture, data foundations, and systems integration behind <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and every web-facing surface. The team's mission is to make Harvey's web presence evolve at the velocity of the product itself — reliable, observable, and fast enough that Marketing and GTM can ship without waiting on engineering.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns the technical strategy for that platform: the Next.js and Sanity architecture, the integration layer connecting the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, and GTM systems, and the automation and testing practices the team currently lacks. You will be the most senior engineer on a small, front-end-leaning team, setting standards and mentoring as much as building.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You partner directly with Harvey's product engineering, security, and infrastructure organizations to make sure the web platform meets the same bar as the rest of the company. It is a rare opportunity to build foundational systems from scratch at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with unusually direct line of sight from your work to the company's growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the architecture of Harvey's web platform end to end — the Next.js/Vercel application, the Sanity content layer, and the services and APIs behind them — with a focus on reliability, performance, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the data foundations and integration patterns that connect the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, CRM, and GTM systems, supporting both real-time and batch workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish automation, CI/CD, preview/deploy tooling, and robust automated testing where little exists today, reducing operational toil and increasing team velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set observability standards — structured logging, tracing, Core Web Vitals and performance budgets, alerting — so the team can catch and resolve issues before Marketing does.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead how the team applies AI and ML to web workflows, from content operations to personalization to internal tooling, and act as the bridge between product engineering and web engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security and Infrastructure to harden the platform without slowing developer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical leadership and mentorship to a small, front-end-focused team through code review, design review, and architectural guidance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of Web Engineering experience with deep back-end and systems expertise, and a track record of owning technical architecture at a staff level of scope and ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of the modern web stack — React/Next.js, TypeScript, and server-side rendering — paired with genuine back-end depth (Node, Python, or comparable) rather than front-end specialization alone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience architecting and operating headless CMS and content platforms (Sanity, Contentful, or similar) at scale, including schema design and publishing workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience building and operating reliable production systems: CI/CD, infrastructure-as-code, observability tooling, and performance optimization against real user metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with data infrastructure fundamentals — SQL/NoSQL databases, caching, queuing, API and webhook integration patterns — in service of marketing and GTM systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production web experiences or content workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to mentor less experienced engineers, influence across functions, and operate autonomously in a small team where you are the deepest technical voice.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Vercel platform experience; marketing/GTM systems integration (HubSpot, Salesforce, Segment, analytics); SEO and web performance engineering; prior experience as the first or most senior engineer on a web platform team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$146,600 - $201,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Staff Web Engineer joins Harvey's Web team as the senior technical leader for the architecture, data foundations, and systems integration behind harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and every web-facing surface. The team's mission is to make Harvey's web presence evolve at the velocity of the product itself — reliable, observable, and fast enough that Marketing and GTM can ship without waiting on engineering.\n\nThis role owns the technical strategy for that platform: the Next.js and Sanity architecture, the integration layer connecting the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, and GTM systems, and the automation and testing practices the team currently lacks. You will be the most senior engineer on a small, front-end-leaning team, setting standards and mentoring as much as building.\n\nYou partner directly with Harvey's product engineering, security, and infrastructure organizations to make sure the web platform meets the same bar as the rest of the company. It is a rare opportunity to build foundational systems from scratch at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with unusually direct line of sight from your work to the company's growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the architecture of Harvey's web platform end to end — the Next.js/Vercel application, the Sanity content layer, and the services and APIs behind them — with a focus on reliability, performance, and scalability.\n\n - Design and build the data foundations and integration patterns that connect the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, CRM, and GTM systems, supporting both real-time and batch workloads.\n\n - Establish automation, CI/CD, preview/deploy tooling, and robust automated testing where little exists today, reducing operational toil and increasing team velocity.\n\n - Set observability standards — structured logging, tracing, Core Web Vitals and performance budgets, alerting — so the team can catch and resolve issues before Marketing does.\n\n - Lead how the team applies AI and ML to web workflows, from content operations to personalization to internal tooling, and act as the bridge between product engineering and web engineering.\n\n - Partner with Security and Infrastructure to harden the platform without slowing developer experience.\n\n - Provide technical leadership and mentorship to a small, front-end-focused team through code review, design review, and architectural guidance.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of Web Engineering experience with deep back-end and systems expertise, and a track record of owning technical architecture at a staff level of scope and ambiguity.\n\n - Strong command of the modern web stack — React/Next.js, TypeScript, and server-side rendering — paired with genuine back-end depth (Node, Python, or comparable) rather than front-end specialization alone.\n\n - Experience architecting and operating headless CMS and content platforms (Sanity, Contentful, or similar) at scale, including schema design and publishing workflows.\n\n - Proven experience building and operating reliable production systems: CI/CD, infrastructure-as-code, observability tooling, and performance optimization against real user metrics.\n\n - Fluency with data infrastructure fundamentals — SQL/NoSQL databases, caching, queuing, API and webhook integration patterns — in service of marketing and GTM systems.\n\n - Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production web experiences or content workflows.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to mentor less experienced engineers, influence across functions, and operate autonomously in a small team where you are the deepest technical voice.\n\nNice to have: Vercel platform experience; marketing/GTM systems integration (HubSpot, Salesforce, Segment, analytics); SEO and web performance engineering; prior experience as the first or most senior engineer on a web platform team.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$146,600 - $201,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JC2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$146.6K – $201.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$146.6K - $201.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a7e9e2bb-4e95-4998-9e21-296dbf28d9a7","tierSummary":"$146.6K – $201.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3a4c0409-f273-414c-bfc7-62587f2213ef","summary":"$146.6K – $201.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":201500},{"id":"a161b38c-d182-4052-8e2b-c95973492c57","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5a3a62e7-30f7-429a-82db-0e9394560f0f","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":201500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7a3b9337-ac67-4255-8db5-08bb3d57541e","title":"Senior Product Manager, Command Center","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T19:14:32.396+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7a3b9337-ac67-4255-8db5-08bb3d57541e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7a3b9337-ac67-4255-8db5-08bb3d57541e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the definitive AI platform for legal, and as our enterprise customer base grows, the tools that let firms and legal departments observe, govern, and act on how Harvey is used have never been more critical. The Senior Product Manager, Command Center will own the product vision and roadmap for Harvey's Command Center and internal admin platform — the operational control surface where enterprise administrators monitor adoption and usage, manage users and access, and steer their organization's deployment of Harvey at scale. This role sits within the Product organization and partners closely with Engineering, Design, Security, and Go-to-Market teams to ensure Command Center meets the rigorous requirements of the world's largest and most regulated enterprises. You will have a direct and measurable impact on Harvey's ability to land and expand within complex organizations by making the platform observable, governable, and easy to administer at scale. This is a high-visibility, scale-up surface with significant room to shape the team and the product as our enterprise footprint expands.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and drive the product strategy and roadmap for Command Center, spanning usage and adoption analytics, administrative controls, and organizational governance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering and Design to deliver scalable, secure, and intuitive admin experiences that meet the operational needs of large enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage directly with enterprise customers, customer success, and sales teams to deeply understand admin pain points, reporting and governance requirements, and integration needs — and translate those insights into high-impact product investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and track key metrics for platform adoption, admin efficiency, and governance coverage, using data to inform prioritization and measure success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design the dashboards, reporting, and controls that turn product usage data into actionable visibility for customer administrators and internal leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive alignment across stakeholders on trade-offs, sequencing, and scope, communicating clearly at both the executive and working-team levels.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience, with significant time spent building B2B SaaS products for large enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with enterprise admin, analytics, and governance domains such as usage reporting, identity management (SSO, SCIM, RBAC), audit logging, and access controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A technical background or a strong desire to go deep on engineering design and trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to navigate complex enterprise environments, working with security, compliance, and IT stakeholders to deliver products that satisfy rigorous organizational requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and communication skills, with experience using data to drive decisions and the ability to articulate a clear product vision to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of shipping high-quality products end-to-end, from discovery and definition through launch and iteration, in fast-paced and ambiguous environments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$177,700 - $266,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the definitive AI platform for legal, and as our enterprise customer base grows, the tools that let firms and legal departments observe, govern, and act on how Harvey is used have never been more critical. The Senior Product Manager, Command Center will own the product vision and roadmap for Harvey's Command Center and internal admin platform — the operational control surface where enterprise administrators monitor adoption and usage, manage users and access, and steer their organization's deployment of Harvey at scale. This role sits within the Product organization and partners closely with Engineering, Design, Security, and Go-to-Market teams to ensure Command Center meets the rigorous requirements of the world's largest and most regulated enterprises. You will have a direct and measurable impact on Harvey's ability to land and expand within complex organizations by making the platform observable, governable, and easy to administer at scale. This is a high-visibility, scale-up surface with significant room to shape the team and the product as our enterprise footprint expands.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define and drive the product strategy and roadmap for Command Center, spanning usage and adoption analytics, administrative controls, and organizational governance.\n\n - Partner with Engineering and Design to deliver scalable, secure, and intuitive admin experiences that meet the operational needs of large enterprise customers.\n\n - Engage directly with enterprise customers, customer success, and sales teams to deeply understand admin pain points, reporting and governance requirements, and integration needs — and translate those insights into high-impact product investments.\n\n - Establish and track key metrics for platform adoption, admin efficiency, and governance coverage, using data to inform prioritization and measure success.\n\n - Design the dashboards, reporting, and controls that turn product usage data into actionable visibility for customer administrators and internal leadership.\n\n - Drive alignment across stakeholders on trade-offs, sequencing, and scope, communicating clearly at both the executive and working-team levels.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience, with significant time spent building B2B SaaS products for large enterprise customers.\n\n - Deep familiarity with enterprise admin, analytics, and governance domains such as usage reporting, identity management (SSO, SCIM, RBAC), audit logging, and access controls.\n\n - A technical background or a strong desire to go deep on engineering design and trade-offs.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to navigate complex enterprise environments, working with security, compliance, and IT stakeholders to deliver products that satisfy rigorous organizational requirements.\n\n - Strong analytical and communication skills, with experience using data to drive decisions and the ability to articulate a clear product vision to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n - A track record of shipping high-quality products end-to-end, from discovery and definition through launch and iteration, in fast-paced and ambiguous environments.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$177,700 - $266,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$177.7K - $266.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"91252946-397a-483e-be82-4f391d24ea74","tierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7bdac2d3-c6af-47d3-8385-cb95744d5315","summary":"$177.7K – $266.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"id":"2fffb35b-8508-4622-b8e5-0a61b949d51b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"90134cbf-708a-46fa-bc65-28211a757ad1","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2a708f5d-9396-4712-9c9c-68bfbd0b8304","title":"Sales Development Representative  (German Speaking)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Stockholm","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Milan","address":{"postalAddress":{}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:41:50.631+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2a708f5d-9396-4712-9c9c-68bfbd0b8304","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2a708f5d-9396-4712-9c9c-68bfbd0b8304/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h3>Please note that this role requires relocation to Dublin, Ireland.</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Role Overview</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in written and spoken English and German.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-KS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nPLEASE NOTE THAT THIS ROLE REQUIRES RELOCATION TO DUBLIN, IRELAND.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Sales Development Representative at Harvey, you will be at the forefront of driving the growth and adoption of our AI solutions across the legal and professional services markets. You will own early-stage pipeline creation across EMEA by engaging law firms, professional services organizations, and in-house legal teams, understanding their unique challenges, and introducing Harvey’s AI platform.\n\nThis role combines highly personalized outbound prospecting with thoughtful inbound qualification. Your ability to articulate the value of Harvey's products, paired with curiosity about AI and a rigorous approach to your work, will help us expand our reach and shape the future of knowledge work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build revenue pipeline aligned with Harvey’s strategic customer profile using a variety of outbound tools and highly personalized outreach.\n\n - Proactively prospect into target accounts across EMEA through email, phone, LinkedIn, and other creative outbound strategies.\n\n - Source and qualify new sales opportunities through both outbound prospecting and inbound lead follow-up.\n\n - Conduct thoughtful discovery conversations to understand customer workflows and determine strong opportunities for the sales team.\n\n - Respond quickly to inbound interest and ensure timely qualification and follow-up.\n\n - Partner closely with Account Executives to develop opportunities and support early-stage deal progression.\n\n - Provide data-driven insights to inform sales strategies and improve prospecting effectiveness.\n\n - Contribute to developing Harvey’s sales playbook and document learnings as we scale the team globally.\n\n - Consistently achieve and exceed qualified pipeline and activity targets.\n\n\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - 1–2+ years of experience in a fast-growing startup, preferably in sales development or project management.\n\n - Fluent in written and spoken English and German.\n\n - Strong executive presence and comfort presenting to sophisticated executive buyers.\n\n - Independent, driven, and approach work with rigor and thoughtfulness.\n\n - Ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Proficient with Salesforce, Salesloft, and reporting tools.\n\n - Collaborative team player able to work across internal functions.\n\n - Passionate about Harvey’s mission with a strong understanding of AI applications in knowledge work.\n\n - Interest in the legal profession; experience in the legal industry is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-KS2\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"04aa6087-3ca1-4b73-9320-3f1e95cf9e6e","title":"Senior Product Manager, Command Center","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T19:14:42.645+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04aa6087-3ca1-4b73-9320-3f1e95cf9e6e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/04aa6087-3ca1-4b73-9320-3f1e95cf9e6e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the definitive AI platform for legal, and as our enterprise customer base grows, the tools that let firms and legal departments observe, govern, and act on how Harvey is used have never been more critical. The Senior Product Manager, Command Center will own the product vision and roadmap for Harvey's Command Center and internal admin platform — the operational control surface where enterprise administrators monitor adoption and usage, manage users and access, and steer their organization's deployment of Harvey at scale. This role sits within the Product organization and partners closely with Engineering, Design, Security, and Go-to-Market teams to ensure Command Center meets the rigorous requirements of the world's largest and most regulated enterprises. You will have a direct and measurable impact on Harvey's ability to land and expand within complex organizations by making the platform observable, governable, and easy to administer at scale. This is a high-visibility, scale-up surface with significant room to shape the team and the product as our enterprise footprint expands.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and drive the product strategy and roadmap for Command Center, spanning usage and adoption analytics, administrative controls, and organizational governance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering and Design to deliver scalable, secure, and intuitive admin experiences that meet the operational needs of large enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage directly with enterprise customers, customer success, and sales teams to deeply understand admin pain points, reporting and governance requirements, and integration needs — and translate those insights into high-impact product investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and track key metrics for platform adoption, admin efficiency, and governance coverage, using data to inform prioritization and measure success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design the dashboards, reporting, and controls that turn product usage data into actionable visibility for customer administrators and internal leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive alignment across stakeholders on trade-offs, sequencing, and scope, communicating clearly at both the executive and working-team levels.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience, with significant time spent building B2B SaaS products for large enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with enterprise admin, analytics, and governance domains such as usage reporting, identity management (SSO, SCIM, RBAC), audit logging, and access controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A technical background or a strong desire to go deep on engineering design and trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to navigate complex enterprise environments, working with security, compliance, and IT stakeholders to deliver products that satisfy rigorous organizational requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and communication skills, with experience using data to drive decisions and the ability to articulate a clear product vision to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of shipping high-quality products end-to-end, from discovery and definition through launch and iteration, in fast-paced and ambiguous environments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$177,700 - $266,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the definitive AI platform for legal, and as our enterprise customer base grows, the tools that let firms and legal departments observe, govern, and act on how Harvey is used have never been more critical. The Senior Product Manager, Command Center will own the product vision and roadmap for Harvey's Command Center and internal admin platform — the operational control surface where enterprise administrators monitor adoption and usage, manage users and access, and steer their organization's deployment of Harvey at scale. This role sits within the Product organization and partners closely with Engineering, Design, Security, and Go-to-Market teams to ensure Command Center meets the rigorous requirements of the world's largest and most regulated enterprises. You will have a direct and measurable impact on Harvey's ability to land and expand within complex organizations by making the platform observable, governable, and easy to administer at scale. This is a high-visibility, scale-up surface with significant room to shape the team and the product as our enterprise footprint expands.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define and drive the product strategy and roadmap for Command Center, spanning usage and adoption analytics, administrative controls, and organizational governance.\n\n - Partner with Engineering and Design to deliver scalable, secure, and intuitive admin experiences that meet the operational needs of large enterprise customers.\n\n - Engage directly with enterprise customers, customer success, and sales teams to deeply understand admin pain points, reporting and governance requirements, and integration needs — and translate those insights into high-impact product investments.\n\n - Establish and track key metrics for platform adoption, admin efficiency, and governance coverage, using data to inform prioritization and measure success.\n\n - Design the dashboards, reporting, and controls that turn product usage data into actionable visibility for customer administrators and internal leadership.\n\n - Drive alignment across stakeholders on trade-offs, sequencing, and scope, communicating clearly at both the executive and working-team levels.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience, with significant time spent building B2B SaaS products for large enterprise customers.\n\n - Deep familiarity with enterprise admin, analytics, and governance domains such as usage reporting, identity management (SSO, SCIM, RBAC), audit logging, and access controls.\n\n - A technical background or a strong desire to go deep on engineering design and trade-offs.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to navigate complex enterprise environments, working with security, compliance, and IT stakeholders to deliver products that satisfy rigorous organizational requirements.\n\n - Strong analytical and communication skills, with experience using data to drive decisions and the ability to articulate a clear product vision to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n - A track record of shipping high-quality products end-to-end, from discovery and definition through launch and iteration, in fast-paced and ambiguous environments.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$177,700 - $266,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$177.7K - $266.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2ad7fd28-87bd-4a05-b78c-1d2b85e8b600","tierSummary":"$177.7K – $266.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4b3a60ef-41d9-4997-85d9-bf94585a136a","summary":"$177.7K – $266.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"id":"25db56d8-d9fe-442e-aa2d-55fd38374b0c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5c00c537-c79d-47b7-b40e-604d08756ffe","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177700,"maxValue":266500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f0e4e24a-2a7a-4fc4-8872-9a8a762fecf5","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager, Evaluation Quality","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-04T16:25:51.563+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f0e4e24a-2a7a-4fc4-8872-9a8a762fecf5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f0e4e24a-2a7a-4fc4-8872-9a8a762fecf5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a senior operator to own the quality bar behind Harvey’s human evaluations. As we scale globally, the volume of eval work is growing 10x, but volume only matters if the output is trusted. This role makes Human Data’s signal decision-grade: rigorous, calibrated, and reproducible enough that Product, Engineering, and AI Research act on it to ship.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a member of our <strong>Evaluation Operations</strong> team, you’ll work alongside our Evaluation Operations Manager (who runs throughput and coordination) and partner closely with Applied Legal Researchers, Product, Engineering, and AI Research. You'll set the standard for what \"good\" looks like across eval data and methodology, and own the data analyses to make conclusions that teams will rely on, building the stakeholder trust that lets EPD act on the signal.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the quality bar for Harvey’s human evaluations: define what “good” looks like for eval methodology and data analysis, and produce decision-grade outputs for EPD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Author and maintain the evaluation guidelines, instructions, and databases that contract attorneys work from</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Standardize and streamline rubric and evaluation design into repeatable templates and one documented methodology, partnering with Applied Legal Research (ALR), who supplies feature-specific legal depth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own contract-attorney quality: onboarding, calibration training, inter-rater reliability, and the feedback loop (including benchmarks and gold references) that keeps judgment consistent across attorneys and over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting quantitative and qualitative statistical analyses, diagnosing error states, investigating root causes, and turning raw eval results into a structured, prioritized signal Product and ALR can act on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run QA on vendor and contract-attorney deliverables against a defined bar before results inform a launch decision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure the quality bar holds across jurisdictions and non-English geographies as coverage expands</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish one standard, documented way to analyze eval results, and build lightweight operational dashboards to track rater capability and eval-program health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ALR in a review step that certifies an evaluation is sound before it scales to contract attorneys</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with ALR and Analytics to determine where human eval aligns with online signal and where it can provide expanded insights</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years in product operations, research operations, evaluation/QA operations, or quality program management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning quality inputs (guidelines, instructions, benchmarks, QA procedures) for complex, expert-driven or human-in-the-loop work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience onboarding, training, and calibrating a distributed pool of expert raters, annotators, or reviewers, and running the feedback loop that improves their quality over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enough grounding in measurement concepts (calibration, inter-rater reliability, sampling, rubric design) to independently set up and own the quality of our evaluation loop yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with running quantitative and qualitative data analyses, interpreting and running statistical tests on evaluation data (natively or with AI tool support), and communicating conclusions to various stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A record of scaling and streamlining evaluation quality processes under shipping pressure, with a bias toward documentation and reproducibility over one-off analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work deeply with domain experts (e.g., ALR / lawyers) and translate nuanced judgment into repeatable, documented standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional coordination across Product, Engineering, Research, ALR, and data providers/vendors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can build credibility and trust with stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias to action and high ownership, from writing the guideline to auditing a vendor batch line by line</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in legal tech or working with domain experts in regulated industries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning quality across multiple markets, languages, or jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built calibration, inter-rater reliability, or capability-tracking systems for annotation or evaluation pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience transitioning evaluation work in-house or otherwise improving evaluation ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with LLM-as-judge / automated evaluation used alongside human eval</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Early employee at a hyper-growth startup, or experience at a world-class product or platform operations org</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re looking for a senior operator to own the quality bar behind Harvey’s human evaluations. As we scale globally, the volume of eval work is growing 10x, but volume only matters if the output is trusted. This role makes Human Data’s signal decision-grade: rigorous, calibrated, and reproducible enough that Product, Engineering, and AI Research act on it to ship.\n\n\n\nAs a member of our Evaluation Operations team, you’ll work alongside our Evaluation Operations Manager (who runs throughput and coordination) and partner closely with Applied Legal Researchers, Product, Engineering, and AI Research. You'll set the standard for what \"good\" looks like across eval data and methodology, and own the data analyses to make conclusions that teams will rely on, building the stakeholder trust that lets EPD act on the signal.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the quality bar for Harvey’s human evaluations: define what “good” looks like for eval methodology and data analysis, and produce decision-grade outputs for EPD\n\n - Author and maintain the evaluation guidelines, instructions, and databases that contract attorneys work from\n\n - Standardize and streamline rubric and evaluation design into repeatable templates and one documented methodology, partnering with Applied Legal Research (ALR), who supplies feature-specific legal depth\n\n - Own contract-attorney quality: onboarding, calibration training, inter-rater reliability, and the feedback loop (including benchmarks and gold references) that keeps judgment consistent across attorneys and over time\n\n - Conducting quantitative and qualitative statistical analyses, diagnosing error states, investigating root causes, and turning raw eval results into a structured, prioritized signal Product and ALR can act on\n\n - Run QA on vendor and contract-attorney deliverables against a defined bar before results inform a launch decision\n\n - Ensure the quality bar holds across jurisdictions and non-English geographies as coverage expands\n\n - Establish one standard, documented way to analyze eval results, and build lightweight operational dashboards to track rater capability and eval-program health\n\n - Support ALR in a review step that certifies an evaluation is sound before it scales to contract attorneys\n\n - Partner with ALR and Analytics to determine where human eval aligns with online signal and where it can provide expanded insights\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years in product operations, research operations, evaluation/QA operations, or quality program management\n\n - A track record of owning quality inputs (guidelines, instructions, benchmarks, QA procedures) for complex, expert-driven or human-in-the-loop work\n\n - Experience onboarding, training, and calibrating a distributed pool of expert raters, annotators, or reviewers, and running the feedback loop that improves their quality over time\n\n - Enough grounding in measurement concepts (calibration, inter-rater reliability, sampling, rubric design) to independently set up and own the quality of our evaluation loop yourself\n\n - Experience with running quantitative and qualitative data analyses, interpreting and running statistical tests on evaluation data (natively or with AI tool support), and communicating conclusions to various stakeholders\n\n - A record of scaling and streamlining evaluation quality processes under shipping pressure, with a bias toward documentation and reproducibility over one-off analysis\n\n - Ability to work deeply with domain experts (e.g., ALR / lawyers) and translate nuanced judgment into repeatable, documented standards\n\n - Strong cross-functional coordination across Product, Engineering, Research, ALR, and data providers/vendors\n\n - Clear communicator who can build credibility and trust with stakeholders\n\n - Bias to action and high ownership, from writing the guideline to auditing a vendor batch line by line\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience in legal tech or working with domain experts in regulated industries\n\n - Experience owning quality across multiple markets, languages, or jurisdictions\n\n - Built calibration, inter-rater reliability, or capability-tracking systems for annotation or evaluation pipelines\n\n - Experience transitioning evaluation work in-house or otherwise improving evaluation ROI\n\n - Familiarity with LLM-as-judge / automated evaluation used alongside human eval\n\n - Early employee at a hyper-growth startup, or experience at a world-class product or platform operations org\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"117b7723-8136-4391-900b-71c3b145d2a3","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7231277b-21ec-4e02-a53d-88c39abdc65a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f26fd626-2c45-4ae3-96eb-a4bc47eb0373","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"28d9e19d-5129-4eab-b8db-d317b2cf9861","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}},{"id":"563d87ad-14e7-4eef-86dc-ae06accc6b9f","title":"Mid Market Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T22:06:44.240+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/563d87ad-14e7-4eef-86dc-ae06accc6b9f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/563d87ad-14e7-4eef-86dc-ae06accc6b9f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training &amp; Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Customer Success Manager you’ll play a critical role in guiding our clients through their journey with Harvey, and help define the future of work at both law firms and in-house teams. This position is pivotal in ensuring our clients not only adopt but also derive maximum value from our technology. You'll act as a trusted advisor, deeply integrating Harvey into their business processes and workflows. This individual will also have a chance to design and deploy scalable 1:many solutions that will impact how we serve our broad mid-market customer base in a highly efficient manner at scale.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Strategic Implementation: Lead the integration of Harvey into client workflows, ensuring seamless adoption and optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Evangelize the power of LLMs as you meet with and enable end users to adopt Harvey on a daily-basis as it becomes a “must have” product.\n\n - Client Relationship Management: Serve as the primary contact for 40+ mid-market clients with a prescriptive and consultative approach and delivering a superior customer experience.\n\n - Process Creation: Drive scalability in the way we operate through documentation, designing playbooks, self-help materials, email cadences, and automation to ensure we drive efficiency in our long term mid-market strategy.\n\n - Success Metrics Management: Utilize adoption rates, benchmarks, and other key metrics to drive strategies ensuring client satisfaction and high ROI.\n\n - Advocacy and Engagement: Encourage user and stakeholder engagement, transforming them into Harvey advocates within their organizations.\n\n - Customer Health Monitoring: Use analytics and feedback to maintain customer satisfaction, ensuring readiness for renewal and expansion opportunities.\n\n - Feedback Loop: Relay client insights back to our internal teams, aiding in the continuous improvement of our product and services.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experienced professionals from legal firms or SaaS organizations, with direct experience managing a high volume of client cases and/or customers.\n\n - Individuals with excellent communication and strategic planning skills, capable of influencing stakeholders at various levels.\n\n - Results driven candidates who are able to ruthlessly prioritize competing tasks and demanding customers seamlessly.\n\n - Team players described as empathetic, committed, structured, motivated, and collaborative with a team-first mentality.\n\n - Experience with Salesforce and Catalyst, are preferred, but not required.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-EL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b85907be-9937-4bf1-91a0-4474c35e4402","title":"Head of GTM Strategy & Operations, AMER","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T18:41:18.486+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b85907be-9937-4bf1-91a0-4474c35e4402","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b85907be-9937-4bf1-91a0-4474c35e4402/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring an experienced, hands-on leader for the GTM Strategy &amp; Operations team within the Revenue Operations organization. This team serves as the core strategic and business partner function to the GTM organization, playing a critical role in driving GTM growth and operational excellence. In this role, you will lead a team of AMER Sales Business Partners and serve as a trusted advisor to AMER Sales Leadership.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership on sales planning, including annual, half year, and quarterly GTM planning cycles. This will include leading AMER territory planning, headcount planning, and quota planning to help the organization achieve aggressive growth targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership to develop field strategy for the Americas and ensure alignment with the global operating model. This includes driving forecast rigor, pipeline generation strategies, CRM hygiene, data accuracy, and operating discipline to enable predictable growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive operating rigor and scalability by establishing and evolving the operating rhythms, processes, and cadences that enable disciplined execution and support sustained GTM growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with GTM Enablement to identify capability gaps, develop targeted training programs, and support the onboarding and ramp of new AEs and SDRs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a high performing team of AMER Sales Business Partners; continuously raise the bar on team capabilities, talent development, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead high priority GTM initiatives that address complex, high-impact problems</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years in Revenue Operations or Sales Strategy &amp; Operations, or a closely related field. Ideal candidates will have a combination of operational experience in GTM Strategy &amp; Operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, and experience in investment banking, private equity, venture capital, strategy / management consulting, or other highly analytical roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of people management experience required. A nice to have would be prior experience managing managers as well.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional collaboration skills; you're energized by working across teams and can bring people together around shared goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to be an effective business partner and lead a team of business partners, with the ability to build trusted relationships, navigate diverse working styles, and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$212,000-$290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re hiring an experienced, hands-on leader for the GTM Strategy & Operations team within the Revenue Operations organization. This team serves as the core strategic and business partner function to the GTM organization, playing a critical role in driving GTM growth and operational excellence. In this role, you will lead a team of AMER Sales Business Partners and serve as a trusted advisor to AMER Sales Leadership.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership on sales planning, including annual, half year, and quarterly GTM planning cycles. This will include leading AMER territory planning, headcount planning, and quota planning to help the organization achieve aggressive growth targets.\n\n - Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership to develop field strategy for the Americas and ensure alignment with the global operating model. This includes driving forecast rigor, pipeline generation strategies, CRM hygiene, data accuracy, and operating discipline to enable predictable growth.\n\n - Drive operating rigor and scalability by establishing and evolving the operating rhythms, processes, and cadences that enable disciplined execution and support sustained GTM growth.\n\n - Partner with GTM Enablement to identify capability gaps, develop targeted training programs, and support the onboarding and ramp of new AEs and SDRs.\n\n - Lead and develop a high performing team of AMER Sales Business Partners; continuously raise the bar on team capabilities, talent development, and operational excellence.\n\n - Lead high priority GTM initiatives that address complex, high-impact problems\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in Revenue Operations or Sales Strategy & Operations, or a closely related field. Ideal candidates will have a combination of operational experience in GTM Strategy & Operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, and experience in investment banking, private equity, venture capital, strategy / management consulting, or other highly analytical roles.\n\n - 3+ years of people management experience required. A nice to have would be prior experience managing managers as well.\n\n - Strong cross-functional collaboration skills; you're energized by working across teams and can bring people together around shared goals\n\n - Demonstrated ability to be an effective business partner and lead a team of business partners, with the ability to build trusted relationships, navigate diverse working styles, and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$212,000-$290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-TM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$212K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$212K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0328417e-9d1c-46cd-9e1d-2b232ca69cf4","tierSummary":"$212K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8f657d30-ac36-4c4b-b4bb-c47a410282ab","summary":"$212K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":212000,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"c985b6a5-0fa0-441b-bbbc-daae681f7e8f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"56b979cc-783b-4439-82ed-02c6d68d3d50","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":212000,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"24175721-f785-4f85-a9b7-e80973ecdfd4","title":"Head of GTM Strategy & Operations, AMER","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T18:41:21.721+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24175721-f785-4f85-a9b7-e80973ecdfd4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/24175721-f785-4f85-a9b7-e80973ecdfd4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring an experienced, hands-on leader for the GTM Strategy &amp; Operations team within the Revenue Operations organization. This team serves as the core strategic and business partner function to the GTM organization, playing a critical role in driving GTM growth and operational excellence. In this role, you will lead a team of AMER Sales Business Partners and serve as a trusted advisor to AMER Sales Leadership.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership on sales planning, including annual, half year, and quarterly GTM planning cycles. This will include leading AMER territory planning, headcount planning, and quota planning to help the organization achieve aggressive growth targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership to develop field strategy for the Americas and ensure alignment with the global operating model. This includes driving forecast rigor, pipeline generation strategies, CRM hygiene, data accuracy, and operating discipline to enable predictable growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive operating rigor and scalability by establishing and evolving the operating rhythms, processes, and cadences that enable disciplined execution and support sustained GTM growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with GTM Enablement to identify capability gaps, develop targeted training programs, and support the onboarding and ramp of new AEs and SDRs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a high performing team of AMER Sales Business Partners; continuously raise the bar on team capabilities, talent development, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead high priority GTM initiatives that address complex, high-impact problems</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years in Revenue Operations or Sales Strategy &amp; Operations, or a closely related field. Ideal candidates will have a combination of operational experience in GTM Strategy &amp; Operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, and experience in investment banking, private equity, venture capital, strategy / management consulting, or other highly analytical roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of people management experience required. A nice to have would be prior experience managing managers as well.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional collaboration skills; you're energized by working across teams and can bring people together around shared goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to be an effective business partner and lead a team of business partners, with the ability to build trusted relationships, navigate diverse working styles, and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$212,000-$290,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re hiring an experienced, hands-on leader for the GTM Strategy & Operations team within the Revenue Operations organization. This team serves as the core strategic and business partner function to the GTM organization, playing a critical role in driving GTM growth and operational excellence. In this role, you will lead a team of AMER Sales Business Partners and serve as a trusted advisor to AMER Sales Leadership.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership on sales planning, including annual, half year, and quarterly GTM planning cycles. This will include leading AMER territory planning, headcount planning, and quota planning to help the organization achieve aggressive growth targets.\n\n - Partner with AMER Enterprise Sales Leadership to develop field strategy for the Americas and ensure alignment with the global operating model. This includes driving forecast rigor, pipeline generation strategies, CRM hygiene, data accuracy, and operating discipline to enable predictable growth.\n\n - Drive operating rigor and scalability by establishing and evolving the operating rhythms, processes, and cadences that enable disciplined execution and support sustained GTM growth.\n\n - Partner with GTM Enablement to identify capability gaps, develop targeted training programs, and support the onboarding and ramp of new AEs and SDRs.\n\n - Lead and develop a high performing team of AMER Sales Business Partners; continuously raise the bar on team capabilities, talent development, and operational excellence.\n\n - Lead high priority GTM initiatives that address complex, high-impact problems\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in Revenue Operations or Sales Strategy & Operations, or a closely related field. Ideal candidates will have a combination of operational experience in GTM Strategy & Operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, and experience in investment banking, private equity, venture capital, strategy / management consulting, or other highly analytical roles.\n\n - 3+ years of people management experience required. A nice to have would be prior experience managing managers as well.\n\n - Strong cross-functional collaboration skills; you're energized by working across teams and can bring people together around shared goals\n\n - Demonstrated ability to be an effective business partner and lead a team of business partners, with the ability to build trusted relationships, navigate diverse working styles, and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$212,000-$290,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n \n\n#LI-TM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$212K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$212K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0328417e-9d1c-46cd-9e1d-2b232ca69cf4","tierSummary":"$212K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8f657d30-ac36-4c4b-b4bb-c47a410282ab","summary":"$212K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":212000,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"c985b6a5-0fa0-441b-bbbc-daae681f7e8f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"56b979cc-783b-4439-82ed-02c6d68d3d50","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":212000,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c84964b6-9e60-4005-8580-b865f3e47b4f","title":"Staff Web Designer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T19:36:08.977+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c84964b6-9e60-4005-8580-b865f3e47b4f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c84964b6-9e60-4005-8580-b865f3e47b4f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Web Designer joins Harvey's Web team to define and elevate the design experience across <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and all web-facing surfaces. The team is responsible for translating Harvey's brand and product story into compelling, accessible, and high-performing web experiences that drive awareness, engagement, and pipeline. In this role, you will own and evolve the website design system, lead user research and testing initiatives, and set the quality bar for every page that ships. You will partner closely with web engineers, motion designers, product marketing, and brand stakeholders to deliver end-to-end design solutions at the pace a category-defining legal AI company demands. It is a rare opportunity to shape how the world first encounters Harvey—and to build the design infrastructure that scales that experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve the website design system—establishing scalable patterns, component libraries, and governance standards that maintain consistency and accelerate delivery across all web surfaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the end-to-end design process for web projects, from concept and user research through interaction design, prototyping, and detailed technical specification hand-off to web engineers and motion designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive innovation through exploration, prototyping, and user testing to continuously improve user experience, conversion, and accessibility across <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and related properties.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor junior web designers, embedding best practices around responsive design, accessibility, and design-system governance to raise the team's collective quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run design demos, present work to marketing leadership and cross-functional stakeholders, and articulate design rationale with clarity and expertise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools and emerging technologies to accelerate design workflows, explore new interaction paradigms, and push the boundary of what a best-in-class legal AI website can be.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of professional design experience with a significant focus on web and digital product design, including demonstrated impact at a staff or senior-staff level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio that showcases mastery of user experience design, interaction design, responsive web design, and design-system architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in systems thinking—building, scaling, and governing design systems that serve multiple teams and use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of modern design tools (e.g., Figma) and comfort working at the intersection of design and front-end development, including providing pixel-level specifications and technical hand-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to leverage AI-assisted design workflows and a track record of raising quality and velocity in fast-paced, high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running design reviews, stakeholder demos, and cross-functional critiques.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$146,600 - $219,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Staff Web Designer joins Harvey's Web team to define and elevate the design experience across harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and all web-facing surfaces. The team is responsible for translating Harvey's brand and product story into compelling, accessible, and high-performing web experiences that drive awareness, engagement, and pipeline. In this role, you will own and evolve the website design system, lead user research and testing initiatives, and set the quality bar for every page that ships. You will partner closely with web engineers, motion designers, product marketing, and brand stakeholders to deliver end-to-end design solutions at the pace a category-defining legal AI company demands. It is a rare opportunity to shape how the world first encounters Harvey—and to build the design infrastructure that scales that experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and evolve the website design system—establishing scalable patterns, component libraries, and governance standards that maintain consistency and accelerate delivery across all web surfaces.\n\n - Lead the end-to-end design process for web projects, from concept and user research through interaction design, prototyping, and detailed technical specification hand-off to web engineers and motion designers.\n\n - Drive innovation through exploration, prototyping, and user testing to continuously improve user experience, conversion, and accessibility across harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and related properties.\n\n - Mentor junior web designers, embedding best practices around responsive design, accessibility, and design-system governance to raise the team's collective quality bar.\n\n - Run design demos, present work to marketing leadership and cross-functional stakeholders, and articulate design rationale with clarity and expertise.\n\n - Leverage AI tools and emerging technologies to accelerate design workflows, explore new interaction paradigms, and push the boundary of what a best-in-class legal AI website can be.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of professional design experience with a significant focus on web and digital product design, including demonstrated impact at a staff or senior-staff level.\n\n - A portfolio that showcases mastery of user experience design, interaction design, responsive web design, and design-system architecture.\n\n - Deep expertise in systems thinking—building, scaling, and governing design systems that serve multiple teams and use cases.\n\n - Strong command of modern design tools (e.g., Figma) and comfort working at the intersection of design and front-end development, including providing pixel-level specifications and technical hand-offs.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to leverage AI-assisted design workflows and a track record of raising quality and velocity in fast-paced, high-growth environments.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running design reviews, stakeholder demos, and cross-functional critiques.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$146,600 - $219,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LR1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$146.6K – $219.8K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$146.6K - $219.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0ce0f0af-7b68-4a31-8c24-529c051a6660","tierSummary":"$146.6K – $219.8K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"77008d87-4331-4db8-99aa-98d3aaa58310","summary":"$146.6K – $219.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":219800}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":219800}]}},{"id":"199379ba-e421-42ac-bb68-b89eaa848cbd","title":"Senior Corporate Paralegal","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T21:25:28.453+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/199379ba-e421-42ac-bb68-b89eaa848cbd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/199379ba-e421-42ac-bb68-b89eaa848cbd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Senior Corporate Paralegal to join our legal team! In this role, you will provide critical support to the legal department and be responsible for a wide range of corporate legal tasks. We are looking for someone who is organized, proactive, takes initiative, is adaptable to business needs, and thrives in a fast-paced environment. If you are excited about a high-impact legal opportunity at a rapidly growing AI company, we want to hear from you!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Corporate entity governance and maintenance for domestic and foreign entities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare board materials, written consents, resolutions, certifications, minutes, and other corporate documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with legal aspects of special projects, including financings, real estate, insurance, and M&amp;A: transactions documents, due diligence, and ongoing obligations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support compliance function, including maintaining policy database and providing guidance on legal processes and procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the drafting and maintenance of employment-related documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct legal research and benchmarking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to internal and external legal inquiries (e.g., vendor KYC)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with other members of the legal team and as well as other company functional departments on special initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide operational support to the legal team (e.g., manage legal subscriptions)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum of five years of corporate paralegal experience in a law firm or technology company, with a broad scope of practice: corporate governance, securities, employment, and strategic transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Registered notary</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree (paralegal certificate is a plus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated individual with strong organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable problem solver who is able to work in a fast-paced environment and adapt quickly to changing priorities with a service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plus: Experience with private-company employee equity and cap table management software (e.g., Carta) or willingness to learn</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$108,700 - $163,100 USD</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Corporate Paralegal to join our legal team! In this role, you will provide critical support to the legal department and be responsible for a wide range of corporate legal tasks. We are looking for someone who is organized, proactive, takes initiative, is adaptable to business needs, and thrives in a fast-paced environment. If you are excited about a high-impact legal opportunity at a rapidly growing AI company, we want to hear from you!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Corporate entity governance and maintenance for domestic and foreign entities\n\n - Prepare board materials, written consents, resolutions, certifications, minutes, and other corporate documentation\n\n - Assist with legal aspects of special projects, including financings, real estate, insurance, and M&A: transactions documents, due diligence, and ongoing obligations.\n\n - Support compliance function, including maintaining policy database and providing guidance on legal processes and procedures\n\n - Support the drafting and maintenance of employment-related documents\n\n - Conduct legal research and benchmarking\n\n - Respond to internal and external legal inquiries (e.g., vendor KYC)\n\n - Work with other members of the legal team and as well as other company functional departments on special initiatives\n\n - Provide operational support to the legal team (e.g., manage legal subscriptions)\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum of five years of corporate paralegal experience in a law firm or technology company, with a broad scope of practice: corporate governance, securities, employment, and strategic transactions\n\n - Registered notary\n\n - Bachelor’s degree (paralegal certificate is a plus)\n\n - Self-motivated individual with strong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Reliable problem solver who is able to work in a fast-paced environment and adapt quickly to changing priorities with a service-oriented attitude\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Plus: Experience with private-company employee equity and cap table management software (e.g., Carta) or willingness to learn\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$108,700 - $163,100 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$108.7K – $163.1K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$108.7K - $163.1K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5ad3a35e-0f9c-44b3-aa37-dd6aa8c3e862","tierSummary":"$108.7K – $163.1K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e29cf538-a203-42d3-a212-c3c83193eee6","summary":"$108.7K – $163.1K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":108700,"maxValue":163100},{"id":"8339b89e-8070-488c-a59b-49e32901cd7b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"42841ae1-a8fc-4a85-81ef-777af08017a5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":108700,"maxValue":163100},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"bcc3d29e-31c1-45d7-8229-52bd143a4667","title":"Head of Product Communications","department":"Communications","team":"Communications","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T14:53:02.318+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bcc3d29e-31c1-45d7-8229-52bd143a4667","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bcc3d29e-31c1-45d7-8229-52bd143a4667/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The communications team builds and protects Harvey’s reputation. In this role you will lead tech and product communications for Harvey, shaping how two audiences understand our business: the AI community that wants to know how we build, and the lawyers who want to know what we deliver. You will partner closely with executive leadership, eng, product, and go-to-market. Reports to the Global Head of Communications.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's product narrative: the story of what we build, how we build it, and why it matters for legal teams and society.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn complex engineering and product work into compelling stories for both technical and legal audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cultivate and deepen relationships with top-tier journalists, newsletter writers, podcasters, and influencers shaping how people talk about AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reach our target audiences where they are: generate high-impact coverage across business, tech, and legal press, as well as creative placements beyond traditional media.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Elevate the external profiles of Harvey's executives, product leaders, and researchers through media training, press strategy, thought leadership, and speaking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI tools and workflows for yourself and the team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in AI. You use AI tools to do your own work better and make everyone more efficient.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years in product communications at a high-growth technology company or at a PR agency supporting engineering and product clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of earned media across top-tier publications, podcasts, newsletters, and new media, and deep relationships with the people behind them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A creative approach to reaching audiences, and a willingness to test new channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting senior leaders and building executive visibility programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, concise, human writing that makes complex technical work easy to understand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort moving quickly in a very fast-paced environment, and a collaborative approach to working with others.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$177,000 - $260,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe communications team builds and protects Harvey’s reputation. In this role you will lead tech and product communications for Harvey, shaping how two audiences understand our business: the AI community that wants to know how we build, and the lawyers who want to know what we deliver. You will partner closely with executive leadership, eng, product, and go-to-market. Reports to the Global Head of Communications.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own Harvey's product narrative: the story of what we build, how we build it, and why it matters for legal teams and society.\n\n - Turn complex engineering and product work into compelling stories for both technical and legal audiences.\n\n - Cultivate and deepen relationships with top-tier journalists, newsletter writers, podcasters, and influencers shaping how people talk about AI.\n\n - Reach our target audiences where they are: generate high-impact coverage across business, tech, and legal press, as well as creative placements beyond traditional media.\n\n - Elevate the external profiles of Harvey's executives, product leaders, and researchers through media training, press strategy, thought leadership, and speaking.\n\n - Build AI tools and workflows for yourself and the team.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Fluency in AI. You use AI tools to do your own work better and make everyone more efficient.\n\n - 8+ years in product communications at a high-growth technology company or at a PR agency supporting engineering and product clients.\n\n - A track record of earned media across top-tier publications, podcasts, newsletters, and new media, and deep relationships with the people behind them.\n\n - A creative approach to reaching audiences, and a willingness to test new channels.\n\n - Experience supporting senior leaders and building executive visibility programs.\n\n - Clear, concise, human writing that makes complex technical work easy to understand.\n\n - Comfort moving quickly in a very fast-paced environment, and a collaborative approach to working with others.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$177,000 - $260,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-RB1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$177K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$177K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8cce88f3-10e6-4a7b-b4b1-e60f885aa85c","tierSummary":"$177K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cbd87957-035a-4f8c-a5f5-050a41081323","summary":"$177K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177000,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"684b78be-4f36-46d9-8175-31750a4f7343","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"80c74be7-4e91-4f44-8c72-9070dd2448df","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":177000,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"851b416f-9869-4b9c-9c10-5105bded4330","title":"Staff Web Designer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T19:34:52.631+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/851b416f-9869-4b9c-9c10-5105bded4330","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/851b416f-9869-4b9c-9c10-5105bded4330/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Web Designer joins Harvey's Web team to define and elevate the design experience across <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and all web-facing surfaces. The team is responsible for translating Harvey's brand and product story into compelling, accessible, and high-performing web experiences that drive awareness, engagement, and pipeline. In this role, you will own and evolve the website design system, lead user research and testing initiatives, and set the quality bar for every page that ships. You will partner closely with web engineers, motion designers, product marketing, and brand stakeholders to deliver end-to-end design solutions at the pace a category-defining legal AI company demands. It is a rare opportunity to shape how the world first encounters Harvey—and to build the design infrastructure that scales that experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve the website design system—establishing scalable patterns, component libraries, and governance standards that maintain consistency and accelerate delivery across all web surfaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the end-to-end design process for web projects, from concept and user research through interaction design, prototyping, and detailed technical specification hand-off to web engineers and motion designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive innovation through exploration, prototyping, and user testing to continuously improve user experience, conversion, and accessibility across <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and related properties.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor junior web designers, embedding best practices around responsive design, accessibility, and design-system governance to raise the team's collective quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run design demos, present work to marketing leadership and cross-functional stakeholders, and articulate design rationale with clarity and expertise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools and emerging technologies to accelerate design workflows, explore new interaction paradigms, and push the boundary of what a best-in-class legal AI website can be.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of professional design experience with a significant focus on web and digital product design, including demonstrated impact at a staff or senior-staff level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio that showcases mastery of user experience design, interaction design, responsive web design, and design-system architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in systems thinking—building, scaling, and governing design systems that serve multiple teams and use cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of modern design tools (e.g., Figma) and comfort working at the intersection of design and front-end development, including providing pixel-level specifications and technical hand-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to leverage AI-assisted design workflows and a track record of raising quality and velocity in fast-paced, high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running design reviews, stakeholder demos, and cross-functional critiques.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$146,600 - $219,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Staff Web Designer joins Harvey's Web team to define and elevate the design experience across harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and all web-facing surfaces. The team is responsible for translating Harvey's brand and product story into compelling, accessible, and high-performing web experiences that drive awareness, engagement, and pipeline. In this role, you will own and evolve the website design system, lead user research and testing initiatives, and set the quality bar for every page that ships. You will partner closely with web engineers, motion designers, product marketing, and brand stakeholders to deliver end-to-end design solutions at the pace a category-defining legal AI company demands. It is a rare opportunity to shape how the world first encounters Harvey—and to build the design infrastructure that scales that experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and evolve the website design system—establishing scalable patterns, component libraries, and governance standards that maintain consistency and accelerate delivery across all web surfaces.\n\n - Lead the end-to-end design process for web projects, from concept and user research through interaction design, prototyping, and detailed technical specification hand-off to web engineers and motion designers.\n\n - Drive innovation through exploration, prototyping, and user testing to continuously improve user experience, conversion, and accessibility across harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and related properties.\n\n - Mentor junior web designers, embedding best practices around responsive design, accessibility, and design-system governance to raise the team's collective quality bar.\n\n - Run design demos, present work to marketing leadership and cross-functional stakeholders, and articulate design rationale with clarity and expertise.\n\n - Leverage AI tools and emerging technologies to accelerate design workflows, explore new interaction paradigms, and push the boundary of what a best-in-class legal AI website can be.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of professional design experience with a significant focus on web and digital product design, including demonstrated impact at a staff or senior-staff level.\n\n - A portfolio that showcases mastery of user experience design, interaction design, responsive web design, and design-system architecture.\n\n - Deep expertise in systems thinking—building, scaling, and governing design systems that serve multiple teams and use cases.\n\n - Strong command of modern design tools (e.g., Figma) and comfort working at the intersection of design and front-end development, including providing pixel-level specifications and technical hand-offs.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to leverage AI-assisted design workflows and a track record of raising quality and velocity in fast-paced, high-growth environments.\n\n - Excellent communication and presentation skills, with experience running design reviews, stakeholder demos, and cross-functional critiques.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$146,600 - $219,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LR1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$146.6K – $219.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$146.6K - $219.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"da137b02-2a2d-497d-b4cd-4ba3fb454d6c","tierSummary":"$146.6K – $219.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2e37124e-96a4-42e4-a02b-d79b4cef89f2","summary":"$146.6K – $219.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":219800},{"id":"cff95569-2712-4f43-a99b-3f3aa6796310","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"042dc625-269a-4827-8637-f3da458bfde7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":219800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"78d412a6-d63a-4475-802b-934aa0e12ccb","title":"Senior Manager, Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T05:42:38.306+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/78d412a6-d63a-4475-802b-934aa0e12ccb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/78d412a6-d63a-4475-802b-934aa0e12ccb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building the infrastructure foundation behind one of the most ambitious AI product companies in the world. Our Core Infrastructure team powers every user interaction across Harvey’s legal AI platform, which already processes billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests for leading law firms, enterprises, and other high-stakes customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead Core Infrastructure from Bengaluru as we scale the platform, the team, and the next generation of Harvey products. This is a high-leverage role for a builder-leader who can grow strong engineers, drive technical execution, and raise the bar on reliability, performance, security, and developer velocity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is not a pure operations role. Core Infrastructure at Harvey is responsible for building new systems as well as hardening existing ones, with an emphasis on architecture, scale, and long-term platform leverage rather than reactive firefighting alone.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is in a build era, not a maintenance era. New product surfaces ship rapidly, and India engineering is expected to play a foundational role in shaping the architecture, culture, and roadmap of Harvey’s next decade.<br /><br />At Harvey, we value <strong>Decisiveness</strong>, <strong>Simplicity</strong>, and the mindset that <strong>Job's Not Finished</strong>. We move fast, prioritize clarity, and are always striving for excellence. If this resonates with you, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why This Role Matters:</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Core Infrastructure exists to “deliver core infrastructure that powers our products and teams,” and its current mission is operational excellence at scale. The team serves two critical user groups: external customers who need Harvey to be as reliable as the tools it replaces, and internal product engineering teams who need infrastructure they can build on without firefighting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The systems this team owns are directly tied to Harvey’s next wave of growth, including agent infrastructure, database resilience, site reliability, vector search, job execution, regional data residency, and multi-cloud scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, hire, and develop a high-agency infrastructure team in Bengaluru, creating a culture of accountability, technical excellence, and strong mentorship.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own delivery for core infrastructure investments spanning cloud infrastructure, observability, container orchestration, reliability, and platform foundations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, and adjacent platform teams so infrastructure accelerates product delivery instead of constraining it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide technical strategy across multi-cloud infrastructure, including Azure- and GCP-based systems, Kubernetes orchestration, networking, container management, and infrastructure as code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive operational excellence through better observability, incident response, disaster recovery, runbooks, alerting, and recovery tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help the organization scale safely by improving system design quality, hardening critical paths, and pushing durable solutions to reliability bottlenecks before they become customer-facing failures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AI and product teams to support Harvey’s next major product surfaces, including agent workflows, model infrastructure, and large-scale document processing systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute as a hands-on technical leader when needed, especially in architecture reviews, incident leadership, prioritization, and high-stakes cross-functional programs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Representative Problems You May Lead:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hardening the Agent Platform so product teams can ship AI agent experiences with resource isolation, authenticated sandbox access, and resilient execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improving database resilience and recovery so incidents are mitigated quickly and the main database never becomes the bottleneck during critical events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raising site reliability through stronger alerting, failover strategy, autoscaling, and runbooks so customers are never the first to know Harvey is degraded.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scaling vector and retrieval infrastructure that underpins document-heavy workflows and enterprise search, including migrations that improve reliability and unlock new capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building a multi-region, enterprise-grade platform that meets strict data residency, security, and uptime expectations for global customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of hands-on infrastructure or platform engineering experience in production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep technical strength across cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, networking, observability, CI/CD, and infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform or Pulumi.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of designing and scaling reliable distributed systems, with strong judgment around performance, fault tolerance, and operational tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading complex cross-functional initiatives and translating ambiguous platform needs into clear execution plans and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong people leadership: hiring well, coaching engineers, creating accountability, and building a healthy, high-performing team culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communication and calm execution during incidents, escalations, and high-stakes customer-impacting situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A systems mindset, bias for simplicity, and the ability to raise standards while keeping teams moving fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI/ML infrastructure, high-throughput inference systems, or model platform reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant, security-sensitive platforms for enterprise or regulated customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Azure at scale; GCP or AWS experience also transfers well.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting global, follow-the-sun operations or building teams across regions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AS2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building the infrastructure foundation behind one of the most ambitious AI product companies in the world. Our Core Infrastructure team powers every user interaction across Harvey’s legal AI platform, which already processes billions of prompt tokens and millions of daily requests for leading law firms, enterprises, and other high-stakes customers.\n\nWe are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead Core Infrastructure from Bengaluru as we scale the platform, the team, and the next generation of Harvey products. This is a high-leverage role for a builder-leader who can grow strong engineers, drive technical execution, and raise the bar on reliability, performance, security, and developer velocity.\n\nThis is not a pure operations role. Core Infrastructure at Harvey is responsible for building new systems as well as hardening existing ones, with an emphasis on architecture, scale, and long-term platform leverage rather than reactive firefighting alone.\n\nHarvey is in a build era, not a maintenance era. New product surfaces ship rapidly, and India engineering is expected to play a foundational role in shaping the architecture, culture, and roadmap of Harvey’s next decade.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the mindset that Job's Not Finished. We move fast, prioritize clarity, and are always striving for excellence. If this resonates with you, we'd love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS:\n\nCore Infrastructure exists to “deliver core infrastructure that powers our products and teams,” and its current mission is operational excellence at scale. The team serves two critical user groups: external customers who need Harvey to be as reliable as the tools it replaces, and internal product engineering teams who need infrastructure they can build on without firefighting.\n\nThe systems this team owns are directly tied to Harvey’s next wave of growth, including agent infrastructure, database resilience, site reliability, vector search, job execution, regional data residency, and multi-cloud scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO:\n\n - Lead, hire, and develop a high-agency infrastructure team in Bengaluru, creating a culture of accountability, technical excellence, and strong mentorship.\n\n - Own delivery for core infrastructure investments spanning cloud infrastructure, observability, container orchestration, reliability, and platform foundations.\n\n - Partner closely with Product Engineering, Security, and adjacent platform teams so infrastructure accelerates product delivery instead of constraining it.\n\n - Guide technical strategy across multi-cloud infrastructure, including Azure- and GCP-based systems, Kubernetes orchestration, networking, container management, and infrastructure as code.\n\n - Drive operational excellence through better observability, incident response, disaster recovery, runbooks, alerting, and recovery tooling.\n\n - Help the organization scale safely by improving system design quality, hardening critical paths, and pushing durable solutions to reliability bottlenecks before they become customer-facing failures.\n\n - Partner with AI and product teams to support Harvey’s next major product surfaces, including agent workflows, model infrastructure, and large-scale document processing systems.\n\n - Contribute as a hands-on technical leader when needed, especially in architecture reviews, incident leadership, prioritization, and high-stakes cross-functional programs.\n\n\n\n\nREPRESENTATIVE PROBLEMS YOU MAY LEAD:\n\n - Hardening the Agent Platform so product teams can ship AI agent experiences with resource isolation, authenticated sandbox access, and resilient execution.\n\n - Improving database resilience and recovery so incidents are mitigated quickly and the main database never becomes the bottleneck during critical events.\n\n - Raising site reliability through stronger alerting, failover strategy, autoscaling, and runbooks so customers are never the first to know Harvey is degraded.\n\n - Scaling vector and retrieval infrastructure that underpins document-heavy workflows and enterprise search, including migrations that improve reliability and unlock new capabilities.\n\n - Building a multi-region, enterprise-grade platform that meets strict data residency, security, and uptime expectations for global customers.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR:\n\n - 4+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of hands-on infrastructure or platform engineering experience in production environments.\n\n - Deep technical strength across cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, networking, observability, CI/CD, and infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform or Pulumi.\n\n - A track record of designing and scaling reliable distributed systems, with strong judgment around performance, fault tolerance, and operational tradeoffs.\n\n - Experience leading complex cross-functional initiatives and translating ambiguous platform needs into clear execution plans and measurable outcomes.\n\n - Strong people leadership: hiring well, coaching engineers, creating accountability, and building a healthy, high-performing team culture.\n\n - Clear communication and calm execution during incidents, escalations, and high-stakes customer-impacting situations.\n\n - A systems mindset, bias for simplicity, and the ability to raise standards while keeping teams moving fast.\n   \n   \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AI/ML infrastructure, high-throughput inference systems, or model platform reliability.\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant, security-sensitive platforms for enterprise or regulated customers.\n\n - Familiarity with Azure at scale; GCP or AWS experience also transfers well.\n\n - Experience supporting global, follow-the-sun operations or building teams across regions.\n   \n   \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-AS2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"19ab8a3f-1aff-446b-90b9-1941c164aebc","title":"Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst, EMEA","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Dublin","address":{"postalAddress":{}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T17:18:32.122+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/19ab8a3f-1aff-446b-90b9-1941c164aebc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/19ab8a3f-1aff-446b-90b9-1941c164aebc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst joins Harvey's Total Rewards team to support administering and improving employee benefits and leave programs across a rapidly scaling, global workforce. The team's mission is to deliver competitive, compliant, and employee-centric programs in every region where Harvey operates. This role manages day-to-day Tier 1 benefits support globally while partnering on benefits programs and vendor operations across EMEA and APAC, ensuring employees receive timely, accurate guidance and that programs run smoothly as Harvey expands into new markets. You’ll work closely with People Operations, Payroll, and external brokers, building operational rigor into a function that directly touches every employee. It is a chance to scale benefit operations at a category-defining AI company during a period of exceptional international growth.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for Tier 1 global benefits inquiries across all regions (including the US) with a responsive, service-oriented approach—resolving standard requests directly while escalating complex cases to the Benefits Program Managers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in administration and support of benefits programs and vendor relationships across EMEA and APAC, ensuring compliance with local regulations and alignment with Harvey's total rewards philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate leave-of-absence processes end-to-end — including statutory and company-provided leaves — across multiple jurisdictions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Payroll and external brokers to ensure accurate benefits enrollment, changes, and offboarding workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze benefits utilization data and employee queries to identify trends and propose process improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Benefit Program Managers on open enrollment execution, new-country benefit launches, and drafting employee communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track, process, and reconcile benefits-related invoices from vendors and brokers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, maintain and update internal benefits documentation, employee FAQs, and standard operating procedures (SOPs) as programs scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate vendor onboarding, administrative PO creation, and contract workflows with guidance from Finance and Legal</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–4 years of experience in benefits administration, leave management, or a related HR operations role, ideally within a global or multi-country environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of EMEA and/or APAC benefits structures, statutory requirements, and leave entitlements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and service orientation, with a track record of delivering responsive, empathetic employee support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with HRIS platforms (e.g., Workday), HR ticketing or case management systems (e.g., ServiceNow, Zendesk, Jira, or Workday Help), and benefits administration tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience or exposure to benefits vendor/broker management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret benefits data and produce actionable insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage day-to-day workflows independently while knowing when to seek guidance or escalate complex issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (vlookups, pivot tables) for basic data analysis and invoice reconciliation</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst joins Harvey's Total Rewards team to support administering and improving employee benefits and leave programs across a rapidly scaling, global workforce. The team's mission is to deliver competitive, compliant, and employee-centric programs in every region where Harvey operates. This role manages day-to-day Tier 1 benefits support globally while partnering on benefits programs and vendor operations across EMEA and APAC, ensuring employees receive timely, accurate guidance and that programs run smoothly as Harvey expands into new markets. You’ll work closely with People Operations, Payroll, and external brokers, building operational rigor into a function that directly touches every employee. It is a chance to scale benefit operations at a category-defining AI company during a period of exceptional international growth.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for Tier 1 global benefits inquiries across all regions (including the US) with a responsive, service-oriented approach—resolving standard requests directly while escalating complex cases to the Benefits Program Managers.\n\n - Assist in administration and support of benefits programs and vendor relationships across EMEA and APAC, ensuring compliance with local regulations and alignment with Harvey's total rewards philosophy.\n\n - Coordinate leave-of-absence processes end-to-end — including statutory and company-provided leaves — across multiple jurisdictions.\n\n - Partner with Payroll and external brokers to ensure accurate benefits enrollment, changes, and offboarding workflows.\n\n - Analyze benefits utilization data and employee queries to identify trends and propose process improvements.\n\n - Partner with Benefit Program Managers on open enrollment execution, new-country benefit launches, and drafting employee communications.\n\n - Track, process, and reconcile benefits-related invoices from vendors and brokers.\n\n - Develop, maintain and update internal benefits documentation, employee FAQs, and standard operating procedures (SOPs) as programs scale.\n\n - Coordinate vendor onboarding, administrative PO creation, and contract workflows with guidance from Finance and Legal\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 2–4 years of experience in benefits administration, leave management, or a related HR operations role, ideally within a global or multi-country environment\n\n - Working knowledge of EMEA and/or APAC benefits structures, statutory requirements, and leave entitlements\n\n - Excellent communication and service orientation, with a track record of delivering responsive, empathetic employee support\n\n - Experience working with HRIS platforms (e.g., Workday), HR ticketing or case management systems (e.g., ServiceNow, Zendesk, Jira, or Workday Help), and benefits administration tools\n\n - Experience or exposure to benefits vendor/broker management\n\n - Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret benefits data and produce actionable insights\n\n - Ability to manage day-to-day workflows independently while knowing when to seek guidance or escalate complex issues\n\n - Proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (vlookups, pivot tables) for basic data analysis and invoice reconciliation\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4e8b714c-98fb-461f-b05f-82d56ad08e2b","title":"Executive Assistant","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T22:38:10.799+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4e8b714c-98fb-461f-b05f-82d56ad08e2b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4e8b714c-98fb-461f-b05f-82d56ad08e2b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is seeking highly strategic, proactive, and polished Executive Assistants to support senior leaders across the organization. This role goes beyond traditional administrative support. It requires a partner who can help maximize executive leverage, operate as a force multiplier, and bring structure to a fast-moving, high-stakes environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate has experience supporting senior, externally-facing executives and is comfortable navigating complex stakeholder landscapes across internal teams, customers, and partners. This person exercises strong judgment, is highly discerning about priorities, and plays an active role in ensuring the executive’s time is deployed against the highest-impact opportunities. They bring a track record of owning executive time, acting as an opinionated partner, and helping drive meaningful business outcomes.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive executive leverage by owning and optimizing complex calendars, ensuring time is allocated to the highest-priority internal and external engagements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic gatekeeper for the executive’s time, triaging inbound requests, prioritizing effectively, and making clear, confident recommendations on where attention is needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate and scale the executive request flow, bringing structure and clarity across a wide set of stakeholders and ensuring efficient intake, prioritization, and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a central point of coordination across internal teams and external stakeholders, ensuring communication is seamless, proactive, and high quality while maintaining strong relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own meeting preparation end to end, including agenda setting, materials development, and driving follow-ups to ensure strong execution and momentum</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage complex inboxes and communications, helping synthesize information, draft responses, and ensure the executive is consistently well-prepared and ahead by surfacing key decisions and recommending actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute high-impact travel and logistics with a focus on efficiency, foresight, and minimizing friction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support strategic projects and initiatives, bringing organization, follow-through, and a bias for action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to presentations and materials, ensuring executive communications are clear, polished, and aligned to priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a steady, calm, and positive presence across a broad set of relationships, helping maintain alignment and trust</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle highly sensitive and confidential information with discretion and sound judgment</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience supporting senior executives, ideally in a high-growth, externally-facing environment, with a strong preference for experience supporting C-level or equivalent leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage complex stakeholder ecosystems, including senior external partners and cross-functional internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment and prioritization skills, with the ability to triage competing demands and make clear, confident decisions on behalf of the executive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing high-volume, complex inboxes and communications, with a focus on creating leverage and clarity while proactively driving decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of building and operating scalable systems for managing requests, workflows, and executive engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to draft executive-level messaging and engage credibly with senior stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High degree of professionalism and executive presence, with the ability to influence and build trust across all levels of an organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Calm, steady, and solutions-oriented under pressure, with the ability to bring structure to ambiguous situations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly proactive and resourceful, with a strong ownership mindset and bias for action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discreet and trustworthy when handling sensitive information</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$113,000 - $169,600 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TA1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is seeking highly strategic, proactive, and polished Executive Assistants to support senior leaders across the organization. This role goes beyond traditional administrative support. It requires a partner who can help maximize executive leverage, operate as a force multiplier, and bring structure to a fast-moving, high-stakes environment.\n\n\n\nThe ideal candidate has experience supporting senior, externally-facing executives and is comfortable navigating complex stakeholder landscapes across internal teams, customers, and partners. This person exercises strong judgment, is highly discerning about priorities, and plays an active role in ensuring the executive’s time is deployed against the highest-impact opportunities. They bring a track record of owning executive time, acting as an opinionated partner, and helping drive meaningful business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Drive executive leverage by owning and optimizing complex calendars, ensuring time is allocated to the highest-priority internal and external engagements\n\n - Act as a strategic gatekeeper for the executive’s time, triaging inbound requests, prioritizing effectively, and making clear, confident recommendations on where attention is needed\n\n - Operate and scale the executive request flow, bringing structure and clarity across a wide set of stakeholders and ensuring efficient intake, prioritization, and follow-through\n\n - Serve as a central point of coordination across internal teams and external stakeholders, ensuring communication is seamless, proactive, and high quality while maintaining strong relationships\n\n - Own meeting preparation end to end, including agenda setting, materials development, and driving follow-ups to ensure strong execution and momentum\n\n - Manage complex inboxes and communications, helping synthesize information, draft responses, and ensure the executive is consistently well-prepared and ahead by surfacing key decisions and recommending actions\n\n - Plan and execute high-impact travel and logistics with a focus on efficiency, foresight, and minimizing friction\n\n - Support strategic projects and initiatives, bringing organization, follow-through, and a bias for action\n\n - Contribute to presentations and materials, ensuring executive communications are clear, polished, and aligned to priorities\n\n - Act as a steady, calm, and positive presence across a broad set of relationships, helping maintain alignment and trust\n\n - Handle highly sensitive and confidential information with discretion and sound judgment\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience supporting senior executives, ideally in a high-growth, externally-facing environment, with a strong preference for experience supporting C-level or equivalent leaders\n\n - Proven ability to manage complex stakeholder ecosystems, including senior external partners and cross-functional internal teams\n\n - Strong judgment and prioritization skills, with the ability to triage competing demands and make clear, confident decisions on behalf of the executive\n\n - Experience managing high-volume, complex inboxes and communications, with a focus on creating leverage and clarity while proactively driving decision-making\n\n - Track record of building and operating scalable systems for managing requests, workflows, and executive engagement\n\n - Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to draft executive-level messaging and engage credibly with senior stakeholders\n\n - High degree of professionalism and executive presence, with the ability to influence and build trust across all levels of an organization\n\n - Calm, steady, and solutions-oriented under pressure, with the ability to bring structure to ambiguous situations\n\n - Highly proactive and resourceful, with a strong ownership mindset and bias for action\n\n - Discreet and trustworthy when handling sensitive information\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$113,000 - $169,600 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-TA1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$113K – $169.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$113K - $169.6K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b424b939-6ae7-427f-9509-4a08f56dfda8","tierSummary":"$113K – $169.6K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4118133f-211f-416e-8363-0024037eb310","summary":"$113K – $169.6K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":113000,"maxValue":169600},{"id":"a182bc7d-dc5a-49d7-8ad5-fdb24aa36b84","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"833dbe83-1dcf-472b-8d38-abb97d7d046e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":113000,"maxValue":169600},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7af73358-0a99-4d3a-8fde-b0f735045613","title":"Product Designer, Design Systems","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T00:17:55.225+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7af73358-0a99-4d3a-8fde-b0f735045613","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/7af73358-0a99-4d3a-8fde-b0f735045613/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Why Design Systems matter at Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.\n\nThis is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.\n\n \n\n\nWHY DESIGN SYSTEMS MATTER AT HARVEY\n\nHarvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.\n\n - Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.\n\n - Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.\n\n - Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.\n\n - Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.\n\n - Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.\n\n - Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.\n\n - Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.\n\n - Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.\n\n - Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.\n\n - Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n \n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4cea74f1-7c08-4a9c-884f-796903aa77ed","title":"Product Designer, Design Systems","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T23:52:31.660+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4cea74f1-7c08-4a9c-884f-796903aa77ed","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4cea74f1-7c08-4a9c-884f-796903aa77ed/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why Design Systems matter at Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$150,800 - $226,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.\n\nThis is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.\n\n\n\n\nWHY DESIGN SYSTEMS MATTER AT HARVEY\n\nHarvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.\n\n - Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.\n\n - Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.\n\n - Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.\n\n - Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.\n\n - Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.\n\n - Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.\n\n - Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.\n\n - Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.\n\n - Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.\n\n - Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$150,800 - $226,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150.8K – $226.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150.8K - $226.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"96bc4a02-2a3c-47bb-9f95-1518f4975fe1","tierSummary":"$150.8K – $226.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7c7ff590-8299-4362-80f2-ef711902926a","summary":"$150.8K – $226.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150800,"maxValue":226200},{"id":"bc908a19-83be-4bc3-9d55-05ea074e0a5d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d6402fe1-db85-4a3f-8c63-9a9c4e4dfe09","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150800,"maxValue":226200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6541a2da-ab46-467b-8aaa-289a6a1d087b","title":"Product Designer, Design Systems","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T00:05:31.170+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6541a2da-ab46-467b-8aaa-289a6a1d087b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6541a2da-ab46-467b-8aaa-289a6a1d087b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why Design Systems matter at Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$150,800 - $226,200 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Designer on the Design Systems team at Harvey, you will support in defining the foundations that make our product coherent, scalable, and trustworthy as it grows in complexity. The design system is not just a library of components. It is the shared language between design, engineering, and AI that ensures consistency, quality, and confidence across every interaction.\n\nThis is an ideal role for someone who loves precision, consistency, and execution, operating as a hands-on builder and trusted partner to the Design Systems team. Working closely with product designers and frontend engineers, you will craft, maintain, and scale the components, patterns, documentation, and system assets that power Harvey's product, improving the quality, consistency, and speed with which teams build.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-moving environments, has exceptional attention to detail, and takes pride in producing thoughtful, polished work. As the Design Systems team continues to grow, you'll help shape not only the system itself, but also the processes, workflows, and ways of working that enable the team to scale successfully.\n\n\n\n\nWHY DESIGN SYSTEMS MATTER AT HARVEY\n\nHarvey is an AI-native product. As the system reasons, responds, and adapts in real time, the interface must remain consistent and legible. A strong design system ensures that complexity does not leak into the experience. It enables teams to move faster, reduces cognitive load for users, and builds trust in moments where clarity matters most.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build, maintain, and evolve production-ready design system components, patterns, documentation, and reusable assets across Figma and emerging AI-native design workflows.\n\n - Partner with the Senior Design Systems Designer to scale Harvey's visual language and support the rollout of new system foundations across the product.\n\n - Collaborate with product designers and frontend engineers to ensure system components are intuitive to use, accurately implemented, and consistently adopted.\n\n - Own and create polished production assets, libraries, prototypes, and documentation that enable teams to build quickly and with confidence.\n\n - Support AI-assisted design workflows by preparing components, documentation, and system assets that are optimized for both designers and AI tools.\n\n - Maintain the quality and health of the design system through QA, organization, continuous refinement, and operational improvements.\n\n - Advocate for exceptional craftsmanship, consistency, and usability across every product surface.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3–5 years of experience as a Product Designer, Production Designer, UI Designer, or Design Systems Designer working on digital products.\n\n - Exceptional visual craft with a meticulous eye for detail, layout, spacing, consistency, and production quality.\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams while maintaining a high quality bar.\n\n - Experience building and maintaining component libraries and design systems in Figma, including auto layout, variables, components, and variants.\n\n - Curiosity and experience in AI-assisted design tools and evolving implementation workflows, you don't need to be an engineer, but you're excited about where the discipline is heading.\n\n - Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a desire to learn through close partnership with design and engineering.\n\n - Comfort working in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment and enthusiasm for helping shape an evolving Design Systems practice.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$150,800 - $226,200 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n \n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150,800 – $207,350 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150,800 - $207,350","compensationTiers":[{"id":"70d57287-2589-4a13-8c85-09cfe6ec24af","tierSummary":"$150,800 – $207,350 • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"436606a4-c17a-4894-87c9-b6eb9df74f5c","summary":"$150,800 – $207,350","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150800,"maxValue":207350},{"id":"e821dab4-a315-434f-a8d0-afaab9c6df97","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"aa3bd53f-be26-433a-b24a-2be2615a410b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150800,"maxValue":207350},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f361b7ea-82c6-4061-ad24-1419b4ca3c7b","title":"Partner Manager","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T13:59:33.131+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f361b7ea-82c6-4061-ad24-1419b4ca3c7b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f361b7ea-82c6-4061-ad24-1419b4ca3c7b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a Partner Manager to help operationalize and scale Harvey’s legal partnerships. This role will own the day-to-day management and execution of legal partnerships, ensuring each one translates into a clear, repeatable go-to-market motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Harvey’s legal partners and internal teams across Sales, Enablement, and Customer Success to develop joint GTM plans, enable partner teams, coordinate customer opportunities, establish governance and operating cadences, and track performance against shared goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a strong, detail-oriented operator who can bring structure to complex partnerships, drive cross-functional execution, and ensure partners are engaged and delivering measurable commercial value. They are equally comfortable managing strategic partner relationships and owning the operational work required to make those partnerships successful.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the day-to-day execution of select partnerships, including partner onboarding, enablement, joint planning, and ongoing program management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong working relationships with partner stakeholders and serve as a consistent point of contact across active initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate across cross-functional teams like Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Operations, Finance, Legal, and Product to ensure partner commitments are executed effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clear project plans, operating cadences, partner materials, and internal processes that make partnership programs scalable and repeatable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track partner activity, pipeline, engagement, and program performance, and provide clear updates to internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive partner sourced pipeline to achieve pipeline generation targets and company goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather feedback from partners, customers, and internal teams to improve existing programs and inform future partnership strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support partner-facing meetings, business reviews, training sessions, and executive updates</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-7 years of professional experience in partnerships, consulting, business operations, strategy, sales, customer success, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and a strong sense of ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management skills, including the ability to manage multiple workstreams, establish clear owners and timelines, and drive follow-through from planning through execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build strong relationships with external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and communicate clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business judgment and the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence and maintain momentum across teams with competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and highly collaborative environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000 - $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Partner Manager to help operationalize and scale Harvey’s legal partnerships. This role will own the day-to-day management and execution of legal partnerships, ensuring each one translates into a clear, repeatable go-to-market motion.\n\nYou will work closely with Harvey’s legal partners and internal teams across Sales, Enablement, and Customer Success to develop joint GTM plans, enable partner teams, coordinate customer opportunities, establish governance and operating cadences, and track performance against shared goals.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a strong, detail-oriented operator who can bring structure to complex partnerships, drive cross-functional execution, and ensure partners are engaged and delivering measurable commercial value. They are equally comfortable managing strategic partner relationships and owning the operational work required to make those partnerships successful.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manage the day-to-day execution of select partnerships, including partner onboarding, enablement, joint planning, and ongoing program management.\n\n - Build strong working relationships with partner stakeholders and serve as a consistent point of contact across active initiatives.\n\n - Coordinate across cross-functional teams like Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Operations, Finance, Legal, and Product to ensure partner commitments are executed effectively.\n\n - Develop clear project plans, operating cadences, partner materials, and internal processes that make partnership programs scalable and repeatable.\n\n - Track partner activity, pipeline, engagement, and program performance, and provide clear updates to internal stakeholders.\n\n - Drive partner sourced pipeline to achieve pipeline generation targets and company goals.\n\n - Gather feedback from partners, customers, and internal teams to improve existing programs and inform future partnership strategy.\n\n - Support partner-facing meetings, business reviews, training sessions, and executive updates\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5-7 years of professional experience in partnerships, consulting, business operations, strategy, sales, customer success, or a related field.\n\n - High attention to detail and a strong sense of ownership.\n\n - Strong program management skills, including the ability to manage multiple workstreams, establish clear owners and timelines, and drive follow-through from planning through execution.\n\n - Proven ability to build strong relationships with external stakeholders.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and communicate clear recommendations.\n\n - Strong business judgment and the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous situations.\n\n - Ability to influence and maintain momentum across teams with competing priorities.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and highly collaborative environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$160,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-TM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2d3edc7f-3cfb-4f02-87cc-04be3db0dfc1","tierSummary":"OTE $160K – $220K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"52c6bc79-7b6a-4e3c-9760-c1871d9bc931","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d78a3b6a-9412-4f43-b42a-cc711af4d180","summary":"OTE $160K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"6ef4e19f-b414-4547-be73-a573c1de4949","title":"Partner Manager","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T14:00:35.474+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6ef4e19f-b414-4547-be73-a573c1de4949","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6ef4e19f-b414-4547-be73-a573c1de4949/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a Partner Manager to help operationalize and scale Harvey’s legal partnerships. This role will own the day-to-day management and execution of legal partnerships, ensuring each one translates into a clear, repeatable go-to-market motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Harvey’s legal partners and internal teams across Sales, Enablement, and Customer Success to develop joint GTM plans, enable partner teams, coordinate customer opportunities, establish governance and operating cadences, and track performance against shared goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a strong, detail-oriented operator who can bring structure to complex partnerships, drive cross-functional execution, and ensure partners are engaged and delivering measurable commercial value. They are equally comfortable managing strategic partner relationships and owning the operational work required to make those partnerships successful.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the day-to-day execution of select partnerships, including partner onboarding, enablement, joint planning, and ongoing program management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong working relationships with partner stakeholders and serve as a consistent point of contact across active initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate across cross-functional teams like Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Operations, Finance, Legal, and Product to ensure partner commitments are executed effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clear project plans, operating cadences, partner materials, and internal processes that make partnership programs scalable and repeatable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track partner activity, pipeline, engagement, and program performance, and provide clear updates to internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive partner sourced pipeline to achieve pipeline generation targets and company goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather feedback from partners, customers, and internal teams to improve existing programs and inform future partnership strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support partner-facing meetings, business reviews, training sessions, and executive updates</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-7 years of professional experience in partnerships, consulting, business operations, strategy, sales, customer success, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and a strong sense of ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management skills, including the ability to manage multiple workstreams, establish clear owners and timelines, and drive follow-through from planning through execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build strong relationships with external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and communicate clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business judgment and the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence and maintain momentum across teams with competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and highly collaborative environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000 - $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Partner Manager to help operationalize and scale Harvey’s legal partnerships. This role will own the day-to-day management and execution of legal partnerships, ensuring each one translates into a clear, repeatable go-to-market motion.\n\nYou will work closely with Harvey’s legal partners and internal teams across Sales, Enablement, and Customer Success to develop joint GTM plans, enable partner teams, coordinate customer opportunities, establish governance and operating cadences, and track performance against shared goals.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a strong, detail-oriented operator who can bring structure to complex partnerships, drive cross-functional execution, and ensure partners are engaged and delivering measurable commercial value. They are equally comfortable managing strategic partner relationships and owning the operational work required to make those partnerships successful.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manage the day-to-day execution of select partnerships, including partner onboarding, enablement, joint planning, and ongoing program management.\n\n - Build strong working relationships with partner stakeholders and serve as a consistent point of contact across active initiatives.\n\n - Coordinate across cross-functional teams like Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Operations, Finance, Legal, and Product to ensure partner commitments are executed effectively.\n\n - Develop clear project plans, operating cadences, partner materials, and internal processes that make partnership programs scalable and repeatable.\n\n - Track partner activity, pipeline, engagement, and program performance, and provide clear updates to internal stakeholders.\n\n - Drive partner sourced pipeline to achieve pipeline generation targets and company goals.\n\n - Gather feedback from partners, customers, and internal teams to improve existing programs and inform future partnership strategy.\n\n - Support partner-facing meetings, business reviews, training sessions, and executive updates\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5-7 years of professional experience in partnerships, consulting, business operations, strategy, sales, customer success, or a related field.\n\n - High attention to detail and a strong sense of ownership.\n\n - Strong program management skills, including the ability to manage multiple workstreams, establish clear owners and timelines, and drive follow-through from planning through execution.\n\n - Proven ability to build strong relationships with external stakeholders.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and communicate clear recommendations.\n\n - Strong business judgment and the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous situations.\n\n - Ability to influence and maintain momentum across teams with competing priorities.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and highly collaborative environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$160,000 - $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-TM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9afb5757-dcb4-493a-abb1-763bd41ad388","tierSummary":"$160K – $220K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b358bbb0-b39c-48dc-b780-ba9b5543841e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ae11369a-4032-459d-a8f1-113b9975f75b","summary":"$160K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"cd4f3be2-97e1-4968-9b75-f342006be5a5","title":"Corporate Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T16:57:38.290+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cd4f3be2-97e1-4968-9b75-f342006be5a5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cd4f3be2-97e1-4968-9b75-f342006be5a5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is hiring a Corporate Counsel to play a critical role during a period of rapid growth. You’ll work closely on complex, high-impact corporate matters (including M&amp;A, securities, corporate governance, and entity management) while maintaining the versatility to support the full breadth of corporate legal needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for someone who can own and drive work streams, design scalable legal processes from the ground up, and partner cross-functionally to enable business growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute on M&amp;A and other strategic transactions, including due diligence, drafting and negotiating definitive agreements, managing post-closing integration matters, and overseeing outside counsel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support financing activities, stock transfers, equity administration, and corporate governance matters (including investor relations support and board preparation)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support global expansion efforts, including entity formation, subsidiary maintenance, governance, and compliance (e.g., board meetings, annual reporting, and more)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage real estate transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage insurance matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and continuously improve scalable legal processes, templates, and playbooks to drive efficiency, consistency, and best practices across corporate and strategic transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a trusted business partner to stakeholders across the company, including Finance, People, Operations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD degree and licensed to practice in either California or New York</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-6+ years of legal experience with a strong foundation in corporate law, including deep expertise in the following: M&amp;A, securities and equity matters, corporate governance, and the ability to flex across adjacent corporate matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting fast-growing technology companies, preferably including at least one year in-house</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting global expansion and multinational corporate structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, and think creatively and strategically under tight timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative working style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to drive stakeholder alignment, exercise sound judgment and provide solutions-oriented legal advice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with employment matters and later stage company governance is a plus, but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$200,000 - $252,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is hiring a Corporate Counsel to play a critical role during a period of rapid growth. You’ll work closely on complex, high-impact corporate matters (including M&A, securities, corporate governance, and entity management) while maintaining the versatility to support the full breadth of corporate legal needs.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who can own and drive work streams, design scalable legal processes from the ground up, and partner cross-functionally to enable business growth.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Execute on M&A and other strategic transactions, including due diligence, drafting and negotiating definitive agreements, managing post-closing integration matters, and overseeing outside counsel\n\n - Support financing activities, stock transfers, equity administration, and corporate governance matters (including investor relations support and board preparation)\n\n - Support global expansion efforts, including entity formation, subsidiary maintenance, governance, and compliance (e.g., board meetings, annual reporting, and more)\n\n - Manage real estate transactions\n\n - Manage insurance matters\n\n - Design, implement, and continuously improve scalable legal processes, templates, and playbooks to drive efficiency, consistency, and best practices across corporate and strategic transactions\n\n - Act as a trusted business partner to stakeholders across the company, including Finance, People, Operations\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - JD degree and licensed to practice in either California or New York\n\n - 3-6+ years of legal experience with a strong foundation in corporate law, including deep expertise in the following: M&A, securities and equity matters, corporate governance, and the ability to flex across adjacent corporate matters\n\n - Experience supporting fast-growing technology companies, preferably including at least one year in-house\n\n - Experience supporting global expansion and multinational corporate structures\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, and think creatively and strategically under tight timelines\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative working style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to drive stakeholder alignment, exercise sound judgment and provide solutions-oriented legal advice\n\n - Experience with employment matters and later stage company governance is a plus, but not required\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$200,000 - $252,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $252K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $252K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"66465634-154c-4d4e-8f90-afa4f63ca9a8","tierSummary":"$200K – $252K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"359aa661-c7a9-40b8-a39f-032468570d4b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2c642873-aefa-425c-9f28-2b430df1b4a9","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"bab8b20a-1bcd-48de-aa4e-bb44ff048aeb","summary":"$200K – $252K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":252000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":252000}]}},{"id":"154007c0-8f5d-4737-a0eb-0a3f418e1596","title":"Senior Program Manager, Web","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T23:16:30.005+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/154007c0-8f5d-4737-a0eb-0a3f418e1596","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/154007c0-8f5d-4737-a0eb-0a3f418e1596/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Program Manager joins Harvey's Web team to orchestrate the digital experiences that connect Harvey's brand, product, and go-to-market efforts with the outside world. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's web presence evolves at the same velocity as the product itself, translating complex AI capabilities into clear, compelling digital touchpoints. This role drives the operational backbone behind cross-functional web initiatives — managing roadmaps, vendors, and capacity across engineering, design, creative, and marketing stakeholders to ship high-quality digital experiences on time and at scale. They partner directly with leadership in brand, marketing, and product to set priorities and keep a fast-moving portfolio of work accountable and visible. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining legal AI company presents itself to the world while building program management craft in one of the fastest-growing startups in the space.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end program management for Harvey's digital experience portfolio — from requirements gathering and roadmap planning through delivery and retrospective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive cross-functional coordination across marketing, brand, design, engineering, and creative teams to ensure web initiatives ship on time and meet quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage vendor relationships, capacity planning, and resource allocation to maximize the team's throughput without sacrificing craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and maintain accountability mechanisms — status reporting, dependency tracking, and escalation paths — that keep stakeholders aligned in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with GTM and marketing leadership to translate business priorities into actionable project plans and delivery milestones.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10 years of experience in program or project management, with a strong focus on web, digital, or cross-functional marketing/creative programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience working in agile environments, including sprint planning and management (e.g., structuring and running stand-ups, facilitating retrospectives, and producing clear progress reports for stakeholders).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity and strong skills with modern project management tools such as Linear, Asana, Airtable, and JIRA; Linear and Asana experience is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive complex, multi-workstream programs from intake through launch, aligning engineering, design, brand/creative, and marketing partners around a shared roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills; you can influence without authority and create clarity amidst ambiguity in a fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$123,800 - $185,800 USD</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Program Manager joins Harvey's Web team to orchestrate the digital experiences that connect Harvey's brand, product, and go-to-market efforts with the outside world. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's web presence evolves at the same velocity as the product itself, translating complex AI capabilities into clear, compelling digital touchpoints. This role drives the operational backbone behind cross-functional web initiatives — managing roadmaps, vendors, and capacity across engineering, design, creative, and marketing stakeholders to ship high-quality digital experiences on time and at scale. They partner directly with leadership in brand, marketing, and product to set priorities and keep a fast-moving portfolio of work accountable and visible. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining legal AI company presents itself to the world while building program management craft in one of the fastest-growing startups in the space.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end program management for Harvey's digital experience portfolio — from requirements gathering and roadmap planning through delivery and retrospective.\n\n - Drive cross-functional coordination across marketing, brand, design, engineering, and creative teams to ensure web initiatives ship on time and meet quality standards.\n\n - Manage vendor relationships, capacity planning, and resource allocation to maximize the team's throughput without sacrificing craft.\n\n - Establish and maintain accountability mechanisms — status reporting, dependency tracking, and escalation paths — that keep stakeholders aligned in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Partner with GTM and marketing leadership to translate business priorities into actionable project plans and delivery milestones.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6–10 years of experience in program or project management, with a strong focus on web, digital, or cross-functional marketing/creative programs.\n\n - Deep experience working in agile environments, including sprint planning and management (e.g., structuring and running stand-ups, facilitating retrospectives, and producing clear progress reports for stakeholders).\n\n - Familiarity and strong skills with modern project management tools such as Linear, Asana, Airtable, and JIRA; Linear and Asana experience is strongly preferred.\n\n - Proven ability to drive complex, multi-workstream programs from intake through launch, aligning engineering, design, brand/creative, and marketing partners around a shared roadmap.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills; you can influence without authority and create clarity amidst ambiguity in a fast-paced environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$123,800 - $185,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LR1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$123.8K – $185.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$123.8K - $185.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"aaf76587-b3ce-45f6-a871-a70a971ca18f","tierSummary":"$123.8K – $185.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d45e4b17-9136-4b09-95ef-5bce00cb5148","summary":"$123.8K – $185.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":123800,"maxValue":185800},{"id":"5a405c48-e1c4-4726-b788-f7b56d5a2b76","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"537fd835-6fe9-4627-85af-c6bd23139fb3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":123800,"maxValue":185800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f51c534a-cd96-40ee-8f6a-b39d9c99c8be","title":" Senior Program Manager, Web","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T23:17:05.466+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f51c534a-cd96-40ee-8f6a-b39d9c99c8be","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f51c534a-cd96-40ee-8f6a-b39d9c99c8be/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Program Manager joins Harvey's Web team to orchestrate the digital experiences that connect Harvey's brand, product, and go-to-market efforts with the outside world. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's web presence evolves at the same velocity as the product itself, translating complex AI capabilities into clear, compelling digital touchpoints. This role drives the operational backbone behind cross-functional web initiatives — managing roadmaps, vendors, and capacity across engineering, design, creative, and marketing stakeholders to ship high-quality digital experiences on time and at scale. They partner directly with leadership in brand, marketing, and product to set priorities and keep a fast-moving portfolio of work accountable and visible. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining legal AI company presents itself to the world while building program management craft in one of the fastest-growing startups in the space.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end program management for Harvey's digital experience portfolio — from requirements gathering and roadmap planning through delivery and retrospective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive cross-functional coordination across marketing, brand, design, engineering, and creative teams to ensure web initiatives ship on time and meet quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage vendor relationships, capacity planning, and resource allocation to maximize the team's throughput without sacrificing craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and maintain accountability mechanisms — status reporting, dependency tracking, and escalation paths — that keep stakeholders aligned in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with GTM and marketing leadership to translate business priorities into actionable project plans and delivery milestones.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10 years of experience in program or project management, with a strong focus on web, digital, or cross-functional marketing/creative programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience working in agile environments, including sprint planning and management (e.g., structuring and running stand-ups, facilitating retrospectives, and producing clear progress reports for stakeholders).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity and strong skills with modern project management tools such as Linear, Asana, Airtable, and JIRA; Linear and Asana experience is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive complex, multi-workstream programs from intake through launch, aligning engineering, design, brand/creative, and marketing partners around a shared roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills; you can influence without authority and create clarity amidst ambiguity in a fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$123,800 - $185,800 USD</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Program Manager joins Harvey's Web team to orchestrate the digital experiences that connect Harvey's brand, product, and go-to-market efforts with the outside world. The team's mission is to ensure Harvey's web presence evolves at the same velocity as the product itself, translating complex AI capabilities into clear, compelling digital touchpoints. This role drives the operational backbone behind cross-functional web initiatives — managing roadmaps, vendors, and capacity across engineering, design, creative, and marketing stakeholders to ship high-quality digital experiences on time and at scale. They partner directly with leadership in brand, marketing, and product to set priorities and keep a fast-moving portfolio of work accountable and visible. It is a rare opportunity to shape how a category-defining legal AI company presents itself to the world while building program management craft in one of the fastest-growing startups in the space.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end program management for Harvey's digital experience portfolio — from requirements gathering and roadmap planning through delivery and retrospective.\n\n - Drive cross-functional coordination across marketing, brand, design, engineering, and creative teams to ensure web initiatives ship on time and meet quality standards.\n\n - Manage vendor relationships, capacity planning, and resource allocation to maximize the team's throughput without sacrificing craft.\n\n - Establish and maintain accountability mechanisms — status reporting, dependency tracking, and escalation paths — that keep stakeholders aligned in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Partner with GTM and marketing leadership to translate business priorities into actionable project plans and delivery milestones.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6–10 years of experience in program or project management, with a strong focus on web, digital, or cross-functional marketing/creative programs.\n\n - Deep experience working in agile environments, including sprint planning and management (e.g., structuring and running stand-ups, facilitating retrospectives, and producing clear progress reports for stakeholders).\n\n - Familiarity and strong skills with modern project management tools such as Linear, Asana, Airtable, and JIRA; Linear and Asana experience is strongly preferred.\n\n - Proven ability to drive complex, multi-workstream programs from intake through launch, aligning engineering, design, brand/creative, and marketing partners around a shared roadmap.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills; you can influence without authority and create clarity amidst ambiguity in a fast-paced environment.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$123,800 - $185,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LR1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$123.8K – $185.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$123.8K - $185.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f7d4db8b-333d-4dbf-b0eb-287de48ed7ca","tierSummary":"$123.8K – $185.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4889e2d4-038c-43e3-95f4-76ad2c0ff6ec","summary":"$123.8K – $185.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":123800,"maxValue":185800},{"id":"1fc47a40-97af-482a-b496-33406c44b67d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e9b4d52a-1905-4e76-bcee-56a2d4cb8430","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":123800,"maxValue":185800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"812cdf8b-1702-460e-84b4-ffbfb2088ceb","title":"Staff Web Engineer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T23:02:17.274+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/812cdf8b-1702-460e-84b4-ffbfb2088ceb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/812cdf8b-1702-460e-84b4-ffbfb2088ceb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Web Developer joins Harvey's Web team as the senior technical leader for the architecture, data foundations, and systems integration behind <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://harvey.ai\">harvey.ai</a> and every web-facing surface. The team's mission is to make Harvey's web presence evolve at the velocity of the product itself — reliable, observable, and fast enough that Marketing and GTM can ship without waiting on engineering.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns the technical strategy for that platform: the Next.js and Sanity architecture, the integration layer connecting the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, and GTM systems, and the automation and testing practices the team currently lacks. You will be the most senior engineer on a small, front-end-leaning team, setting standards and mentoring as much as building.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You partner directly with Harvey's product engineering, security, and infrastructure organizations to make sure the web platform meets the same bar as the rest of the company. It is a rare opportunity to build foundational systems from scratch at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with unusually direct line of sight from your work to the company's growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the architecture of Harvey's web platform end to end — the Next.js/Vercel application, the Sanity content layer, and the services and APIs behind them — with a focus on reliability, performance, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the data foundations and integration patterns that connect the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, CRM, and GTM systems, supporting both real-time and batch workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish automation, CI/CD, preview/deploy tooling, and robust automated testing where little exists today, reducing operational toil and increasing team velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set observability standards — structured logging, tracing, Core Web Vitals and performance budgets, alerting — so the team can catch and resolve issues before Marketing does.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead how the team applies AI and ML to web workflows, from content operations to personalization to internal tooling, and act as the bridge between product engineering and web engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security and Infrastructure to harden the platform without slowing developer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical leadership and mentorship to a small, front-end-focused team through code review, design review, and architectural guidance.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of Web Development experience with deep back-end and systems expertise, and a track record of owning technical architecture at a staff level of scope and ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of the modern web stack — React/Next.js, TypeScript, and server-side rendering — paired with genuine back-end depth (Node, Python, or comparable) rather than front-end specialization alone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience architecting and operating headless CMS and content platforms (Sanity, Contentful, or similar) at scale, including schema design and publishing workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience building and operating reliable production systems: CI/CD, infrastructure-as-code, observability tooling, and performance optimization against real user metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with data infrastructure fundamentals — SQL/NoSQL databases, caching, queuing, API and webhook integration patterns — in service of marketing and GTM systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production web experiences or content workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to mentor less experienced engineers, influence across functions, and operate autonomously in a small team where you are the deepest technical voice.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Vercel platform experience; marketing/GTM systems integration (HubSpot, Salesforce, Segment, analytics); SEO and web performance engineering; prior experience as the first or most senior engineer on a web platform team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$146,600 - $201,500 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC2</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Staff Web Developer joins Harvey's Web team as the senior technical leader for the architecture, data foundations, and systems integration behind harvey.ai http://harvey.ai and every web-facing surface. The team's mission is to make Harvey's web presence evolve at the velocity of the product itself — reliable, observable, and fast enough that Marketing and GTM can ship without waiting on engineering.\n\nThis role owns the technical strategy for that platform: the Next.js and Sanity architecture, the integration layer connecting the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, and GTM systems, and the automation and testing practices the team currently lacks. You will be the most senior engineer on a small, front-end-leaning team, setting standards and mentoring as much as building.\n\nYou partner directly with Harvey's product engineering, security, and infrastructure organizations to make sure the web platform meets the same bar as the rest of the company. It is a rare opportunity to build foundational systems from scratch at one of the fastest-growing AI companies, with unusually direct line of sight from your work to the company's growth.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the architecture of Harvey's web platform end to end — the Next.js/Vercel application, the Sanity content layer, and the services and APIs behind them — with a focus on reliability, performance, and scalability.\n\n - Design and build the data foundations and integration patterns that connect the website to Harvey's marketing, analytics, CRM, and GTM systems, supporting both real-time and batch workloads.\n\n - Establish automation, CI/CD, preview/deploy tooling, and robust automated testing where little exists today, reducing operational toil and increasing team velocity.\n\n - Set observability standards — structured logging, tracing, Core Web Vitals and performance budgets, alerting — so the team can catch and resolve issues before Marketing does.\n\n - Lead how the team applies AI and ML to web workflows, from content operations to personalization to internal tooling, and act as the bridge between product engineering and web engineering.\n\n - Partner with Security and Infrastructure to harden the platform without slowing developer experience.\n\n - Provide technical leadership and mentorship to a small, front-end-focused team through code review, design review, and architectural guidance.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of Web Development experience with deep back-end and systems expertise, and a track record of owning technical architecture at a staff level of scope and ambiguity.\n\n - Strong command of the modern web stack — React/Next.js, TypeScript, and server-side rendering — paired with genuine back-end depth (Node, Python, or comparable) rather than front-end specialization alone.\n\n - Experience architecting and operating headless CMS and content platforms (Sanity, Contentful, or similar) at scale, including schema design and publishing workflows.\n\n - Proven experience building and operating reliable production systems: CI/CD, infrastructure-as-code, observability tooling, and performance optimization against real user metrics.\n\n - Fluency with data infrastructure fundamentals — SQL/NoSQL databases, caching, queuing, API and webhook integration patterns — in service of marketing and GTM systems.\n\n - Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production web experiences or content workflows.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to mentor less experienced engineers, influence across functions, and operate autonomously in a small team where you are the deepest technical voice.\n\nNice to have: Vercel platform experience; marketing/GTM systems integration (HubSpot, Salesforce, Segment, analytics); SEO and web performance engineering; prior experience as the first or most senior engineer on a web platform team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$146,600 - $201,500 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JC2\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$146.6K – $201.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$146.6K - $201.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1457f37a-65f1-4abc-9c45-1a09aeae0515","tierSummary":"$146.6K – $201.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"419498f0-63d6-406b-9bf0-e9cb67dd8c78","summary":"$146.6K – $201.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":201500},{"id":"79fa04d5-23ea-4023-b9a3-1b999d696f34","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"2ea81dcc-aac7-4511-a1f1-1517dfba3c58","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":146600,"maxValue":201500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1f65a3b9-0900-482a-ba6f-a028ba5fc85f","title":"Senior Public Sector Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T18:25:27.656+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1f65a3b9-0900-482a-ba6f-a028ba5fc85f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1f65a3b9-0900-482a-ba6f-a028ba5fc85f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an<strong> </strong>experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A law degree from an accredited law school</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ninja-like project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210,300 - $300,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\n \n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements\n\n - Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations\n\n - Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams\n\n \n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\n \n\nThis role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A law degree from an accredited law school\n\n - Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)\n\n - 7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience\n\n - Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions\n\n - Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors\n\n - Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes\n\n - Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude\n\n - Ninja-like project management skills\n\n - Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210,300 - $300,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$210.3K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"961dde61-522c-48b8-9fe9-6104e63aff9b","tierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8f64660b-3d65-43f6-bb47-3aaa0f2495dc","summary":"$210.3K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"39a01048-53d5-4380-a22c-698804777725","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0070202c-9558-4f17-aa33-32b48ba177d4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8bec95c8-b625-49e9-bd82-c8eb83e170ee","title":"Senior Public Sector Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T18:26:08.880+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8bec95c8-b625-49e9-bd82-c8eb83e170ee","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8bec95c8-b625-49e9-bd82-c8eb83e170ee/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an<strong> </strong>experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A law degree from an accredited law school</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ninja-like project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210,300 - $300,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\n \n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements\n\n - Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations\n\n - Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams\n\n \n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\n \n\nThis role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A law degree from an accredited law school\n\n - Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)\n\n - 7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience\n\n - Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions\n\n - Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors\n\n - Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes\n\n - Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude\n\n - Ninja-like project management skills\n\n - Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210,300 - $300,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$210.3K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b80cc924-5472-4deb-955f-d702ece9d1e6","tierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3aa218b8-f4da-4cb9-8b4c-ae304042c218","summary":"$210.3K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"3d9d2758-23d9-4c1c-b6c3-c42478e5b096","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"dd6c5a06-616f-459d-a906-491aa87d33aa","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"34f47d94-34f6-4730-87e8-c52651ac9ce9","title":"Senior Public Sector Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T18:25:42.506+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/34f47d94-34f6-4730-87e8-c52651ac9ce9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/34f47d94-34f6-4730-87e8-c52651ac9ce9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an<strong> </strong>experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A law degree from an accredited law school</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ninja-like project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210,300 - $300,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\n \n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements\n\n - Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations\n\n - Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams\n\n \n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\n \n\nThis role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A law degree from an accredited law school\n\n - Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)\n\n - 7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience\n\n - Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions\n\n - Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors\n\n - Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes\n\n - Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude\n\n - Ninja-like project management skills\n\n - Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210,300 - $300,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$210.3K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"60b0fde7-37f8-4428-b234-839558a534f1","tierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"98857e06-e28a-40af-8d24-db4058af5496","summary":"$210.3K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"e2482a99-fedc-412c-905d-3b56cd308816","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"56a3586e-9ef6-40bb-852d-129978687f8a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"10f05e63-0673-4fe7-9bec-61baff2cd86d","title":"Senior Public Sector Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T18:25:57.113+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/10f05e63-0673-4fe7-9bec-61baff2cd86d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/10f05e63-0673-4fe7-9bec-61baff2cd86d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an<strong> </strong>experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A law degree from an accredited law school</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ninja-like project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210,300 - $300,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\n \n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements\n\n - Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations\n\n - Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams\n\n \n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\n \n\nThis role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A law degree from an accredited law school\n\n - Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)\n\n - 7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience\n\n - Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions\n\n - Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors\n\n - Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes\n\n - Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude\n\n - Ninja-like project management skills\n\n - Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210,300 - $300,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$210.3K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"65270fa8-5c14-4f17-99d6-40bfe1dfd53d","tierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"387c937d-fca2-4736-8de2-62c41aff02f9","summary":"$210.3K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"e1edbe93-824f-4a18-804e-6fdc0434ac69","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6c212414-2582-4c4a-adf8-bce8e6f6cde9","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1bb62bbb-22bd-4057-8ad6-8556e05eeebc","title":"Senior Public Sector Counsel","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T18:26:02.264+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1bb62bbb-22bd-4057-8ad6-8556e05eeebc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1bb62bbb-22bd-4057-8ad6-8556e05eeebc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an<strong> </strong>experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A law degree from an accredited law school</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ninja-like project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210,300 - $300,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for an experienced public sector lawyer to join our legal team to help build and lead Harvey’s government and public sector legal function. You will help drive our efforts to build relationships with, and sell to, government agencies. You will interface with our go-to-market, business and cross-functional teams (including Engineering, Product and Security) to help ensure the fast, efficient execution of our agreements with government customers and prime contractors.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done, including how governments and public sector agencies serve the public.  Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers.  This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations.  And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\n \n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams on potential opportunities and advise on public sector procurement processes, proposals, and strategies for selling Harvey’s platform to government agencies\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate complex government contracts, AI SaaS agreements, and other technology-related agreements with federal, state, and local government customers and prime contractors, ensuring compliance with the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and agency-specific requirements\n\n - Provide contract lifecycle counsel across the public sector business, including contract administration, performance issues, and government contracting compliance obligations\n\n - Provide training and develop resources for legal and cross-functional teams\n\n \n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\n \n\nThis role has flexibility to either be based in New York, N.Y.; San Francisco, CA; Chicago, IL; or Dallas, TX on a hybrid work model of 3 days per week in the office, or fully remote if based in another location within the US (DC preferred).\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - A law degree from an accredited law school\n\n - Admitted to practice law and in good standing in at least one jurisdiction (California, New York, or DC preferred)\n\n - 7+ years of law firm and/or in-house experience\n\n - Transactional background, including with strong experience with complex SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing and commercial agreements, with a particular focus on government contracts and public sector transactions\n\n - Experience negotiating complex agreements with federal, state, and/or local government customers and prime contractors\n\n - Working knowledge of government procurement regimes, including the FAR, DFARS, and related government contracting regulations and processes\n\n - Experience advising businesses on selling into the government and public sector, including go-to-market and procurement strategy\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude\n\n - Ninja-like project management skills\n\n - Bonus qualifications include prior government service, experience with AI, supporting Go-To-Market/ Sales, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210,300 - $300,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$210.3K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"500796a2-7f90-4e87-808b-7666f6079c0e","tierSummary":"$210.3K – $300K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8c0b534a-73af-407b-a0f1-07f6c343f372","summary":"$210.3K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"cb7cb14e-eeab-4bcf-8fc8-615bcf2f888a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"08e30130-9b5c-4496-892b-8e1ee6c6e04e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":210300,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"4c98476d-7afb-4669-917b-b2f49040d31d","title":"Legal Operations Project Manager","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T22:26:11.856+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4c98476d-7afb-4669-917b-b2f49040d31d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4c98476d-7afb-4669-917b-b2f49040d31d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Legal Operations Project Manager to join our legal team to help modernize how Legal operates through both best-in-class legal operations practices and hands-on use of AI. By combining traditional legal ops experience with familiarity with AI tools and automation platforms, you will help turn operational problems into scalable, AI-enabled solutions. You will partner closely with Legal and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver on the Legal Ops roadmap and help ensure that Legal’s tooling, data, and processes support Harvey’s rapid growth. It is a unique opportunity to be a key contributor to an AI-native legal operations function inside a company that is itself defining the future of AI for legal work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end legal operations projects, including gathering requirements, designing and improving workflows, coordinating cross-functional stakeholders and managing implementation and iteration for areas such as intake, matter management, advice requests and policy changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate priorities and direction into concrete project plans, timelines and execution steps, serving as the connective tissue between strategy and day-to-day delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support AI enablement across Legal, including identifying use cases, evaluating and piloting AI tools (including Harvey), and helping with training and adoption efforts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to building and maintain legal metrics, dashboards and operational reporting across workload, turnaround times, risk patterns and operational performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the evaluation, implementation, administration and continuous improvement of the legal technology stack and vendor relationships across knowledge management, matter tracking, e-billing and spend management, document management and contract-related tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain legal knowledge assets, including templates, playbooks, FAQs, self-service resources and internal documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support routine operational, administrative, systems and data work as priorities evolve</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 to 6 years of experience in an operations or project management role, with responsibility for running and improving cross-functional systems, processes or programs; experience may come from legal operations, business operations, systems operations or a related function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful experience working in or closely with an in-house legal team, with a practical understanding of how Legal supports the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder’s mindset: comfortable owning many moving pieces at once and energized by creating structure in a function that is still taking shape, rather than optimizing an established playbook</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to the design and implementation of processes, systems and programs for Legal or other G&amp;A functions, from requirements gathering through rollout and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with both Legal and technical teams, helping turn business needs into practical process and system requirements, with experience or strong interest in applying AI tools in a legal or professional services setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating with general guidance, seeking direction on new or unfamiliar issues, and balancing competing priorities and sustaining momentum in a globally distributed organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and systems-thinking skills, with familiarity across legal technology (e.g. matter management, knowledge management, ticketing and document repositories) and experience building and interpreting metrics</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with CLM or contracting systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience building or deploying AI-driven workflows, with familiarity with agentic behavior, orchestration, prompt engineering, performance metrics and safety protocols</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience helping design AI guidance, guardrails, or adoption programs for a legal or professional services team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Legal Operations Project Manager to join our legal team to help modernize how Legal operates through both best-in-class legal operations practices and hands-on use of AI. By combining traditional legal ops experience with familiarity with AI tools and automation platforms, you will help turn operational problems into scalable, AI-enabled solutions. You will partner closely with Legal and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver on the Legal Ops roadmap and help ensure that Legal’s tooling, data, and processes support Harvey’s rapid growth. It is a unique opportunity to be a key contributor to an AI-native legal operations function inside a company that is itself defining the future of AI for legal work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manage end-to-end legal operations projects, including gathering requirements, designing and improving workflows, coordinating cross-functional stakeholders and managing implementation and iteration for areas such as intake, matter management, advice requests and policy changes\n\n - Translate priorities and direction into concrete project plans, timelines and execution steps, serving as the connective tissue between strategy and day-to-day delivery\n\n - Support AI enablement across Legal, including identifying use cases, evaluating and piloting AI tools (including Harvey), and helping with training and adoption efforts\n\n - Contribute to building and maintain legal metrics, dashboards and operational reporting across workload, turnaround times, risk patterns and operational performance\n\n - Support the evaluation, implementation, administration and continuous improvement of the legal technology stack and vendor relationships across knowledge management, matter tracking, e-billing and spend management, document management and contract-related tooling\n\n - Develop and maintain legal knowledge assets, including templates, playbooks, FAQs, self-service resources and internal documentation\n\n - Support routine operational, administrative, systems and data work as priorities evolve\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3 to 6 years of experience in an operations or project management role, with responsibility for running and improving cross-functional systems, processes or programs; experience may come from legal operations, business operations, systems operations or a related function\n\n - Meaningful experience working in or closely with an in-house legal team, with a practical understanding of how Legal supports the business\n\n - A builder’s mindset: comfortable owning many moving pieces at once and energized by creating structure in a function that is still taking shape, rather than optimizing an established playbook\n\n - Experience contributing to the design and implementation of processes, systems and programs for Legal or other G&A functions, from requirements gathering through rollout and iteration\n\n - Comfortable working with both Legal and technical teams, helping turn business needs into practical process and system requirements, with experience or strong interest in applying AI tools in a legal or professional services setting\n\n - Comfortable operating with general guidance, seeking direction on new or unfamiliar issues, and balancing competing priorities and sustaining momentum in a globally distributed organization\n\n - Strong analytical and systems-thinking skills, with familiarity across legal technology (e.g. matter management, knowledge management, ticketing and document repositories) and experience building and interpreting metrics\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Hands-on experience with CLM or contracting systems\n\n - Practical experience building or deploying AI-driven workflows, with familiarity with agentic behavior, orchestration, prompt engineering, performance metrics and safety protocols\n\n - Experience helping design AI guidance, guardrails, or adoption programs for a legal or professional services team\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ad164e93-5d99-48b5-99af-a99a8c87f9d5","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ac1c2269-dd93-463c-a45c-3c254bf106de","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"id":"484dd2ad-2816-42b3-b14c-10ed0fdd8c6e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"14c77e43-9219-469c-b73d-f5c0b1104b34","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8c6d0bb5-4c01-4455-9bc9-6f9a2177aa87","title":"Legal Operations Project Manager","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T22:26:05.908+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8c6d0bb5-4c01-4455-9bc9-6f9a2177aa87","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/8c6d0bb5-4c01-4455-9bc9-6f9a2177aa87/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Legal Operations Project Manager to join our legal team to help modernize how Legal operates through both best-in-class legal operations practices and hands-on use of AI. By combining traditional legal ops experience with familiarity with AI tools and automation platforms, you will help turn operational problems into scalable, AI-enabled solutions. You will partner closely with Legal and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver on the Legal Ops roadmap and help ensure that Legal’s tooling, data, and processes support Harvey’s rapid growth. It is a unique opportunity to be a key contributor to an AI-native legal operations function inside a company that is itself defining the future of AI for legal work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end legal operations projects, including gathering requirements, designing and improving workflows, coordinating cross-functional stakeholders and managing implementation and iteration for areas such as intake, matter management, advice requests and policy changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate priorities and direction into concrete project plans, timelines and execution steps, serving as the connective tissue between strategy and day-to-day delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support AI enablement across Legal, including identifying use cases, evaluating and piloting AI tools (including Harvey), and helping with training and adoption efforts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to building and maintain legal metrics, dashboards and operational reporting across workload, turnaround times, risk patterns and operational performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the evaluation, implementation, administration and continuous improvement of the legal technology stack and vendor relationships across knowledge management, matter tracking, e-billing and spend management, document management and contract-related tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain legal knowledge assets, including templates, playbooks, FAQs, self-service resources and internal documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support routine operational, administrative, systems and data work as priorities evolve</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 to 6 years of experience in an operations or project management role, with responsibility for running and improving cross-functional systems, processes or programs; experience may come from legal operations, business operations, systems operations or a related function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful experience working in or closely with an in-house legal team, with a practical understanding of how Legal supports the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder’s mindset: comfortable owning many moving pieces at once and energized by creating structure in a function that is still taking shape, rather than optimizing an established playbook</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to the design and implementation of processes, systems and programs for Legal or other G&amp;A functions, from requirements gathering through rollout and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with both Legal and technical teams, helping turn business needs into practical process and system requirements, with experience or strong interest in applying AI tools in a legal or professional services setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating with general guidance, seeking direction on new or unfamiliar issues, and balancing competing priorities and sustaining momentum in a globally distributed organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and systems-thinking skills, with familiarity across legal technology (e.g. matter management, knowledge management, ticketing and document repositories) and experience building and interpreting metrics</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with CLM or contracting systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience building or deploying AI-driven workflows, with familiarity with agentic behavior, orchestration, prompt engineering, performance metrics and safety protocols</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience helping design AI guidance, guardrails, or adoption programs for a legal or professional services team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$99,200 - $148,800 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-ML3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Legal Operations Project Manager to join our legal team to help modernize how Legal operates through both best-in-class legal operations practices and hands-on use of AI. By combining traditional legal ops experience with familiarity with AI tools and automation platforms, you will help turn operational problems into scalable, AI-enabled solutions. You will partner closely with Legal and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver on the Legal Ops roadmap and help ensure that Legal’s tooling, data, and processes support Harvey’s rapid growth. It is a unique opportunity to be a key contributor to an AI-native legal operations function inside a company that is itself defining the future of AI for legal work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manage end-to-end legal operations projects, including gathering requirements, designing and improving workflows, coordinating cross-functional stakeholders and managing implementation and iteration for areas such as intake, matter management, advice requests and policy changes\n\n - Translate priorities and direction into concrete project plans, timelines and execution steps, serving as the connective tissue between strategy and day-to-day delivery\n\n - Support AI enablement across Legal, including identifying use cases, evaluating and piloting AI tools (including Harvey), and helping with training and adoption efforts\n\n - Contribute to building and maintain legal metrics, dashboards and operational reporting across workload, turnaround times, risk patterns and operational performance\n\n - Support the evaluation, implementation, administration and continuous improvement of the legal technology stack and vendor relationships across knowledge management, matter tracking, e-billing and spend management, document management and contract-related tooling\n\n - Develop and maintain legal knowledge assets, including templates, playbooks, FAQs, self-service resources and internal documentation\n\n - Support routine operational, administrative, systems and data work as priorities evolve\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3 to 6 years of experience in an operations or project management role, with responsibility for running and improving cross-functional systems, processes or programs; experience may come from legal operations, business operations, systems operations or a related function\n\n - Meaningful experience working in or closely with an in-house legal team, with a practical understanding of how Legal supports the business\n\n - A builder’s mindset: comfortable owning many moving pieces at once and energized by creating structure in a function that is still taking shape, rather than optimizing an established playbook\n\n - Experience contributing to the design and implementation of processes, systems and programs for Legal or other G&A functions, from requirements gathering through rollout and iteration\n\n - Comfortable working with both Legal and technical teams, helping turn business needs into practical process and system requirements, with experience or strong interest in applying AI tools in a legal or professional services setting\n\n - Comfortable operating with general guidance, seeking direction on new or unfamiliar issues, and balancing competing priorities and sustaining momentum in a globally distributed organization\n\n - Strong analytical and systems-thinking skills, with familiarity across legal technology (e.g. matter management, knowledge management, ticketing and document repositories) and experience building and interpreting metrics\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Hands-on experience with CLM or contracting systems\n\n - Practical experience building or deploying AI-driven workflows, with familiarity with agentic behavior, orchestration, prompt engineering, performance metrics and safety protocols\n\n - Experience helping design AI guidance, guardrails, or adoption programs for a legal or professional services team\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$99,200 - $148,800 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-ML3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$99.2K - $148.8K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e612109e-7379-46b5-a095-8a66e79f8061","tierSummary":"$99.2K – $148.8K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7dc100d6-9ce0-439c-a407-74f8d7bedefa","summary":"$99.2K – $148.8K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"id":"31d2ebd7-9f5a-4161-8fc5-a9f3acc4c8a7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"aa8d694a-cee3-40c6-8689-a4c2cc8474c7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":99200,"maxValue":148800},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9d35820a-c40c-44e1-89f7-1952ba06fda6","title":"Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst, EMEA","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T17:18:53.736+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9d35820a-c40c-44e1-89f7-1952ba06fda6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9d35820a-c40c-44e1-89f7-1952ba06fda6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst joins Harvey's Total Rewards team to support administering and improving employee benefits and leave programs across a rapidly scaling, global workforce. The team's mission is to deliver competitive, compliant, and employee-centric programs in every region where Harvey operates. This role manages day-to-day Tier 1 benefits support globally while partnering on benefits programs and vendor operations across EMEA and APAC, ensuring employees receive timely, accurate guidance and that programs run smoothly as Harvey expands into new markets. You’ll work closely with People Operations, Payroll, and external brokers, building operational rigor into a function that directly touches every employee. It is a chance to scale benefit operations at a category-defining AI company during a period of exceptional international growth.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for Tier 1 global benefits inquiries across all regions (including the US) with a responsive, service-oriented approach—resolving standard requests directly while escalating complex cases to the Benefits Program Managers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in administration and support of benefits programs and vendor relationships across EMEA and APAC, ensuring compliance with local regulations and alignment with Harvey's total rewards philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate leave-of-absence processes end-to-end — including statutory and company-provided leaves — across multiple jurisdictions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Payroll and external brokers to ensure accurate benefits enrollment, changes, and offboarding workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze benefits utilization data and employee queries to identify trends and propose process improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Benefit Program Managers on open enrollment execution, new-country benefit launches, and drafting employee communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track, process, and reconcile benefits-related invoices from vendors and brokers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, maintain and update internal benefits documentation, employee FAQs, and standard operating procedures (SOPs) as programs scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate vendor onboarding, administrative PO creation, and contract workflows with guidance from Finance and Legal</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong><br /></strong><br /><br /><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–4 years of experience in benefits administration, leave management, or a related HR operations role, ideally within a global or multi-country environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of EMEA and/or APAC benefits structures, statutory requirements, and leave entitlements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and service orientation, with a track record of delivering responsive, empathetic employee support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with HRIS platforms (e.g., Workday), HR ticketing or case management systems (e.g., ServiceNow, Zendesk, Jira, or Workday Help), and benefits administration tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience or exposure to benefits vendor/broker management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret benefits data and produce actionable insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage day-to-day workflows independently while knowing when to seek guidance or escalate complex issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (vlookups, pivot tables) for basic data analysis and invoice reconciliation</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Global Benefits and Leaves Analyst joins Harvey's Total Rewards team to support administering and improving employee benefits and leave programs across a rapidly scaling, global workforce. The team's mission is to deliver competitive, compliant, and employee-centric programs in every region where Harvey operates. This role manages day-to-day Tier 1 benefits support globally while partnering on benefits programs and vendor operations across EMEA and APAC, ensuring employees receive timely, accurate guidance and that programs run smoothly as Harvey expands into new markets. You’ll work closely with People Operations, Payroll, and external brokers, building operational rigor into a function that directly touches every employee. It is a chance to scale benefit operations at a category-defining AI company during a period of exceptional international growth.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for Tier 1 global benefits inquiries across all regions (including the US) with a responsive, service-oriented approach—resolving standard requests directly while escalating complex cases to the Benefits Program Managers.\n\n - Assist in administration and support of benefits programs and vendor relationships across EMEA and APAC, ensuring compliance with local regulations and alignment with Harvey's total rewards philosophy.\n\n - Coordinate leave-of-absence processes end-to-end — including statutory and company-provided leaves — across multiple jurisdictions.\n\n - Partner with Payroll and external brokers to ensure accurate benefits enrollment, changes, and offboarding workflows.\n\n - Analyze benefits utilization data and employee queries to identify trends and propose process improvements.\n\n - Partner with Benefit Program Managers on open enrollment execution, new-country benefit launches, and drafting employee communications.\n\n - Track, process, and reconcile benefits-related invoices from vendors and brokers.\n\n - Develop, maintain and update internal benefits documentation, employee FAQs, and standard operating procedures (SOPs) as programs scale.\n\n - Coordinate vendor onboarding, administrative PO creation, and contract workflows with guidance from Finance and Legal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 2–4 years of experience in benefits administration, leave management, or a related HR operations role, ideally within a global or multi-country environment\n\n - Working knowledge of EMEA and/or APAC benefits structures, statutory requirements, and leave entitlements\n\n - Excellent communication and service orientation, with a track record of delivering responsive, empathetic employee support\n\n - Experience working with HRIS platforms (e.g., Workday), HR ticketing or case management systems (e.g., ServiceNow, Zendesk, Jira, or Workday Help), and benefits administration tools\n\n - Experience or exposure to benefits vendor/broker management\n\n - Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret benefits data and produce actionable insights\n\n - Ability to manage day-to-day workflows independently while knowing when to seek guidance or escalate complex issues\n\n - Proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (vlookups, pivot tables) for basic data analysis and invoice reconciliation\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n \n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"796b7f8d-5135-4419-bb89-6d00989b21f4","title":"Customer Success, Enterprise","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Madrid","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T15:15:02.343+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/796b7f8d-5135-4419-bb89-6d00989b21f4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/796b7f8d-5135-4419-bb89-6d00989b21f4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong>: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationships</strong>: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics</strong>: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expansion and Renewal</strong>: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing customer-facing projects and timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Running in-person meetings w/ executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Driving key customer metrics and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Onboarding: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.\n\n - Training & Enablement: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.\n\n - Relationships: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.\n\n - Success Metrics: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.\n\n - Expansion and Renewal: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.\n\n - Product Feedback: Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nIdeal candidates for the Enterprise CSM role at Harvey can demonstrate comfort and experience with the following qualifications:\n\n - 3-4+ years in customer-owning roles at tech or SaaS platforms\n\n - Adapting seamlessly in the face of high-speed change and growth\n\n - Strategic planning, revenue-based prioritization\n\n - Managing customer-facing projects and timelines\n\n - Running in-person meetings w/ executives\n\n - Mapping an organization and influencing stakeholders\n\n - Driving key customer metrics and outcomes\n\n - Owning a revenue, expansion, and renewal target\n\n - Demonstrating a strong point of view and proactive self-management\n\n - Working cross-functionally with Product and Sales teams\n   \n   \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4ee35126-b33d-4928-a2e7-11d28fc8dab5","title":"Global Manager, Recruiting Operations and Coordination","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T00:02:18.900+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4ee35126-b33d-4928-a2e7-11d28fc8dab5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/4ee35126-b33d-4928-a2e7-11d28fc8dab5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Head of Recruiting Coordination joins Harvey's Talent team to lead and scale the recruiting coordination function across the company's global offices. The team's mission is to deliver an exceptional candidate experience while driving operational efficiency throughout the interview lifecycle. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns the strategy and execution for recruiting coordination programs, automation initiatives, and process improvement that enable Harvey to hire world-class talent at the pace a hypergrowth AI company demands. They partner directly with recruiting leadership, People Operations, and systems teams to architect scalable workflows that maintain a high-quality bar as the organization grows. It is a rare opportunity to build and lead a coordination function at a company redefining an industry through AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and manage a team of recruiting coordinators across multiple offices, setting standards for candidate experience, interview logistics, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own internal recruiting programs including interviewer enablement, onboarding for new interviewers, and coordination training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Tier 1 operational backlog, including things like creating and closing job requisitions, ATS data upkeep, interview plan maintenance, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement process improvements within tier one operations that reduce friction for recruiters, hiring managers, and candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Recruiting Operations on ATS architecture, workflow optimization, and data integrity to support hiring at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain metrics and dashboards that track coordination team performance, candidate experience, and process efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as an escalation point for scheduling and coordination issues, ensuring a consistently high-quality candidate and interviewer experience</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations or coordination, with progressive team management responsibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building and managing a coordination team in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in ATS platforms (e.g., Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever) and workflow automation tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use data to drive process improvements and inform stakeholder decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills and the ability to influence without authority across recruiting, People Operations, and hiring manager stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000- $220,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Head of Recruiting Coordination joins Harvey's Talent team to lead and scale the recruiting coordination function across the company's global offices. The team's mission is to deliver an exceptional candidate experience while driving operational efficiency throughout the interview lifecycle. \n\n\n\nThis role owns the strategy and execution for recruiting coordination programs, automation initiatives, and process improvement that enable Harvey to hire world-class talent at the pace a hypergrowth AI company demands. They partner directly with recruiting leadership, People Operations, and systems teams to architect scalable workflows that maintain a high-quality bar as the organization grows. It is a rare opportunity to build and lead a coordination function at a company redefining an industry through AI.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, mentor, and manage a team of recruiting coordinators across multiple offices, setting standards for candidate experience, interview logistics, and operational excellence.\n\n - Own internal recruiting programs including interviewer enablement, onboarding for new interviewers, and coordination training.\n\n - Own Tier 1 operational backlog, including things like creating and closing job requisitions, ATS data upkeep, interview plan maintenance, etc.\n\n - Design and implement process improvements within tier one operations that reduce friction for recruiters, hiring managers, and candidates\n\n - Partner with Recruiting Operations on ATS architecture, workflow optimization, and data integrity to support hiring at scale.\n\n - Develop and maintain metrics and dashboards that track coordination team performance, candidate experience, and process efficiency.\n\n - Serve as an escalation point for scheduling and coordination issues, ensuring a consistently high-quality candidate and interviewer experience\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5–8+ years of experience in recruiting operations or coordination, with progressive team management responsibility.\n\n - Demonstrated success building and managing a coordination team in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.\n\n - Deep expertise in ATS platforms (e.g., Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever) and workflow automation tools.\n\n - Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use data to drive process improvements and inform stakeholder decisions.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills and the ability to influence without authority across recruiting, People Operations, and hiring manager stakeholders.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$180,000- $220,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1040608f-e9aa-43ac-974e-9341e8a73422","tierSummary":"$180K – $220K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"746e4f11-bc37-4317-a25a-0a94f45032fb","summary":"$180K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000},{"id":"4b3ca0cd-c32d-463b-bf1b-4aec231f3333","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9d7153fc-111a-438d-bd40-37c07355078c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":220000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"50b4605a-5f3a-4805-ac3e-50c1d3c6a2e0","title":"Legal Engineer - Custom Solutions","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sydney","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T23:44:09.771+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Australia","addressLocality":"Sydney"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/50b4605a-5f3a-4805-ac3e-50c1d3c6a2e0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/50b4605a-5f3a-4805-ac3e-50c1d3c6a2e0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineers in Custom Solutions are experienced lawyers who immerse themselves in the Harvey platform to design, build, and deploy tailored AI-powered workflows for the firm's most strategic customers in the Asia-Pacific region. Sitting within the Legal Engineering organization, this role partners closely with Account Executives, Customer Success, and Product to deliver high-impact implementations that drive deep adoption and measurable value for law firms and in-house legal teams across Australia and the broader APAC market. The Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions owns the end-to-end solution lifecycle — from scoping requirements through delivery — translating complex legal workflows into purpose-built Harvey configurations that solve real problems at scale. This is a rare opportunity to serve as the face of Harvey's Custom Solutions function in Sydney, working at the intersection of legal expertise, product depth, and client partnership in one of Harvey's fastest-growing markets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with lawyers at current and prospective customers to understand complex workflow challenges, scope custom solution requirements, and design tailored Harvey implementations that address them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine custom workflows, playbooks, and product configurations within the Harvey platform, ensuring each solution is credible, scalable, and grounded in how legal teams actually work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Account Executives and Customer Success to support post-sale adoption, change management strategy, and account expansion by delivering ongoing legal engineering value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the Voice of the Customer, translating legal workflow insights and user feedback into concrete product direction for Harvey's engineering and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing and Legal Innovation teams to develop Australia - and APAC-relevant content, use cases, and enablement materials that resonate with the region's legal community.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified to practice law in Australia with at least 3 years of post-qualification experience at a top-tier law firm or in-house legal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with the ability to establish strong relationships with key decision-makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using product demonstrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and workflows relevant to the Australia legal market, with curiosity about AI's potential to transform them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating at speed in ambiguous, fast-moving environments; excitement about building at an early-stage company where the ability to ship solutions and iterate quickly is rewarded.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience — including law firm business development, client secondments, or managing client relationships — is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GW1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineers in Custom Solutions are experienced lawyers who immerse themselves in the Harvey platform to design, build, and deploy tailored AI-powered workflows for the firm's most strategic customers in the Asia-Pacific region. Sitting within the Legal Engineering organization, this role partners closely with Account Executives, Customer Success, and Product to deliver high-impact implementations that drive deep adoption and measurable value for law firms and in-house legal teams across Australia and the broader APAC market. The Legal Engineer, Custom Solutions owns the end-to-end solution lifecycle — from scoping requirements through delivery — translating complex legal workflows into purpose-built Harvey configurations that solve real problems at scale. This is a rare opportunity to serve as the face of Harvey's Custom Solutions function in Sydney, working at the intersection of legal expertise, product depth, and client partnership in one of Harvey's fastest-growing markets.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Work directly with lawyers at current and prospective customers to understand complex workflow challenges, scope custom solution requirements, and design tailored Harvey implementations that address them.\n\n - Build and refine custom workflows, playbooks, and product configurations within the Harvey platform, ensuring each solution is credible, scalable, and grounded in how legal teams actually work.\n\n - Partner with Account Executives and Customer Success to support post-sale adoption, change management strategy, and account expansion by delivering ongoing legal engineering value.\n\n - Act as the Voice of the Customer, translating legal workflow insights and user feedback into concrete product direction for Harvey's engineering and product teams.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing and Legal Innovation teams to develop Australia - and APAC-relevant content, use cases, and enablement materials that resonate with the region's legal community.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Qualified to practice law in Australia with at least 3 years of post-qualification experience at a top-tier law firm or in-house legal team.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with the ability to establish strong relationships with key decision-makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using product demonstrations.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and workflows relevant to the Australia legal market, with curiosity about AI's potential to transform them.\n\n - Comfort operating at speed in ambiguous, fast-moving environments; excitement about building at an early-stage company where the ability to ship solutions and iterate quickly is rewarded.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience — including law firm business development, client secondments, or managing client relationships — is a strong plus.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-GW1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"83215ffd-c901-4cd6-8081-35e072e966cd","title":"Integrated Campaigns Lead","department":"Marketing","team":"Demand Generation","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T23:21:13.848+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/83215ffd-c901-4cd6-8081-35e072e966cd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/83215ffd-c901-4cd6-8081-35e072e966cd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's users are among the most sophisticated professionals - from managing partners and practice leaders at global law firms to GCs and legal operations executives in-house, and tax and finance leaders adopting AI across their organizations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">These professionals are navigating a fundamental shift in how their work gets done. Reaching them starts with deeply understanding the realities of that work: the problems worth solving, the outcomes that matter, and the questions and skepticism that come with adopting AI. Our best campaigns turn that understanding into ideas and experiences that are useful, credible, and relevant to where each audience is on that journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Integrated Campaigns Lead will build the function responsible for doing exactly that.You'll set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy: defining our priority audiences, sharpening how we position Harvey, and designing coordinated programs that build awareness, deepen engagement, and drive growth. You'll establish the campaign operating model, prove what works, and build the team and capabilities to scale it globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a strategic player-coach role with meaningful influence across the company. You'll shape go-to-market priorities alongside leadership across marketing, product, GTM, and you'll stay close enough to the work to write the message, understand the data, and improve the campaign when it matters.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy.</strong> Define the audiences, segments, narratives, and campaign architecture that build relevance with our audiences and drive awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn audience insight into differentiated positioning.</strong> Develop messaging rooted in primary research, customer insight, competitive intelligence, and demonstrated use cases. Build claims on evidence and create narratives sophisticated audiences find credible.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Translate company priorities into market-facing programs.</strong> Partner with Product, Sales, and business leaders to develop marketing strategies around Harvey's most important growth initiatives, connecting what matters to the business with what matters to our audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Orchestrate the full marketing system.</strong> Bring together digital, social, communications and analyst relations, alliances, events, field marketing, and other channels into cohesive global campaigns, spanning major launches, category-building moments, and always-on programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the measurement system.</strong> Define the KPIs, dashboards, attribution signals, and operating cadence that connect campaign investment to audience and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the team and operating model.</strong> Design how the campaigns function works, hire exceptional marketers, and develop them into strategic owners of audiences, programs, and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raise the creative and strategic bar.</strong> Establish what great campaign thinking looks like at Harvey, from the quality of the insight and sharpness of the message to the craft of the execution and rigor of the measurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build an AI-native campaign engine.</strong> Apply AI across audience research and modeling, creative development, experimentation, personalization, localization, and performance analysis. Develop repeatable approaches that raise the capabilities of the broader marketing organization.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>8+ years of B2B marketing experience</strong>, including significant ownership of integrated campaigns, demand generation, or go-to-market programs within enterprise software or high-growth SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A record of building and scaling.</strong> You've created teams, programs, or operating models and know how to introduce structure without introducing unnecessary process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience building and leading exceptional teams.</strong> You've hired, developed, and retained high-performing marketers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong commercial instincts.</strong> You've owned multi-million-dollar investments and understand how to connect marketing decisions to audience impact, pipeline, revenue, and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional positioning and messaging judgment.</strong> You know how to get from audience research and market insight to a differentiated point of view, and you're a strong enough writer to do the work yourself when the stakes are high.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional cross-functional influence.</strong> You've orchestrated digital, social, communications, analyst relations, partnerships, events, and field marketing as one system rather than optimizing a single channel in isolation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hands-on fluency with AI.</strong> AI is already part of your campaign workflow. You have informed opinions about where it meaningfully improves marketing, and where human judgment remains the advantage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A player-coach operating style.</strong> You're comfortable setting strategy with senior leaders and equally comfortable opening the doc, digging into the dashboard, rewriting the brief, or working through the details with the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambition and ambiguity.</strong> You can create clarity where there isn't yet a playbook, move quickly without lowering the bar, and build systems that become more sophisticated as Harvey grows.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$196,000 - $269,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's users are among the most sophisticated professionals - from managing partners and practice leaders at global law firms to GCs and legal operations executives in-house, and tax and finance leaders adopting AI across their organizations.\n\n\n\nThese professionals are navigating a fundamental shift in how their work gets done. Reaching them starts with deeply understanding the realities of that work: the problems worth solving, the outcomes that matter, and the questions and skepticism that come with adopting AI. Our best campaigns turn that understanding into ideas and experiences that are useful, credible, and relevant to where each audience is on that journey.\n\n\n\nThe Integrated Campaigns Lead will build the function responsible for doing exactly that.You'll set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy: defining our priority audiences, sharpening how we position Harvey, and designing coordinated programs that build awareness, deepen engagement, and drive growth. You'll establish the campaign operating model, prove what works, and build the team and capabilities to scale it globally.\n\n\n\nThis is a strategic player-coach role with meaningful influence across the company. You'll shape go-to-market priorities alongside leadership across marketing, product, GTM, and you'll stay close enough to the work to write the message, understand the data, and improve the campaign when it matters.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy. Define the audiences, segments, narratives, and campaign architecture that build relevance with our audiences and drive awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue.\n\n - Turn audience insight into differentiated positioning. Develop messaging rooted in primary research, customer insight, competitive intelligence, and demonstrated use cases. Build claims on evidence and create narratives sophisticated audiences find credible.\n\n - Translate company priorities into market-facing programs. Partner with Product, Sales, and business leaders to develop marketing strategies around Harvey's most important growth initiatives, connecting what matters to the business with what matters to our audiences.\n\n - Orchestrate the full marketing system. Bring together digital, social, communications and analyst relations, alliances, events, field marketing, and other channels into cohesive global campaigns, spanning major launches, category-building moments, and always-on programs.\n\n - Build the measurement system. Define the KPIs, dashboards, attribution signals, and operating cadence that connect campaign investment to audience and business outcomes.\n\n - Build the team and operating model. Design how the campaigns function works, hire exceptional marketers, and develop them into strategic owners of audiences, programs, and business outcomes.\n\n - Raise the creative and strategic bar. Establish what great campaign thinking looks like at Harvey, from the quality of the insight and sharpness of the message to the craft of the execution and rigor of the measurement.\n\n - Build an AI-native campaign engine. Apply AI across audience research and modeling, creative development, experimentation, personalization, localization, and performance analysis. Develop repeatable approaches that raise the capabilities of the broader marketing organization.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of B2B marketing experience, including significant ownership of integrated campaigns, demand generation, or go-to-market programs within enterprise software or high-growth SaaS.\n\n - A record of building and scaling. You've created teams, programs, or operating models and know how to introduce structure without introducing unnecessary process.\n\n - Experience building and leading exceptional teams. You've hired, developed, and retained high-performing marketers.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts. You've owned multi-million-dollar investments and understand how to connect marketing decisions to audience impact, pipeline, revenue, and ROI.\n\n - Exceptional positioning and messaging judgment. You know how to get from audience research and market insight to a differentiated point of view, and you're a strong enough writer to do the work yourself when the stakes are high.\n\n - Exceptional cross-functional influence. You've orchestrated digital, social, communications, analyst relations, partnerships, events, and field marketing as one system rather than optimizing a single channel in isolation.\n\n - Hands-on fluency with AI. AI is already part of your campaign workflow. You have informed opinions about where it meaningfully improves marketing, and where human judgment remains the advantage.\n\n - A player-coach operating style. You're comfortable setting strategy with senior leaders and equally comfortable opening the doc, digging into the dashboard, rewriting the brief, or working through the details with the team.\n\n - Comfort with ambition and ambiguity. You can create clarity where there isn't yet a playbook, move quickly without lowering the bar, and build systems that become more sophisticated as Harvey grows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$196,000 - $269,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$196K – $269.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$196K - $269.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ff8098b7-7249-4b26-a1e3-815dcbca1570","tierSummary":"$196K – $269.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2e5f6e4a-c786-4fad-8552-1775d56667c0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"9edc694a-9a4c-49a2-83d4-80efd149d91d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"16b12870-b631-44dd-a9ca-09b4c99618a2","summary":"$196K – $269.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196000,"maxValue":269500}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196000,"maxValue":269500}]}},{"id":"cbf49618-c6ce-4a9a-a806-2a0133622910","title":"Integrated Campaigns Lead","department":"Marketing","team":"Demand Generation","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T23:22:28.921+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cbf49618-c6ce-4a9a-a806-2a0133622910","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cbf49618-c6ce-4a9a-a806-2a0133622910/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's users are among the most sophisticated professionals - from managing partners and practice leaders at global law firms to GCs and legal operations executives in-house, and tax and finance leaders adopting AI across their organizations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">These professionals are navigating a fundamental shift in how their work gets done. Reaching them starts with deeply understanding the realities of that work: the problems worth solving, the outcomes that matter, and the questions and skepticism that come with adopting AI. Our best campaigns turn that understanding into ideas and experiences that are useful, credible, and relevant to where each audience is on that journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Integrated Campaigns Lead will build the function responsible for doing exactly that. You'll set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy: defining our priority audiences, sharpening how we position Harvey, and designing coordinated programs that build awareness, deepen engagement, and drive growth. You'll establish the campaign operating model, prove what works, and build the team and capabilities to scale it globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a strategic player-coach role with meaningful influence across the company. You'll shape go-to-market priorities alongside leadership across marketing, product, GTM, and you'll stay close enough to the work to write the message, understand the data, and improve the campaign when it matters.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy.</strong> Define the audiences, segments, narratives, and campaign architecture that build relevance with our audiences and drive awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn audience insight into differentiated positioning.</strong> Develop messaging rooted in primary research, customer insight, competitive intelligence, and demonstrated use cases. Build claims on evidence and create narratives sophisticated audiences find credible.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Translate company priorities into market-facing programs.</strong> Partner with Product, Sales, and business leaders to develop marketing strategies around Harvey's most important growth initiatives, connecting what matters to the business with what matters to our audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Orchestrate the full marketing system.</strong> Bring together digital, social, communications and analyst relations, alliances, events, field marketing, and other channels into cohesive global campaigns, spanning major launches, category-building moments, and always-on programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the measurement system.</strong> Define the KPIs, dashboards, attribution signals, and operating cadence that connect campaign investment to audience and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the team and operating model.</strong> Design how the campaigns function works, hire exceptional marketers, and develop them into strategic owners of audiences, programs, and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raise the creative and strategic bar.</strong> Establish what great campaign thinking looks like at Harvey, from the quality of the insight and sharpness of the message to the craft of the execution and rigor of the measurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build an AI-native campaign engine.</strong> Apply AI across audience research and modeling, creative development, experimentation, personalization, localization, and performance analysis. Develop repeatable approaches that raise the capabilities of the broader marketing organization.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>8+ years of B2B marketing experience</strong>, including significant ownership of integrated campaigns, demand generation, or go-to-market programs within enterprise software or high-growth SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A record of building and scaling.</strong> You've created teams, programs, or operating models and know how to introduce structure without introducing unnecessary process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience building and leading exceptional teams.</strong> You've hired, developed, and retained high-performing marketers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong commercial instincts.</strong> You've owned multi-million-dollar investments and understand how to connect marketing decisions to audience impact, pipeline, revenue, and ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional positioning and messaging judgment.</strong> You know how to get from audience research and market insight to a differentiated point of view, and you're a strong enough writer to do the work yourself when the stakes are high.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional cross-functional influence.</strong> You've orchestrated digital, social, communications, analyst relations, partnerships, events, and field marketing as one system rather than optimizing a single channel in isolation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hands-on fluency with AI.</strong> AI is already part of your campaign workflow. You have informed opinions about where it meaningfully improves marketing, and where human judgment remains the advantage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A player-coach operating style.</strong> You're comfortable setting strategy with senior leaders and equally comfortable opening the doc, digging into the dashboard, rewriting the brief, or working through the details with the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambition and ambiguity.</strong> You can create clarity where there isn't yet a playbook, move quickly without lowering the bar, and build systems that become more sophisticated as Harvey grows.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$196,000 - $269,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's users are among the most sophisticated professionals - from managing partners and practice leaders at global law firms to GCs and legal operations executives in-house, and tax and finance leaders adopting AI across their organizations.\n\n\n\nThese professionals are navigating a fundamental shift in how their work gets done. Reaching them starts with deeply understanding the realities of that work: the problems worth solving, the outcomes that matter, and the questions and skepticism that come with adopting AI. Our best campaigns turn that understanding into ideas and experiences that are useful, credible, and relevant to where each audience is on that journey.\n\n\n\nThe Integrated Campaigns Lead will build the function responsible for doing exactly that. You'll set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy: defining our priority audiences, sharpening how we position Harvey, and designing coordinated programs that build awareness, deepen engagement, and drive growth. You'll establish the campaign operating model, prove what works, and build the team and capabilities to scale it globally.\n\n\n\nThis is a strategic player-coach role with meaningful influence across the company. You'll shape go-to-market priorities alongside leadership across marketing, product, GTM, and you'll stay close enough to the work to write the message, understand the data, and improve the campaign when it matters.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Set Harvey's global integrated campaign strategy. Define the audiences, segments, narratives, and campaign architecture that build relevance with our audiences and drive awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue.\n\n - Turn audience insight into differentiated positioning. Develop messaging rooted in primary research, customer insight, competitive intelligence, and demonstrated use cases. Build claims on evidence and create narratives sophisticated audiences find credible.\n\n - Translate company priorities into market-facing programs. Partner with Product, Sales, and business leaders to develop marketing strategies around Harvey's most important growth initiatives, connecting what matters to the business with what matters to our audiences.\n\n - Orchestrate the full marketing system. Bring together digital, social, communications and analyst relations, alliances, events, field marketing, and other channels into cohesive global campaigns, spanning major launches, category-building moments, and always-on programs.\n\n - Build the measurement system. Define the KPIs, dashboards, attribution signals, and operating cadence that connect campaign investment to audience and business outcomes.\n\n - Build the team and operating model. Design how the campaigns function works, hire exceptional marketers, and develop them into strategic owners of audiences, programs, and business outcomes.\n\n - Raise the creative and strategic bar. Establish what great campaign thinking looks like at Harvey, from the quality of the insight and sharpness of the message to the craft of the execution and rigor of the measurement.\n\n - Build an AI-native campaign engine. Apply AI across audience research and modeling, creative development, experimentation, personalization, localization, and performance analysis. Develop repeatable approaches that raise the capabilities of the broader marketing organization.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of B2B marketing experience, including significant ownership of integrated campaigns, demand generation, or go-to-market programs within enterprise software or high-growth SaaS.\n\n - A record of building and scaling. You've created teams, programs, or operating models and know how to introduce structure without introducing unnecessary process.\n\n - Experience building and leading exceptional teams. You've hired, developed, and retained high-performing marketers.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts. You've owned multi-million-dollar investments and understand how to connect marketing decisions to audience impact, pipeline, revenue, and ROI.\n\n - Exceptional positioning and messaging judgment. You know how to get from audience research and market insight to a differentiated point of view, and you're a strong enough writer to do the work yourself when the stakes are high.\n\n - Exceptional cross-functional influence. You've orchestrated digital, social, communications, analyst relations, partnerships, events, and field marketing as one system rather than optimizing a single channel in isolation.\n\n - Hands-on fluency with AI. AI is already part of your campaign workflow. You have informed opinions about where it meaningfully improves marketing, and where human judgment remains the advantage.\n\n - A player-coach operating style. You're comfortable setting strategy with senior leaders and equally comfortable opening the doc, digging into the dashboard, rewriting the brief, or working through the details with the team.\n\n - Comfort with ambition and ambiguity. You can create clarity where there isn't yet a playbook, move quickly without lowering the bar, and build systems that become more sophisticated as Harvey grows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$196,000 - $269,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-BG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$196K – $269.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$196K - $269.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"94c43978-55a0-46c2-a917-21970cf142ca","tierSummary":"$196K – $269.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9af7707f-ca3b-4624-b114-63b2380b86d3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0a4ca65a-db04-4df2-a44a-02917199ad92","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5b38b170-e6b9-476b-b4c3-a71dc028296f","summary":"$196K – $269.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196000,"maxValue":269500}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":196000,"maxValue":269500}]}},{"id":"94495873-2f90-4c42-a45d-b10b2b0756a7","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager, Data","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T17:55:04.874+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/94495873-2f90-4c42-a45d-b10b2b0756a7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/94495873-2f90-4c42-a45d-b10b2b0756a7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Operations Manager, Data at Harvey, you'll be the connective tissue between our data product surfaces, Engineering, GTM, and the external technology partners we rely on — making sure customer and partner signals turn into fast, well-coordinated action. You'll own intake and triage for feature requests and data issues, run early-access programs and cross-functional launches, and manage the partner relationships that keep our data pipeline reliable for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a role for someone who's comfortable being in the weeds of a technical issue one hour and briefing leadership on launch risk the next — and who'd rather build a lightweight system that scales than a heavy process that doesn't get used.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer, Partner &amp; Issue Intake</strong> — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of customer feature requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage customer-reported data and product issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage relationships with external technology partners, including onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs &amp; Launches</strong> — Getting new capabilities into customers' hands, then out the door broadly</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and run early-access programs for new features, including customer selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional launches by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems That Scale</strong> — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate customer, partner, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials that help internal teams communicate and operate effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring operational challenges and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes that enable the team to scale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Technical Program Management, or a related operational role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally supporting data, integrations, or technical product surface.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience triaging and prioritizing inbound requests and issues at volume — you know how to separate signal from noise and route things to the right owner without becoming a bottleneck.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable engaging with data and technical issues directly enough to assess severity and impact, even when you're not the one fixing them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing external vendor or technology partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication — you can turn messy feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that other teams actually use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, and GTM without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Operations Manager, Data at Harvey, you'll be the connective tissue between our data product surfaces, Engineering, GTM, and the external technology partners we rely on — making sure customer and partner signals turn into fast, well-coordinated action. You'll own intake and triage for feature requests and data issues, run early-access programs and cross-functional launches, and manage the partner relationships that keep our data pipeline reliable for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.\n\nThis is a role for someone who's comfortable being in the weeds of a technical issue one hour and briefing leadership on launch risk the next — and who'd rather build a lightweight system that scales than a heavy process that doesn't get used.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nCustomer, Partner & Issue Intake — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast\n\n - Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of customer feature requests.\n\n - Triage customer-reported data and product issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.\n\n - Manage relationships with external technology partners, including onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.\n\nPrograms & Launches — Getting new capabilities into customers' hands, then out the door broadly\n\n - Plan and run early-access programs for new features, including customer selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional launches by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.\n\nSystems That Scale — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process\n\n - Translate customer, partner, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations.\n\n - Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials that help internal teams communicate and operate effectively.\n\n - Identify recurring operational challenges and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes that enable the team to scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Technical Program Management, or a related operational role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally supporting data, integrations, or technical product surface.\n\n - Experience triaging and prioritizing inbound requests and issues at volume — you know how to separate signal from noise and route things to the right owner without becoming a bottleneck.\n\n - Comfortable engaging with data and technical issues directly enough to assess severity and impact, even when you're not the one fixing them.\n\n - Experience managing external vendor or technology partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.\n\n - Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.\n\n - Strong written communication — you can turn messy feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that other teams actually use.\n\n - Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, and GTM without direct authority.\n\n - A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"84492754-5497-4a71-9214-fc91060adb61","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f3887806-5659-458d-a61e-44aae217faa3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b19054e0-2548-4917-8e89-01d0add723f5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a4920a4b-f96c-4dcb-98f6-c513246d80e3","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200}]}},{"id":"88905094-1b46-41e1-a88a-cae239431b04","title":"IT Operations Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T23:12:47.656+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88905094-1b46-41e1-a88a-cae239431b04","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/88905094-1b46-41e1-a88a-cae239431b04/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Bonus Points</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$109,100 - $150,100 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.\n\nThe IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.\n\nYou’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.\n\n - Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.\n\n - Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.\n\n - Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.\n\n - Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.\n\n - Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.\n\n - Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.\n\n - Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.\n\n - Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.\n\n - Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.\n\n - A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.\n\n - Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.\n\n\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.\n\n - Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$109,100 - $150,100 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$109.1K – $150.1K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$109.1K - $150.1K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bbc40274-7877-4ba4-9a6e-e96692f684c3","tierSummary":"$109.1K – $150.1K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c1e9c19d-0df2-4948-9022-5594db591416","summary":"$109.1K – $150.1K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":150100},{"id":"cdecb40e-6fd2-47c2-85d4-197552937cf4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"71a196b6-9a18-46e9-9db3-1300cc707175","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":150100},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f940d275-4719-4aa9-b2fb-31d8046127d8","title":"IT Operations Analyst","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T23:13:03.902+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f940d275-4719-4aa9-b2fb-31d8046127d8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f940d275-4719-4aa9-b2fb-31d8046127d8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Bonus Points</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$109,100 - $150,100 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re seeking an IT Operations Analyst to join our Business Technology (BizTech) team and help deliver a seamless employee experience through hands-on IT support in our New York City office. This role will be instrumental in ensuring our employees have the tools and technology they need to be productive, from their first day of onboarding through their entire lifecycle at Harvey.\n\nThe IT Operations Analyst joins Harvey's BizTech team to deliver seamless, high-touch technology support that keeps employees productive across a fast-moving AI company. The team's mission is to ensure every Harvey employee—from new hires to senior leadership—has frictionless access to the tools and systems they need to do their best work. This role drives day-to-day IT operations while contributing to automation, process improvement, and systems integration initiatives that scale support as the company grows. They partner closely with engineering, security, and cross-functional stakeholders to maintain reliable, secure infrastructure across Harvey's global offices. It is an opportunity to shape IT operations at a defining moment for legal AI—where initiative, technical curiosity, and a service-first mindset have outsized impact.\n\nYou’ll handle employee onboarding, lifecycle tasks, and aid employees with technology issues and workplace technology (A/V). This is a role ideal for someone with past experience in a fast-paced environment who is ready to make an impact.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Create a great employee experience through hands-on IT support for employees in our New York City office.\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding processes to ensure new hires are productive from day one and departures are handled cleanly and securely.\n\n - Provide white-glove IT support to employees across all levels, triaging requests via Slack, ticketing systems, and in-person interactions with a focus on speed and empathy.\n\n - Administer and optimize core SaaS platforms including Google Workspace, Okta, Slack, Zoom, and MDM solutions (Jamf/InTune) to ensure secure and reliable access.\n\n - Assist with meeting room tech and corporate events to ensure smooth hybrid meetings and high-quality A/V experiences.\n\n - Troubleshoot employee problems with applications, laptops, access, peripherals, printers, video conferencing, and networking issues.\n\n - Maintain IT asset inventory and coordinate hardware repairs, upgrades, and procurement.\n\n - Identify and resolve systemic issues through root cause analysis, escalating patterns to improve reliability across the technology stack.\n\n - Collaborate with the IT team on automation, documentation, and process improvements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in IT support experience in a fast-paced startup or tech environment.\n\n - Strong proficiency with identity and access management platforms (Okta preferred), Google Workspace administration, and macOS device management.\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace, Okta (SSO/MFA), Slack, and other SaaS tools.\n\n - Hands-on scripting or automation experience (e.g., Python, Bash, Okta Workflows) that goes beyond basic helpdesk troubleshooting.\n\n - Excellent communication and customer service skills with the ability to support senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders with patience and clarity.\n\n - A proactive, employee-first mindset—you notice problems before they're reported and take initiative to fix them.\n\n - Comfort working in a high-growth, ambiguous environment where priorities shift and resourcefulness is essential.\n\n\n\n\nBONUS POINTS\n\n - Experience with scripting or automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to streamline IT tasks.\n\n - Experience managing MDM tools like Jamf, Kandji, or Intune.\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Office and Windows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$109,100 - $150,100 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-DB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$109.1K – $150.1K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$109.1K - $150.1K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"eeb12631-8f91-457c-93c9-f7a6c8f66ba7","tierSummary":"$109.1K – $150.1K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0842eb16-a9de-4c38-b680-5ca14eb447e4","summary":"$109.1K – $150.1K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":150100}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":109100,"maxValue":150100}]}},{"id":"f3323080-b727-461e-9a21-9b2ea8db2d45","title":"GTM Enablement Manager, FLM Coaching","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T18:57:58.547+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f3323080-b727-461e-9a21-9b2ea8db2d45","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f3323080-b727-461e-9a21-9b2ea8db2d45/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontline managers are the most important lever in GTM performance. They set the coaching culture, run team reviews, and decide whether reps are actually developing or just executing. Right now, we don't have a dedicated person helping our managers get better at that work. This role builds that program — and owns it end to end.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The job is to build repeatable systems: a leader program that strengthens coaching habits and team effectiveness, a methodology reinforcement model that works in the flow of the quarter, and a new hire experience that gets NAMER reps ramped as fast as anyone. You define the vision, build the operating model, and track whether it's actually changing behavior.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manager coaching program</strong> — Build and own a structured program for frontline managers: what great looks like in a coaching conversation, a team review, a development plan. Make it repeatable with governance and success metrics that scale beyond you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Methodology reinforcement</strong> — Translate our sales methodology into practical field behaviors and a reinforcement model that sticks long after the initial rollout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Rep skills programs</strong> — Own foundational skill-building programs managers can't run alone: discovery, competitive positioning, core seller skills. Build the architecture, drive adoption, measure behavior change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>GTM process alignment</strong> — Partner with RevOps and Revenue Leadership to ensure coaching and training reinforce how we run the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Measurement</strong> — Define what success looks like (manager adoption, behavior change, field productivity) and use that signal to continuously improve. You're accountable for outcomes, not just delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manager Onboarding —</strong> Partner with our GTM Onboarding PM to develop best in class content and delivery for our newest managers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–8 years in enablement, learning &amp; development, program management, or a related GTM role — ideally at a high-growth tech company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building programs for frontline managers and leaders, not just individual contributors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with a structured sales methodology (MEDDPICC, Command of the Message, or similar) and experience translating it into field behaviors and reinforcement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management instincts: governance, stakeholder rhythms, measurement frameworks — not just curriculum design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You understand what drives durable behavior change and build for that, not just completion rates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence leaders and managers across functions without formal authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can bring clarity and structure to ambiguous, build-from-scratch work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $187,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nFrontline managers are the most important lever in GTM performance. They set the coaching culture, run team reviews, and decide whether reps are actually developing or just executing. Right now, we don't have a dedicated person helping our managers get better at that work. This role builds that program — and owns it end to end.\n\nThe job is to build repeatable systems: a leader program that strengthens coaching habits and team effectiveness, a methodology reinforcement model that works in the flow of the quarter, and a new hire experience that gets NAMER reps ramped as fast as anyone. You define the vision, build the operating model, and track whether it's actually changing behavior.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manager coaching program — Build and own a structured program for frontline managers: what great looks like in a coaching conversation, a team review, a development plan. Make it repeatable with governance and success metrics that scale beyond you.\n\n - Methodology reinforcement — Translate our sales methodology into practical field behaviors and a reinforcement model that sticks long after the initial rollout.\n\n - Rep skills programs — Own foundational skill-building programs managers can't run alone: discovery, competitive positioning, core seller skills. Build the architecture, drive adoption, measure behavior change.\n\n - GTM process alignment — Partner with RevOps and Revenue Leadership to ensure coaching and training reinforce how we run the business.\n\n - Measurement — Define what success looks like (manager adoption, behavior change, field productivity) and use that signal to continuously improve. You're accountable for outcomes, not just delivery.\n\n - Manager Onboarding — Partner with our GTM Onboarding PM to develop best in class content and delivery for our newest managers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6–8 years in enablement, learning & development, program management, or a related GTM role — ideally at a high-growth tech company\n\n - Proven track record building programs for frontline managers and leaders, not just individual contributors\n\n - Familiarity with a structured sales methodology (MEDDPICC, Command of the Message, or similar) and experience translating it into field behaviors and reinforcement\n\n - Strong program management instincts: governance, stakeholder rhythms, measurement frameworks — not just curriculum design\n\n - You understand what drives durable behavior change and build for that, not just completion rates\n\n - Ability to influence leaders and managers across functions without formal authority\n\n - Strong communicator who can bring clarity and structure to ambiguous, build-from-scratch work\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $187,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-TM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $187K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ee3e3b77-fe11-4702-af84-9806773f1170","tierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f5b5c086-12ea-4d92-97a3-2d0876c2c75c","summary":"$136K – $187K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000},{"id":"7090cfff-4132-46b2-a269-ecb32fba5613","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d9835886-9fda-436f-8891-625bfcd44fb5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5dfffd0a-4a80-4248-ba41-b02335e8100c","title":"GTM Enablement Manager, FLM Coaching","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T18:58:02.943+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5dfffd0a-4a80-4248-ba41-b02335e8100c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5dfffd0a-4a80-4248-ba41-b02335e8100c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontline managers are the most important lever in GTM performance. They set the coaching culture, run team reviews, and decide whether reps are actually developing or just executing. Right now, we don't have a dedicated person helping our managers get better at that work. This role builds that program — and owns it end to end.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The job is to build repeatable systems: a leader program that strengthens coaching habits and team effectiveness, a methodology reinforcement model that works in the flow of the quarter, and a new hire experience that gets NAMER reps ramped as fast as anyone. You define the vision, build the operating model, and track whether it's actually changing behavior.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manager coaching program</strong> — Build and own a structured program for frontline managers: what great looks like in a coaching conversation, a team review, a development plan. Make it repeatable with governance and success metrics that scale beyond you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Methodology reinforcement</strong> — Translate our sales methodology into practical field behaviors and a reinforcement model that sticks long after the initial rollout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Rep skills programs</strong> — Own foundational skill-building programs managers can't run alone: discovery, competitive positioning, core seller skills. Build the architecture, drive adoption, measure behavior change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>GTM process alignment</strong> — Partner with RevOps and Revenue Leadership to ensure coaching and training reinforce how we run the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Measurement</strong> — Define what success looks like (manager adoption, behavior change, field productivity) and use that signal to continuously improve. You're accountable for outcomes, not just delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manager Onboarding —</strong> Partner with our GTM Onboarding PM to develop best in class content and delivery for our newest managers.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–8 years in enablement, learning &amp; development, program management, or a related GTM role — ideally at a high-growth tech company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building programs for frontline managers and leaders, not just individual contributors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with a structured sales methodology (MEDDPICC, Command of the Message, or similar) and experience translating it into field behaviors and reinforcement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong program management instincts: governance, stakeholder rhythms, measurement frameworks — not just curriculum design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You understand what drives durable behavior change and build for that, not just completion rates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence leaders and managers across functions without formal authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can bring clarity and structure to ambiguous, build-from-scratch work</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $187,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-TM1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nFrontline managers are the most important lever in GTM performance. They set the coaching culture, run team reviews, and decide whether reps are actually developing or just executing. Right now, we don't have a dedicated person helping our managers get better at that work. This role builds that program — and owns it end to end.\n\nThe job is to build repeatable systems: a leader program that strengthens coaching habits and team effectiveness, a methodology reinforcement model that works in the flow of the quarter, and a new hire experience that gets NAMER reps ramped as fast as anyone. You define the vision, build the operating model, and track whether it's actually changing behavior.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Manager coaching program — Build and own a structured program for frontline managers: what great looks like in a coaching conversation, a team review, a development plan. Make it repeatable with governance and success metrics that scale beyond you.\n\n - Methodology reinforcement — Translate our sales methodology into practical field behaviors and a reinforcement model that sticks long after the initial rollout.\n\n - Rep skills programs — Own foundational skill-building programs managers can't run alone: discovery, competitive positioning, core seller skills. Build the architecture, drive adoption, measure behavior change.\n\n - GTM process alignment — Partner with RevOps and Revenue Leadership to ensure coaching and training reinforce how we run the business.\n\n - Measurement — Define what success looks like (manager adoption, behavior change, field productivity) and use that signal to continuously improve. You're accountable for outcomes, not just delivery.\n\n - Manager Onboarding — Partner with our GTM Onboarding PM to develop best in class content and delivery for our newest managers.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6–8 years in enablement, learning & development, program management, or a related GTM role — ideally at a high-growth tech company\n\n - Proven track record building programs for frontline managers and leaders, not just individual contributors\n\n - Familiarity with a structured sales methodology (MEDDPICC, Command of the Message, or similar) and experience translating it into field behaviors and reinforcement\n\n - Strong program management instincts: governance, stakeholder rhythms, measurement frameworks — not just curriculum design\n\n - You understand what drives durable behavior change and build for that, not just completion rates\n\n - Ability to influence leaders and managers across functions without formal authority\n\n - Strong communicator who can bring clarity and structure to ambiguous, build-from-scratch work\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $187,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-TM1\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $187K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"26d272c4-9aaf-4de1-9c0a-c147b27a505c","tierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ccaf8690-a38f-4402-8637-dcc8694f2fc0","summary":"$136K – $187K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000},{"id":"b7778030-20f5-4d96-b89c-dc06eb745a77","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ecacf8d9-f039-4f85-96ce-a9ea4879e985","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5ce5fe86-8e2f-4003-b88a-77fbbdeaecad","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager, Solutions","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:05:26.596+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5ce5fe86-8e2f-4003-b88a-77fbbdeaecad","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5ce5fe86-8e2f-4003-b88a-77fbbdeaecad/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a <strong>Senior Product Marketing Manager</strong> to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$137,600 - $206,400 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Senior Product Marketing Manager to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.\n\n - Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.\n\n - Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.\n\n - Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.\n\n - Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.\n\n - Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.\n\n - Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.\n\n - Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.\n\n - Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$137,600 - $206,400 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-LR1 \n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$137.6K - $206.4K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"05155be2-001b-4ac6-b65f-84ce878c59dc","tierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5909a7ed-1382-4404-92d8-658b6abff334","summary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}},{"id":"53645e07-5a0e-4257-ba0d-f8b2fc676c44","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager, Solutions","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:05:51.235+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/53645e07-5a0e-4257-ba0d-f8b2fc676c44","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/53645e07-5a0e-4257-ba0d-f8b2fc676c44/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a <strong>Senior Product Marketing Manager</strong> to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$137,600 - $206,400 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1 </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are hiring a Senior Product Marketing Manager to join the Solutions Marketing team to build the foundation for how Harvey's products show up as real, usable solutions for legal professionals. You'll set the standard for how Harvey packages, launches, and enables solutions across legal teams and emerging markets. Working closely with Marketing, Product, and GTM teams to define clear workflows, practical use cases, and repeatable, customer-ready assets across different segments and buyers. Success shows up as shared clarity across GTM, faster customer adoption and value realization, quality pipeline, and a durable story that scales as Harvey grows.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead go-to-market strategy for a core solution area, translating product capabilities into messaging and positioning tailored to the vertical, persona, and segment size.\n\n - Enable GTM teams with solution-led messaging, demo storylines, playbooks, and customer-ready materials that support the enterprise sales motion.\n\n - Partner with Product and Core Product Marketing to shape launches and own how it gets packaged and adapted across target verticals and personas.\n\n - Partner with Demand Gen and Content to develop full funnel campaigns that build thought leadership, drive demand, and mature pipeline.\n\n - Regularly conduct market, customer, and competitive research, grounding positioning and strategy in real customer needs and differentiated value.\n\n - Align on solutions prioritization and market opportunity across Product, GTM, and Marketing leadership teams.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 6-8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, Solutions Marketing, or a related role in B2B SaaS.\n\n - Proven experience marketing complex, workflow-driven products to enterprise buyers.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to connect technical product capabilities to customer problems, outcomes, and business value.\n\n - Expertise in developing positioning and messaging, and translating it into sales-facing and customer-facing assets across different audiences, segments, and verticals.\n\n - Experience contributing to product launches, including translating core launch messaging into content for specific industries or personas and building out assets.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$137,600 - $206,400 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-LR1 \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$137.6K - $206.4K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"05155be2-001b-4ac6-b65f-84ce878c59dc","tierSummary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5909a7ed-1382-4404-92d8-658b6abff334","summary":"$137.6K – $206.4K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":137600,"maxValue":206400}]}},{"id":"235f1793-7b5a-470b-b6ee-4f0f0249623c","title":"Senior Engineering Manager, Backend","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Bengaluru","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T16:36:58.819+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/235f1793-7b5a-470b-b6ee-4f0f0249623c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/235f1793-7b5a-470b-b6ee-4f0f0249623c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is redefining what’s possible in legal work by combining cutting-edge AI with intuitive product experiences. As we scale rapidly and take on increasingly complex use cases, we’re expanding our product engineering team to accelerate our ability to ship fast, delight users, and build infrastructure that scales with us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Engineering Manager for Product Engineering, you’ll lead teams of backend engineers building the core product surfaces that lawyers and legal professionals use every day—from complex workflows and collaboration tools to elegant user interfaces powered by sophisticated backend systems. This role is equal parts product intuition and technical execution. You’ll be trusted to make fast, high-quality decisions, ship impactful features, and grow a team that embodies engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We move with urgency, bias toward simplicity, and expect our leaders to be hands-on when needed. If you’re energized by ownership, decisive execution, and solving real user problems, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead engineers define, build, and drive the multi-quarter technical strategy for user-facing features across our product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Design, Product, and AI teams to identify and execute on high-impact initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define and evolve the architecture for a fast-moving, AI-powered application.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, grow, and retain exceptional engineers who thrive in a high-trust, high-impact environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of simplicity, quality, and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to code and architecture reviews, unblock teams, and lead by example when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with cross-functional partners to align product initiatives with company goals.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in a software engineering management role leading product engineering teams, preferably in high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12+ years of software engineering experience as a backend engineer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of leading high-performing, engaged engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product sense and an instinct for balancing speed, quality, and user impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with backend systems (e.g., Python, Java, Go) and modern cloud-native infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A plus: Exposure to AI-powered applications or complex internal tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to anticipate scaling bottlenecks before they occur and take decisive, proactive measures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building RAG pipelines and managing the data lifecycle.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-DM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is redefining what’s possible in legal work by combining cutting-edge AI with intuitive product experiences. As we scale rapidly and take on increasingly complex use cases, we’re expanding our product engineering team to accelerate our ability to ship fast, delight users, and build infrastructure that scales with us.\n\n\n\nAs a Senior Engineering Manager for Product Engineering, you’ll lead teams of backend engineers building the core product surfaces that lawyers and legal professionals use every day—from complex workflows and collaboration tools to elegant user interfaces powered by sophisticated backend systems. This role is equal parts product intuition and technical execution. You’ll be trusted to make fast, high-quality decisions, ship impactful features, and grow a team that embodies engineering excellence.\n\n\n\nWe move with urgency, bias toward simplicity, and expect our leaders to be hands-on when needed. If you’re energized by ownership, decisive execution, and solving real user problems, we'd love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead engineers define, build, and drive the multi-quarter technical strategy for user-facing features across our product.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Design, Product, and AI teams to identify and execute on high-impact initiatives.\n\n - Help define and evolve the architecture for a fast-moving, AI-powered application.\n\n - Hire, grow, and retain exceptional engineers who thrive in a high-trust, high-impact environment.\n\n - Foster a culture of simplicity, quality, and continuous improvement.\n\n - Contribute to code and architecture reviews, unblock teams, and lead by example when needed.\n\n - Work closely with cross-functional partners to align product initiatives with company goals.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in a software engineering management role leading product engineering teams, preferably in high-growth environments.\n\n - 12+ years of software engineering experience as a backend engineer.\n\n - A track record of leading high-performing, engaged engineering teams.\n\n - Strong product sense and an instinct for balancing speed, quality, and user impact.\n\n - Experience with backend systems (e.g., Python, Java, Go) and modern cloud-native infrastructure.\n\n - A plus: Exposure to AI-powered applications or complex internal tools.\n\n - Ability to anticipate scaling bottlenecks before they occur and take decisive, proactive measures.\n\n - Experience building RAG pipelines and managing the data lifecycle.\n   \n   \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Work eligibility: Must be authorized to work in India. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/india-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-DM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"08ea1c81-85a9-46fc-ad11-9db1d7dc5334","title":"CX Vendor Manager","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T23:43:43.802+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08ea1c81-85a9-46fc-ad11-9db1d7dc5334","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/08ea1c81-85a9-46fc-ad11-9db1d7dc5334/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits alongside Harvey's tenured, full-time global support team, a group already operating at a high bar. The BPO partnership is a deliberate extension of that team, and how well it's run is one of the biggest levers Harvey has for shaping what customers actually experience when they need help. Done right, this partnership pushes our bar of support excellence higher.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The CX Vendor Manager is the single, fully dedicated owner of that partnership. Agent volume is small to start, so this role needs to flex across the full range of vendor management.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary, fully dedicated point of contact for Harvey's BPO partner, owning the relationship end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and implement the framework for this new partnership, then own the vendor's performance against Harvey's core support metrics, CSAT, response time SLAs, QA score, and escalation rate, through a tiered cadence of weekly check-ins and monthly/quarterly business reviews, personally accountable for those outcomes, not just for reporting on them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Harvey's support team to make strategic routing and escalations decisions, what work the vendor handles versus what stays in-house, by tier and channel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and deliver scalable solutions and workflows as volume grows, rather than solving the same problem manually every time it recurs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own workforce management for the partnership end to end: staffing plans, capacity forecasts, and the WFM tooling and process built to support it, starting scrappy and formalizing as volume grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay embedded in the vendor's day-to-day operations so problems in areas such as training, performance, and QA are caught on the floor before they show up in a report.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the quality, enablement, and hiring bar the vendor must staff, train, and manage against, in collaboration with Harvey's enablement team and the vendor's training organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape how AI and automation factor into the vendor's service delivery, and connect what the vendor system strategy is to Harvey's broader support and product vision.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience successfully owning a BPO or outsourced vendor relationship end to end, as the single point of contact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating at Harvey's rapid pace, not a typical enterprise speed. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong CX vendor managers to clear.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has kept a vendor accountable to SLAs and support metrics through a regular operating cadence, backed by independent data rather than just the vendor's own reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on knowledge of Zendesk configured across blended FTE and vendor teams: ticket routing, permissions, and escalation paths that keep both sides working cleanly in the same system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has found a way to get meaningfully more value out of a vendor or partner relationship than the standard playbook would produce, spotting a leverage point (a new capability, a shift like AI, a structural change) that most people in the seat would have missed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record defining quality and enablement standards with a vendor's QA and training functions, pushing back when scoring or training doesn't hold up, and keeping teams aligned on product knowledge, content updates, and quality feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI fluency is required: can speak concretely to how AI and automation are reshaping vendor-delivered support, and has factored that into how a partnership like this should evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">General program management: has stood up processes end to end, SLAs, reporting cadences, staffing approaches, without an existing system or playbook to build from.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knows how to identify the right cross-functional stakeholders early, and builds working relationships with them fast enough to keep a program like this moving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$151,100 - $181,300 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis role sits alongside Harvey's tenured, full-time global support team, a group already operating at a high bar. The BPO partnership is a deliberate extension of that team, and how well it's run is one of the biggest levers Harvey has for shaping what customers actually experience when they need help. Done right, this partnership pushes our bar of support excellence higher.\n\nThe CX Vendor Manager is the single, fully dedicated owner of that partnership. Agent volume is small to start, so this role needs to flex across the full range of vendor management.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as the primary, fully dedicated point of contact for Harvey's BPO partner, owning the relationship end to end.\n\n - Build and implement the framework for this new partnership, then own the vendor's performance against Harvey's core support metrics, CSAT, response time SLAs, QA score, and escalation rate, through a tiered cadence of weekly check-ins and monthly/quarterly business reviews, personally accountable for those outcomes, not just for reporting on them.\n\n - Partner with Harvey's support team to make strategic routing and escalations decisions, what work the vendor handles versus what stays in-house, by tier and channel.\n\n - Design and deliver scalable solutions and workflows as volume grows, rather than solving the same problem manually every time it recurs.\n\n - Own workforce management for the partnership end to end: staffing plans, capacity forecasts, and the WFM tooling and process built to support it, starting scrappy and formalizing as volume grows.\n\n - Stay embedded in the vendor's day-to-day operations so problems in areas such as training, performance, and QA are caught on the floor before they show up in a report.\n\n - Define the quality, enablement, and hiring bar the vendor must staff, train, and manage against, in collaboration with Harvey's enablement team and the vendor's training organization.\n\n - Shape how AI and automation factor into the vendor's service delivery, and connect what the vendor system strategy is to Harvey's broader support and product vision.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven experience successfully owning a BPO or outsourced vendor relationship end to end, as the single point of contact.\n\n - Comfortable operating at Harvey's rapid pace, not a typical enterprise speed. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong CX vendor managers to clear.\n\n - Has kept a vendor accountable to SLAs and support metrics through a regular operating cadence, backed by independent data rather than just the vendor's own reporting.\n\n - Hands-on knowledge of Zendesk configured across blended FTE and vendor teams: ticket routing, permissions, and escalation paths that keep both sides working cleanly in the same system.\n\n - Has found a way to get meaningfully more value out of a vendor or partner relationship than the standard playbook would produce, spotting a leverage point (a new capability, a shift like AI, a structural change) that most people in the seat would have missed.\n\n - Proven track record defining quality and enablement standards with a vendor's QA and training functions, pushing back when scoring or training doesn't hold up, and keeping teams aligned on product knowledge, content updates, and quality feedback.\n\n - AI fluency is required: can speak concretely to how AI and automation are reshaping vendor-delivered support, and has factored that into how a partnership like this should evolve.\n\n - General program management: has stood up processes end to end, SLAs, reporting cadences, staffing approaches, without an existing system or playbook to build from.\n\n - Knows how to identify the right cross-functional stakeholders early, and builds working relationships with them fast enough to keep a program like this moving.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$151,100 - $181,300 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-CG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$151.1K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$151.1K - $181.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a297a5bb-ac87-4bf3-922d-4cd62027eaf4","tierSummary":"$151.1K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"02842a19-f4a9-4ea1-b73d-d130ac5551f4","summary":"$151.1K – $181.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":151100,"maxValue":181300},{"id":"6c138cb0-eb07-4e02-95d6-352443b26aac","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8b519876-93c1-41eb-9c51-ac56d4bafdb7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":151100,"maxValue":181300},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ddba7b8c-d44b-48f5-982f-c4ca651f5ab3","title":"CX Vendor Manager","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T23:45:48.252+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ddba7b8c-d44b-48f5-982f-c4ca651f5ab3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ddba7b8c-d44b-48f5-982f-c4ca651f5ab3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits alongside Harvey's tenured, full-time global support team, a group already operating at a high bar. The BPO partnership is a deliberate extension of that team, and how well it's run is one of the biggest levers Harvey has for shaping what customers actually experience when they need help. Done right, this partnership pushes our bar of support excellence higher.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The CX Vendor Manager is the single, fully dedicated owner of that partnership. Agent volume is small to start, so this role needs to flex across the full range of vendor management.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary, fully dedicated point of contact for Harvey's BPO partner, owning the relationship end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and implement the framework for this new partnership, then own the vendor's performance against Harvey's core support metrics, CSAT, response time SLAs, QA score, and escalation rate, through a tiered cadence of weekly check-ins and monthly/quarterly business reviews, personally accountable for those outcomes, not just for reporting on them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Harvey's support team to make strategic routing and escalations decisions, what work the vendor handles versus what stays in-house, by tier and channel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and deliver scalable solutions and workflows as volume grows, rather than solving the same problem manually every time it recurs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own workforce management for the partnership end to end: staffing plans, capacity forecasts, and the WFM tooling and process built to support it, starting scrappy and formalizing as volume grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay embedded in the vendor's day-to-day operations so problems in areas such as training, performance, and QA are caught on the floor before they show up in a report.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the quality, enablement, and hiring bar the vendor must staff, train, and manage against, in collaboration with Harvey's enablement team and the vendor's training organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape how AI and automation factor into the vendor's service delivery, and connect what the vendor system strategy is to Harvey's broader support and product vision.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience successfully owning a BPO or outsourced vendor relationship end to end, as the single point of contact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating at Harvey's rapid pace, not a typical enterprise speed. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong CX vendor managers to clear.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has kept a vendor accountable to SLAs and support metrics through a regular operating cadence, backed by independent data rather than just the vendor's own reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on knowledge of Zendesk configured across blended FTE and vendor teams: ticket routing, permissions, and escalation paths that keep both sides working cleanly in the same system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has found a way to get meaningfully more value out of a vendor or partner relationship than the standard playbook would produce, spotting a leverage point (a new capability, a shift like AI, a structural change) that most people in the seat would have missed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record defining quality and enablement standards with a vendor's QA and training functions, pushing back when scoring or training doesn't hold up, and keeping teams aligned on product knowledge, content updates, and quality feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI fluency is required: can speak concretely to how AI and automation are reshaping vendor-delivered support, and has factored that into how a partnership like this should evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">General program management: has stood up processes end to end, SLAs, reporting cadences, staffing approaches, without an existing system or playbook to build from.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knows how to identify the right cross-functional stakeholders early, and builds working relationships with them fast enough to keep a program like this moving.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$151,100 - $181,300 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis role sits alongside Harvey's tenured, full-time global support team, a group already operating at a high bar. The BPO partnership is a deliberate extension of that team, and how well it's run is one of the biggest levers Harvey has for shaping what customers actually experience when they need help. Done right, this partnership pushes our bar of support excellence higher.\n\nThe CX Vendor Manager is the single, fully dedicated owner of that partnership. Agent volume is small to start, so this role needs to flex across the full range of vendor management.\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as the primary, fully dedicated point of contact for Harvey's BPO partner, owning the relationship end to end.\n\n - Build and implement the framework for this new partnership, then own the vendor's performance against Harvey's core support metrics, CSAT, response time SLAs, QA score, and escalation rate, through a tiered cadence of weekly check-ins and monthly/quarterly business reviews, personally accountable for those outcomes, not just for reporting on them.\n\n - Partner with Harvey's support team to make strategic routing and escalations decisions, what work the vendor handles versus what stays in-house, by tier and channel.\n\n - Design and deliver scalable solutions and workflows as volume grows, rather than solving the same problem manually every time it recurs.\n\n - Own workforce management for the partnership end to end: staffing plans, capacity forecasts, and the WFM tooling and process built to support it, starting scrappy and formalizing as volume grows.\n\n - Stay embedded in the vendor's day-to-day operations so problems in areas such as training, performance, and QA are caught on the floor before they show up in a report.\n\n - Define the quality, enablement, and hiring bar the vendor must staff, train, and manage against, in collaboration with Harvey's enablement team and the vendor's training organization.\n\n - Shape how AI and automation factor into the vendor's service delivery, and connect what the vendor system strategy is to Harvey's broader support and product vision.\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven experience successfully owning a BPO or outsourced vendor relationship end to end, as the single point of contact.\n\n - Comfortable operating at Harvey's rapid pace, not a typical enterprise speed. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong CX vendor managers to clear.\n\n - Has kept a vendor accountable to SLAs and support metrics through a regular operating cadence, backed by independent data rather than just the vendor's own reporting.\n\n - Hands-on knowledge of Zendesk configured across blended FTE and vendor teams: ticket routing, permissions, and escalation paths that keep both sides working cleanly in the same system.\n\n - Has found a way to get meaningfully more value out of a vendor or partner relationship than the standard playbook would produce, spotting a leverage point (a new capability, a shift like AI, a structural change) that most people in the seat would have missed.\n\n - Proven track record defining quality and enablement standards with a vendor's QA and training functions, pushing back when scoring or training doesn't hold up, and keeping teams aligned on product knowledge, content updates, and quality feedback.\n\n - AI fluency is required: can speak concretely to how AI and automation are reshaping vendor-delivered support, and has factored that into how a partnership like this should evolve.\n\n - General program management: has stood up processes end to end, SLAs, reporting cadences, staffing approaches, without an existing system or playbook to build from.\n\n - Knows how to identify the right cross-functional stakeholders early, and builds working relationships with them fast enough to keep a program like this moving.\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$151,100 - $181,300 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$151.1K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$151.1K - $181.3K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"adb830a6-1139-4544-a3d1-27c2550a66f0","tierSummary":"$151.1K – $181.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"997e5f35-9215-4411-97a6-f999c4a5d340","summary":"$151.1K – $181.3K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":151100,"maxValue":181300},{"id":"7aa2e24c-2d9d-456a-89b0-4c3696747b83","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6f82806a-b45d-457d-9985-de1b97942b33","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":151100,"maxValue":181300},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5e68f8ed-1e00-4bd4-acfd-54405f553a0e","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager, Integrations","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T20:10:15.069+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5e68f8ed-1e00-4bd4-acfd-54405f553a0e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5e68f8ed-1e00-4bd4-acfd-54405f553a0e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Operations Manager, Integrations at Harvey, you'll own the operating system behind our integrations and partner ecosystem — the APIs, MCP servers, and third-party connectors that let law firms and in-house legal teams plug Harvey into the rest of their tech stack. You'll triage and prioritize integration requests, manage the technology and ISV partners building on our platform, run early-access programs for new integrations, and coordinate the launches that bring them to market — all while building the lightweight systems that let the integrations program scale as our partner ecosystem grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a role for someone who's spent real time inside an integrations team or a marketplace/app store business, understands what makes an API- or MCP-based integration actually hold up in production, and knows how to balance partner needs against Harvey's own roadmap and security bar.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner &amp; Integration Request Intake</strong> — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of integration and API/MCP feature requests from customers and partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage partner- and customer-reported integration issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage relationships with technology and ISV partners across the integration lifecycle — onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs &amp; Launches</strong> — Getting new integrations into partners' and customers' hands, then out the door broadly</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and run early-access programs for new integrations and API/MCP capabilities, including partner selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional launches of new integrations by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems That Scale</strong> — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate partner, customer, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations for the integrations roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials — including partner-facing API/MCP documentation — that help internal teams and partners communicate and operate effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring operational challenges in the partner and integration lifecycle, and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes (partner onboarding checklists, certification criteria, listing standards) that let the program scale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Partner or Ecosystem Operations, or a related role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally on a team responsible for integrations, APIs, or a partner platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience working on an integrations team — you've sat inside the function that builds, ships, and supports third-party connections, not just consumed them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of APIs and MCP (Model Context Protocol) — comfortable in conversations about auth, rate limits, schemas, and what separates a reliable integration from a fragile one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience from an app store, marketplace, or partner ecosystem business — managing listings, partner certification, marketplace policies, or developer relations — so you understand both sides of a two-sided platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing external technology or ISV partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication — you can turn partner and customer feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that both internal and partner teams actually use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, Partner/BD and GTM without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Operations Manager, Integrations at Harvey, you'll own the operating system behind our integrations and partner ecosystem — the APIs, MCP servers, and third-party connectors that let law firms and in-house legal teams plug Harvey into the rest of their tech stack. You'll triage and prioritize integration requests, manage the technology and ISV partners building on our platform, run early-access programs for new integrations, and coordinate the launches that bring them to market — all while building the lightweight systems that let the integrations program scale as our partner ecosystem grows.\n\nThis is a role for someone who's spent real time inside an integrations team or a marketplace/app store business, understands what makes an API- or MCP-based integration actually hold up in production, and knows how to balance partner needs against Harvey's own roadmap and security bar.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nPartner & Integration Request Intake — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast\n\n - Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of integration and API/MCP feature requests from customers and partners.\n\n - Triage partner- and customer-reported integration issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.\n\n - Manage relationships with technology and ISV partners across the integration lifecycle — onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.\n\nPrograms & Launches — Getting new integrations into partners' and customers' hands, then out the door broadly\n\n - Plan and run early-access programs for new integrations and API/MCP capabilities, including partner selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional launches of new integrations by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.\n\nSystems That Scale — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process\n\n - Translate partner, customer, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations for the integrations roadmap.\n\n - Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials — including partner-facing API/MCP documentation — that help internal teams and partners communicate and operate effectively.\n\n - Identify recurring operational challenges in the partner and integration lifecycle, and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes (partner onboarding checklists, certification criteria, listing standards) that let the program scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Partner or Ecosystem Operations, or a related role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally on a team responsible for integrations, APIs, or a partner platform.\n\n - Direct experience working on an integrations team — you've sat inside the function that builds, ships, and supports third-party connections, not just consumed them.\n\n - Working knowledge of APIs and MCP (Model Context Protocol) — comfortable in conversations about auth, rate limits, schemas, and what separates a reliable integration from a fragile one.\n\n - Experience from an app store, marketplace, or partner ecosystem business — managing listings, partner certification, marketplace policies, or developer relations — so you understand both sides of a two-sided platform.\n\n - Experience managing external technology or ISV partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.\n\n - Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.\n\n - Strong written communication — you can turn partner and customer feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that both internal and partner teams actually use.\n\n - Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, Partner/BD and GTM without direct authority.\n\n - A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"34b9c552-a49f-419f-8237-68fa8c0791c6","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a32289be-cd21-40d4-acd8-fed394bd8449","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"id":"35d8e041-ad26-4af3-978b-ba4041df1cd3","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"05e1c389-5f23-4102-9357-127460195f89","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"514b90b4-5b4c-4e64-bc9a-2ab2ca6cf456","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager, Integrations","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T20:11:01.172+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/514b90b4-5b4c-4e64-bc9a-2ab2ca6cf456","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/514b90b4-5b4c-4e64-bc9a-2ab2ca6cf456/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Operations Manager, Integrations at Harvey, you'll own the operating system behind our integrations and partner ecosystem — the APIs, MCP servers, and third-party connectors that let law firms and in-house legal teams plug Harvey into the rest of their tech stack. You'll triage and prioritize integration requests, manage the technology and ISV partners building on our platform, run early-access programs for new integrations, and coordinate the launches that bring them to market — all while building the lightweight systems that let the integrations program scale as our partner ecosystem grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a role for someone who's spent real time inside an integrations team or a marketplace/app store business, understands what makes an API- or MCP-based integration actually hold up in production, and knows how to balance partner needs against Harvey's own roadmap and security bar.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner &amp; Integration Request Intake</strong> — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of integration and API/MCP feature requests from customers and partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage partner- and customer-reported integration issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage relationships with technology and ISV partners across the integration lifecycle — onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs &amp; Launches</strong> — Getting new integrations into partners' and customers' hands, then out the door broadly</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and run early-access programs for new integrations and API/MCP capabilities, including partner selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional launches of new integrations by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems That Scale</strong> — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate partner, customer, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations for the integrations roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials — including partner-facing API/MCP documentation — that help internal teams and partners communicate and operate effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring operational challenges in the partner and integration lifecycle, and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes (partner onboarding checklists, certification criteria, listing standards) that let the program scale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Partner or Ecosystem Operations, or a related role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally on a team responsible for integrations, APIs, or a partner platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience working on an integrations team — you've sat inside the function that builds, ships, and supports third-party connections, not just consumed them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of APIs and MCP (Model Context Protocol) — comfortable in conversations about auth, rate limits, schemas, and what separates a reliable integration from a fragile one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience from an app store, marketplace, or partner ecosystem business — managing listings, partner certification, marketplace policies, or developer relations — so you understand both sides of a two-sided platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing external technology or ISV partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication — you can turn partner and customer feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that both internal and partner teams actually use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, Partner/BD and GTM without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Product Operations Manager, Integrations at Harvey, you'll own the operating system behind our integrations and partner ecosystem — the APIs, MCP servers, and third-party connectors that let law firms and in-house legal teams plug Harvey into the rest of their tech stack. You'll triage and prioritize integration requests, manage the technology and ISV partners building on our platform, run early-access programs for new integrations, and coordinate the launches that bring them to market — all while building the lightweight systems that let the integrations program scale as our partner ecosystem grows.\n\nThis is a role for someone who's spent real time inside an integrations team or a marketplace/app store business, understands what makes an API- or MCP-based integration actually hold up in production, and knows how to balance partner needs against Harvey's own roadmap and security bar.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nPartner & Integration Request Intake — Making sure the right signal reaches the right team, fast\n\n - Own the intake, triage, and prioritization of integration and API/MCP feature requests from customers and partners.\n\n - Triage partner- and customer-reported integration issues, assess severity and impact, coordinate resolution across the appropriate teams, and ensure timely communication.\n\n - Manage relationships with technology and ISV partners across the integration lifecycle — onboarding, ongoing operations, issue resolution, and delivery quality.\n\nPrograms & Launches — Getting new integrations into partners' and customers' hands, then out the door broadly\n\n - Plan and run early-access programs for new integrations and API/MCP capabilities, including partner selection, onboarding, feedback collection, usage analysis, and launch recommendations.\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional launches of new integrations by tracking dependencies, validating operational readiness, surfacing risks, and keeping high-priority initiatives on track.\n\nSystems That Scale — Turning feedback and recurring friction into durable process\n\n - Translate partner, customer, and internal feedback into clear requirements, prioritized workstreams, and actionable recommendations for the integrations roadmap.\n\n - Create and maintain documentation, playbooks, and enablement materials — including partner-facing API/MCP documentation — that help internal teams and partners communicate and operate effectively.\n\n - Identify recurring operational challenges in the partner and integration lifecycle, and implement lightweight systems, automation, and processes (partner onboarding checklists, certification criteria, listing standards) that let the program scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3-5+ years in Product Operations, Program Management, Partner or Ecosystem Operations, or a related role at a high-growth tech or SaaS company — ideally on a team responsible for integrations, APIs, or a partner platform.\n\n - Direct experience working on an integrations team — you've sat inside the function that builds, ships, and supports third-party connections, not just consumed them.\n\n - Working knowledge of APIs and MCP (Model Context Protocol) — comfortable in conversations about auth, rate limits, schemas, and what separates a reliable integration from a fragile one.\n\n - Experience from an app store, marketplace, or partner ecosystem business — managing listings, partner certification, marketplace policies, or developer relations — so you understand both sides of a two-sided platform.\n\n - Experience managing external technology or ISV partner relationships, including onboarding and ongoing delivery quality.\n\n - Hands-on experience running early-access or beta programs and coordinating launches in a fast-moving product environment.\n\n - Strong written communication — you can turn partner and customer feedback into clear requirements, playbooks, and documentation that both internal and partner teams actually use.\n\n - Proven ability to drive cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, Partner/BD and GTM without direct authority.\n\n - A bias toward lightweight systems over heavy processes — you'd rather ship a simple fix that scales than a perfect framework nobody uses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-CD1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7f82d555-e7c2-4efd-abd0-4c535287ed01","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4d714cc6-b4da-4369-8d7e-c9e8d00ecdab","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"id":"24e4c929-6244-4105-898a-c99394060b36","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"936e1718-0fb1-4a3b-ace9-2e91bfd74a19","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f3627435-2e0a-4c6b-bf66-967b52231a8c","title":"Mid-Market Account Executive, Singapore","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T16:28:16.145+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f3627435-2e0a-4c6b-bf66-967b52231a8c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f3627435-2e0a-4c6b-bf66-967b52231a8c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Account Executive, Mid Market joins Harvey's expanding APAC sales organization to bring AI-powered solutions to mid-sized law firms and professional services clients across Singapore and the broader Southeast Asian market. This role sits within the Mid Market Sales team, whose mission is to accelerate adoption of Harvey's platform among firms that are primed for transformation but underserved by legacy legal technology. The AE will own the full sales cycle — from prospecting and discovery through contracting and renewal — serving as the primary commercial relationship for their named accounts. They will partner closely with Solutions Architects, Legal Engineers, and Customer Success to tailor Harvey's offering to the nuances of the APAC legal market. It is a rare opportunity to shape Harvey's mid-market presence in a high-growth region at the intersection of AI and legal services.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a named account list across Singapore and Southeast Asia, managing inbound leads and driving outbound prospecting to high-potential mid-market firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from initial outreach through contracting, onboarding, expansion, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed quarterly and annual revenue targets and key sales performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers — including Managing Partners, General Counsel, and Heads of Innovation — understanding their challenges and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high-velocity, tailored client evaluations including product demonstrations and presentations that showcase Harvey's AI capabilities to prospects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal Engineering, and Customer Success to shape solutions for APAC-specific client needs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record selling complex B2B SaaS solutions with a consultative, value-based methodology; experience in mid-market or enterprise segments preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast performance metrics, and maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at leading multi-threaded sales with stakeholders ranging from senior executives to day-to-day product users, with strong ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for AI and its potential applications in knowledge work, with genuine interest in the legal profession.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Energized by contributing to team development, refining sales processes, and building the playbook for a new regional market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in or adjacent to the legal industry or professional services in APAC is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Please find the Applicant Privacy for this region </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Account Executive, Mid Market joins Harvey's expanding APAC sales organization to bring AI-powered solutions to mid-sized law firms and professional services clients across Singapore and the broader Southeast Asian market. This role sits within the Mid Market Sales team, whose mission is to accelerate adoption of Harvey's platform among firms that are primed for transformation but underserved by legacy legal technology. The AE will own the full sales cycle — from prospecting and discovery through contracting and renewal — serving as the primary commercial relationship for their named accounts. They will partner closely with Solutions Architects, Legal Engineers, and Customer Success to tailor Harvey's offering to the nuances of the APAC legal market. It is a rare opportunity to shape Harvey's mid-market presence in a high-growth region at the intersection of AI and legal services.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own a named account list across Singapore and Southeast Asia, managing inbound leads and driving outbound prospecting to high-potential mid-market firms.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from initial outreach through contracting, onboarding, expansion, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed quarterly and annual revenue targets and key sales performance metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers — including Managing Partners, General Counsel, and Heads of Innovation — understanding their challenges and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high-velocity, tailored client evaluations including product demonstrations and presentations that showcase Harvey's AI capabilities to prospects.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Legal Engineering, and Customer Success to shape solutions for APAC-specific client needs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record selling complex B2B SaaS solutions with a consultative, value-based methodology; experience in mid-market or enterprise segments preferred.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast performance metrics, and maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Skilled at leading multi-threaded sales with stakeholders ranging from senior executives to day-to-day product users, with strong ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for AI and its potential applications in knowledge work, with genuine interest in the legal profession.\n\n - Energized by contributing to team development, refining sales processes, and building the playbook for a new regional market.\n\n - Experience working in or adjacent to the legal industry or professional services in APAC is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nPLEASE FIND THE APPLICANT PRIVACY FOR THIS REGION HERE https://www.harvey.ai/legal/singapore-applicant-privacy-notice.\n\n\n\n#LI-SG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"dc967ec2-5fd8-4a92-9c81-513265cec47e","title":"Senior Product Operations Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T23:14:18.607+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dc967ec2-5fd8-4a92-9c81-513265cec47e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/dc967ec2-5fd8-4a92-9c81-513265cec47e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Product Operations Manager at Harvey, you will be the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams — turning strategy into execution across our entire product lifecycle. You'll build and scale the operating systems that help our product teams make better decisions, ship with confidence, and drive measurable impact for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work as an extension of product leadership, balancing hands-on execution with strategic initiatives. This is a role for someone who builds from 0 to 1, thrives in ambiguity, and creates structure where none exists.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inputs to Product Teams</strong> — Ensuring teams have the information they need to make great decisions</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain Voice of Customer systems that synthesize feedback from law firm partners, in-house clients, CSMs, and sales into actionable product signals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish rigorous mechanisms for measuring product success and user impact, including analytics dashboards, KPIs, and clear hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create high-leverage engagement points with customers and partners throughout the product lifecycle — from alpha through post-GA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Streamline key decision points across teams, reducing friction and improving prioritization quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ops of the Product Org</strong> — Creating the operating systems that enable product teams to thrive</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and improve core product development processes, tooling, and team rituals (planning cycles, monthly reviews, roadmap prioritization, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reliable run-of-business systems that scale as Harvey grows — launch calendars, intake frameworks, RACI structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive cross-functional alignment between Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate roadmap planning by coordinating stakeholder inputs and maintaining transparency across the org</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Outputs from Product Teams</strong> — Amplifying product impact by connecting what we build to those who need it</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run Early Access Programs and alpha testing programs that validate product-market fit and surface refinement signals before broad release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own launch coordination end-to-end — ensuring timely, high-confidence rollouts with clear success metrics and post-launch monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain cross-team roadmap visibility that keeps GTM, Legal, and leadership aligned on what's shipping and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make it clear across Harvey what Product is building, how it's progressing, and what's coming nextd optimize operational workflows to ensure agility and scalability as the company grows.</p></li></ul></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in Product Operations, Product Management, or a closely related operational role at a high growth tech or SaaS company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've built processes and programs from scratch and scaled them thoughtfully — not just inherited and maintained them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with AI-native products, ideally in a domain where model quality and output reliability are central to the user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to translate complex qualitative and quantitative data — usage metrics, feedback themes, retention signals — into clear recommendations and roadmap inputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to drive alignment across Product, GTM, and Engineering without direct authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with launch coordination, EAPs, or customer feedback loops in a fast-moving product environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're a natural bridge builder: fluent in strategy, comfortable in the weeds, and skilled at creating clarity where none exists. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down — it's where you do your best work.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> $155,400 - $233,200 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CD1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Senior Product Operations Manager at Harvey, you will be the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams — turning strategy into execution across our entire product lifecycle. You'll build and scale the operating systems that help our product teams make better decisions, ship with confidence, and drive measurable impact for law firms and in-house legal teams pushing the frontier of AI adoption.\n\nYou'll work as an extension of product leadership, balancing hands-on execution with strategic initiatives. This is a role for someone who builds from 0 to 1, thrives in ambiguity, and creates structure where none exists.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Inputs to Product Teams — Ensuring teams have the information they need to make great decisions\n   \n   - Build and maintain Voice of Customer systems that synthesize feedback from law firm partners, in-house clients, CSMs, and sales into actionable product signals\n   \n   - Establish rigorous mechanisms for measuring product success and user impact, including analytics dashboards, KPIs, and clear hypotheses\n   \n   - Create high-leverage engagement points with customers and partners throughout the product lifecycle — from alpha through post-GA\n   \n   - Streamline key decision points across teams, reducing friction and improving prioritization quality\n   \n   Ops of the Product Org — Creating the operating systems that enable product teams to thrive\n   \n   - Own and improve core product development processes, tooling, and team rituals (planning cycles, monthly reviews, roadmap prioritization, etc.)\n   \n   - Build reliable run-of-business systems that scale as Harvey grows — launch calendars, intake frameworks, RACI structures\n   \n   - Drive cross-functional alignment between Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success\n   \n   - Facilitate roadmap planning by coordinating stakeholder inputs and maintaining transparency across the org\n   \n   Outputs from Product Teams — Amplifying product impact by connecting what we build to those who need it\n   \n   - Design and run Early Access Programs and alpha testing programs that validate product-market fit and surface refinement signals before broad release\n   \n   - Own launch coordination end-to-end — ensuring timely, high-confidence rollouts with clear success metrics and post-launch monitoring\n   \n   - Maintain cross-team roadmap visibility that keeps GTM, Legal, and leadership aligned on what's shipping and why\n   \n   - Make it clear across Harvey what Product is building, how it's progressing, and what's coming nextd optimize operational workflows to ensure agility and scalability as the company grows.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years in Product Operations, Product Management, or a closely related operational role at a high growth tech or SaaS company\n\n - You've built processes and programs from scratch and scaled them thoughtfully — not just inherited and maintained them\n\n - Experience working with AI-native products, ideally in a domain where model quality and output reliability are central to the user experience\n\n - Strong ability to translate complex qualitative and quantitative data — usage metrics, feedback themes, retention signals — into clear recommendations and roadmap inputs\n\n - Proven ability to drive alignment across Product, GTM, and Engineering without direct authority\n\n - Hands-on experience with launch coordination, EAPs, or customer feedback loops in a fast-moving product environment\n\n - You're a natural bridge builder: fluent in strategy, comfortable in the weeds, and skilled at creating clarity where none exists. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down — it's where you do your best work.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n $155,400 - $233,200 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n \n\n#LI-CD1\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.4K - $233.2K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"635199c5-7d53-4271-b1bb-5e3db7af5b43","tierSummary":"$155.4K – $233.2K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d21e6bed-e678-42aa-924f-c89f064f1be9","summary":"$155.4K – $233.2K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"id":"887f9aac-1a3b-4a78-8033-931c99c38188","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6430c054-a3f0-454f-8867-4d49f796ef66","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155400,"maxValue":233200},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ba1dd03d-f8fa-4097-8aa1-757fe17b2166","title":"Account Executive, Mid-Market - ANZ","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sydney","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T08:06:40.710+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Australia","addressLocality":"Sydney"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ba1dd03d-f8fa-4097-8aa1-757fe17b2166","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/ba1dd03d-f8fa-4097-8aa1-757fe17b2166/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Mid Market Account Executive joins Harvey's growing ANZ sales team to drive adoption of AI-powered solutions among mid-sized law firms and professional services organizations across Australia and New Zealand. The team's mission is to establish and scale Harvey's commercial presence in the ANZ market, building durable relationships with firms navigating the integration of AI into legal practice. This role owns the full sales cycle—from prospecting through contracting and renewal—for a named book of mid-market accounts across the region. The Account Executive partners directly with local and global cross-functional teams, including legal engineering, customer success, and product, to tailor Harvey's platform to the needs of ANZ clients. It is a rare opportunity to shape an emerging market for a category-defining legal AI platform at a company moving with exceptional speed and ambition.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a named account list of mid-market prospects and clients across ANZ, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads and proactively outbounding to high-potential accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, expansion, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high-velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI platform to prospects and clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, engineering, legal engineering, and customer success teams to shape Harvey's solutions for ANZ market requirements and develop go-to-market playbooks that enable regional scaling.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from senior partners and executives to day-to-day product users—especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in legal and professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player who collaborates effectively across internal functions and is energized by contributing to the development of sales processes, culture, and go-to-market playbooks in an emerging market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently; experience working in or adjacent to the legal industry is a plus but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Information</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family &amp; Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement &amp; Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wellness &amp; Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-EP3</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Mid Market Account Executive joins Harvey's growing ANZ sales team to drive adoption of AI-powered solutions among mid-sized law firms and professional services organizations across Australia and New Zealand. The team's mission is to establish and scale Harvey's commercial presence in the ANZ market, building durable relationships with firms navigating the integration of AI into legal practice. This role owns the full sales cycle—from prospecting through contracting and renewal—for a named book of mid-market accounts across the region. The Account Executive partners directly with local and global cross-functional teams, including legal engineering, customer success, and product, to tailor Harvey's platform to the needs of ANZ clients. It is a rare opportunity to shape an emerging market for a category-defining legal AI platform at a company moving with exceptional speed and ambition.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own a named account list of mid-market prospects and clients across ANZ, prioritizing and cultivating inbound leads and proactively outbounding to high-potential accounts.\n\n - Manage the full customer lifecycle from prospecting to contracting, onboarding, expansion, and renewals.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and other key sales performance metrics.\n\n - Build strong relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders, understanding their pain points and aligning Harvey's solutions with their needs.\n\n - Conduct high-velocity, tailored client evaluations, including product demonstrations and presentations, showcasing the power of Harvey's AI platform to prospects and clients.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, engineering, legal engineering, and customer success teams to shape Harvey's solutions for ANZ market requirements and develop go-to-market playbooks that enable regional scaling.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Proven track record of selling complex software solutions, with the ability to successfully execute on a consultative, solutions-oriented, value-based selling methodology.\n\n - Excited about prospecting, and capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish.\n\n - Ability to independently manage a pipeline, accurately forecast key sales performance metrics, and consistently maintain CRM hygiene.\n\n - Ability to lead a complex, multi-threaded sale with stakeholders ranging from senior partners and executives to day-to-day product users—especially the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated passion for Harvey's mission and strong understanding of AI and its potential applications in legal and professional services.\n\n - Team player who collaborates effectively across internal functions and is energized by contributing to the development of sales processes, culture, and go-to-market playbooks in an emerging market.\n\n - Interest in the legal profession and helping lawyers do their jobs better and more efficiently; experience working in or adjacent to the legal industry is a plus but not required.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n - Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home\n\n - Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.\n\n - Family & Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.\n\n - Retirement & Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.\n\n - Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.\n\n - Wellness & Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.\n\n - Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.\n\n - Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.\n\n - Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-EP3\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5d8a05b8-d203-4e69-9e0c-8692433f3bc1","title":"Contracts Manager, EMEA","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T09:05:58.467+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5d8a05b8-d203-4e69-9e0c-8692433f3bc1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5d8a05b8-d203-4e69-9e0c-8692433f3bc1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Contracts Manager to join our legal team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will interface with cross-functional teams including our procurement, go-to-market, deal operations and marketing teams to ensure fast and efficient execution of agreements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will also focus on the efficient operation of the commercial team (including its contracts management system) and Harvey’s legal department.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done. Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers. This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations. And this role will put you in the center of all of this.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">More specifically, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate NDAs, Master Service Agreements, Statements of Work, Marketing and Sponsorship Agreements, Staffing Agreements, and other Procurement Agreements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain contract templates and playbooks, refine approval workflows and intake processes, and leverage Harvey to continuously improve and scale the legal team's contracting operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flag non-standard terms and issues affecting product, privacy, and regulatory compliance, escalate to legal counsel as needed, negotiate Data Processing Agreements, and ensure contracts comply with internal policies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training and develop resources in support of our go-to-market and other cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Dublin, IE.  We use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week.</p><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of in-house experience, ideally supporting a SaaS or tech company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with Procurement, Master Services Agreements, NDAs, SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing commercial agreements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with contracts management systems and related systems (such as or similar to Ironclad, Zip and Docusign)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI experience welcomed but not required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe are looking for a Contracts Manager to join our legal team.\n\n \n\n - You will interface with cross-functional teams including our procurement, go-to-market, deal operations and marketing teams to ensure fast and efficient execution of agreements.\n\n - You will also focus on the efficient operation of the commercial team (including its contracts management system) and Harvey’s legal department.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nGenerative AI has the power to greatly change the world and directly impact how things get done. Harvey is at the forefront of this change, and our mission is to make generative AI actionable and useful for our customers. This is a fast moving environment (we are a start-up!) that is serving some of the world’s most renowned law firms and professional organizations. And this role will put you in the center of all of this.\n\nMore specifically, you will:\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate NDAs, Master Service Agreements, Statements of Work, Marketing and Sponsorship Agreements, Staffing Agreements, and other Procurement Agreements\n\n - Develop and maintain contract templates and playbooks, refine approval workflows and intake processes, and leverage Harvey to continuously improve and scale the legal team's contracting operations\n\n - Flag non-standard terms and issues affecting product, privacy, and regulatory compliance, escalate to legal counsel as needed, negotiate Data Processing Agreements, and ensure contracts comply with internal policies\n\n - Provide training and develop resources in support of our go-to-market and other cross-functional teams\n\nWe are a small, but growing company, and one of the best things about working in such an environment is that there is lots of opportunity to pick up other aspects of the legal work that supports our company.  While the principal job will be as described above, there will be ample opportunities to broaden your wheelhouse here at Harvey!\n\nThis role is based in Dublin, IE.  We use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Bachelors degree\n\n - 4+ years of in-house experience, ideally supporting a SaaS or tech company\n\n - Hands-on experience with Procurement, Master Services Agreements, NDAs, SaaS, technology, and/or IP licensing commercial agreements\n\n - Experience with contracts management systems and related systems (such as or similar to Ironclad, Zip and Docusign)\n\n - Exceptional project management skills\n\n - AI experience welcomed but not required\n\n - Ability to think creatively, function independently and work proactively in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Team-focused and collaborative work style; willingness to build expertise and solve new challenges in an evolving practice\n\n - Hyper-responsive and service-oriented attitude, and a love for solving hard problems with a small tight-knit team\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3feed577-6157-4fb4-b416-d4f493e1eb5c","title":"Senior Brand Designer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T20:17:11.715+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3feed577-6157-4fb4-b416-d4f493e1eb5c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3feed577-6157-4fb4-b416-d4f493e1eb5c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Brand Designer crafts how Harvey shows up across every touchpoint, translating a complex legal AI product into clear, compelling stories and systems. They sit on the Brand &amp; Creative team, partnering closely with growth marketing, product marketing, content marketing and creative operations to ship high-impact work that’s cohesive and scalable. This role drives the evolution of Harvey’s brand system and campaigns so that every asset reinforces our position as the category-defining legal AI platform. They make key calls on creative direction within their projects and are a trusted collaborator to cross-functional partners. It’s a chance to help define a fast-moving brand from the inside, with direct line-of-sight to the impact of your work.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end creative for priority initiatives — from brief to concept to launch — across social, product marketing, sales enablement and external events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve and extend Harvey’s brand system (visual language, layout, motion, and templates) so it’s recognizable, flexible, and easy for others to use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with PMM, marketing, and product partners to clarify goals, shape briefs, and turn complex ideas into simple, high-impact narratives and visuals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work hand-in-hand with creative operations and producers to scope projects, set milestones, and keep work moving smoothly from kickoff through delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Give and receive clear, constructive feedback; help raise the quality bar for the broader creative team through critique, documentation, and mentorship of other designers.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Significant experience in brand or marketing design roles (in-house or agency), including owning complex, multi-channel projects end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio that demonstrates strong visual craft, systems thinking, and clear storytelling across campaigns, product marketing, and/or B2B tech or SaaS work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to collaborate with PMM, marketing, and other cross-functional partners, turning ambiguous briefs into focused creative directions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working within and evolving a brand system — knowing when to extend patterns and when to introduce new ones thoughtfully.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills: you can explain the “why” behind your work, incorporate feedback, and advocate for the brand and audience effectively.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,600 - $214,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Brand Designer crafts how Harvey shows up across every touchpoint, translating a complex legal AI product into clear, compelling stories and systems. They sit on the Brand & Creative team, partnering closely with growth marketing, product marketing, content marketing and creative operations to ship high-impact work that’s cohesive and scalable. This role drives the evolution of Harvey’s brand system and campaigns so that every asset reinforces our position as the category-defining legal AI platform. They make key calls on creative direction within their projects and are a trusted collaborator to cross-functional partners. It’s a chance to help define a fast-moving brand from the inside, with direct line-of-sight to the impact of your work.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end creative for priority initiatives — from brief to concept to launch — across social, product marketing, sales enablement and external events.\n\n - Evolve and extend Harvey’s brand system (visual language, layout, motion, and templates) so it’s recognizable, flexible, and easy for others to use.\n\n - Collaborate closely with PMM, marketing, and product partners to clarify goals, shape briefs, and turn complex ideas into simple, high-impact narratives and visuals.\n\n - Work hand-in-hand with creative operations and producers to scope projects, set milestones, and keep work moving smoothly from kickoff through delivery.\n\n - Give and receive clear, constructive feedback; help raise the quality bar for the broader creative team through critique, documentation, and mentorship of other designers.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Significant experience in brand or marketing design roles (in-house or agency), including owning complex, multi-channel projects end-to-end.\n\n - A portfolio that demonstrates strong visual craft, systems thinking, and clear storytelling across campaigns, product marketing, and/or B2B tech or SaaS work.\n\n - Proven ability to collaborate with PMM, marketing, and other cross-functional partners, turning ambiguous briefs into focused creative directions.\n\n - Comfort working within and evolving a brand system — knowing when to extend patterns and when to introduce new ones thoughtfully.\n\n - Strong communication skills: you can explain the “why” behind your work, incorporate feedback, and advocate for the brand and audience effectively.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,600 - $214,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-LR1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.6K – $214K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.6K - $214K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b4bd208b-acf3-47ee-98c6-e4f4b9b7ddd4","tierSummary":"$155.6K – $214K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5b55c365-8677-4722-aefc-7a68cd33f4e3","summary":"$155.6K – $214K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155600,"maxValue":214000},{"id":"39d7d987-ab7e-4c89-89e3-9fbbe7b67f40","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b8a165e4-a7a2-4e74-8a3e-1c240c388a9d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155600,"maxValue":214000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"b6cfee1e-67c7-420e-a3fc-24677eda6d2c","title":"Senior Brand Designer","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T20:17:19.948+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b6cfee1e-67c7-420e-a3fc-24677eda6d2c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b6cfee1e-67c7-420e-a3fc-24677eda6d2c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Brand Designer crafts how Harvey shows up across every touchpoint, translating a complex legal AI product into clear, compelling stories and systems. They sit on the Brand &amp; Creative team, partnering closely with growth marketing, product marketing, content marketing and creative operations to ship high-impact work that’s cohesive and scalable. This role drives the evolution of Harvey’s brand system and campaigns so that every asset reinforces our position as the category-defining legal AI platform. They make key calls on creative direction within their projects and are a trusted collaborator to cross-functional partners. It’s a chance to help define a fast-moving brand from the inside, with direct line-of-sight to the impact of your work.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end creative for priority initiatives — from brief to concept to launch — across social, product marketing, sales enablement and external events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve and extend Harvey’s brand system (visual language, layout, motion, and templates) so it’s recognizable, flexible, and easy for others to use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with PMM, marketing, and product partners to clarify goals, shape briefs, and turn complex ideas into simple, high-impact narratives and visuals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work hand-in-hand with creative operations and producers to scope projects, set milestones, and keep work moving smoothly from kickoff through delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Give and receive clear, constructive feedback; help raise the quality bar for the broader creative team through critique, documentation, and mentorship of other designers.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Significant experience in brand or marketing design roles (in-house or agency), including owning complex, multi-channel projects end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A portfolio that demonstrates strong visual craft, systems thinking, and clear storytelling across campaigns, product marketing, and/or B2B tech or SaaS work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to collaborate with PMM, marketing, and other cross-functional partners, turning ambiguous briefs into focused creative directions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working within and evolving a brand system — knowing when to extend patterns and when to introduce new ones thoughtfully.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills: you can explain the “why” behind your work, incorporate feedback, and advocate for the brand and audience effectively.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$155,600 - $214,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Brand Designer crafts how Harvey shows up across every touchpoint, translating a complex legal AI product into clear, compelling stories and systems. They sit on the Brand & Creative team, partnering closely with growth marketing, product marketing, content marketing and creative operations to ship high-impact work that’s cohesive and scalable. This role drives the evolution of Harvey’s brand system and campaigns so that every asset reinforces our position as the category-defining legal AI platform. They make key calls on creative direction within their projects and are a trusted collaborator to cross-functional partners. It’s a chance to help define a fast-moving brand from the inside, with direct line-of-sight to the impact of your work.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end creative for priority initiatives — from brief to concept to launch — across social, product marketing, sales enablement and external events.\n\n - Evolve and extend Harvey’s brand system (visual language, layout, motion, and templates) so it’s recognizable, flexible, and easy for others to use.\n\n - Collaborate closely with PMM, marketing, and product partners to clarify goals, shape briefs, and turn complex ideas into simple, high-impact narratives and visuals.\n\n - Work hand-in-hand with creative operations and producers to scope projects, set milestones, and keep work moving smoothly from kickoff through delivery.\n\n - Give and receive clear, constructive feedback; help raise the quality bar for the broader creative team through critique, documentation, and mentorship of other designers.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Significant experience in brand or marketing design roles (in-house or agency), including owning complex, multi-channel projects end-to-end.\n\n - A portfolio that demonstrates strong visual craft, systems thinking, and clear storytelling across campaigns, product marketing, and/or B2B tech or SaaS work.\n\n - Proven ability to collaborate with PMM, marketing, and other cross-functional partners, turning ambiguous briefs into focused creative directions.\n\n - Comfort working within and evolving a brand system — knowing when to extend patterns and when to introduce new ones thoughtfully.\n\n - Strong communication skills: you can explain the “why” behind your work, incorporate feedback, and advocate for the brand and audience effectively.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$155,600 - $214,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-LR1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155.6K – $214K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155.6K - $214K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b4bd208b-acf3-47ee-98c6-e4f4b9b7ddd4","tierSummary":"$155.6K – $214K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5b55c365-8677-4722-aefc-7a68cd33f4e3","summary":"$155.6K – $214K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155600,"maxValue":214000},{"id":"39d7d987-ab7e-4c89-89e3-9fbbe7b67f40","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b8a165e4-a7a2-4e74-8a3e-1c240c388a9d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155600,"maxValue":214000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1b2c2891-8152-4cc5-8bd1-f2cf0a552532","title":"Sales Manager, Public Sector","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:01:52.660+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1b2c2891-8152-4cc5-8bd1-f2cf0a552532","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/1b2c2891-8152-4cc5-8bd1-f2cf0a552532/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Sales Manager, Public Sector leads our go-to-market into United States federal, state, and local government legal organizations. This is a build role. You will recruit and lead a team of Enterprise Account Executives covering federal agencies and state and local government, and you will own the number for the segment — quota, pipeline, forecast, and execution. Harvey already has active engagements at government agencies; your job is to turn early momentum into a durable, repeatable government sales motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recruit, coach, and lead a team of Enterprise AEs across Federal and State &amp; Local, including sourcing and closing the founding hires.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own quota attainment, pipeline generation, and forecast accuracy for the Public Sector segment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the public sector sales playbook from zero — qualification criteria, procurement path selection, security review sequencing, and fiscal-year timing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Carry a small number of strategic accounts personally through the first two quarters while the team ramps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Head of Public Sector on channel strategy and on FedRAMP and StateRAMP/GovRAMP positioning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Security and Compliance, Legal, and Finance to move agency security reviews, authorizations, and contract vehicles forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Harvey across the government legal and gov-tech community in Washington and in-market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel as required, including agency sites and Harvey offices.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8–10+ years of technology sales experience, including 3–5+ years managing public sector sellers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personally carried and hit a public sector quota as an individual contributor before moving into management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience standing up a public sector sales team, region, or territory from scratch — not advising or supporting one that already existed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in government procurement: GSA schedules, GWACs, OTAs, sole-source and exemption pathways, FAR fundamentals, and state tender and cooperative purchasing processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with long, non-linear cycles and fiscal-year budget dynamics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lead complex, multi-threaded sales spanning agency general counsel, CIO and CISO organizations, contracting officers, and end-user attorneys.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine conviction about the mission and about equipping public servants with frontier technology.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships across federal agency legal, CIO, or CISO organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal departments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing a government reseller or channel relationship.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$400,000 - $440,000 USD OTE 50/50</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD2</p><h3></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Sales Manager, Public Sector leads our go-to-market into United States federal, state, and local government legal organizations. This is a build role. You will recruit and lead a team of Enterprise Account Executives covering federal agencies and state and local government, and you will own the number for the segment — quota, pipeline, forecast, and execution. Harvey already has active engagements at government agencies; your job is to turn early momentum into a durable, repeatable government sales motion.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Recruit, coach, and lead a team of Enterprise AEs across Federal and State & Local, including sourcing and closing the founding hires.\n\n - Own quota attainment, pipeline generation, and forecast accuracy for the Public Sector segment.\n\n - Build the public sector sales playbook from zero — qualification criteria, procurement path selection, security review sequencing, and fiscal-year timing.\n\n - Carry a small number of strategic accounts personally through the first two quarters while the team ramps.\n\n - Partner with the Head of Public Sector on channel strategy and on FedRAMP and StateRAMP/GovRAMP positioning.\n\n - Work cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Security and Compliance, Legal, and Finance to move agency security reviews, authorizations, and contract vehicles forward.\n\n - Represent Harvey across the government legal and gov-tech community in Washington and in-market.\n\n - Travel as required, including agency sites and Harvey offices.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8–10+ years of technology sales experience, including 3–5+ years managing public sector sellers.\n\n - Personally carried and hit a public sector quota as an individual contributor before moving into management.\n\n - Experience standing up a public sector sales team, region, or territory from scratch — not advising or supporting one that already existed.\n\n - Fluency in government procurement: GSA schedules, GWACs, OTAs, sole-source and exemption pathways, FAR fundamentals, and state tender and cooperative purchasing processes.\n\n - Comfort with long, non-linear cycles and fiscal-year budget dynamics.\n\n - Ability to lead complex, multi-threaded sales spanning agency general counsel, CIO and CISO organizations, contracting officers, and end-user attorneys.\n\n - Genuine conviction about the mission and about equipping public servants with frontier technology.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Existing relationships across federal agency legal, CIO, or CISO organizations.\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal departments.\n\n - Experience managing a government reseller or channel relationship.\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$400,000 - $440,000 USD OTE 50/50\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AD2\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$400K – $440K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$400K - $440K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"06dc092c-23e0-4edf-8b6a-ba65fe17c5a4","tierSummary":"$400K – $440K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b72a06f0-9d29-4606-bda9-e9ecd02cee71","summary":"$400K – $440K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":440000},{"id":"dd913587-b8a2-4f4f-ad1a-20b528650a3e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":440000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f4b3077c-69dd-4656-851d-d9da65529634","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Security","department":"Security","team":"SA","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T22:31:27.330+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4b3077c-69dd-4656-851d-d9da65529634","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/f4b3077c-69dd-4656-851d-d9da65529634/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team at Harvey, you'll build and operate the foundational security services every other engineer at Harvey depends on: identity and access management, secrets and privileged access, and the tooling that makes the secure path the fast path. You'll design these systems, write the code, run them in production, and own the results. Agentic systems make this harder than it is at a typical SaaS company: when an AI agent acts on a user's behalf against their most sensitive documents, identity and authorization stop being solved problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Security at Harvey is an engineering discipline, not a gatekeeper function. We build platforms and libraries that make it hard for engineers to get security wrong, and we measure ourselves on adoption and outcomes rather than tickets filed. Our program is informed by risk: we invest where the actual exposure to our customers' data is greatest, rather than where a framework tells us to.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and operate Harvey's core security services — authentication, authorization, access governance, secrets management, and privileged access — across workforce, infrastructure, and production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's identity infrastructure end-to-end, including SSO, SCIM, and the fine-grained authorization our enterprise customers require</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build secure-by-default libraries, paved-road abstractions, and self-service tooling so engineering teams can identify, remediate, and prevent security issues without waiting on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take these systems from greenfield to production-grade: define the architecture, ship it, instrument it, and own its reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to incident response and drive technical mitigation when security issues surface</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the security bar across engineering through design reviews, code reviews, and technical mentorship</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software engineering experience with a track record of shipping and operating production services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building security infrastructure — IAM, authn/authz, secrets management, or privileged access</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of common vulnerability classes and the ability to reason about how a system fails under an attacker, not just under load</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills and a willingness to work across the stack and across unfamiliar domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency building and maintaining production services with agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Codex, or similar) — you know how to get real leverage from them and where they need supervision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP, or AWS) and modern distributed system patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to turn security requirements into scalable engineering solutions rather than manual process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills; you can influence engineering teams without formal authority</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building security platforms or programs at hyper-growth startups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in developer platform or infrastructure engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SCIM, OIDC/SAML, policy engines (OPA, Cedar, Zanzibar-style systems), or hardware-backed credentials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in highly regulated enterprise environments</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$188,000 - $282,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NP1</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Senior Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team at Harvey, you'll build and operate the foundational security services every other engineer at Harvey depends on: identity and access management, secrets and privileged access, and the tooling that makes the secure path the fast path. You'll design these systems, write the code, run them in production, and own the results. Agentic systems make this harder than it is at a typical SaaS company: when an AI agent acts on a user's behalf against their most sensitive documents, identity and authorization stop being solved problems.\n\nSecurity at Harvey is an engineering discipline, not a gatekeeper function. We build platforms and libraries that make it hard for engineers to get security wrong, and we measure ourselves on adoption and outcomes rather than tickets filed. Our program is informed by risk: we invest where the actual exposure to our customers' data is greatest, rather than where a framework tells us to.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and operate Harvey's core security services — authentication, authorization, access governance, secrets management, and privileged access — across workforce, infrastructure, and production environments\n\n - Own Harvey's identity infrastructure end-to-end, including SSO, SCIM, and the fine-grained authorization our enterprise customers require\n\n - Build secure-by-default libraries, paved-road abstractions, and self-service tooling so engineering teams can identify, remediate, and prevent security issues without waiting on us\n\n - Take these systems from greenfield to production-grade: define the architecture, ship it, instrument it, and own its reliability\n\n - Contribute to incident response and drive technical mitigation when security issues surface\n\n - Raise the security bar across engineering through design reviews, code reviews, and technical mentorship\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of software engineering experience with a track record of shipping and operating production services\n\n - Hands-on experience building security infrastructure — IAM, authn/authz, secrets management, or privileged access\n\n - Working knowledge of common vulnerability classes and the ability to reason about how a system fails under an attacker, not just under load\n\n - Strong programming skills and a willingness to work across the stack and across unfamiliar domains\n\n - Fluency building and maintaining production services with agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Codex, or similar) — you know how to get real leverage from them and where they need supervision\n\n - Experience with cloud infrastructure (Azure, GCP, or AWS) and modern distributed system patterns\n\n - Demonstrated ability to turn security requirements into scalable engineering solutions rather than manual process\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills; you can influence engineering teams without formal authority\n   \n   \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building security platforms or programs at hyper-growth startups\n\n - Background in developer platform or infrastructure engineering\n\n - Experience with SCIM, OIDC/SAML, policy engines (OPA, Cedar, Zanzibar-style systems), or hardware-backed credentials\n\n - Experience in highly regulated enterprise environments\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$188,000 - $282,000 USD\n\n \n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-NP1\n\n \n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$188K – $282K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$188K - $282K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2ce0f61f-ea69-4716-9c4d-7742d4051fca","tierSummary":"$188K – $282K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"169294bb-b805-4814-ba43-28ae66d1520f","summary":"$188K – $282K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":282000},{"id":"4fe5a736-3fd2-4a17-b993-01ebd642ab6f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b1a24e31-ae0a-4e2c-a91b-da459f770c62","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":188000,"maxValue":282000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c3e194f0-77a0-4f68-88a2-bbf430bc981a","title":"Head of EA Operations","department":"Business Operations","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T17:26:29.877+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c3e194f0-77a0-4f68-88a2-bbf430bc981a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c3e194f0-77a0-4f68-88a2-bbf430bc981a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Head of EA Operations leads Harvey’s team of Executive Assistants - the first dedicated leader the function has had. As our leadership team and global footprint have grown, so has the group of EAs supporting them, largely one hire at a time. You’ll bring that group together as one team, owning hiring, standards, and coverage globally so every executive has consistent, reliable support and every EA has a leader invested in their development.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who has built and run an executive support team before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Harvey's Executive Assistants as one coordinated team, including directly managing EAs to our VPs, setting the standard for what great executive support looks like across every org and office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own hiring for the team end to end and make the match between each assistant and the executive(s) they support, with input from those leaders, managing transitions and re-matches as the org evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set shared expectations, service levels, and ways of working for the role, and partner with executives on each assistant's performance and development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive leveling and compensation fairness across the EA team, working with leaders, Compensation, and People Business Partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage support coverage and ratios globally — keeping coverage reliable, balancing load across the team, and planning capacity ahead of new executive hires and expansion into new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide interim, hands-on coverage when needed — stepping in to support a leader directly when a new executive starts before their EA is hired, or when an EA is out — so no executive is left without support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Onboarding, IT, and People Business Partner teams to give new executives a smooth, well-coordinated start, helping shape their first weeks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing a team of Executive Assistants or executive-support professionals — hiring, developing, and setting the standard for others in the role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record supporting C-level and senior leaders, with the judgment and presence to earn their trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high-growth, fast-scaling company, where structure is built while the business keeps moving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational instincts — you build the systems, playbooks, and ratios — paired with excellent judgment around sensitive, confidential information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing across multiple offices and time zones, ideally globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional leadership ability and executive communication skills, with experience influencing without direct authority across engineering, product, go-to-market, and G&amp;A teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias toward ownership, speed, and accountability; you finish what you start and hold others to the same standard.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$187,600 - $258,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Head of EA Operations leads Harvey’s team of Executive Assistants - the first dedicated leader the function has had. As our leadership team and global footprint have grown, so has the group of EAs supporting them, largely one hire at a time. You’ll bring that group together as one team, owning hiring, standards, and coverage globally so every executive has consistent, reliable support and every EA has a leader invested in their development.\n\nThis is a hands-on leadership role for someone who has built and run an executive support team before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead Harvey's Executive Assistants as one coordinated team, including directly managing EAs to our VPs, setting the standard for what great executive support looks like across every org and office.\n\n - Own hiring for the team end to end and make the match between each assistant and the executive(s) they support, with input from those leaders, managing transitions and re-matches as the org evolves.\n\n - Set shared expectations, service levels, and ways of working for the role, and partner with executives on each assistant's performance and development.\n\n - Drive leveling and compensation fairness across the EA team, working with leaders, Compensation, and People Business Partners.\n\n - Manage support coverage and ratios globally — keeping coverage reliable, balancing load across the team, and planning capacity ahead of new executive hires and expansion into new markets.\n\n - Provide interim, hands-on coverage when needed — stepping in to support a leader directly when a new executive starts before their EA is hired, or when an EA is out — so no executive is left without support.\n\n - Partner with the Onboarding, IT, and People Business Partner teams to give new executives a smooth, well-coordinated start, helping shape their first weeks.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience managing a team of Executive Assistants or executive-support professionals — hiring, developing, and setting the standard for others in the role.\n\n - A track record supporting C-level and senior leaders, with the judgment and presence to earn their trust.\n\n - Experience in a high-growth, fast-scaling company, where structure is built while the business keeps moving.\n\n - Strong operational instincts — you build the systems, playbooks, and ratios — paired with excellent judgment around sensitive, confidential information.\n\n - Experience managing across multiple offices and time zones, ideally globally.\n\n - Strong cross-functional leadership ability and executive communication skills, with experience influencing without direct authority across engineering, product, go-to-market, and G&A teams.\n\n - Bias toward ownership, speed, and accountability; you finish what you start and hold others to the same standard.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$187,600 - $258,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$187.6K – $258K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$187.6K - $258K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"cee08aa4-90e2-4821-bbba-c5011bda3fe5","tierSummary":"$187.6K – $258K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9364d52b-a026-4121-bd15-5b8a4aa4e0d0","summary":"$187.6K – $258K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":187600,"maxValue":258000},{"id":"26c1db16-cc92-438f-a208-68d644ec5040","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6679b80e-093a-48b9-8b6c-76a537a7bcec","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":187600,"maxValue":258000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2813571d-cfb6-4762-ba9d-28f8b85215f2","title":"Head of EA Operations","department":"Business Operations","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T17:27:07.820+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2813571d-cfb6-4762-ba9d-28f8b85215f2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2813571d-cfb6-4762-ba9d-28f8b85215f2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Head of EA Operations leads Harvey’s team of Executive Assistants - the first dedicated leader the function has had. As our leadership team and global footprint have grown, so has the group of EAs supporting them, largely one hire at a time. You’ll bring that group together as one team, owning hiring, standards, and coverage globally so every executive has consistent, reliable support and every EA has a leader invested in their development.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who has built and run an executive support team before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Harvey's Executive Assistants as one coordinated team, including directly managing EAs to our VPs, setting the standard for what great executive support looks like across every org and office.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own hiring for the team end to end and make the match between each assistant and the executive(s) they support, with input from those leaders, managing transitions and re-matches as the org evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set shared expectations, service levels, and ways of working for the role, and partner with executives on each assistant's performance and development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive leveling and compensation fairness across the EA team, working with leaders, Compensation, and People Business Partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage support coverage and ratios globally — keeping coverage reliable, balancing load across the team, and planning capacity ahead of new executive hires and expansion into new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide interim, hands-on coverage when needed — stepping in to support a leader directly when a new executive starts before their EA is hired, or when an EA is out — so no executive is left without support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Onboarding, IT, and People Business Partner teams to give new executives a smooth, well-coordinated start, helping shape their first weeks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing a team of Executive Assistants or executive-support professionals — hiring, developing, and setting the standard for others in the role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record supporting C-level and senior leaders, with the judgment and presence to earn their trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high-growth, fast-scaling company, where structure is built while the business keeps moving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational instincts — you build the systems, playbooks, and ratios — paired with excellent judgment around sensitive, confidential information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing across multiple offices and time zones, ideally globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional leadership ability and executive communication skills, with experience influencing without direct authority across engineering, product, go-to-market, and G&amp;A teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias toward ownership, speed, and accountability; you finish what you start and hold others to the same standard.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$187,600 - $258,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Head of EA Operations leads Harvey’s team of Executive Assistants - the first dedicated leader the function has had. As our leadership team and global footprint have grown, so has the group of EAs supporting them, largely one hire at a time. You’ll bring that group together as one team, owning hiring, standards, and coverage globally so every executive has consistent, reliable support and every EA has a leader invested in their development.\n\nThis is a hands-on leadership role for someone who has built and run an executive support team before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead Harvey's Executive Assistants as one coordinated team, including directly managing EAs to our VPs, setting the standard for what great executive support looks like across every org and office.\n\n - Own hiring for the team end to end and make the match between each assistant and the executive(s) they support, with input from those leaders, managing transitions and re-matches as the org evolves.\n\n - Set shared expectations, service levels, and ways of working for the role, and partner with executives on each assistant's performance and development.\n\n - Drive leveling and compensation fairness across the EA team, working with leaders, Compensation, and People Business Partners.\n\n - Manage support coverage and ratios globally — keeping coverage reliable, balancing load across the team, and planning capacity ahead of new executive hires and expansion into new markets.\n\n - Provide interim, hands-on coverage when needed — stepping in to support a leader directly when a new executive starts before their EA is hired, or when an EA is out — so no executive is left without support.\n\n - Partner with the Onboarding, IT, and People Business Partner teams to give new executives a smooth, well-coordinated start, helping shape their first weeks.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Experience managing a team of Executive Assistants or executive-support professionals — hiring, developing, and setting the standard for others in the role.\n\n - A track record supporting C-level and senior leaders, with the judgment and presence to earn their trust.\n\n - Experience in a high-growth, fast-scaling company, where structure is built while the business keeps moving.\n\n - Strong operational instincts — you build the systems, playbooks, and ratios — paired with excellent judgment around sensitive, confidential information.\n\n - Experience managing across multiple offices and time zones, ideally globally.\n\n - Strong cross-functional leadership ability and executive communication skills, with experience influencing without direct authority across engineering, product, go-to-market, and G&A teams.\n\n - Bias toward ownership, speed, and accountability; you finish what you start and hold others to the same standard.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$187,600 - $258,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$187.6K – $258K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$187.6K - $258K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d09d4553-1ae2-4e99-acde-d92f30599644","tierSummary":"$187.6K – $258K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d6e36ed7-4157-4411-a671-b65177576eab","summary":"$187.6K – $258K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":187600,"maxValue":258000},{"id":"f1514d2d-c875-43ba-9afb-760bb1fa7968","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"06590716-0d2f-49a9-a572-66e114f0ebe7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":187600,"maxValue":258000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"953b710f-3c48-4409-ad30-6416da8ed043","title":"GTM Systems Administrator","department":"Business Operations","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T09:25:09.699+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/953b710f-3c48-4409-ad30-6416da8ed043","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/953b710f-3c48-4409-ad30-6416da8ed043/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is building a best-in-class go-to-market engine, and we're looking for a GTM Systems Administrator to join the GTM Systems team and help scale the systems that power both our pipeline and our customer experience. You'll take on a variety of projects across the full GTM lifecycle, from how we source, enrich, and route leads at the top of the funnel to how we support and engage customers through Zendesk and our Customer Success platforms. This is not a traditional RevOps or Salesforce admin role: we expect this person to work AI-first, using AI tools and agents to build, automate, and maintain systems that would traditionally require engineering support or manual admin work. Reporting to the Head of GTM Systems, you'll partner closely with Sales, Marketing, Support, and Customer Success to translate business needs into scalable, reliable systems that directly drive revenue and retention outcomes.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work across a variety of projects on the GTM Systems team, with some sprints focused on top-of-funnel growth and others on support and customer success tooling, flexing to where the business needs you most.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and improve top-of-funnel systems including lead sourcing, enrichment, scoring, and routing, building enrichment workflows in Clay and across data providers (ZoomInfo, Cognism, Apollo, Clearbit, etc.) to power inbound and outbound pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure and optimize Zendesk as Harvey's primary support platform (ticket routing, triggers, automations, macros, SLA policies, agent workspace) and support adjacent CS platforms like Catalyst.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Salesforce configuration across the funnel, including lead routing, scoring, lifecycle stages, and automation (Flows, validation rules, custom objects), and how data flows across Salesforce, marketing automation, support, and enrichment tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI as a default working method: build and maintain AI agents, automations, and workflows (AI triage, copilots, agent-based enrichment, LLM-powered data quality checks) to eliminate manual admin work and extend what the systems team can ship without engineering support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate GTM and CS tools with Harvey's broader ecosystem (CRM, product data, internal tools, communication platforms) to ensure a unified view of the customer, and build reporting and dashboards that provide visibility into pipeline conversion, support performance, and customer health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high data quality and compliance through deduplication, normalization, enrichment governance, and consent/opt-out handling, and document system architecture, workflows, and processes so everything scales as the company grows.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4-8+ years of experience in GTM Systems, RevOps, Growth Ops, Support Ops, or similar roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency in Salesforce (data modeling, Flows, lead routing, account hierarchy, reporting) plus hands-on experience administering Zendesk (routing, automations, triggers, SLA policies), or deep expertise in one with proven ability to ramp fast on the other.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with Clay and at least one major enrichment/data provider (ZoomInfo, Cognism, Apollo, Clearbit, etc.), and experience with marketing automation platforms (Marketo, HubSpot, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated AI fluency: you already use AI tools (Claude, ChatGPT, Clay AI, Zendesk AI, or similar) to build workflows, automate admin tasks, draft configurations, and troubleshoot, and you can point to concrete things you've shipped this way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinking, with the ability to design and debug end-to-end data flows across tools, spanning both reactive support workflows and proactive growth motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, team-first working style: comfortable operating in a pod, picking up varied projects, and working cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Support, Customer Success, and Operations. Highly organized and documentation-oriented, with a focus on scalable, maintainable systems.</p></li></ul><h3>Bonus</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Customer Success platforms (Gainsight, Catalyst) or Zendesk certification(s).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building integrations using APIs, webhooks, or iPaaS tools (Workato, Zapier, MuleSoft), or integrating GTM systems with data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or deploying AI agents in production (e.g., agentic prospecting, AI ticket triage, health-score automation)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of SQL and/or scripting (Python, JavaScript) for data workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in high-growth or early-stage environments where systems are built from the ground up.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is building a best-in-class go-to-market engine, and we're looking for a GTM Systems Administrator to join the GTM Systems team and help scale the systems that power both our pipeline and our customer experience. You'll take on a variety of projects across the full GTM lifecycle, from how we source, enrich, and route leads at the top of the funnel to how we support and engage customers through Zendesk and our Customer Success platforms. This is not a traditional RevOps or Salesforce admin role: we expect this person to work AI-first, using AI tools and agents to build, automate, and maintain systems that would traditionally require engineering support or manual admin work. Reporting to the Head of GTM Systems, you'll partner closely with Sales, Marketing, Support, and Customer Success to translate business needs into scalable, reliable systems that directly drive revenue and retention outcomes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Work across a variety of projects on the GTM Systems team, with some sprints focused on top-of-funnel growth and others on support and customer success tooling, flexing to where the business needs you most.\n\n - Design and improve top-of-funnel systems including lead sourcing, enrichment, scoring, and routing, building enrichment workflows in Clay and across data providers (ZoomInfo, Cognism, Apollo, Clearbit, etc.) to power inbound and outbound pipeline.\n\n - Configure and optimize Zendesk as Harvey's primary support platform (ticket routing, triggers, automations, macros, SLA policies, agent workspace) and support adjacent CS platforms like Catalyst.\n\n - Contribute to Salesforce configuration across the funnel, including lead routing, scoring, lifecycle stages, and automation (Flows, validation rules, custom objects), and how data flows across Salesforce, marketing automation, support, and enrichment tools.\n\n - Use AI as a default working method: build and maintain AI agents, automations, and workflows (AI triage, copilots, agent-based enrichment, LLM-powered data quality checks) to eliminate manual admin work and extend what the systems team can ship without engineering support.\n\n - Integrate GTM and CS tools with Harvey's broader ecosystem (CRM, product data, internal tools, communication platforms) to ensure a unified view of the customer, and build reporting and dashboards that provide visibility into pipeline conversion, support performance, and customer health.\n\n - Maintain high data quality and compliance through deduplication, normalization, enrichment governance, and consent/opt-out handling, and document system architecture, workflows, and processes so everything scales as the company grows.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4-8+ years of experience in GTM Systems, RevOps, Growth Ops, Support Ops, or similar roles.\n\n - Strong proficiency in Salesforce (data modeling, Flows, lead routing, account hierarchy, reporting) plus hands-on experience administering Zendesk (routing, automations, triggers, SLA policies), or deep expertise in one with proven ability to ramp fast on the other.\n\n - Hands-on experience with Clay and at least one major enrichment/data provider (ZoomInfo, Cognism, Apollo, Clearbit, etc.), and experience with marketing automation platforms (Marketo, HubSpot, or similar).\n\n - Demonstrated AI fluency: you already use AI tools (Claude, ChatGPT, Clay AI, Zendesk AI, or similar) to build workflows, automate admin tasks, draft configurations, and troubleshoot, and you can point to concrete things you've shipped this way.\n\n - Strong systems thinking, with the ability to design and debug end-to-end data flows across tools, spanning both reactive support workflows and proactive growth motions.\n\n - A collaborative, team-first working style: comfortable operating in a pod, picking up varied projects, and working cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Support, Customer Success, and Operations. Highly organized and documentation-oriented, with a focus on scalable, maintainable systems.\n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Experience with Customer Success platforms (Gainsight, Catalyst) or Zendesk certification(s).\n\n - Experience building integrations using APIs, webhooks, or iPaaS tools (Workato, Zapier, MuleSoft), or integrating GTM systems with data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery).\n\n - Experience building or deploying AI agents in production (e.g., agentic prospecting, AI ticket triage, health-score automation)\n\n - Working knowledge of SQL and/or scripting (Python, JavaScript) for data workflows.\n\n - Background in high-growth or early-stage environments where systems are built from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bc479bb5-445f-4e9f-a0bc-d2e1bab03947","title":"Manager, Enterprise Application Engineering","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dublin","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T09:25:57.157+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bc479bb5-445f-4e9f-a0bc-d2e1bab03947","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/bc479bb5-445f-4e9f-a0bc-d2e1bab03947/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're seeking a Manager, Enterprise Application Engineering to build and lead the engineering team behind Harvey's internal business systems. You'll manage a group of Enterprise Application Engineers and AI Enablement Engineers who build the applications, integrations, and agents that Harvey's business teams run on — and you'll stay hands-on in the code and architecture yourself. This is Harvey's first Business Technology leadership role in Dublin, so you'll also anchor the EMEA engineering bench for BizTech as the company scales internationally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll inherit a small nucleus and hire out from there, which means your first year is as much about recruiting, defining the team's charter, and setting the engineering bar as it is about shipping. The ideal candidate is a working manager: someone who has built internal applications and integrations at a fast-moving company, has led a small engineering team, and is genuinely excited about applying AI agents to internal business problems rather than just talking about it. Harvey builds AI for legal professionals - the internal bar has to match the external one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the mindset that Job's Not Finished. We move fast, prioritize clarity, and are always striving for excellence. If this resonates with you, we'd love to hear from you.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and lead the team.</strong> Hire, onboard, and develop a Dublin-based team of Enterprise Application Engineers and AI Enablement Engineers. Own the interview loop, ramp plans, and performance for the function.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stay hands-on.</strong> Spend a meaningful share of your time in the work - designing systems, reviewing code, writing integrations, unblocking your engineers on production issues. You set the technical bar by demonstrating it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the internal application layer.</strong> Take responsibility for the custom applications, services, and automations that sit on top of and between Harvey's core platforms (Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Okta, Marketo, Zendesk, Google Workspace, Slack, Zip, Linear, Notion), including their reliability, security posture, and lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive AI enablement into the business.</strong> Lead the team that puts agents, MCP servers, and internal AI tooling into the hands of Harvey’s teams - building the connective plumbing to internal systems, the evaluation and guardrail practices that make it safe, and the enablement that makes it stick.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with business and systems owners.</strong> Work directly with teams across Finance, People, GTM, Marketing, Customer Experience, Legal, and Workplace leaders to turn ambiguous business problems into scoped, sequenced engineering work - and to say no clearly when something shouldn't be built.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Establish engineering standards.</strong> Define how this team writes, tests, deploys, documents, and monitors what it builds. Introduce the practices that scale a growing team without adding process for its own sake.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Anchor BizTech in EMEA.</strong> Provide senior BizTech presence in Dublin for a growing international office and region, and hold enough overlap with US stakeholders to stay tightly coupled to the wider org.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Make build-vs-buy calls.</strong> Assess when a business need is better solved by configuration, a vendor, an integration, or custom code - and make that call with cost, security, and long-term maintenance in view.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 2 years of engineering management experience, and 7+ years of hands-on enterprise application, integration, or internal platform engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on engineering depth in a modern language (Python, TypeScript, Go, or similar) and real experience designing and operating API-based integrations between business systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of the enterprise SaaS landscape - CRM, HRIS, ERP, IdP, Marketing automation, and support / CX platforms (Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Okta, Marketo/Braze, Zendesk, or comparable) - and how business processes like Lead-to-Cash, Hire-to-Retire, and the post-sale support lifecycle actually flow across them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience applying LLMs or AI agents to real production problems, with a clear point of view on evaluation, guardrails, and where the technology does and doesn't hold up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of hiring and developing engineers, and of raising the technical bar on a team you inherited or built.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience standing up a Business Technology, internal tools, or enterprise engineering function in a new office or region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS company scaling through 2,000+ employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on work with MCP, agent orchestration frameworks, or LLM gateway and evaluation tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) as a daily working practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with enterprise iPaaS platforms (e.g., Workato) and event-driven integration patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to legal, professional services, or another regulated industry.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SH1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe're seeking a Manager, Enterprise Application Engineering to build and lead the engineering team behind Harvey's internal business systems. You'll manage a group of Enterprise Application Engineers and AI Enablement Engineers who build the applications, integrations, and agents that Harvey's business teams run on — and you'll stay hands-on in the code and architecture yourself. This is Harvey's first Business Technology leadership role in Dublin, so you'll also anchor the EMEA engineering bench for BizTech as the company scales internationally.\n\nYou'll inherit a small nucleus and hire out from there, which means your first year is as much about recruiting, defining the team's charter, and setting the engineering bar as it is about shipping. The ideal candidate is a working manager: someone who has built internal applications and integrations at a fast-moving company, has led a small engineering team, and is genuinely excited about applying AI agents to internal business problems rather than just talking about it. Harvey builds AI for legal professionals - the internal bar has to match the external one.\n\nAt Harvey, we value Decisiveness, Simplicity, and the mindset that Job's Not Finished. We move fast, prioritize clarity, and are always striving for excellence. If this resonates with you, we'd love to hear from you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and lead the team. Hire, onboard, and develop a Dublin-based team of Enterprise Application Engineers and AI Enablement Engineers. Own the interview loop, ramp plans, and performance for the function.\n\n - Stay hands-on. Spend a meaningful share of your time in the work - designing systems, reviewing code, writing integrations, unblocking your engineers on production issues. You set the technical bar by demonstrating it.\n\n - Own the internal application layer. Take responsibility for the custom applications, services, and automations that sit on top of and between Harvey's core platforms (Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Okta, Marketo, Zendesk, Google Workspace, Slack, Zip, Linear, Notion), including their reliability, security posture, and lifecycle.\n\n - Drive AI enablement into the business. Lead the team that puts agents, MCP servers, and internal AI tooling into the hands of Harvey’s teams - building the connective plumbing to internal systems, the evaluation and guardrail practices that make it safe, and the enablement that makes it stick.\n\n - Partner with business and systems owners. Work directly with teams across Finance, People, GTM, Marketing, Customer Experience, Legal, and Workplace leaders to turn ambiguous business problems into scoped, sequenced engineering work - and to say no clearly when something shouldn't be built.\n\n - Establish engineering standards. Define how this team writes, tests, deploys, documents, and monitors what it builds. Introduce the practices that scale a growing team without adding process for its own sake.\n\n - Anchor BizTech in EMEA. Provide senior BizTech presence in Dublin for a growing international office and region, and hold enough overlap with US stakeholders to stay tightly coupled to the wider org.\n\n - Make build-vs-buy calls. Assess when a business need is better solved by configuration, a vendor, an integration, or custom code - and make that call with cost, security, and long-term maintenance in view.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 2 years of engineering management experience, and 7+ years of hands-on enterprise application, integration, or internal platform engineering.\n\n - Hands-on engineering depth in a modern language (Python, TypeScript, Go, or similar) and real experience designing and operating API-based integrations between business systems.\n\n - Working knowledge of the enterprise SaaS landscape - CRM, HRIS, ERP, IdP, Marketing automation, and support / CX platforms (Salesforce, Workday, NetSuite, Okta, Marketo/Braze, Zendesk, or comparable) - and how business processes like Lead-to-Cash, Hire-to-Retire, and the post-sale support lifecycle actually flow across them.\n\n - Demonstrated experience applying LLMs or AI agents to real production problems, with a clear point of view on evaluation, guardrails, and where the technology does and doesn't hold up.\n\n - Track record of hiring and developing engineers, and of raising the technical bar on a team you inherited or built.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\nBonus Points:\n\n - Experience standing up a Business Technology, internal tools, or enterprise engineering function in a new office or region.\n\n - Background at a high-growth B2B SaaS company scaling through 2,000+ employees.\n\n - Hands-on work with MCP, agent orchestration frameworks, or LLM gateway and evaluation tooling.\n\n - Fluency with agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) as a daily working practice.\n\n - Experience with enterprise iPaaS platforms (e.g., Workato) and event-driven integration patterns.\n\n - Exposure to legal, professional services, or another regulated industry.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SH1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fea3ab0e-d5f0-4f89-9ac2-9b4a1f851ee7","title":"Director Global Benefits","department":"Human Resources","team":"Total Rewards","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T14:55:17.580+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fea3ab0e-d5f0-4f89-9ac2-9b4a1f851ee7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/fea3ab0e-d5f0-4f89-9ac2-9b4a1f851ee7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy and plan design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team and service delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs, vendors, and spend</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>10+ years in benefits</strong>, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep US benefits expertise</strong> across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real international experience</strong>: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor and broker management</strong>: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial fluency</strong>: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication</strong>: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mentality.</strong> You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI experience.</strong> You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$227,100 - $310,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.\n\n\n\nThis is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nStrategy and plan design\n\n - Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.\n\n - Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.\n\n - Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.\n\nTeam and service delivery\n\n - Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.\n\n - Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.\n\n - Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.\n\nPrograms, vendors, and spend\n\n - Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.\n\n - Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.\n\n - Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.\n\n - Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.\n\n - Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in benefits, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Deep US benefits expertise across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).\n\n - Real international experience: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.\n\n - Strategic and hands-on: You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.\n\n - Vendor and broker management: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.\n\n - Financial fluency: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.\n\n - Exceptional communication: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.\n\n - Builder mentality. You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.\n\n - AI experience. You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$227,100 - $310,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$227.1K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2337de31-c09b-41e6-b164-e0266392e305","tierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"79a6e5b7-9893-44e6-9255-ac87e44a7b9f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8d0ec933-fe83-4b4c-9567-d0819ee5e547","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f2beee7d-0b71-4424-ac07-24398b115bb8","summary":"$227.1K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"2807b46b-3ea5-43e2-94ea-4e6cdc6d4bb2","title":"Legal Engineer, Product Specialist","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Seoul","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T20:39:22.107+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"South Korea","addressCountry":"South Korea","addressLocality":"Seoul"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2807b46b-3ea5-43e2-94ea-4e6cdc6d4bb2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2807b46b-3ea5-43e2-94ea-4e6cdc6d4bb2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey's Legal Engineer - Product Specialist joins the LEPS team to serve as the face of Harvey in Korea, building trust with partners, counsel, and legal teams at one of Harvey's key global accounts and across the Korean legal market. This role sits within Harvey's post-sales organization and partners closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive adoption, deepen utilization, and support long-term expansion and renewal. The Legal Product Specialist draws on Korean legal training and practice experience to develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel—advising them on how Harvey's AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency. They translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for Product and Engineering while feeding Korean market insights back to the broader GTM organization. It is a rare opportunity to pioneer Harvey's presence in the Korean market and shape how a category-defining legal AI platform is adopted across one of Asia's most sophisticated legal systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams in Korea by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey's AI into their daily practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey's platform for Korean-speaking legal professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through the lens of Korean legal practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to customer-facing content geared toward the Korean market (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Korean legal qualification (변호사 자격) or equivalent with 3+ years of experience as a qualified lawyer at a top-tier Korean or international law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Korean and English, with the ability to operate seamlessly across both languages in professional settings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision-makers and build credibility at all levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals, with curiosity about AI's potential to transform the legal industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-GE1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey's Legal Engineer - Product Specialist joins the LEPS team to serve as the face of Harvey in Korea, building trust with partners, counsel, and legal teams at one of Harvey's key global accounts and across the Korean legal market. This role sits within Harvey's post-sales organization and partners closely with Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to drive adoption, deepen utilization, and support long-term expansion and renewal. The Legal Product Specialist draws on Korean legal training and practice experience to develop consultative relationships with law firm partners, associates, innovation teams, and in-house counsel—advising them on how Harvey's AI solutions can enhance legal effectiveness and efficiency. They translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for Product and Engineering while feeding Korean market insights back to the broader GTM organization. It is a rare opportunity to pioneer Harvey's presence in the Korean market and shape how a category-defining legal AI platform is adopted across one of Asia's most sophisticated legal systems.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build trusted relationships with law firm and in-house legal teams in Korea by understanding their unique workflows and offering tailored guidance on how to incorporate Harvey's AI into their daily practice.\n\n - Design and lead onboarding sessions, training workshops, and ongoing enablement programs that drive adoption and maximize the value of Harvey's platform for Korean-speaking legal professionals.\n\n - Act as a strategic partner to Customer Success Managers and Account Executives to identify expansion opportunities and support renewal efforts through demonstrated impact and engagement.\n\n - Proactively surface obstacles to adoption by engaging users with thoughtful questions and legal empathy, then develop and implement strategies to overcome them.\n\n - Translate legal practice needs into actionable feedback for the product and engineering teams, helping to shape product development through the lens of Korean legal practice.\n\n - Contribute to customer-facing content geared toward the Korean market (e.g., training materials, use case guides, FAQ resources) to ensure continued customer success across a range of practice areas.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Korean legal qualification (변호사 자격) or equivalent with 3+ years of experience as a qualified lawyer at a top-tier Korean or international law firm.\n\n - Fluency in Korean and English, with the ability to operate seamlessly across both languages in professional settings.\n\n - Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision-makers and build credibility at all levels.\n\n - Outstanding presentation skills to both legal and executive audiences, whether impromptu on a whiteboard or using presentations and demos.\n\n - Strong understanding of legal processes and challenges faced by legal professionals, with curiosity about AI's potential to transform the legal industry.\n\n - Sales or customer-facing experience, including law firm business development and/or secondment, is a plus, as is experience directly managing law firm client matters and client relationships.\n   \n   \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-GE1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cb89e7ec-6643-4cfa-b4d6-ce34b345f46a","title":"Scaled Customer Success Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T22:42:08.500+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cb89e7ec-6643-4cfa-b4d6-ce34b345f46a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cb89e7ec-6643-4cfa-b4d6-ce34b345f46a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Scaled Customer Success Manager joins Harvey's Scaled Customer Success team to drive retention, renewal, and expansion outcomes across a high-volume book of business. The team's mission is to deliver strategic, efficient value at scale—ensuring customers adopt Harvey's AI solutions deeply and renew with confidence. This role owns the full commercial lifecycle for a portfolio of accounts, blending consultative customer engagement with a data-driven renewals motion to maximize net revenue retention. Scaled CSMs partners closely with Sales, Legal Engineering, and Product to translate customer feedback into roadmap influence and expansion opportunity. It is a rare opportunity to shape a growing function at the intersection of AI innovation and customer value delivery.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own renewals and expansions across a named portfolio of accounts, driving net revenue retention and gross retention targets through proactive commercial engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead scaled customer engagement motions—including QBRs, value reviews, and enablement sessions—to maximize product adoption and demonstrate ongoing ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor customer health using data and analytics, identifying churn signals early and executing structured intervention plans to protect and grow revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a trusted advisor to customers with a prescriptive, consultative approach, integrating Harvey into their workflows and championing the power of LLMs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Product, and Sales to relay customer insights, influence the product roadmap, and align on shared goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine scalable playbooks and processes that elevate the team's approach to customer engagement, renewals, and expansion.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or a renewals-focused role within Enterprise SaaS, legal technology, or management consulting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of managing a high-volume book of business and consistently meeting or exceeding retention and expansion targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial acumen with experience owning renewals conversations and identifying upsell or expansion opportunities within existing accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders at multiple levels and deliver polished QBRs and value reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven mindset with experience leveraging customer health metrics, adoption data, and CS platforms to inform strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, proactive disposition with a team-first mentality and comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguity-rich environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$115,000 - $130,000 USD OTE 80/20</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BS1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Scaled Customer Success Manager joins Harvey's Scaled Customer Success team to drive retention, renewal, and expansion outcomes across a high-volume book of business. The team's mission is to deliver strategic, efficient value at scale—ensuring customers adopt Harvey's AI solutions deeply and renew with confidence. This role owns the full commercial lifecycle for a portfolio of accounts, blending consultative customer engagement with a data-driven renewals motion to maximize net revenue retention. Scaled CSMs partners closely with Sales, Legal Engineering, and Product to translate customer feedback into roadmap influence and expansion opportunity. It is a rare opportunity to shape a growing function at the intersection of AI innovation and customer value delivery.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own renewals and expansions across a named portfolio of accounts, driving net revenue retention and gross retention targets through proactive commercial engagement.\n\n - Lead scaled customer engagement motions—including QBRs, value reviews, and enablement sessions—to maximize product adoption and demonstrate ongoing ROI.\n\n - Monitor customer health using data and analytics, identifying churn signals early and executing structured intervention plans to protect and grow revenue.\n\n - Serve as a trusted advisor to customers with a prescriptive, consultative approach, integrating Harvey into their workflows and championing the power of LLMs.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Product, and Sales to relay customer insights, influence the product roadmap, and align on shared goals.\n\n - Build and refine scalable playbooks and processes that elevate the team's approach to customer engagement, renewals, and expansion.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or a renewals-focused role within Enterprise SaaS, legal technology, or management consulting.\n\n - Demonstrated track record of managing a high-volume book of business and consistently meeting or exceeding retention and expansion targets.\n\n - Strong commercial acumen with experience owning renewals conversations and identifying upsell or expansion opportunities within existing accounts.\n\n - Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders at multiple levels and deliver polished QBRs and value reviews.\n\n - Data-driven mindset with experience leveraging customer health metrics, adoption data, and CS platforms to inform strategy.\n\n - Collaborative, proactive disposition with a team-first mentality and comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguity-rich environment.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$115,000 - $130,000 USD OTE 80/20\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BS1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$115K – $130K • Offers Equity • OTE 80/20","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$115K - $130K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"879893b2-2d1b-4ae2-9157-6fecfddbea0c","tierSummary":"$115K – $130K • Offers Equity • OTE 80/20","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 80/20","components":[{"id":"baeb1b90-e02c-4f9a-94f1-6cb243782598","summary":"$115K – $130K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":115000,"maxValue":130000},{"id":"fd4920f3-8e3a-41a1-a66d-5b7440ca145a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":115000,"maxValue":130000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a725492f-3412-4699-a8cd-0d195bde3450","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Data Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T21:52:52.675+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a725492f-3412-4699-a8cd-0d195bde3450","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a725492f-3412-4699-a8cd-0d195bde3450/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.\n\nAs one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.\n\nThe near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.\n\nFrom there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.\n\nYou'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows\n\n - Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project\n\n - Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering\n\n - Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph\n\n - Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe\n\n - Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting\n\n - Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it\n\n - Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements\n\n - Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on\n\n - Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management\n\n - Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming\n\n - Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it\n\n - Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL\n\n - Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way\n\n - Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime\n\n - Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency\n\n - Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams\n\n - Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements\n\n - Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products\n\n - Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"22347a40-a244-4b73-a7bf-5f7095c8ca9c","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"83ad18f1-c697-4a43-a9c3-58fbc8ce4bea","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"53a1ebf6-1f8b-4f68-ae8b-e6fa0c40e8fc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ef1e7f78-4132-4654-ab3a-3e27db18e5e7","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"79bef873-33b0-4b8b-b5f0-2256b2751907","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Data Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T21:54:16.866+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/79bef873-33b0-4b8b-b5f0-2256b2751907","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/79bef873-33b0-4b8b-b5f0-2256b2751907/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - $290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.\n\nAs one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.\n\nThe near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.\n\nFrom there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.\n\nYou'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows\n\n - Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project\n\n - Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering\n\n - Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph\n\n - Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe\n\n - Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting\n\n - Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it\n\n - Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements\n\n - Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on\n\n - Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management\n\n - Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming\n\n - Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it\n\n - Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL\n\n - Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way\n\n - Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime\n\n - Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency\n\n - Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams\n\n - Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements\n\n - Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products\n\n - Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - $290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7d782eb5-2eb0-40c0-b0dd-4673bda64f29","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3c5db5cd-7084-4113-bf44-9ff6bc074cb2","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"id":"615e715c-dd8b-4d53-8dd8-8ead5c8a417e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ba63c378-dd9e-4330-a977-3a4ed3e58328","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"504ba806-2e23-47f4-887f-b4aa777faae5","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Data Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T23:38:55.348+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/504ba806-2e23-47f4-887f-b4aa777faae5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/504ba806-2e23-47f4-887f-b4aa777faae5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.\n\nAs one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.\n\nThe near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.\n\nFrom there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.\n\nYou'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows\n\n - Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project\n\n - Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering\n\n - Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph\n\n - Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe\n\n - Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting\n\n - Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it\n\n - Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements\n\n - Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on\n\n - Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management\n\n - Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming\n\n - Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it\n\n - Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL\n\n - Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way\n\n - Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime\n\n - Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency\n\n - Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams\n\n - Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements\n\n - Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products\n\n - Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7aaca79f-0600-485e-916e-11dfa11bd62f","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2121bbe0-9e7d-472a-8f16-a1083bd29905","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"888b7af3-2d5d-4291-9d07-87c9a709fe47","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e9bc899b-aabb-4c31-808b-c70c7a49a419","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"976a512f-7665-4350-8258-098993c10ea1","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Data Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T23:39:01.991+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/976a512f-7665-4350-8258-098993c10ea1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/976a512f-7665-4350-8258-098993c10ea1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AN2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is generating far more data than we currently know how to use well. Product telemetry, agent execution traces, model usage, customer engagement, financial and operational systems — the volume and the number of teams who need to work with it are both growing faster than any single team can serve by hand.\n\nAs one of the first hires on our central data platform team, you'll build the systems that let every team at Harvey work with data confidently and independently. This is a platform charter, not a pipeline queue: you're building the frameworks, tooling, and paved paths that product engineers, data engineers, and analysts all build on, and you're measured by their leverage and general trust in our data systems.\n\nThe near-term foundation is ingestion and the warehouse — reliable streaming and batch paths into Snowflake, CDC off production systems, orchestration, and schema evolution that absorbs upstream change instead of breaking under it, and factors in the hard data sensitivity requirements our domain requires.\n\nFrom there the charter expands to the rest of what a modern data platform owes its users: transformation and compute frameworks, self-serve tooling so teams can stand up their own pipelines against well-tested primitives, real-time and stream processing for products and internal systems that can't wait for a nightly batch, and the quality, lineage, and governance layers that make the whole thing trustworthy. Handling PII correctly and honoring multi-region data residency aren't nice to have features here — they're constraints the platform has to satisfy by construction, for customers who are among the most security-conscious institutions in the world.\n\nYou'll sit between Analytics, Data Engineering, product teams, and Infrastructure. Today this work is distributed and improvised. You'll make it a system, set the technical direction, and help build the team around you.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA or New York, NY\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the data platform's architecture and technical direction — treating data infrastructure as a software product built from reusable frameworks, and making deliberate build-vs-buy tradeoffs as the platform grows\n\n - Build and operate the ingestion layer across streaming, batch, CDC, and third-party connectors, including schema evolution that absorbs upstream change safely rather than silently breaking consumers, so onboarding a new source is a paved path instead of a project\n\n - Land data into Snowflake with the freshness, completeness, and cost characteristics downstream consumers can plan around, and define a clean handoff for Analytics Engineering\n\n - Own the orchestration platform — scheduling, retries, backfills, and dependency management across the full data graph\n\n - Build the transformation and compute frameworks teams can use to process data at scale, and the self-serve tooling that lets product engineers and analysts stand up their own pipelines against primitives you've already made safe\n\n - Design and operate stream processing infrastructure for use cases that can't wait for batch — real-time product features, operational alerting, and near-live reporting\n\n - Build the trust layer: quality and observability (freshness, validation, reconciliation, anomaly detection, alerting routed to the right owner) alongside lineage, cataloging, and discovery, so anyone can find data and know where it came from and what depends on it\n\n - Build the patterns and tooling for PII and sensitive data — classification, masking, retention, access control — and for multi-region residency requirements\n\n - Set the technical bar for data at Harvey through design reviews, standards, documentation, and mentorship as the team grows\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years building and operating production data infrastructure, with ownership of systems other teams depend on\n\n - Deep experience with cloud data warehouses — Snowflake strongly preferred (BigQuery, Databricks, or Redshift experience transfers well) — including performance tuning and cost management\n\n - Hands-on experience building CDC and streaming pipelines with technologies like Kafka, Debezium, Flink, or Spark Streaming\n\n - Experience with managed ingestion tooling (Fivetran, Airbyte, or similar) and clear judgment about when to buy the connector and when to build it\n\n - Strong fluency with workflow orchestration — Temporal, Airflow, Dagster, or similar — operated at scale, not just configured\n\n - Strong programming skills in Python and advanced SQL\n\n - Experience building frameworks or internal tooling that other engineers use, and the product instinct to know when an abstraction is helping versus getting in the way\n\n - Practical experience with data quality, observability, and lineage tooling, and with schema evolution in systems that can't afford downtime\n\n - Working knowledge of data governance in a regulated environment: PII classification, masking, access control, retention, and data residency\n\n - Familiarity with cloud data services (Azure, AWS, GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, Pulumi)\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining scope where none exists\n   \n   \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with dbt and a close working relationship with analytics engineering teams\n\n - Experience with lakehouse architectures and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake) or query engines like Trino\n\n - Experience operating multi-tenant platforms with strict security, compliance, or data residency requirements\n\n - Exposure to data infrastructure for AI products\n\n - Prior experience as an early or founding data platform hire at a fast-growing company\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-AN2\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"5741cf3a-b86b-4a1b-8bf1-558c50bad9af","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"923c2eb2-9bfb-4dde-8d42-508c35996668","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"0293f12c-76d8-4f2d-86d0-0724ac41936c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5874db75-27a6-4727-9eda-a8eed3927c4b","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"da36fca6-0d0b-492e-b8d2-7a7f971f3e8e","title":"Customer Success Leader, Southern Europe & DACH","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Munich","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T10:10:33.766+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/da36fca6-0d0b-492e-b8d2-7a7f971f3e8e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/da36fca6-0d0b-492e-b8d2-7a7f971f3e8e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Enterprise Customer Success Leader, you are tasked with more than just facilitating the adoption of our technology. As a member of the broader Customer Success Leadership team, you will craft and execute a strategic vision for ensuring customers reach their desired outcomes, emphasizing scalability, process rigor, and the development of playbooks to fuel expansion and mitigate churn.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through empathetic leadership and a focus on value, you will spearhead efforts to enhance renewal and expansion rates, manage and develop talent, and drive forward customer relationships with proactive engagement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will also play an integral part in helping to drive strategy and execution in how we deliver an end-to-end excellent customer experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead by Example: Lead a dynamic customer success team towards exceptional performance, promoting a culture of accountability, execution, growth, and relentless improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scalability and Process: Develop and implement strategic improvements to drive scalable strategies and playbooks, ensuring a systematic approach to all stages of the customer journey, including: implementation, adoption, value realization, retention, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent Coaching and Development: Inspire and mentor your team, elevating their capabilities to become strategic partners through influencing and advising decision makers  and fostering customer advocacy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advance Customer Relationships: Deepen client engagements through strategic interactions, serving as an advisor and advocate for key stakeholders, driving advocacy, organic growth, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Retention: introduce processes and early warning systems to reduce churn, mitigate risk, and ensure we are multi-threaded within customer accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effective Collaboration: Work with leaders across the broader GTM organization, Product, and Engineering teams to deliver the voice-of-customer and drive a culture of customer-centricity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product Feedback: Ensure we develop a feedback flywheel, turning customer insights into meaningful product enhancements and service optimizations.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leadership Experience: You are a natural leader, with a proven background in leading high performing customer success teams within late-stage or post-IPO Enterprise SaaS organizations, with a specific emphasis on “Strategic”, “Large Enterprise / Enterprise”, and/or top-tier / lighthouse accounts with multi-million dollar spend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Acumen: Expertise in designing and executing customer success strategies that foster adoption, reduce churn, and promote expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathy and Influence: A leadership style characterized by empathy, with a proven track record in team development through hiring, coaching, and fostering talent.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outcome-Oriented: Exceptional ability to drive results through owning strategic initiatives, KPI reporting, and adept at navigating complex customer scenarios.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communication Mastery: Superior communication skills, capable of effectively engaging and influencing at all organizational levels both internally, and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agility: Capacity to excel in a rapidly expanding, dynamic setting and swiftly adjust to evolving requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Innovation:  A genuine passion for technology and innovation, constantly seeking novel solutions to complex challenges.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Enterprise Customer Success Leader, you are tasked with more than just facilitating the adoption of our technology. As a member of the broader Customer Success Leadership team, you will craft and execute a strategic vision for ensuring customers reach their desired outcomes, emphasizing scalability, process rigor, and the development of playbooks to fuel expansion and mitigate churn.\n\nThrough empathetic leadership and a focus on value, you will spearhead efforts to enhance renewal and expansion rates, manage and develop talent, and drive forward customer relationships with proactive engagement.\n\nYou will also play an integral part in helping to drive strategy and execution in how we deliver an end-to-end excellent customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead by Example: Lead a dynamic customer success team towards exceptional performance, promoting a culture of accountability, execution, growth, and relentless improvement.\n\n - Scalability and Process: Develop and implement strategic improvements to drive scalable strategies and playbooks, ensuring a systematic approach to all stages of the customer journey, including: implementation, adoption, value realization, retention, and expansion.\n\n - Talent Coaching and Development: Inspire and mentor your team, elevating their capabilities to become strategic partners through influencing and advising decision makers  and fostering customer advocacy.\n\n - Advance Customer Relationships: Deepen client engagements through strategic interactions, serving as an advisor and advocate for key stakeholders, driving advocacy, organic growth, and referrals.\n\n - Own Retention: introduce processes and early warning systems to reduce churn, mitigate risk, and ensure we are multi-threaded within customer accounts.\n\n - Effective Collaboration: Work with leaders across the broader GTM organization, Product, and Engineering teams to deliver the voice-of-customer and drive a culture of customer-centricity.\n\n - Product Feedback: Ensure we develop a feedback flywheel, turning customer insights into meaningful product enhancements and service optimizations.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Leadership Experience: You are a natural leader, with a proven background in leading high performing customer success teams within late-stage or post-IPO Enterprise SaaS organizations, with a specific emphasis on “Strategic”, “Large Enterprise / Enterprise”, and/or top-tier / lighthouse accounts with multi-million dollar spend.\n\n - Strategic Acumen: Expertise in designing and executing customer success strategies that foster adoption, reduce churn, and promote expansion.\n\n - Empathy and Influence: A leadership style characterized by empathy, with a proven track record in team development through hiring, coaching, and fostering talent.\n\n - Outcome-Oriented: Exceptional ability to drive results through owning strategic initiatives, KPI reporting, and adept at navigating complex customer scenarios.\n\n - Communication Mastery: Superior communication skills, capable of effectively engaging and influencing at all organizational levels both internally, and externally.\n\n - Agility: Capacity to excel in a rapidly expanding, dynamic setting and swiftly adjust to evolving requirements.\n\n - Innovation:  A genuine passion for technology and innovation, constantly seeking novel solutions to complex challenges.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5a1452ff-566c-4a80-905d-61281a02a40f","title":"Recruiting Coordinator","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T20:52:14.569+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5a1452ff-566c-4a80-905d-61281a02a40f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5a1452ff-566c-4a80-905d-61281a02a40f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Recruiting Coordinator joins Harvey's Talent team to support the company's rapidly growing hiring efforts across the business. The team is responsible for delivering a seamless, high-touch interview experience that reflects Harvey's brand and pace of growth. This role drives the operational backbone of recruiting — owning end-to-end interview coordination, candidate communications, and scheduling logistics for a fast-scaling office. The Recruiting Coordinator partners closely with recruiters, hiring managers, and cross-functional leaders across the US and globally to ensure every candidate interaction is thoughtful and efficient. It is a rare opportunity to help build the coordination function in one of Harvey's newest and most dynamic markets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end interview scheduling and coordination for roles across the G&amp;A, GTM, and Engineering, Product, and Design, ensuring a smooth and timely process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for candidates throughout the interview lifecycle, delivering an exceptional and on-brand experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with recruiters and hiring managers to manage interview logistics, panel selection, calendar coordination, and candidate communications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and continuously improve scheduling workflows, documentation, and coordination processes to support team efficiency and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding logistics and broader talent operations projects as the operations team scales</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in recruiting coordination, executive assistance, or a similar fast-paced operational role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a candidate-first mindset and the ability to represent Harvey's brand to external audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a hybrid environment and adapting quickly to shifting priorities in a high-growth setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with applicant tracking systems (e.g., Greenhouse) and modern scheduling tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, solutions-oriented approach with a bias toward action and continuous improvement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$80,000 - 125,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Recruiting Coordinator joins Harvey's Talent team to support the company's rapidly growing hiring efforts across the business. The team is responsible for delivering a seamless, high-touch interview experience that reflects Harvey's brand and pace of growth. This role drives the operational backbone of recruiting — owning end-to-end interview coordination, candidate communications, and scheduling logistics for a fast-scaling office. The Recruiting Coordinator partners closely with recruiters, hiring managers, and cross-functional leaders across the US and globally to ensure every candidate interaction is thoughtful and efficient. It is a rare opportunity to help build the coordination function in one of Harvey's newest and most dynamic markets.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end interview scheduling and coordination for roles across the G&A, GTM, and Engineering, Product, and Design, ensuring a smooth and timely process\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for candidates throughout the interview lifecycle, delivering an exceptional and on-brand experience\n\n - Partner with recruiters and hiring managers to manage interview logistics, panel selection, calendar coordination, and candidate communications\n\n - Maintain and continuously improve scheduling workflows, documentation, and coordination processes to support team efficiency and accuracy\n\n - Support onboarding logistics and broader talent operations projects as the operations team scales\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - 1–3 years of experience in recruiting coordination, executive assistance, or a similar fast-paced operational role\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines simultaneously\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a candidate-first mindset and the ability to represent Harvey's brand to external audiences\n\n - Comfort working in a hybrid environment and adapting quickly to shifting priorities in a high-growth setting\n\n - Experience with applicant tracking systems (e.g., Greenhouse) and modern scheduling tools\n\n - A proactive, solutions-oriented approach with a bias toward action and continuous improvement\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$80,000 - 125,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$80K – $125K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$80K - $125K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a7c6f7b1-02ca-4700-b3e8-a2f04b206c46","tierSummary":"Salary $80K – $125K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d8ba15ee-042f-4b05-a0d1-cbac9d7137ba","summary":"Salary $80K – $125K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":125000},{"id":"401bdf43-4905-45a0-bf14-54ac2271a2cc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":125000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"891889e0-0a4b-4496-85a6-3d42fb05304d","title":"Customer Success Leader, Southern Europe & DACH","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Paris","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T10:10:59.470+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"France"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/891889e0-0a4b-4496-85a6-3d42fb05304d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/891889e0-0a4b-4496-85a6-3d42fb05304d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Enterprise Customer Success Leader, you are tasked with more than just facilitating the adoption of our technology. As a member of the broader Customer Success Leadership team, you will craft and execute a strategic vision for ensuring customers reach their desired outcomes, emphasizing scalability, process rigor, and the development of playbooks to fuel expansion and mitigate churn.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through empathetic leadership and a focus on value, you will spearhead efforts to enhance renewal and expansion rates, manage and develop talent, and drive forward customer relationships with proactive engagement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will also play an integral part in helping to drive strategy and execution in how we deliver an end-to-end excellent customer experience.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead by Example: Lead a dynamic customer success team towards exceptional performance, promoting a culture of accountability, execution, growth, and relentless improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scalability and Process: Develop and implement strategic improvements to drive scalable strategies and playbooks, ensuring a systematic approach to all stages of the customer journey, including: implementation, adoption, value realization, retention, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent Coaching and Development: Inspire and mentor your team, elevating their capabilities to become strategic partners through influencing and advising decision makers  and fostering customer advocacy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advance Customer Relationships: Deepen client engagements through strategic interactions, serving as an advisor and advocate for key stakeholders, driving advocacy, organic growth, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Retention: introduce processes and early warning systems to reduce churn, mitigate risk, and ensure we are multi-threaded within customer accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effective Collaboration: Work with leaders across the broader GTM organization, Product, and Engineering teams to deliver the voice-of-customer and drive a culture of customer-centricity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product Feedback: Ensure we develop a feedback flywheel, turning customer insights into meaningful product enhancements and service optimizations.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leadership Experience: You are a natural leader, with a proven background in leading high performing customer success teams within late-stage or post-IPO Enterprise SaaS organizations, with a specific emphasis on “Strategic”, “Large Enterprise / Enterprise”, and/or top-tier / lighthouse accounts with multi-million dollar spend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Acumen: Expertise in designing and executing customer success strategies that foster adoption, reduce churn, and promote expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathy and Influence: A leadership style characterized by empathy, with a proven track record in team development through hiring, coaching, and fostering talent.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outcome-Oriented: Exceptional ability to drive results through owning strategic initiatives, KPI reporting, and adept at navigating complex customer scenarios.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communication Mastery: Superior communication skills, capable of effectively engaging and influencing at all organizational levels both internally, and externally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agility: Capacity to excel in a rapidly expanding, dynamic setting and swiftly adjust to evolving requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Innovation:  A genuine passion for technology and innovation, constantly seeking novel solutions to complex challenges.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs the Enterprise Customer Success Leader, you are tasked with more than just facilitating the adoption of our technology. As a member of the broader Customer Success Leadership team, you will craft and execute a strategic vision for ensuring customers reach their desired outcomes, emphasizing scalability, process rigor, and the development of playbooks to fuel expansion and mitigate churn.\n\nThrough empathetic leadership and a focus on value, you will spearhead efforts to enhance renewal and expansion rates, manage and develop talent, and drive forward customer relationships with proactive engagement.\n\nYou will also play an integral part in helping to drive strategy and execution in how we deliver an end-to-end excellent customer experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead by Example: Lead a dynamic customer success team towards exceptional performance, promoting a culture of accountability, execution, growth, and relentless improvement.\n\n - Scalability and Process: Develop and implement strategic improvements to drive scalable strategies and playbooks, ensuring a systematic approach to all stages of the customer journey, including: implementation, adoption, value realization, retention, and expansion.\n\n - Talent Coaching and Development: Inspire and mentor your team, elevating their capabilities to become strategic partners through influencing and advising decision makers  and fostering customer advocacy.\n\n - Advance Customer Relationships: Deepen client engagements through strategic interactions, serving as an advisor and advocate for key stakeholders, driving advocacy, organic growth, and referrals.\n\n - Own Retention: introduce processes and early warning systems to reduce churn, mitigate risk, and ensure we are multi-threaded within customer accounts.\n\n - Effective Collaboration: Work with leaders across the broader GTM organization, Product, and Engineering teams to deliver the voice-of-customer and drive a culture of customer-centricity.\n\n - Product Feedback: Ensure we develop a feedback flywheel, turning customer insights into meaningful product enhancements and service optimizations.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Leadership Experience: You are a natural leader, with a proven background in leading high performing customer success teams within late-stage or post-IPO Enterprise SaaS organizations, with a specific emphasis on “Strategic”, “Large Enterprise / Enterprise”, and/or top-tier / lighthouse accounts with multi-million dollar spend.\n\n - Strategic Acumen: Expertise in designing and executing customer success strategies that foster adoption, reduce churn, and promote expansion.\n\n - Empathy and Influence: A leadership style characterized by empathy, with a proven track record in team development through hiring, coaching, and fostering talent.\n\n - Outcome-Oriented: Exceptional ability to drive results through owning strategic initiatives, KPI reporting, and adept at navigating complex customer scenarios.\n\n - Communication Mastery: Superior communication skills, capable of effectively engaging and influencing at all organizational levels both internally, and externally.\n\n - Agility: Capacity to excel in a rapidly expanding, dynamic setting and swiftly adjust to evolving requirements.\n\n - Innovation:  A genuine passion for technology and innovation, constantly seeking novel solutions to complex challenges.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-JM1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b63348d7-af4f-4030-83d7-663b495bfacc","title":"Recruiting Coordinator","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T20:52:56.090+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b63348d7-af4f-4030-83d7-663b495bfacc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b63348d7-af4f-4030-83d7-663b495bfacc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Recruiting Coordinator joins Harvey's Talent team to support the company's rapidly growing hiring efforts across the business. The team is responsible for delivering a seamless, high-touch interview experience that reflects Harvey's brand and pace of growth. This role drives the operational backbone of recruiting — owning end-to-end interview coordination, candidate communications, and scheduling logistics for a fast-scaling office. The Recruiting Coordinator partners closely with recruiters, hiring managers, and cross-functional leaders across the US and globally to ensure every candidate interaction is thoughtful and efficient. It is a rare opportunity to help build the coordination function in one of Harvey's newest and most dynamic markets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end interview scheduling and coordination for roles across the G&amp;A, GTM, and Engineering, Product, and Design, ensuring a smooth and timely process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for candidates throughout the interview lifecycle, delivering an exceptional and on-brand experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with recruiters and hiring managers to manage interview logistics, panel selection, calendar coordination, and candidate communications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and continuously improve scheduling workflows, documentation, and coordination processes to support team efficiency and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding logistics and broader talent operations projects as the operations team scales</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have </strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in recruiting coordination, executive assistance, or a similar fast-paced operational role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a candidate-first mindset and the ability to represent Harvey's brand to external audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a hybrid environment and adapting quickly to shifting priorities in a high-growth setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with applicant tracking systems (e.g., Greenhouse) and modern scheduling tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, solutions-oriented approach with a bias toward action and continuous improvement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$80,000 - 125,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Recruiting Coordinator joins Harvey's Talent team to support the company's rapidly growing hiring efforts across the business. The team is responsible for delivering a seamless, high-touch interview experience that reflects Harvey's brand and pace of growth. This role drives the operational backbone of recruiting — owning end-to-end interview coordination, candidate communications, and scheduling logistics for a fast-scaling office. The Recruiting Coordinator partners closely with recruiters, hiring managers, and cross-functional leaders across the US and globally to ensure every candidate interaction is thoughtful and efficient. It is a rare opportunity to help build the coordination function in one of Harvey's newest and most dynamic markets.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own end-to-end interview scheduling and coordination for roles across the G&A, GTM, and Engineering, Product, and Design, ensuring a smooth and timely process\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for candidates throughout the interview lifecycle, delivering an exceptional and on-brand experience\n\n - Partner with recruiters and hiring managers to manage interview logistics, panel selection, calendar coordination, and candidate communications\n\n - Maintain and continuously improve scheduling workflows, documentation, and coordination processes to support team efficiency and accuracy\n\n - Support onboarding logistics and broader talent operations projects as the operations team scales\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE \n\n - 1–3 years of experience in recruiting coordination, executive assistance, or a similar fast-paced operational role\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines simultaneously\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a candidate-first mindset and the ability to represent Harvey's brand to external audiences\n\n - Comfort working in a hybrid environment and adapting quickly to shifting priorities in a high-growth setting\n\n - Experience with applicant tracking systems (e.g., Greenhouse) and modern scheduling tools\n\n - A proactive, solutions-oriented approach with a bias toward action and continuous improvement\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$80,000 - 125,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$80K – $125K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$80K - $125K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a7c6f7b1-02ca-4700-b3e8-a2f04b206c46","tierSummary":"Salary $80K – $125K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d8ba15ee-042f-4b05-a0d1-cbac9d7137ba","summary":"Salary $80K – $125K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":125000},{"id":"401bdf43-4905-45a0-bf14-54ac2271a2cc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":125000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"02005c77-4871-4100-8030-27aa08ed7aa7","title":"Sr. Systems Engineer, Client Engineering","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T19:59:49.596+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/02005c77-4871-4100-8030-27aa08ed7aa7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/02005c77-4871-4100-8030-27aa08ed7aa7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey runs on a fleet of Macs and Windows devices, and every one of them is the front door to how each Harvey employee does their work. We're seeking a Senior Systems Engineer to own client engineering end to end - Jamf, Intune, Autopilot, Okta device trust, and more, and the automation that ties them together. This is the person who decides how a laptop gets built, secured, patched, recovered, and retired, and who makes those decisions hold up as we scale across offices globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate has run a production device management environment at scale and can move between writing the deployment tooling, debugging a broken enrollment, and pushing for improvements to policy, process, and systems along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the endpoint platform.</strong> Jamf Pro for macOS, Intune and Autopilot for Windows, and the mobile fleet alongside them. You set configuration standards, patching cadence, and compliance baselines in partnership with Security, and you're accountable for the fleet actually meeting them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engineer the device lifecycle.</strong> Zero-touch provisioning through Apple Business Manager and Autopilot, automated onboarding and offboarding, hardware refreshes, DLP, and forensics. Where the lifecycle still depends on someone remembering to do something, replace that with code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the automation the fleet runs on.</strong> Most of this role's leverage comes from tooling - Python and scripts against Jamf, Intune, and Okta APIs, event-driven workflows, and self-service that lets employees fix their own problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with Security on endpoint posture.</strong> Work directly with Security on endpoint policies, EDR coverage, device trust and Okta FastPass, disk encryption and key escrow, browser management, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be the final escalation for endpoint issues.</strong> IT Operations handles tier 1 and 2 globally; the problems that reach you are the strange ones. You'll fix them, and then fix the class of problem so the next person doesn't file the ticket.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support a global, in-person-heavy company.</strong> Harvey has offices across the US, EMEA, and APAC. You'll build for time zones you aren't in, and document and train the team well enough that someone in each location can resolve issues independently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 5 years in endpoint, client, or IT systems engineering, including direct ownership of a macOS MDM environment at 1000+ devices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on Jamf experience, plus real Windows management experience via Intune, Autopilot, and Entra.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong scripting and automation ability in Python, Bash, or Swift, with a track record of building tooling against vendor APIs rather than clicking through admin consoles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working fluency with an IdP, Okta preferred, covering SSO, MFA, device trust, and how identity and endpoint policy interact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running endpoint security tooling in a production environment - CrowdStrike or equivalent EDR, managed Chrome Enterprise, DLP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Endpoint work inside a compliance program (SOC 2, ISO 27001).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$153,000 - $210,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey runs on a fleet of Macs and Windows devices, and every one of them is the front door to how each Harvey employee does their work. We're seeking a Senior Systems Engineer to own client engineering end to end - Jamf, Intune, Autopilot, Okta device trust, and more, and the automation that ties them together. This is the person who decides how a laptop gets built, secured, patched, recovered, and retired, and who makes those decisions hold up as we scale across offices globally.\n\nThe ideal candidate has run a production device management environment at scale and can move between writing the deployment tooling, debugging a broken enrollment, and pushing for improvements to policy, process, and systems along the way.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the endpoint platform. Jamf Pro for macOS, Intune and Autopilot for Windows, and the mobile fleet alongside them. You set configuration standards, patching cadence, and compliance baselines in partnership with Security, and you're accountable for the fleet actually meeting them.\n\n - Engineer the device lifecycle. Zero-touch provisioning through Apple Business Manager and Autopilot, automated onboarding and offboarding, hardware refreshes, DLP, and forensics. Where the lifecycle still depends on someone remembering to do something, replace that with code.\n\n - Build the automation the fleet runs on. Most of this role's leverage comes from tooling - Python and scripts against Jamf, Intune, and Okta APIs, event-driven workflows, and self-service that lets employees fix their own problems.\n\n - Partner with Security on endpoint posture. Work directly with Security on endpoint policies, EDR coverage, device trust and Okta FastPass, disk encryption and key escrow, browser management, and more.\n\n - Be the final escalation for endpoint issues. IT Operations handles tier 1 and 2 globally; the problems that reach you are the strange ones. You'll fix them, and then fix the class of problem so the next person doesn't file the ticket.\n\n - Support a global, in-person-heavy company. Harvey has offices across the US, EMEA, and APAC. You'll build for time zones you aren't in, and document and train the team well enough that someone in each location can resolve issues independently.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 5 years in endpoint, client, or IT systems engineering, including direct ownership of a macOS MDM environment at 1000+ devices.\n\n - Deep hands-on Jamf experience, plus real Windows management experience via Intune, Autopilot, and Entra.\n\n - Strong scripting and automation ability in Python, Bash, or Swift, with a track record of building tooling against vendor APIs rather than clicking through admin consoles.\n\n - Working fluency with an IdP, Okta preferred, covering SSO, MFA, device trust, and how identity and endpoint policy interact.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\n\nBONUS POINTS:\n\n - Experience running endpoint security tooling in a production environment - CrowdStrike or equivalent EDR, managed Chrome Enterprise, DLP.\n\n - Endpoint work inside a compliance program (SOC 2, ISO 27001).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$153,000 - $210,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$153K – $210.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$153K - $210.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a01b1b0b-123b-4eb4-a6b7-654375da58ef","tierSummary":"$153K – $210.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2aadb0d6-8d50-42c3-a372-3e58ac066771","summary":"$153K – $210.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":153000,"maxValue":210500},{"id":"da700d2d-16a8-4f92-879b-567aaa9aff3f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"36ea67fc-9322-4bd5-955b-c6db600533a3","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":153000,"maxValue":210500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d926b184-364b-49f5-a269-bef158c1c408","title":"Sr. Systems Engineer, Client Engineering","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T19:59:51.674+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d926b184-364b-49f5-a269-bef158c1c408","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d926b184-364b-49f5-a269-bef158c1c408/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey runs on a fleet of Macs and Windows devices, and every one of them is the front door to how each Harvey employee does their work. We're seeking a Senior Systems Engineer to own client engineering end to end - Jamf, Intune, Autopilot, Okta device trust, and more, and the automation that ties them together. This is the person who decides how a laptop gets built, secured, patched, recovered, and retired, and who makes those decisions hold up as we scale across offices globally.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate has run a production device management environment at scale and can move between writing the deployment tooling, debugging a broken enrollment, and pushing for improvements to policy, process, and systems along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the endpoint platform.</strong> Jamf Pro for macOS, Intune and Autopilot for Windows, and the mobile fleet alongside them. You set configuration standards, patching cadence, and compliance baselines in partnership with Security, and you're accountable for the fleet actually meeting them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engineer the device lifecycle.</strong> Zero-touch provisioning through Apple Business Manager and Autopilot, automated onboarding and offboarding, hardware refreshes, DLP, and forensics. Where the lifecycle still depends on someone remembering to do something, replace that with code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the automation the fleet runs on.</strong> Most of this role's leverage comes from tooling - Python and scripts against Jamf, Intune, and Okta APIs, event-driven workflows, and self-service that lets employees fix their own problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with Security on endpoint posture.</strong> Work directly with Security on endpoint policies, EDR coverage, device trust and Okta FastPass, disk encryption and key escrow, browser management, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be the final escalation for endpoint issues.</strong> IT Operations handles tier 1 and 2 globally; the problems that reach you are the strange ones. You'll fix them, and then fix the class of problem so the next person doesn't file the ticket.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support a global, in-person-heavy company.</strong> Harvey has offices across the US, EMEA, and APAC. You'll build for time zones you aren't in, and document and train the team well enough that someone in each location can resolve issues independently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 5 years in endpoint, client, or IT systems engineering, including direct ownership of a macOS MDM environment at 1000+ devices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on Jamf experience, plus real Windows management experience via Intune, Autopilot, and Entra.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong scripting and automation ability in Python, Bash, or Swift, with a track record of building tooling against vendor APIs rather than clicking through admin consoles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working fluency with an IdP, Okta preferred, covering SSO, MFA, device trust, and how identity and endpoint policy interact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running endpoint security tooling in a production environment - CrowdStrike or equivalent EDR, managed Chrome Enterprise, DLP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Endpoint work inside a compliance program (SOC 2, ISO 27001).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$153,000 - $210,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey runs on a fleet of Macs and Windows devices, and every one of them is the front door to how each Harvey employee does their work. We're seeking a Senior Systems Engineer to own client engineering end to end - Jamf, Intune, Autopilot, Okta device trust, and more, and the automation that ties them together. This is the person who decides how a laptop gets built, secured, patched, recovered, and retired, and who makes those decisions hold up as we scale across offices globally.\n\nThe ideal candidate has run a production device management environment at scale and can move between writing the deployment tooling, debugging a broken enrollment, and pushing for improvements to policy, process, and systems along the way.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the endpoint platform. Jamf Pro for macOS, Intune and Autopilot for Windows, and the mobile fleet alongside them. You set configuration standards, patching cadence, and compliance baselines in partnership with Security, and you're accountable for the fleet actually meeting them.\n\n - Engineer the device lifecycle. Zero-touch provisioning through Apple Business Manager and Autopilot, automated onboarding and offboarding, hardware refreshes, DLP, and forensics. Where the lifecycle still depends on someone remembering to do something, replace that with code.\n\n - Build the automation the fleet runs on. Most of this role's leverage comes from tooling - Python and scripts against Jamf, Intune, and Okta APIs, event-driven workflows, and self-service that lets employees fix their own problems.\n\n - Partner with Security on endpoint posture. Work directly with Security on endpoint policies, EDR coverage, device trust and Okta FastPass, disk encryption and key escrow, browser management, and more.\n\n - Be the final escalation for endpoint issues. IT Operations handles tier 1 and 2 globally; the problems that reach you are the strange ones. You'll fix them, and then fix the class of problem so the next person doesn't file the ticket.\n\n - Support a global, in-person-heavy company. Harvey has offices across the US, EMEA, and APAC. You'll build for time zones you aren't in, and document and train the team well enough that someone in each location can resolve issues independently.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Minimum 5 years in endpoint, client, or IT systems engineering, including direct ownership of a macOS MDM environment at 1000+ devices.\n\n - Deep hands-on Jamf experience, plus real Windows management experience via Intune, Autopilot, and Entra.\n\n - Strong scripting and automation ability in Python, Bash, or Swift, with a track record of building tooling against vendor APIs rather than clicking through admin consoles.\n\n - Working fluency with an IdP, Okta preferred, covering SSO, MFA, device trust, and how identity and endpoint policy interact.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, especially with non-technical teams.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and global environment.\n\n\nBONUS POINTS:\n\n - Experience running endpoint security tooling in a production environment - CrowdStrike or equivalent EDR, managed Chrome Enterprise, DLP.\n\n - Endpoint work inside a compliance program (SOC 2, ISO 27001).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$153,000 - $210,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$153K – $210.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$153K - $210.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"378d728b-3abe-47f2-918c-7473ee418b08","tierSummary":"$153K – $210.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"79574c8d-a605-4132-a7f6-370970185173","summary":"$153K – $210.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":153000,"maxValue":210500},{"id":"b896f435-4465-429b-a4d7-273678a39a32","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"85ae80ab-1deb-46a7-a2c1-e91f2cb77ed6","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":153000,"maxValue":210500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5d13546d-9cd6-4aed-a520-93fdc945f5fc","title":"Senior Business Recruiter, GTM","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:12:33.060+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5d13546d-9cd6-4aed-a520-93fdc945f5fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5d13546d-9cd6-4aed-a520-93fdc945f5fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$126,400 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.\n\n - Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.\n\n - Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.\n\n - Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.\n\n - Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.\n\n - Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.\n\n - Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$126,400 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-NB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$126.4K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fd50dcda-5e97-424c-acee-5c30dfc8131a","tierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e029c6f1-0c5c-405f-b8d8-e07f14339f4d","summary":"$126.4K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"112e3abb-6c2e-48de-b5f4-5a515e0b1cae","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"66f5e8fc-a896-4d64-9dfe-8e51c186ead2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e6c2aef1-4ed9-4b21-abed-36846ccdadca","title":"Senior Business Recruiter, GTM","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:12:45.339+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e6c2aef1-4ed9-4b21-abed-36846ccdadca","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/e6c2aef1-4ed9-4b21-abed-36846ccdadca/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$126,400 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.\n\n - Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.\n\n - Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.\n\n - Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.\n\n - Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.\n\n - Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.\n\n - Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$126,400 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-NB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$126.4K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"55aa39a8-f69c-46f6-913c-46b76c627530","tierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7238207c-644e-4ee2-835d-b9546967a362","summary":"$126.4K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"7f66377e-f180-4f2f-b46f-9d9860bb9be0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"008af7df-227b-4e3b-8208-148c900d82a2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6fc91ace-0467-4400-be50-b4d11f817b9e","title":"Senior Business Recruiter, GTM","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:12:42.399+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCoun