ull-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$126,400 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.\n\n - Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.\n\n - Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.\n\n - Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.\n\n - Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.\n\n - Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.\n\n - Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$126,400 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-NB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$126.4K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1935b353-49da-4494-b539-33240d82049c","tierSummary":"$126.4K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f4b14758-658b-4168-aaca-bf54ece221c0","summary":"$126.4K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"9b302250-71d4-4ea6-a92b-3dfd172375fc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e14c9dec-385d-431b-96bd-315f778a49c0","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":126400,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"51b1579a-7a75-42c0-bf26-516543c4e251","title":"Senior Business Recruiter, GTM","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Toronto","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:12:38.021+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/51b1579a-7a75-42c0-bf26-516543c4e251","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/51b1579a-7a75-42c0-bf26-516543c4e251/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Business Recruiter, GTM partners with Harvey's go-to-market leadership to attract and close top talent across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations. Sitting within the Talent organization under the North America Business Recruiting team, this role owns full-cycle recruiting for some of Harvey's highest-volume and most strategically critical functions. The Senior Business Recruiter drives hiring velocity and pipeline quality while operating as a trusted advisor to hiring managers navigating rapid growth across multiple geographies. They partner cross-functionally with Recruiting Operations, People Business Partners, and Sales leadership to ensure process rigor without sacrificing speed or candidate experience. This is an opportunity to shape how a category-defining AI company builds its revenue engine during a period of exceptional growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, Partnerships, and Revenue Operations — from sourcing through close — across multiple North American locations.\n\n - Build and maintain high-quality, diverse candidate pipelines through proactive sourcing, referral cultivation, and market mapping.\n\n - Serve as a strategic partner to hiring managers: leading intake meetings, setting calibration bars, advising on market conditions, and resetting expectations when needed.\n\n - Drive process improvement and operational excellence — identifying bottlenecks, implementing scalable workflows, and tracking recruiting metrics to inform decisions.\n\n - Manage competing priorities across multiple open requisitions while maintaining a high-touch candidate experience and meeting aggressive hiring timelines.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a meaningful portion supporting GTM or business functions (Sales, CS, RevOps, Partnerships) at a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to partner with senior hiring managers, influence decisions with data, and manage stakeholder expectations in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Strong sourcing toolkit and a creative approach to building pipelines in competitive talent markets.\n\n - Excellent project management skills with the ability to juggle multiple requisitions, drive process improvements, and maintain attention to detail under pressure.\n\n - Clear, confident communication skills and high emotional intelligence — comfortable navigating ambiguity and competing priorities with poise.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-NB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"940d071d-5093-44f3-97c8-afa5b78cd869","title":"Director Global Benefits","department":"Human Resources","team":"Total Rewards","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T23:57:52.399+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/940d071d-5093-44f3-97c8-afa5b78cd869","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/940d071d-5093-44f3-97c8-afa5b78cd869/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy and plan design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team and service delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs, vendors, and spend</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>10+ years in benefits</strong>, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep US benefits expertise</strong> across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real international experience</strong>: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor and broker management</strong>: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial fluency</strong>: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication</strong>: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mentality.</strong> You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI experience.</strong> You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$227,100 - $310,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.\n\n\n\nThis is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nStrategy and plan design\n\n - Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.\n\n - Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.\n\n - Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.\n\nTeam and service delivery\n\n - Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.\n\n - Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.\n\n - Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.\n\nPrograms, vendors, and spend\n\n - Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.\n\n - Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.\n\n - Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.\n\n - Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.\n\n - Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in benefits, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Deep US benefits expertise across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).\n\n - Real international experience: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.\n\n - Strategic and hands-on: You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.\n\n - Vendor and broker management: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.\n\n - Financial fluency: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.\n\n - Exceptional communication: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.\n\n - Builder mentality. You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.\n\n - AI experience. You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$227,100 - $310,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$227.1K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e2b3f5a4-b4f4-4daf-b3d7-ba168d91b725","tierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9539264d-cd2a-4b0d-af5d-a3ede6ccacc5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"aa98f918-6afa-4cd6-8a54-bd175b494857","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a725564e-b598-4d2e-a9b6-9d79a88451cd","summary":"$227.1K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"c9432042-1f8c-4de0-82c0-9a4ecce71cf6","title":"Director Global Benefits","department":"Human Resources","team":"Total Rewards","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-29T00:01:47.793+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c9432042-1f8c-4de0-82c0-9a4ecce71cf6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c9432042-1f8c-4de0-82c0-9a4ecce71cf6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy and plan design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team and service delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs, vendors, and spend</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>10+ years in benefits</strong>, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep US benefits expertise</strong> across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real international experience</strong>: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor and broker management</strong>: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial fluency</strong>: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication</strong>: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mentality.</strong> You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI experience.</strong> You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$227,100 - $310,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.\n\n\n\nThis is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nStrategy and plan design\n\n - Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.\n\n - Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.\n\n - Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.\n\nTeam and service delivery\n\n - Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.\n\n - Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.\n\n - Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.\n\nPrograms, vendors, and spend\n\n - Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.\n\n - Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.\n\n - Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.\n\n - Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.\n\n - Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in benefits, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Deep US benefits expertise across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).\n\n - Real international experience: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.\n\n - Strategic and hands-on: You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.\n\n - Vendor and broker management: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.\n\n - Financial fluency: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.\n\n - Exceptional communication: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.\n\n - Builder mentality. You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.\n\n - AI experience. You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$227,100 - $310,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$227.1K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4d8557e5-e233-45d5-85f9-74679475132b","tierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b4d83163-c9ce-488b-af5d-f95f1be05117","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"93cc3650-ffd3-4834-892b-14070785bf69","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cdf2d31b-492d-4d32-9176-f9b1142116a1","summary":"$227.1K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"5f1aea02-8e48-4adc-9e6a-51f9645bef70","title":"Director Global Benefits","department":"Human Resources","team":"Total Rewards","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T14:54:20.482+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5f1aea02-8e48-4adc-9e6a-51f9645bef70","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/5f1aea02-8e48-4adc-9e6a-51f9645bef70/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy and plan design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team and service delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs, vendors, and spend</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>10+ years in benefits</strong>, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep US benefits expertise</strong> across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real international experience</strong>: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor and broker management</strong>: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial fluency</strong>: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication</strong>: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mentality.</strong> You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI experience.</strong> You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$227,100 - $310,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.\n\n\n\nThis is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nStrategy and plan design\n\n - Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.\n\n - Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.\n\n - Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.\n\nTeam and service delivery\n\n - Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.\n\n - Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.\n\n - Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.\n\nPrograms, vendors, and spend\n\n - Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.\n\n - Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.\n\n - Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.\n\n - Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.\n\n - Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in benefits, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Deep US benefits expertise across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).\n\n - Real international experience: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.\n\n - Strategic and hands-on: You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.\n\n - Vendor and broker management: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.\n\n - Financial fluency: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.\n\n - Exceptional communication: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.\n\n - Builder mentality. You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.\n\n - AI experience. You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$227,100 - $310,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$227.1K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e15876ce-a656-4c12-9811-ed798cdf572a","tierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8b0b6639-32aa-4daf-9b7c-0c0c41465cbc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8002353b-b587-4e02-b0a3-a89fd27bf8d2","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6a4767bf-fb31-4b1c-bde4-55ac81879b7b","summary":"$227.1K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"c550bb3a-8bfa-4a8f-93de-a00df94c6bbe","title":"Director Global Benefits","department":"Human Resources","team":"Total Rewards","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T14:54:15.751+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c550bb3a-8bfa-4a8f-93de-a00df94c6bbe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c550bb3a-8bfa-4a8f-93de-a00df94c6bbe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy and plan design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team and service delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programs, vendors, and spend</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>10+ years in benefits</strong>, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep US benefits expertise</strong> across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real international experience</strong>: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor and broker management</strong>: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial fluency</strong>: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication</strong>: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mentality.</strong> You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI experience.</strong> You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$227,100 - $310,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-BL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is scaling fast across headcount, geographies, and the complexity that comes with both. Our benefits and leave programs are now the daily, tangible experience of working here for employees in a dozen countries, and they need an owner who can lead them at that scale.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for our first Director of Global Benefits to own Harvey's benefits and leave of absence strategy end to end, building on the foundations we have as we head into the next phase of our growth. You'll set the philosophy and stay close enough to the work to know whether a plan design holds up in practice.\n\n\n\nThis is a player/coach role for someone who has built and run a global benefits function before, ideally in a fast-scaling environment. You'll manage and grow our global benefits team, while engaging deeply in our highest-stakes workstreams: annual renewals, open enrollment, new-country launches, and the vendor relationships that underpin it all. You'll also own how benefits support feels day to day. Most employees meet this function through a single question at a stressful moment, and how that's handled matters as much as the plan design behind it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to our Head of Total Rewards and partner closely with People Operations, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and Recruiting.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nStrategy and plan design\n\n - Define Harvey's global benefits and leave philosophy, including what \"global consistency, local relevance\" means as we enter new markets.\n\n - Lead plan design and redesign across the US and our international footprint (10+ markets and growing), balancing employee impact, competitiveness, and cost.\n\n - Build a program roadmap and business case for benefits, wellness, and leave, grounded in benchmarking and market analysis.\n\nTeam and service delivery\n\n - Grow and develop the global benefits team across the US and EMEA, setting priorities, raising the operating bar, and creating room for people to stretch.\n\n - Set and hold the standard for service delivery: response times, escalation, and follow-through on employee questions. Use AI and automation to take volume off the team without letting the experience get more distant.\n\n - Make our benefits legible, with clear, honest, localized communication so employees use what we offer and a partnership with Recruiting that makes our benefits a real differentiator in candidate conversations.\n\nPrograms, vendors, and spend\n\n - Oversee the annual cycle end to end: renewals, open enrollment, plan changes, carrier transitions, and new-country benefit launches.\n\n - Lead the global leave of absence program with consistency and care as volume scales.\n\n - Hold brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators to account globally, including RFPs, negotiations, contracting, and performance management.\n\n - Ensure compliance with local regulations in each market, partnering with Legal, Security, and Finance on vendor onboarding, data privacy, and risk review.\n\n - Manage the benefits budget with Finance and leverage utilization, cost, and sentiment data to decide what changes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years in benefits, including 3+ years leading and developing a team, ideally in a high-growth technology company.\n\n - Deep US benefits expertise across health and welfare plan design, 401(k), leave, and the compliance landscape (ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA and state equivalents).\n\n - Real international experience: you've designed or administered benefits in EMEA and/or APAC and understand that statutory minimums are a floor, not a program.\n\n - Strategic and hands-on: You can present a plan-design recommendation to executives in the morning and untangle a Workday eligibility rule in the afternoon.\n\n - Vendor and broker management: You've run RFPs, negotiated renewals, and held partners accountable across a fragmented global vendor landscape.\n\n - Financial fluency: You can build and defend a benefits budget, model cost scenarios, and explain the tradeoffs plainly.\n\n - Exceptional communication: You translate complexity into clarity for employees, executives, and everyone in between.\n\n - Builder mentality. You're energized by ambiguity and by programs that don't exist yet.\n\n - AI experience. You’re using AI tools to streamline benefits work. We believe AI can meaningfully expand what a small benefits team can deliver, and we want someone who shares that belief.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$227,100 - $310,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-BL1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$227.1K - $310K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a76e9121-4fa3-403e-a295-da2030912793","tierSummary":"$227.1K – $310K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6820b403-5dd0-460f-bdce-8e41359ff1a5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"bad3ada2-6b7b-4b0f-9ff5-91153b7d4c46","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"30a0dd62-9e59-40f8-9391-26c59dd1b496","summary":"$227.1K – $310K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":227100,"maxValue":310000}]}},{"id":"6c95865e-0803-47c2-889d-103afa385b53","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise (Public Sector - Federal)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Washington DC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T12:57:09.023+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6c95865e-0803-47c2-889d-103afa385b53","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/6c95865e-0803-47c2-889d-103afa385b53/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Account Executive on Harvey's Federal team, you will own a named list of United States federal agencies and drive adoption of Harvey across their legal organizations. Federal legal work — litigation, investigations, FOIA, procurement, and regulatory drafting — is exactly the work Harvey is built for, and the agencies doing it are largely untouched by AI today. You will run the full cycle: prospecting into agency general counsel and component leadership, navigating security review and authorization, selecting the right procurement path, and closing. This is an early seat on a new team, so you will help write the playbook as you sell.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a named list of federal agencies and components, and run the full sales cycle from prospecting through contracting, onboarding, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets and pipeline generation metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multi-thread across agency general counsel, component leadership, CIO and CISO organizations, and contracting officers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Select and drive the right procurement path for each opportunity — direct award, GSA schedule, GWAC, OTA, or reseller — in partnership with the Head of Public Sector.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the security review workstream with Harvey's Security and Compliance team, including FedRAMP artifacts and agency-specific questionnaires.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and execute against the federal fiscal calendar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run product demonstrations for agency legal teams and translate Harvey's capability into mission outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document learnings into a repeatable federal playbook.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years selling complex enterprise software, with a meaningful portion of that time carrying a federal quota.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Closed federal deals yourself, through at least one of direct award, GSA schedule, GWAC, OTA, or reseller channel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience navigating agency security review and authorization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with the federal buying calendar and the ability to manage a cycle that spans it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional detail discipline. Federal deals are lost on paperwork, security questionnaires, and missed procurement windows, not on demos.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuinely excited to prospect, and capable of independently running a cycle end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong consultative, value-based selling instincts, and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated interest in AI and in helping government lawyers do their work better.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice to Have</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships in federal agency legal or CIO organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience selling into legal departments or to law firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a company that achieved FedRAMP authorization while you were selling there.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$400,000 USD; OTE 50/50<br /><br /></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD2</p><h3></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs an Enterprise Account Executive on Harvey's Federal team, you will own a named list of United States federal agencies and drive adoption of Harvey across their legal organizations. Federal legal work — litigation, investigations, FOIA, procurement, and regulatory drafting — is exactly the work Harvey is built for, and the agencies doing it are largely untouched by AI today. You will run the full cycle: prospecting into agency general counsel and component leadership, navigating security review and authorization, selecting the right procurement path, and closing. This is an early seat on a new team, so you will help write the playbook as you sell.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own a named list of federal agencies and components, and run the full sales cycle from prospecting through contracting, onboarding, and expansion.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets and pipeline generation metrics.\n\n - Multi-thread across agency general counsel, component leadership, CIO and CISO organizations, and contracting officers.\n\n - Select and drive the right procurement path for each opportunity — direct award, GSA schedule, GWAC, OTA, or reseller — in partnership with the Head of Public Sector.\n\n - Own the security review workstream with Harvey's Security and Compliance team, including FedRAMP artifacts and agency-specific questionnaires.\n\n - Plan and execute against the federal fiscal calendar.\n\n - Run product demonstrations for agency legal teams and translate Harvey's capability into mission outcomes.\n\n - Document learnings into a repeatable federal playbook.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years selling complex enterprise software, with a meaningful portion of that time carrying a federal quota.\n\n - Closed federal deals yourself, through at least one of direct award, GSA schedule, GWAC, OTA, or reseller channel.\n\n - Practical experience navigating agency security review and authorization.\n\n - Fluency with the federal buying calendar and the ability to manage a cycle that spans it.\n\n - Exceptional detail discipline. Federal deals are lost on paperwork, security questionnaires, and missed procurement windows, not on demos.\n\n - Genuinely excited to prospect, and capable of independently running a cycle end to end.\n\n - Strong consultative, value-based selling instincts, and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated interest in AI and in helping government lawyers do their work better.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Existing relationships in federal agency legal or CIO organizations.\n\n - Prior experience selling into legal departments or to law firms.\n\n - Experience at a company that achieved FedRAMP authorization while you were selling there.\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$400,000 USD; OTE 50/50\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AD2\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$400K • Offers Equity • OTE 50/50","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$400K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6cf997d7-35aa-4723-839b-bdfb5b5f815c","tierSummary":"$400K • Offers Equity • OTE 50/50","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE 50/50","components":[{"id":"24da66ff-e9a3-4bc8-88dd-7c31da3ed34c","summary":"$400K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":400000},{"id":"b4bbba54-598e-47d5-943c-4f828958a22c","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":400000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9b76c7e3-4c05-47c6-852c-60b6e1e2ef16","title":"Scaled Customer Success Manager, EMEA","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T19:10:06.067+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9b76c7e3-4c05-47c6-852c-60b6e1e2ef16","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9b76c7e3-4c05-47c6-852c-60b6e1e2ef16/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Scaled Customer Success Manager joins Harvey's Scaled Customer Success team to drive retention, renewal, and expansion outcomes across a high-volume book of business. The team's mission is to deliver strategic, efficient value at scale—ensuring customers adopt Harvey's AI solutions deeply and renew with confidence. This role owns the full commercial lifecycle for a portfolio of accounts, blending consultative customer engagement with a data-driven renewals motion to maximize net revenue retention. Scaled CSMs partners closely with Sales, Legal Engineering, and Product to translate customer feedback into roadmap influence and expansion opportunity. It is a rare opportunity to shape a growing function at the intersection of AI innovation and customer value delivery.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own renewals and expansions across a named portfolio of accounts, driving net revenue retention and gross retention targets through proactive commercial engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead scaled customer engagement motions—including QBRs, value reviews, and enablement sessions—to maximize product adoption and demonstrate ongoing ROI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor customer health using data and analytics, identifying churn signals early and executing structured intervention plans to protect and grow revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a trusted advisor to customers with a prescriptive, consultative approach, integrating Harvey into their workflows and championing the power of LLMs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Product, and Sales to relay customer insights, influence the product roadmap, and align on shared goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine scalable playbooks and processes that elevate the team's approach to customer engagement, renewals, and expansion.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or a renewals-focused role within Enterprise SaaS, legal technology, or management consulting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of managing a high-volume book of business and consistently meeting or exceeding retention and expansion targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial acumen with experience owning renewals conversations and identifying upsell or expansion opportunities within existing accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders at multiple levels and deliver polished QBRs and value reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven mindset with experience leveraging customer health metrics, adoption data, and CS platforms to inform strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, proactive disposition with a team-first mentality and comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguity-rich environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Scaled Customer Success Manager joins Harvey's Scaled Customer Success team to drive retention, renewal, and expansion outcomes across a high-volume book of business. The team's mission is to deliver strategic, efficient value at scale—ensuring customers adopt Harvey's AI solutions deeply and renew with confidence. This role owns the full commercial lifecycle for a portfolio of accounts, blending consultative customer engagement with a data-driven renewals motion to maximize net revenue retention. Scaled CSMs partners closely with Sales, Legal Engineering, and Product to translate customer feedback into roadmap influence and expansion opportunity. It is a rare opportunity to shape a growing function at the intersection of AI innovation and customer value delivery.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own renewals and expansions across a named portfolio of accounts, driving net revenue retention and gross retention targets through proactive commercial engagement.\n\n - Lead scaled customer engagement motions—including QBRs, value reviews, and enablement sessions—to maximize product adoption and demonstrate ongoing ROI.\n\n - Monitor customer health using data and analytics, identifying churn signals early and executing structured intervention plans to protect and grow revenue.\n\n - Serve as a trusted advisor to customers with a prescriptive, consultative approach, integrating Harvey into their workflows and championing the power of LLMs.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Legal Engineering, Product, and Sales to relay customer insights, influence the product roadmap, and align on shared goals.\n\n - Build and refine scalable playbooks and processes that elevate the team's approach to customer engagement, renewals, and expansion.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or a renewals-focused role within Enterprise SaaS, legal technology, or management consulting.\n\n - Demonstrated track record of managing a high-volume book of business and consistently meeting or exceeding retention and expansion targets.\n\n - Strong commercial acumen with experience owning renewals conversations and identifying upsell or expansion opportunities within existing accounts.\n\n - Excellent communication and strategic planning skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders at multiple levels and deliver polished QBRs and value reviews.\n\n - Data-driven mindset with experience leveraging customer health metrics, adoption data, and CS platforms to inform strategy.\n\n - Collaborative, proactive disposition with a team-first mentality and comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguity-rich environment.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LL1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d2624850-8dd4-4eb4-b5dc-f386b715a26f","title":"Software Engineer, Security","department":"Security","team":"SA","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T14:38:55.762+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d2624850-8dd4-4eb4-b5dc-f386b715a26f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d2624850-8dd4-4eb4-b5dc-f386b715a26f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Role Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team at Harvey, you'll build and operate foundational security services for both our customer-facing product and the internal systems our workforce depends on: identity and access management, secrets and privileged access, agent sandboxes, and tooling that makes the secure path the fast path. You'll turn security needs into production systems and own the reliability and security of what you build, working closely with engineers and partner teams along the way. Attackers increasingly operate at agent speed, so we’re building defenses that can keep pace.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Security at Harvey is an engineering discipline, not a gatekeeper function. We build platforms and libraries that make it hard for engineers to get security wrong, and we measure ourselves on adoption and outcomes rather than tickets filed. Our program is informed by risk: we invest where the actual exposure to our most sensitive data and resources is greatest, rather than where a framework tells us to.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate Harvey’s core identity and access services across customer-facing product, workforce, and infrastructure systems, including authentication, authorization, access governance, secrets, and privileged access</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve how Harvey customers set up and manage their environments, making security-critical configuration—from identity and access to policies and integrations—delightful to use and secure by default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build identity controls, sandboxes, and safety harnesses that let services and AI agents operate with least privilege, constrained actions, clear auditability, and effective monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create secure-by-default libraries, paved-road abstractions, self-service tooling, and agentic workflows that automate security triage, remediation, and evidence collection</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take security systems from design through production, accounting for trust boundaries, attacker paths, and operational failure modes while owning their reliability and security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share an on-call rotation for Harvey’s mission-critical security services, contribute to incident response, and raise the engineering bar through design reviews, code reviews, and clear documentation</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of software engineering experience, including experience shipping and operating production services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to security infrastructure such as identity and access management, authentication and authorization, secrets management, or privileged access</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming, debugging, testing, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work across unfamiliar systems and domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud infrastructure such as Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, or Amazon Web Services and familiarity with modern distributed-system patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of translating security requirements into maintainable, automated systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using agentic coding tools and creating workflows that automate repetitive security work, with the judgment to review their output critically and measure whether they improve security outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to explain technical risks, decisions, and tradeoffs to engineering partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of common vulnerability classes and the ability to reason about how a system fails under an attacker, not just under load</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building security infrastructure at a fast-growing company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SCIM; OpenID Connect (OIDC); Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML); policy engines such as Open Policy Agent (OPA), Cedar, or Zanzibar-style systems; or hardware-backed credentials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience securing agentic or AI-powered systems, especially systems that act on behalf of users against sensitive data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a highly regulated enterprise environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$161,000 - $245,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team at Harvey, you'll build and operate foundational security services for both our customer-facing product and the internal systems our workforce depends on: identity and access management, secrets and privileged access, agent sandboxes, and tooling that makes the secure path the fast path. You'll turn security needs into production systems and own the reliability and security of what you build, working closely with engineers and partner teams along the way. Attackers increasingly operate at agent speed, so we’re building defenses that can keep pace.\n\nSecurity at Harvey is an engineering discipline, not a gatekeeper function. We build platforms and libraries that make it hard for engineers to get security wrong, and we measure ourselves on adoption and outcomes rather than tickets filed. Our program is informed by risk: we invest where the actual exposure to our most sensitive data and resources is greatest, rather than where a framework tells us to.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and operate Harvey’s core identity and access services across customer-facing product, workforce, and infrastructure systems, including authentication, authorization, access governance, secrets, and privileged access\n\n - Evolve how Harvey customers set up and manage their environments, making security-critical configuration—from identity and access to policies and integrations—delightful to use and secure by default\n\n - Build identity controls, sandboxes, and safety harnesses that let services and AI agents operate with least privilege, constrained actions, clear auditability, and effective monitoring\n\n - Create secure-by-default libraries, paved-road abstractions, self-service tooling, and agentic workflows that automate security triage, remediation, and evidence collection\n\n - Take security systems from design through production, accounting for trust boundaries, attacker paths, and operational failure modes while owning their reliability and security\n\n - Share an on-call rotation for Harvey’s mission-critical security services, contribute to incident response, and raise the engineering bar through design reviews, code reviews, and clear documentation\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 2+ years of software engineering experience, including experience shipping and operating production services\n\n - Experience building or contributing to security infrastructure such as identity and access management, authentication and authorization, secrets management, or privileged access\n\n - Strong programming, debugging, testing, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work across unfamiliar systems and domains\n\n - Experience with cloud infrastructure such as Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, or Amazon Web Services and familiarity with modern distributed-system patterns\n\n - A track record of translating security requirements into maintainable, automated systems\n\n - Experience using agentic coding tools and creating workflows that automate repetitive security work, with the judgment to review their output critically and measure whether they improve security outcomes\n\n - Clear communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to explain technical risks, decisions, and tradeoffs to engineering partners\n\n - Working knowledge of common vulnerability classes and the ability to reason about how a system fails under an attacker, not just under load\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building security infrastructure at a fast-growing company\n\n - Experience with SCIM; OpenID Connect (OIDC); Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML); policy engines such as Open Policy Agent (OPA), Cedar, or Zanzibar-style systems; or hardware-backed credentials\n\n - Experience securing agentic or AI-powered systems, especially systems that act on behalf of users against sensitive data\n\n - Experience working in a highly regulated enterprise environment\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$161,000 - $245,000 USD\n\n\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-NP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$161K – $245K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$161K - $245K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c58699e7-c74d-419c-b423-7d257b04613a","tierSummary":"$161K – $245K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1e48dbce-ae3b-40ae-bef4-f6b3e39962a7","summary":"$161K – $245K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":245000},{"id":"fa03f367-821e-4a88-a440-4cb242aa3bc0","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6b512d4f-8f09-459b-abc9-74f878b1f82c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":245000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"89d41987-0df3-4817-bb55-c83e321a8b2f","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise (Public Sector - State & Local)","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Washington DC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T17:52:21.596+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/89d41987-0df3-4817-bb55-c83e321a8b2f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/89d41987-0df3-4817-bb55-c83e321a8b2f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enterprise Account Executive on Harvey's State &amp; Local team, you will own a multi-state territory of state Attorneys General offices, state agencies, judiciaries, and large county and municipal legal departments. These are substantial legal organizations — a single state AG office can run to hundreds of attorneys — and almost none of them are using AI today. Compared with federal, the territory is broader and higher-velocity: more accounts, more procurement variation across jurisdictions, and paths to direct purchase that can move faster than the federal cycle. You will run the full cycle and help define how Harvey sells to government at the state level.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a named multi-state territory of AG offices, state agencies, judiciaries, and large local government legal departments, running the full cycle from prospecting through contracting and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and exceed revenue targets while managing a higher account volume than a federal book.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Map the procurement path per jurisdiction — competitive solicitation, state tender panels, cooperative purchasing vehicles, or direct purchase under a legal services or professional services exemption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multi-thread across Attorneys General and deputies, general counsel, division heads, state CIO and CISO organizations, and procurement officers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work against state fiscal calendars and legislative budget cycles, which vary by jurisdiction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reference strength deliberately — state government buys heavily on peer proof, so early wins must be turned into referenceable stories.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document learnings into a repeatable state and local playbook.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years selling complex enterprise software, with a meaningful portion of that time carrying a state, local, or education quota.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Closed SLED deals yourself, and can speak specifically to how you got them through procurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating across multiple jurisdictions with genuinely different procurement rules, rather than treating SLED as one market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage a broader book with more concurrent cycles and a lower average deal size than federal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong detail discipline around solicitations, deadlines, and security documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuinely excited to prospect, and capable of independently running a cycle end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong consultative, value-based selling instincts, and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated interest in AI and in helping government lawyers do their work better.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$400,000 USD</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AD2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\n\nAs an Enterprise Account Executive on Harvey's State & Local team, you will own a multi-state territory of state Attorneys General offices, state agencies, judiciaries, and large county and municipal legal departments. These are substantial legal organizations — a single state AG office can run to hundreds of attorneys — and almost none of them are using AI today. Compared with federal, the territory is broader and higher-velocity: more accounts, more procurement variation across jurisdictions, and paths to direct purchase that can move faster than the federal cycle. You will run the full cycle and help define how Harvey sells to government at the state level.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n - Own a named multi-state territory of AG offices, state agencies, judiciaries, and large local government legal departments, running the full cycle from prospecting through contracting and expansion.\n\n - Achieve and exceed revenue targets while managing a higher account volume than a federal book.\n\n - Map the procurement path per jurisdiction — competitive solicitation, state tender panels, cooperative purchasing vehicles, or direct purchase under a legal services or professional services exemption.\n\n - Multi-thread across Attorneys General and deputies, general counsel, division heads, state CIO and CISO organizations, and procurement officers.\n\n - Work against state fiscal calendars and legislative budget cycles, which vary by jurisdiction.\n\n - Build reference strength deliberately — state government buys heavily on peer proof, so early wins must be turned into referenceable stories.\n\n - Document learnings into a repeatable state and local playbook.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n - 5+ years selling complex enterprise software, with a meaningful portion of that time carrying a state, local, or education quota.\n\n - Closed SLED deals yourself, and can speak specifically to how you got them through procurement.\n\n - Comfort operating across multiple jurisdictions with genuinely different procurement rules, rather than treating SLED as one market.\n\n - Ability to manage a broader book with more concurrent cycles and a lower average deal size than federal.\n\n - Strong detail discipline around solicitations, deadlines, and security documentation.\n\n - Genuinely excited to prospect, and capable of independently running a cycle end to end.\n\n - Strong consultative, value-based selling instincts, and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences.\n\n - Demonstrated interest in AI and in helping government lawyers do their work better.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$400,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AD2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$400K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$400K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6971c409-a473-42ca-9a73-b30d409545bb","tierSummary":"$400K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"dd2fe240-bb5f-45d1-8672-c1002949c4a4","summary":"$400K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":400000},{"id":"ceec2c9c-f1d4-4469-a65c-6d82ff7e58d5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":400000,"maxValue":400000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d16bd223-cb68-46f3-8bf6-41267b9770cb","title":"Staff Security Software Engineer, IAM","department":"Security","team":"SecENG","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T23:13:53.367+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d16bd223-cb68-46f3-8bf6-41267b9770cb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/d16bd223-cb68-46f3-8bf6-41267b9770cb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Role Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team, you will be a founding member of the team and define and drive the technical strategy for identity and access at Harvey — both how customers authenticate to Harvey, as well as how internal employees, contractors, and non-human identities access company systems, what they are authorized to do, and how seamlessly access adapts as needs change.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Challenges ahead include exploring how AI-powered access management can understand employee needs, recommend appropriate permissions, streamline decisions, and adapt access as roles and responsibilities evolve, as well as shaping an end user/agent authentication experience that makes signing in to Harvey fast, consistent, reliable, and secure across every surface where our customers work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate at the boundary of security, infrastructure, and product engineering — turning ambitious business and technical requirements into durable identity platforms, clear architectural direction, and exceptional user experiences. This role is hands-on, but its primary leverage comes through technical direction, platform adoption, cross-functional alignment, and enabling other engineers to build on strong identity foundations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What you'll do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's multi-year technical strategy for identity, authentication, authorization, and privileged access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build complex identity systems from greenfield — writing the code, instrumenting it, and owning it in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the architecture and execution of cross-functional initiatives to right-size access at scale, spanning identity and authentication, permissions and authorization, entitlement modeling, and access controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extend the identity model to non-human and agentic identities, so that AI agents acting on behalf of users are authenticated, scoped, and auditable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the technical authority for identity and access architecture and guide major design reviews, investment decisions, and long-term roadmaps.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>What You Have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years experience building and operating production software, with demonstrated impact across multiple teams or technical domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in several identity and access engineering domains — authentication, federation, authorization, entitlement modeling, or privileged access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI: you use AI-assisted development tools effectively while applying strong engineering judgment, and you design agentic workflows that automate repetitive toil and improve how teams operate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing identity or authorization platforms, libraries, or abstractions used by other engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering foundational systems that achieve meaningful adoption and improve organizational or customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud infrastructure, such as Azure, Google Cloud Platform, or Amazon Web Services, and modern distributed-system patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and the ability to create alignment across technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Nice to have</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with System for Cross-domain Identity Management (SCIM), OpenID Connect (OIDC), Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML), policy engines such as Open Policy Agent (OPA) or Cedar, Zanzibar-style authorization systems, or hardware-backed credentials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with identity governance and administration (IGA) or privileged access management (PAM) platforms, and with automating joiner, mover, and leaver workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building identity platforms or programs at a hyper-growth startup.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with regulated environments such as FedRAMP, including phishing-resistant authentication and authenticator assurance requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-NP1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Security Engineering team, you will be a founding member of the team and define and drive the technical strategy for identity and access at Harvey — both how customers authenticate to Harvey, as well as how internal employees, contractors, and non-human identities access company systems, what they are authorized to do, and how seamlessly access adapts as needs change.\n\nChallenges ahead include exploring how AI-powered access management can understand employee needs, recommend appropriate permissions, streamline decisions, and adapt access as roles and responsibilities evolve, as well as shaping an end user/agent authentication experience that makes signing in to Harvey fast, consistent, reliable, and secure across every surface where our customers work.\n\nYou will operate at the boundary of security, infrastructure, and product engineering — turning ambitious business and technical requirements into durable identity platforms, clear architectural direction, and exceptional user experiences. This role is hands-on, but its primary leverage comes through technical direction, platform adoption, cross-functional alignment, and enabling other engineers to build on strong identity foundations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Define Harvey's multi-year technical strategy for identity, authentication, authorization, and privileged access.\n\n - Design and build complex identity systems from greenfield — writing the code, instrumenting it, and owning it in production.\n\n - Lead the architecture and execution of cross-functional initiatives to right-size access at scale, spanning identity and authentication, permissions and authorization, entitlement modeling, and access controls.\n\n - Extend the identity model to non-human and agentic identities, so that AI agents acting on behalf of users are authenticated, scoped, and auditable.\n\n - Serve as the technical authority for identity and access architecture and guide major design reviews, investment decisions, and long-term roadmaps.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years experience building and operating production software, with demonstrated impact across multiple teams or technical domains.\n\n - Deep expertise in several identity and access engineering domains — authentication, federation, authorization, entitlement modeling, or privileged access.\n\n - Fluency with AI: you use AI-assisted development tools effectively while applying strong engineering judgment, and you design agentic workflows that automate repetitive toil and improve how teams operate.\n\n - Experience designing identity or authorization platforms, libraries, or abstractions used by other engineering teams.\n\n - Experience delivering foundational systems that achieve meaningful adoption and improve organizational or customer outcomes.\n\n - Experience with cloud infrastructure, such as Azure, Google Cloud Platform, or Amazon Web Services, and modern distributed-system patterns.\n\n - Strong communication skills and the ability to create alignment across technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with System for Cross-domain Identity Management (SCIM), OpenID Connect (OIDC), Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML), policy engines such as Open Policy Agent (OPA) or Cedar, Zanzibar-style authorization systems, or hardware-backed credentials.\n\n - Experience with identity governance and administration (IGA) or privileged access management (PAM) platforms, and with automating joiner, mover, and leaver workflows.\n\n - Experience building identity platforms or programs at a hyper-growth startup.\n\n - Experience with regulated environments such as FedRAMP, including phishing-resistant authentication and authenticator assurance requirements.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n \n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-NP1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"94b63e82-62aa-4c53-a523-14116beb2fe0","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f85e728c-f8f0-4901-adfc-5fd2ed4dcaaa","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4edeec37-3ed6-45ac-bec9-34fefa992537","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a4c22696-f102-4b42-95b7-864d9785e9e3","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000}]}},{"id":"201ed7d8-0e04-4e0e-a012-1b9200b989b4","title":"Global Operations Program Manager","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T17:39:26.354+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/201ed7d8-0e04-4e0e-a012-1b9200b989b4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/201ed7d8-0e04-4e0e-a012-1b9200b989b4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">People Operations is taking on more complex, cross-functional program work as Harvey grows globally — from opening new entities and markets, to integrating acquisitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff</strong>, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&amp;A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and drive the program plan</strong>, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Connect the dots across functions.</strong> Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own program communication and change management</strong>, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale</strong>, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep the employee experience at the center.</strong> Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&amp;A integration, or related work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nPeople Operations is taking on more complex, cross-functional program work as Harvey grows globally — from opening new entities and markets, to integrating acquisitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.\n\nYou’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n - Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.\n\n - Build and drive the program plan, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.\n\n - Connect the dots across functions. Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.\n\n - Own program communication and change management, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.\n\n - Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.\n\n - Keep the employee experience at the center. Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&A integration, or related work.\n\n - A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.\n\n - Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.\n\n - Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.\n\n - Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,000 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b1812eb9-9944-4874-aa4b-f9032bfd7f19","tierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1918e1be-d38e-4c84-8998-cf55fff1ee75","summary":"$120K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"e68d97d1-b545-4873-b92d-0ae6433dbbe6","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"316286b8-8c68-414b-af48-462df4e8e6c8","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"23a93539-af9f-400d-9da6-dd9165364002","title":"Transformation Associate","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:53:09.739+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/23a93539-af9f-400d-9da6-dd9165364002","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/23a93539-af9f-400d-9da6-dd9165364002/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel: up to ~25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn data into insight.</strong> Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build playbooks and frameworks that scale.</strong> Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Capture best practices from strategic transformation engagements.</strong> Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive-ready communications.</strong> Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional coordination.</strong> Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Synthesize learnings and feed thought leadership.</strong> Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: up to 25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$116,000 - 159,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.\n\nThis is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.\n\nThis is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.\n\nTravel: up to ~25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nTurn data into insight. Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.\n\nBuild playbooks and frameworks that scale. Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.\n\nCapture best practices from strategic transformation engagements. Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.\n\nBuild executive-ready communications. Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.\n\nDrive cross-functional coordination. Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.\n\nSynthesize learnings and feed thought leadership. Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.\n\nTravel required: up to 25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.\n\n - Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.\n\n - A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.\n\n - Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$116,000 - 159,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$116K - $159.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"90ca4449-7423-4094-8602-d2302cf09d8b","tierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e4c09430-866a-4be8-8447-3b6116ed5a56","summary":"$116K – $159.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"id":"8d143f6a-34e9-45aa-b5b2-6f071e16bc79","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b967c7d9-7ed7-4be5-9022-60e653ae0087","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"b9c5964f-40ef-46c5-a1db-58dbdd2c314e","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Model Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-06T21:40:28.062+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b9c5964f-40ef-46c5-a1db-58dbdd2c314e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b9c5964f-40ef-46c5-a1db-58dbdd2c314e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Build</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model Reliability &amp; Operations</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated failover and recovery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity provisioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational tooling and incident automation</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unified Model Controller (UMC)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Policy-based model routing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intelligent Model Selector</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Traffic management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliability and latency optimization</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provider Platform</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multi-provider architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">API and SDK integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rapid adoption of new frontier models</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Observability &amp; Cost Platform</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Token usage analytics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cost attribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Latency and reliability dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilization optimization</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI Platform Foundation</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Infrastructure supporting model evaluation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model deployment and operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Future model training platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agent infrastructure and CcaaS</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating highly available production services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$193,400 - 290,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BUILD\n\n - Model Reliability & Operations\n   \n   - Model health monitoring\n   \n   - Automated failover and recovery\n   \n   - Capacity provisioning\n   \n   - Operational tooling and incident automation\n\n - Unified Model Controller (UMC)\n   \n   - Policy-based model routing\n   \n   - Intelligent Model Selector\n   \n   - Model health monitoring\n   \n   - Traffic management\n   \n   - Reliability and latency optimization\n\n - Provider Platform\n   \n   - Multi-provider architecture\n   \n   - API and SDK integrations\n   \n   - OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers\n   \n   - Rapid adoption of new frontier models\n\n - Observability & Cost Platform\n   \n   - Token usage analytics\n   \n   - Cost attribution\n   \n   - Latency and reliability dashboards\n   \n   - Capacity forecasting\n   \n   - Utilization optimization\n\n - AI Platform Foundation\n   \n   - Infrastructure supporting model evaluation\n   \n   - Model deployment and operations\n   \n   - Future model training platform\n   \n   - Agent infrastructure and CcaaS\n     \n     \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.\n\n - Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.\n\n - Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.\n\n - Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.\n\n - Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.\n\n - Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.\n\n - Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.\n\n - Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.\n\n - Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.\n\n - Experience designing and operating highly available production services.\n\n - Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.\n\n - Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.\n\n - Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.\n\n - Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\n - Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.\n\n - Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.\n\n - Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.\n\n - Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.\n\n - Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.\n\n - Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.\n\n - Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$193,400 - 290,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$193.4K - $290K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"08b4d476-3d6f-4b2c-b80c-d7f2af46981e","tierSummary":"$193.4K – $290K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"30e41154-339b-4f2b-b497-696854088137","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"0ae85701-410e-44f4-be79-36cc3efad33e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"8862442d-08cd-4f6a-b416-dc6fd74ab00c","summary":"$193.4K – $290K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":193400,"maxValue":290000}]}},{"id":"3ae2aecf-16c4-4e6e-a8fd-0db33ebeb16c","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Model Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-06T21:50:17.241+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3ae2aecf-16c4-4e6e-a8fd-0db33ebeb16c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3ae2aecf-16c4-4e6e-a8fd-0db33ebeb16c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.</p><h1><strong><br />What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You’ll Build</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model Reliability &amp; Operations</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated failover and recovery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity provisioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational tooling and incident automation</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unified Model Controller (UMC)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Policy-based model routing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intelligent Model Selector</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model health monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Traffic management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliability and latency optimization</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provider Platform</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multi-provider architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">API and SDK integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rapid adoption of new frontier models</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Observability &amp; Cost Platform</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Token usage analytics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cost attribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Latency and reliability dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilization optimization</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI Platform Foundation</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Infrastructure supporting model evaluation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model deployment and operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Future model training platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agent infrastructure and CcaaS</p></li></ul></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating highly available production services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$231,000 - $340,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer on the Model Infrastructure team, you'll lead the design and development of the systems that power every AI request at Harvey. You'll partner closely with AI Research, Product Engineering, Infrastructure, and external model providers to build a platform that is highly reliable, scalable, observable, and efficient.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead the design and implementation of Harvey's Model Infrastructure platform.\n\n - Build systems to ensure high availability, low latency, and operational excellence for AI inference.\n\n - Design and improve Harvey's Unified Model Controller (UMC) and Model Selector platform to automatically detect model degradations and intelligently route traffic based on reliability, latency, quality, compliance, and cost.\n\n - Develop systems for model provisioning, capacity management, failover, and traffic engineering across multiple AI providers.\n\n - Integrate new model providers and maintain provider APIs and SDKs, enabling Harvey to rapidly adopt emerging frontier models.\n\n - Improve observability through health dashboards, alerting, token usage analytics, cost reporting, and end-to-end telemetry.\n\n - Partner with Product Engineering to support model launches, experimentation, and proactive monitoring of production AI workloads.\n\n - Drive infrastructure efficiency through capacity planning, utilization optimization, and cost visibility.\n\n - Collaborate with AI Research to build the infrastructure foundation for future model evaluation, training, and deployment.\n\n - Lead cross-functional technical initiatives and mentor engineers across the organization.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BUILD\n\n - Model Reliability & Operations\n   \n   - Model health monitoring\n   \n   - Automated failover and recovery\n   \n   - Capacity provisioning\n   \n   - Operational tooling and incident automation\n\n - Unified Model Controller (UMC)\n   \n   - Policy-based model routing\n   \n   - Intelligent Model Selector\n   \n   - Model health monitoring\n   \n   - Traffic management\n   \n   - Reliability and latency optimization\n\n - Provider Platform\n   \n   - Multi-provider architecture\n   \n   - API and SDK integrations\n   \n   - OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, and future providers\n   \n   - Rapid adoption of new frontier models\n\n - Observability & Cost Platform\n   \n   - Token usage analytics\n   \n   - Cost attribution\n   \n   - Latency and reliability dashboards\n   \n   - Capacity forecasting\n   \n   - Utilization optimization\n\n - AI Platform Foundation\n   \n   - Infrastructure supporting model evaluation\n   \n   - Model deployment and operations\n   \n   - Future model training platform\n   \n   - Agent infrastructure and CcaaS\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of software engineering experience building large-scale distributed systems.\n\n - Experience designing and operating highly available production services.\n\n - Strong programming skills in Go, Java, Python, Rust, or C++.\n\n - Deep understanding of distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, networking, and observability.\n\n - Experience leading technical projects across multiple engineering teams.\n\n - Ability to balance long-term architecture with pragmatic execution.\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\n - Passion for building foundational platforms that enable other engineering teams.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AI infrastructure, LLM serving, or machine learning platforms.\n\n - Experience with model routing, inference gateways, or policy-based serving systems.\n\n - Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Fireworks, Baseten, or open-source LLMs.\n\n - Experience with Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, and service mesh technologies.\n\n - Experience with large-scale observability and SRE best practices.\n\n - Experience with data infrastructure technologies such as Kafka, Spark, Flink, Airflow, or Iceberg.\n\n - Familiarity with GPU infrastructure or model training platforms.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$231,000 - $340,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-AK1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$231K - $340K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3c0804db-919a-483b-b46b-7bf3d652f3d7","tierSummary":"$231K – $340K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5367449e-7b2a-4124-b4b5-39e29953fd03","summary":"$231K – $340K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"id":"dd27c85d-387a-48ec-a451-be5568e0d551","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d9602684-60ff-49b8-a761-39c1b714c669","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":231000,"maxValue":340000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"446091c7-8a78-4c1c-8de3-4a2289be6072","title":"Transformation Associate","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:55:25.151+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/446091c7-8a78-4c1c-8de3-4a2289be6072","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/446091c7-8a78-4c1c-8de3-4a2289be6072/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel: up to ~25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn data into insight.</strong> Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build playbooks and frameworks that scale.</strong> Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Capture best practices from strategic transformation engagements.</strong> Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive-ready communications.</strong> Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional coordination.</strong> Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Synthesize learnings and feed thought leadership.</strong> Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: up to 25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$116,000 - 159,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nAs a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.\n\nThis is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.\n\nThis is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.\n\nTravel: up to ~25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\nTurn data into insight. Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.\n\nBuild playbooks and frameworks that scale. Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.\n\nCapture best practices from strategic transformation engagements. Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.\n\nBuild executive-ready communications. Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.\n\nDrive cross-functional coordination. Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.\n\nSynthesize learnings and feed thought leadership. Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.\n\nTravel required: up to 25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.\n\n - Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.\n\n - A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.\n\n - Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$116,000 - 159,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$116K - $159.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"84dffae8-46ae-45a8-a02e-a5b07c439ba1","tierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"eaae48e8-49ea-43e2-891b-12f7d1c9c7f3","summary":"$116K – $159.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"id":"8aad87dc-6b4e-48ac-9a50-4da2b103099f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"17beb800-0601-47b1-8fcb-c58f4bceb1e4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"73be92d9-6762-4985-9beb-7ef6bcce6029","title":"Transformation Associate","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:55:13.798+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/73be92d9-6762-4985-9beb-7ef6bcce6029","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/73be92d9-6762-4985-9beb-7ef6bcce6029/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel: up to ~25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn data into insight.</strong> Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build playbooks and frameworks that scale.</strong> Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Capture best practices from strategic transformation engagements.</strong> Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive-ready communications.</strong> Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional coordination.</strong> Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Synthesize learnings and feed thought leadership.</strong> Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: up to 25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$116,000 - 159,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nAs a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.\n\nThis is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.\n\nThis is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.\n\nTravel: up to ~25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\nTurn data into insight. Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.\n\nBuild playbooks and frameworks that scale. Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.\n\nCapture best practices from strategic transformation engagements. Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.\n\nBuild executive-ready communications. Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.\n\nDrive cross-functional coordination. Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.\n\nSynthesize learnings and feed thought leadership. Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.\n\nTravel required: up to 25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.\n\n - Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.\n\n - A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.\n\n - Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$116,000 - 159,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$116K - $159.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ac265400-4baf-4e89-ac44-ccb3ab29b16a","tierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"211831ed-a044-47ad-a6d1-27af4b34369e","summary":"$116K – $159.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"id":"3aae0ca4-c2c8-46cc-9e5f-2da6edc626a9","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"07dc7784-b4d6-445e-ae8e-00ad1f735558","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"86a851c2-92d5-4ac4-bf2f-b314e888591f","title":"Transformation Associate","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:46.790+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/86a851c2-92d5-4ac4-bf2f-b314e888591f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/86a851c2-92d5-4ac4-bf2f-b314e888591f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel: up to ~25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn data into insight.</strong> Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build playbooks and frameworks that scale.</strong> Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Capture best practices from strategic transformation engagements.</strong> Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive-ready communications.</strong> Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional coordination.</strong> Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Synthesize learnings and feed thought leadership.</strong> Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: up to 25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$116,000 - 159,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nAs a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.\n\nThis is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.\n\nThis is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.\n\nTravel: up to ~25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\nTurn data into insight. Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.\n\nBuild playbooks and frameworks that scale. Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.\n\nCapture best practices from strategic transformation engagements. Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.\n\nBuild executive-ready communications. Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.\n\nDrive cross-functional coordination. Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.\n\nSynthesize learnings and feed thought leadership. Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.\n\nTravel required: up to 25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.\n\n - Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.\n\n - A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.\n\n - Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$116,000 - 159,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$116K - $159.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"80c741f4-d553-4bcb-b7ca-3ee265bfcd9a","tierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1db4d34f-8051-4b7d-8cbd-3a55d6659644","summary":"$116K – $159.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"id":"be53f04f-735e-4ad7-a6e0-80916ada8c1d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ed0faec1-bf5e-4b2a-9ae5-fdead340bb38","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c1872581-6069-4c6d-84e4-272d74b290ad","title":"Global Operations Program Manager","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T17:39:36.599+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c1872581-6069-4c6d-84e4-272d74b290ad","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c1872581-6069-4c6d-84e4-272d74b290ad/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">People Operations is taking on more complex, cross-functional program work as Harvey grows globally — from opening new entities and markets, to integrating acquisitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff</strong>, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&amp;A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and drive the program plan</strong>, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Connect the dots across functions.</strong> Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own program communication and change management</strong>, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale</strong>, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep the employee experience at the center.</strong> Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&amp;A integration, or related work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nPeople Operations is taking on more complex, cross-functional program work as Harvey grows globally — from opening new entities and markets, to integrating acquisitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.\n\nYou’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n - Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.\n\n - Build and drive the program plan, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.\n\n - Connect the dots across functions. Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.\n\n - Own program communication and change management, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.\n\n - Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.\n\n - Keep the employee experience at the center. Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&A integration, or related work.\n\n - A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.\n\n - Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.\n\n - Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.\n\n - Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,000 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"428a1bf6-e984-42bb-b800-f14c7e2998ef","tierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5bda6367-d33c-4080-8d3d-b2baf79a72f1","summary":"$120K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"3f397aa9-d424-482c-bff8-a90544bcedb5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"72604aa6-a28a-49ba-8106-53ca61c943bc","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"3f7894ac-ba57-462f-ad0b-1e52a46d4bd3","title":"Global Operations Program Manager","department":"Human Resources","team":"Human Resources","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T03:55:48.005+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3f7894ac-ba57-462f-ad0b-1e52a46d4bd3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/3f7894ac-b