sitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.</p><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff</strong>, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&amp;A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and drive the program plan</strong>, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Connect the dots across functions.</strong> Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own program communication and change management</strong>, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale</strong>, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep the employee experience at the center.</strong> Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&amp;A integration, or related work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $200,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-RB1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nPeople Operations is taking on more complex, cross-functional program work as Harvey grows globally — from opening new entities and markets, to integrating acquisitions, to evolving the systems and providers that support our employees around the world. These programs span People, Finance, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams, and need a dedicated owner who can bring the whole thing together.\n\nYou’ll run point on these initiatives end-to-end: defining requirements, building the plan, driving decisions and execution across teams, and making sure we’re ready to go live. This is a hands-on program management role — you’ll work closely with functional experts, but you’re expected to get into the substance, develop a point of view, and personally execute work wherever needed to drive the program forward.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n - Own complex global programs from scope through go-live and handoff, including new entity formation and geographic expansion, M&A integrations, and the ongoing evolution of our infrastructure in existing markets — such as EOR and vendor transitions, payroll migrations, and other major operational changes.\n\n - Build and drive the program plan, translating a messy objective into clear requirements, workstreams, owners, dependencies, readiness gates, and decisions; proactively surface risks, resolve blockers, and adjust the plan as facts change.\n\n - Connect the dots across functions. Partner deeply with People Ops, People Systems, Finance, Payroll, Legal, Tax, IT, and other teams to understand how decisions in one workstream affect another and make sure nothing falls between the cracks.\n\n - Own program communication and change management, from crisp executive updates and decision points to clear, thoughtful communications for employees affected by a change.\n\n - Build repeatable infrastructure as we scale, turning what we learn from each program into better templates, SOPs, playbooks, and operating processes for the next one.\n\n - Keep the employee experience at the center. Make sure operational complexity behind the scenes translates into a coordinated, thoughtful experience for employees — particularly during high-change moments like entering a new market, transitioning employment infrastructure, or integrating an acquired team.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 7+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, with experience in global People infrastructure such as geographic expansion, entity formation, M&A integration, or related work.\n\n - A hands-on operating style and strong bias toward action. You dig into the substance, step into gaps, and do what’s needed to keep complex work moving. You’re comfortable figuring things out as you go and have good judgment about what requires deeper diligence versus what simply needs to get done.\n\n - Strong stakeholder management and judgment, with the ability to align specialists and senior leaders across functions without formal authority.\n\n - Clear, direct executive communication. You can distill a complicated program into the decisions, risks, and tradeoffs that matter and communicate them appropriately to everyone from executives to affected employees.\n\n - Strong AI fluency. You use AI as a core part of how you work — to move faster, synthesize information, work through ambiguity, and increase the quality and leverage of your output.\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120,000 - $200,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-RB1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ab4fc221-5583-4213-b942-55bc794f2c90","tierSummary":"$120K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"839caeca-85bf-41fc-9ed1-81dcf424f887","summary":"$120K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"67fc1da7-5e62-4246-88c9-cb1d9b698734","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"13144ebd-f753-499b-880d-7af7b189c8a1","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"132ae71e-9874-43dc-95d5-1cd96c9e2224","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Search","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T23:02:50.422+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/132ae71e-9874-43dc-95d5-1cd96c9e2224","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/132ae71e-9874-43dc-95d5-1cd96c9e2224/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Search Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Search Growth\n\n - Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.\n\n - Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.\n\n - Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.\n\n - Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.\n\n - Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.\n\n - Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.\n\n - Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.\n\n - Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.\n\n - Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.\n\n - Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.\n\n - Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.\n\n - Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.\n\n - Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LT1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"31d6d9c2-65ac-41f9-93ff-14ec00d27e89","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"19fe38f9-3e1d-46d9-815e-40486fc93e12","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"43c8c0a4-3677-473b-8ff0-1564de34c644","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cdea7643-853a-48a4-b4d7-3ee5404b8052","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"22d2d3c5-ddc2-48ef-8453-e7092c6ee53b","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Search","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T23:03:20.058+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/22d2d3c5-ddc2-48ef-8453-e7092c6ee53b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/22d2d3c5-ddc2-48ef-8453-e7092c6ee53b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Search Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LT1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Search Growth\n\n - Own Harvey's global paid search strategy across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, defining the vision for how paid search drives customer acquisition, pipeline, and revenue growth across segments.\n\n - Manage end-to-end search performance, including budget allocation, forecasting, pacing, and investment strategy to consistently achieve ambitious pipeline and revenue targets.\n\n - Build, launch, and optimize paid search campaigns across global markets, continuously refining campaign structure, bidding strategies, audience targeting, keyword expansion, and messaging to maximize performance and efficiency.\n\n - Manage significant paid search budgets, optimizing ROI through sophisticated bid management, search intent analysis, landing page optimization, and conversion rate improvements.\n\n - Stay ahead of the evolving search landscape—including AI-powered search experiences, emerging ad products, and platform innovations—to identify new growth opportunities before competitors.\n\n - Develop executive-ready performance reports and strategic business reviews, surfacing insights, opportunities, and recommendations that connect paid search investments to measurable business outcomes.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and execute a robust experimentation roadmap across bidding strategies, keyword expansion, ad copy, audience segmentation, landing pages, campaign structure, and emerging Google product betas.\n\n - Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate creative development, automate workflows, uncover insights, and improve campaign optimization at scale.\n\n - Continuously optimize performance by analyzing search intent, auction dynamics, competitive trends, user behavior, and platform innovations.\n\n - Build scalable testing frameworks, operational playbooks, and optimization processes that enable continuous optimization and long-term growth.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Partner with Web, Design, Content, and PMM to ensure paid search messaging is consistent across channels and tied into integrated, full-funnel campaigns.\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing Operations and Data Analytics to strengthen attribution, conversion tracking, offline conversion optimization, reporting infrastructure, and measurement frameworks.\n\n - Communicate performance trends, experimentation results, and translate performance data into clear, actional insights and strategic recommendations for cross-functional partners and executive leadership.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of experience in performance marketing with deep, hands-on expertise in managing Google Ads and Microsoft Ads.\n\n - Track record managing large-scale paid search budgets with demonstrated impact on lead generation and pipeline.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional communication skills with the ability to translate campaign data into strategic recommendations and align with stakeholders across marketing, sales, and operations.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience with Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics, Conversion APIs, offline conversion tracking, and value-based bidding.\n\n - Experience scaling international paid search programs across multiple regions and languages.\n\n - Experience marketing to enterprise B2B audiences—ideally within legal technology, AI, SaaS, or professional services—with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n#LI-LT1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"95c6261b-4998-4d4d-b439-df565d49aa71","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6e4c82e7-d1b9-4e10-b19d-72226f05755b","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"83886d5c-e988-4c67-90c7-2aa5ef02e982","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"98d4bdde-6f74-4976-8b3c-ed39a80bfda5","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a8f060ad-1e57-40f8-94f7-402c2611eb90","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T23:28:15.498+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Illinois","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a8f060ad-1e57-40f8-94f7-402c2611eb90","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/a8f060ad-1e57-40f8-94f7-402c2611eb90/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Social Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Social Growth\n\n - Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.\n\n - Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.\n\n - Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.\n\n - Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.\n\n - Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.\n\n - Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n - Bachelor's Degree\n\n - 5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.\n\n - Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.\n\n - Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.\n\n - Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.\n\n - Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b1da3116-5c3b-4c72-921f-1d12fce3bb0d","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"433cd40e-6abe-4b26-8455-b447674e4be3","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"a8ac8c8e-238d-4d6f-b20f-d35d7ed58ed7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a969823e-c151-4e21-bdbd-ebf2f7241b79","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"275f3315-2ea8-4fb4-bfe8-e0dd4e238e86","title":"Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T23:29:03.491+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Dallas"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/275f3315-2ea8-4fb4-bfe8-e0dd4e238e86","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/275f3315-2ea8-4fb4-bfe8-e0dd4e238e86/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and Scale Paid Social Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Experimentation and Performance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the Business</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><h1></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - $204,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices [</strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>].</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-AK2</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is transforming how legal professionals work through AI. We're looking for a Senior Performance Marketing Manager, Paid Social to help unlock the next stage of growth across our paid media programs.\n\nYou'll own and scale paid social as a key driver of pipeline, revenue, and market awareness—reaching legal decision-makers across law firms and corporate legal departments worldwide.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution. You'll develop audience strategies, launch and optimize full-funnel campaigns, partner closely with creative and content teams, and use data to uncover new growth opportunities. You'll own the roadmap and end-to-end execution while helping shape how paid social contributes to Harvey's broader growth strategy.\n\nWe're looking for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, embraces experimentation, and has a track record of turning paid media investments into measurable business outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\n\nOwn and Scale Paid Social Growth\n\n - Own end-to-end strategy, execution, and optimization of paid social campaigns across LinkedIn, Meta, and emerging social platforms, managing a significant budget to hit aggressive pipeline targets.\n\n - Build full-funnel programs that generate awareness, engagement, pipeline, and revenue across enterprise audiences.\n\n - Develop audience strategies leveraging first-party data, account-based targeting, lookalike modeling, and platform-native targeting capabilities.\n\nDrive Experimentation and Performance\n\n - Design and run experiments across creative, messaging, audiences, landing pages to identify scalable growth opportunities.\n\n - Continuously evaluate emerging channels, ad formats, audience targeting and platform capabilities to expand reach and improve efficiency.\n\n - Establish testing frameworks and best practices that improve campaign performance over time.\n\nPartner Across the Business\n\n - Collaborate closely with lifecycle marketing, content, and brand teams to ensure paid social campaigns are integrated into holistic customer journeys with consistent messaging.\n\n - Partner with design teams to develop compelling campaign concepts and provide performance-driven feedback on messaging and creative assets.\n\n - Work closely with Marketing Operations and Analytics teams to ensure accurate attribution, measurement, and reporting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n\n - Bachelor's Degree\n\n - 5–7+ years of experience managing paid social programs in B2B SaaS, with a strong focus on pipeline and revenue generation.\n\n - Deep expertise across LinkedIn, Meta, and YouTube advertising platforms.\n\n - Proven success scaling paid social programs while improving efficiency and business outcomes.\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities with experience using performance data to drive strategic decisions.\n\n - Experience building and executing campaigns targeting enterprise buyers with long and complex sales cycles.\n\n - Working knowledge of attribution, conversion tracking, CRM integrations, and marketing measurement frameworks.\n\n - Ability to operate both strategically and tactically—you can define the roadmap and execute the details.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and experience collaborating across marketing, operations, and sales teams.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience managing seven-figure annual media budgets and scaling paid media programs in high-growth B2B SaaS companies.\n\n - Experience with CTV, Reddit, programmatic media, or other emerging paid acquisition channels.\n\n - Experience marketing to legal, professional services, or other enterprise audiences with complex buying cycles.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - $204,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES [HERE https://www.notion.so/harveyai/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Policies-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922].\n\n\n\n#LI-AK2\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $204K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"85827bc4-1e00-4161-8663-50daf97608a7","tierSummary":"$136K – $204K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3d12e573-566c-4ef0-b85f-51f86e263611","summary":"$136K – $204K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"id":"019daa16-7e8a-496b-a3bc-9daf06707999","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ce817813-77aa-4772-b6df-b433984b023a","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":204000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2dfacb2e-8ac9-4f27-86df-73770a774d65","title":"SMB Sales Manager","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sydney","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T01:50:30.206+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Australia","addressLocality":"Sydney"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2dfacb2e-8ac9-4f27-86df-73770a774d65","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2dfacb2e-8ac9-4f27-86df-73770a774d65/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role Overview</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>As the founding APAC SMB Sales Manager at Harvey, </em>you will shape the future of our Small and Medium-sized Business (SMB) go-to-market strategy. You’ll build, coach and develop a high-performing team of Account Executives while also rolling up your sleeves to engage directly with clients. Beyond hitting ambitious sales targets, you’ll establish the cultural and operational foundations of our SMB sales team: building playbooks, creating scalable best practices, and setting expectations that drive both accountability and collaboration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll build feedback loops with Product, Marketing, and Customer Success that inform product development, pipeline generation, and the SMB customer lifecycle. Success will mean using data to forecast accurately, improve team performance and prioritise accounts where Harvey can deliver the most impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a highly analytical self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and solve complex problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have superb core sales skills, experience scaling high-velocity teams and mentoring colleagues, outstanding communication skills, and an affinity for understanding customer needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire &amp; lead a team of analytical, solution-based, SMB software sales professionals to achieve ARR targets through high velocity  net new logo deals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive recruiting for your team, including refining the ideal candidate profile, participating in sourcing, and interviewing candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own managing and reporting on your book of business, including accurate revenue forecasting and pipeline maintenance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach and develop SMB account executives to promote career growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Refine our SMB sales playbook to enable all sellers to better deliver results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally across the organisation to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey’s clients.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive tech sales experience.  Ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; Minimum 2+ years of people management experience building, training and coaching a high-performing sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">What We Offer</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family &amp; Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement &amp; Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wellness &amp; Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CL1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\nRole Overview\n\nAs the founding APAC SMB Sales Manager at Harvey, you will shape the future of our Small and Medium-sized Business (SMB) go-to-market strategy. You’ll build, coach and develop a high-performing team of Account Executives while also rolling up your sleeves to engage directly with clients. Beyond hitting ambitious sales targets, you’ll establish the cultural and operational foundations of our SMB sales team: building playbooks, creating scalable best practices, and setting expectations that drive both accountability and collaboration.\n\n\n\nIn this role, you’ll build feedback loops with Product, Marketing, and Customer Success that inform product development, pipeline generation, and the SMB customer lifecycle. Success will mean using data to forecast accurately, improve team performance and prioritise accounts where Harvey can deliver the most impact.\n\n\n\nWe are looking for a highly analytical self-starter who can navigate ambiguity, operate in a fast-paced environment, and solve complex problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have superb core sales skills, experience scaling high-velocity teams and mentoring colleagues, outstanding communication skills, and an affinity for understanding customer needs.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Hire & lead a team of analytical, solution-based, SMB software sales professionals to achieve ARR targets through high velocity  net new logo deals\n\n - Drive recruiting for your team, including refining the ideal candidate profile, participating in sourcing, and interviewing candidates\n\n - Own managing and reporting on your book of business, including accurate revenue forecasting and pipeline maintenance.\n\n - Coach and develop SMB account executives to promote career growth\n\n - Refine our SMB sales playbook to enable all sellers to better deliver results\n\n - Work cross-functionally across the organisation to build effective sales processes and solutions that meet the needs of Harvey’s clients.\n\nWhat You Have\n\n - Extensive tech sales experience.  Ideally closing new business at the Mid Market or Enterprise level; Minimum 2+ years of people management experience building, training and coaching a high-performing sales team.\n\n - Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth environment. Demonstrated ability to design and improve systems from scratch\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate technical concepts to a variety of audiences.\n\n\n\nAdditional Information\n\n - Location: Sydney, NSW (Hybrid with flexibility)\n\n - Work eligibility: Must have valid Australian work rights; Harvey does not currently offer visa sponsorship for this role\n\n\n\nWhat We Offer\n\n - Structured hybrid working arrangement: 3 days in our Sydney office, 2 days working from home\n\n - Health Coverage: Fully covered private hospital insurance, plus extras for dental, optical, physio, mental health, and more.\n\n - Family & Fertility Support: Support for fertility treatments, adoption, and surrogacy through Carrot.\n\n - Retirement & Security: Comprehensive coverage designed to support your long-term well-being.\n\n - Paid Leave: Paid annual leave, sick leave, and fully paid parental leave for all parents.\n\n - Wellness & Perks: Daily in-office lunch, wellness memberships through Wellhub, and monthly commuting support.\n\n - Professional Development: Annual support for courses, certifications, conferences, and books.\n\n - Remote Work Allowance: Monthly support for home office, internet, and phone expenses.\n\n - Harvey Holiday: After four years, enjoy a four-week paid sabbatical to rest, travel, or explore new experiences.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-CL1\n\n\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cc432807-dda4-4baa-84ce-905b0362e664","title":"Transformation Associate","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:53:51.655+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cc432807-dda4-4baa-84ce-905b0362e664","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/cc432807-dda4-4baa-84ce-905b0362e664/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel: up to ~25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn data into insight.</strong> Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build playbooks and frameworks that scale.</strong> Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Capture best practices from strategic transformation engagements.</strong> Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build executive-ready communications.</strong> Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional coordination.</strong> Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Synthesize learnings and feed thought leadership.</strong> Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required: up to 25% of the time.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$116,000 - 159,500 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-SZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\n\n\nAs a Strategy Associate on Harvey's Transformation Office, you will be the analytical and content engine behind how we help the world's most sophisticated legal and professional services organizations adopt AI. Reporting to the Transformation Strategy Partner, you'll turn raw inputs — usage data, client context, and engagement learnings — into the playbooks, frameworks, analyses, and executive-ready materials that make transformation repeatable, scalable, and measurable.\n\nThis is a high-ownership, high-leverage role inside a function that is still being built from the ground up. You'll work across the full arc of transformation: helping size where Harvey can have the most impact, building the methodology that scales it, and supporting the strategic engagements that prove it out. You'll partner closely with Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success, and gain direct exposure to senior partners, General Counsel, and Harvey leadership. Strong performers will grow into owning engagements of their own.\n\nThis is a builder's role for someone early in their career who wants disproportionate ownership, range, and visibility.\n\nTravel: up to ~25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\n\nTurn data into insight. Pull, structure, and analyze adoption and usage data across accounts to understand what drives transformation. Build the models, dashboards, and impact analyses that tell us what's working, where the gaps are, and where Harvey can create the most value. You make the numbers tell a clear story.\n\nBuild playbooks and frameworks that scale. Take what works in individual engagements and codify it into reusable playbooks, templates, and methodology. You're not producing one-off decks; you're building the operating system of the Transformation Office so every engagement gets faster, sharper, and more repeatable.\n\nCapture best practices from strategic transformation engagements. Synthesize lessons learned from engagements into repeatable materials, stakeholder maps, workflow analyses, and tracking that keep engagements on plan. Sit close to live client work, own discrete workstreams, and take on more end-to-end responsibility as you grow.\n\nBuild executive-ready communications. Translate complex analysis into crisp narratives, decks, and one-pagers for senior partners, GCs, and internal leadership. You can hold a high bar on both rigor and polish, and you make complex things feel simple.\n\nDrive cross-functional coordination. Act as connective tissue across Legal Engineering, GTM, and Customer Success — chasing down inputs, aligning teams, and making sure things actually move. You surface risk early and keep work on track without being asked.\n\nSynthesize learnings and feed thought leadership. Capture patterns across engagements and turn them into internal knowledge and external thought leadership that sharpens how the market — and Harvey — thinks about AI transformation.\n\nTravel required: up to 25% of the time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n\n\n - 2–3 years at a top-tier strategy consulting firm (MBB — McKinsey, BCG, Bain — or equivalent), where you owned analytically rigorous workstreams on real, complex client problems.\n\n - Exceptional quantitative and data analysis skills. You are deeply comfortable in Excel/Sheets, can structure messy data into clear insight, and build analyses leaders trust. Familiarity with BI tools (e.g. Omni, Looker, Tableau) or SQL is a plus, not a requirement.\n\n - A track record of building playbooks, frameworks, or repeatable methodology — not just polished one-off deliverables.\n\n - Exposure to transformation, change management, and strategy work, ideally in or adjacent to legal, financial services, or professional services.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication. You make complex things simple, write with precision, and can hold your own in a room with senior stakeholders.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity and a bias to action. You thrive where the playbook is still being written, and you'd rather ship and iterate than wait for perfect information.\n\n - Genuine curiosity about AI and what it means for the future of professional work. You don't need to be a technologist, but you need to care deeply about the problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$116,000 - 159,500 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-SZ1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$116K - $159.5K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6b6583a7-510b-4ccc-94d0-53b9f3894fe8","tierSummary":"$116K – $159.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e776faaa-3905-451c-b695-f1475877f35e","summary":"$116K – $159.5K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"id":"d538c6e0-36fe-450f-b460-401bfa0bd98b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e03876c0-d2d7-45cf-bce0-dc31705c0115","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":116000,"maxValue":159500},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c0d56938-468a-43dc-b8ec-84f17b04338a","title":"Senior Manager, Product Design, Platform","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:10.378+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c0d56938-468a-43dc-b8ec-84f17b04338a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c0d56938-468a-43dc-b8ec-84f17b04338a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior Manager, Product Design to lead two parts of Harvey: our Admin experience and our Platform design system team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Admin</strong> is how firm leaders and innovation teams configure, govern, and scale Harvey inside their organizations, from workflow configuration to usage visibility. These champions are the main decision makers in whether Harvey succeeds at an account, and Admin is where they turn their investment into measurable return. The team also owns our knowledge platform and how legal connectors get integrated into Harvey. A general model can reason about law. But it can't reach a firm's precedent, its matter files, or the systems its lawyers work in every day. Making that context usable is the moat in legal AI, and design decides how much of it a lawyer can actually get to.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Platform</strong> is the spine of the design team. It defines how we work in an AI-native way and sets the standard every product team builds on. Most design systems are run as a service: product teams decide what to build, the system team supplies the parts. On an AI-native team, the system sets the craft bar instead of serving it, and its users aren't only designers. When anyone in EPD can generate an interface, the system is what keeps quality consistent and gets teams to a shipped implementation faster. Building that is one of the highest-leverage jobs at Harvey, and you'll shape the team around it. You'll own the system every team builds from and the AI tooling that changes what a designer can produce.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to the VP Design as a foundational member of the Design leadership team, with portfolio-wide impact on how our product, team, and culture scale. You'll set the operating bar for how we work, and lay foundations for the product that hold for years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own Admin as a product</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive strategy and execution for the Admin platform in close partnership with Product and Engineering, rooted in how champions actually run Harvey inside their firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with customers, research, and usage data to find where champions lose time or lose confidence, and design the workflow configuration, knowledge management, and visibility experiences that fix it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tie your roadmap to customer outcomes: faster rollout, wider adoption, and evidence of ROI our champions can take to their own leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the system, not the service</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's design system as a set of product decisions: what good looks like for AI-powered legal work, encoded as patterns product teams inherit rather than requests they submit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the craft bar across interaction, systems thinking, content design, and visual execution, and hold it as our surface area grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the governance model that lets the system move fast without fragmenting: contribution paths, adoption expectations, and clear calls on when a team may deviate.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own AI tooling for the design org</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Decide how Harvey's designers use AI: what tools we adopt, what we build ourselves, and what the new default workflow looks like from problem to prototype.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the floor and the ceiling. Make the whole team faster, and make it possible for a single designer to ship things that used to take a pod.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Treat this as a live experiment with real rigor. Try things, measure them, kill what doesn't work, and share what does across EPD.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and lead the team</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, grow, and develop a team of high-craft ICs across systems, product, and prototyping from a small starting footprint.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own org design, resourcing, and prioritization across four surfaces with very different rhythms, including the conference deadlines that don't move.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Give strategic, systems-level feedback on end-to-end flows, not just screens.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead across the org</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design, product, and engineering leaders to evolve how Harvey builds, and represent Platform in high-stakes conversations with executives and customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish how we make design decisions in high-trust, high-stakes environments where clarity and accuracy are non-negotiable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a foundational member of the Design leadership team and help set the operating model the rest of the org runs on.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8-10+ years in Product Design, with 5+ years directly managing product designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning a design system at real scale, including the political work of getting it adopted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and shipping AI-powered or highly technical products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong portfolio showing leadership of complex products from concept through launch, with clear impact on users and the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI tooling in your own practice, and a real opinion about how it changes design work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience leading design strategy and execution alongside Product and Engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to define and ship high-quality experiences in complex, ambiguous problem spaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment about when to go deep, when to delegate, and when to push.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills and the ability to influence senior stakeholders, internally and in front of customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep commitment to growing people and raising the craft bar across a team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in fast-moving environments with evolving priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathy for users, teammates, and the realities of high-stakes professional work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A growth mindset, resilience, and a bias toward learning through doing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong people leadership instincts with a bias toward clarity, empathy, and accountability.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$235,500 - $325,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Manager, Product Design to lead two parts of Harvey: our Admin experience and our Platform design system team.\n\nAdmin is how firm leaders and innovation teams configure, govern, and scale Harvey inside their organizations, from workflow configuration to usage visibility. These champions are the main decision makers in whether Harvey succeeds at an account, and Admin is where they turn their investment into measurable return. The team also owns our knowledge platform and how legal connectors get integrated into Harvey. A general model can reason about law. But it can't reach a firm's precedent, its matter files, or the systems its lawyers work in every day. Making that context usable is the moat in legal AI, and design decides how much of it a lawyer can actually get to.\n\nPlatform is the spine of the design team. It defines how we work in an AI-native way and sets the standard every product team builds on. Most design systems are run as a service: product teams decide what to build, the system team supplies the parts. On an AI-native team, the system sets the craft bar instead of serving it, and its users aren't only designers. When anyone in EPD can generate an interface, the system is what keeps quality consistent and gets teams to a shipped implementation faster. Building that is one of the highest-leverage jobs at Harvey, and you'll shape the team around it. You'll own the system every team builds from and the AI tooling that changes what a designer can produce.\n\nYou'll report to the VP Design as a foundational member of the Design leadership team, with portfolio-wide impact on how our product, team, and culture scale. You'll set the operating bar for how we work, and lay foundations for the product that hold for years.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn Admin as a product\n\n - Drive strategy and execution for the Admin platform in close partnership with Product and Engineering, rooted in how champions actually run Harvey inside their firms.\n\n - Work directly with customers, research, and usage data to find where champions lose time or lose confidence, and design the workflow configuration, knowledge management, and visibility experiences that fix it.\n\n - Tie your roadmap to customer outcomes: faster rollout, wider adoption, and evidence of ROI our champions can take to their own leadership.\n\nOwn the system, not the service\n\n - Define Harvey's design system as a set of product decisions: what good looks like for AI-powered legal work, encoded as patterns product teams inherit rather than requests they submit.\n\n - Set the craft bar across interaction, systems thinking, content design, and visual execution, and hold it as our surface area grows.\n\n - Build the governance model that lets the system move fast without fragmenting: contribution paths, adoption expectations, and clear calls on when a team may deviate.\n\nOwn AI tooling for the design org\n\n - Decide how Harvey's designers use AI: what tools we adopt, what we build ourselves, and what the new default workflow looks like from problem to prototype.\n\n - Raise the floor and the ceiling. Make the whole team faster, and make it possible for a single designer to ship things that used to take a pod.\n\n - Treat this as a live experiment with real rigor. Try things, measure them, kill what doesn't work, and share what does across EPD.\n\nBuild and lead the team\n\n - Build, grow, and develop a team of high-craft ICs across systems, product, and prototyping from a small starting footprint.\n\n - Own org design, resourcing, and prioritization across four surfaces with very different rhythms, including the conference deadlines that don't move.\n\n - Give strategic, systems-level feedback on end-to-end flows, not just screens.\n\nLead across the org\n\n - Partner with design, product, and engineering leaders to evolve how Harvey builds, and represent Platform in high-stakes conversations with executives and customers.\n\n - Establish how we make design decisions in high-trust, high-stakes environments where clarity and accuracy are non-negotiable.\n\n - Be a foundational member of the Design leadership team and help set the operating model the rest of the org runs on.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8-10+ years in Product Design, with 5+ years directly managing product designers.\n\n - Experience owning a design system at real scale, including the political work of getting it adopted.\n\n - Experience designing and shipping AI-powered or highly technical products.\n\n - A strong portfolio showing leadership of complex products from concept through launch, with clear impact on users and the business.\n\n - Fluency with AI tooling in your own practice, and a real opinion about how it changes design work.\n\n - Proven experience leading design strategy and execution alongside Product and Engineering.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to define and ship high-quality experiences in complex, ambiguous problem spaces.\n\n - Excellent judgment about when to go deep, when to delegate, and when to push.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills and the ability to influence senior stakeholders, internally and in front of customers.\n\n - Deep commitment to growing people and raising the craft bar across a team.\n\n - Comfort operating in fast-moving environments with evolving priorities.\n\n - Empathy for users, teammates, and the realities of high-stakes professional work.\n\n - A growth mindset, resilience, and a bias toward learning through doing.\n\n - Strong people leadership instincts with a bias toward clarity, empathy, and accountability.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$235,500 - $325,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$235.5K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$235.5K - $325K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"55dca9fa-d9d1-43b3-bfa9-ab600d624d43","tierSummary":"$235.5K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6de86328-0530-42ea-ad30-dc0291e18ef9","summary":"$235.5K – $325K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":235500,"maxValue":325000},{"id":"cd224c00-5e42-4072-95c2-9fda837d9fd7","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fa5c0392-e7b1-4c9b-8440-4db3751cc45c","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":235500,"maxValue":325000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c143ce81-2b61-428b-a275-391514bd4eb4","title":"Senior Manager, Product Design, Platform","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T21:08:11.999+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c143ce81-2b61-428b-a275-391514bd4eb4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/c143ce81-2b61-428b-a275-391514bd4eb4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior Manager, Product Design to lead two parts of Harvey: our Admin experience and our Platform design system team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Admin</strong> is how firm leaders and innovation teams configure, govern, and scale Harvey inside their organizations, from workflow configuration to usage visibility. These champions are the main decision makers in whether Harvey succeeds at an account, and Admin is where they turn their investment into measurable return. The team also owns our knowledge platform and how legal connectors get integrated into Harvey. A general model can reason about law. But it can't reach a firm's precedent, its matter files, or the systems its lawyers work in every day. Making that context usable is the moat in legal AI, and design decides how much of it a lawyer can actually get to.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Platform</strong> is the spine of the design team. It defines how we work in an AI-native way and sets the standard every product team builds on. Most design systems are run as a service: product teams decide what to build, the system team supplies the parts. On an AI-native team, the system sets the craft bar instead of serving it, and its users aren't only designers. When anyone in EPD can generate an interface, the system is what keeps quality consistent and gets teams to a shipped implementation faster. Building that is one of the highest-leverage jobs at Harvey, and you'll shape the team around it. You'll own the system every team builds from and the AI tooling that changes what a designer can produce.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to the VP Design as a foundational member of the Design leadership team, with portfolio-wide impact on how our product, team, and culture scale. You'll set the operating bar for how we work, and lay foundations for the product that hold for years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own Admin as a product</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive strategy and execution for the Admin platform in close partnership with Product and Engineering, rooted in how champions actually run Harvey inside their firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with customers, research, and usage data to find where champions lose time or lose confidence, and design the workflow configuration, knowledge management, and visibility experiences that fix it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tie your roadmap to customer outcomes: faster rollout, wider adoption, and evidence of ROI our champions can take to their own leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the system, not the service</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define Harvey's design system as a set of product decisions: what good looks like for AI-powered legal work, encoded as patterns product teams inherit rather than requests they submit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the craft bar across interaction, systems thinking, content design, and visual execution, and hold it as our surface area grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the governance model that lets the system move fast without fragmenting: contribution paths, adoption expectations, and clear calls on when a team may deviate.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own AI tooling for the design org</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Decide how Harvey's designers use AI: what tools we adopt, what we build ourselves, and what the new default workflow looks like from problem to prototype.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the floor and the ceiling. Make the whole team faster, and make it possible for a single designer to ship things that used to take a pod.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Treat this as a live experiment with real rigor. Try things, measure them, kill what doesn't work, and share what does across EPD.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and lead the team</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, grow, and develop a team of high-craft ICs across systems, product, and prototyping from a small starting footprint.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own org design, resourcing, and prioritization across four surfaces with very different rhythms, including the conference deadlines that don't move.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Give strategic, systems-level feedback on end-to-end flows, not just screens.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead across the org</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with design, product, and engineering leaders to evolve how Harvey builds, and represent Platform in high-stakes conversations with executives and customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish how we make design decisions in high-trust, high-stakes environments where clarity and accuracy are non-negotiable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a foundational member of the Design leadership team and help set the operating model the rest of the org runs on.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8-10+ years in Product Design, with 5+ years directly managing product designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning a design system at real scale, including the political work of getting it adopted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and shipping AI-powered or highly technical products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong portfolio showing leadership of complex products from concept through launch, with clear impact on users and the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI tooling in your own practice, and a real opinion about how it changes design work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience leading design strategy and execution alongside Product and Engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to define and ship high-quality experiences in complex, ambiguous problem spaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment about when to go deep, when to delegate, and when to push.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills and the ability to influence senior stakeholders, internally and in front of customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep commitment to growing people and raising the craft bar across a team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in fast-moving environments with evolving priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathy for users, teammates, and the realities of high-stakes professional work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A growth mindset, resilience, and a bias toward learning through doing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong people leadership instincts with a bias toward clarity, empathy, and accountability.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$235,500 - $325,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JC1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Manager, Product Design to lead two parts of Harvey: our Admin experience and our Platform design system team.\n\nAdmin is how firm leaders and innovation teams configure, govern, and scale Harvey inside their organizations, from workflow configuration to usage visibility. These champions are the main decision makers in whether Harvey succeeds at an account, and Admin is where they turn their investment into measurable return. The team also owns our knowledge platform and how legal connectors get integrated into Harvey. A general model can reason about law. But it can't reach a firm's precedent, its matter files, or the systems its lawyers work in every day. Making that context usable is the moat in legal AI, and design decides how much of it a lawyer can actually get to.\n\nPlatform is the spine of the design team. It defines how we work in an AI-native way and sets the standard every product team builds on. Most design systems are run as a service: product teams decide what to build, the system team supplies the parts. On an AI-native team, the system sets the craft bar instead of serving it, and its users aren't only designers. When anyone in EPD can generate an interface, the system is what keeps quality consistent and gets teams to a shipped implementation faster. Building that is one of the highest-leverage jobs at Harvey, and you'll shape the team around it. You'll own the system every team builds from and the AI tooling that changes what a designer can produce.\n\nYou'll report to the VP Design as a foundational member of the Design leadership team, with portfolio-wide impact on how our product, team, and culture scale. You'll set the operating bar for how we work, and lay foundations for the product that hold for years.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nOwn Admin as a product\n\n - Drive strategy and execution for the Admin platform in close partnership with Product and Engineering, rooted in how champions actually run Harvey inside their firms.\n\n - Work directly with customers, research, and usage data to find where champions lose time or lose confidence, and design the workflow configuration, knowledge management, and visibility experiences that fix it.\n\n - Tie your roadmap to customer outcomes: faster rollout, wider adoption, and evidence of ROI our champions can take to their own leadership.\n\nOwn the system, not the service\n\n - Define Harvey's design system as a set of product decisions: what good looks like for AI-powered legal work, encoded as patterns product teams inherit rather than requests they submit.\n\n - Set the craft bar across interaction, systems thinking, content design, and visual execution, and hold it as our surface area grows.\n\n - Build the governance model that lets the system move fast without fragmenting: contribution paths, adoption expectations, and clear calls on when a team may deviate.\n\nOwn AI tooling for the design org\n\n - Decide how Harvey's designers use AI: what tools we adopt, what we build ourselves, and what the new default workflow looks like from problem to prototype.\n\n - Raise the floor and the ceiling. Make the whole team faster, and make it possible for a single designer to ship things that used to take a pod.\n\n - Treat this as a live experiment with real rigor. Try things, measure them, kill what doesn't work, and share what does across EPD.\n\nBuild and lead the team\n\n - Build, grow, and develop a team of high-craft ICs across systems, product, and prototyping from a small starting footprint.\n\n - Own org design, resourcing, and prioritization across four surfaces with very different rhythms, including the conference deadlines that don't move.\n\n - Give strategic, systems-level feedback on end-to-end flows, not just screens.\n\nLead across the org\n\n - Partner with design, product, and engineering leaders to evolve how Harvey builds, and represent Platform in high-stakes conversations with executives and customers.\n\n - Establish how we make design decisions in high-trust, high-stakes environments where clarity and accuracy are non-negotiable.\n\n - Be a foundational member of the Design leadership team and help set the operating model the rest of the org runs on.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8-10+ years in Product Design, with 5+ years directly managing product designers.\n\n - Experience owning a design system at real scale, including the political work of getting it adopted.\n\n - Experience designing and shipping AI-powered or highly technical products.\n\n - A strong portfolio showing leadership of complex products from concept through launch, with clear impact on users and the business.\n\n - Fluency with AI tooling in your own practice, and a real opinion about how it changes design work.\n\n - Proven experience leading design strategy and execution alongside Product and Engineering.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to define and ship high-quality experiences in complex, ambiguous problem spaces.\n\n - Excellent judgment about when to go deep, when to delegate, and when to push.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills and the ability to influence senior stakeholders, internally and in front of customers.\n\n - Deep commitment to growing people and raising the craft bar across a team.\n\n - Comfort operating in fast-moving environments with evolving priorities.\n\n - Empathy for users, teammates, and the realities of high-stakes professional work.\n\n - A growth mindset, resilience, and a bias toward learning through doing.\n\n - Strong people leadership instincts with a bias toward clarity, empathy, and accountability.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$235,500 - $325,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JC1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$235.5K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$235.5K - $325K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"19c25c60-4f38-40e5-9ef6-57790aef9319","tierSummary":"$235.5K – $325K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"82af5dc5-d36e-496b-b04c-e80bae791397","summary":"$235.5K – $325K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":235500,"maxValue":325000},{"id":"a7e4b940-b62a-4bcb-a013-22115770a551","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"628528d7-af39-49db-81c1-744a273df596","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":235500,"maxValue":325000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"65f46384-53c0-46ab-b87a-ab228c562f55","title":"Customer Experience Manager, US","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T23:10:38.178+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/65f46384-53c0-46ab-b87a-ab228c562f55","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/65f46384-53c0-46ab-b87a-ab228c562f55/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harvey is looking for a Customer Experience (CX) Manager to lead a high-performing support team serving lawyers and professional services teams. Our customers hold their own work to a high standard of accuracy and timeliness, and expect the same from our support. How well your region runs is one of the biggest levers Harvey has on what customers actually experience when they need help. Reporting to the Head of CX, you'll drive operational excellence and accountability across Harvey's global support organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll balance strategic oversight with hands-on execution. This is a role for a leader who thrives in motion: proactive, decisive, and deeply motivated by achieving results through your team. You'll inherit a metric set and processes that need to be better, and we expect you to diagnose what's broken and fix it without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll also be one of five CX Managers across the globe, and that peer group is where our operating standard gets set. You're expected to trade what's working across regions and push for the changes you think we should make everywhere, shaping the culture and cadence of a growing support organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run day-to-day support delivery for your region: queue and coverage, triage and handoff, and escalation judgment, measured by First Response Time, Resolution Time, QA, and cSAT. When a number moves, you find the root cause and fix it or scale it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set individual performance expectations and stay close enough to the work to spot drift early. Coach against QA results in the moment, and move to a documented plan only when coaching hasn't landed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own escalations end to end: triage and severity judgment, customer communication through to resolution, and bug reports Engineering can act on without a follow-up thread. Partner with Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market to turn recurring escalations into fixes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take part in the on-call rotation for customer-impacting incidents, owning the coordination of response and customer communication strategy while an incident is live.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive adoption of the AI tools and systems we provide across triage, drafting, deflection, and QA, and pressure-test what CX Ops ships against real queue conditions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track how your region performs against the other four, bring what's working to your peers, adopt what's working in theirs, and propose the practices you think should apply globally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forecast coverage and staffing against volume, and flag gaps before they have impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, onboard, and develop team members to ensure readiness for future growth and evolving support needs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years in customer support or customer experience, including 4+ years managing teams in a high-volume environment serving enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating at Harvey's pace, not a typical enterprise pace. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong support managers to clear.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A deep focus on the customer, and real satisfaction in solving the problems that make their work harder than it needs to be.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are genuinely invested in developing your team, and you know a high bar is part of that.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You manage close to the work. You know what your team's tickets actually look like, not just what the dashboard says.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A change you made to how a support team works that produced a step change, not an incremental gain. You saw the leverage point others in the seat missed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership of a metric set (FRT, TTR, cSAT, QA, backlog, deflection): what drives each one, what to change when one slips, and the ability to build your own reporting. We use Zendesk, Salesforce, Omni, and Snowflake.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You understand enterprise escalations, from severity judgment through the customer conversation, and can work one yourself: reproduce the issue, read error logs, and troubleshoot API, authentication, and AI output quality issues well enough to brief Engineering accurately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can take a process improvement from idea to shipped yourself, and you know which ones to handover to someone on your team instead.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Day-to-day proficiency using AI tools in a production support workflow, not experimentation, and a concrete point of view on how AI is changing what a support team should look like.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Admin-level fluency with Zendesk or an equivalent platform: views, triggers, macros, and routing logic.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$144,000 - $216,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-CG1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nHarvey is looking for a Customer Experience (CX) Manager to lead a high-performing support team serving lawyers and professional services teams. Our customers hold their own work to a high standard of accuracy and timeliness, and expect the same from our support. How well your region runs is one of the biggest levers Harvey has on what customers actually experience when they need help. Reporting to the Head of CX, you'll drive operational excellence and accountability across Harvey's global support organization.\n\n\n\nYou'll balance strategic oversight with hands-on execution. This is a role for a leader who thrives in motion: proactive, decisive, and deeply motivated by achieving results through your team. You'll inherit a metric set and processes that need to be better, and we expect you to diagnose what's broken and fix it without being asked.\n\nYou'll also be one of five CX Managers across the globe, and that peer group is where our operating standard gets set. You're expected to trade what's working across regions and push for the changes you think we should make everywhere, shaping the culture and cadence of a growing support organization.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Run day-to-day support delivery for your region: queue and coverage, triage and handoff, and escalation judgment, measured by First Response Time, Resolution Time, QA, and cSAT. When a number moves, you find the root cause and fix it or scale it.\n\n - Set individual performance expectations and stay close enough to the work to spot drift early. Coach against QA results in the moment, and move to a documented plan only when coaching hasn't landed.\n\n - Own escalations end to end: triage and severity judgment, customer communication through to resolution, and bug reports Engineering can act on without a follow-up thread. Partner with Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market to turn recurring escalations into fixes.\n\n - Take part in the on-call rotation for customer-impacting incidents, owning the coordination of response and customer communication strategy while an incident is live.\n\n - Drive adoption of the AI tools and systems we provide across triage, drafting, deflection, and QA, and pressure-test what CX Ops ships against real queue conditions.\n\n - Track how your region performs against the other four, bring what's working to your peers, adopt what's working in theirs, and propose the practices you think should apply globally.\n\n - Forecast coverage and staffing against volume, and flag gaps before they have impact.\n\n - Hire, onboard, and develop team members to ensure readiness for future growth and evolving support needs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 8+ years in customer support or customer experience, including 4+ years managing teams in a high-volume environment serving enterprise customers.\n\n - Comfortable operating at Harvey's pace, not a typical enterprise pace. This is consistently the hardest bar for otherwise-strong support managers to clear.\n\n - A deep focus on the customer, and real satisfaction in solving the problems that make their work harder than it needs to be.\n\n - You are genuinely invested in developing your team, and you know a high bar is part of that.\n\n - You manage close to the work. You know what your team's tickets actually look like, not just what the dashboard says.\n\n - A change you made to how a support team works that produced a step change, not an incremental gain. You saw the leverage point others in the seat missed.\n\n - Ownership of a metric set (FRT, TTR, cSAT, QA, backlog, deflection): what drives each one, what to change when one slips, and the ability to build your own reporting. We use Zendesk, Salesforce, Omni, and Snowflake.\n\n - You understand enterprise escalations, from severity judgment through the customer conversation, and can work one yourself: reproduce the issue, read error logs, and troubleshoot API, authentication, and AI output quality issues well enough to brief Engineering accurately.\n\n - You can take a process improvement from idea to shipped yourself, and you know which ones to handover to someone on your team instead.\n\n - Day-to-day proficiency using AI tools in a production support workflow, not experimentation, and a concrete point of view on how AI is changing what a support team should look like.\n\n - Admin-level fluency with Zendesk or an equivalent platform: views, triggers, macros, and routing logic.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$144,000 - $216,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-CG1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$144K – $216K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$144K - $216K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d25d6a6c-87c5-42b4-a7d0-ab1b5ae163a3","tierSummary":"$144K – $216K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d3a5f595-8b1d-4bd7-a87a-0f4c1e3cd23c","summary":"$144K – $216K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":216000},{"id":"c06dd885-725c-4589-9393-b7e876ac8328","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b1941704-169b-49b0-b437-ffa35a2ed543","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":216000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9cf781f8-6203-4cd7-a1c8-0c149fc2afc5","title":"Content Marketing Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:11.967+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9cf781f8-6203-4cd7-a1c8-0c149fc2afc5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/9cf781f8-6203-4cd7-a1c8-0c149fc2afc5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Content Marketing Manager will develop content that advances Harvey's brand and business goals across editorial, campaigns, and social. This person will turn company priorities, customer insights, and market opportunities into high-quality content, then work across teams to distribute it effectively and measure its impact. This is a role for a strong writer and editor who is equally comfortable shaping strategy and producing the work itself, and who can translate complex legal, technical, and product ideas into clear, compelling stories.</p><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to Harvey's editorial strategy and help execute the content roadmap set by the Head of Content and Social Strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and edit content across formats, including website articles, guides, reports, thought leadership, social series, video scripts, and campaign copy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn complex legal, technical, and product ideas into clear, compelling stories for Harvey's audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop content-led campaigns in partnership with product marketing, demand generation, communications, social, and other teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create distribution strategies that extend the reach and value of each major content asset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write planned social copy and captions connected to editorial content, campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the SEO lead to apply search insights to content planning, development, and optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use audience and performance data to understand what is working and improve future content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a consistent, distinctive Harvey voice across channels and formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Content Operations and Publishing to move work efficiently through production, review, and publication.</p></li></ul><h1></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in content marketing, editorial, or a closely related discipline, ideally in B2B technology, SaaS, or professional services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional writing and editing skills, with a portfolio that demonstrates range across long-form editorial, thought leadership, campaign copy, and social.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven ability to translate complex or technical subject matter into clear, engaging narratives for sophisticated audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to an editorial strategy and delivering against a content roadmap, taking ownership of high-quality output end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with a track record of partnering with product marketing, demand generation, communications, and social teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SEO fundamentals and comfort using search insights to shape content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with content performance metrics and the judgment to turn data into better editorial decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A sharp eye for brand voice and the discipline to maintain it consistently across channels and formats.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$136,000 - 187,000 USD</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-LR1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThe Content Marketing Manager will develop content that advances Harvey's brand and business goals across editorial, campaigns, and social. This person will turn company priorities, customer insights, and market opportunities into high-quality content, then work across teams to distribute it effectively and measure its impact. This is a role for a strong writer and editor who is equally comfortable shaping strategy and producing the work itself, and who can translate complex legal, technical, and product ideas into clear, compelling stories.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Contribute to Harvey's editorial strategy and help execute the content roadmap set by the Head of Content and Social Strategy.\n\n - Write and edit content across formats, including website articles, guides, reports, thought leadership, social series, video scripts, and campaign copy.\n\n - Turn complex legal, technical, and product ideas into clear, compelling stories for Harvey's audiences.\n\n - Develop content-led campaigns in partnership with product marketing, demand generation, communications, social, and other teams.\n\n - Create distribution strategies that extend the reach and value of each major content asset.\n\n - Write planned social copy and captions connected to editorial content, campaigns, launches, and brand initiatives.\n\n - Partner with the SEO lead to apply search insights to content planning, development, and optimization.\n\n - Use audience and performance data to understand what is working and improve future content.\n\n - Maintain a consistent, distinctive Harvey voice across channels and formats.\n\n - Partner with Content Operations and Publishing to move work efficiently through production, review, and publication.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 5+ years of experience in content marketing, editorial, or a closely related discipline, ideally in B2B technology, SaaS, or professional services.\n\n - Exceptional writing and editing skills, with a portfolio that demonstrates range across long-form editorial, thought leadership, campaign copy, and social.\n\n - A proven ability to translate complex or technical subject matter into clear, engaging narratives for sophisticated audiences.\n\n - Experience contributing to an editorial strategy and delivering against a content roadmap, taking ownership of high-quality output end to end.\n\n - Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with a track record of partnering with product marketing, demand generation, communications, and social teams.\n\n - Familiarity with SEO fundamentals and comfort using search insights to shape content.\n\n - Fluency with content performance metrics and the judgment to turn data into better editorial decisions.\n\n - A sharp eye for brand voice and the discipline to maintain it consistently across channels and formats.\n   \n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$136,000 - 187,000 USD\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n\n\n#LI-LR1\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$136K - $187K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ea386f8e-5527-40e5-bf7f-4d28dc0b5c32","tierSummary":"$136K – $187K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b8e32b4a-e7ce-41ec-98ef-6b3fd5d7ded5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7c168a22-a9d5-4611-bd4b-fb4bc9119c1e","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"a8b6efa2-bd0a-4062-9c51-f4ba16eb2a94","summary":"$136K – $187K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":136000,"maxValue":187000}]}},{"id":"2beb0375-9708-4ae3-bd64-9b892b8ac184","title":"Head of Mid-Market Sales","department":"Go to Market","team":"Go to Market","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T23:56:03.134+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"England","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2beb0375-9708-4ae3-bd64-9b892b8ac184","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/2beb0375-9708-4ae3-bd64-9b892b8ac184/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a second-line leadership role where you will lead frontline managers, build a world-class team, and own the regional Mid-Market number. You will be responsible for turning strong early traction into a repeatable, high-performing go-to-market engine across legal and professional services.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are still early. That means you will operate across altitudes, setting strategy, building structure, and staying close to the field on critical deals. You will help define how Harvey shows up in the EMEA market, shape our sales motion, and ensure we are delivering real value to customers adopting AI in high-stakes, knowledge-heavy environments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for someone who has done this before, built through managers, scaled teams in ambiguity, and knows what great looks like in enterprise sales.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach and develop a team of Mid Market Sales Managers across EMEA, driving accountability for net new logo and expansion ARR targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the regional sales strategy, including territory design, coverage models, and go-to-market execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own EMEA mid-market forecasting and pipeline health, providing accurate reporting to senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, coach, and retain top managerial talent; build a strong leadership bench across the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with global mid-market leadership to localize and refine the sales playbook for EMEA markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with marketing, solutions engineering, legal, and customer success to ensure a cohesive customer experience across the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent EMEA mid-market in global planning cycles, headcount discussions, and strategic initiatives.</p></li></ul><h1><strong><br />What You Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of B2B tech sales experience, including 4+ years managing and developing sales managers or senior individual contributors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success leading a regional or multi-market sales organization in a high-growth, early-stage environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record of selling complex software to enterprise or mid-market clients using a consultative, value-based methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating across EMEA markets, with an understanding of regional dynamics, buyer behaviors, and legal industry nuances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication and executive presence — able to influence both frontline teams and senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine passion for Harvey's mission and a strong interest in how AI is transforming knowledge work and the legal profession.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Depending on your location, an Applicant Privacy Notice may apply to you. You can find all of our Applicant Privacy Notices </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-JM1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Harvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:accommodations@harvey.ai\">accommodations@harvey.ai</a></p>","descriptionPlain":"WHY HARVEY\n\nAt Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.\n\nThis is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.\n\nOur team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.\n\nAt Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.\n\n\n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nThis is a second-line leadership role where you will lead frontline managers, build a world-class team, and own the regional Mid-Market number. You will be responsible for turning strong early traction into a repeatable, high-performing go-to-market engine across legal and professional services.\n\nWe are still early. That means you will operate across altitudes, setting strategy, building structure, and staying close to the field on critical deals. You will help define how Harvey shows up in the EMEA market, shape our sales motion, and ensure we are delivering real value to customers adopting AI in high-stakes, knowledge-heavy environments.\n\nWe are looking for someone who has done this before, built through managers, scaled teams in ambiguity, and knows what great looks like in enterprise sales.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Lead, coach and develop a team of Mid Market Sales Managers across EMEA, driving accountability for net new logo and expansion ARR targets.\n\n - Set the regional sales strategy, including territory design, coverage models, and go-to-market execution.\n\n - Own EMEA mid-market forecasting and pipeline health, providing accurate reporting to senior leadership.\n\n - Hire, coach, and retain top managerial talent; build a strong leadership bench across the region.\n\n - Partner with global mid-market leadership to localize and refine the sales playbook for EMEA markets.\n\n - Work cross-functionally with marketing, solutions engineering, legal, and customer success to ensure a cohesive customer experience across the region.\n\n - Represent EMEA mid-market in global planning cycles, headcount discussions, and strategic initiatives.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - 10+ years of B2B tech sales experience, including 4+ years managing and developing sales managers or senior individual contributors.\n\n - Demonstrated success leading a regional or multi-market sales organization in a high-growth, early-stage environment.\n\n - Strong track record of selling complex software to enterprise or mid-market clients using a consultative, value-based methodology.\n\n - Experience operating across EMEA markets, with an understanding of regional dynamics, buyer behaviors, and legal industry nuances.\n\n - Exceptional communication and executive presence — able to influence both frontline teams and senior stakeholders.\n\n - Genuine passion for Harvey's mission and a strong interest in how AI is transforming knowledge work and the legal profession.\n\n\n\n\nDEPENDING ON YOUR LOCATION, AN APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICE MAY APPLY TO YOU. YOU CAN FIND ALL OF OUR APPLICANT PRIVACY NOTICES HERE https://harveyai.notion.site/Harvey-Candidate-Privacy-Notices-319ac3fcdd7a803bb807d5094f249922?pvs=74.\n\n#LI-JM1\n\n\n\nHarvey is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.\n\nWe are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made by emailing accommodations@harvey.ai","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}